\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says Omicron Covid variant a \u8216\'20\'18cause for concern, not panic\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano (now) and Vivian Ho (earlier) \par \uc2 6,010 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2021\par 01:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight and beat this new variant\u8217\'20\'19Biden says best protection is to get vaccinated and boostedSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * The CDC announced Monday that all adults should get a Covid-19 booster shot, strengthening its previous recommendation amid growing concerns over the Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  is reportedly planning to request authorization from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for its Covid booster for 16- and 17-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 * Dr Oz is expected to join the Pennsylvania Senate race as a Republican to replace \uc2 Pat Toomey\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  postponed his remarks about the supply chain for Tuesday instead.\par \par \uc2 * Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  hung up on a phone call with far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 . The phone call was to address Islamophobic comments that Boebert made about Omar - Omar wanted a public apology while Boebert also wanted an apology from Omar.\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol announced on Monday that it will vote to recommend the criminal prosecution of top former Trump justice department official Jeffrey Clark, after he defied a subpoena seeking his cooperation with the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 * The justice department is accusing Trump ally \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  of seeking to try his charge of criminal contempt of Congress through the media.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Vivian Ho and Dani Anguiano\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Dr Oz expected to join Pennsylvania Senate race\par \par \uc2 Dr Mehmet Oz is expected to join the Pennsylvania Senate race, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/news/dr-oz-joins-pa-senate-race-2022-20211129.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Philadelphia Inquirer}}}\uc2  reports. Several news reports in recent weeks have indicated the TV doctor, who until recently lived in New Jersey, was considering running as a Republican to replace Senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Army veteran Sean Parnell was previously considered the lead contender in the race and had gained an endorsement from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but he suspended his campaign after losing a custody battle with his estranged wife. His wife had accused him of abusing her and striking one of their children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing more important to me than my children, and while I plan to ask the court to reconsider, I can\u8217\'20\'19t continue with a Senate campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D Parnell said.\par \par \uc2 Oz would enter the race with widespread name recognition, but not without controversy. He has a history of promoting dubious medical treatments on his show. In 2015, a group of prominent doctors urged \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  to cut ties with Oz for \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2015/apr/17/dr-oz-columbia-doctors-quack-treatments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an egregious lack of integrity}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cquack treatments\u8221\'20\'1D unsupported by scientific evidence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Alabama will get another union election after the company was found to have violated labor law in the previous election, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The move is a major blow to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which had spent about a year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/mar/29/amazon-bessemer-alabama-union-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressively campaigning}}}\uc2  for warehouse workers in Bessemer to reject the union, which they ultimately did by a wide margin.\par \par \uc2 It also comes at a time of widespread labor unrest in the US as a somewhat rejuvenated American union movement is flexing its muscles in an economy that is seeking to recover from the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The rare move was first announced on Monday by the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU), which spearheaded the union organizing movement. A \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) spokeswoman confirmed the decision.\par \par \uc2 The RWDSU charged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  with illegal misconduct during the first vote. In August, the hearing officer at NLRB who presided over the case determined that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  violated labor law and recommended that the regional director set aside the results and direct another election.\par \par \uc2 Full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/nov/29/amazon-union-election-bessemer-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon workers in Alabama to get another union election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin has told reporters he won\u8217\'20\'19t commit to passing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better bill by Christmas, the timeline laid out by Chuck Schumer, the Senate majority leader. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will wait to see what we have,\u8221\'20\'1D the West Virginia Democrat said.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust spoke with Sen. Manchin, whose vote remains crucial to passing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better bill. He wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t commit to Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s Christmas timeframe. And wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t commit to voting to proceed to the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will wait to see what we have,\u8221\'20\'1D he told a group of us\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1465438907693211655?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Manchin and Arizona Senator Krysten Sinema have wielded outsize influence over the president\u8217\'20\'19s $1.75tn social spending and climate package, which was passed by Democrats in the House of Representatives earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The conservative pair, who present the last hurdle to the president\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better plan, pressured colleagues to cut the cost of the plan in half and continue to raise concerns over its cost. The Senate holdouts have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/28/joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema-build-back-better-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavily criticized}}}\uc2  for accepting a flood of money from Republican and corporate donors.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/28/joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema-build-back-better-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Manchin and Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s status as Senate holdouts is proving lucrative}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  is reportedly planning to request authorization for its Covid booster for 16- and 17-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 The company and partner BioNTech are expected to ask the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to authorize its booster shot for the age group in the coming days, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/11/29/covid-vaccine-16-17-year-olds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 . All adults are currently eligible for the booster shot after the CDC strengthened its booster recommendation on Monday amid growing fears over the new Omicron variant. The variant has not yet been detected in the US, but the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  warns it poses a high global risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the current overall situation of the pandemic, \uc2 FDA\uc2  will evaluate any such EUA request in a very timely manner,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency told the Post.\par \par \uc2 A Pfizer spokesperson said the company expects \u8220\'20\'1Cto share updates on this soon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon. I\u8217\'20\'19m Dani Anguiano and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be taking over our live US politics coverage for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 The CDC announced Monday that all adults should get a Covid-19 booster shot, strengthening its previous recommendation amid growing concerns over the Omicron variant. The agency now recommends that everyone 18 and older get a booster shot within two months of receiving the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine or within six months of receiving the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna shots.\par \par \uc2 enltrCDC is strengthening its recommendation on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19}}}\uc2  vaccine booster doses. Everyone ages 18 and older should get a booster shot either when they are 6 months after their initial \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna series or 2 months after initial J&J vaccine. Learn more: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/77CTFuJFcO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/77CTFuJFcO}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oW2hyHRPmr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oW2hyHRPmr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CDC (@CDCgov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CDCgov/status/1465440956870803457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  has said the Omicron variant carries a very {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/29/omicron-covid-variant-poses-very-high-global-risk-says-who"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high global risk}}}\uc2  of infection surges. Though significant questions remain, including whether the new variant is more transmissible. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/biden-omicron-covid-coronavirus-vaccines-boosters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Monday that the variant is a \u8220\'20\'1Ccause for concern, not a cause for panic\u8221\'20\'1D, and urged Americans to get vaccinated and get booster shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not wait,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CGo get your booster if it\u8217\'20\'19s time for you to do so. And if you are not vaccinated, now is the time to go get vaccinated and to bring your children to go get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  postponed his remarks about the supply chain for tomorrow instead.\par \par \uc2 * Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  hung up on a phone call with far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 . The phone call was to address Islamophobic comments that Boebert made about Omar - Omar wanted a public apology while Boebert also wanted an apology from Omar.\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol announced on Monday that it will vote to recommend the criminal prosecution of top former Trump justice department official Jeffrey Clark, after he defied a subpoena seeking his cooperation with the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 * The justice department is accusing Trump ally \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , the Trump ally of charging his criminal contempt of Congress through the media.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 So far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  has posted on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  her version of the phone call with Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , and the Islamophobic remarks she made about Omar for which she had to issue an apology.\par \par \uc2 Turns out, Boebert went into the phone call expecting Omar to apologize to her.\par \par \uc2 enltrBoebert's play-by-play of the call:\par \par \uc2 - Omar asked Boebert for a "public apology"\par \par \uc2 - Boebert told Omar she should apologize for "anti-American, anti-semitic, anti-police rhetoric"\par \par \uc2 - Some back n forth\par \par \uc2 - Omar hung up, which Boebert argues is part of "cancel culture 101" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/faRS4iYGUA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/faRS4iYGUA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ursula Perano (@UrsulaPerano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UrsulaPerano/status/1465428536924295173?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In 1973, supreme court justices issued a landmark ruling in the case of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , effectively legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the US.\par \par \uc2 In Roe, the court affirmed that access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a constitutional right. The court ruled that states could not ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus can survive outside the womb, roughly considered to be 24 weeks gestation (a full-term pregnancy is considered to be 39 weeks).\par \par \uc2 Now, Roe faces a direct challenge. The supreme court justices has taken up the case of Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Clinic, in which they will consider whether the state of Mississippi can ban nearly all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 15 weeks. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates believe the choice to take the case implies that at last four justices see it as a chance to reconsider the precedent set by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments in the case are set to be heard on 1 December, Wednesday, with a ruling expected in June next year. But already, pro-choice campaigners are warning of a future where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may no longer be legal in the majority of the US.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What will US\u8217\'20\'19s future look like if \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  becomes a crime again?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was set to speak about the supply chain today, his second public remarks of the day. But at last minute, the White House postponed the event until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden was scheduled to deliver remarks on the supply chain today at 3:45 p.m.\par \par \uc2 But the White House now says he will do so on Wednesday instead.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yamiche Alcindor (@Yamiche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1465418809544777733?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  has issued a new statement regarding a phone call she had with far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  regarding the Islamophobic remarks Boebert made about Omar.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of apologizing for her Islamophobic comments and fabricated lies, Representative Boebert refused to publicly acknowledge her hurtful and dangerous comments,\u8221\'20\'1D Omar said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe instead doubled down on her rhetoric and I decided to end the unproductive call.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Omar\u8217\'20\'19s statement on her conversation with \uc2 Rep. Lauren Boebert\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B5JJVijXKI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B5JJVijXKI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1465408483512180738?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CToday, I graciously accepted a call from \uc2 Rep. Lauren Boebert\uc2  in the hope of receiving a direct apology for falsely claiming she met me in an elevator, suggesting I was a terrorist, and for a history of anti-Muslim hate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1465408484883812352?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CInstead of apologizing for her Islamophobic comments and fabricated lies, Rep. Boebert refused to publicly acknowledge her hurtful and dangerous comments. She instead doubled down on her rhetoric and I decided to end the unproductive call.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1465408485861036044?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CTo date, the Republican Party leadership has done nothing to condemn and hold their own members accountable for repeated instances of anti-Muslim hate and harassment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1465408487710769154?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about one hateful statement or one politician; it is about a party that has mainstreamed bigotry and hatred. It is time for Republican Leader McCarthy to actually hold his party accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1465408488671256579?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/27/ilhan-omar-lauren-boebert-bigotry-republicans-trump-pelosi-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments in her home district}}}\uc2 , Boebert referred to Omar as part of the \u8220\'20\'1CJihad Squad\u8221\'20\'1D and described her as a suicide bomber. R epublican congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois called her \u8220\'20\'1Ctrash\u8221\'20\'1D for her remarks, but House minority leader Kevin McCarthy has been noticably silent on the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/trump-press-democrats-debate-electoral-fraud-lie-schiff-meadows-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact-free}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D approach to the presidency created unprecedented challenges for intelligence officials responsible for briefing him, according to a newly released account from the CIA.\par \par \uc2 The 45th president\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic and freewheeling style, which included rarely reading anything put in front of him, resulted in the presidential daily briefing, or PDB \u8211\'20\'13 a crucial security update including information about potential threats to the US \u8211\'20\'13 being delivered more regularly to Vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence}}}\uc2  instead, the report states.\par \par \uc2 By the middle of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term in office, his briefings were reduced to two weekly sessions of 45 minutes each. Briefings were discontinued altogether following the deadly insurrection of 6 January, which was sparked by Trump urging his supporters to march on the US Capitol in a failed attempt to overturn his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/donald-trump-fact-free-presidential-briefings-cia-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18fact-free\u8217\'20\'19 approach caused briefing challenges, CIA report says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 6 January committee targets Clark for contempt charge\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack announced on Monday that it will vote to recommend the criminal prosecution of top former Trump justice department official Jeffrey Clark, after he defied a subpoena seeking his cooperation with the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 The move to pursue contempt of Congress charges against Clark reflects the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive approach to warn recalcitrant witnesses against attempting to derail their investigation as Trump tried during his administration.\par \par \uc2 Members on the select committee will convene on Wednesday evening to vote on the contempt report \u8211\'20\'13 which is expected to be unanimous, according to a source familiar with the matter \u8211\'20\'13 and send it to a vote before the full House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/jeffrey-clark-capitol-attack-committee-contempt-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol riot panel to vote for contempt charges against Trump DoJ official}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The former Florida congresswoman Carrie Meek, who died on Sunday, has been remembered as a trailblazer, a descendent of enslaved people who became one of the first Black Floridians elected to Congress since Reconstruction.\par \par \uc2 Carrie Meek. Photograph: Steve Cannon/AP\par \par \uc2 The late congressman John Lewis had another way of describing her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see showboats and we see tugboats. She\u8217\'20\'19s a tugboat. I never want to be on the side of issues against her,\u8221\'20\'1D Lewis said of Meek in 1999.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, politicians and public figures including \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the House speaker, recalled a pioneering career, many noting Meek\u8217\'20\'19s devotion to working-class families in her Miami district as well as her powerful oratory, in an outpouring of support after her death at 95 after a long illness.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/29/carrie-meek-daughter-sharecroppers-florida-congresswoman-dies-aged-95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carrie Meek, daughter of Black sharecroppers who blazed path to Congress, dies aged 95}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  has accused \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , the Trump ally and adviser charged with criminal contempt of Congress, of trying to try his own case through the media.\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 . Photograph: Drew Angerer/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Bannon pleaded not guilty to the rare charge, which carries jail time and a fine and which arises from his refusal to co-operate with the House select committee investigating the deadly attack on the US Capitol on 6 January, by Trump supporters seeking to overturn the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, the DoJ filed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=0000017d-6993-d3d7-a37d-ef9f021a0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a response to Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s request}}}\uc2  for all records in the case to be made public.\par \par \uc2 Assistant US attorney Amanda Vaughn wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe defense\u8217\'20\'19s misleading claims, failure to confer, unexplained wholesale opposition, and extrajudicial statements make clear the defense\u8217\'20\'19s real purpose: to abuse criminal discovery to try this case in the media rather than in court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s request, last Wednesday, came with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/stephen-k-bannons-lawyers-file-opposition-to-keeping-documents-from-being-released/2021/11/25/29889174-4e3e-11ec-b73b-a00d6e559a6e_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  to the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMembers of the public should make their own independent judgment as to whether the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  is committed to a just result based upon all the facts,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the opposition filed today, Mr Bannon asked the judge to follow the normal process and allow unfettered access to and use of the documents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vaughan made clear prosecutors have been aware of Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s tactics from the start, writing with reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/15/steve-bannon-contempt-charges-surrenders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his appearance in court earlier in November}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CUpon release from custody, the defendant and his counsel gathered the press outside of the courthouse and made a five-minute statement about the pending charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-diE7kCCidE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Misdemeanor from Hell\u8217\'20\'19: Watch Bannon Speak Out After He\u8217\'20\'19s Released}}}\uc2 , CNN, 15 November 2021\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vaughan also wrote that Bannon had \u8220\'20\'1Cindicated he intends to publicly disseminate [court] materials for an improper purpose: to make extrajudicial arguments about the merits of the case pending against him and the validity of the government\u8217\'20\'19s decision to seek an indictment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CContrary to what the defendant told the Washington Post, allowing unfettered public access to discovery materials, regardless of their use or relevance to public judicial proceedings, is not the \u8216\'20\'18normal process\u8217\'20\'19. It is the opposite of normal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/28/capitol-attack-mark-meadows-trump-contempt-of-congress-schiff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more}}}\uc2  on the 6 January committee and what might be coming this week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/28/capitol-attack-mark-meadows-trump-contempt-of-congress-schiff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack: Schiff says Mark Meadows contempt decision imminent }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressed Americans about the omicron variant of Covid-19, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ccause for concern, not a cause for panic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Both Biden and White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  defended the travel ban issued against eight southern African countries - but not against the number of other countries in Europe and beyond where scientists have detected the variant. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s much more wider spread\u8221\'20\'1D in southern Africa, Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 * Congress is expected to be busy this week with the debt limit, with the House of Representatives set to introduce a stopgap funding bill to extend government funding beyond the current deadline \u8211\'20\'13 Friday 3 December \u8211\'20\'13 through mid- to late January, with 21 January and 28 January the dates up for discussion.\par \par \uc2 * Democrat congressman Tom Suozzi has just announced that he will be running for governor of New York, making him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1465348382340403212?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 18th Democrat}}}\uc2  in Congress to not seek reelection in 2022 - very much putting the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 narrow majority at risk.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today a f ederal court issued an injunction pausing the vaccine mandate for most healthcare workers.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  had a response:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re obviously going to abide by the law and fight any efforts in court or otherwise to prevent local authorities, officials, leaders in the health care industries and other industries from protecting their workforces,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: in suit Missouri and Kansas brought, a federal judge has temporarily halted Biden administration's vaccine mandate for most health care workers, writing "the public would suffer little, if any, harm from maintaining the 'status quo'" during litigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/moleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #moleg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ksleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ksleg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeanne Kuang (@JeanneKuang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeanneKuang/status/1465364303125622785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki noted that private, individual companies can put in place requirements in order to protect their workforce and that is something a number of companies have done across the company. \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to encourage leaders to take steps to protect their workforces,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  addressed the travel ban that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  issued against eight southern African countries - the omicron variant of Covid-19 was first detected in that region.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe objective here is not to punish, but to protect the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs you just heard the president say, this is not going to prevent - this is going to delay and that delay is going to help us have the necessary time to do the research by our health and medical teams to get more people vaccinated and more people boosted. He is always going to air on the side of protecting the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though the omicron variant has since been detected the United Kingdom, Australia, Belgium, Botswana, Denmark, Germany, Hong Kong, Israel, Italy, the Netherlands, France and Canada. Psaki said the reason why the ban applied to southern Africa rather than these other countries is because there were thousands of omicron cases in southern Africa while only a few cases in the other countries..\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The new omicron variant is at the forefront of today\u8217\'20\'19s White House press briefing. Again, there have been no reported cases on US soil yet. But White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said today the administration\u8217\'20\'19s top health officials are \u8220\'20\'1Cworking around the clock\u8221\'20\'1D to be prepared and the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2  is meeting today with state labs and state health associations to make sure everybody is ready on a federal, state and local level.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the president was trying to convey is that there are several layers of work to be done right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has taken the podium for the White House press briefing, prepping the press corps for the president\u8217\'20\'19s round table meeting for Cyber Monday with the chief executives of several companies to discuss issues with the supply chain, which he will be speaking about later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was immediately asked about the travel ban he issued, which he said was because \u8220\'20\'1Cthere were a significant number of cases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe needed time to get people the opportunity to get the vaccination now before it moved around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden. said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t anticipate any more travel restrictions. \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, took to the podium to explain the stringent requirements already in place for those traveling internationally to the US - travellers must both be vaccinated and be tested before entering.\par \par \uc2 Biden said he does not anticipate the need for any future lockdowns. \u8220\'20\'1CIf people are vaccinated and wear their masks, there won\u8217\'20\'19t be a need for a lockdown,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to fast-track vaccine development should Omicron require it\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the event, hopefully unlikely, that updated vaccinations or boosters are needed to respond to this new variant, we will accelerate their development and deployment with every available tool.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not yet believe that additional measures will be needed. But so that we are prepared if needed, my team is already working with officials at \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna and \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  to develop contingency plans for vaccines and boosters if needed. I will also direct the \uc2 FDA\uc2  (\uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 ) and CDC (\uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2 ) to use the fastest process possible without cutting any corners for safekeeping to get vaccines approved and on the market as soon as possible if needed.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  takes the podium to answer a question at the address on Monday. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sparing no effort. I\u8217\'20\'19m removing all road blocks to keep the American people safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: best protection against Omicron is vaccination and booster\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are 1 8 years and older and got fully vaccinated before 1 June go get the get booster shot today,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said today. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re free and they\u8217\'20\'19re available at 80,000 locations coast to coast. A fully vaccinated booster person is the most protected against Covid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not wait. Go get your booster if it\u8217\'20\'19s time for you to do so. And if you are not vaccinated, now is the time to go get vaccinated and to bring your children to go get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far, no cases of the new omicron variant of Covid-19 have been reported in the US. But Biden said it\u8217\'20\'19s only a matter of time. \u8220\'20\'1CSooner or later, we are going to see new cases of this new variant here in the United States and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to face this new threat just as we have faced the ones that came before it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: Omicron variant is cause for concern, not panic\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took to the podium to tell Americans that the new omicron variant of Covid-19 \u8220\'20\'1Cis a cause for concern, not a cause for panic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll fight this variant with scientific and knowledgeable actions and speed, not chaos and confusion,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have more tools today to fight the variant than we ever had before, from vaccines to boosters, to vaccines for children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA year ago, America was floundering against the first variant of Covid,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWe beat that variant significantly, and then we got hit by a far more powerful threat, the Delta variant. But we took action and now we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing deaths from Delta come down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight and beat this new variant as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to speak momentarily about the new omicron variant of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-joe-biden-health-infectious-diseases-anthony-fauci-44fab8b3448ad31f0865aebb26f91741?fbclid=IwAR2_yf9HnD5Jyr1a5Q3xouCHzvQjaYkLoDhacPFO6hKaugpCD9yPXceeiAo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reporting }}}\uc2  that the president is expected to urge Americans to get vaccinated - but not push for more restrictions - in the face of this new variant, of which there are no reported cases yet in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat congressman Tom Suozzi has just announced that he will be running for governor of New York.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Long Island Rep. Tom Suozzi officially announces he is running for governor of New York. Says three things set him apart from other candidates: competence, ideology and vision for the future\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rebecca C. Lewis (@_rebeccaclewis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_rebeccaclewis/status/1465351303094276097?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"I'm a common-sense Democrat... I'll work with anybody to actually solve problems," Suozzi says of ideology. "It's not about being politically correct, it's about doing the correct thing to actually help people."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rebecca C. Lewis (@_rebeccaclewis)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_rebeccaclewis/status/1465352055778852875?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This is significant in that Suozzi is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1465348382340403212?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now the 18th Democrat}}}\uc2  in Congress to not seek reelection in 2022, putting at risk the very narrow majority that the left holds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Actor Matthew McConaughey has officially announced that he will not be running for governor of Texas, a seat for which former Democratic congressman and candidate for Senate and president \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  is also vying.\par \par \uc2 Read more about it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/matthew-mcconaughey-texas-governor-will-not-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matthew McConaughey says he will not run for Texas governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tis the season for the White House to unveil its holiday decorations - a task that falls under the purview of first lady Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 enltrExcited to share that the Official White House Christmas tree is up in the Blue Room! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/od943V0k5Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/od943V0k5Q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill Biden (@FLOTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS/status/1465310444344725512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst Lady Jill Biden unveiled her holiday decorations at the White House this morning. The theme is \u8220\'20\'1CGifts from the Heart.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G466FLbURb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/G466FLbURb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1465333941381050368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the White House FLOTUS added children\u8217\'20\'19s books. Decorations include stacks of books with butterflies made out of recycled paper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UHACCAgRaE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UHACCAgRaE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emily Goodin (@Emilylgoodin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Emilylgoodin/status/1465294772353081349?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLots of blue and and white thus far within the first part of the White House Christmas decor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZBO01MTgxm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZBO01MTgxm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Beatrice-Elizabeth Peterson (@MissBeaE) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MissBeaE/status/1465294041260646400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDecorations on tree are thank you notes the Bidens have received while in White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ptw1fw9NoI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ptw1fw9NoI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emily Goodin (@Emilylgoodin)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Emilylgoodin/status/1465299371629682689?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWreaths up on the windows at the White House. This morning the \u8220\'20\'1CGifts from the Heart\u8221\'20\'1D theme holiday decorations will be unveiled. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  set to speak this afternoon. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OwjRIEFqbo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OwjRIEFqbo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Bennett (@KateBennett_DC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateBennett_DC/status/1465284299805102089?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrArt (of all forms) is a major theme this year in the White House Christmas decorations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A3otfyIBRO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A3otfyIBRO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Beatrice-Elizabeth Peterson (@MissBeaE)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MissBeaE/status/1465310935187402756?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThese shoes were made for dancing and decorations at The White House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qAKh1pnDX0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qAKh1pnDX0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Beatrice-Elizabeth Peterson (@MissBeaE) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MissBeaE/status/1465311222136463367?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , a senator from Kentucky, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/20/anthony-fauci-rand-paul-coronavirus-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clashed publicly}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  over virus research carried out before the pandemic. Ted Cruz, from Texas, has said Fauci should be prosecuted regarding his handling of the Covid response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci told \uc2 CBS\uc2  in his Sunday interview. \u8220\'20\'1CI have to laugh at that. I should be prosecuted? What happened on 6 January, senator?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cruz was among Republicans who voted to object to electoral college results in key states, even after Trump supporters mounted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/28/capitol-attack-mark-meadows-trump-contempt-of-congress-schiff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deadly attack on the US Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked if he was being made a scapegoat for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s failings under Covid, Fauci said: \u8220\'20\'1COf course, you have to be asleep not to figure that one out \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s OK, I\u8217\'20\'19m just going to do my job and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be saving lives and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be lying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Playing politics with his role in the Covid response, Fauci said, was \u8220\'20\'1Cunbelievably bad because all I want to do is save people\u8217\'20\'19s lives. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I have done for the last 50 years \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, anybody who\u8217\'20\'19s looking at this carefully realises that there\u8217\'20\'19s a distinct anti-science flavor to this. So if they get up and criticize science, nobody\u8217\'20\'19s going to know what they\u8217\'20\'19re talking about. But if they get up and really aim their bullets at \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2 , well, people could recognize there\u8217\'20\'19s a person there. There\u8217\'20\'19s a face, there\u8217\'20\'19s a voice you can recognize, you see him on television.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo it\u8217\'20\'19s easy to criticise, but they\u8217\'20\'19re really criticising science because I represent science. That\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous. To me, that\u8217\'20\'19s more dangerous than the slings and the arrows that get thrown at me.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to be around here forever, but science is going to be here forever. And if you damage science, you are doing something very detrimental to society long after I leave. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what I worry about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of one memorable exchange between Paul and Fauci, from a Senate hearing in July:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/28/us-covid-omicron-variant-fifth-wave-fauci"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadcast by CBS on Sunday}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  had strong words for Republicans attacking him over his role in the federal coronavirus response.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 . Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser has served seven presidents since 1984 and is now to the fore in preparations for the arrival of the Omicron coronavirus variant and efforts to increase vaccination against Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Fauci was often at odds with his boss or attacked by him. He attracted death threats as well as the ire of Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 He told \uc2 CBS\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI dealt with it by focusing on what my job is from the time that I went into medicine to right now. Where I am at my age\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 nearly 81 \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cmy job has been totally focused on doing what I can with the talents and the influence I had to make scientific advances to protect the health of the American public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo anybody who spins lies and threatens and all that theatre that goes on with some of the investigations and the congressional committees and the Rand Pauls and all that other nonsense \u8230\'20\'26 that\u8217\'20\'19s noise. I know what my job is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/28/us-covid-omicron-variant-fifth-wave-fauci"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fauci: US could face \u8216\'20\'18fifth wave\u8217\'20\'19 of Covid as Omicron variant nears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 , a Capitol Hill-focused outlet, is reporting that House leaders are ready to introduce a stopgap funding bill to extend government funding beyond the current deadline \u8211\'20\'13 Friday 3 December \u8211\'20\'13 through mid- to late January, with 21 January and 28 January the dates up for discussion.\par \par \uc2 A floor vote could take place as early as Wednesday, but then Senate leaders will need an agreement to push the resolution through by Friday.\par \par \uc2 There is also the small matter of the debt limit, the arbitrary borrowing cap that is raised each year to prevent the US from defaulting on its debts \u8211\'20\'13 a move that would cause economic catastrophe across the globe. The treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , has said the US can meet its obligations till 15 December or so.\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl isn\u8217\'20\'19t expecting the same high drama on the issue as October, when Biden bluffed on filibuster reform to get Republicans to move amid heated words from both sides. But the week\u8217\'20\'19s still young.\par \par \uc2 Republicans believe Democrats and Democrats alone should raise the debt limit, which would be fine if the Democrats held workable majorities in both the House and the Senate. Last time, the Republicans twice used their beloved filibuster to block efforts to raise the debt limit which required 60 votes.\par \par \uc2 In October, Republicans wanted Democrats to raise the debt limit through budget reconciliation, a complicated process that neither Biden nor Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  were very keen on \u8211\'20\'13 in part because there are only so many times Congress can consider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbpp.org/research/federal-budget/introduction-to-budget-reconciliation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reconciliation bills}}}\uc2  each year. One has already gone to the Covid bill and the ambitious Build Back Better Act is now before the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Last time out, Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  eventually agreed to a short-term deal that increased the borrowing limit by $480bn \u8211\'20\'13 sufficient to prevent the government from defaulting by keeping debt payments up until mid-December.\par \par \uc2 Which is quite soon, if not so soon as the deadline to fund government itself.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to deliver remarks on Omicron Covid variant\par \par \uc2 Ahoy there, live blog readers. Let\u8217\'20\'19s strap in for the week, shall we?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to deliver remarks at the White House twice today. He\u8217\'20\'19s sure to field questions about supposedly impending economic doom but the main purposes of the remarks will be the spread of the Omicron coronavirus variant (first, at 11.45am ET) and issues with the supply chain (second, at 3.45pm ET).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  said this morning Omicron is likely to spread internationally, posing a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery high\u8221\'20\'1D global risk where Covid-19 surges could have \u8220\'20\'1Csevere consequences\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COmicron has an unprecedented number of spike mutations, some of which are concerning for their potential impact on the trajectory of the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D the WHO said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe overall global risk related to the new variant of concern Omicron is assessed as very high.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No cases have yet been reported in the US. Press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is scheduled brief too, at 1pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Congress has plenty on its plate too. We\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of December, which for all those keeping score out there means it\u8217\'20\'19s time to once again talk about the possibility of the federal government shutting down and/or disaster over the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 More to come.\par \par \uc2 2021-11-29T14:44:44Z 2021-11-30T01:18:46Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/43d65a2232b5f71edc159e5bc53bacf907db167c/0_315_8192_4915/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/43d65a2232b5f71edc159e5bc53bacf907db167c/0_315_8192_4915/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Biden at the White House on Monday. He said: \u8216\'20\'18If you are not vaccinated, now is the time to go get vaccinated.\u8217\'20\'19 Carrie Meek. \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 . \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  takes the podium to answer a question at the address on Monday. \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211129ehbt0020e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
