\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House committee subpoenas far-right groups and leaders over Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 6,984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2021\par 00:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Proud Boys, Oath Keepers and 1st Amendment Praetorian get subpoenasProud Boys leader denied early release from Washington DC jailPresident touts effort to lower gas prices as inflation hits 31-year highBiden to release 50m barrels of oil in effort to bring down US gas pricesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection issued five subpoenas to far-right groups and leaders, including the Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers. The extremist groups are believed to have been involved in planning the Capitol attack on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 * Biden delivered a speech on the steps his administration is taking to address rising prices in the US, including mitigating bottlenecks at ports and ensuring store shelves remain stocked for Thanksgiving. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech came as inflation has hit a 31-year high, with prices increasing by 6.2% over the past 12 months. That\u8217\'20\'19s the most rapid acceleration since December 1990.\par \par \uc2 * Biden announced he will release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve, in an effort to lower gas prices. The price of gas has increased by 49.6% over the past year, bringing the national average for a gallon of gas to $3.40, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per AAA}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt will take time, but before long, you should see the price of gas fall where you fill up your tank,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his speech this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration has asked a federal court to lift the stay on a coronavirus vaccination rule for large businesses. The rule, which was set to go into effect on 4 January, would require those working for companies with at least 100 employees to get vaccinated or receive weekly coronavirus tests to mitigate the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates are pushing local bans, city by small city\par \par \uc2 Audra Jane Heidrichs reports:\par \par \uc2 In May of this year, six city council members in Lebanon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , a city located just north of Cincinnati, voted on an ordinance that would effectively outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 21,000 people that call it home.\par \par \uc2 As in countless council meetings in small cities across the country where mask mandates, teaching about race in schools and access to reproductive healthcare have become politically charged in America\u8217\'20\'19s current climate, the night unfolded in a series of near-Shakespearean acts.\par \par \uc2 On the morning the meeting was scheduled, Krista Wyatt, a former firefighter elected to city council in 2018 and the only member expected to vote against the ordinance, formally resigned. In an accompanying statement, Wyatt wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a core group of people who have hijacked the council to force their personal, political and religious views on the entire citizenship of Lebanon. It is not fair to the citizens and is not the role of a City Council member to be a moral compass.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dozens of people spoke at the meeting later that evening. Some sang, many shared deeply personal experiences of rape or miscarriages and a few even led prayers. Just outside the doors of city hall, pro-choice and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups similarly squared off, shouting at each other and urging passersby to honk in support of one side or the other.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately though, the vote was a resolute 6-0, making Lebanon the 29th city in the nation, and the first city in Ohio, to pass an enforceable ordinance outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within their city limits. As the nation waits for a supreme court ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, pro-choice advocates and activists across the US know first-hand that any upcoming national ruling might be almost irrelevant given what\u8217\'20\'19s already taken place in Ohio and beyond.\par \par \uc2 For the last few months, small municipalities \u8211\'20\'13 many without any standing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://local12.com/news/local/will-more-ohio-cities-follow-in-mason-lebanons-footsteps-to-outlaw-abortion-cincinnati"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvxu.org/local-news/2021-10-25/mason-city-council-bans-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mason}}}\uc2  and soon maybe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2021/10/26/abortion-ban-proposed-london-ohio-outlaw-clinics-and-drugs/8549391002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others}}}\uc2 , have outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Though women in those cities can still travel to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bans send an intimidating message.\par \par \uc2 Bypassing statehouses and targeting smaller towns and cities governed by council has emerged as a successful strategy for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates in recent years. In July, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/07/state-policy-trends-midyear-2021-already-worst-legislative-year-ever-us-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  revealed that at least 30 towns in six states \u8211\'20\'13 Arkansas, Indiana, New Mexico, New York, Ohio and Texas \u8211\'20\'13 have approved municipal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the last three years. Some of these ordinances also target specific \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and organizations providing other types of practical support to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/23/anti-abortion-local-bans-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  advocates are pushing local bans, city by small city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jury awards $25m in damages over deadly 2017 Charlottesville far-right rally\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 A jury has awarded more than $25m in damages against white nationalist leaders for violence that erupted during the deadly 2017 far-right rally in Charlottesville.\par \par \uc2 The defendants were accused of promoting and then carrying out racially motivated violence during the \u8220\'20\'1CUnite the Right\u8221\'20\'1D rally. After a nearly monthlong civil trial, a jury in US district court in Charlottesville deadlocked on two claims but found the white nationalists liable on four other counts in the lawsuit that was filed by nine people who suffered physical or emotional injuries during the two days of demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 Attorney Roberta Kaplan said the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 lawyers plan to refile the suit so a new jury can decide the two claims this jury could not reach a verdict on. She called the amount of damages awarded from the other counts \u8220\'20\'1Ceye opening\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat sends a loud message,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaplan said.\par \par \uc2 The verdict, though mixed, is a rebuke to the white nationalist movement, particularly for the two dozen individuals and organizations who were accused in a federal lawsuit of orchestrating violence against African Americans, Jews and others in a meticulously planned conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 White nationalist leader \uc2 Richard Spencer\uc2  vowed to appeal. He said plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 attorneys made it clear before the trial that they wanted to use the case to bankrupt him and other defendants.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the plaintiffs invoked a 150-year-old law passed after the civil war to shield freed slaves from violence and protect their civil rights. Commonly known as the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  Act, the law contains a rarely used provision that allows private citizens to sue other citizens for civil rights violations.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/charlottesville-white-nationalist-rally-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jury awards $25m in damages over deadly 2017 Charlottesville far-right rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A statue of Thomas Jefferson has been removed from city hall in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2 , because the founder and third president enslaved people.\par \par \uc2 A work crew spent several hours freeing the 884lb, 7ft statue from its pedestal in the council chambers and carefully maneuvering it into a padded wooden crate, for the short journey to the New York Historical Society.\par \par \uc2 The city public design commission, appointed by the mayor, \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2 , voted earlier in the day to exile the statue, sculpted in 1833, on a 10-year loan.\par \par \uc2 Opinions are mixed about the removal.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nyassembly.gov/mem/Charles-Barron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charles Barron}}}\uc2 , a member of the New York assembly and a former council member, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/15/nyregion/thomas-jefferson-statue-nyc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt should be destroyed. A statue should be for those who we honor for their exemplary service and duty to all of this country, not just the white race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/art/people/faculty-staff/michele-h-bogart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michele Bogart}}}\uc2 , professor emeritus of art history at \uc2 Stony Brook University\uc2 , said the statue\u8217\'20\'19s removal \u8220\'20\'1Cdeflects attention\u8221\'20\'1D from the actions of such controversial figures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a philosophical problem with removing it from city hall,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you can remove the Thomas Jefferson statue, then you can remove works from other city buildings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/thomas-jefferson-statuue-new-york-city-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York city hall removes Thomas Jefferson statue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection issued five subpoenas to far-right groups and leaders, including the Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers. The extremist groups are believed to have been involved in planning the Capitol attack on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 * Biden delivered a speech on the steps his administration is taking to address rising prices in the US, including mitigating bottlenecks at ports and ensuring store shelves remain stocked for Thanksgiving. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech came as inflation has hit a 31-year high, with prices increasing by 6.2% over the past 12 months. That\u8217\'20\'19s the most rapid acceleration since December 1990.\par \par \uc2 * Biden announced he will release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve, in an effort to lower gas prices. The price of gas has increased by 49.6% over the past year, bringing the national average for a gallon of gas to $3.40, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per AAA}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt will take time, but before long, you should see the price of gas fall where you fill up your tank,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his speech this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration has asked a federal court to lift the stay on a coronavirus vaccination rule for large businesses. The rule, which was set to go into effect on 4 January, would require those working for companies with at least 100 employees to get vaccinated or receive weekly coronavirus tests to mitigate the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the Thanksgiving holiday on Thursday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are participating in a service event at the non-profit DC Central Kitchen.\par \par \uc2 The president and the vice-president -- joined by their spouses, first lady Jill Biden and second gentleman Doug Emhoff -- are helping prepare meals for DC Central Kitchen\u8217\'20\'19s clients.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden, Dr. Biden, Vice President Harris and Doug Emhoff are all helping prepare meals for those in need at DC Central Kitchen. The non-profit makes 5,000 meals a day. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/diPBds17r6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/diPBds17r6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Bixby (@scottbix) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottbix/status/1463264488191401988?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the White House, the non-profit prepares roughly 5,000 meals a day for homeless shelters, rehabilitation clinics and after-school programs in the DC area.\par \par \uc2 After the event, the Bidens will head to Nantucket, where they will spend Thanksgiving with their family.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Centrist senator Joe Manchin questioned \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s energy policies after the president announced he would release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, the Democratic chair of the Senate energy and natural resources committee, argued Biden should be undergoing a broader review of his approach to oil supply in the face of rising gas prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s release from the strategic petroleum reserve is an important policy Band-Aid for rising gas prices but does not solve for the self-inflicted wound that shortsighted energy policy is having on our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI continue to call on President Biden to responsibly increase energy production here at home and to reverse course to allow the Keystone XL pipeline to be built which would have provided our country with up to 900,000 barrels of oil per day from Canada, one of our closest allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of course, that position is extremely unpopular with environmentalists, who say the US is already not doing enough to combat the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, at the daily White House press briefing, energy secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  spoke to reporters about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans to address high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 Granholm touted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve, while acknowledging it will take time to see lower prices at the pump.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelvscott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RachelVScott}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CHow soon will Americans see prices at the pump drop and how long do you expect that to last?"\par \par \uc2 Energy Sec. \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2 : "I'm not going to make a prediction about how much and how long." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zKtwP5hc4R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zKtwP5hc4R}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gbR8JaDhdC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gbR8JaDhdC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1463248020963799045?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to make a prediction about how much and how long,\u8221\'20\'1D Granholm said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt won\u8217\'20\'19t happen tomorrow, but it\u8217\'20\'19ll happen over the next few weeks that people will hopefully start to see the difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The energy secretary added that the administration is focused on ensuring gas prices are \u8220\'20\'1Cnot being held artificially high\u8221\'20\'1D because of oil and gas companies\u8217\'20\'19 profit-driven strategies.\par \par \uc2 Biden sent a letter to the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  last week asking the agency to investigate \u8220\'20\'1Cmounting evidence of anti-consumer behavior by oil and gas companies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The latest round of subpoenas from the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection comes one day after the panel subpoenaed a group of far-right political activists, including \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and Alex Jones.\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reported yesterday:\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas demanding documents and testimony expand the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry focused on the planning and financing of the rally at the Ellipse, by targeting operatives who appear to have had contacts with the Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 House investigators issued subpoenas to the veteran operatives Stone and Jones, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson Taylor Budowich, and the pro-Trump activists Dustin Stockton and his wife, Jennifer Lawrence.\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the select committee, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , said the subpoenas aimed to uncover \u8216\'20\'18who organized, planned, paid for, and received funds related to those events, as well as what communications organizers had with officials in the White House and Congress\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/22/roger-stone-alex-jones-subpoenas-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roger Stone and Alex Jones among five to receive Capitol attack subpoenas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Proud Boys leader \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , who was just subpoenaed by the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, is currently sitting in a DC jail.\par \par \uc2 Tarrio is about halfway through a five-month sentence for his illegal activity at a pro-Trump rally last December, during which he set fire to a stolen Black Lives Matter banner.\par \par \uc2 Although Tarrio did not actually participate in the insurrection, the Proud Boys leader is believed to have been involved in the preparation for the Capitol attack, according to the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s latest statement.\par \par \uc2 (On a related note, Tarrio\u8217\'20\'19s request for an early release from jail due to unsanitary conditions was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/23/joe-biden-economy-inflation-speech-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-619d277d8f08adafd16025d6#block-619d277d8f08adafd16025d6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just denied}}}\uc2  by a judge.)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the chair of the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, said the subpoenaed far-right groups and leaders would be able to shed light on the days leading up to the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the individuals and organizations we subpoenaed today have relevant information about how violence erupted at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and the preparation leading up to this violent attack,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said in a statement announcing the latest round of subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Select Committee is moving swiftly to uncover the facts of what happened on that day and we expect every witness to comply with the law and cooperate so we can get answers to the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Capitol attack committee subpoenas far-right groups and leaders\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection has subpoenaed far-right groups believed to have been involved in planning the attack.\par \par \uc2 The five new subpoenas were sent to the far-right groups Proud Boys, Oath Keepers and 1st Amendment Praetorian.\par \par \uc2 Leaders of those groups -- \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  of Proud Boys, Elmer Stewart Rhodes of Oath Keepers and Robert Patrick Lewis of 1st Amendment Praetorian -- were also subpoenaed by the committee.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Select Committee subpoenas individuals and organizations linked to the violent attack on the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Proud Boys International, L.L.C.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Henry \u8220\'20\'1CEnrique\u8221\'20\'1D Tarrio\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Oath Keepers\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Elmer Stewart Rhodes\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Robert Patrick Lewis/1st Amendment Praetorian\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 January 6th Committee (@January6thCmte) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/January6thCmte/status/1463236995543617539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also promised that grocery stores will be \u8220\'20\'1Cwell-stocked\u8221\'20\'1D for the Thanksgiving holiday on Thursday, amid concerns about shortages caused by supply-chain issues.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted his administration is working to mitigate bottlenecks at ports by working to increase hours of operation at those sites, thus allowing more products to be delivered.\par \par \uc2 The president said the number of containers sitting on docks has decreased in recent weeks, as shipping prices have also fallen.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Families can rest easy: grocery stores are well-stocked with turkey and everything else you need for Thanksgiving," Pres. Biden says. "And the major retailers I mentioned have confirmed that their shelves will be well-stocked...this holiday season." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FJN5bDYKsY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/FJN5bDYKsY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MJkRZs9K9g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MJkRZs9K9g}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1463229150949519367?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore goods are moving more quickly and more cheaply out of our ports -- onto your doorsteps and onto store shelves,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Noting that he recently met with the CEOs of companies like \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and Target, Biden added, \u8220\'20\'1CFamilies can rest easy: grocery stores are well-stocked with turkey and everything else you need for Thanksgiving. And the major retailers I mentioned have confirmed that their shelves will be well-stocked in stores this holiday season.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president concluded his prepared remarks and did not answer any of the questions that reporters shouted at him as he departed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pushed back against the \u8220\'20\'1Cmyth\u8221\'20\'1D that efforts to combat the climate crisis, like investing in the production of electric vehicles, is raising gas prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy effort to combat climate change is not raising the price of gas,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat it\u8217\'20\'19s doing, it\u8217\'20\'19s increasing the availability of jobs -- jobs building electric cars like the one I drove at the GM factory in Detroit last week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden noted those who buy electric vehicles will save $800 to $1,000 in fuel costs this year, and he expressed hope that those savings will soon be made available to more Americans through his economic policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden touts decision to release oil from strategic reserve: 'We\u8217\'20\'19re taking action'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  acknowledged many Americans are struggling with the rising price of gas, which has increased by 49.6% over the past year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is, we always get through those spikes. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get through this one and hopefully faster,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we should just stand by idly and wait for prices to drop on their own. Instead, we\u8217\'20\'19re taking action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president touted his administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve to help lower gas prices as the country enters the holiday season.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will take time, but before long, you should see the price of gas fall where you fill up your tank,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden delivers remarks on the need to lower prices\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on the state of the US economy and the need to lower prices for American families.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes as the country grapples with the highest rate of inflation in 31 years, with prices rising by 6.2% over the past 12 months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve made historic progress over the last 10 months,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, pointing to the 5.6m jobs added to the economy since he took office in January.\par \par \uc2 But the president acknowledged the economy is still struggling in certain sectors, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CDisruptions related to the pandemic have caused challenges in our supply chain, which have sparked concern about shortages and contributed to higher prices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/23/joe-biden-economy-inflation-speech-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-619cfc818f0866e46b621d40#block-619cfc818f0866e46b621d40"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced today}}}\uc2  that he will release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve to help address high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 The move is being done in coordination with other major energy consumers like China, India, Japan, South Korea and the UK.\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear whether the move will actually lower gas prices, which have increased by 49.6% over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-11-23/will-biden-s-u-s-crude-oil-stockpile-release-actually-bring-down-gas-prices?srnd=premium"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explains}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Everyone\u8217\'20\'19s been talking about this possibility for so long that many traders say the plan for the release was already baked into oil prices. That would explain why oil prices are up following the announcement. There\u8217\'20\'19s also a fear OPEC+ officials, who don\u8217\'20\'19t like being bossed around, could respond by canceling plans to boost their own production, negating the addition of stockpiled oil onto the market. The standoff sets up a fight for control of the global energy market. In short, consumers looking for relief at the pump may not see lower gasoline prices for months yet, if at all.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump ally Gohmert enters Texas AG race\par \par \uc2 The rightwing Texas congressman Louie Gohmert, a prominent climate change denier and Covid anti-masker, has joined an already rambunctious pursuit for the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general office involving \uc2 George P Bush\uc2 , nephew of the former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , and the embattled incumbent \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Louie Gohmert. Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The entry of the fierce \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalist into the race is seen by some in Republican circles as part of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s push to install allies in powerful state positions ahead of the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 Efforts by Trump to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the courts and several state legislatures fell flat, and analysts say he is determined to secure a friendlier playing field if he runs again.\par \par \uc2 He could not ask for a more supportive candidate than the allegedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/06/01/louie-gohmert-qanon-texas-insurrection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 QAnon-aligned Gohmert}}}\uc2 , a proponent of extreme conspiracy theories including one that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2010/08/rep-louie-gohmerts-terror-baby-meltdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terrorists were sending pregnant women to the US}}}\uc2  to raise America-hating offspring.\par \par \uc2 In December 2020, Gohmert filed a federal lawsuit against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , swiftly rejected by courts up to and including the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , seeking to allow him to replace certified state electors with those chosen by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 One problem for Gohmert is that Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/07/26/trump-endorses-paxton-500804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already endorsed Paxton}}}\uc2 , who is battling a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/aug/03/texas-attorney-general-ken-paxton-securities-fraud-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-running securities fraud indictment}}}\uc2  and is under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcdfw.com/news/local/texas-news/state-bar-investigating-texas-attorney-general-ken-paxton-ap-exclusive/2653029/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate investigations}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the Texas state bar.\par \par \uc2 George P Bush\uc2 , the current Texas land commissioner and son of the former Florida governor Jeb Bush, had hoped Trump would back him, despite his apparent loathing of the Bush family. His efforts to ingratiate himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/27/politics/george-p-bush-donald-trump-ken-paxton/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended in humiliation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A jury in Georgia has begun deliberations in the trial of the three white men accused of murdering Ahmaud Arbery, after 10 days of evidence and lengthy closing arguments in the closely watched case, which like that of Kyle Rittenhouse in Wisconsin has become part of the ongoing movement for, and debate over, racial justice in the US.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday morning, prosecutors ended closing arguments before Judge Timothy Walmsley, who briefed the jury on the multiple counts of murder, false imprisonment and other charges faced by the three defendants.\par \par \uc2 Travis McMichael, his father Greg McMichael and their neighbour William \u8220\'20\'1CRoddie\u8221\'20\'1D Bryan pursued Arbery, a Black 25 year-old, for five minutes in February 2020 in the neighborhood of Satilla Shores, south Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Travis McMichael, armed with a pump action shotgun, fire three times at Arbery, who was unarmed. Prosecutors say the three men had no legal justification to chase Arbery and box him in with their trucks. The shooting was captured on video by Bryan who, prosecutors say, repeatedly attempted to ram Arbery during the pursuit.\par \par \uc2 The three men have pleaded not guilty to all charges, claiming they attempted to enact a citizen\u8217\'20\'19s arrest. The McMichaels have claimed they believed Arbery was involved in a spate of break-ins and burglaries in the neighborhood, and that Travis McMichael opened fire in self-defense.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, lead prosecutor Linda Dunikoski repeatedly ripped into the claim of self-defense.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t claim self-defense if you are the unjustified aggressor,\u8221\'20\'1D Dunikoski said. \u8220\'20\'1CWho started this? It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t Ahmaud Arbery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/ahmaud-arbery-killing-jury-to-begin-deliberations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ahmaud Arbery killing: three men charged provoked confrontation, prosecutor says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pollster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/11/23/trump-2024-map-523230?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=0000014e-f116-dd93-ad7f-f917ef350000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thinks he will run}}}\uc2  for the White House again in 2024, with a clear path to victory through five states he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020: Arizona, Georgia, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney and fixer who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/13/trump-organization-michael-cohen-legal-bills-judge-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fresh out of house arrest}}}\uc2 , thinks he will not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis fragile ego cannot stand to be considered a two-time loser,\u8221\'20\'1D Cohen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2021/11/22/michael-cohen-trump-2024-election-camerota-intv-sot-vpx.cnn/video/playlists/this-week-in-politics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Trump lost the five states in question by narrow margins \u8211\'20\'13 defeats he refuses to accept, continuing to promote the lie that Biden won thanks to electoral fraud, which led to deadly violence at the US Capitol on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Politico obtained a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=0000017d-49fd-dddc-a77f-4dff81830000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pollster, Tony Fabrizio, which said a poll carried out for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s fundraising committee put him up over Biden in all five states, by margins ranging from three points in Georgia to 12 in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/donald-trump-snapped-im-f-084919566.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent books}}}\uc2  about the Trump administration, Fabrizio is depicted as willing to give Trump polling news he did not want.\par \par \uc2 But he told Politico: \u8220\'20\'1CPoll after poll clearly demonstrates that \u8230\'20\'26 Trump is still the 800lb gorilla in the [Republican party] and would be its 2024 nominee should he run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis new data clearly shows that today the voters in these five key states would be happy to return Trump to the White House and send Biden packing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid speculation, the White House said on Monday Biden, 79, intends to run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 The same day, Cohen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2021/11/22/michael-cohen-trump-2024-election-camerota-intv-sot-vpx.cnn/video/playlists/this-week-in-politics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CDonald will not run. Why? Because first of all, he has an incredibly fragile ego. He lost by 9m votes the first time [ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2020/results/president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 actually}}}\uc2  a little more than 7m]. He will lose by more than 9m the second and his fragile ego cannot stand to be considered a two-time loser.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/michael-cohen-donald-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Cohen says Trump will not run in 2024: \u8216\'20\'18His ego can\u8217\'20\'19t stand to be a two-time loser\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver a speech this afternoon on the US economy and the need to lower prices for American families. The speech comes as inflation has hit a 31-year high, with prices increasing by 6.2% over the past 12 months. That\u8217\'20\'19s the most rapid acceleration since December 1990.\par \par \uc2 * Biden announced he will release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve, in an effort to lower gas prices. The price of gas has increased by 49.6% over the past year, bringing the national average for a gallon of gas to $3.40, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per AAA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration has asked a federal court to lift the stay on a coronavirus vaccination rule for large businesses. The rule, which was set to go into effect on January 4, would require those working for companies with at least 100 employees to get vaccinated or receive weekly coronavirus tests to mitigate the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , a leader of the far-right group Proud Boys, was denied early release from a DC jail after complaining of unsanitary conditions there.\par \par \uc2 Tarrio has served about half of a five-month sentence for illegal acts during a pro-Trump rally in DC last December, during which the Proud Boys leader set fire to a stolen Black Lives Matter banner.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/public-safety/tarrio-proud-boy-dc-jail/2021/11/22/8e097efe-4ba7-11ec-b73b-a00d6e559a6e_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In a written ruling Friday night, D.C. Superior Court Judge Jonathan H. Pittman said he largely believed Tarrio\u8217\'20\'19s allegations, made at a Nov. 15 hearing, about experiencing unsanitary conditions and mistreatment at the jail. The judge noted that the D.C. Department of Corrections \u8216\'20\'18admits that much of what the defendant has claimed did in fact occur.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 But after reviewing Tarrio\u8217\'20\'19s three legal arguments for being let out of jail, Pittman said each argument fell short.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy theorist Alex Jones said he will likely invoke his Fifth Amendment rights against self-incrimination after being subpoenaed by the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 enltrJones says "I'm probably going to declare the 5th, not because of anything wrong, not because of anything wrong but because these people are political criminals that have an axe to grind..."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1463193899049046023?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 On his far-right show, Jones said he would invoke the Fifth Amendment not because of his own potentially illegal deeds but because the committee members are \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical criminals that have an axe to grind,\u8221\'20\'1D per Politico.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/news/press-releases/select-committee-subpoenas-individuals-involved-planning-and-organizing-rallies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the statement}}}\uc2  released by the committee yesterday, investigators are seeking Jones\u8217\'20\'19 testimony about his alleged involvement in the planning of the January 6 rally that culminated in the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In case you missed it yesterday: the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection issued five more subpoenas to right-wing political operatives, including former Trump associate \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  and conspiracy theorist Alex Jones.\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reports:\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas demanding documents and testimony expand the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry focused on the planning and financing of the rally at the Ellipse, by targeting operatives who appear to have had contacts with the Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 House investigators issued subpoenas to the veteran operatives Stone and Jones, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson Taylor Budowich, and the pro-Trump activists Dustin Stockton and his wife, Jennifer Lawrence.\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the select committee, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , said the subpoenas aimed to uncover \u8216\'20\'18who organized, planned, paid for, and received funds related to those events, as well as what communications organizers had with officials in the White House and Congress\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/22/roger-stone-alex-jones-subpoenas-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roger Stone and Alex Jones among five to receive Capitol attack subpoenas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Eric Berger reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 While people are expected to again travel at levels similar to a pre-pandemic Thanksgiving, airlines are still contending with staffing shortages, which could lead to additional flight cancelations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really matter if a travel disruption is coming from a lack of staffing or shortage of routes or weather, it\u8217\'20\'19s still something that is very frustrating for customers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lindsey Roeschke, travel and hospitality analyst for the Morning Consult, a market research firm.\par \par \uc2 In spite of the Covid-19 pandemic, Thanksgiving flight bookings in the United States are up 78% from 2020 and 3.2% from 2019, according to a Adobe Digital Economy Index {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.adobe.com/en/publish/2021/11/11/adobe-digital-economy-index-thanksgiving-flight-bookings-exceeding-2019-levels#gs.glbiab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it is busy, it\u8217\'20\'19s very possible that [flights] will be over capacity \u8211\'20\'13 and that means the possibility of things going wrong is very high,\u8221\'20\'1D said Narendra Khatri, principal of Insubuy, a travel insurance company.\par \par \uc2 Over the Halloween weekend, \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  canceled more than 2,000 flights because of weather and staffing issues.\par \par \uc2 In letters to employees, David Seymour, chief operating officer of the airline, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://context-cdn.washingtonpost.com/notes/prod/default/documents/6b52c9ac-49d2-40b7-9089-a2a57b4b2d51/note/8710eea0-8d49-4090-b03e-b3fcb70ac7be."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  the weekend as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrief irregular ops period\u8221\'20\'1D and said that \u8220\'20\'1Con the schedule front, we\u8217\'20\'19ve ensured that November and December are built to meet customer demand and that they are fully supportable by our staffing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/thanksgiving-travel-airports-staffing-cancelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thanksgiving challenges airlines as US travel nears pre-pandemic levels}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden administration asks court to lift stay on vaccination rule\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has asked a court to immediately lift a stay on a rule requiring employees of large businesses to get vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/health-coronavirus-mandate-lawsuit/u-s-govt-asks-court-to-immediately-lift-stay-on-covid-vaccine-rule-idUSL1N2SE16T"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Delaying the rule by \uc2 the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) \uc2 that requires employees to be vaccinated or tested weekly would lead to thousands of hospitalizations and deaths, the government said in a Tuesday filing with the 6th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals....\par \par \uc2 The rule was challenged by Republican-led states, businesses and trade groups and the U.S. 5th Circuit Court of Appeals in New Orleans quickly blocked it, calling it \u8216\'20\'18staggeringly overbroad\u8217\'20\'19 and a \u8216\'20\'18one-size-fits-all sledgehammer.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 After the stay was imposed by the 5th Circuit, lawsuits from around the country were transferred to the 6th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals in Cincinnati.\par \par \uc2 The rule requires those working at companies with 100 or more employees to get vaccinated or receive weekly coronavirus tests to mitigate the spread of the virus. It was set to go into effect on January 4.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/23/us-government-asks-court-lift-stay-covid-vaccine-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US asks court to immediately lift stay on workplace vaccine rule}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Energy secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  will join the daily White House briefing this afternoon, giving her an opportunity to offer more details on the release of oil from the strategic reserve.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s briefing, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  noted the Biden administration is using a variety of tools to address high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/biden-asks-ftc-redouble-probe-possible-illegal-conduct-by-oil-gas-companies-2021-11-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent a letter}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  asking the agency to investigate \u8220\'20\'1Cmounting evidence of anti- consumer behavior by oil and gas companies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to press oil companies who have made record profits and are overseeing what we consider to be price gouging out there,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said aboard Air Force One yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen there\u8217\'20\'19s a supply of oil or the price of oil is coming down and the price of gas is not coming down, it does not take an economic expert to know that\u8217\'20\'19s a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 campaign arm is using high gas prices to attack Democrats as Americans travel for Thanksgiving, which the country will celebrate on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/meet-the-press/blog/meet-press-blog-latest-news-analysis-data-driving-political-discussion-n988541/ncrd1284337#blogHeader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Americans on the road for Thanksgiving will be reminded of high gas and grocery prices with an ad push from the Republican Senate campaign arm airing at gas stations across the country this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You like high gas prices?\u8217\'20\'19 the ad intones, with cartoonish graphics and sound effects. \u8216\'20\'18If so, introducing: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democrats.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The National Republican Senatorial Committee\u8217\'20\'19s five-figure, multi-day buy \u8212\'20\'14 first reported by NBC News \u8212\'20\'14 goes across ten battleground states where Republicans hope to flip or keep Senate seats in the upcoming 2022 midterms. The advertisements are intended to hit travelers on the road for the Thanksgiving holiday who are filling up their gas tanks.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is currently split 50-50, but Democrats control the chamber because of Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 tie-breaking vote.\par \par \uc2 So Republicans only need to flip one Senate seat in next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections to regain control of the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who have been attacking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over the rising prices of gas and groceries, criticized the release of oil from the strategic reserve as a political ploy.\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement \u8211\'20\'13 which will release just three days\u8217\'20\'19 worth of oil onto the market \u8211\'20\'13 is not about a real solution to our energy crisis. It is a crass political ploy just ahead of Thanksgiving.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  similarly criticized Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThose reserves are meant to be used for serious emergencies, like war, and nothing else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to release 50m barrels of oil from strategic reserve to address high gas prices\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced this morning that his administration will release 50m barrels of oil from the strategic petroleum reserve to help address high gas prices.\par \par \uc2 The president said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that the action \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be taken in parallel with other major energy consuming nations including China, India, Japan, Republic of Korea and the United Kingdom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday I'm announcing action to lower the cost of gas and oil for American families.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Energy will make available releases of 50 million barrels of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve to lower gas and oil prices for Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1463130215295684612?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The news comes as gas prices have increased by 49.6% over the past year, bringing the national average for a gallon of gas to $3.40, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per AAA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we come out of an unprecedented global economic shutdown, oil supply has not kept up with demand, forcing working families and businesses to pay the price,\u8221\'20\'1D energy secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis action underscores the President\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to using the tools available to bring down costs for working families and to continue our economic recovery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more about the announcement here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/23/gas-prices-biden-release-us-oil-barrels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to release 50m barrels of oil in effort to bring down rising US gas prices}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has argued that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $1.75tn social spending package, which passed the House on Friday, will help families struggling with higher prices by lowering the costs of healthcare and childcare.\par \par \uc2 However, there are lingering concerns about how the high rate of inflation may impact the negotiations over the bill in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin, one of the key holdouts in Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 negotiations over the bill, has said he is hearing more from constituents who are concerned about their gas and grocery bills.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy all accounts, the threat posed by record inflation to the American people is not \u8216\'20\'18transitory\u8217\'20\'19 and is instead getting worse,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said earlier this month. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the grocery store to the gas pump, Americans know the inflation tax is real and DC can no longer ignore the economic pain Americans feel every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin has previously expressed concern that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 spending package, known as the Build Back Better Act, could negatively contribute to inflation.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/manchin-pelosi-biden-3-5-trillion-reconciliation-government-spending-debt-deficit-inflation-11630605657"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September op-ed}}}\uc2  for the Wall Street Journal, Manchin warned against approving more government spending, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CAn overheating economy has imposed a costly \u8216\'20\'18inflation tax\u8217\'20\'19 on every middle- and working-class American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, since that op-ed was written, the cost of the package has been cut in half -- from $3.5tn to $1.75tn. And a number of economists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/exclusive-rating-agencies-say-bidens-spending-plans-will-not-add-inflationary-2021-11-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said}}}\uc2  the bill will not add to inflationary pressure.\par \par \uc2 Biden is hoping those arguments will be enough to make Manchin a \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D vote, as he will need all 50 Democratic senators\u8217\'20\'19 support to get the bill through the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/nov/21/democrats-worry-inflation-imperil-legislative-agenda-congressional-majorities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats worry inflation could imperil agenda and congressional majorities}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominees for the \uc2 Federal Reserve board\uc2  have also pledged to tackle inflation aggressively if they are confirmed by the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , who has been nominated to a second term as the chair of the Fed board, said yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that high inflation takes a toll on families, especially those less able to meet the higher costs of essentials, like food, housing and transportation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  speaks as \uc2 Lael Brainard\uc2  listens during an announcement. Photograph: Alex Wong/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Powell, who was first nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , said he would use the tools of the central bank \u8220\'20\'1Cto prevent higher inflation from becoming entrenched\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dr Lael Brainard\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for vice-chair of the board, echoed that message, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m committed to putting working Americans at the center of my work at the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . This means getting inflation down at a time when people are focused on their jobs and how far their paychecks will go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to address lowering prices as inflation hits 31-year high\par \par \uc2 Greetings, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver a speech this afternoon on the state of the US economy and the need to lower prices for American families.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes as inflation has hit a 31-year high, with prices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing by 6.2%}}}\uc2  over the past 12 months. That\u8217\'20\'19s the fastest acceleration since December 1990.\par \par \uc2 And Americans are growing more concerned about high prices as they continue to rise. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://navigatorresearch.org/most-americans-find-link-between-inflation-and-corporate-greed-convincing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll conducted by the progressive firm Navigator Research}}}\uc2  earlier this month, 54% of Americans now say the cost of groceries and gas is a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announces \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  as his nominee for a second term as the Federal Reserve chair. Photograph: Yuri Gripas/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Biden has pledged to tackle the issue, arguing that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $1.75tn social spending package will lower families\u8217\'20\'19 costs for healthcare and childcare.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an event yesterday to announce his nominations for the \uc2 Federal Reserve board\uc2 , Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CBecause so much of the rest of our economy is doing well, because we have created so many new jobs as fast as we have, we\u8217\'20\'19re in a position to attack inflation from a position of strength, not weakness.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But if Americans don\u8217\'20\'19t start to see prices come down soon, it could make it all the more difficult to enact Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 2021-11-23T14:34:58Z 2021-11-24T01:04:33Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/111839f9921d084d3b73e1a435853076c9b388a7/0_288_6000_3600/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/111839f9921d084d3b73e1a435853076c9b388a7/0_288_6000_3600/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Part of the mob outside the US Capitol on 6 January. Louie Gohmert. \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  speaks as \uc2 Lael Brainard\uc2  listens during an announcement. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announces \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  as his nominee for a second term as the Federal Reserve chair.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211123ehbn0025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
