\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 How anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  advocates are pushing local bans, city by small city\b0\par\par\uc2 Audra Jane Heidrichs \par \uc2 1,669 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 November 2021\par 16:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Across Ohio, tactics pioneered in Texas are being deployed in disruptive city council meetings\par \par \uc2 In May of this year, six city council members in Lebanon, Ohio, a city located just north of Cincinnati, voted on an ordinance that would effectively outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 21,000 people that call it home.\par \par \uc2 As in countless council meetings in small cities across the country where mask mandates, teaching about race in schools and access to reproductive healthcare have become politically charged in America\u8217\'20\'19s current climate, the night unfolded in a series of near-Shakespearean acts.\par \par \uc2 On the morning the meeting was scheduled, Krista Wyatt, a former firefighter elected to city council in 2018 and the only member expected to vote against the ordinance, formally resigned. In an accompanying statement, Wyatt wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a core group of people who have hijacked the council to force their personal, political and religious views on the entire citizenship of Lebanon. It is not fair to the citizens and is not the role of a City Council member to be a moral compass.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dozens of people spoke at the meeting later that evening. Some sang, many shared deeply personal experiences of rape or miscarriages and a few even led prayers. Just outside the doors of city hall, pro-choice and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups similarly squared off, shouting at each other and urging passersby to honk in support of one side or the other.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately though, the vote was a resolute 6-0, making Lebanon the 29th city in the nation, and the first city in Ohio, to pass an enforceable ordinance outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within their city limits. As the nation waits for a supreme court ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, pro-choice advocates and activists across the US know first-hand that any upcoming national ruling might be almost irrelevant given what\u8217\'20\'19s already taken place in Ohio and beyond.\par \par \uc2 For the last few months, small municipalities \u8211\'20\'13 many without any standing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://local12.com/news/local/will-more-ohio-cities-follow-in-mason-lebanons-footsteps-to-outlaw-abortion-cincinnati"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvxu.org/local-news/2021-10-25/mason-city-council-bans-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mason}}}\uc2  and soon maybe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2021/10/26/abortion-ban-proposed-london-ohio-outlaw-clinics-and-drugs/8549391002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others}}}\uc2 , have outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Though women in those cities can still travel to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bans send an intimidating message.\par \par \uc2 Bypassing statehouses and targeting smaller towns and cities governed by council has emerged as a successful strategy for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates in recent years. In July, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/07/state-policy-trends-midyear-2021-already-worst-legislative-year-ever-us-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  revealed that at least 30 towns in six states \u8211\'20\'13 Arkansas, Indiana, New Mexico, New York, Ohio and Texas \u8211\'20\'13 have approved municipal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the last three years. Some of these ordinances also target specific \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and organizations providing other types of practical support to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients.\par \par \uc2 Today, pro-choice advocates are preparing for the supreme court to hear arguments in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/case-files/cases/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2 . Scheduled for December, the hearing marks the first time since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  that the court will rule on the constitutionality of a pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and will determine whether all state laws that ban abortions are unconstitutional. If the court were to overturn Roe , the consequences would be felt widely and immediately, as several states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/06/us-abortion-restrictions-laws-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in place that would automatically go into effect and outlaw most or all abortions.\par \par \uc2 Ohio is on the brink of passing its own trigger ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkbn.com/news/ohio/ohio-senate-debates-abortion-trigger-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Bill 123}}}\uc2 , and has recently introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/open/2021/11/ohio-gop-lawmakers-introduce-texas-style-abortion-ban-bill.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Bill 480}}}\uc2 , the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the country, a copycat of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/10/14/texas-abortion-restrictions-appeal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Bill 8}}}\uc2  (SB 8). This would be a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, without exceptions for rape, incest or the safety of those who are pregnant and would also empower private citizens to sue anyone that provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or helps someone access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The tactic of outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by city began in Texas, due mostly to the traveling preacher and director of the non-profit Right to Life of East Texas, Mark Lee Dickson. Since 2019, Dickson has traversed the country encouraging municipalities to pass ordinances outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including laws that defined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as premeditated murder and others that made it illegal for anyone to help someone obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within city limits \u8211\'20\'13 and declare themselves \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary cities for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-us-supreme-court-laws-185e383ba4aa6cfc558231dcabd4104a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 success story}}}\uc2  was Waskom, a city of under 2,000 residents in east Texas, in June 2019. In the year and a half that followed, despite an enduring, evolving pandemic, Dickson did the same in 22 Texas municipalities. Ultimately, SB 8, which banned almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas and landed before Scotus \u8211\'20\'13 which did not intervene \u8211\'20\'13 heeded the Waskom model in terms of how the law is enforced.\par \par \uc2 Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s initiative, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanctuarycitiesfortheunborn.org/sanctuary-cities-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sanctuary Cities for the Unborn}}}\uc2 , has now helped 41 cities \u8211\'20\'13 37 in Texas alone \u8211\'20\'13 create custom-tailored ordinances that outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on the state\u8217\'20\'19s law and the city\u8217\'20\'19s charter. First to follow Texas\u8217\'20\'19s suit were Ohio and Nebraska with two cities respectively. But how?\par \par \uc2 The president of Ohio Right to Life, Mike Gonidakis, has referred to Ohio as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe bedrock of the pro-life movement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Veronica Strevel, a military veteran, social worker and reproductive justice activist in Lebanon, agrees, asserting that Dickson has a pattern when it comes to determining which cities to target for these ordinances.\par \par \uc2 While Dickson has said in more recent interviews that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t approach city leadership, rather they reach out to him for help, this wasn\u8217\'20\'19t always his story. Strevel points to interviews like this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.news-journal.com/news/local/white-oak-native-behind-sanctuary-cities-for-the-unborn-says-movement-just-getting-started/article_3c0f9bc4-aa69-11e9-a2b2-d70f07fafb37.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one}}}\uc2  in 2019, wherein Dickson admits to initiating contact with the mayor of Waskom, as he felt the city was \u8220\'20\'1Cvulnerable\u8221\'20\'1D to pro-choice advocacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t bring these ordinances to a city unless he knows that he has enough people there to support them,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Strevel, who has been actively protesting against anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordinances at city council meetings throughout Ohio. \u8220\'20\'1CDickson and advocates like him aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking for towns that have just a conservative church or a Republican city council. They\u8217\'20\'19re looking for one with an extreme Republican city council and Trump supporters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In October, just five months after the ruling in Lebanon, a second Ohio city {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-religion-ohio-cincinnati-3557d90811680623d4f94acd1adb602f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  the same ordinance. Like Lebanon, Mason \u8211\'20\'13 which is located just 14 minutes away \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bestplaces.net/voting/city/ohio/mason"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known}}}\uc2  as a solidly conservative city. The Mason city council received the ordinance draft from Sanctuary Cities for the Unborn and Dickson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/news/2021/08/08/mason-city-council-may-consider-abortion-ban-like-lebanons/8030764002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  he was in talks with officials in Mason before the Lebanon ordinance was even finalized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people do not think Ohio is as red or as right as Texas, but these anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups just copy and paste policy from statehouse to statehouse and city to city,\u8221\'20\'1D says Jordyn Close, Ohio state coordinator with Urge: Unite for Reproductive and Gender Equity. \u8220\'20\'1CIn city council meetings, the people that are testifying in favor of these bans and unconstitutional bills are not from here. They\u8217\'20\'19re there representing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations, forcing these things on our communities when they\u8217\'20\'19re not always what citizens actually want.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Strevel, who has lived in Lebanon for the last 10 years, says the effects on the community have been palpable.\par \par \uc2 Within two months of the ordinance taking effect, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cincinnati.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2F2021%2F08%2F05%2Fwhat-impact-has-the-abortion-ban-had-on-lebanon-businesses%2F5486339001%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  was conducted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mainstreetlebanon.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Main Street Lebanon}}}\uc2  and led by University of Cincinnati professor Michael Cook. It revealed local businesses were already seeing decreased sales, leaving their owners, who were already struggling with a pandemic, questioning if it was a good thing for the community after all. Lebanon business owners reported sales in June 2021 suffered in comparison with 2020 and 2019.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just a natural side-effect of instituting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Cook {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsrecord.org/opinion/opinion-lebanon-abortion-ban-does-more-harm-than-good/article_a2838d20-0485-11ec-a1b3-07f83c77d98d.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/news/2021/08/05/what-impact-has-the-abortion-ban-had-on-lebanon-businesses/5486339001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cincinnati Enquirer}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen evidence of a formal boycott, but there are people boycotting. And socially, Strevel says dynamics have become so contentious between locals that whisper societies of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  residents are thriving behind closed doors and it\u8217\'20\'19s not uncommon for strangers to find ways to quietly thank her for her outspoken advocacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of my friends spoke at last night\u8217\'20\'19s city council meeting and a sitting councilman told her, \u8216\'20\'18this is a conservative town and you should have done your research before you moved here,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Strevel. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had friends who\u8217\'20\'19ve been followed home from council meetings and many of them won\u8217\'20\'19t go on record. I definitely have felt targeted, not only in Lebanon but also in Mason.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Apart from Ohio, Nebraska has also followed Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s ordinances \u8211\'20\'13 first in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.knopnews2.com/2021/04/08/hayes-center-is-first-nebraska-town-to-make-abortion-illegal-and-punishable-by-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hayes Center}}}\uc2  in April and again just weeks after in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1011now.com/2021/04/15/blue-hill-is-second-nebraska-town-to-outlaw-abortion-in-city-limits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blue Hill}}}\uc2 . Two more cities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.knopnews2.com/2021/11/07/another-nebraska-town-moves-toward-outlawing-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dunning}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newschannelnebraska.com/story/45203202/curtis-considers-outlawing-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Curtis}}}\uc2 , are considering outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for their collective 1,000 population. But Andi Curry Grubb, executive director of Planned Parenthood in Nebraska, is confident those who identify as pro-choice in the state will prevail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think folks are recognizing the threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a new way and the immediacy of an impact to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and access is being understood differently,\u8221\'20\'1D said Grubb. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you combine that with local municipalities trying to bring ordinances like this forward, it just is a bit of a continuation of what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing across the state, which is folks saying, \u8216\'20\'18this is not who we are in Nebraska. This is not what we want.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As for Ohio, in the coming weeks two more city councils \u8211\'20\'13 in Celina and London \u8211\'20\'13will consider similar measures. While many pro-choice advocates and activists remain confident like Grubb, others, such as Strevel, are resigned to the fate of their own city and are instead focusing on others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t go to last night\u8217\'20\'19s council meeting. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing I can do for Lebanon in the next two years. If all I\u8217\'20\'19m going to get is resistance from a now completely white male extremist rightwing council \u8211\'20\'13 because that\u8217\'20\'19s what this city elected \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m not wasting my time on Lebanon. Y\u8217\'20\'19all want that for yourself? Fine. Everybody knows who I am and where to find me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211123ehbn002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
