\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden battles political headwinds as he hits the road to sell his agenda \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Gloria Oladipo and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 7,439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2021\par 01:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president, beset by sagging poll numbers, will visit New Hampshire on the first leg of a tour promoting bipartisan legislationBiden basks in bipartisan triumph \u8211\'20\'13 but is it a new start or a swansong?Mnuchin and Pompeo discussed removing Trump after Capitol attack, book claimsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and leading figures in his administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-619429488f085ed4b8c1a7db#block-619429488f085ed4b8c1a7db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan a flurry}}}\uc2  of further visits, following the president\u8217\'20\'19s trip to New Hampshire today, to promote the benefits of the $1.2tn bipartisan infrastructure legislation signed into law yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * Top US infectious disease expert \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  said that it is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61940c6e8f08d09d4ebd8848#block-61940c6e8f08d09d4ebd8848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conceivable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for the spread of Covid-19 to downgrade to endemic levels rather than a pandemic, but that boosters and continued vaccinations are key.\par \par \uc2 * The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193f3ed8f08d09d4ebd86f8#block-6193f3ed8f08d09d4ebd86f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is confident}}}\uc2  the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s $1.85tn Build Back Better social program and climate action legislation will get voted through by the House before Thanksgiving, and maybe this week, before it goes back to the Senate, where the president also expressed optimism that it can get passed.\par \par \uc2 * California representative Jackie Speier announced that she will not be seeking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600#block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reelection}}}\uc2 , adding to the list of Democrats who will not be running for reelection ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/audio/2021/aug/13/are-the-democrats-doomed-in-2022-politics-weekly-extra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shaky 2022 midterm election cycle.}}}\par \par \uc2 * Dick Durbin, chairman of the Senate judiciary committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193ccb78f086da755c23c50#block-6193ccb78f086da755c23c50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded}}}\uc2  that attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  immediately fire the director of the federal Bureau of Prisons over reports of misconduct involving corrections officers.\par \par \uc2 * The House will vote Wednesday on a resolution to censure \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 , the Arizona Republican congressman who posted an anime video that depicted him attacking the New York Democrat Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez with a sword and threatening \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joanna Walters and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin and Pompeo discussed removing Trump after Capitol attack, book claims\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state and treasury secretary discussed removing him from power after the deadly Capitol attack by invoking the 25th amendment, according to a new book.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitutioncenter.org/interactive-constitution/amendment/amendment-xxv?gclid=Cj0KCQiAys2MBhDOARIsAFf1D1fxB9BWFfaobZjSSSV8C0tl-9itE21xR7qH2so0ux5Htegz1oMEwa0aAvf9EALw_wcB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amendment}}}\uc2 , added to the constitution after the assassination of \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  in 1963, provides for the removal of an incapacitated president, potentially on grounds of mental as well as physical fitness. It has never been used.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/nov/13/betrayal-review-donald-trump-jonathan-karl-capitol-attack-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Betrayal: The Final Act of the Trump Show}}}\uc2 , by the ABC Washington correspondent \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2 , the treasury secretary, \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2 , talked to other cabinet members about using the amendment on the night of 6 January, the day of the attack, and the following day.\par \par \uc2 Removing Trump via the amendment would have required a majority vote in the cabinet. Karl reports that Mnuchin spoke to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pompeo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pompeo}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state and an avowed loyalist.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin did not comment for Karl\u8217\'20\'19s book, which is published on Tuesday. Karl writes that Pompeo responded only after Karl told Trump the former secretary of state had not done so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPompeo through a spokesman denied there have ever been conversations around invoking the 25th amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D Karl writes. \u8220\'20\'1CThe spokesman declined to put his name to the statement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/16/mnuchin-pompeo-trump-25th-amendment-capitol-attack-betrayal-book-jon-karl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mnuchin and Pompeo discussed removing Trump after Capitol attack, book claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll fight like hell\u8217\'20\'19: US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights leader on finding hope in a moment of crisis\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju, president of Naral Pro-Choice America, braces for an era in which the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may no longer exist.\par \par \uc2 Born a month after the landmark 1973 supreme court decision establishing a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mini Timmaraju has never lived in an America without the rights enshrined by the landmark Roe v Wade supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 Now she is helping lead the reproductive rights movement into an uncertain, \u8220\'20\'1Cfrightening\u8221\'20\'1D future where the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may no longer exist.\par \par \uc2 Just days into her new role as president of Naral Pro-Choice America, a conservative supreme court will hear arguments in a case that many advocates fear will be the death knell for Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s frightening times for advocates of reproductive freedom \u8211\'20\'13 for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview. And yet, Timmaraju sees reason for optimism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt can be the bleakest of times and it can be terribly scary,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt can also be an incredible opportunity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the supreme court took up two separate challenges to a Texas law effectively banning abortions in the second most populous state in the nation. But the more direct threat to Roe comes on 1 December, when the court will consider the constitutionality of a Mississippi law that bans abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 about two months earlier than Roe and subsequent decisions allow.\par \par \uc2 These are the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases to be considered by the expanded, 6-3 conservative majority, which includes three appointees of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who had promised to nominate only \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D justices.\par \par \uc2 If Roe were to be overturned, there are 26 states that are \u8220\'20\'1Ccertain or likely\u8221\'20\'1D to ban the procedure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . The list includes nine states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans still on the books from before Roe, and 12 states with so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D laws, which would be enacted if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Scotus in mind and with the midterms at play,\u8221\'20\'1D Timmaraju said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have a real opportunity to wake up a big majority of the electorate that we know supports reproductive freedom and double down and ramp up that work to meet the moment we\u8217\'20\'19re facing right now, this moment of crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/16/mini-timmaraju-abortion-interview-naral-pro-choice-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll fight like hell\u8217\'20\'19: US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights leader on finding hope in a moment of crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House will vote Wednesday on a resolution to censure \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 , the Arizona Republican congressman who posted an anime video that depicted him attacking the New York Democrat Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez with a sword and threatening \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the resolution passes, Gosar would be the only first representative to be censured in more than a decade. Censure resolutions are rare in Congress and require the censured member to stand in the well of the chamber while the resolution is read out loud.\par \par \uc2 Gosar, who sits alongside Ocasio-Cortez on the oversight committee would lose his position if censured.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe video was posted on Representative Gosar\u8217\'20\'19s official \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account and used the resources of the House of Representatives to further violence against elected officials,\u8221\'20\'1D the censure resolution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-117hres789ih/pdf/BILLS-117hres789ih.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reads}}}\uc2 , in part. \u8220\'20\'1CDepictions of violence can foment actual violence and jeopardize the safety of elected officials, as witnessed in this chamber on January 6, 2021.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/09/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-paul-gosar-video-anime-sword"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House decries Republican over video depicting violence against AOC}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18An egregious breach of public trust\u8217\'20\'19: Ohio sues Meta over whistleblower revelations\par \par \uc2 Alexandra Villarreal reports:\par \par \uc2 Filing suit in response to whistleblower allegations which have rocked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/facebook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Facebook}}}\uc2 , the attorney general of Ohio, \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2 , accused the social media company of \u8220\'20\'1Ccreating misery and divisiveness for profit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yost sued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/meta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meta}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as \uc2 Facebook\uc2  was recently renamed \u8211\'20\'13 after revelations from the whistleblower Frances Haugen shocked consumers and sent stock prices tumbling.\par \par \uc2 Filed in the northern district of California, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  suit claims that chief executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  and associates violated federal securities law by knowingly deceiving the public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Facebook\uc2  said it was looking out for our children and weeding out online trolls, but in reality was creating misery and divisiveness for profit,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Media/News-Releases/November-2021/Attorney-General-Yost-Sues-Facebook-for-Securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yost said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not people to \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , we are the product and we are being used against each other out of greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Files/Briefing-Room/News-Releases/Facebook-Initial-Complaint-(Filed).aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 litigation}}}\uc2  comes amid a larger backlash against Zuckerberg and his online empire, after Haugen shared what the suit calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca trove of internal company documents\u8221\'20\'1D showing \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s complicity in the harm its platforms cause.\par \par \uc2 Through Wall Street Journal articles and other reportage, Haugen\u8217\'20\'19s leaks uncovered how little \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership was doing to protect users or even abide by its own rules.\par \par \uc2 The revelations have further eroded trust in the social media behemoth and caused financial repercussions. Between 13 September and 21 October \u8211\'20\'13 as the Wall Street Journal published its expos\u233\'00\'E9s \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stock price declined by $54.08 a share, or over 14%\u8221\'20\'1D, the Ohio lawsuit states.\par \par \uc2 Yost filed the complaint on behalf of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  investors and the \uc2 Ohio Public Employees Retirement System\uc2 , a public pension fund affected by falls in \uc2 Facebook\uc2  shares.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/nov/16/ohio-sues-meta-securities-laws-deceiving-public"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18An egregious breach of public trust\u8217\'20\'19: Ohio sues Meta over whistleblower revelations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The US politics live blog will now hand over from the east coast to the west coast and our colleague in California, Maanvi Singh, will take you through events over the next few hours. So do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Today so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and leading figures in his administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-619429488f085ed4b8c1a7db#block-619429488f085ed4b8c1a7db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan a flurry}}}\uc2  of further visits, following the president\u8217\'20\'19s trip to New Hampshire today, to promote the benefits of the $1.2tr bipartisan infrastructure legislation signed into law yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * Top US infectious disease expert \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  said that it is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61940c6e8f08d09d4ebd8848#block-61940c6e8f08d09d4ebd8848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conceivable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for the spread of Covid-19 to downgrade to endemic levels rather than a pandemic, but that boosters and continued vaccinations are key.\par \par \uc2 * The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193f3ed8f08d09d4ebd86f8#block-6193f3ed8f08d09d4ebd86f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is confident}}}\uc2  the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s $1.85tn Build Back Better social program and climate action legislation will get voted through by the House before Thanksgiving, and maybe this week, before it goes back to the Senate, where the president also expressed optimism that it can get passed.\par \par \uc2 * California representative Jackie Speier announced that she will not be seeking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600#block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reelection}}}\uc2 , adding to the list of Democrats who will not be running for reelection ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/audio/2021/aug/13/are-the-democrats-doomed-in-2022-politics-weekly-extra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shaky 2022 midterm election cycle.}}}\par \par \uc2 * Dick Durbin, chairman of the Senate judiciary committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193ccb78f086da755c23c50#block-6193ccb78f086da755c23c50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded}}}\uc2  that attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  immediately fire the director of the federal Bureau of Prisons over reports of misconduct involving corrections officers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden and leading figures in administration fan out to promote legislation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is wrapping up his visit to New Hampshire and returning to the White House right now. But he intends a further flurry of visits, himself and by some of his top figures this week to, as the White House puts it, communicate the benefits of infrastructure investment and \u8220\'20\'1Chighlight how the president forged consensus to demonstrate how democracies can deliver real results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks to reporters before boarding Air Force One to depart Manchester, New Hampshire, this afternoon. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, Biden will visit Detroit. Interior secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  will visit Barnstable, Massachusetts, on Thursday, San Francisco on Saturday and then head for her native New Mexico on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  intends to travel to Columbus, Ohio, on Friday and on that day labor secretary \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2  will follow in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s footsteps to visit Detroit, while transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  goes to Arizona.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, housing secretary Marcia Fudge goes to Atlanta and on Monday energy secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  will visit Oak Ridge, Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 The White House has been at pains to emphasize the mix of destinations between red and blue states, cities large and small.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Public health officials are warning about a surge in coronavirus cases in several states with one saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe whole midwest is lighting up\u8221\'20\'1D with Covid.\par \par \uc2 Masks at a \uc2 3M\uc2  factory in Maplewood, Minnesota as the pandemic gathered pace last year. Photograph: Nicholas Pfosi/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s rate of new infections has been worst in the nation over the week and is putting a strain on hospitals in the state, the Star Tribune {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/minnesota-has-nation-s-worst-7-day-rate-of-new-covid-19-infections/600116980/?refresh=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports today}}}\uc2 , citing federal statistics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in the middle of a Covid blizzard right now in Minnesota, so that\u8217\'20\'19s a challenge,\u8221\'20\'1D state infectious disease director \uc2 Kris Ehresmann\uc2  has said. The official echoes the country\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious diseases public health expert, \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , in continuing to encourage people to get vaccinated and, for those who are already immunized, getting their booster shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we could get more people vaccinated and if people continue to seek out boosters, that will make a difference,\u8221\'20\'1D Ehresmann said.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota yesterday reported another 5,266 coronavirus infections and a 9.7% positivity rate that brings Minnesota close to its 10% high-risk threshold for widespread viral transmission for the first time since December, the Star Tribune further reports, noting also that unvaccinated people make up the majority of new cases, hospitalizations and deaths.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Michael Osterholm\uc2 , director of the University of Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Infectious Disease Research and Policy has warned that the \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole Midwest is lighting up\u8221\'20\'1D with infection.\par \par \uc2 He also reiterated that vaccination is the key strategy against a winter surge and getting the coronavirus pandemic finally under control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe size of the surge is completely related to vaccine levels,\u8221\'20\'1D Osterholm added.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full Minneapolis Star Tribune report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/minnesota-has-nation-s-worst-7-day-rate-of-new-covid-19-infections/600116980/?refresh=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  asked US regulators today to authorize its experimental treatment pill for Covid-19, an approval that could result in a take-home treatment for coronavirus by this winter, the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pill comes as coronavirus infection rates increase across the country, particularly as colder weather causes more people to stay indoors. In addition to \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 , the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  is currently reviewing an anti-viral pill from Merck, with other smaller drug producers expected to seek approval for their own Covid-19 pills.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are moving as quickly as possible in our effort to get this potential treatment into the hands of patients, and we look forward to working with the \uc2 US FDA\uc2  on its review of our application,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pfizer\u8217\'20\'19s CEO \uc2 Albert Bourla\uc2 , in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  noted earlier this month that their pill cut the rate of hospitalisations and deaths by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/nov/05/pfizer-covid-pills-highly-effective-at-preventing-deaths-trial-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 90% for adults who had early symptoms of Covid-19}}}\uc2 , were unvaccinated and had risk factors including age or co-morbid health factors.\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  also signed a deal with a \uc2 UN\uc2 -backed group to allow drugmakers to produce generic, cheaper versions of the pill for certain countries. Merck, whose anti-viral pill was approved in Britain earlier this month, has a similar deal.\par \par \uc2 The US has approved one other antiviral drug for Covid-19, remdesivir, and authorized three antibody therapies that help the immune system fight the virus, notes the AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fauci says Covid-19 could go into 'endemic' phase by spring 2022 with boosters\par \par \uc2 Top US infectious disease expert \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  said that it is \u8220\'20\'1Cconceivable\u8221\'20\'1D for the spread of Covid-19 to downgrade to endemic levels rather than a pandemic, but that boosters and continued vaccinations are key.\par \par \uc2 A nurse gives a boy a shot of the Pfizer Covid-19 vaccine at a vaccination site for 5-11-year-olds at Eastmonte Park in Altamonte Springs, Florida. Photograph: Paul Hennessy/Sopa Images/Rex/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Fauci spoke about trends in the Covid-19 pandemic, noting that while there is no \u8216\'20\'18magic number\u8217\'20\'19 of daily coronavirus cases to determine when the US is an endemic phase, reaching that stage is possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo me if you want to get endemic, you have got to get the level of infection so low that it does not have an impact on society, on your life, on your economy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fauci in an interview during the Reuters Total Health conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople will still get infected. People might still get hospitalized, but the level would be so low that we don\u8217\'20\'19t think about it all the time and it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t influence what we do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fauci went on to say that if the US makes boosters available to everyone, the virus could be under control by spring 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook what other countries are doing now about adopting a booster campaign virtually for everybody. I think if we do that, and we do it in earnest, I think by the spring we can have pretty good control of this,\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D that his \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D bill will get passed by the House within a week and urged bipartisanship to address US infrastructure needs, including those exacerbated by climate change, during remarks he made today in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Biden also touted that the bill would lower the deficit, pre-empting a potentially negative assessment from the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  about the bill\u8217\'20\'19s cost estimates.\par \par \uc2 During his speech, Biden also highlighted many benefits to his recently passed infrastructure laws, including fixing blighted bridges, road, and other infrastructure across the country, fixing \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D of lead pipes in the country, and providing high-speed internet, a service proved even more essential during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the cynics, Democrats and Republicans, we can work together, we can deliver real results,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe middle class built this country and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been left out,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke in Woodstock, New Hampshire, located two hours outside of New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s capital, and at the Pemigewasset River Bridge, which is in need of major repairs, according to the WMUR, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmur.com/article/joe-biden-woodstock-new-hampshire/38254441#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a local news affiliate.}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden has had low approval ratings in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/581450-biden-job-approval-at-record-low-in-washington-post-abc-news-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar to dismal approval ratings nationwide}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholars.unh.edu/survey_center_polls/673/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent poll }}}\uc2  from 20 October by the UNH Survey Center, only 37% of Democratic primary voters said they would vote for Biden in the 2024 primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  released a statement on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600#block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retirement announcement of long-serving California representative }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600#block-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Jackie Speier. }}}\par \par \uc2 In a press release about Speier\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that she will not be seeking reelection in 2022, Pelosi spoke about Speier\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments and legacy in the House, calling Speier \u8220\'20\'1Can extraordinary Member of Congress and a significant leader in our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHer courageous and values-based leadership, particularly on behalf of the women, survivors and the vulnerable, has made a difference in the lives of countless Americans and has strengthened our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pelosi via the statement.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi also spoke Speier\u8217\'20\'19s role as chair of the military personnel subcommittee of the armed services committee as well as her work to address sexual harassment and assault in the military, college campuses, and in Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHer colleagues in the Congress look forward to continuing to benefit from her leadership for the remainder of her term, and from her legacy for years to come. It has been my personal honor to share representation of San Francisco with her and work with her to save the San Francisco Bay,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 Speier, 71, who has served seven terms as congresswoman for the San Francisco Bay Area, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSpeier/status/1460608717674598404?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1460608717674598404%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2021%2Fnov%2F16%2Fus-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live%3Fpage%3Dwith3Ablock-6193e6218f08d09d4ebd8600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced her retirement in a video message published to Twitter}}}\uc2 , saying that while it was an \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary privilege\u8221\'20\'1D to serve in public office, she was ready to move on.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House downplayed pending, potentially negative CBO scores on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s $1.85tn \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D bill, calling the CBO\u8217\'20\'19s experience into question.\par \par \uc2 In his first gaggle as White House deputy press secretary, Andrew Bates discussed the potential impact cost estimates from the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  could have on the bill being passed, directly challenging the CBO\u8217\'20\'19s expertise, reported Politico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C There has been wide agreement on the part of everyone involved, moderates, liberals, etc, that CBO does not have experience analyzing revenue amounts gained from cracking down on wealthy tax cheats who are taking advantage of every honest taxpayer,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bates.\par \par \uc2 Bates also said that several economists, including former US Treasury secretary and controversial figure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/larry-summers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Summers}}}\uc2 , have said the White House is underestimating the amount of revenue Biden\u8217\'20\'19s spending package could bring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge body of work, \u8221\'20\'1D Bates said, \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom economic experts \u8211\'20\'13 including Republican former Treasury secretaries, \uc2 IRS\uc2  commissioners who have served under presidents of both parties, as well as \uc2 Larry Summers\uc2 , with whom we have sometimes had important differences \u8211\'20\'13 affirming that, if anything, our estimates lowball how much revenue can be brought in by cracking down on rich tax cheats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is something that has been known for months and everyone is on the same page,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Bates.\par \par \uc2 Previously, CBO scores have hampered legislation discussion including drafts of the Obamacare bill. Former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was reportedly so fed up with the budget office that the name was banned in his presence, instead calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cbanana\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is en route to New Hampshire this morning, to North Woodstock, and is due to make remarks on his infrastructure bill and related matters at 2.25pm ET there.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D bill will pass in both House and Senate\par \par \uc2 * California representative Jackie Speier announced that she will not be seeking re-election.\par \par \uc2 * US House Majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  said today that a House vote on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D agenda could happen on Friday\par \par \uc2 * The Chairman of the Senate judiciary committee demanded that Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  immediately fire the director of the federal Bureau of Prisons (BOP) following an investigation by the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy privately urged House Republicans not to punish {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/10/republicans-biden-infrastructure-bill-threatened-punishment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 13 members who voted}}}\uc2  for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193b8a68f086da755c23ada#block-6193b8a68f086da755c23ada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that was signed into law yesterday. }}}\par \par \uc2 During a closed meeting with members, McCarthy and others urged that now was not the time for retaliation against those who supported the bipartisan bill, asking Republicans to remain unified ahead of a House vote on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D plan.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear though if future punishment was still possible, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/11-16-2021/GOP-turmoil/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico. }}}\par \par \uc2 Far-right Republicans, including Colorado congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , had been pushing for those who were key in getting Biden\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure bill passed to face punishment, including having their committee assignments stripped.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks will limit immediate consequences for members who crossed party lines. Following the talk, Freedom Caucus member Representative Ralph Norman of South Carolina called McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8220\'20\'1Cgood message\u8221\'20\'1D but also said that dissenting members should \u8220\'20\'1Caccept some responsibility.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following public admonishment from some fellow Republicans, some members who were among the GOP rank and file who helped the bill pass the House say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/gop-rep-fred-upton-receives-death-threats-after-voting-for-bipartisan-infrastructure-deal/2021/11/09/78fe5ac8-4195-11ec-9ea7-3eb2406a2e24_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they have received death threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reminder: Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  voted for the infrastructure bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/580763-mcconnell-infrastructure-bill-a-godsend-for-home-state-of-kentucky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cgodsend\u8221\'20\'1D for his homestate of Kentucky. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House "confident" Build Back Better bill will pass in both House and Senate\par \par \uc2 In the briefing on Air Force One en route to New Hampshire just now, deputy press secretary Andrew Bates was asked whether the White House was concerned that the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  scoring of the financials on the $1.85tn Build Back Better bill \u8220\'20\'1Cmay not be as favorable as you have projected\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the door of Air Force One today. Photograph: Gemunu Amarasinghe/AP\par \par \uc2 And he was also asked whether moderate Democrats in the Senate can be persuaded to agree to pass the bill.\par \par \uc2 The bill, slimmed down to a $1.85tn price tag from its previous size of more than three trillion, is currently awaiting a vote in the House.\par \par \uc2 As previously mentioned, House leaders are hoping for it to pass this week and certainly before Thanksgiving and the CBO expects to indicate its estimates for the spending bill by Friday.\par \par \uc2 But even if this happens, there is still expected to be conflict in the Senate over the price and content of the bill.\par \par \uc2 Taking the second point first, Bates said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are confident that we are going to obtain 50 votes in the Senate for the Build Back Better Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democrats intend to pass BBB via the reconciliation process, as it is a budgetary item, meaning they need a simple majority in the senate, not the 60-vote majority normally needed to satisfy the filibuster rule.\par \par \uc2 But with the 100-seat Senate split 50-50 Dems and GOP, Biden can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to have even one Democratic senator vote against Build Back Better, which is why moderates Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona, are holding such sway in their opposition to a big price tag and some of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s social spending and climate action elements.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Bates said, essentially, that the CBO\u8217\'20\'19s estimates are not the be all and end all and the Biden administration is supremely satisfied that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is going to be paid for\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will reduce the deficit, that\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line for us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is en route to New Hampshire right now. Air Force One is in the air and deputy press secretary Andrew Bates is gathering now with reporters onboard, for a briefing.\par \par \uc2 Bates just began and we are tuning into the audio-only live stream online and Bates is talking infrastructure and now basketball \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you anything meaty.\par \par \uc2 The US president\u8217\'20\'19s long, virtual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/16/xi-biden-virtual-summit-us-china-conflict-taiwan-hong-kong"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summit last night}}}\uc2  with Chinese president \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  is the first topic that\u8217\'20\'19s come up from reporters.\par \par \uc2 Bates says he has nothing to add to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/16/us-politics-joe-biden-infrastructure-democrats-republicans-live?page=with:block-6193d4068f086da755c23cef#block-6193d4068f086da755c23cef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  this morning in the Washington Post that Biden and his administration plan a diplomatic boycott of the winter Olympics, being held next February in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was not part of their conversation \u8230\'20\'26 it was not part of their discussion\u8221\'20\'1D last night, Bates says.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  makes his way to Air Force One today before departing from Andrews airbase in Maryland for Woodstock, New Hampshire. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Tuning into an AF1 gaggle is intriguing! We just heard a loud rattle and Bates, who is still gaggling \u8211\'20\'13 this is his first such briefing \u8211\'20\'13 had a gaggle giggle and said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the first time I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever landed standing up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We hear the roar of engines going into reverse thrust, as the Boeing 747 slows after landing, and the party has arrived in New Hampshire and is preparing to alight. Just before Bates talked about the expected House and Senate votes on Build Back Better \u8211\'20\'13 catch you in the next post on that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Long-serving Democratic congresswoman Jackie Speier of California to retire\par \par \uc2 California representative Jackie Speier announced that she will not be seeking reelection, adding to the list of Democrats who will not be running for reelection ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/audio/2021/aug/13/are-the-democrats-doomed-in-2022-politics-weekly-extra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shaky 2022 midterm election cycle. }}}\par \par \uc2 Speier, 71, who has served seven terms as congresswoman for the San Francisco Bay Area, announced her retirement in a video message published to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying that while it was an \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary privilege\u8221\'20\'1D to serve in public office, she is ready to move on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for me to come home,\u8221\'20\'1D Speier said. \u8220\'20\'1CTime for me to be more than a weekend wife, mother and friend.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nEr9AnqN7A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nEr9AnqN7A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jackie Speier (@RepSpeier) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSpeier/status/1460608717674598404?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Speier noted that she was motivated to serve in public office after accompanying Representative Leo J. Ryan of California to Guyana in 1978 during an attempt to rescue 900 followers of the cult leader Jim Jones.\par \par \uc2 The trip ended in massacre, with Ryan and four others killed and Speier herself shot five times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI vowed that if I survived, I would dedicate my life to public service. I lived and I served,\u8221\'20\'1D said Speier during her retirement announcement.\par \par \uc2 Speier is one of 14 Democratic representatives who have said they will not seek re-election in 2022. While many have cited reasons such as spending more time with family or allowing others to serve in public office, the growing list of retirees, in addition to the more expected, is a sign of Democrats losing representation in Congress and potentially becoming the minority party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US House Majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  has been speaking with reporters about the latest development concerning the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2 , a $1.85tn, 10-year, social spending package.\par \par \uc2 Hoyer noted to reporters that debate on the bill should be happening tomorrow, with a House vote expected on either Friday or Saturday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/11-16-2021/vote-timing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports Politico. }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get it done this week,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hoyer, with House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  telling House representatives that the Congress will not go on Thanksgiving break, as Thanksgiving is next Thursday, until the House passes the bill.\par \par \uc2 enltrSteny Hoyer is sharing the confidence of other Democrats that they\u8217\'20\'19ll pass the Build Back Better bill this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get it done this week.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aED6maDtyI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aED6maDtyI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anthony Adragna (@AnthonyAdragna) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnthonyAdragna/status/1460646255621726219?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  released a statement saying that it would provide cost estimates for sections of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/11-15-2021/rip-fridays/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D agenda by Friday}}}\uc2 . The stalled cost estimates are an upset for moderate Democrats who want the estimates before voting, increasing the chances of a weekend vote. The cost estimates that will be published by Friday include:\par \par \uc2 * Education and Labor\par \par \uc2 * Energy and Commerce\par \par \uc2 * Judiciary\par \par \uc2 * Natural Resources\par \par \uc2 * Ways and Means\par \par \uc2 If the House passes the bill, the plan will advance to the Senate where it currently faces united Republican opposition and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/09/stop-calling-joe-manchin-moderate-greedy-reactionary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 difficulty amid moderate Democrats. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Majority Leader says "Build Back Better" House vote could happen by Friday\par \par \uc2 US House Majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  said today that a House vote on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CBuild Back Better\u8221\'20\'1D agenda could happen on Friday, though acknowledged the vote could be pushed to the weekend instead, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy expectation is that we will vote on this Thursday or Friday,\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer told reporters.\par \par \uc2 More details to follow.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will soon announce a diplomatic boycott of the Beijing Winter Olympics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/11/16/beijing-olympics-2022-biden-partial-boycott/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the Washington Post reports}}}\par \par \uc2 Exiled Tibetans use the Olympic Rings as a prop as they hold a street protest against the holding of 2022 Winter Olympics in Beijing in Dharmsala, India. Photograph: Ashwini Bhatia/AP\par \par \uc2 Citing multiple sources familiar with the planned boycott, the Post wrote that while the decision has not been finalized, the White House is expected to announce that neither Biden nor any \uc2 US government\uc2  official will attend the games, with Biden expected to approve the plan before the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 The timing of this process was not linked to the Biden-Xi virtual meeting Monday evening, which was billed as a way for the two leaders to demonstrate their ability to manage complex U.S.-China relations in an era of rising tensions. Various reports this week have said that \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  intended to bring up the Olympics issue with Biden, perhaps even inviting him to personally attend. But the issue didn\u8217\'20\'19t come up at all during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2021/11/15/world/biden-xi-summit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3\u189\'00\'BD-hour meeting}}}\uc2 , according to initial reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden raised concerns about the [People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China\u8217\'20\'19s] practices in Xinjiang, Tibet, and Hong Kong, as well as human rights more broadly,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/11/16/readout-of-president-bidens-virtual-meeting-with-president-xi-jinping-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House readout}}}\uc2  of the Biden-Xi meeting stated.\par \par \uc2 Biden administration officials have been virtually silent on Olympics-related issues in recent months, refusing to speculate on whether Biden would support a full athlete boycott (as human rights groups and activists are calling for), or a more limited boycott, or no boycott at all. Now that the Biden-Xi virtual summit is complete, sources said, the administration has one less reason to hold off on announcing the diplomatic boycott. The administration will inform allies but leave them to make their own decisions on whether to follow the U.S. lead...\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/www.speaker.gov/newsroom/51821-5__;!!M9LbjjnYNg9jBDflsQ!RyOgxyyU-sCe2J8GcHVs6QoZSpUkFUpYwd_Mq8MdeO5dNBKO04BHrEB_qNMZf_NjlA$"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a May hearing}}}\uc2 , House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D-Calif.) called for a U.S. diplomatic boycott of the Beijing Olympics as a way to express international concern about China\u8217\'20\'19s human rights abuses without punishing U.S. athletes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat moral authority do you have to speak again about human rights any place in the world if you\u8217\'20\'19re willing to pay your respects to the Chinese government as they commit genocide?\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, honor your athletes at home. Let\u8217\'20\'19s have a diplomatic boycott. \u8230\'20\'26 Silence on this issue is unacceptable. It enables China\u8217\'20\'19s abuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Officials from China have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/nancy-pelosi-calls-for-us-diplomatic-boycott-of-beijing-winter-olympics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vehemently denied allegations of human rights abuse}}}\uc2 , citing the US\u8217\'20\'19s own track record of human rights issues including \u8220\'20\'1Cthe continuing spread of xenophobia, white supremacy and discrimination against people of African and Asian descent and Islamophobia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/vincent-ni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vincent Ni}}}\uc2  wrote on the pushback from officials in China following Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s call for a boycott:\par \par \uc2 China has labelled the US House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cfull of lies and disinformation\u8221\'20\'1D after her calls for a diplomatic boycott of next year\u8217\'20\'19s Beijing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/winter-olympics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Winter Olympics}}}\uc2  and Paralympics on human rights grounds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome US individuals\u8217\'20\'19 remarks are full of lies and disinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D a foreign ministry spokesperson, \uc2 Zhao Lijian\uc2 , said on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CUS politicians should stop using the Olympic movement to play despicable political games\u8221\'20\'1D or using \u8220\'20\'1Cthe so-called human rights issue as a pretext to smear and slander China\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/11/16/beijing-olympics-2022-biden-partial-boycott/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full Post report here (paywall). }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/nancy-pelosi-calls-for-us-diplomatic-boycott-of-beijing-winter-olympics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the Guardian report here. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Demands for AG to fire director of Federal Bureau of Prisons following investigation\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the Senate judiciary committee demanded that Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  immediately fire the director of the federal Bureau of Prisons (BOP) following an investigation by the Associated Press detailing ongoing, unchecked misconduct involving correctional officers.\par \par \uc2 Senator Dick Durbin of Illinois, who chairs the committee, called on Garland to dismiss BOP\u8217\'20\'19s director Michael Carvajal who has led the organization during a series of ongoing crises including the unmitigated spread of Covid-19 in prisons as well as dozens of escapes \u8211\'20\'13 at least 36 within the last 22 months, deaths and chronic understaffing that has limited critical emergency responses.\par \par \uc2 AP\u8217\'20\'19s investigation published two days ago also found that over 100 BOP employees had been arrested, convicted or sentenced for crimes since the start of 2019 and that the agency failed to address allegations of misconduct or suspend employees that had been arrested for crimes, including one official at a prison in Mississippi who remained in his position despite being arrested on charges of stalking and harassing fellow employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear that there is much going wrong in our federal prisons, and we urgently need to fix it. That effort must start with new leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Senate judiciary committee in a statement posted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryDems/status/1460613333967593476"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 , also calling the BOP a \u8220\'20\'1Chotbed of abuse, graft and corruption.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Following an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AP}}}\uc2  investigation which found that the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Prisons\uc2  is a "hotbed of abuse, graft and corruption" that "turned a blind eye to employees accused of misconduct," Senate Judiciary Chair Durbin calls on AG Garland to dismiss BOP Director Carvajal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qyrnnoFArB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qyrnnoFArB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  (@JudiciaryDems) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryDems/status/1460613333967593476?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Durbin also noted the need for new leadership in an ongoing attempt by some Democrats to reform America\u8217\'20\'19s criminal justice system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a new Administration and a new opportunity to reform our criminal justice system. It\u8217\'20\'19s clear that there is much going wrong in our federal prisons, and we urgently need to fix it. That effort must start with new leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted Durbin.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have a new Administration and a new opportunity to reform our criminal justice system. It\u8217\'20\'19s clear that there is much going wrong in our federal prisons, and we urgently need to fix it. That effort must start with new leadership. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PPFuHYb1fm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PPFuHYb1fm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Dick Durbin (@SenatorDurbin)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1460614128180117522?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Carvajal had been appointed to his position by then-Attorney General \uc2 William Barr\uc2 , one of the few holdovers from the Trump administration. Deputy Attorney General Lisa Monaco also said that she had confidence in Carvajal despite continued issues during his leadership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/24/democrats-republicans-inflation-rising-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Despite inflation increasing the price of goods nationwide}}}\uc2 , Americans have increased their spending in the last month at retail stores and online, providing gains to the US economy.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, the \uc2 US Commerce Department\uc2  reported on Tuesday that retails sales increased by 1.7% since September, the biggest spending gain since March:\par \par \uc2 Solid hiring, strong pay raises, and healthy savings for many households are underpinning robust spending.\par \par \uc2 Americans are also still buying more cars, furniture, and other goods than they did before the pandemic, which is overwhelming U.S. ports and shipping firms and pushing up prices. The solid spending last month suggests the holiday shopping season is off to a strong start.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s retail sales figures aren\u8217\'20\'19t adjusted for inflation, which rose 0.9% in October, the government said last Wednesday. In some categories, such as gas station sales, which rose 3.9% in October, a jump in gas prices accounted for nearly all the gain...\par \par \uc2 Businesses and other employers are rapidly increasing pay to fill a near-record number of open jobs. Wages and salaries jumped in the July-September quarter, compared with a year earlier, by the most in 20 years. That\u8217\'20\'19s giving more Americans extra money to spend.\par \par \uc2 Yet inflation has eroded those gains for most Americans. Prices jumped 6.2% in October from a year earlier, the government said, Wednesday the most in 31 years.\par \par \uc2 Read the full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-economy-prices-retail-sales-85c933a1ca63498c68111af4b59a006b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top experts warn that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/14/biden-approval-ratings-plunge-inflation-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  inflation surge widely felt nationwide }}}\uc2  will get worse this winter before it gets better.\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1Cnow hiring\u8221\'20\'1D sign is seen at a Kost Tire and Auto center in Bloomsburg, Pennsylvania. Photograph: Paul Weaver/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Addressing clients via a report titled \u8220\'20\'1C2022 U.S. Economic Outlook,\u8221\'20\'1D Goldman Sachs Global Investment Research spoke to current US inflation trends, saying that, \u8220\'20\'1CThe current inflation surge will get worse this winter before it gets better,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-179ae4db-38d6-4843-94a5-59b6c043b9fa.html?chunk=2&utm_term=emshare#story2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Axios.}}}\par \par \uc2 Researches from \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  though also noted that they expect the economy to \u8220\'20\'1Creaccelerate to a 4%+ growth pace over the next few quarters,\u8221\'20\'1D noting that the economy will likely approve as the service sector continues opening, consumers increase their spending, and inventory stocking increases.\par \par \uc2 Experts also expect unemployment rates to fall from 4.6% recorded in October to 3.7% by mid-2022 and 3.5% by the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A new poll has Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings at a record low, showing increasing frustration from Democrats and independents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/581450-biden-job-approval-at-record-low-in-washington-post-abc-news-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports the Hill. }}}\par \par \uc2 A volunteer loads food into a car at an Armed Services YMCA food distribution in San Diego. Photograph: Gregory Bull/AP\par \par \uc2 A weekend survey conducted by The Washington Post and ABC News put Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rate at a dismal 41%, a slight drop from 44% recorded in September. The poll also f0und that 53% of people disapprove of the way that Biden is handeling his job with 6% having no opinion.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/14/biden-approval-ratings-plunge-inflation-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is specifically dropping }}}\uc2  among Democrats and Independents. Only 80% of Democrats surveyed said they approved of the job Biden was doing compared to 94% in September. Similarly, among independents, only 35% said they approved of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance while 58% said they disapprove.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poll numbers could be indicative of much-felt frustration by many Americans over economic hardships, including increasing prices for goods and inflations, as well as the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 In better news, the recent poll did demonstrate that the majority of Americans support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the recently passed infrastructure bill,}}}\uc2  with 63% of those surveyed saying they approved of the government \u8220\'20\'1Cspending one trillion dollars on roads, bridges and other infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D and 58% saying they supported the government \u8220\'20\'1Cspending about two trillion dollars to address climate change and to create or expand preschool, health care and other social programs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be making a trip to New Hampshire today to speak on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.2tn infrastructure bill that was signed into law yesterday. }}}\par \par \uc2 The president will be traveling to Woodstock, New Hampshire, located two hours outside of New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s capital, and speaking at the Pemigewasset River Bridge, which is in need of major repairs, according to the WMUR, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmur.com/article/joe-biden-woodstock-new-hampshire/38254441#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a local news affiliate. }}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech will primarily focus on how the newly passed infrastructure bill will benefit rural communities such as Woodstock, as town officials have spent nearly $250,000 across the past decade doing temporary repairs on the bridge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a great compliment to the Granite State that this is the first stop he\u8217\'20\'19s making after signing the infrastructure bill,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic state representative Steve Shurtleff, who also said that the money New Hampshire will receive from the bill is very needed.\par \par \uc2 Biden has had low approval ratings in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/581450-biden-job-approval-at-record-low-in-washington-post-abc-news-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar to dismal approval ratings nationwide}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholars.unh.edu/survey_center_polls/673/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent poll }}}\uc2  from 20 October by the UNH Survey Center, only 37% of Democratic primary voters said they would vote for Biden in the 2024 primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden sets off to sell big win on infrastructure bill but polls, inflation, divisions make tough hurdles\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading to the regions today to sell his legislative agenda, fresh from signing the $1.2tn bipartisan infrastructure deal yesterday in Washington. So please stay tuned for a lively day.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s afoot:\par \par \uc2 * The US president is heading to New Hampshire this morning, to North Woodstock, and is due to make remarks on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/16/america-is-moving-again-joe-biden-signs-hard-fought-1tn-infrastructure-deal-into-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infrastructure bil}}}\uc2  l and related matters at 2.25pm ET there.\par \par \uc2 * Deputy press secretar y Andrew Bates will \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D with the media aboard Air Force One today after the expected departure at 11.15 of the presidential party from the White House.\par \par \uc2 * But Biden is pushing forward against strong headwinds. The latest ABC/Washington Post poll has him at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/581450-biden-job-approval-at-record-low-in-washington-post-abc-news-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record low}}}\uc2  approval rating, especially because of frustration from Democrats and independents.\par \par \uc2 * Inflation is set to keep going this winter, a new report yesterday from \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  concluded, and this is always a big worry for any president as they are limited in their ability to control it.\par \par \uc2 * Homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas testifies before the Senate judiciary committee this morning on the US-Mexico border situation and immigration policy in general.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 2021-11-16T14:01:55Z 2021-11-17T01:48:11Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/5183cbd16f3bc64bf017e8766e45593bb811cc21/0_341_5414_3250/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/5183cbd16f3bc64bf017e8766e45593bb811cc21/0_341_5414_3250/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks on infrastructure at the NH 175 bridge over the Pemigewasset River in Woodstock, New Hampshire. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks to reporters before boarding Air Force One to depart Manchester, New Hampshire, this afternoon. Masks at a \uc2 3M\uc2  factory in Maplewood, Minnesota as the pandemic gathered pace last year. A nurse gives a boy a shot of the Pfizer Covid-19 vaccine at a vaccination site for 5-11-year-olds at Eastmonte Park in Altamonte Springs, Florida. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the door of Air Force One today. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  makes his way to Air Force One today before departing from Andrews airbase in Maryland for Woodstock, New Hampshire. Exiled Tibetans use the Olympic Rings as a prop as they hold a street protest against the holding of 2022 Winter Olympics in Beijing in Dharmsala, India. A \u8220\'20\'1Cnow hiring\u8221\'20\'1D sign is seen at a Kost Tire and Auto center in Bloomsburg, Pennsylvania. A volunteer loads food into a car at an Armed Services YMCA food distribution in San Diego.\par \par 