\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll fight like hell\u8217\'20\'19: US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights leader on finding hope in a moment of crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,035 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2021\par 14:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju, president of Naral Pro-Choice America, braces for an era in which the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may no longer exist\par \par \uc2 Born a month after the landmark 1973 supreme court decision establishing a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mini Timmaraju has never lived in an America without the rights enshrined by the landmark Roe v Wade supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 Now she is helping lead the reproductive rights movement into an uncertain, \u8220\'20\'1Cfrightening\u8221\'20\'1D future where the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may no longer exist.\par \par \uc2 Just days into her new role as president of Naral Pro-Choice America, a conservative supreme court will hear arguments in a case that many advocates fear will be the death knell for Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s frightening times for advocates of reproductive freedom \u8211\'20\'13 for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview. And yet, Timmaraju sees reason for optimism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt can be the bleakest of times and it can be terribly scary,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt can also be an incredible opportunity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the supreme court took up two separate challenges to a Texas law effectively banning abortions in the second most populous state in the nation. But the more direct threat to Roe comes on 1 December, when the court will consider the constitutionality of a Mississippi law that bans abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 about two months earlier than Roe and subsequent decisions allow.\par \par \uc2 These are the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases to be considered by the expanded, 6-3 conservative majority, which includes three appointees of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who had promised to nominate only \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D justices.\par \par \uc2 If Roe were to be overturned, there are 26 states that are \u8220\'20\'1Ccertain or likely\u8221\'20\'1D to ban the procedure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . The list includes nine states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans still on the books from before Roe, and 12 states with so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D laws, which would be enacted if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Scotus in mind and with the midterms at play,\u8221\'20\'1D Timmaraju said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have a real opportunity to wake up a big majority of the electorate that we know supports reproductive freedom and double down and ramp up that work to meet the moment we\u8217\'20\'19re facing right now, this moment of crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Timmaraju, the daughter of immigrants from India, is the first woman of color to lead the organization, which is one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s oldest and most powerful \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy groups.\par \par \uc2 Most recently, she worked as a senior adviser for the Biden administration on diversity, equity, inclusion and accessibility. In 2016, she led efforts to mobilize female voters as a director for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign. She also led diversity efforts at \uc2 Comcast Corporation\uc2 , held leadership roles with Planned Parenthood and served as the national director of the National Council of Asian Pacific Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like I\u8217\'20\'19ve been at the intersection of race and gender my whole career,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Timmaraju said it was time to \u8220\'20\'1Craise the alarm\u8221\'20\'1D on the \u8220\'20\'1Cvery organized, concerted effort by the extremist right to whittle away at reproductive rights since the minute Roe became law of the land\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Exposing these tactics, she believes, will help energize voters, especially those who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights but may not have realized the extent to which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is under threat, particularly at the state and local level.\par \par \uc2 At the federal level, she called for the immediate passage of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/3755/text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act}}}\uc2 , which would effectively codify Roe and counter state-level restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The House passed the bill in September, but it faces daunting odds in the Senate, where a Republican filibuster awaits.\par \par \uc2 Naral has been outspoken in calling on Democrats to eliminate the filibuster, which requires 60 votes to pass most legislation.\par \par \uc2 Yet it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear the legislation would pass with just a simple majority, as two Democratic senators, Joe Manchin and Bob Casey, have not yet signed on to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/1975/cosponsors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate version of the bill}}}\uc2 . Nor have the two pro-choice Republican senators, Lisa Murkowski and \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, Chuck Schumer, the Senate majority leader, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democrats.senate.gov/dsoc/press-releases/schumer-murray-blumenthal-durbin-joint-statement-on-house-passage-of-the-womens-health-protection-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised}}}\uc2  to bring the measure to the floor for a vote \u8211\'20\'13 a sign, Democrats believe, that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a potent issue in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 In her new role, Timmaraju hopes to build on the solidarity between progressive organizations, leveraging their collective power to resist the tide of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and voting rights restrictions, while fighting for LGBTQ rights and climate justice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know there\u8217\'20\'19s a throughline of white supremacy throughout,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not new playbooks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, she said that overturning Roe would have a disproportionate impact on people of color, low-income people and people who live in rural areas, all of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/women-color-will-lose-roe-v-wade-overturned/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already}}}\uc2  experience higher barriers to accessing reproductive and maternal health services.\par \par \uc2 Despite the myriad political and legal setbacks, she said the reproductive rights movement has made critical gains.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer a \u8220\'20\'1Ctaboo\u8221\'20\'1D topic, Timmaraju said, crediting the decades of work by activists and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/30/congresswomen-personal-abortion-stories-cori-bush-barbara-lee-pramila-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new generation of female lawmakers }}}\uc2  who have publicly shared the story of their decision to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to not be afraid of talking about it. When we become afraid or we get, you know, uncomfortable with it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s when we give all this opportunity for our opponents to push and spread misinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Timmaraju said pro-choice advocates must be prepared to forcefully counter attempts by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to portray the fall of Roe as \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable\u8221\'20\'1D, by pointing to medical advances or the availability of birth control, for example.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re going to downplay it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be very ready to say, absolutely not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the nation awaits a ruling from the supreme court next year, Timmaraju\u8217\'20\'19s message to the movement is to keep the faith.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe may have some short-term losses \u8211\'20\'13 and we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna fight like hell to avoid them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we also have some really significant long-term gains, the seeds [of which] are being planted now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211116ehbg001ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
