\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Catastrophic implications\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 UN\uc2  health expert condemns US over threat to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 994 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2021\par 17:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Special rapporteur Dr Tlaleng Mofokeng argues in brief filed in a US court that overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would violate international human rights treaties ratified by the US\par \par \uc2 The United Nations special rapporteur on the right to health has called on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to uphold the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America or risk undermining international human rights law and threatening that right elsewhere in the world.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/issues/health/pages/srrighthealthindex.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special rapporteur}}}\uc2 , Dr Tlaleng Mofokeng, is one of just a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2017/dec/15/america-extreme-poverty-un-special-rapporteur"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handful of global observers}}}\uc2  whose mandate is to travel the world defending human rights.\par \par \uc2 Mofokeng has argued in a brief filed in a US court that overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would violate international human rights treaties ratified by the US, including the convention against torture, should women be forced to carry pregnancies to term.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Mofokeng told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  she could have filed a brief on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, \u8220\'20\'1Cin any other court, in any other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case,\u8221\'20\'1D globally. However, she chose the US courts because of the direct threat posed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming session.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have this joke among us that when the US sneezes the rest of the world catches a [cold],\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng. \u8220\'20\'1CSo we know that politically that what happens in the United States\u8230\'20\'26 does have an impact in precedents elsewhere in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/193045/20210920163400578_19-1392%20bsac%20United%20Nations%20Mandate%20Holders.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mofokeng\u8217\'20\'19s brief}}}\uc2  was filed ahead of oral arguments in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a case advocates fear}}}\uc2  will undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally. Dobbs poses a direct threat to Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 case that established a Constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  based in privacy.\par \par \uc2 Roe invalidated dozens of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions, and allowed people to terminate a pregnancy up to the point a fetus can survive outside the womb, generally understood to be about 24 weeks gestation. A full term pregnancy is 39 weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that gets overturned, it has catastrophic implications, not just for the US,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng, who said she feared overturning Roe would embolden global attacks on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Mofokeng is also a practicing doctor and well-known sex-positive author in South Africa. Most often, she goes by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08TZM3QN9/ref=dp-kindle-redirect?_encoding=UTF8&btkr=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDr T\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , an informal title which underscores the empathy in her academic analysis. Her most recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documents-dds-ny.un.org/doc/UNDOC/GEN/N21/195/83/PDF/N2119583.pdf?OpenElement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN report}}}\uc2  outlined the challenges Covid-19 posed to reproductive rights, and how colonialism continues to affect global policies on reproduction, from sterilization to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 We know that politically what happens in the United States \u8230\'20\'26 does have an impact in precedents elsewhere in the world\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt means that even those people who are conservative, who are anti-rights, in any country in the world, will actually now start referencing the US court as an example of jurisprudence that should be followed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is why this is so dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Dobbs, the court will consider whether Mississippi can ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks gestation. For the court to uphold Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law, it would require the court to rewrite standards that determine whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are constitutional. Advocates fear that could once again allow states to severely restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A majority of the court\u8217\'20\'19s nine justices would need to agree to rewrite such standards. Conservative justices hold a 6-3 supermajority on the court. Many observers view the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to take the Mississippi case as an ominous sign. About six in 10 Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/05/06/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all or most cases}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Roe \u8230\'20\'26 [were] overturned, many US states will implement bans or near-bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access that will make individual state laws irreconcilable with international human rights law,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/193045/20210920163400578_19-1392%20bsac%20United%20Nations%20Mandate%20Holders.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the brief argued}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis would cause irreparable harm to women and girls in violation of the United States\u8217\'20\'19 obligations under the human rights treaties it has signed and ratified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the US has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/blog/human-rights/treaty-ratification/theres-only-one-country-hasnt-ratified-convention-childrens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not ratified}}}\uc2  several United Nations treaties, it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tbinternet.ohchr.org/_layouts/15/TreatyBodyExternal/Treaty.aspx?CountryID=187&Lang=EN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ratified the convention against torture}}}\uc2 , which Mofokeng\u8217\'20\'19s brief argued would be violated if states were allowed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe denial of safe abortions and subjecting women and girls to humiliating and judgmental attitudes in such contexts of extreme vulnerability and where timely health care is essential amount to torture or ill treatment,\u8221\'20\'1D Mofokeng\u8217\'20\'19s brief said, citing a 2016 report by the rapporteur on torture and other cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment or punishment.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, Mofokeng\u8217\'20\'19s brief argued, contrary to Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s assertions, that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right to life emanating from human rights treaties does not apply prenatally,\u8221\'20\'1D and that the \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelming trend for the past half-century has been toward the liberalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws worldwide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Further, since the court has accepted the Dobbs case, it also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed a six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  to go into effect in Texas in September, effectively allowing the nation\u8217\'20\'19s second largest state to nullify Roe within its borders. Experts estimate that if Roe were overturned, roughly two dozen US states mostly in the south and midwest would immediately ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such bans would have immediate and direct consequences for women and people seeking abortions.\par \par \uc2 In one recent analysis, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2  found 26 states are certain or likely to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should Roe be overturned. In just one example, that would require a woman seeking a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Louisiana to travel to Kansas to access care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rise in global anti-gender and anti-women\u8217\'20\'19s rights is such that people will grasp at anything that seems to make their case solid,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng. And, she said, the case before the supreme court now relies on \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-medical, non-scientific\u8221\'20\'1D misinformation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt means we have a risk of now having global jurisprudence \u8211\'20\'13 or at least influences in the global world \u8211\'20\'13 using jurisprudence that\u8217\'20\'19s ill-informed. And that\u8217\'20\'19s very dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mofokeng. \u8220\'20\'1CTo undo the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions takes decades, sometimes a lifetime \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211108ehb80018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
