\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Trevor Noah on Virginia election: \u8216\'20\'18A Kim Kardashian going from Kanye to Pete Davidson level swing\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Adrian Horton \par \uc2 1,030 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2021\par 15:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts unpack a disappointing election night for Democrats and a big supreme court term for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Trevor Noah\par \par \uc2 Trevor Noah unpacked the closely watched governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in Virginia, where voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/02/glenn-youngkin-wins-virginia-governor-election-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected}}}\uc2  a Republican, Glenn Youngkin, in a state Biden won by 10 points just a year prior. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a huge swing, people,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Daily Show host on Wednesday evening. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s like a Kim Kardashian going from Kanye to Pete Davidson level swing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Why did Democrats do so badly in Virginia last night? It depends who you ask. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WS5JgRoMGy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WS5JgRoMGy}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1456081453972955136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Virginia gubernatorial election, in which Youngkin beat incumbent \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  by over two points, could be a \u8220\'20\'1Cbellwether of the things to come in the midterms next year\u8221\'20\'1D, Noah explained, \u8220\'20\'1Cin the same way your girlfriend saying \u8216\'20\'18that guy\u8217\'20\'19s cute!\u8217\'20\'19 is a bellwether that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be single soon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Why did Democrats perform so poorly in Virginia? \u8220\'20\'1CIt depends on who you ask,\u8221\'20\'1D said Noah before a series of pundit clips positing a variety of reasons, from dissatisfaction with progressive policy ideas to the weaponization of critical race theory to the absence of a single loathed figure in Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be bad enough if Democrats had one reason they lost. But they have like 50,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean it\u8217\'20\'19s Biden\u8217\'20\'19s unpopularity, it\u8217\'20\'19s worries about the economy, it\u8217\'20\'19s the fact that the pandemic is still hanging around like the Tootsie Rolls three weeks after Halloween.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats kept trying to fire up their base by making this race about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing: Trump wasn\u8217\'20\'19t running,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CHonestly, Democrats, you should enjoy this break from Trump while you can! Because after he wins in 2024, and declares himself emperor, you\u8217\'20\'19ll be running against him forever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stephen Colbert\par \par \uc2 On the Late Show, Stephen Colbert also processed a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointing night\u8221\'20\'1D for Democrats, though the party is \u8220\'20\'1Cused to being disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D, he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why they\u8217\'20\'19re changing their logo from the donkey to Eeyore.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, and maybe I\u8217\'20\'19m alone, but I\u8217\'20\'19m not that upset,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve already endured the worst election in American history live on TV sitting over there drinking a cocktail of bourbon and my own tears. This one just seems like another election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Virginia, he noted, has a long tradition of electing a governor in off-cycle elections from the opposite party of the president, as has been the case in 10 of the last 11 elections. People tend to vote when they are dissatisfied with the people in power, Colbert explained, since \u8220\'20\'1Cvoting is like democracy\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Yelp\uc2  review. You never leave a comment when the soup was tasty, but if you bring me still water when I asked for sparkling, I will burn your bistro to the ground.\par \par \uc2 Seth Meyers\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s flip to the Republican governor is \u8220\'20\'1Cjust kinda how American public opinion works\u8221\'20\'1D, said Seth Meyers on Late Night. \u8220\'20\'1CIt waffles back and forth like your mom deciding between chicken or fish at a restaurant. You know as soon as the waiter takes your order and walks away she\u8217\'20\'19s gonna turn to the rest of the table and say, \u8216\'20\'18I think I should\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten the fish.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile this is true that this has happened before, and that public opinion is cyclical, the Democrats know how badly they got their asses kicked last night,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Meyers decried the blame game directed at progressive members of the party, such as a Politico reporter tweeting \u8220\'20\'1CDem members are already texting me blaming progressives for \u8216\'20\'18debacle\u8217\'20\'19 in Virginia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, are you insane?\u8221\'20\'1D Meyers said. \u8220\'20\'1CProgressives are the ones trying to pass a bill that actually follows through on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda and improves people\u8217\'20\'19s lives. The Manchins and Sinemas of the world are the ones shitting on it and dragging it out so it\u8217\'20\'19s longer and more painful than \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  dancing on stage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many individual Democratic policies such as paid family leave and drug pricing reform are popular, Meyers added, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut you actually need to pass them and give people a reason to vote for you. Because just saying \u8216\'20\'18we\u8217\'20\'19re not Trump!\u8217\'20\'19 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work when Trump himself isn\u8217\'20\'19t on the ballot. It\u8217\'20\'19s like if Taco Bell\u8217\'20\'19s slogan was \u8216\'20\'18hey, at least we\u8217\'20\'19re not Chipotle!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Samantha Bee\par \par \uc2 And on Full Frontal, Samantha Bee delved into the start of what is probably the most important supreme court term for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in at least three decades. This week, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/01/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-law-oral-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard two fast-track cases}}}\uc2  against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/22/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, makes no exception for rape or incest, and empowers private citizens to sue anyone who facilitates an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we don\u8217\'20\'19t yet have an official ruling, it appeared on Monday that the court might be leaning toward allowing lower courts to block the Texas law, and some of the leaners might surprise you,\u8221\'20\'1D Bee said.\par \par \uc2 Two Trump appointees, Amy Coney Barrett and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , questioned the structure of the Texas law to evade federal judicial review; Kavanaugh also theorized that the arguments put forth in Texas could be used to pass a law allowing private citizens to sue neighbors with guns in a left-leaning state. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I guess he\u8217\'20\'19s protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by protecting gun rights \u8230\'20\'26?\u8221\'20\'1D said Bee.\par \par \uc2 The court will also hear a case brought by the only remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi, which banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks in 2018. \u8220\'20\'1CIt can\u8217\'20\'19t be overstated how significant this case is in the battle to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, particularly with a supreme court so conservative they make their statue of Lady Justice stand behind a statue of Mr Justice,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe decisions the supreme court is making will impact lives for generations,\u8221\'20\'1D she concluded. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t give up hope and we cannot stop fighting because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211104ehb40025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
