\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US director of national intelligence releases declassified Covid report \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Joan E Greve \par \uc2 7,849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2021\par 00:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Report: first human exposure to coronavirus occurred \u8216\'20\'18no later than November 2019\u8217\'20\'19FDA clears \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for children ages five to 11Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda remains unrealized as Democrats fail to close deal againSenate\u8217\'20\'19s 50-50 split lets Manchin and Sinema revel in outsize influenceLeticia James confirms run for New York governorSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * The office of the US director of national intelligence released a declassified report on the origins of coronavirus. The 18-page report concludes that the virus \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not developed as a biological weapon\u8221\'20\'1D. However, the US intelligence community could not reach a definitive assessment on the virus\u8217\'20\'19 origins, and the report notes that officials will likely be unable to do so unless new information comes to light.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  approved a lower dose of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine for children ages five to 11. The decision marks a key development in the approval process, but the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  still needs to authorize shots for children in that age group. A CDC advisory committee will meet next week to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application, and the ultimate decision on authorization will be made by CDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court denied a request to block a statewide requirement in Maine that healthcare workers get vaccinated against Covid-19. However, conservative justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Neil M Gorsuch\uc2  issued a dissent noting that the \u8220\'20\'1Cplight\u8221\'20\'1D of workers with religious beliefs against vaccination \u8220\'20\'1Cis worthy of our attention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The court has also agreed to hear a case involving the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to limit carbon emissions. The news comes just days before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to arrive in Glasgow for the Cop26 climate change conference, where the US president is expected to strongly urge fellow leaders to take significant steps to limit emissions.\par \par \uc2 * Biden met with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  at the Vatican this morning. The US president told reporters that the pope said Biden should keep receiving communion, despite criticism from some Catholic leaders. A number of American bishops have called for Biden to be denied communion because of his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two House Republicans serving on the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, announced he would not seek reelection. As one of the ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the insurrection, Kinzinger had already attracted several primary opponents. Illinois\u8217\'20\'19 redistricting plan also meant that Kinzinger would likely need to face off against another Republican congressman, \uc2 Darin LaHood\uc2 , to win reelection.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The Capitol police officer who was charged with helping hide evidence of a rioter\u8217\'20\'19s participation in the 6 January insurrection has pleaded not guilty and resigned from his post.\par \par \uc2 Michael Riley, 50, allegedly told a rioter to delete \uc2 Facebook\uc2  posts to shield themself from investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a capitol police officer who agrees with your political stance,\u8221\'20\'1D Riley allegedly wrote, per the indictment. \u8220\'20\'1CTake down the part about being in the building they are currently investigating and everyone who was in the building is going to be charged. Just looking out!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His legal team contests wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith regard to the charges against him, the evidence will show that it is not a felony for one person to suggest to another that they take down ill-conceived \uc2 Facebook\uc2  posts,\u8221\'20\'1D the former officer\u8217\'20\'19s legal team told NBC News.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The Liberty Counsel said that more than 2,000 individuals in Maine had objected to being vaccinated on religious and philosophical grounds.\par \par \uc2 Requests for religious exemptions have been growing as state and local governments enact coronavirus vaccine requirements.\par \par \uc2 A cottage industry of anti-vaccine and religious groups has cropped up to help people dodge requirements. In Rocklin, California \u8211\'20\'13 just north-east of the state capital, Sacramento \u8211\'20\'13 a megachurch pastor has been offering religious exemption letters to all who want them. Pastor Greg Fairrington of Destiny Christian church, who has organized protests at the state capitol against the state\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine requirements for school children, healthcare workers and first responders, has held that he is not anti-vaccine, but \u8220\'20\'1Cthe vaccine poses a morally compromising situation for many people of faith\u8221\'20\'1D. The Christian legal advocacy group Liberty Counsel offers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lc.org/Site%20Images/Resources/examples/Employment-sample-request.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter templates}}}\uc2  to claim a religious exemption, as well.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what it all means:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/19/religious-exemptions-us-covid-vaccine-mandates-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Religious exemptions threaten to undermine US Covid vaccine mandates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court refused to block Maine vaccine requirement\par \par \uc2 The supreme court denied a request to block a statewide requirement in Maine that healthcare workers get vaccinated against Covid-19, after a group of workers argued that the mandate violated their religious beliefs.\par \par \uc2 The state for decades has required health workers to get vaccinated against contagious diseases regardless or religious or philosophical disagreement. The court has for now allowed the policy to continue.\par \par \uc2 However, conservative justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Neil M. Gorsuch\uc2  issued a dissent noting that \u8220\'20\'1Chealth care workers who have served on the front line of a pandemic for the last 18 months are now being fired and their practices shuttered. All for adhering to their constitutionally protected religious beliefs. Their plight is worthy of our attention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nearly $3tn domestic agenda remains unrealized after an 11th-hour push to rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  around a pared-down package that he framed as historic, failed to close the deal in time for his meeting with world leaders in Rome at the G20 summit.\par \par \uc2 But after a dramatic Thursday of bold promises and dashed hopes, the House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi}}}\uc2 , was forced to postpone a vote on a $1tn infrastructure bill for a second time in a month, as progressives demanded more assurances that a compromise $1.75tn social policy plan would also pass.\par \par \uc2 It was a setback \u8211\'20\'13 though perhaps only a temporary one \u8211\'20\'13 for Democratic leaders, who had hoped to hand the president a legislative victory that he could tout during his six-day trip to Europe for a pair of international economic and climate summits.\par \par \uc2 The delay underscored the depth of mistrust among Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 between the House and Senate, progressives and centrists, leadership and members \u8211\'20\'13 after a lengthy negotiating process yielded a plan that was about half the size of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s initial vision.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/29/joe-biden-domestic-agenda-democrats-infrastructure-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda remains unrealized as Democrats fail to close deal again}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Countless newspaper columns and hours of airtime have been expended trying to understand the motives of the two holdouts, who can effectively decide whether Democrats keep their campaign promises \u8211\'20\'13 with huge implications for next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Manchin is not so mysterious. He hails from coal-rich West Virginia, a conservative state that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won twice in a landslide, and once {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/joe-manchin-ad-dead-aim_n_758457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran a campaign ad}}}\uc2  in which he shot a rifle at a legislative bill. He owns about $1m in shares in his son\u8217\'20\'19s coal brokerage company and has raised campaign funds from oil and gas interests.\par \par \uc2 Critics accuse him of putting personal and local concerns ahead of his party, the nation and the world. The \uc2 USA Today\uc2  newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/restricted/?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.usatoday.com%2Fstory%2Fopinion%2Ftodaysdebate%2F2021%2F10%2F28%2Fmanchin-risks-earth-save-west-virginia%2F8539317002%2F&gnt-tng-s=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in an editorial}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no stretch to conclude that Democratic \uc2 Sen. Joe Manchin\uc2  is risking the planet\u8217\'20\'19s future to protect a dwindling pool of 14,000 coal mining jobs in his home state of West Virginia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/10/kyrsten-sinema-arizona-senate-senator-infrastructure-spending-biden-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sinema, however}}}\uc2 , has been described as enigmatic, sphinx-like and whimsical. In 2018 she became Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s first Democratic senator for more than two decades and, despite progressive credentials and a flair for fashion statements, has taken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/arizona-democrats-mark-kelly-kyrsten-sinema"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative positions}}}\uc2  on several issues.\par \par \uc2 She also provokes the left with stunts such as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/03/06/sinema-thumbs-down/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thumbs-down gesture}}}\uc2  on the Senate floor when she voted against raising the federal minimum wage and, on Thursday, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MittRomney/status/1453752691868438533?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 parody of the TV comedy Ted Lasso}}}\uc2  with the Republican senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 . Perhaps tellingly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/10/15/sinema-campaign-money-pharma-finance-516110"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sinema raised $1.1m}}}\uc2  in campaign funds in the last quarter with significant donations from the pharmaceutical and financial industries.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/29/senate-manchin-sinema-biden-democrats-outsize-influence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate\u8217\'20\'19s 50-50 split lets Manchin and Sinema revel in outsize influence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate\u8217\'20\'19s 50-50 split lets Manchin and Sinema revel in outsize influence\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  recently summed up his problems getting things done.\par \par \uc2 In an America where the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is split 50-50, then effectively any single senator can hold a veto over the president\u8217\'20\'19s entire agenda. \u8220\'20\'1CLook,\u8221\'20\'1D laughed Biden at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/21/politics/full-president-joe-biden-cnn-town-hall-july-21/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a CNN town hall}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cyou have 50 Democrats, every one is a president. Every single one. So, you got to work things out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It explains why the most powerful man in the world is currently struggling to get his way in Washington \u8211\'20\'13 and why two members of his own party, Senators J oe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/03/joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema-democrats-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are standing in his way}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such is the distribution of power that American presidents can only impose their will up to a point if Congress refuses to yield. While the White House can do much with executive orders and actions, major legislation must gain a majority of votes in the House of Representatives and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Democrats do currently control both chambers \u8211\'20\'13 but only just. The Senate is evenly divided between 50 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  and 50 Republicans, meaning that Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  must cast the tie-breaking vote. That means all 50 Democratic senators must be on board in the face of united Republican opposition \u8211\'20\'13 an increasingly safe (and bleak) assumption in polarised era.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, President \uc2 Franklin Roosevelt\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cookpolitical.com/analysis/national/national-politics/comparing-bidens-mandate-fdrs-and-lbjs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached 59 seats}}}\uc2  in the then 96-member Senate, while President Lyndon Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s Democrats had 68 in what by then was a 100-seat chamber. Biden is trying to match the scale of both men\u8217\'20\'19s ambition with no room for error.\par \par \uc2 This is why his agenda \u8211\'20\'13 huge investments in infrastructure and expanding the social safety net \u8211\'20\'13 depends on the blessing of Manchin and Sinema in what might seem to the watching world as a case of the tail wagging the dog.\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, an independent senator from Vermont defeated by Biden in last year\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1443926661792210945?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted earlier this month}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C2 senators cannot be allowed to defeat what 48 senators and 210 House members want.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the cold reality is that, after months of painful wrangling and concessions, Manchin and Sinema have almost single-handedly narrowed the scale and scope of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s grand vision.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The office of the US director of national intelligence released a declassified report on the origins of coronavirus. The 18-page report concludes that the virus \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not developed as a biological weapon\u8221\'20\'1D. However, the US intelligence community could not reach a definitive assessment on the virus\u8217\'20\'19 origins, and the report notes that officials will likely be unable to do so unless new information comes to light.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  approved a lower dose of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine for children between the ages of five and 11. The decision marks a key development in the approval process, but the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  still needs to authorize shots for children in that age group. A CDC advisory committee will meet next week to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application, and the ultimate decision on authorization will be made by CDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court has agreed to hear a case involving the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to limit carbon emissions. The news comes just days before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to arrive in Glasgow for the Cop26 climate change conference, where the US president is expected to strongly urge fellow leaders to take significant steps to limit emissions.\par \par \uc2 * Biden met with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  at the Vatican this morning. The US president told reporters that the pope said Biden should keep receiving communion, despite criticism from some Catholic leaders. A number of American bishops have called for Biden to be denied communion because of his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ rights.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two House Republicans serving on the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, announced he would not seek reelection. As one of the ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the insurrection, Kinzinger had already attracted several primary opponents. Illinois\u8217\'20\'19 redistricting plan also meant that Kinzinger would likely need to face off against another Republican congressman, \uc2 Darin LaHood\uc2 , to win reelection.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 With no major climate legislation firmly in hand and international allies still smarting after four bruising years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  faces a major challenge to reassert American credibility as he heads to crucial \uc2 UN\uc2  climate talks in Scotland.\par \par \uc2 The US president, who has vowed to tackle a climate crisis he has described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cexistential threat\u8221\'20\'1D to civilization, will be welcomed to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/cop26-glasgow-climate-change-conference-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop26}}}\uc2  talks with a sense of relief following the decisions of his predecessor, who pulled his country out of the landmark Paris climate agreement and derided climate science as \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Biden, who departed to Europe on Thursday and arrived in Rome on Friday morning for a G20 summit, will head to Glasgow with his domestic climate agenda whittled away by a recalcitrant Congress and a barrage of criticism from climate activists who claim Biden\u8217\'20\'19s actions have yet to match his words.\par \par \uc2 This disconnect has perturbed delegates keen to see a reliable American partner emerge from the Trump era, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/aug/09/humans-have-caused-unprecedented-and-irreversible-change-to-climate-scientists-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid increasingly dire warnings}}}\uc2  from scientists that \u8220\'20\'1Cirreversible\u8221\'20\'1D heatwaves, floods, crop failures and other effects are being locked in by governments\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/28/world-failing-make-changes-avoid-climate-breakdown-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sluggish response}}}\uc2  to global heating.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is still the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy, other nations pay attention to it, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve never had a president more committed to climate action,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alice Hill, who was a climate adviser to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut there is skepticism being expressed by other countries. They saw our dramatic flip from Obama to Trump and the worry is we will flip again. A lack of consistency is the issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/29/joe-biden-glasgow-cop-26-summit-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden heads to crucial climate talks as wary allies wonder if US will deliver}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court agrees to hear case involving federal government's ability to curb emissions\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to hear a case involving how far the federal government can go to limit carbon emissions, as environmental experts warn that countries must act quickly to address the climate crisis and prevent catastrophic temperature increases.\par \par \uc2 Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-supreme-court-hear-bid-curb-federal-power-limit-carbon-emissions-2021-10-29/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to take up the case could complicate efforts by President Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s administration to issue new and more stringent regulations under the Clean Air Act aimed at reducing emissions linked to global climate change....\par \par \uc2 About 20 states and various industry groups, including coal interests, had appealed a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling striking down a regulation issued by Republican former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration intended to constrain the regulation of carbon emissions from power plants. The ruling was made in January 2021 by the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit.\par \par \uc2 Those states and groups have opposed regulating carbon emissions under the Clean Air Act. The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s Affordable Clean Energy rule was challenged in court by states and groups that support aggressive action to curb such emissions.\par \par \uc2 The news comes just days before Biden is set to arrive in Glasgow for the Cop26 climate change conference, where the US president is expected to strongly urge fellow leaders to take significant steps to limit emissions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s advisory committee will meet next week to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application to make a lower dose of its coronavirus vaccine available to children between the ages of five and 11.\par \par \uc2 If the panel endorses the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for children in that age group, CDC Director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  is expected to swiftly approve the company\u8217\'20\'19s application.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has already started taking steps to ensure the vaccine can be quickly administered to those children, coordinating with with pharmacies, hospitals and doctors\u8217\'20\'19 offices to get them prepared for the expected approval.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know millions of parents have been waiting for Covid-19 vaccine for kids in this age group,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House pandemic response team, said last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd should the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and CDC authorize the vaccine, we will be ready to get shots in arms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  clears \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  shot for children aged five to 11\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has cleared another hurdle on the way to making vaccinations against Covid-19 available to children aged five to 11, authorising the use of child-sized shots of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech vaccine for emergency use.\par \par \uc2 Up to 28 million American children could be eligible for vaccinations as early as next week, once advisers to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) make more detailed recommendations on who should get vaccinated. A final decision from the CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , is expected shortly after that.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a major moment in the US effort against the coronavirus. As the Associated Press puts it: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile children are at lower risk of severe illness or death from Covid-19 than older people, five- to 11-year-olds in the US have been seriously affected, including more than 8,300 hospitalisations, about a third requiring intensive care, and nearly 100 deaths.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government has also counted more than 2,000 coronavirus-related school closings since the start of the school year, affecting more than a million children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ODNI report reiterated the importance of getting more information from the Chinese government about the initial outbreak of coronavirus in Wuhan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChina\u8217\'20\'19s cooperation most likely would be needed to reach a conclusive assessment of the origins of COVID-19,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dni.gov/files/ODNI/documents/assessments/Declassified-Assessment-on-COVID-19-Origins.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the report}}}\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeijing, however, continues to hinder the global investigation, resist sharing information, and blame other countries, including the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese actions reflect, in part, China\u8217\'20\'19s government\u8217\'20\'19s own uncertainty about where an investigation could lead as well as its frustration the international community is using the issue to exert political pressure on China.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  leveled similar criticism against the Chinese government after he received an intelligence report on the origins of coronavirus in August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCritical information about the origins of this pandemic exists in the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said after receiving the report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYet from the beginning, government officials in China have worked to prevent international investigators and members of the global public health community from accessing it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ODNI report notes that the US intelligence community \u8220\'20\'1Cremains divided on the most likely origin of COVID-19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll agencies assess that two hypotheses are plausible: natural exposure to an infected animal and a laboratory-associated incident,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe IC judges they will be unable to provide a more definitive explanation for the origin of COVID-19 unless new information allows them to determine the specific pathway for initial natural contact with an animal or to determine that a laboratory in Wuhan was handling SARS-CoV-2 or a close progenitor virus before COVID-19 emerged.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In short, the US intelligence community cannot say for certain how the virus started unless officials get more information about the early days of the pandemic, and the Chinese government has been very reluctant to share such data.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 US director of national intelligence releases declassified Covid-19 report\par \par \uc2 The office of the US director of national intelligence has released a declassified report on the origin of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The 18-page report concludes that the first human exposure to the virus occurred \u8220\'20\'1Cno later than November 2019\u8221\'20\'1D and resulted in the initial outbreak in Wuhan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe judge the virus was not developed as a biological weapon,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost agencies also assess with low confidence that SARS-CoV-2 probably was not genetically engineered; however, two agencies believe there was not sufficient evidence to make an assessment either way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report adds that the US intelligence community concluded Chinese officials \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not have foreknowledge of the virus before the initial outbreak\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cuomo to appear in Albany court next month to face sexual misconduct charge\par \par \uc2 Former New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  will appear in Albany city court next month to face a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/28/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-misdemeanor-complaint"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misdemeanor charge for his alleged sexual misconduct}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a press conference this afternoon, Albany county sheriff Craig Apple said Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s court appearance had been scheduled for November 17. After appearing in court, Cuomo will be processed and likely released, Apple added.\par \par \uc2 enltrAndrew Cuomo could face an arrest warrant if he doesn't show up for November 17 court date for misdemeanor charge of forcible touching, Albany County Sheriff Craig Apple says\par \par \uc2 "It's my hope that he shows up. I don't think he wouldn't." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qz9BkdxFLb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qz9BkdxFLb}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/THiba9dAqZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/THiba9dAqZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1454160314413588480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Cuomo is facing a misdemeanor charge for allegedly groping a woman at the New York Executive Mansion last year, one of several accusations of sexual misconduct that led to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s resignation in August.\par \par \uc2 Apple applauded his investigative team for building a \u8220\'20\'1Csolid case\u8221\'20\'1D for the misdemeanor charge.\par \par \uc2 Asked about whether he expects Cuomo to appear in court next month, Apple said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my hope that he shows up. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But if Cuomo doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear, Apple added, \u8220\'20\'1CAt that point, you could have a criminal arrest warrant issued.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reactions are pouring in to an announcement this morning from Illinois Representative \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two House Republicans serving on the select committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/29/house-capitol-attack-committee-trump-officials-resistance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigating the Capitol insurrection}}}\uc2 , that he will not be running for re-election and would be retiring from Congress.\par \par \uc2 Many pro-Trump Republican representatives have already released statements celebrating Kinzinger\u8217\'20\'19s decision, including North Carolina representative Madison Cawthorn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe RINO turncoats will keep falling...Enjoy your CNN contract, loser,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cawthron in a statement provided to Politico. (RINO refers to the label \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican in name only\u8221\'20\'1D used by Trumpist GOPers to insult those in their party they think have drifted too far left.)\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's a taste:\par \par \uc2 Rep. MTG in stmt called Kinzinger a \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitor to the Republican party\u8221\'20\'1D and said he is retiring to avoiding losing in a primary.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Cawthorn in stmt said: "The RINO turncoats will keep falling...Enjoy your CNN contract, loser."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1454109170035306500?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement obtained by Politico, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also commented on Kinzinger\u8217\'20\'19s retirement, saying \u8220\'20\'1C2 down, 8 to go!\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/31/trump-pac-targets-republicans-voted-to-impeach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referencing the 10 Republicans who crossed party lines to approve one article of impeachment against Trump in January.}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump statement re: Kinzinger retirement: "2 down, 8 to go!"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meridith McGraw (@meridithmcgraw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/meridithmcgraw/status/1454113568320806918?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Illinois representative \uc2 Darin LaHood{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/oct/29/biden-economic-agenda-delayed-vote-infrastructure-us-politics-live?page=with:block-617c1df48f08fe3ad9f4376c#block-617c1df48f08fe3ad9f4376c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has already announced that he will be running for re-election }}}\uc2  in Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s newly drawn 16th ward, the district that he and Kinzinger would\u8217\'20\'19ve faced off in if Kinzinger were running for re-election.\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger made the announcement in a video posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this morning, where he recounted how he was first elected to the House in 2010 following his deployment in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also remember during that campaign saying that, if I ever thought it was time to move on from Congress, I would. And that time is now,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said in the video.\par \par \uc2 There are reports that Kinzinger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jimsciutto/status/1454097245448523785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has not ruled out running for other office positions. }}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLooking forward to the next chapter! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SvdFCVtrlE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SvdFCVtrlE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  (@AdamKinzinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamKinzinger/status/1454090582586974218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressional progressives have endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s framework for the $1.75tn reconciliation package, but some Democrats have still not given up hope on getting certain initiatives included in the bill.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  is specifically calling for Medicare drug price negotiation to be added back to the reconciliation package, after it was omitted from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s framework.\par \par \uc2 enltrBig Pharma doesn\u8217\'20\'19t own the government, the people do.\par \par \uc2 And the vast majority of the people want Medicare to be able to negotiate lower drug prices. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get it done.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  (@amyklobuchar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amyklobuchar/status/1454151628207136775?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBig Pharma doesn\u8217\'20\'19t own the government, the people do,\u8221\'20\'1D the Minnesota senator said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the vast majority of the people want Medicare to be able to negotiate lower drug prices. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get it done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Medicare drug price negotiation proposal was a key priority for Senate budget committee chair Bernie Sanders, and he has also indicated he will keep fighting for it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have some serious concerns about what is not in the bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawmakers-push-to-include-medicare-drug-pricing-provision-in-biden-plan-11635516651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, we have been talking about lowering the cost of prescription drugs and that is not in the bill. At all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/06/letitia-james-new-york-attorney-general-donald-trump-andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James}}}\uc2  , the first woman of color ever to hold statewide elected office in New York, just issued a campaign video announcing that she\u8217\'20\'19ll run to be the next governor of New York.\par \par \uc2 Letitia James. Photograph: Michael M Santiago/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve spent my career guided by a simple principle, stand up to the powerful on behalf of the vulnerable, to be a force for change.\par \par \uc2 She added that she had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/mar/28/opioid-crisis-sackler-family-purdue-pharma-new-york-sues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gone after}}}\uc2  the drug companies \u8220\'20\'1Cfor fueling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opioid crisis}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and had fought for better conditions and transparency in nursing homes during the coronavirusa pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve sued the Trump administration 76 times,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, then, raising her eyebrows and shrugging ironically, added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut who\u8217\'20\'19s counting?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve taken action to divest our pension funds from fossil fuels. I\u8217\'20\'19ve held accountable those to mistreat and harass women in the workplace, no matter how powerful the offenders. I\u8217\'20\'19ve fought for affordable housing and worked to eliminate the NRA,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Then, smiling, while sitting in a leather office chair, James said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, I am announcing my campaign to be your next governor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An explosive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ag.ny.gov/sites/default/files/2021.08.03_nyag_-_investigative_report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 165-page report}}}\uc2  released in early August by James delivered a mountain of damning and often graphic evidence that played an instrumental role in bringing down the career of now-former New York governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Cuomo}}}\uc2 , a leading figure in the Democratic party who served in \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cabinet. Cuomo accused her of going after him for political gain.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/06/letitia-james-new-york-attorney-general-donald-trump-andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also investigating}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 . The current governor, Democrat \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , is New York\u8217\'20\'19s first female governor. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if she plans to seek election next November, having assumed her role after Cuomo resigned, per protocol as she was the lieutenant governor. But there\u8217\'20\'19s been every expectation that Hochul would seek to remain in the office.\par \par \uc2 NYS Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 . Photograph: Lev Radin/ZUMA Press Wire/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York state attorney general Letitia James makes run for governor official\par \par \uc2 Breaking, though not surprising, news. It\u8217\'20\'19s on! NY AG Tish James is going to challenge incumbent Democrat \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  for the governorship of New York.\par \par \uc2 Hochul took over from her post as lieutenant governor in August when \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  resigned after multiple women accused him of misconduct ranging from alleged sexual assault to sexual harassment at work and cultivating a toxic workplace in Albany.\par \par \uc2 James investigated and backed the women, issuing a devastating report in the summer that damned Cuomo even though he denied assaulting or harassing people.\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm running for Governor of New York because I have the experience, vision, and courage to take on the powerful on behalf of all New Yorkers.\par \par \uc2 Let's do this, together. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JA21M19p5m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JA21M19p5m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tish James (@TishJames) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TishJames/status/1454138856987631622?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration issues new memo ending Trump-era 'remain in Mexico' policy for migrants\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration was expected to reinstate the harsh Trump-era policy around the middle of next month, whereby migrants unlawfully crossing into the US from Mexico are forced to wait south of the US border while their legal cases, principally to be granted asylum, are processed \u8211\'20\'13 which in the past has taken months or years for some, in an overwhelmed US immigration system.\par \par \uc2 But today officials are making fresh efforts to cancel the policy started by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Reuters news agency reports that:\par \par \uc2 Biden officials made a renewed attempt to end a Trump-era immigration program that forced asylum seekers to wait in Mexico for US court hearings, according to a \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) memo previewed by officials.\par \par \uc2 The administration first ended the Migrant Protection Protocols (MPP) program, informally called \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D, earlier this year, but was ordered to restart it by a federal judge, who said it had failed to follow proper regulatory procedure.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in August rejected an effort by the Biden administration to block the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 The new memo is comprehensive, DHS officials said on a call with reporters. It \u8220\'20\'1Csquarely addresses some of the alleged failures of the prior memo,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the officials said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes into account a whole range of new information that\u8217\'20\'19s been made available or that\u8217\'20\'19s occurred since June,\u8221\'20\'1D when the previous memo was issued, one official said. The administration will seek to have the court order vacated in light of the new memo, the officials said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Biden administration will continue to take steps to restart the program by mid-November, to comply with the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, officials said.\par \par \uc2 The possible reinstatement of MPP - even on a short-term basis - would add to a confusing mix of U.S. policies in place at the U.S.-Mexico border, where arrests of migrants crossing into the United States have hit record highs.\par \par \uc2 The administration said it can only move forward if Mexico agrees. The DHS officials said Mexico and the United States are still in talks.\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  said earlier this month that it has expressed a \u8220\'20\'1Cnumber of concerns\u8221\'20\'1D over MPP to U.S. officials, particularly around due process, legal certainty, access to legal aid and the safety of migrants.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 US regulators expected today to approve coronavirus vaccine for younger kids \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The US Food and Drug Adminstration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) is expected to authorize a reduced dose of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 vaccine, on an emergency use basis for children aged five to 11.\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus shots are already allowed for children in the US ages 12 and up. But word on the vaccine for younger children has been \u8220\'20\'1Ceagerly anticipated by millions of families looking to protect some of the only remaining Americans left out of the vaccination campaign\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has reported today, citing unnamed sources familiar with the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s planning.\par \par \uc2 About 28 million children in the group would be eligible to receive one-third of the adult dose, with two injections three weeks apart. If the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  signs off, as is expected, they could start getting shots as early as Wednesday, the newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/10/29/us/politics/covid-vaccine-children.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two House Republicans serving on the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, announced he would not seek reelection. As one of the ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the insurrection, Kinzinger had already attracted several primary opponents. Illinois\u8217\'20\'19 redistricting plan also meant that Kinzinger would likely need to face off against another Republican congressman, \uc2 Darin LaHood\uc2 , to win reelection.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  at the Vatican this morning. The US president told reporters that the pope said Biden should keep receiving communion, despite criticism from some Catholic leaders. A number of American bishops have called for Biden to be denied communion because of his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ rights.\par \par \uc2 * The House vote on the bipartisan infrastructure bill was delayed last night, after progressives demanded the reconciliation package advance at the same time. But the Congressional Progressive Caucus has formally endorsed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s framework for the $1.75tn reconciliation package, raising Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 hopes that both bills will ultimately pass.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with Italian Prime Minister \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  today, ahead of the start of the G20 summit in Rome tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoth leaders recognized the historic achievement of a global minimum tax, building resilience against future pandemics, and the commitment to rapidly decarbonize how we produce electricity,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in its readout of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden thanked Prime Minister Draghi for all Italy has done to support the people of Afghanistan, including by convening an extraordinary G20 session to address counter-terrorism efforts and humanitarian aid, and by temporarily housing over 4,000 Afghans en route to the United States last August.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House also noted that the two leaders expressed their ongoing commitment to ensuring \u8220\'20\'1Cthe rules governing the 21st century economy are based in shared democratic values\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 In June, the US Conference of Bishops {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-government-and-politics-religion-ea0179cd6c8eddbf66693a7e2b28e2da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took steps}}}\uc2  to rebuke Catholic politicians like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ rights.\par \par \uc2 After the conference took those steps, Biden was asked whether he was concerned about the potential rebuke and calls from some Catholic leaders to deny him communion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a private matter, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in June.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pope said Biden should 'keep receiving communion,' president tells reporters\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  told him during their one-on-one meeting this morning that he should keep receiving communion, amid some Catholic leaders\u8217\'20\'19 criticism of the president\u8217\'20\'19s views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the start of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Italian Prime Minister \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 , a reporter asked the president whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  came up during his discussion with the pope.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, it didn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just talked about the fact that he was happy that I was a good Catholic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  meets United States President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Photograph: Vatican Media/UPI/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Biden, who is only the second Catholic to ever serve as president of the United States, then added that the pope told him he should \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep receiving communion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Some Catholic leaders have suggested that Biden and other Democratic politicians should be denied communion because of their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pope-francis-joe-biden-communion-d58f0eec9ac1a1ff576e38fb85bf532f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last month}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  said Catholic bishops should focus on leading with \u8220\'20\'1Ccompassion and tenderness,\u8221\'20\'1D rather than condemnation, but he did not explicitly say whether politicians like Biden should receive communion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack is confronting a pivotal moment as resistance from top {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  aides threatens to undermine their efforts to uncover the extent of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The select committee remains in the evidence-gathering phase of the investigation that now encompasses at least five different lines of inquiry from whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  abused the presidency to reinstall himself in office or coordinated with far-right rally organizers.\par \par \uc2 But unless House investigators can secure a breakthrough to obtain documents and testimony from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , and others in the next few weeks, the most pressing questions about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in 6 January may go unanswered, two sources said.\par \par \uc2 The select committee has designated its \u8220\'20\'1Cgold\u8221\'20\'1D team to examine the extent of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal involvement in the events that left five dead and more than 140 injured as his supporters stormed the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  in his name, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 One major focus of the investigation is whether Trump had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/capitol-riot-white-house-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advance knowledge of the insurrection}}}\uc2 , the sources said \u8211\'20\'13 since if they uncover evidence of conspiracy to violently stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win, that could constitute a crime.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/29/house-capitol-attack-committee-trump-officials-resistance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack panel faces pivotal moment as Trump allies stonewall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his video announcing his retirement from Congress, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  also denounced the tribalism that has come to define the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this day, to prevail or survive, you must belong to a tribe. Our political parties only survive by appealing to the most motivated and the most extreme elements within it,\u8221\'20\'1D the Illinois congressman said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the price tag to power has skyrocketed, and fear and distrust has served as an effective strategy to meet that cost. After all, if a man is convinced that his very survival is at stake, he\u8217\'20\'19ll part with anything, including money to ensure he does survive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger emphasized his commitment to changing the narrative around party politics, and he said he wanted to focus on \u8220\'20\'1Ca broader fight nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D instead of a reelection battle.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  had decided to seek reelection, he would have faced a bruising primary campaign that will likely include another Republican congressman.\par \par \uc2 As one of the ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the Capitol insurrection in January, Kinzinger had already attracted several primary opponents.\par \par \uc2 But perhaps even more challenging for Kinzinger was the reality that he would have to face off against Republican incumbent \uc2 Darin LaHood\uc2  in the race.\par \par \uc2 As Politico reports, the newly approved congressional map in Illinois would have pitted Kinzinger against LaHood, after the state lost one House seat due to the results of the 2020 Census.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe incumbent pairings in the new Illinois 14D-3R congressional map, which passed both chambers & is headed to Gov JB Pritzker's desk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IL04?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IL04}}}\uc2  - Reps Chuy Garcia (D) & \uc2 Marie Newman\uc2  (D) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IL16?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IL16}}}\uc2  - Reps Darin LaHood (R) & Adam Kinzinger (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IL12?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IL12}}}\uc2  - Reps Mike Bost (R) & Mary Miller (R) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UVijr8gpqM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UVijr8gpqM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ally Mutnick (@allymutnick) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/allymutnick/status/1453957084517597191?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger, House Republican on Capitol attack committee, will not seek reelection\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two House Republicans serving on the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, will not seek reelection next year.\par \par \uc2 The Illinois congressman made the announcement in a video posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this morning.\par \par \uc2 In the video, Kinzinger recounted how he was first elected to the House in 2010, after he returned from a deployment in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also remember during that campaign saying that, if I ever thought it was time to move on from Congress, I would. And that time is now,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said in the video.\par \par \uc2 enltrLooking forward to the next chapter! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SvdFCVtrlE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SvdFCVtrlE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  (@AdamKinzinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamKinzinger/status/1454090582586974218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But Kinzinger made clear that he will remain involved in politics, possibly hinting at a statewide or national campaign in the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy desire to make a difference is bigger than it\u8217\'20\'19s ever been,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t the end of my political future but the beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger is one of ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the Capitol insurrection in January. Another one of those members, Anthony Gonzalez, has already announced he will also not seek reelection next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has urged world leaders to take \u8220\'20\'1Cradical decisions\u8221\'20\'1D at next week\u8217\'20\'19s global environmental summit in a special message recorded for BBC Radio 4\u8217\'20\'19s Thought for the Day.\par \par \uc2 Leaders attending the Cop26 conference in Glasgow must offer \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete hope to future generations\u8221\'20\'1D, the pontiff said.\par \par \uc2 Francis is not attending the summit, despite earlier suggestions that he would fly in for a brief appearance to reinforce the significance of the event. His message was recorded in Italian and lasted almost five minutes. It was broadcast on Friday morning with a voiceover in English.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CClimate change and the Covid-19 pandemic have exposed our deep vulnerability and raised numerous doubts and concerns about our economic systems and the way we organise our societies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have lost our sense of security, and are experiencing a sense of powerlessness and loss of control over our lives. We find ourselves increasingly frail and even fearful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/29/pope-francis-world-leaders-climate-action-cop26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis urges leaders to take \u8216\'20\'18radical\u8217\'20\'19 climate action at Cop26}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tweeted another photo from his one-on-one meeting with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  at the Vatican this morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt was an honor to meet with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  again at the Vatican today. I thanked His Holiness for his advocacy for the world\u8217\'20\'19s poor and those suffering from hunger, conflict, and persecution, and lauded his leadership in fighting the climate crisis and ending the pandemic. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PGF5axSK4X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PGF5axSK4X}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1454082724289986572?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an honor to meet with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  again at the Vatican today,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in the tweet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thanked His Holiness for his advocacy for the world\u8217\'20\'19s poor and those suffering from hunger, conflict, and persecution, and lauded his leadership in fighting the climate crisis and ending the pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And in an extremely on-brand moment for Biden, the US president apparently parted ways with the pope by telling him, \u8220\'20\'1CGod love ya!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden departed with a final, "God love ya!" to the pope.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Memoli (@mikememoli) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli/status/1454065605993193480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden meets with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  in Vatican City\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  in Vatican City this morning, marking the first time that the president has met with the Catholic leader since taking office in January.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who is only the second Catholic to ever serve as president of the United States, met one-on-one with the pope for about 90 minutes before participating in a bilateral meeting with Cardinal \uc2 Pietro Parolin\uc2 , the Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  meets with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during an audience at the Apostolic Palace on October 29. Photograph: Vatican Pool/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn his audience with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  today, President Biden thanked His Holiness for his advocacy for the world\u8217\'20\'19s poor and those suffering from hunger, conflict, and persecution,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in its readout of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe lauded \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 leadership in fighting the climate crisis, as well as his advocacy to ensure the pandemic ends for everyone through vaccine sharing and an equitable global economic recovery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Complicating the reconciliation bill negotiations for Democratic leaders was a lack of certainty from the key holdouts, Senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joe-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin}}}\uc2  of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona. Both sounded hopeful that a deal was within reach, but stopped short of offering their firm support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter months of productive, good-faith negotiations with Biden and the White House, we have made significant progress on the proposed budget reconciliation package,\u8221\'20\'1D Sinema said yesterday, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to getting this done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin also did not commit to supporting the legislation he played a significant role in shaping. Asked whether he would vote for the plan, he said only that its fate was presently \u8220\'20\'1Cin the hands of the House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 After months of prolonged negotiations, the proposed framework is far smaller in size and scope than the $3.5tn package \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  initially envisioned. Even so, the president claimed a pre-emptive legislative achievement on par with those enacted by \uc2 Franklin D Roosevelt\uc2  and Lyndon Johnson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny single element of this framework would be viewed as a fundamental change in America. Taken together they\u8217\'20\'19re truly consequential,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said yesterday before leaving for Europe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we make these investments, we will own the future,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/28/biden-capitol-hill-democrats-struggle-reach-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urges Democrats to unite around \u8216\'20\'18historic\u8217\'20\'19 $1.75tn investment package}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's economic agenda hangs in the balance after another delayed vote on infrastructure\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  did not get the vote she wanted on the bipartisan infrastructure bill yesterday, after the Congressional Progressive Caucus indicated its members would not support the proposal until the reconciliation package advanced as well.\par \par \uc2 But there was some good news for Pelosi yesterday: while delaying the infrastructure vote (again), the CPC also indicated its members support \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s framework for the $1.75tn reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 The president released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/28/biden-spending-bill-framework-childcare-climate-crisis-whats-in-it-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the framework}}}\uc2  yesterday just before leaving for his week-long trip to Europe. The proposal includes $555bn to invest in climate initiatives and $400bn to expand access to prekindergarten and affordable childcare.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur statement regarding a vote on the infrastructure bill and the Build Back Better Act ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Hu0KGh3UYv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Hu0KGh3UYv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Progressive Caucus (@USProgressives) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USProgressives/status/1453834563424329728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Congressional Progressive Caucus just overwhelmingly voted to endorse, in principle, the entire Build Back Better Act framework announced by President Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D CPC chair \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  said in a statement yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is that while talks around the infrastructure bill lasted months in the Senate, there has only been serious discussion around the specifics of the larger Build Back Better Act in recent weeks, thanks to the Progressive Caucus holding the line and putting both parts of the agenda back on the table. Now, Congress needs to finish the job and bring both bills to a vote together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So it is looking more and more likely that Democrats will be able to pass both the reconciliation package and the infrastructure bill, but it remains unclear when they will be able to do so.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211029ehat001uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
