\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Guardian view on US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws: freedoms hanging by a thread\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 607 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2021\par 17:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 By allowing the Texas law banning abortions after six weeks to stand, the supreme court has joined the attack\par \par \uc2 The announcement by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s new law banning abortions after six weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/22/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be allowed to stand}}}\uc2 , until it hears the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s case against it on 1 November, was a blow to anyone hoping that the court might block attempts to remove women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The 1973 decision that established this right, Roe v Wade, is a landmark in the history of the court.\par \par \uc2 The challenge brought by the Biden administration aims to overturn the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/02/the-guardian-view-on-the-texas-abortion-ban-this-is-not-the-end"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law}}}\uc2  on grounds that the state has violated the court\u8217\'20\'19s authority. By outsourcing enforcement of its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to private citizens, who since September have been allowed to sue anyone who helps a woman obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Texas legislators have sought \u8220\'20\'1Cto evade the traditional mechanisms for judicial review\u8221\'20\'1D, the suit states. The justice department argues that this is a dangerous precedent with the potential to undermine other supreme court decisions. While some employers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/sf/article/In-wake-of-Texas-abortion-law-Benioff-tells-16452020.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering to relocate}}}\uc2  staff to other states, the women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/blog/2021/texass-new-abortion-law-will-harm-people-color-further-entrench-racist-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most likely to be harmed}}}\uc2  by the ban are the poorest and least mobile, who in Texas are disproportionately women of colour.\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/10/19/supreme-court-gets-second-chance-texas-abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should rule in the administration\u8217\'20\'19s favour}}}\uc2 , and should have taken the opportunity to block the law in the interim. By framing their ban as they did, Texas legislators have brazenly gamed the system. Unlike in other countries that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there are no exemptions for pregnancies that result from rape or incest, or for teenage girls. Nor is there any special provision for foetal anomalies, although the limit of six weeks after conception \u8211\'20\'13 before many women know that they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 is in any case so early as to make such diagnoses impossible. The current situation in Texas, with vigilantes able to seek bounties of $10,000 if they bring lawsuits, makes the state one of the most oppressive jurisdictions for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights in the world.\par \par \uc2 Whatever happens next month, the stage is already set for a further confrontation. In December, the supreme court will hear another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization. This challenges a ban on abortions after 15 weeks imposed in Mississippi in 2018, but subsequently blocked. The case is a crucial test and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/04/us-supreme-court-term-analysis-abortion-gun-rights-credibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority}}}\uc2 , with its three Trump appointees, is widely expected to side with the state.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade enshrined a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to terminate a pregnancy until the point that a foetus can survive outside the womb, currently around 24 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation. For decades, states that oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have worked to undermine this right, with poor and black women far more likely to be caught in legislative traps designed to punish women whose pregnancies do not result in live births. Astonishingly cruel and unjust outcomes have included the imprisonment of women who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/16/policing-pregnancy-miscarriage-corporate-drug-pushers-go-free"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had miscarriages}}}\uc2  claimed by prosecutors to be linked to drug use.\par \par \uc2 American women were in the forefront of feminist activism in the 1960s and 1970s. Increased reproductive freedoms, including access to contraception as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were one of that movement\u8217\'20\'19s great gains. Internationally, the trend remains towards rather than away from a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Argentina}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2019/oct/03/why-irelands-battle-over-abortion-is-far-from-over-anti-abortionists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ireland}}}\uc2  among countries that have liberalised laws. But the US wields vast influence and already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/apr/30/biden-urged-to-repeal-helms-amendment-allow-us-aid-fund-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricts overseas aid}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. The threat to women posed by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  stretches far beyond Texas and Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211025ehap002mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
