\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House votes to hold Bannon in contempt for defying Capitol attack subpoena \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Joan E Greve in Washington and Joanna Walters in New York (earlier) \par \uc2 7,775 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2021\par 23:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 House votes 229-202 with nine Republicans supporting resolutionBiden, staff and Congress continue to negotiate on Build Back BetterTrump to launch social media platform called Truth SocialSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * The House voted to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas issued by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection. The matter will now be referred to the justice department, which will have to determine whether to prosecute Bannon, a former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Nine House Republicans joined all 220 Democrats in supporting the contempt resolution. In addition to \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , who serve on the select committee, seven other House Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2 , \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2 , \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2 , \uc2 John Katko\uc2 , Nancy Mace, Peter Meijer and \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 voted to hold Bannon in criminal contempt.\par \par \uc2 * Cheney delivered an impassioned floor speech encouraging her colleagues to vote for the contempt resolution. Pointing to Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s comments on his podcast the day before and the day of the insurrection, Cheney said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no doubt that Mr Bannon knows far more than what he said on the video \u8230\'20\'26 The American people deserve to hear his testimony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized his commitment to fighting for voting rights a day after Senate Republicans blocked Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Freedom to Vote Act. Speaking at a ceremony marking the 10th anniversary of the commemoration of the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial in Washington, Biden said of enacting national voting rights legislation, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to keep up the fight and get it done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 The presentation outlining the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s new company, Trump Media & Technology Group, is rich with hyperbole, but low on detail.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/truth-social/id1586018825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TRUTH}}}\uc2  is out there, according to known factualness provider \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . On Wednesday the former president, who has been banned from the major social media platforms since January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pss.nucleusemail.com/amplify/v/rPyBQj8n8c?s=e6995e02-7efd-4f24-817e-a3c0e4feb289&utm_medium=email&utm_source=bd8aa48a5-ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=20211021-announcing_trump_media_technology_group&utm_content=ncl-n5dhHnsEgg&_nlid=n5dhHnsEgg&_nsid=e6995e02-7efd-4f24-817e-a3c0e4feb289"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that he will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/donald-trump-truth-social-app-apple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launching his own social media company}}}\uc2  called Truth Social. Although, in typical Trump style, it\u8217\'20\'19s styled TRUTH Social.\par \par \uc2 The network, which from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/truth-social/id1586018825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Apple App Store screengrabs}}}\uc2  looks suspiciously like a clone of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , will open to \u8220\'20\'1Cinvited users\u8221\'20\'1D next month and be rolled out to the public early next year. The app is apparently part of a wider media network called Trump Media & Technology Group (TMTG) that aims to take on the \u8220\'20\'1Cliberal media consortium\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI created TRUTH Social and TMTG to stand up to the tyranny of Big Tech,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a world where the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  has a huge presence on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , yet your favorite American President has been silenced. This is unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for TMTG are extremely ambitious. Not only does he want to take on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he wants to disrupt \uc2 Disney\uc2 , Apple, \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . How exactly is he going to do that? Good question. The 22-page company presentation outlining TMTG\u8217\'20\'19s vision is rich with hyperbole, but low on detail. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the gist:he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/truth-social/id1586018825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TRUTH}}}\uc2  is out there, according to known factualness provider \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . On Wednesday the former president, who has been banned from the major social media platforms since January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pss.nucleusemail.com/amplify/v/rPyBQj8n8c?s=e6995e02-7efd-4f24-817e-a3c0e4feb289&utm_medium=email&utm_source=bd8aa48a5-ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=20211021-announcing_trump_media_technology_group&utm_content=ncl-n5dhHnsEgg&_nlid=n5dhHnsEgg&_nsid=e6995e02-7efd-4f24-817e-a3c0e4feb289"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that he will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/donald-trump-truth-social-app-apple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launching his own social media company}}}\uc2  called Truth Social. Although, in typical Trump style, it\u8217\'20\'19s styled TRUTH Social.\par \par \uc2 The network, which from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/truth-social/id1586018825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Apple App Store screengrabs}}}\uc2  looks suspiciously like a clone of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , will open to \u8220\'20\'1Cinvited users\u8221\'20\'1D next month and be rolled out to the public early next year. The app is apparently part of a wider media network called Trump Media & Technology Group (TMTG) that aims to take on the \u8220\'20\'1Cliberal media consortium\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI created TRUTH Social and TMTG to stand up to the tyranny of Big Tech,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a world where the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  has a huge presence on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , yet your favorite American President has been silenced. This is unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for TMTG are extremely ambitious. Not only does he want to take on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he wants to disrupt \uc2 Disney\uc2 , Apple, \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . How exactly is he going to do that? Good question.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the gist:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/21/trump-truth-social-media-platform-tmtg-presentation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8216\'20\'18non-cancellable\u8217\'20\'19 community: the \u8216\'20\'18truth\u8217\'20\'19 about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s social media platform}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 US border agents engaged in \u8216\'20\'18shocking abuses\u8217\'20\'19 against asylum seekers, report finds\par \par \uc2 Shocking instances of sexual and physical abuse of asylum seekers at the southern US border by federal officers have been uncovered by \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2 , after a years-long battle to wrestle the information from the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  under freedom of information laws.\par \par \uc2 A stash of redacted documents released to the human rights group after six years of legal tussles uncover more than 160 cases of misconduct and abuse by leading government agencies, notably Customs and Border Protection (CBP) and US Border Patrol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/report/2021/10/21/they-treat-you-you-are-worthless/internal-dhs-reports-abuses-us-border-officials#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The papers}}}\uc2  record events between 2016 and 2021 that range from child sexual assault to enforced hunger, threats of rape and brutal detention conditions.\par \par \uc2 Some of the incidents involve alleged criminal activity by federal agents.\par \par \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  said that the documents \u8220\'20\'1Cpaint a picture of DHS as an agency that appears to have normalized shocking abuses at the US border. The US should take urgent and sustained action to stop such abuses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The newly released documents record a case of alleged child sexual abuse reported by a supervisor in the San Francisco asylum office. An asylum officer interviewed \u8220\'20\'1Ca young child who was sexually molested by someone we believe to be a CBP or Border Patrol Officer \u8230\'20\'26 The young girl was forced to undress and touched inappropriately by a guard wearing green\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Border Patrol uniform is green.\par \par \uc2 Another report recounts an incident in 2018 when a male asylum seeker was detained and taken to a detention center in San Ysidro, California. An officer told the man that \u8220\'20\'1Cif he gave him sex, he would be set free\u8221\'20\'1D, and when the detainee refused \u8220\'20\'1Cthe officer swore at him in English and said that he would be locked up as punishment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/21/us-border-agents-shocking-abuses-asylum-seekers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US border agents engaged in \u8216\'20\'18shocking abuses\u8217\'20\'19 against asylum seekers, report finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Negotiations are still under way on the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s social safety net and climate change package \u8211\'20\'13 AKA the reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Kyrsten Sinema has reportedly come on board with some key provisions:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Source familiar ways Sinema "has agreed to provisions in each of President Biden's four proposed revenue categories -- international, domestic corporate, high net worth individuals, and tax enforcement -- providing sufficient revenue to fully pay" for reconciliation package\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1451280793054154762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the West Virginia senator with deep ties to the oil and gas industry, reportedly still remains at odd with his Democratic colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Axios reports that despite a seemingly friendly meeting with Vermont\u8217\'20\'19s Bernie Sanders, Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s vision for the bill remains in conflict with that of other Democrats.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/manchin-sanders-reconciliation-fight-789c8441-fa49-404f-9d36-4adaa8e1d908.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Sen. Jon Tester (D-Mont.), chairman of a Senate Appropriations subcommittee, described the incident as a \u8220\'20\'1Ca difference in opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m comfortable with nothing,\u8217\'20\'19 Bernie said, \u8216\'20\'18We need to do three-and-a-half [trillion dollars].\u8217\'20\'19 The truth is both of them are in different spots.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m comfortable with zero,\u8221\'20\'1D forming a \u8220\'20\'1Czero\u8221\'20\'1D with his thumb and index finger, Tester reiterated, saying he believes the West Virginia Democrat can live with himself if the Senate doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass any of the president\u8217\'20\'19s $2-$3.5 trillion package.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Climate crisis likely to fuel conflicts over water and migration, US analyses say\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  is likely to intensify cross-border clashes, aggravate conflicts over water and migration and cause instability, especially in developing countries, in ways that could threaten global security, the Biden administration warned on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A clutch of simultaneously released reports by the White House, the US intelligence community and the Department of Defense paint a grim picture of the raft of security and humanitarian disasters that could strike at once as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/ng-interactive/2021/oct/14/climate-change-happening-now-stats-graphs-maps-cop26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate disaster}}}\uc2  continues to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/21/language-used-to-describe-the-climate-becoming-more-urgent-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set in}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They warn that rising temperatures and extreme physical effects are likely to lead to conflicts over water and to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/jul/29/guatemala-climate-crisis-migration-drought-famine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the displacement}}}\uc2  of tens of millions of people over the next 30 years, including within the US where sea-level rise, drought and wildfires already menace communities.\par \par \uc2 In one of the more ominous forebodings, US intelligence predicts that new disputes could erupt between countries that seek to protect themselves unilaterally by deploying a strategy known as large-scale {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ucsusa.org/resources/what-solar-geoengineering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 solar geoengineering}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Should a country conclude that international efforts to limit the global temperature increase to 1.5C over pre-industrial levels had failed, it might turn to its own use of geoengineering \u8211\'20\'13 an attempt to cool the planet by reflecting solar rays back to space through the injection of stratospheric aerosols or other risky techniques.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout an international agreement on these technologies, we assess that such a unilateral effort probably would cause blowback,\u8221\'20\'1D the intelligence report said.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/21/climate-crisis-conflicts-water-migration-us-analyses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Climate crisis likely to fuel conflicts over water and migration, US analyses say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The House voted to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas issued by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection. The matter will now be referred to the justice department, which will have to determine whether to prosecute Bannon, a former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Nine House Republicans joined all 220 Democrats in supporting the contempt resolution. In addition to \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , who serve on the select committee, seven other House Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2 , \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2 , \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2 , \uc2 John Katko\uc2 , Nancy Mace, Peter Meijer and \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 voted to hold Bannon in criminal contempt.\par \par \uc2 * Cheney delivered an impassioned floor speech encouraging her colleagues to vote for the contempt resolution. Pointing to Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s comments on his podcast the day before and the day of the insurrection, Cheney said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no doubt that Mr Bannon knows far more than what he said on the video \u8230\'20\'26 The American people deserve to hear his testimony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized his commitment to fighting for voting rights a day after Senate Republicans blocked Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Freedom to Vote Act. Speaking at a ceremony marking the 10th anniversary of the commemoration of the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial in Washington, Biden said of enacting national voting rights legislation, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to keep up the fight and get it done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that the only House member who did not vote on the contempt resolution was \uc2 Greg Pence\uc2 , the brother of former Vice-President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Greg Pence\uc2 , who represents Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s 6th congressional district in the House, previously attracted scrutiny for voting against impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 During the insurrection, rioters chanted \u8220\'20\'1CHang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D over the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to fulfill his constitutional duty of overseeing the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the nine Republicans who voted in support of the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in contempt for defying subpoenas from the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  of Wyoming\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2  of Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2  of Ohio\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2  of Washington\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 John Katko\uc2  of New York\par \par \uc2 * Nancy Mace of South Carolina\par \par \uc2 * Peter Meijer of Michigan\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2  of Michigan\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 House votes to hold Bannon in contempt for defying Capitol attack subpoena\par \par \uc2 It is official: the House has voted to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas issued by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 229 to 202, with all Democrats and nine Republicans supporting the resolution.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House adopted H. Res. 730 - contempt resolution regarding \uc2 Stephen K. Bannon\uc2 's refusal to comply with a subpoena issued by the Select Committee to Investigate the Jan 6th Attack on the US Capitol on a vote of 229-202.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1451280271957970952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The matter will now be referred to the justice department, which will have to determine whether to prosecute Bannon, a former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Testifying before the House judiciary committee earlier today, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said the justice department would fairly review any referral sent by the House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department of justice will do what it always does in such circumstances,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland told the committee. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll apply the facts and the law and make a decision, consistent with the principles of prosecution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 House secures votes to hold Bannon in contempt for defying Capitol attack subpoena\par \par \uc2 The House vote remains open, but the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt has now gained enough support to pass the chamber.\par \par \uc2 As of now, 221 House members, including eight Republicans, have voted to hold the Trump ally in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas issued by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 However, the vote remains open, so the result is not yet official. If the House passes the resolution as expected, the matter will then be referred to the justice department, which will have to determine whether to prosecute Bannon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House vote is still open, but as of now, six Republicans have joined Democrats in supporting the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas from the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 As a reminder, if the House passes the resolution as expected, the matter will then be referred to the justice department, which will have to determine whether to prosecute Bannon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 House votes on measure to hold Bannon in criminal contempt\par \par \uc2 The House is now voting on a measure to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying subpoenas issued by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House is voting NOW on H. Res. 730 - contempt resolution regarding \uc2 Stephen K. Bannon\uc2 's refusal to comply with a subpoena issued by the Select Committee to Investigate the Jan 6th Attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1451271537844264967?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The vote comes after the House completed an hour of debate on the contempt measure, with all but two Republicans denouncing the proposal.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the Democratic chairman of the select committee, accused his Republican colleagues of avoiding the truth and \u8220\'20\'1Cperforming for an audience of one,\u8221\'20\'1D meaning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will be watching the vote closely, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , the other Republican member of the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, joined \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  in endorsing the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: GOP Rep. Adam Kinzinger: "\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  went out of his way to earn this resolution before us and now we must approve it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K39NM7r6C5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/K39NM7r6C5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EPVXRajoFa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EPVXRajoFa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1451268138411102214?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  went out of his way to earn this resolution before us and now we must approve it,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said of the Trump ally\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to comply with the committee\u8217\'20\'19s subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have no doubt that Mr Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s scorn for our subpoena is real. But no one \u8212\'20\'14 and I repeat no one \u8212\'20\'14 is above the law, and we need to hear from him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that Kinzinger was introduced by the Democratic chairman of the select committee, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , and he delivered his remarks from the Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 side of the House chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the House debate on the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in contempt, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  entered an interesting document into the official record.\par \par \uc2 Per CNN, the document submitted by Cheney shows that Republican congressman Jim Banks has been sending letters to government officials, such as interior secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2 , seeking information provided to the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the House floor, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  entered this into the record calling out Jim Banks for sending letters to government agencies claiming he is the ranking member of the 1/6 committee even though he is not on the committee. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/C1OxGeVhXN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/C1OxGeVhXN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Annie Grayer (@AnnieGrayerCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnieGrayerCNN/status/1451263342727806984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In the letter, Banks identifies himself as one of the Republican members chosen by minority leader Kevin McCarthy to serve on the select committee and criticizes \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  for blocking his appointment.\par \par \uc2 However, McCarthy pulled all of his nominees from the committee after Pelosi objected to two of the selections, Banks and Jim Jordan. So Banks is not actually a member of the select committee and yet is still claiming that he has a right to information gathered by the panel.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cheney endorses Bannon contempt measure: Americans 'deserve to hear his testimony'\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , one of just two Republicans serving on the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, encouraged her colleagues to support the resolution to hold \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt for defying the panel\u8217\'20\'19s subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 In her House floor speech during the debate on the resolution, Cheney argued that Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s comments on his podcast the day before and the day of the insurrection were \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking and indefensible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe said all hell is going to break loose. He said, \u8216\'20\'18We are coming in right over the target. This is the point of attack we have always wanted,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney said.\par \par \uc2 enltr"He said all hell is going to break loose. He said, 'We are coming in right over the target,'" Rep. Cheney recalls what \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  said before Jan. 6.\par \par \uc2 "There is no doubt that Mr. Bannon knows far more... There is no doubt that all hell did break loose." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KV94QMnFHY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KV94QMnFHY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1451260904629280772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Wyoming congresswoman lamented that many of her fellow House Republicans, who have staunchly opposed the committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation and the contempt measure, \u8220\'20\'1Cnow seem to have forgotten the danger of the moment, the assault on the Constitution, the assault on our Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, there is no doubt that Mr Bannon knows far more than what he said on the video. There is no doubt that all hell did broke loose. Just ask the scores of brave police officers who were injured that day protecting all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney said.\par \par \uc2 She concluded, \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people deserve to hear his testimony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 If the Democratic-controlled House passes the contempt resolution as expected, the matter will then be referred to the justice department, which will have to decide whether to prosecute \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  for defying congressional subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 Speaking before the House judiciary committee today, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said his department would fairly review any referral sent by the chamber.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department of justice will do what it always does in such circumstances,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll apply the facts and the law and make a decision, consistent with the principles of prosecution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAttorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheJusticeDept?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheJusticeDept}}}\uc2  will follow the law on \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  contempt resolution and the House's referral. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/42JlePxEwJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/42JlePxEwJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1451217531532886024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 House passes procedural measure to advance Bannon contempt resolution\par \par \uc2 The House has cleared a key procedural hurdle in approving a contempt resolution for \uc2 Steven Bannon\uc2 , after the former Trump adviser defied subpoenas from the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The House approved the rule to consider the contempt resolution in a vote of 221 to 205, which fell mostly along party lines.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House adopted H.Res. 727 by a vote of 221-205. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OGpqIZgfqa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OGpqIZgfqa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1451255234379096067?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The House is now beginning up to one hour of debate on the measure, after which the full chamber will vote on whether Bannon should be held in criminal contempt for defying the committee\u8217\'20\'19s subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 The blog will be watching the debate closely, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The state leadership in Texas has asked the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  to leave in place its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law banning}}}\uc2  almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that the official message from Texas also told the justices there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason to rush into the case.\par \par \uc2 The state filed its response Thursday to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/15/texas-abortion-ban-supreme-court-biden-administration-request"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s call}}}\uc2  on the court to block the law, the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  curb in the nation, and rule conclusively this term on the measure\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionality.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s intervention at this early stage, before a federal appeals court has ruled on the law, would be highly unusual but not unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 In its court filing, Texas defended an order by a three-judge panel of the 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals that allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to go back into effect after a lower-court judge put it on hold.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In sum, far from being demonstrably wrong, the Fifth Circuit\u8217\'20\'19s conclusion that Texas is likely to prevail was entirely right,\u8217\'20\'19 the state wrote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8216\'20\'18Roe v Wade is a husk\u8217\'20\'19: anguish and anger in Texas after \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 As Guardian US (with The 19th) has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/15/no-one-wants-to-get-sued-some-abortion-providers-have-stopped-working-in-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  : On 31 August, there were 17 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers serving at the four locations of the Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health clinics in Texas. On 1 September \u8211\'20\'13 the day that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive active \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law went into effect}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 there were just eight.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/15/no-one-wants-to-get-sued-some-abortion-providers-have-stopped-working-in-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Treating us like criminals\u8217\'20\'19: Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban creates chilling effect across state}}}\par \par \uc2 And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this report}}}\uc2  by our Stephanie Kirchgaessner and Jessica Glenza, which outlined: Former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  solicitor general Jonathan Mitchell, who played a pivotal role in designing the legal framework of the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, also argued on behalf of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Texas Right to Life that women would still be able to terminate pregnancies if Roe was overturned by traveling to \u8220\'20\'1Cwealthy pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D states like California and New York with the help of \u8220\'20\'1Ctaxpayer subsidies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen can \u8216\'20\'18control their reproductive lives\u8217\'20\'19 without access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; they can do so by refraining from sexual intercourse,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell wrote in the brief.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women can say no to sex if Roe falls, says architect of Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  pumps brakes on imminent spending package framework deal\par \par \uc2 Another dip on the Capitol Hill roller coaster as latest reports have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/joe-manchin-oil-and-gas-fossil-fuels-senator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative Senator Joe Manchin}}}\uc2  telling reporters he thinks there won\u8217\'20\'19t be an outline deal agreed on the heart of the Build Back Better legislation by tomorrow - despite growing expectations that that had been in reach.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  at the US Capitol on Tuesday this week. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not going to happen anytime soon,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin told reporters following him around in Washington, DC, noting that \u8220\'20\'1Cgood progress\u8221\'20\'1D was being made, as intense negotiations continue, but there is still a lot of detail to be sorted out, Reuters has just reported.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sounded optimistic earlier that there could be a framework deal announced as early as tomorrow. But the Democratic human road block from West Virginia appears once again to be standing in his party\u8217\'20\'19s way.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Democrats are trying to thrash out the size and nature of the flagship spending package, aiming for it to be passed in the Senate on a simple majority vote via the reconciliation process.\par \par \uc2 Originally priced at $3.5tn, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/03/joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema-democrats-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moderate nub}}}\uc2  of Manchin and Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Kyrsten Sinema are instrumental in moves to beat down the top line of wide-ranging investments to expand social programs and attack climate change to less than $2tn at this rate - possibly minus a major element to reduce emissions targets to reduce global heating.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 'We have to keep up the fight and get it done,' Biden says of voting rights legislation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned Republican efforts to enact voting restrictions, describing such attempts at voter suppression as \u8220\'20\'1Cun-American\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president was speaking one day after Senate Republicans blocked Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 Freedom to Vote Act from advancing, dealing another blow to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of enacting national voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to keep up the fight and get it done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his speech at the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial. \u8220\'20\'1CI know the stakes. You know the stakes. This is far from over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden calls voter suppression the most "un-American thing any of us can imagine" and thanks Dr. King Jr.'s son Martin Luther King III for leading marches on voting rights on the anniversary of the 1968 March on Washington. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7lD8KIapPz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7lD8KIapPz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1451236341124116496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden added that his administration was also working to confront \u8220\'20\'1Cthe deep stain on the soul of the nation: hate and white supremacy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president drew a historical line from America\u8217\'20\'19s shameful enslavement of African people to \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  terrorism to the 2017 neo-Nazi rally in Charlottesville and the deadly Capitol insurrection on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe through line is that hate never goes away,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt only hides.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  reflected on Congress\u8217\'20\'19 failure to pass police reform legislation as he spoke at the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The president had hoped to sign the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act by the one-year anniversary of Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s murder at the hands of a white Minneapolis police officer, but that deadline came and went in May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the frustration we all feel that... meaningful police reform in George\u8217\'20\'19s name has still not passed Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 But the president committed to continuing to work to pass the bill, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight\u8217\'20\'19s not anywhere near over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial in Washington, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  emphasized the need to enact national voting rights legislation, as Republican-led legislatures across the country approve voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president, who has been named as the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s point person on voting rights, was speaking one day after Senate Republicans blocked Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 Freedom to Vote Act from advancing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should not have to keep fighting to secure our fundamental rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut fight we must. And fight we will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  spoke before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to commemorate the tenth anniversary of the dedication of the \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  memorial in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker recounted how she was in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital for the March on Washington in 1963 but could not stay for King\u8217\'20\'19s famous \u8220\'20\'1CI Have a Dream\u8221\'20\'1D speech because \u8220\'20\'1CI had to leave to go get married.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said it was \u8220\'20\'1Csuch an occasion to see so many people converging on Washington, DC,\u8221\'20\'1D including her beloved late colleague \uc2 John Lewis\uc2 , the civil rights icon who died last year.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi quoted King\u8217\'20\'19s words, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time to make real the promises of democracy. Now is the time to make justice a reality for all of America\u8217\'20\'19s children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have arrived at the memorial for \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King\uc2  at the Tidal Basin in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The president and the vice-president will soon deliver remarks to mark the tenth anniversary of the dedication of the memorial. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden and Vice President Harris at the MLK memorial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vif53xJlH1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vif53xJlH1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Holland (@steveholland1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steveholland1/status/1451220789869563904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  has addressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2021/10/senator-joe-manchin-democratic-party-exit-plan-biden-infrastructure-deal-exclusive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  that he considered leaving the Democratic party if his demands for the reconciliation package were not met.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on Capitol Hill today, the West Virginia denied threatening to leave the party, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/joe-manchin-democrat-independent-offer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per CBS News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, he acknowledged that he had discussed switching his party affiliation to independent if his stances ever became \u8220\'20\'1Can embarrassment\u8221\'20\'1D for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and fellow Democratic lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing was ever discussed. No one accepted that, and I just said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ll make that offer, if you need it,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said.\par \par \uc2 If Manchin did switch his party affiliation to independent but continued to caucus with Senate Democrats, the party would maintain control of the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi insists reconciliation bill will be 'fully paid for,' despite Sinema's demands\par \par \uc2 This is Joan Greve in Washington, taking over for Joanna Walters.\par \par \uc2 During her press conference, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  also addressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-cut-programs-durations-to-lower-cost-of-social-policy-and-climate-plan-11634747582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that Democratic senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , a crucial vote to get the reconciliation package passed, has voiced criticism of proposals to raise taxes on high-income Americans and corporations.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  asks about Senator Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to increasing corporate and individual taxes rates. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerPelosi}}}\uc2  : "The bill will be fully paid for. The matter is in the hands of our chairs...Her position is well known." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/P2BxcSBzAx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/P2BxcSBzAx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1451206615785484296?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s complaints have raised concerns that the reconciliation package will not be fully paid for, which has been a pivotal selling point for moderate Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bill will be fully paid for, and the matter is in the hands of our chairs of the finance committee and the ways and means committee,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Sinema has conveyed that position to her, the speaker said, \u8220\'20\'1CHer position is well known.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bannon 'had specific knowledge' about Capitol attack before it happened \u8211\'20\'13 Pelosi\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , is covering several major topics that are competing to be top of agenda on Capitol Hill for the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi is looking forward to the House voting this afternoon to advance to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/19/capitol-attack-committee-prosecution-steve-bannon-trump?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next stage}}}\uc2  of holding former Trump aide \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in criminal contempt of Congress, over his defiance of the subpoena issued by the House select committee investigating the run-up to and day of the insurrection at the US Capitol by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . She characterized the storming of Congress on 6 January as an act of \u8220\'20\'1Cdomestic terrorism\u8221\'20\'1D and an attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Cinterfere with the peaceful, constitutional transfer of power\u8221\'20\'1D to the election winner \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  had specific knowledge about the events before they occurred\u8221\'20\'1D and has a lot of evidence \u8220\'20\'1Crelevant to the attack\u8221\'20\'1D, she said, which the committee needed to get to the bottom of in order to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind out the truth\u8221\'20\'1D about the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Pelosi said Democrats on the Hill are \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking great progress\u8221\'20\'1D towards agreeing the framework of the (rapidly shrinking but still huge) social spending bill at the heart of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better legislative agenda relating to infrastructure, social benefits and the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 On climate action, Pelosi said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe point is to reach the goals, the emissions goals of a reduction by 50% by 2030, we have a responsibility not just to meet but to beat the Paris [climate accord of 2015] goals [keeping global heating to no more than 1.5C above pre-industrial levels] and help poor countries with technology and assistance to help them meet their goals... they are paying a big price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Frantic negotiations are taking place over how to meet climate goals since West Virginia senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  said he would not support the climate action policy currently at the heart of the $3.5tn spending bill being chewed over by the House. Pelosi hopes for agreement on the bill framework by House Democrats by tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House judiciary committee chairman, \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , signaled in the way he just addressed the witness, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , that Democrats on the committee are very keen to talk about voting rights, with the New York congressman talking of voting access being \u8220\'20\'1Cunder steady assault\u8221\'20\'1D in the US right now.\par \par \uc2 Nadler brought up the disastrous (for those keen on upholding maximum access to voting rights in America) 2013 supreme court decision, which \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  has called:\par \par \uc2 One of the most consequential rulings in a generation in a case called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/12pdf/12-96_6k47.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shelby county v Holder}}}\uc2 . In a 5-4 vote, the court struck down a formula at the heart of the Voting Rights Act, the landmark 1965 law that required {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/crt/jurisdictions-previously-covered-section-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certain states and}}}\uc2  localities with a history of discrimination against minority voters to get changes cleared by the federal government before they went into effect.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to overstate the significance of this decision. The power of the Voting Rights Act was in the design that the supreme court gutted \u8211\'20\'13 discriminatory voting policies could be blocked before they harmed voters. The law placed the burden of proof on government officials to prove why the changes they were seeking were not discriminatory. Now, voters who are discriminated against now bear the burden of proving they are disenfranchised.\par \par \uc2 Immediately after the decision, Republican lawmakers in Texas and North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 two states previously covered by the law \u8211\'20\'13 moved to enact new voter ID laws and other restrictions. A federal court would later strike down the North Carolina law, writing it was designed to target African Americans \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/wonk/wp/2016/07/29/the-smoking-gun-proving-north-carolina-republicans-tried-to-disenfranchise-black-voters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with almost surgical precision}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe scope of what, frankly, the right could do, in a pre-Shelby world was very limited. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s not so limited,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bryan Sells, a voting rights attorney in Georgia. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I\u8217\'20\'19m a Republican political consultant or strategist, the options that are available to me are now wider than they used to be... It made it more advantageous to tinker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s becoming clear that Republicans on the panel don\u8217\'20\'19t want to talk about this and, based on what Jim Jordan and \uc2 Steve Chabot\uc2 , both Ohio congressmen, have said so far, they want to talk about raging educational policy wars over who should have greater say about what children are taught in schools \u8211\'20\'13 the school/education authority or the parents.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a lively hearing. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is holding her weekly press conference on Capitol Hill now, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll tune into that, too, and see what the House speaker has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The appearance of attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrick Garland}}}\uc2  in front of the House judiciary committee is underway.\par \par \uc2 There was initial chaos with a spat between chair \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2  (Democrat of New York) and Republican Jim Jordan, but Garland is speaking now to give his opening remarks.\par \par \uc2 We will bring you any prominent points that emerge, but if you want to follow the entire hearing live, you can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/calendar/eventsingle.aspx?EventID=4744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watch it here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outrage over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/senate-republicans-voting-rights-bill-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lack of progress}}}\uc2  on voting rights legislation to protect voting access, specifically for Black voters, continues \u8211\'20\'13 and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 There is fury from grassroots group Black Voters Matter, founded by LaTosha Brown, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/georgia-senate-runoff-black-voters-stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 instrumental}}}\uc2  in getting out the Black vote in Georgia in the November 2020 presidential election and, in particular, in the Senate runoff races that followed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAgain, these voter suppression bills are not about voter fraud, they\u8217\'20\'19re about historic Black voter turnout. We need action from the Senate. We need more than just words from @POTUS, voting rights need to be a priority. We need to pass federal legislation to protect the vote,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blackvotersmatterfund.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black Voters Matter}}}\uc2  posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrAgain, these voter suppression bills are not about voter fraud, they\u8217\'20\'19re about historic Black voter turnout. We need action from the Senate. We need more than just words from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2 , voting rights need to be a priority. We need to pass federal legislation to protect the vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Black Voters Matter (@BlackVotersMtr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BlackVotersMtr/status/1450830740489482240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , who narrowly lost the contest to become governor of Georgia and has campaigned hard to get out the vote in her state and uphold voting rights, was also key in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/14/electoral-college-joe-biden-donald-trump-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 election}}}\uc2  and the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/georgia-senate-runoff-black-voters-stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 runoff races}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She tweeted outrage at Republicans blocking yesterday what she called \u8220\'20\'1Cwidely popular legislation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Rs again demonstrated their penchant for obstructionism. Instead of working with their colleagues toward progress on the freedom to vote, they refused to allow debate on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FreedomToVoteAct?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FreedomToVoteAct}}}\uc2 . Our work continues as we urge Senators to pass this widely popular legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  (@staceyabrams) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/staceyabrams/status/1450912055469527049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the advocacy group \uc2 Common Cause\uc2 , which acts as an unofficial watchdog on government action and supports wider voting rights, had a number of pointed comments.\par \par \uc2 enltrHi ???? I\u8217\'20\'19m Dani, an organizer for \uc2 Common Cause\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19ve met thousands of voters who support the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FreedomToVoteAct?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FreedomToVoteAct}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the grassroots support for voting rights grow every day [a thread??] {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zGojcSFQa7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zGojcSFQa7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Common Cause\uc2  (@CommonCause) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CommonCause/status/1450849763654504449?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 And, a little earlier, this:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FreedomToVoteAct?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FreedomToVoteAct}}}\uc2  will remove the obstacles designed to silence Black, Indigenous, young and new Americans, ensuring that each of us has an equal say in the decisions that impact our lives. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6JSrhKOOud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6JSrhKOOud}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Common Cause\uc2  (@CommonCause) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CommonCause/status/1450849782457581570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 NAACP\uc2 's Ifill on dangers of voting rights legislation stalling\par \par \uc2 There is furious reaction to stalled attempts to protect voting rights in the US with new laws at the federal level, in the face of determined and brazen efforts by some Republican-led states to suppress the scope to vote, in particular affecting Black voters in non-urban and/or low income communities.\par \par \uc2 US Senate\uc2  Republicans once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/senate-republicans-voting-rights-bill-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked voting rights legislation}}}\uc2  yesterday.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine writes:\par \par \uc2 The bill, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/117/bills/s2747/BILLS-117s2747pcs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Freedom to Vote Act}}}\uc2 , would impose significant new guardrails on the American democratic process and amount to the most significant overhaul of US elections in a generation. It would require every state to automatically register voters at motor vehicle agencies, offer 15 consecutive days of early voting and allow anyone to request a mail-in ballot. It would also set new standards to ensure voters are not wrongfully removed from the voter rolls, protect election officials against partisan interference, and set out clear alternatives people who lack ID to vote can use at the polls.\par \par \uc2 Sherrilyn Ifill\uc2  , law professor and president and director-counsel of the NAACP Legal Defense Fund, responded on MSNBC. She said she was part of a non-partisan organization, but pointed out there was no getting away from the fact that \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a single Republican\u8221\'20\'1D in the Senate was prepared even to support debating the bill, let alone voting on it. And with filibuster rules requiring 60 Senate votes, Democrats in the 50-50 Senate were not able to advance the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[They were] unwilling to even have the conversation about expanding voter access, and we have seen in states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/06/florida-restrictive-voting-bill-governor-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/27/georgia-governor-painting-slave-plantation-voting-bill-signing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/texas-legislature-voting-restrictions-bill-final-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  what is happening in terms of voter suppression laws that have been passed... restrictive laws targeted at Black and brown voters over the objections of almost every Democrat in those legislatures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change what it is...the reality of what we are dealing with is no different than the reality of what Black voters were dealing with in 1964 and we don\u8217\'20\'19t look back at the great voting rights effort and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/07/amelia-boynton-selma-anniversary-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Selma march}}}\uc2  and say the Democrats were doing this or the Republicans were doing that, we look back and recognize that voter suppression was being perpetuated and advanced to keep fellow citizens from being able to vote and participate in the democratic process today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ifill went on to say that some of the media finds it too convenient to talk about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-fight-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting rights struggles}}}\uc2  now in partisan terms:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd not to confront the racial discrimination that lies at the heart of it. But the voting Right Act talks about Black voters having the right to elect their candidate of choice, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t say who that candidate is or what party they belong to... the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/19/texas-republicans-approve-redrawn-maps-decreasing-representation-minority-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maps that are being drawn}}}\uc2 ... voter suppression laws that are being passed are targeted very specifically at Black and brown voters and that\u8217\'20\'19s the conversation we need to be having... that is the sign that white supremacy still remains a critical flaw in our democracy... it has come to take down our entire democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ICYMI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ICYMI}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sifill_LDF?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Sifill_LDF}}}\uc2  joined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/allinwithchris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @allinwithchris}}}\uc2  on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MSNBC}}}\uc2  to discuss the Freedom to Vote Act's failure to advance in the Senate and what is at stake for our democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/05QbvKk1G0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/05QbvKk1G0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Legal Defense Fund (@NAACP_LDF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NAACP_LDF/status/1451156621325971462?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Republican secretary of state Condoleezza Rice shocked many when she said on ABC that it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime to move on\u8221\'20\'1D from investigating the 6 January Capitol attack when extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stormed Congress in an effort, ostensibly, to stop lawmakers from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certifying}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election victory}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rice told The View yesterday that she wept as she watched rioters breaking into the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and stalking the halls, attacking police officers, invading the chambers and looking for lawmakers and staff to hurt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought: \u8216\'20\'18I study countries that do this. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t think it would happen in my own country,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she said and the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/10/21/condoleezza-rice-the-view-capitol-riot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She said the attack \u8220\'20\'1Cwas wrong\u8221\'20\'1D but then said of the ongoing House investigation into the background to the insurrection, and what the Trump White House, aides and Republican lawmakers knew and did in the run-up and on the day, that it was time to move on.\par \par \uc2 enltrSec. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CondoleezzaRice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CondoleezzaRice}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1COur institutions have to be upheld.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happened on January 6th was wrong. I also know that as a government and as a country, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be concerned about the things that are making life hard for Americans and hard for American families.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GGA3FGfu3J"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GGA3FGfu3J}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The View (@TheView) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheView/status/1450848918540111875?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Post points out:\par \par \uc2 [Rice\u8217\'20\'19s] comments were a response in agreement to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheView/status/1450990218371223560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarks}}}\uc2  Senate Minority Leader Mitch McConnell (R-Ky.) gave on Tuesday. McConnell told reporters it was time for lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Cto be talking about the future and not the past,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the discussion about false claims of election fraud pushed by Trump and his allies, which ultimately led supporters to storm the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  on Jan. 6. McConnell said the issue should no longer be of concern...\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the House\u8217\'20\'19s Jan. 6 committee is moving ahead on the investigation into the insurrection. Over the past few weeks, lawmakers subpoenaed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/jan6-committee-subpoenas-rally-planners/2021/09/29/8c73eb68-216a-11ec-b3d6-8cdebe60d3e2_story.html?itid=lk_inline_manual_11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizers of the pro-Trump rallies}}}\uc2  that preceded the riot and several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/10/13/jan-6-subpoenas/?itid=lk_inline_manual_11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former Trump advisers}}}\uc2 . Among them was \uc2 Stephen K. Bannon\uc2 , who last week refused to comply with the subpoena. The committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/house-jan-6-committee-to-vote-to-hold-bannon-in-contempt/2021/10/19/cc0e836a-3104-11ec-a1e5-07223c50280a_story.html?itid=lk_inline_manual_11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unanimously voted Tuesday}}}\uc2  to hold the former adviser in contempt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 House to vote on holding \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  in contempt over Capitol attack evidence\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers, on a big day in a crucial week in Washington for Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration there is a lot going on, so tune in as we bring you all the developments in short order.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s are some of the main items on the docket today:\par \par \uc2 * The House is due to vote this afternoon on whether to recommend the prosecution of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , former top aide to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , for criminal contempt of Congress for defying the subpoena issued by the bipartisan select committee investigating the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insurrection at the US Capitol}}}\uc2  on 6 January by extremist Trump supporters. If, as expected, the House votes to do so, the next stage involves federal prosecutors, as part of the Department of Justice (DoJ), deciding whether to prosecute. The House vote follows the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/19/capitol-attack-committee-prosecution-steve-bannon-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unanimous select committee vote}}}\uc2  two days ago.\par \par \uc2 * US attorney generalMerrick Garlandwill testify in front of the House judiciary committee from 10am ET and can expect questions from members of Congress on taking actions over defiance of Jan 6 committee subpoenas (also issued to other former top aides of Trump). Garland will also be asked about DoJ efforts - unsuccessful so far - to stop the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/18/biden-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Frantic negotiations between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , top staff and members of Congress to reach a deal on an outline agreement to pass the flagship Build Back Better legislation package, amid a mix of acrimony and determined optimism (a heady Capitol Hill cocktail). Biden is racing to find a way to preserve his climate action agenda ahead of going to Scotland next week to represent the US at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/cop26-glasgow-climate-change-conference-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cop26}}}\uc2  United Nations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 * The fall-out continues from the failure of Democrats to advance voting rights legislation, after Senate Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/20/senate-republicans-voting-rights-bill-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again blocked}}}\uc2  a sweeping voting rights bill yesterday day, a move that will significantly increase pressure on the Biden administration to do away with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/30/what-is-filibuster-meaning-republicans-blocking-biden-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the filibuster}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  heads to Virginia to campaign for Democrat \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  who is neck-and-neck with his Republican rival for the governorship of that state in next month\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial election.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is launching a social media platform. Yep.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211021ehal0020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
