\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The legal mind behind America\u8217\'20\'19s most extreme  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma in Austin \par \uc2 1,849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2021\par 20:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former Texas solicitor general Jonathan F Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 legal strategy lets legislators pass laws that thwart the judiciary\par \par \uc2 At the center of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme}}}\uc2  Texas law that bans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly all}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the second largest state in the US lies a novel legal provision that allows any private citizen to act as vigilantes and sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure. While a federal judge temporarily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/TX-SB-8-DOJ-PI.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  Senate Bill 8 on Wednesday, after 36 days in effect, the fifth circuit court of appeals temporarily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/08/texas-abortion-ban-temporarily-reinstated-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restored}}}\uc2  the law late Friday.\par \par \uc2 In a lawsuit against the measure, the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/21062495/9-14-21-us-motion-for-tro-pi-texas-sb8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Senate Bill 8 an \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented scheme\u8221\'20\'1D designed with the specific objective of evading judicial review of its unconstitutionality. But who crafted this dangerous legal strategy?\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, Texas Right to Life, an influential organization that heavily lobbied for SB8, says it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cteam effort\u8221\'20\'1D from within the state that included players like the Republican state senator \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2 . But a less obvious figure was also working behind the scenes: the organization confirmed that the former Texas solicitor general Jonathan F Mitchell was \u8220\'20\'1Cinstrumental\u8221\'20\'1D in crafting the law\u8217\'20\'19s legal provision.\par \par \uc2 Dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/07/18/business/economy/union-fees-lawyer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brilliant legal mind}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D by a lawyer who worked with him in an anti-union case, Mitchell, a 45-year-old private attorney with ties to the conservative \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  and \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 , has a long history of defending culture war and religious-right legal challenges, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, anti-LGBTQ rights, anti-union and anti-affirmative action lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 Based on court documents, legal experts and his own writings, Mitchell promotes a controversial and some say \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D legal strategy that seeks to thwart judicial review and grant Republican state lawmakers maximum power. With Roe v Wade in the crosshairs \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to hear a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jul/23/abortion-us-supreme-court-mississippi-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi case}}}\uc2  that challenges a 15-week ban this term \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights appears to be an ideal testing ground to promote his legal ideology.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear that Mitchell and allies want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright through their own legal scheme,\u8221\'20\'1D says Amanda Williams, executive director of the Lilith Fund, which is among the groups fighting SB8.\par \par \uc2 A driving force\par \par \uc2 A 2001 graduate of \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  Law School, Mitchell has a formidable r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 that includes a clerkship with the late Justice \uc2 Antonin Scalia\uc2 , a visiting professorship at Stanford Law School, time as an adjunct professor at the University of Texas School of Law, and a role with the justice department under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 . A figure largely out of the public eye, Mitchell declined to be interviewed for this story.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, Mitchell set his sights on landing a federal job under the Trump administration. Mitchell served as a volunteer attorney for the Trump presidential transition team, and the former president sought to nominate him to chair the Administrative Conference of the United States in 2017. However, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/6590185-Whitehouse-Letter-to-Jonathan-F-Mitchell.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  concerns about impartiality}}}\uc2  from the Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse, he failed to secure confirmation.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell is no stranger to defending Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and the state\u8217\'20\'19s ideologically driven reproductive health policies. As solicitor general from 2010 to 2015 he helped uphold an onerous 24-hour pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sonogram law; a decision to kick 50,000 low-income {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.expressnews.com/news/local_news/article/A-lose-lose-for-Planned-Parenthood-3501635.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood patients}}}\uc2  from a Medicaid program; and an omnibus 2013 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/article/2013/10/22/on-first-day-of-texas-abortion-law-trial-state-asserts-interest-in-protecting-unborn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  that in effect shuttered half the state\u8217\'20\'19s clinics before being struck down by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 2016.\par \par \uc2 He continued to defend anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views after his term: in 2019, he represented a former Austin council member who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/zimmerman-v-city-of-austin-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the city}}}\uc2  for investing funds in logistical care for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and east Texas activists who wished to deem \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund groups \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, Mitchell has spent considerable time defending the \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D ordinance \u8211\'20\'13 the blueprint for SB8. With no exception for rape or incest, the municipal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://library.municode.com/tx/rusk/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=TITIXGERE_CH103AB_S103.05PREN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordinances}}}\uc2  allow any \u8220\'20\'1Csurviving relative of the aborted unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or someone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in civil court. Since 2019, the movement has grown to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanctuarycitiesfortheunborn.org/sanctuary-cities-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 37 towns}}}\uc2 , including cities in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/555546-ohio-city-bans-all-abortions-declares-itself-a-sanctuary-city-for-the"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Ohio}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1011now.com/2021/04/15/blue-hill-is-second-nebraska-town-to-outlaw-abortion-in-city-limits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Nebraska}}}\uc2 . While largely symbolic (most of the towns had no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to begin with), in June the movement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/06/01/abortion-planned-parenthood-lubbock/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successfully halted}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in Lubbock, Texas, the largest city to pass the ordinance.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell also represents Mark Lee Dickson \u8211\'20\'13 leader of the \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D movement \u8211\'20\'13 in both a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.news-journal.com/news/local/defamation-lawsuit-filed-against-right-to-life-east-texas-its-director/article_8e100ec6-3a8b-5653-81d5-e92bfbfbccac.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defamation case}}}\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support groups fighting the ordinances and in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/texas-abortion-ban-lawsuit-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 larger legal challenge}}}\uc2  filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers against SB8. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.news-journal.com/news/local/waskom-makes-amendments-to-abortion-ban-ordinance/article_81f33d08-fade-550f-9a31-ea6cac0dd38a.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also represented}}}\uc2 , without cost to the taxpayer, the first seven east Texas towns to pass the ordinance against suit from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund groups. In a phone interview with the Guardian, Dickson called Mitchell a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood guy\u8221\'20\'1D who did an \u8220\'20\'1Cexcellent job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal battles aren\u8217\'20\'19t confined to reproductive rights. A legal crusader against LGBTQ protections, Mitchell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberglaw.com/public/desktop/document/BarbervBryant860F3d3455thCir2017CourtOpinion?1631285256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  businesses who wished to fire employees based on sexual orientation and fought against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/article/2018/10/19/trump-nominee-leads-three-pronged-attack-on-laws-protecting-lgbtq-residents-of-austin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 local protections}}}\uc2  for LGBTQ residents in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell is also the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/07/18/business/economy/union-fees-lawyer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 driving force}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D behind anti-union litigation, filing 21 class-action {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2019/12/23/union-lawsuits-janus-juris-capital/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuits}}}\uc2  against unions over two years in multiple states. And he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicagomaroon.com/article/2019/1/14/uchicago-law-grad-sues-harvard-nyu-law-reviews-all/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represents}}}\uc2  anti-affirmative action suits against the Harvard and NYU Law Reviews that allege bias against white men. The publications engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Crace and sex discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D by giving preference to articles written by women or racial minorities, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.law.com/contrib/content/uploads/documents/292/Faculty_Alumni_and_Students_Opposed_v_Harvard_Law_Review_et_al__madce-18-12105__0001.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suit reads}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The answer to who has funded Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal work has been somewhat elusive. His funds appear to come in part from rightwing and conservative firms including the Thomas More Society; Texas Alliance for Life; Texas Values; and the conservative thinktank the Hoover Institute, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/4388347-Jonathan-F-Mitchell-Financial-Disclosure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial records}}}\uc2  that account for income from 2015 to 2017. In 2019, the powerful conservative religious law group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/display_990/541660459/05_2021_prefixes_54-56%2F541660459_202006_990_2021051818121539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom}}}\uc2  began paying Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s law firm more than $36,000 for services listed as \u8220\'20\'1Creligious freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian previously reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Deeply nihilistic\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s work on defending Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws offers a glimpse into his legal ideology: in those cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scribd.com/document/525249243/Mitchell-Case-2020-Blackwell-v-Lilith-Fund-Petition-FINAL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he argued}}}\uc2  that because Texas has never officially repealed its pre-Roe v Wade statutes that outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , clients should be able to consider the laws largely enforceable. \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s judgment in [Roe] did not cancel or formally revoke the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statutes, and the judiciary has no power to erase a statute that it believes to be unconstitutional,\u8221\'20\'1D he writes.\par \par \uc2 This falls in line with Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s general belief that the judiciary is afforded an all too powerful \u8211\'20\'13 and misunderstood \u8211\'20\'13 role in the public eye. He critiques what he believes is the widespread public misconception of the federal court\u8217\'20\'19s powers, especially when the court \u8220\'20\'1Cblocks\u8221\'20\'1D a law. \u8220\'20\'1CThe judicially disapproved statute continues to exist as a law until it is repealed by the legislature that enacted it, even as it goes unenforced\u8221\'20\'1D by the judiciary or the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 The latest Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, SB8, can be seen as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect reflection\u8221\'20\'1D of Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal philosophy, says Mary Ziegler, a law professor at Florida State University and the author of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Law in America: Roe v Wade to the Present. For instance, using the term \u8220\'20\'1Caiding or abetting,\u8221\'20\'1D which is typically criminal law language, rather than civil, signals that the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Roe didn\u8217\'20\'19t ever invalidate Texas\u8217\'20\'19s criminal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which remains on the books \u8211\'20\'13 it simply meant they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t enforce it.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell seeks to encourage legislators to create laws that could be better shielded from court challenges. In his 2018 legal essay, the Writ of Erasure Fallacy, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3158038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  that legislators can \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide for private enforcement of the statute authorizing civil lawsuits [\u8230\'20\'26] These mechanisms are especially powerful because they enable private litigants to enforce a statute even after a federal district court has enjoined the executive from enforcing it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justsecurity.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/lawsuit-doj.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  against Texas to stop SB8, the US DoJ cites Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s essay as proof that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\u8217\'20\'19s architect intended to stymie judicial review.\par \par \uc2 Steve Vladeck, a University of Texas Law School professor who specializes in federal courts, says Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal views are \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply nihilistic\u8221\'20\'1D. While his attempt to elucidate the judiciary\u8217\'20\'19s role is helpful, he \u8220\'20\'1Cexploits\u8221\'20\'1D the analysis to make constitutional rights \u8220\'20\'1Cdependent on the whims\u8221\'20\'1D of state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt empowers states to deprive their citizens of the most clearly established and unassailable rights,\u8221\'20\'1D says Vladeck. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly dangerous \u8211\'20\'13 if our constitutional rights are only as good as state legislatures choose to allow them to be, then they are not worth anything. It promotes the tyranny of the majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal idea can be applied to anything from \u8220\'20\'1Ccampaign finance law, to a gun-control measure \u8230\'20\'26 to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation,\u8221\'20\'1D he writes. While states pass increasingly onerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  appears poised to chip away at Roe this term, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are tenuous and ripe for testing.\par \par \uc2 And Texas could be considered a perfect breeding ground: the Republican-dominated Texas legislature, which easily passed some of the most draconian \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the US, finds an ally in the largely conservative fifth circuit court of appeals and a supreme court now stacked with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  justices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMitchell uses his intellectual ability to push for fairly significant and radical changes in legal doctrine \u8211\'20\'13 and I can\u8217\'20\'19t see how it is not ideologically motivated,\u8221\'20\'1D says Vladeck. \u8220\'20\'1CEven if you feel so justly in a cause, how do you reconcile the fact you are inflicting so much harm on so many?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ziegler is familiar with Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s legal ideology. As a historian of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement, she considers him a figure who \u8220\'20\'1Cinterestingly bridges the gap between the old school legal elite and populist elements dominating the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8221\'20\'1D. He deviates from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s recent affinity for the judicial system, she says, making his approach different.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSB8 is a radical expansion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the past, states have had concern about cost and consequences when they lose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  court battles. Now, Texas has a \u8216\'20\'18have your cake and eat it too\u8217\'20\'19 approach with this law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That legal scheme appears poised to spread across the US: considering the success of the Texas-based approach, GOP officials in 11 other states including Arkansas, Mississippi, Indiana and North Dakota have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/03/texas-abortion-republicans-six-states-arkansas-florida-indiana-mississippi-north-south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed interest}}}\uc2  in adopting similar measures. A Florida Republican lawmaker recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/09/23/1040132587/florida-abortion-restriction-bill-texas-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  an SB8-like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that would place enforcement in the hands of private citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are horrified to see anti-choice politicians in Florida following in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s footsteps, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no question that lawmakers hostile to reproductive freedom in other states will do the same,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/2021/09/22/naral-pro-choice-america-condems-sb8-copycat-bill-out-of-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Adrienne Kimmell, acting president of Naral Pro-Choice America. \u8220\'20\'1CThe harm of these draconian attacks cannot be overstated and they most acutely impact those who already face the greatest barriers to accessing care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211010ehaa000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
