\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Capitol attack committee considers criminal contempt referral for \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano (now) and Vivian Ho (earlier) \par \uc2 6,418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2021\par 00:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bannon told investigators he would not cooperate with subpoenaDocuments contradict Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims hotel made tens of millionsUS adds 194,000 September jobs, a month of disappointing growthDebt ceiling measure heads to the House as partisan tensions flareSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directed four of his former aides \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , former social media czar Dan Scavino, former defense department official Kash Patel and former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to ignore subpoenas from the House select committee tasked with investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol. He later sent a letter to the National Archives indicating that he wished to assert executive privilege over the documents in question, a power only the person in office can wield. That person, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has since said that he plans to waive that privilege for this set of documents.\par \par \uc2 * Bannon, meanwhile, has informed the House committee that he will not be cooperating with their subpoena. Committee chair Bennie Thompson and vice chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  say they \u8220\'20\'1Cwill swiftly consider advancing a criminal contempt of Congress referral\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * In more Trump news, the House oversight committee revealed today that the Trump International Hotel Washington DC lost almost $74m during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, even while he publicly claimed it was making tens of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became the first president to issue a proclamation commemorating Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day on 11 October, but he also issued a proclamation commemorating Columbus Day on that same day. Still, it\u8217\'20\'19s a significant boost in a nationwide movement to replace a federal holiday that Indigenous rights groups believe overlooks the violent history that followed the Italian explorer\u8217\'20\'19s 1492 arrival in the Americas with one celebrating the contributions of Indigenous people.\par \par \uc2 * The justice department announced Friday that it would not file federal charges against the white police officer who shot and paralyzed Jacob Blake in Kenosha, Wisconsin, last year.\par \par \uc2 * Texas has asked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cdn.cnn.com/cnn/2021/images/10/08/texas.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fifth circuit court of appeals}}}\uc2  to restore the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2021/oct/06/texas-abortion-ban-temporary-block-us-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  the law on Wednesday. The new law banned most abortions in the state and until this week had managed to withstand a wave of early challenges.\par \par \uc2 -Vivian Ho and Dani Anguiano\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 A new Senate report released Thursday offers alarming details on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Trump and \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the White House chief of staff, pressed \uc2 Jeffrey Rosen\uc2 , the acting attorney general, and top DoJ officials to pursue allegations of election fraud, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine on the key takeaways from the report:\par \par \uc2 Trump pressured the justice department to file a lawsuit in the supreme court seeking to invalidate the election results in six states\par \par \uc2 In late December, Trump asked the justice department to take the highly unusual step of filing an election lawsuit directly in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Supreme Court}}}\uc2 . The suit would have asked the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/Interim%20Staff%20Report%20FINAL.pdf#page=27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to nullify}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election victories}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Michigan, Wisconsin, Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 The solicitor general\u8217\'20\'19s office (OSG) and the office of legal counsel (OLC) prepared memos explaining why the department could not file a lawsuit. \u8220\'20\'1CAmong other hurdles, OSG explained that DOJ could not file an original supreme court action for the benefit of a political candidate,\u8221\'20\'1D the senate report says.\par \par \uc2 A plain-English memo from OLC was more blunt. \u8220\'20\'1C[T]here is no legal basis to bring this lawsuit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/08/department-of-justice-report-key-takeaways-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Can you believe this?\u8217\'20\'19: key takeaways from the report on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to steal the election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Texas asks court to reinstate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Texas has asked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://cdn.cnn.com/cnn/2021/images/10/08/texas.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fifth circuit court of appeals}}}\uc2  to restore the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/06/texas-abortion-ban-temporary-block-us-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  the law on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no precedent for the district court\u8217\'20\'19s injunction; it grossly and irreparably interferes with Texas state-court operations,\u8221\'20\'1D the state said in a filing.\par \par \uc2 The new law, signed by Republican governor Greg Abbott in May, banned most abortions in the state and until this week had managed to withstand a wave of early challenges. It bans the procedures once cardiac activity is detected, which can occur as early as six weeks, and makes no exceptions for rape or incest. The law also allows private citizens to sue anyone they suspect of \u8220\'20\'1Caiding or abetting\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A supporter of reproductive rights holds a sign outside the Texas state capitol, 2 October. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The judge who blocked the law earlier this week said it unlawfully prevented women \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom exercising control over their lives in ways that are protected by the constitution\u8221\'20\'1D. Local service providers have said that Texas clinics are in danger of closing while other states are struggling to keep up with a surge of new patients from Texas.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law, which has set up the biggest test of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US in decades, is part of a broader push by Republicans to restrict and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans sow disinformation after $480bn US debt ceiling deal\par \par \uc2 Top {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in the Senate are advancing a campaign of disinformation over the debt ceiling as they seek to distort the reasons for needing to raise the nation\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing cap, after they dropped their blockade on averting a US debt default in a bipartisan manner.\par \par \uc2 The Senate on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/07/debt-ceiling-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a bill}}}\uc2  to allow the debt ceiling to be raised by $480bn through early December, which the treasury department estimates will be enough to allow the government to temporarily avert an unprecedented default on $28tn of debt obligations.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, Chuck Schumer, announced the morning before its passage that he had reached a deal with the Republican Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , to clear the way for the vote on a short-term extension with GOP support.\par \par \uc2 The movement came after McConnell made a tactical retreat to back down from weeks of refusal to allow Democrats to raise the debt ceiling by any measure other than through a complicated procedure known as reconciliation that would have required a party-line vote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/08/senate-republicans-us-debt-ceiling-deal-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans sow disinformation after $480bn US debt ceiling deal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hi everyone. Dani Anguiano taking over our US politics live blog for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 The justice department announced Friday that it would not file federal charges against the white police officer who shot and paralyzed Jacob Blake in Kenosha, Wisconsin, last year. That officer, Rusten Sheskey, was not charged by local prosecutors in the incident and returned to duty earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter a careful and thorough review, a team of experienced federal prosecutors determined that insufficient evidence exists to prove beyond a reasonable doubt that the KPD officer willfully violated the federal criminal civil rights statutes,\u8221\'20\'1D the justice department said in a press release.\par \par \uc2 Blake, a Black man, was shot seven times as officers tried to arrest him on an outstanding warrant. He has not been able to walk since, but said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/29/jacob-blake-jr-paralysed-kenosha-police-shooting-walk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expects}}}\uc2  to do so soon. The shooting, which occurred just months after George Floyd was killed by police in Minnesota, sparked several nights of chaotic protests. During one of those protests, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/20/kyle-rittenhouse-kenosha-shooting-bail-release"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kyle Rittenhouse}}}\uc2 , an Illinois teen, shot three people, killing two.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/08/jacob-blake-police-shooting-kenosha-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No federal charges against officer who shot and paralyzed Jacob Blake}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directed four of his former aides \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , former social media czar Dan Scavino, former defense department official Kash Patel and former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to ignore subpoenas from the House select committee tasked with investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol. He later sent a letter to the National Archives indicating that he wished to assert executive privilege over the documents in question, a power only the person in office can wield. That person, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has since said that he plans to waive that privilege for this set of documents.\par \par \uc2 * Bannon, meanwhile, has full-on informed the House committee that he will not be cooperating with their subpoena. Committee chair Bennie Thompson and vice chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  say they \u8220\'20\'1Cwill swiftly consider advancing a criminal contempt of Congress referral\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * In more Trump news, the House oversight committee revealed today that the Trump International Hotel Washington DC lost almost $74m during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, even while he publicly claimed it was making tens of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became the first president to issue a proclamation commemorating Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day on 11 October, but he also issued a proclamation commemorating Columbus Day on that same day. Still, it\u8217\'20\'19s a significant boost in a nationwide movement to replace a federal holiday that Indigenous rights groups believe overlooks the violent history that followed the Italian explorer\u8217\'20\'19s 1492 arrival in the Americas with one celebrating the contributions of Native Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has issued a lengthy statement regarding the records sought by the House select committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol \u8211\'20\'13 and his failed efforts to withhold them by asserting executive privilege, a power only the person currently in office can wield and in this case has decided to waive.\par \par \uc2 He claims he sent a letter to the National Archives in defense of the office of the presidency and the constitution, among other things. He said the investigation into the attack of the US Capitol was about \u8220\'20\'1Cusing the power of the government to silence \u8216\'20\'18Trump\u8217\'20\'19 and our Make American Great Again movement\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 no explanation why Trump is in quotations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy administration, and the great patriots who worked on behalf of the American people, will not be intimidated,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden issues proclamation commemorating Indigenous Peoples' Day\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became the first president today to issue a proclamation commemorating Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, boosting efforts to shift the focus of the federal holiday celebrating Christopher Columbus \u8211\'20\'13 whose arrival in the Americas led to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/oct/08/columbus-day-2018-decline-holiday-donald-trump-proclamation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deaths of countless Indigenous people}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to a celebration of Native Americans and their contributions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, our nation celebrates the invaluable contributions and resilience of Indigenous peoples, recognizes their inherent sovereignty, and commits to honoring the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s trust and treaty obligations to tribal nations,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Indigenous rights groups have maintained that the federal holiday of Columbus Day overlooks the colonialism, enslavement, discrimination and land grabs that followed the Italian explorer\u8217\'20\'19s 1492 arrival in the Americas.\par \par \uc2 More and more cities have begun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/oct/11/indigenous-peoples-day-columbus-day-native-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recognizing Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day on Columbus Day}}}\uc2  in recent years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor generations, general policies systematically sought to assimilate and displace native people and eradicate native cultures,\u8221\'20\'1D the proclamation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2021/10/08/a-proclamation-indigenous-peoples-day-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we recognize Indigenous peoples\u8217\'20\'19 resilience and strength as well as the immeasurable positive impact that they have made on every aspect of American society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden also issued a separate proclamation commemorating Columbus Day \u8211\'20\'13 one that also declares 11 October Columbus Day as well as Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day \u8211\'20\'13 but that proclamation makes a point to acknowledge \u8220\'20\'1Cthe painful history of wrongs and atrocities that many European explorers inflicted on tribal nations and Indigenous communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a measure of our greatness as a nation that we do not seek to bury these shameful episodes of our past \u8211\'20\'13 that we face them honestly, we bring them to the light, and we do all we can to address them,\u8221\'20\'1D the proclamation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2021/10/08/a-proclamation-on-columbus-day-2021/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiospm&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reads}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are unique and extraordinary circumstances,\u8221\'20\'1D White House counsel Dana Remus wrote in a letter to David Ferriero, archivist of the United States, regarding the records sought by the House select committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/10/08/bannon-jan-6-subpoena-515681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a two-page letter}}}\uc2  to the National Archives, indicated on Friday that he wanted to assert executive privilege over 45 documents identified by the National Archives as responsive to the committee\u8217\'20\'19s request.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShould the committee persist in seeking other privileged information, I will take all necessary and appropriate steps to defend the Office of the Presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 However, only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/oct/08/us-debt-ceiling-senate-house-washington-politics-live?page=with:block-61606be28f08b8251d62228d#block-61606be28f08b8251d62228d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the person currently in office}}}\uc2  can declare executive privilege \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump is not currently in office. \u8220\'20\'1CAfter my consultations with the Office of Legal Counsel at the Department of Justice, President Biden has determined that an assertion of executive privilege is not in the best interests of the United States, and therefore is not justified as to any of the documents,\u8221\'20\'1D Remus wrote in a letter obtained by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She noted \u8211\'20\'13 and White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  later confirmed at the press briefing \u8211\'20\'13 that privilege may be evaluated on a \u8220\'20\'1Ccase-by-case basis\u8221\'20\'1D, and some future material may still be protected.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki: "This was a uniquely dark day in our democracy. A day that we need to get to the bottom of."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1446556164880322565?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is at the podium for the press briefing, talking about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his decision to waive executive privilege for the first set of documents produced at the request of the House committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  on release of January 6th documents: "As a part of this process, the president has determined that an assertion of executive privilege is not warranted for the first set of documents from the Trump White House that have been provided to us by the National Archives." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jRgVfjJjBO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jRgVfjJjBO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1446550703812530179?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki on 6 January insurrection: "What this committee is investigating is not the normal course of government business... This committee is investigating a dark day in our democracy... That context is important here too."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1446550289792868355?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sixteen Democratic senators sent a letter to homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas and secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  denouncing the US treatment of Haitian migrants and asylum seekers at the border.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m standing with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateDems?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateDems}}}\uc2  again against mistreatment of Haitian asylum seekers and to urge action for long-term stability in Haiti\par \par \uc2 The admin must work with a broad range of leaders to find a Haitian-led solution to this crisis and must rescind the awful Trump Title 42 policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1vLkPrket5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1vLkPrket5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1446510424065822726?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnsuring the integrity of US borders is of utmost importance, and is not incompatible with the fundamental duty to respect the dignity, humanity, and rights of all individuals seeking entry to the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter states. \u8220\'20\'1CWe reiterate our call for the Biden administration to act swiftly in appointing a new special envoy for Haiti, and to work with our international partners throughout the region to find immediate solutions that places the protection needs of Haitian migrants and the long-term stability of Haiti at the core of our approach.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This comes after \uc2 Daniel Foote\uc2 , the former special envoy for Haiti, testified before the House foreign affairs committee about his abrupt resignation in September over what he called the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinhumane\u8221\'20\'1D mass deportation of Haitian migrants and asylum seekers.\par \par \uc2 He resigned shortly after shocking photos were published showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/23/men-on-horses-chasing-black-asylum-seekers-sadly-america-has-seen-it-before"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US border patrol agents on horseback}}}\uc2  using their reins on desperate Haitian refugees by the banks of the Rio Grande.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden waives executive privilege on first set of 6 January documents\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has waived executive privilege on the first set of documents produced at the request of the House committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Biden has waived executive privilege on initial set of documents produced at request of Jan 6 Select Cmte.\par \par \uc2 Trump legal team sought to block some, but Biden WH counsel says in letter to National Archives obtained by NBC: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are unique and extraordinary circumstances.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Memoli (@mikememoli)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli/status/1446541295753773059?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Let us recap: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/06/trump-aides-capitol-attack-house-select-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed Bannon and three other former aides}}}\uc2  - former social media czar Dan Scavino, former defense department official Kash Patel and former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  - to ignore subpoenas from the House committee, claiming that the material that investigators were seeking is covered by executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 But only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/oct/08/us-debt-ceiling-senate-house-washington-politics-live?page=with:block-61606be28f08b8251d62228d#block-61606be28f08b8251d62228d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the person currently in office }}}\uc2  can declare executive privilege - and Trump is not currently in office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking about restoring protections to three national monuments : Bears Ears National Monument and Grand Staircase-Escalante in Utah and the Northeast Canyons and Seamounts National Monument off the coast in New England.\par \par \uc2 Protections for all three of these monuments were stripped or scaled down under the Trump administration. \u8220\'20\'1CThe protection of public lands must not become a pendulum that swings back and forth depending on who is in public office,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a partisan issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Interior secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the first Native American interior secretary in US history \u8211\'20\'13 teared up speaking about the importance of these protections.\par \par \uc2 enltrInterior Secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  gets emotional speaking about measures the administration is taking to restore protections for national monuments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3wBxmpbF4j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3wBxmpbF4j}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1446538530084294679?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Mr President, for the profound action you are taking today to permanently protect the homelands of our ancestors,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur songs, our languages and our cultures are strong, and many people from many Indian tribes have sung and spoken in unison to protect this sacred place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 House committee investigating Capitol attack to consider criminal referral for Bannon\par \par \uc2 Earlier, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  informed the House committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol that he will not be cooperating with their subpoena to provide related documents.\par \par \uc2 Committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and vice chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  just released a statement saying they now \u8220\'20\'1Cwill swiftly consider advancing a criminal contempt of Congress referral\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Jan. 6 committee will "swiftly consider" whether to advance a criminal referral due to Bannon's noncompliance with a subpoena.\par \par \uc2 Meadows and Kash Patel are engaging with the committee >>> {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8lIQMaffGN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8lIQMaffGN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1446532633614241798?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/06/trump-aides-capitol-attack-house-select-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed Bannon and three other former aides}}}\uc2  - former social media czar Dan Scavino, former defense department official Kash Patel and former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  - to ignore the subpoena, claiming that the material that the committee is seeking from the four is covered by executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 Thompson and Cheney said Meadows and Patel are \u8220\'20\'1Cengaging\u8221\'20\'1D with the committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'We risk losing our edge as a nation'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  balanced putting a brave face on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/oct/08/us-economy-jobs-growth-september-forecasts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointing September jobs figures}}}\uc2  today with a warning that if Congress doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass his two flagship infrastructure bills \u8220\'20\'1Cwe risk losing our edge as a nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Washington moments ago, the US president said the addition of 194,000 jobs last month \u8211\'20\'13 far fewer than expected and the second month of disappointing growth as the coronavirus Delta variant and a tight labor market appeared to be holding back hiring \u8211\'20\'13 showed the trend of growth \u8220\'20\'1Cis solid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJobs creation in the first eight months\u8221\'20\'1D of his presidency total \u8220\'20\'1Calmost five million jobs\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CJobs are up, wages are up, unemployment is down, that\u8217\'20\'19s progress... real progress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But then Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is still the largest economy in the world, we still have the most productive workers and the most innovative minds in the world, but we risk losing our edge as a nation if we do not move.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden on the September jobs report: \u8220\'20\'1CThe jobs numbers also remind us that we have important work ahead of its and important investments to make. America\u8217\'20\'19s still the largest economy in the world\u8230\'20\'26 but we risk losing our edge as a nation if we don\u8217\'20\'19t move.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FUowhiR8M5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FUowhiR8M5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yahoo Finance (@YahooFinance)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YahooFinance/status/1446526876013449217?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 He pointed out that \u8220\'20\'1Cour infrastructure used to be the best in the world - roads, bridges, ports, etc\u8221\'20\'1D but had fallen to 13th place in the world, according to the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And noted that the \uc2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\uc2  (\uc2 OECD\uc2 ) now ranked the US 35th out of 37 leading countries in the percentage of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) spent on early child education.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have taken our foot off the gas,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The president pledged \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are going to lead the world like we used to\u8221\'20\'1D if Congress will pass the $1tr bipartisan infrastructure bill and a version of the $3.5tr \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/01/joe-biden-capitol-hill-infrastructure-vote-talks-domestic-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now before it}}}\uc2 , which tackle physical structures but also climate change, high speed internet, benefits for families and new technology.\par \par \uc2 He also called for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/03/bernie-sanders-democratic-battle-biden-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less division}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cnoise\u8221\'20\'1D over the legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has claimed executive privilege as a reason for not co-operating with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/05/politics/house-committee-january-6-subpoena-serve-dan-scavino/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subpoena}}}\uc2  from the House select committee investigating the attack on the US Capitol on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 . Photograph: Michal C\u237\'00\'ED\u382\'01\'7Eek/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The letter from his lawyers to the committee ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/oct/08/us-debt-ceiling-senate-house-washington-politics-live?page=with:block-6160515b8f080812a1e1e384#block-6160515b8f080812a1e1e384"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see block here}}}\uc2  ) echoes a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/sites/democrats.judiciary.house.gov/files/documents/nadler.1.9.16.2019%20wh%20letter%20re%20corey%20lewandowski.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  sent to \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2 , the chair of the House judiciary committee, in September 2019, regarding a subpoena issued to \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , a former Trump campaign chair and, until recently, a powerful figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit.\par \par \uc2 The attorney writing on Lewandowski\u8217\'20\'19s behalf indicates that what eventually happened \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/17/corey-lewandowski-trump-house-hearing-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D hearing in which Lewandowski was conclusively not made to reveal damaging information by Democrats considering whether Trump should be impeached \u8211\'20\'13 will happen, thanks to claims of executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 That doctrine, the attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/sites/democrats.judiciary.house.gov/files/documents/nadler.1.9.16.2019%20wh%20letter%20re%20corey%20lewandowski.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 , holds that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president\u8217\'20\'19s communications seeking advice or information in connection with the discharge of his duties are highly confidential and not ordinarily subject to disclosure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There are many potential differences between Lewandowski\u8217\'20\'19s case and Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s but one glaring one is that Lewandowski\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer did not claim blanket executive privilege, as Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s now does.\par \par \uc2 Another difference is that the lawyer who wrote on Lewandowski\u8217\'20\'19s behalf was Pat Cipollone, then White House counsel to Trump.\par \par \uc2 The power of a sitting president is of course huge. But now Trump is not sitting, Bannon does not have such protection from inside the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 In short, like a lot of constitutional law, arguments about executive privilege are in a way like arguments about how many angels can fit on the head of a pin. Doctrine, precedent and evidence matter less that whoever is in the most powerful position.\par \par \uc2 In Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s case, in short, he and other targets of subpoenas from the 6 January committee do not have what \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  once called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/08/donald-trump-900lb-gorilla-republican-party-mitt-romney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 900lb gorilla}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D on their side. So if the committee decides to get cross about their refusal to co-operate, things could get interesting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lest we forget, as all the todo around the debt limit begins to wind down (for now), there\u8217\'20\'19s still the very contentious $3.5tn reconciliation bill up ahead.\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders took the time today to chat with reporters about his displeasure over the role that centrist Democrats senators Joe Manchin and Kysten Sinema in shrinking the bill.\par \par \uc2 He and other progressives in the party have been clear from the start that this \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D bill focused on social services and environmental measures was fine as it was and should be voted on alongside the $1.2tn bipartisan infrastructure bill to give it a better chance of passing. Republicans - and Manchin and Sinema - have long balked at the size, as well as attempts to pass it alongside a bill they had negotiated.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSanders}}}\uc2  : "My criticism of senators Manchin & Sinema is not their views.... My strong criticism is, it is wrong when the American people, when the President of the United States, when 96% of your colleagues want to move forward, it is wrong to obstruct" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g1MBAVIzon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/g1MBAVIzon}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1446500612439482370?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Sanders has especially gone hard at Manchin, who has repeatedly spoken about how he feels that the bill would move the country toward \u8220\'20\'1C an entitlement society \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin responds: \u8220\'20\'1CRespectfully, Sen. Sanders and I share very different policy and political beliefs. As he and I have discussed, Sen. Sanders believes America should be moving towards an entitlement society while I believe we should have a compassionate and rewarding society\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7J4WebE02h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7J4WebE02h}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1445875290752708612?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDo I believe in an "entitlement society"? Yeah, I do.\par \par \uc2 I believe that all Americans are entitled to a quality education, to affordable housing, to a decent standard of living.\par \par \uc2 I do not believe that 2 people are entitled to block what the majority of the American people want.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@BernieSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders/status/1446243096874860547?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBernie, asked about sitting down with Manchin, said \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is not a movie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1446495467668389888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has informed the House committee investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol that he will not be cooperating with their subpoena to provide related documents.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW - Bannon rebuffs congressional subpoena, with lawyer citing Trump team seeking executive privilege, despite Bannon not working for the executive branch when these events took place. Says they\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for the issue to be resolved before proceeding. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8kT9mGKKXB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8kT9mGKKXB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1446493828077264920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This comes after \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/06/trump-aides-capitol-attack-house-select-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed Bannon and three other former aides}}}\uc2  - former social media czar Dan Scavino, former defense department official Kash Patel and former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  - to ignore the subpoena, likely because he will attempt to block their testimony in court.\par \par \uc2 Sources told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  that Trump is claiming that the material that the committee is seeking from the four is covered by executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 Sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/10/08/politics/trump-associates-january-6-subpoena/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  that both Bannon and Meadows have responded to subpoena, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Meadows plans to cooperate. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Scavino or Patel have responded yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee received in July a trove of financial documents from the \uc2 general services administration\uc2  as part of the committee investigation into whether there was a conflict of interest in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his DC hotel, the Trump International Hotel Washington DC, holding a federal government lease on the Old Post Office building during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 These documents revealed what many have been trying to prove for years now but could not because of investigators would not make public the former president\u8217\'20\'19s financial records - that Trump, who has always portrayed himself as a successful businessman who could turn a profit out of anything, was actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/oct/08/us-debt-ceiling-senate-house-washington-politics-live?page=with:block-616054bd8f080812a1e1e3b3#block-616054bd8f080812a1e1e3b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing tens of millions of dollars}}}\uc2  while boasting that he was making tens of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 The documents have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/news/press-releases/committee-uncovers-evidence-that-trump-concealed-millions-in-losses-hid-debts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised a number of other concerns}}}\uc2 , the committee noted. Among them:\par \par \uc2 * Trump received \u8220\'20\'1Cundisclosed preferential treatment\u8221\'20\'1D from \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  - a foreign bank - on a $170m construction loan in 2018, which he did not disclose.\par \par \uc2 * The Trump Hotel received about $3.7m in payments from foreign governments from 2017 to 2020, raising questions about possible violations of the foreign emoluments clause.\par \par \uc2 * Trump concealed debts when he applied for the federal government lease in 2011. According to the documents, he provided the \uc2 general services administration\uc2  with financial information that omitted $1.1bn in outstanding loan balances for properties in Chicago, Las Vegas, New York, and San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 * Trump transferred millions of dollars in and out of the Trump Hotel through affiliated entities and opaque transactions with other Trump businesses, which raises questions on whether the \uc2 general services administration\uc2  was able to enforce provisions that prohibited the president from taking money out of the business.\par \par \uc2 When he took office, Trump resigned from his companies but transferred his business interests to the Donald J. Trump Revocable Trust, and named as trustees his son, \uc2 Donald J. Trump, Jr\uc2 ., and the longtime chief financial officer of the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , Allen Weisselberg. As the House committee noted, Trump remained the beneficiary of the trust, \u8220\'20\'1Cmeaning that any financial benefits that accrued to his businesses ultimately benefited him personally\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's DC hotel lost almost $74m during his presidency\par \par \uc2 While publicly claiming that the Trump International Hotel Washington DC was making more than tens of millions of dollars, the hotel lost almost $74m between 2016 and 2020, according to documents released by the House oversight committee.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump International Hotel in DC--despite all the big bar tabs from lobbyists/White House officials/foreign dignitaries, supporters of Trump and \uc2 RUDY Giuliani\uc2 , of course--lost an estimated $74 million between 2016 and 2020, according to data collected by House Oversight Committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/p6yq7gCP4A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/p6yq7gCP4A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eric Lipton (@EricLiptonNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricLiptonNYT/status/1446479471851327492?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The hotel had to be loaned more than $27m from one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s holding companies, DJT Holdings LLC, according to financial statements the committee obtained, and more than $24m was not repaid and was instead converted to capital contributions.\par \par \uc2 The House committee is investigating the federal government lease of the Old Post Office building to Trump for the hotel. The \uc2 general services administration\uc2  awarded the lease to Trump in 2012 and Trump opened the hotel in 2016 when he was the Republican nominee for president.\par \par \uc2 In a letter from the committee to the \uc2 general services administration\uc2 , representatives \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  and \uc2 Gerald Connolly\uc2  wrote that the newly obtained documents show that \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal financial disclosures projected an exaggerated image of financial success and hid the Trump Hotel\u8217\'20\'19s serious financial problems, raising questions about the effectiveness of the current financial disclosure regime.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn particular, the new documents show that while President Trump privately reported tens of millions of dollars in losses to GSA, he hid these losses from the American public by omitting them from his federally mandated, public financial disclosures,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads. \u8220\'20\'1CBy portraying the hotel as a successful business, President Trump concealed significant ethical issues stemming from his failing business. The hotel\u8217\'20\'19s massive losses decreased President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal net worth, compromised the hotel\u8217\'20\'19s ability to repay loans from other entities owned by the President, and potentially jeopardized his other personal assets due to the personal guarantee he provided for the Trump Hotel\u8217\'20\'19s $170m debt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the whole letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/sites/democrats.oversight.house.gov/files/2021-10-08.CBM%20GEC%20to%20Carnahan-GSA%20re%20Old%20Post%20Office%20Building%20Lease.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 US economy adds far fewer jobs than expected in September\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, our business live blog is tracking the September jobs figures that came out just now and it\u8217\'20\'19s not looking good.\par \par \uc2 The US economy expected to add 500,000 more jobs in September, but in reality added just 194,000 jobs.\par \par \uc2 Follow here for more information:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/oct/08/us-warns-russia-energy-crisis-uk-consumer-groups-warn-fuel-poverty-this-winter-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy adds far fewer jobs than expected; UK consumer groups warn on fuel poverty \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are drawing a line in the sand when it comes to the raising the debt limit again in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have said from the start that they want Democrats to raise the limit \u8220\'20\'1Con their own\u8221\'20\'1D via budget reconciliation, a lengthy and cumbersome process that will stymie the Democratic legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 Congress at most is allowed to go the budget reconciliation route just three times a year, and Democrats have already used it to pass a $1.9tn Covid-19 relief bill and are now trying to use to pass Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D reconciliation bill to boost safety net, health and environmental programs.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the Democrats have the battle for voting rights ahead of them.\par \par \uc2 Senate \uc2 Chris Coons\uc2  is coming out strong in saying that Democrats won\u8217\'20\'19t use reconciliation to deal with the debt ceiling. \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t do it this time, won\u8217\'20\'19t do it next time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Chris Coons\uc2 : "Senator McConnell has put out a statement that he expects over the next six weeks we will use reconciliation to deal with the debt ceiling. We won't. We didn't do it this time, we won't do it next time." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1s1x5oZJT7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1s1x5oZJT7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Hill (@thehill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill/status/1446471943977308201?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the White House statement on Senate passing yesterday the deal to raise the debt limit by $480bn through 3 December. From White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s votes are welcome steps forward in averting a default that would have been devastating for our economy and for working families. President Biden looks forward to signing this bill as soon as it passes the House and reaches his desk. His focus remains on the task before us of swiftly passing his economic agenda and making vital investments in jobs, competitiveness, and lower prices for the middle class.\par \par \uc2 These votes underscore that raising the debt limit is a shared responsibility to pay for debts incurred in the past by Presidents and Congresses of both parties \u8211\'20\'13 debt that has nothing to do with President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s fully paid-for economic agenda. As we move forward, there must be no question of whether America will pay its bills; Congress must address the debt limit in December and beyond \u8211\'20\'13 just as we\u8217\'20\'19ve done almost 80 times over the last 60 years. Eleven Republicans did their part tonight, ending the filibuster and allowing Democrats to do the work of raising the debt limit. As we approach the coming months, we hope that even more Republicans will join Democrats in responsibly addressing the debt limit instead of choosing default or obstruction.\par \par \uc2 We cannot allow partisan politics to hold our economy hostage, and we can\u8217\'20\'19t allow the routine process of paying our bills to turn into a confidence-shaking political showdown every two years or every two months.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Debt limit deal heads to the House amid partisan tensions\par \par \uc2 Hello, live blog readers. Happy Friday.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re not done with the debt limit deal yet - and, of course, let\u8217\'20\'19s all remember, we won\u8217\'20\'19t be done with the debt limit for a while as we\u8217\'20\'19ll have to do this all again in a few weeks because the deal only extends the debt ceiling by $480bn through 3 December.\par \par \uc2 With a 50-48 vote, the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/07/debt-ceiling-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved the deal Thursday night}}}\uc2  to extend the government\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing authority, with the House coming back from recess early to vote on it Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Politico is reporting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca shouting match\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  erupted on the Senate floor after the vote, with Republican senators \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and \uc2 John Thune\uc2  none too pleased with majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and what they thought was an ungracious speech.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of the heated exchange - Schumer is sitting to the middle left when he is approached by Romney and Thune.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/playbookdc?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @playbookdc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/politico?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @politico}}}\uc2  leads with "shouting match" on Senate floor after debt limit vote when Senators Romney and Thune confronted Senate Majority Leader Schumer.\par \par \uc2 Here's the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cspan}}}\uc2  clip. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tWC072o8j3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tWC072o8j3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jeremy Art\uc2  (@cspanJeremy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspanJeremy/status/1446447206597267462?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Schumer had lambasted the Republicans for playing a \u8220\'20\'1C dangerous and risky partisan game \u8221\'20\'1D and said Democrats were able to \u8220\'20\'1Cpull our country back from the cliff\u8217\'20\'19s edge that Republicans tried to push us over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  : "Our caucus held together and we pulled our country back from the cliff's edge that the Republicans tried to push us over." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RG7hexV2Wi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RG7hexV2Wi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Hill (@thehill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill/status/1446460619796910084?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Republicans had twice used the filibuster to block the Democrats from raising the debt limit, and were threatening to do it once again before the deal. Their argument was that Democrats needed to raise the limit \u8220\'20\'1Con their own\u8221\'20\'1D via budget reconciliation, a lengthy and cumbersome process that would have consequences for the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 future legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 Democrats then essentially bluffed by threatening a change to the filibuster rules, after which minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  offered up the deal.\par \par \uc2 enltrTHUNE, who voted yes on cloture said of Schumer's speech: "I thought was totally out of line"\par \par \uc2 "I just thought it was incredibly partisan speech after we had just helped them solve a problem," he said.\par \par \uc2 "I let them have it," he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1446282755982102528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRomney went up to Schumer after his speech to express his displeasure. Schumer hammered Republicans during his speech\par \par \uc2 Romney explained it this way: \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a time to be graceful and there\u8217\'20\'19s a time to be combative. That was a time for grace and common ground\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1446273823997837313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Centrist Democratic senator Joe Manchin could be seen putting his head in his hands during Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s address, which he later called \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin: \u8220\'20\'1CChuck\u8217\'20\'19s frustration was there. But that was not a way to take it out. We just disagree. I\u8217\'20\'19d have done it differently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Claims he did *not* say it was a f\u8211\'20\'13king embarrassment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nJnH2HK6hA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nJnH2HK6hA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caitlin Emma (@caitlinzemma) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/caitlinzemma/status/1446279590083796994?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, top Senate Republicans are now advancing a disinformation campaign over the debt ceiling, distorting the reasons for needing to raise the nation\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing cap, Hugo Lowell reports.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/08/senate-republicans-us-debt-ceiling-deal-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans sow disinformation after $480bn US debt ceiling deal}}}\par \par \uc2 2021-10-08T13:21:52Z 2021-10-09T00:11:43Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/f0a7144b8dee29ab1775b347a2383490eebd88c1/0_68_3500_2101/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/f0a7144b8dee29ab1775b347a2383490eebd88c1/0_68_3500_2101/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  and three other former Trump aides were subpoenaed by the committee investigating the 6 January attack. A supporter of reproductive rights holds a sign outside the Texas state capitol, 2 October. \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211008eha8001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
