\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas activists and Democrats vow to keep fighting after  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban blocked\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 750 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par 15:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 23\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups and Democrats welcome federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision but warn its impact could be temporary\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/10/after-judges-ruling-one-of-texas-biggest-abortion-providers-will-resume-abortions-up-to-18-weeks/?utm_campaign=19th-social&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  after a federal judge ruled on Wednesday that it violated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reproductive rights groups and Democrats have welcomed the decision, while warning its impact could be temporary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the moment SB 8 went into effect, women have been unlawfully prevented from exercising control over their lives in ways that are protected by the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Judge Robert Pitman wrote as part of a 113-page opinion, granting an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/10/06/1040221171/a-u-s-judge-blocks-enforcement-of-texas-controversial-new-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency request from the justice department}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was brought by the Biden administration, which has said the restrictions of Senate Bill 8 (SB 8) were enacted in defiance of the US constitution. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/01/texas-abortion-law-federal-judge-biden-administrations-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration argued}}}\uc2  that Texas has waged an attack on the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SB 8, passed last month, bars abortions after six weeks with no exceptions for rape or incest and also allows private citizens to sue anyone they suspect of \u8220\'20\'1Caiding or abetting\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure.\par \par \uc2 But questions remain if the ruling will hold. The state of Texas has already filed a notice that they will appeal the decision to the fifth circuit court of appeals in New Orleans, a notably conservative court. The appeals court previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/06/politics/texas-abortion-ban-federal-judge-order-block/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied a request}}}\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to block the law.\par \par \uc2 Even with the law on hold, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in Texas may not instantly resume because doctors still fear that they could be sued without a more permanent legal decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSB8 has wreaked havoc on Texans. We\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to fight until our right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is permanently restored,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLUTx/status/1445922998939275271"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  the Texas branch of \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many have voiced their approval with Pitman\u8217\'20\'19s decision, including reproductive rights groups and prominent figures in the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile this fight is far from over,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of the Planned Parenthood Federation of America in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are hopeful that the court\u8217\'20\'19s order blocking SB 8 will allow Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to resume services as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , called the decision a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for women in Texas and for the rule of law\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the foremost responsibility of the Department of Justice to defend the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to protect constitutional rights against all who would seek to undermine them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is good news. Judge Pitman\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is the right one. Women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to decide over their bodies needs to be protected, not put to the criteria of private individuals seeking a bounty. We must continue fighting to protect Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSylviaGarcia/status/1446085502365470728"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  Texas representative Sylvia Garcia.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , described Pitman\u8217\'20\'19s decision as \u8220\'20\'1Can important step forward toward restoring the constitutional rights of women across the state of Texas\u8221\'20\'1D and confirmed that Joe Biden supports \u8220\'20\'1Ccodifying\u8221\'20\'1D the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Roe v Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight has only just begun, both in Texas and in many states across this country where women\u8217\'20\'19s rights are currently under attack,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  on Friday released a report saying that if Roe v Wade were overturned, 26 states are primed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This year alone, nearly 600 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions have been introduced in statehouses nationwide, with more than 90 becoming law, according to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/09/20/1038972266/supreme-court-date-roe-wade-dobbs-jackson-womens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even bigger challenge to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  could come later this year when the supreme court is set to hear Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, a case from Mississippi on if states are able to ban abortions before fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight is far from over, but this is seriously good news,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NARAL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  Naral Pro-Choice America in response to the block.\par \par \uc2 In the face of the decision, some Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics announced their plans to resume abortions that were previously barred under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s rule. Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, a network of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, has said they plan to resume abortions up to 18 weeks \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the justice we have been seeking for weeks and we are grateful that the court has finally stepped in to curb some of the harm Texans have faced,\u8221\'20\'1D said Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health founder and CEO, Amy Hagstrom Miller.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211007eha7002h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
