\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Victoria confirms a record 1,763 cases and four deaths; Frydenberg in isolation \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Nino Bucci and Matilda Boseley \par \uc2 15,420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par 07:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2  in isolation after staff member tests positive; Victoria reports national record of 1,763 cases ; Latrobe Valley will emerge from lockdown from midnight ; NSW records lowest cases since mid-August ; \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  sworn in and will \u8216\'20\'18continue the plan\u8217\'20\'19 for reopening that \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  started; ACT records 33 cases ; no new cases in SA ; Qld records two local cases. This blog is now closedVictoria on track to reopen this month despite national record daily casesGreg Hunt suggests Qld premier has \u8216\'20\'18misled the public\u8217\'20\'19 as hospital funding dispute heats upAustralia cases and data trackerGet our free news app ; get our morning email briefing\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34am BST\par \par \uc2 That's it for today \u8211\'20\'13 thanks for reading\par \par \uc2 Here are the main stories on 5 October, 2021:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  is sworn in as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/dominic-perrottet-wins-liberal-leadership-ballot-to-become-nsw-premier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the premier of NSW}}}\uc2 , after easily winning a party room vote against the planning minister \uc2 Rob Stokes\uc2  ;\par \par \uc2 * Victoria is set to end lockdown as scheduled later this month, despite setting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/victoria-on-track-to-reopen-this-month-despite-national-record-1763-covid-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new national record}}}\uc2  of daily Covid-19 cases on Tuesday;\par \par \uc2 * The federal treasurer, \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2 , confirms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615bb7388f0885f4b086d9b5#block-615bb7388f0885f4b086d9b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he is in isolation}}}\uc2  after a staff member tested positive for Covid-19. He has recorded a negative test for the virus;\par \par \uc2 * The federal health minister, Greg Hunt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/greg-hunt-suggests-queensland-premier-has-misled-the-public-as-hospital-funding-dispute-heats-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls on the Queensland government}}}\uc2  to explain how linking the reopening of its borders to hospital funding is \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the law and spirit\u8221\'20\'1D of public health orders;\par \par \uc2 * As many as 100,000 workers in the West Australian resources sector must be fully vaccinated by the end of the year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615bf9bb8f080431dc31fd12#block-615bf9bb8f080431dc31fd12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under a mandate introduced}}}\uc2  by the state government; and\par \par \uc2 * NSW {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615b95d78f080431dc31f930#block-615b95d78f080431dc31f930"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 records its lowest}}}\uc2  case numbers since August, the ACT records {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615ba15a8f080431dc31f992#block-615ba15a8f080431dc31f992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 33 new cases}}}\uc2  ; New Zealand has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615b9cdd8f0871ecf8fab489#block-615b9cdd8f0871ecf8fab489"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24 new cases}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615ba33e8f080431dc31f9ac#block-615ba33e8f080431dc31f9ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tasmania}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2021/oct/05/australia-news-live-update-construction-restarts-in-victoria-nsw-liberals-meet-to-elect-new-leader-domonic-perrottet-gladys-berejiklian-melbourne-sydney-covid-cfmeu-contact-tracing-daniel-andrews?page=with:block-615bf8798f0871ecf8fab7fe#block-615bf8798f0871ecf8fab7fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Australia}}}\uc2  remain on alert, despite not recording any new cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Vaccination mandate for West Australian FIFO workers\par \par \uc2 The premier of Western Australia, \uc2 Mark McGowan\uc2 , has announced that as many as 100,000 workers in the resources sector must be fully vaccinated by the end of the year, AAP report:\par \par \uc2 Up to 100,000 fly-in, fly-out workers and others engaged in Western Australia\u8217\'20\'19s resources sector will be required to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 by the beginning of January.\par \par \uc2 McGowan says the rules will apply to anyone involved in exploration, mining, the oil and gas industries, the wider resources sector, and others who work in remote locations or operate critical infrastructure including rail services.\par \par \uc2 They will need to have had their first vaccine jabs by December 1.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe aim is clear. We want to protect workers and the wider community and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D the premier said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is also to protect our Aboriginal community and address the obvious risk posed by the movement of resources sector workers to and from regional and remote locations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The mandate follows similar measures put in place for WA\u8217\'20\'19s aged care, health, port and quarantine workers.\par \par \uc2 More industries could be targeted, based on health advice, McGowan said.\par \par \uc2 An iron ore mine in the Pilbara. Photograph: Paul Mayall Australia/Alamy\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04am BST\par \par \uc2 A new exposure site has been listed in South Australia, but no new cases have been reported, AAP report:\par \par \uc2 A new exposure site has been identified but no new Covid-19 cases have been reported following the infection in a South Australian woman who spent time in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 The case, involving a woman in her 40s, has already prompted tough new restrictions for Mt Gambier and two other council areas in SA\u8217\'20\'19s southeast.\par \par \uc2 SA Health said on Tuesday its investigations in the Mt Gambier region were continuing but a new exposure site linked to the woman\u8217\'20\'19s case had been identified at the SipnSave at the South Eastern Hotel on Friday between 5.30pm and 6.05pm.\par \par \uc2 It was considered a tier four site, so anyone there at that time need only monitor for coronavirus symptoms.\par \par \uc2 SA officials also remain concerned about another virus case in an interstate truck driver who visited service stations and truck stops at Ceduna and Port Augusta on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 SA currently has four active Covid-19 infections, with two of those acquired interstate and two in returned overseas travellers.\par \par \uc2 No new infections were reported on Tuesday among more than 4600 tests conducted in the previous 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Morrison praises Perrottet\par \par \uc2 Despite suggestions of hostility between the prime minister and the new NSW premier \uc2 Dom Perrottet\uc2 , Scott Morrison has released a statement congratulating him on his rise to the top job and praising his work as treasurer. Morrison said:\par \par \uc2 Dom and I have worked closely together for a long time, including both when I was treasurer, and as prime minister. I know the commitment and dedication he will bring to his new role, and the energy he will invest in continuing to deliver for NSW.\par \par \uc2 In particular these last 18 months, Dom and I have worked together with \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  and \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2  to ensure that the families and businesses across NSW received the support they needed to fight through the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The Sydney Morning Herald columnist, Niki Savva, has written about tensions between the pair, including a meeting in which Morrison allegedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/prime-minister-scott-morrison-a-cranky-man-in-need-of-a-plan-20210811-p58hpr.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped the \u8220\'20\'1Cf-bomb\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Morrison said Perrottet had been \u8220\'20\'1Ca powerful advocate\u8221\'20\'1D for NSW and Australia throughout the pandemic, and said he was committed to the National Plan, which has agreed to a gradual reopening of the country once vaccination rates reach 70 and 80%. Morrison said:\par \par \uc2 With NSW vaccination levels now at 67.7 per cent double dose, those first steps to eased restrictions and more freedom are just days away.\par \par \uc2 Dom is also someone who has strong beliefs, a keen commitment to family and the Liberal values that respect reward for effort, personal responsibility and doing what\u8217\'20\'19s right by your community.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51am BST\par \par \uc2 This is lovely content to mark the bird of the year poll:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/commentisfree/2021/oct/05/birdwatching-doesnt-make-me-forget-covid-but-it-helps-me-see-life-anew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Birdwatching doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make me forget Covid, but it helps me see life anew | Debbie Lustig}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38am BST\par \par \uc2 A man accused of murdering four people during a shooting spree across Darwin was terrified someone was out to get him before the killings, a court has heard.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/man-accused-of-darwin-shooting-rampage-was-terrified-court-told"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Man accused of Darwin shooting rampage was \u8216\'20\'18terrified\u8217\'20\'19, court told}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the lay of the land Covid-wise in NSW, via AAP :\par \par \uc2 NSW has recorded 608 new locally acquired cases and another seven people have died, as schooling and elective surgery resumes in some areas.\par \par \uc2 The daily case numbers are the lowest since August and it is the fourth day in a row with fewer than 700 cases.\par \par \uc2 Six men and one woman with Covid-19 have died, bringing the toll for the current outbreak to 385 deaths.\par \par \uc2 Five of the people who died were not vaccinated, while two had received one dose of a Covid-19 vaccine.\par \par \uc2 There are 978 people in hospital with COVID-19 in NSW, with 190 in intensive care, and 94 on ventilators.\par \par \uc2 Across the state, 88.6 per cent of people aged 16 and over had received their first vaccine, and 67.7 per cent were fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, more than 140,000 students in NSW regional communities have returned to face-to-face learning at school for the start of term four.\par \par \uc2 In regional NSW, stay-at-home orders are underway for the Lismore local government area and the town of Casino.\par \par \uc2 Gunnedah has also gone into lockdown, after five new cases were detected. Anyone who has been in the local government area since 27 September must also isolate.\par \par \uc2 While Port Macquarie will be freed from lockdown from Wednesday morning, nearby Forster, Tuncurry and Taree have returned to stay-at-home orders.\par \par \uc2 In his first press conference as NSW premier, \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  said he would meet with health minister \uc2 Brad Hazzard\uc2  to discuss \u8220\'20\'1Cissues\u8221\'20\'1D with the roadmap. When asked whether he would give people in NSW an early mark and ease restrictions ahead of schedule, the premier said lockdown would still end on 11 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21am BST\par \par \uc2 The new leader will be pleased with this.\par \par \uc2 enltr88.6% of NSW has received their first dose of the COVID-19 vaccine, and 67.7% are fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 ?? To get vaccinated, find a walk-in clinic or make a booking: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ej3FSanOoF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ej3FSanOoF}}}\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s do this NSW! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jj4ERZV7FG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Jj4ERZV7FG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 NSW Health\uc2  (@NSWHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHealth/status/1445267557477453829?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria is on track to stabilise its Covid case numbers and reopen later this month, despite reporting a national record of 1,763 infections on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , said the government was still committed to \u8220\'20\'1Cdoing everything that we can to deliver the roadmap\u8221\'20\'1D, even though Covid case numbers had been above 1,000 for six days running.\par \par \uc2 He said he was confident the state would still meet its reopening date of 26 October \u8211\'20\'13 the day Victoria was expected to achieve a 70% double-dose vaccination rate.\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of this article here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/victoria-on-track-to-reopen-this-month-despite-national-record-1763-covid-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria on track to reopen this month despite national record 1,763 Covid cases}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian Government has warned the construction sector must adhere to strict Covid-19 protocols if it is to remain open as the industry resumes after a two-week hiatus.\par \par \uc2 Some 10,000 labourers returned to work on Tuesday after an industry roadmap to reopening agreement was reached between the state government, builders, unions and industry partners on 1 October.\par \par \uc2 The private construction sector reopened at 25% capacity for large projects while the construction of state critical infrastructure could resume at full capacity under the roadmap.\par \par \uc2 You can read more on this story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/weve-set-higher-standards-victoria-construction-industry-returns-under-strict-covid-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ve set higher standards\u8217\'20\'19: Victoria construction industry returns under strict Covid rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54am BST\par \par \uc2 The reserve bank did not shift the cash rate today, surprising nobody, AAP reports:\par \par \uc2 As widely anticipated by economists, the RBA left the official cash rate at a record low 0.1% following its monthly board meeting on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Dr Lowe reiterated the cash rate will not be increased until inflation is sustainably within the two to three per cent target range, saying such conditions will not be met before 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis contrasts with several other central banks that seem to be bringing rate hikes forward and arguably reflects more confidence on the RBA\u8217\'20\'19s part that the current spike in global inflationary pressure is transient,\u8221\'20\'1D AMP Capital chief economist \uc2 Shane Oliver\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 However, Dr Lowe remained fairly upbeat about the economic outlook beyond the current spate of lockdowns in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s two largest states - NSW and Victoria.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis setback to the economic expansion in Australia is expected to be only temporary. As vaccination rates increase further and restrictions are eased, the economy is expected to bounce back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Lowe also gave little away about what the banking regulator, the \uc2 Australian Prudential Regulation Authority\uc2 , may introduce to take the heat out of the housing market.\par \par \uc2 He said housing prices are continuing to rise, although turnover in some markets has declined following the virus outbreak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this environment, it is important that lending standards are maintained and that loan serviceability buffers are appropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48am BST\par \par \uc2 These are heady times for staunch #federalicacnow advocates, so it is worth checking in on the reality of how the NSW model actually stacks up against the federal model:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/commonwealth-integrity-commission-what-is-it-and-how-is-it-different-from-icac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commonwealth Integrity Commission: what is it and how is it different from Icac?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42am BST\par \par \uc2 I love a sunburnt country, a land of jabbed-up arms.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy beautiful people of Australia\par \par \uc2 We are have now surpassed the US in terms of % of the population vaccinated with at least 1 dose. And we haven't lost steam.\par \par \uc2 We are on our way to be among the most vaccinated places on earth. And to a much better year in 2022!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/09nizulMoM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/09nizulMoM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nancy Baxter MD PhD (@enenbee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/enenbee/status/1445231579530334211?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31am BST\par \par \uc2 The federal health minister, Greg Hunt, has called on the Queensland government to explain how linking the reopening of its borders to hospital funding is \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the law and spirit\u8221\'20\'1D of public health orders.\par \par \uc2 Hunt\u8217\'20\'19s questioning of Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s border ban on Tuesday marks a significant escalation in hostilities between Canberra and the states over hospital funding.\par \par \uc2 The Queensland premier, Annastacia Palaszczuk, has rejected commonwealth claims she is engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Cshakedown politics\u8221\'20\'1D, noting all states and territories have sought extra cash.\par \par \uc2 The full story is here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/greg-hunt-suggests-queensland-premier-has-misled-the-public-as-hospital-funding-dispute-heats-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Hunt suggests Queensland premier has \u8216\'20\'18misled the public\u8217\'20\'19 as hospital funding dispute heats up}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Dan Andrews\uc2  wants Victorians to be just like Mike Tyson and jab their way out of trouble (do not under any circumstances resort to ear chewing).\par \par \uc2 enltrYesterday 96,337 Victorians got a jab.\par \par \uc2 Another 96,371 made a booking.\par \par \uc2 And for the last three days more Victorians have rolled up a sleeve than any other state.\par \par \uc2 Let's keep going Victoria - we're almost there.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dan Andrews\uc2  (@DanielAndrewsMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielAndrewsMP/status/1445258123342598144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16am BST\par \par \uc2 AAP have filed a report on the Covid survivor who fronted up to the Victorian press conference today:\par \par \uc2 Will Smith was a top-level college athlete in the United States when the young Victorian man was struck down with Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The 24-year-old fell ill in March 2020 after returning to Melbourne from Boston, where he had spent four years on \uc2 Northeastern University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rowing team.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter how young you are, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter how fit you are, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter how indestructible you feel - Covid can still hit you,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe feeling of straining against your own body, trying to expand your lungs against this invisible force, struggling to breathe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith is still grappling with the long-term effects more than 18 months after contracting the virus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMonths after my diagnosis I still couldn\u8217\'20\'19t walk around the block without getting light-headed, needing to lie down, struggling to breathe. I had such debilitating fatigue that I sometimes couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even get out of bed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Victoria aims to hit 80% double-vaccination for those aged over 16 by early November, Smith is urging more Victorians to roll up their sleeves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to be on a ventilator to have your life turned upside down for months, or maybe even years,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Another Covid survivor, 49-year-old Kim Hanrahan, spent six days in intensive care in July last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy lungs had collapsed and I had required a constant flow of oxygen,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCovid also stripped me of my dignity, unable to go to the bathroom or wash myself. I had to rely on the amazing kindness of the ICU nurses, who cared for me at their own risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFourteen months later and I feel like I\u8217\'20\'19ve aged 10 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel a lesser version of myself due to this horrible, debilitating disease.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her message to Victorians, like Smith\u8217\'20\'19s, is simple: get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t play Russian roulette with your health or of those you love,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian Aboriginal Legal Service has sharply criticised the handling of Covid-19 in the state\u8217\'20\'19s prison system.\par \par \uc2 There are now 36 prisoners across at least five sites with the virus.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the legal service said it had repeatedly advised the Andrews government that its policies for managing outbreaks in prisons were not going to be effective.\par \par \uc2 Andreea Lachsz, the head of policy, communications and strategy, said:\par \par \uc2 The Andrews government talks a lot about following expert advice, but they have ignored VALS and experts from across the world about managing outbreaks in Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s prisons.\par \par \uc2 Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are more vulnerable to Covid and are less likely to get appropriate health care in prison.\par \par \uc2 We are concerned about the lack of transparency by Corrections Victoria. When there were outbreaks in other high-risk settings, such as aged care facilities, the public were given much more detail about those outbreaks on a daily basis.\par \par \uc2 People in prison have a right to equitable healthcare. Denying people in prison appropriate health care risks a surge of infections resulting in either long-term complications or deaths in custody. It also risks a larger Covid outbreak in the Victorian community, given the daily movement of large numbers of staff in and out of prisons.\par \par \uc2 As of 1 October, 73% of adults in public and private prisons had received their first dose of vaccine, and 52% were fully vaccinated, AAP reported.\par \par \uc2 Guardian Australia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/jun/03/at-least-half-of-victorias-paramedics-yet-to-receive-covid-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier this year}}}\uc2  that despite prison workers and inmates being in phase 1B of the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s rollout, meaning they had been eligible since March, Victorian facilities did not introduce a vaccination program until June.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Paul Toole will contest NSW Nationals leadership\par \par \uc2 Paul Toole has thrown his hat in the ring to replace outgoing NSW Nationals leader \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2 , saying his three years as deputy make him the best choice for the job, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 The NSW government will have an entirely fresh leadership team by Wednesday, after Deputy Premier Barilaro announced on Monday he was following \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  out the door.\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  has emerged as the state\u8217\'20\'19s new premier, after a Liberal party-room vote on Tuesday, while the Nationals will appoint their new leader on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Water Minister \uc2 Melinda Pavey\uc2  was the first to put her hand up for the job on Monday, but Mr Toole is also eyeing a promotion.\par \par \uc2 After taking 24 hours to consider his position and talk to colleagues, the Bathurst MP on Tuesday announced he wants the top job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a time where we need a strong and stable leadership (as) we are coming out of a pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He talked up his credentials as deputy party leader, and pointed to his track record of working with the incoming premier in crisis cabinet and other committees.\par \par \uc2 When announcing his surprise decision to step down, Mr Barilaro said NSW would be best served by someone who had the passion and fight to forge on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just don\u8217\'20\'19t have the energy anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr Barilaro told reporters on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Bathurst MP Paul Toole has confirmed he will run for the NSW Nationals leadership. Photograph: Dan Himbrechts/AAP\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/nsw-deputy-premier-john-barilaro-resigns-from-politics-days-after-berejiklian-quits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NSW deputy premier John Barilaro resigns from politics days after Berejiklian quits}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Seven Covid cases are now linked to the violent protest at the CFMEU headquarters in Melbourne last month.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\uc2  : The CFMEU says confirmed COVID-19 cases from the protest at its head office have grown to seven.\par \par \uc2 The union said the virus has spread to "family members including, elderly parents, wives, brothers, and sisters as well as dozens of young children including two babies."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eden Gillespie (@edengillespie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edengillespie/status/1445247911399346176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41am BST\par \par \uc2 SA Health have identified a new exposure site in Mount Gambier, in the state\u8217\'20\'19s south-east.\par \par \uc2 enltrCOVID-19 HEALTH ALERT 5 October 2021\par \par \uc2 SA Health has identified a new COVID-19 exposure location in South Australia.\par \par \uc2 If you attended an exposure location, you are required to follow the relevant health advice.\par \par \uc2 More information is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4sJYadglJu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4sJYadglJu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/75xIw5qk5W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/75xIw5qk5W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SA Health (@SAHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SAHealth/status/1445230612701278208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37am BST\par \par \uc2 This is about 20 hours old but as it will remain bizarre in perpetuity I am posting it. A \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  fan compares her resignation to the death of Princess Diana :\par \par \uc2 enltr"It's like Diana," one passer-by said.\par \par \uc2 Only Gladys is still alive and faces serious allegations in the ICAC. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/auspol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #auspol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gladysberejiklian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gladysberejiklian}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/icac?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #icac}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZgOaQnHTTe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZgOaQnHTTe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jason Om (@jason_om) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jason_om/status/1444932812734226433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Covid cases in Victoria's prison system\par \par \uc2 Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s prison system is battling an increasing number of Covid cases, AAP reports:\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Victorian prisoners and staff are battling Covid-19 as the state\u8217\'20\'19s worsening outbreak leaks into jails.\par \par \uc2 Corrections Victoria says 36 prisoners and 15 staff are among the more than 14,000 active cases in the state.\par \par \uc2 Of the infected prisoners, 16 are at the Melbourne Assessment Prison, 11 at the Metropolitan Remand Centre, five at the Ravenhall Correctional Centre, three at the Dame Phyllis Frost Centre and one at Port Phillip Prison.\par \par \uc2 The five Covid-positive prisoners at Ravenhall were in the general prison population.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne has been managed under quarantine arrangements since developing COVID-19 symptoms while in the general prison population on 25 September 2021, and has now been moved to the prison\u8217\'20\'19s isolation unit,\u8221\'20\'1D Corrections Victoria said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe other four prisoners returned positive results as part of extensive surveillance testing of prisoners and staff, and are now in isolation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 All new Victorian prisoners are tested and required to spend 14 days in protective quarantine, regardless of their Covid-19 risk.\par \par \uc2 Prisoner movement at the Dame Phyllis and Port Phillip prisons has been restricted while contact tracing takes place, and all in-person visits to Victorian jails are suspended.\par \par \uc2 Sixteen prisoners at the Melbourne Assessment Prison have tested positive for Covid-19. Photograph: James Ross/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02am BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Josh Taylor can explain to you what happened with \uc2 Facebook\uc2  earlier today:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/oct/05/facebook-outage-what-went-wrong-and-why-did-it-take-so-long-to-fix"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Facebook outage: what went wrong and why did it take so long to fix?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of the Victorian Covid update today, if you missed it earlier:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  sworn in as NSW premier\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  has just been sworn in as premier of New South Wales by the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Margaret Beazley.\par \par \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  will be sworn as the deputy leader of the NSW Liberals shortly, as will the man replacing Perrottet as NSW treasurer, \uc2 Matt Kean\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  (right) and \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  (left) arrive at Government House in Sydney for Perrottet\u8217\'20\'19s swearing in ceremony as the 46th premier of NSW. Photograph: Brook Mitchell/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 I missed this earlier, but it seems very much like another jurisdiction is hoisting the Covid normal banner and quietly packing away its Covid zero one (following on from NSW, Victoria, New Zealand).\par \par \uc2 enltrQueensland's CHO Jeannette Young says the state is transitioning from a phase of stopping the virus entering the state. "The virus will come in no matter what we do."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Mealey (@rachelmealey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelmealey/status/1445184626545217540?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian Greens want nurses in the state paid bonuses over the next six months for the hard graft they\u8217\'20\'19re putting in dealing with a record number of Covid cases.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Greens & I are calling for a bonus for Victorian nurses on the COVID frontline in public hospitals.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve been through a lot & we need them now more than ever.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of talk about nurses being heroes but we think they should be rewarded with action. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SpringSt?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SpringSt}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/svowM5wccK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/svowM5wccK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ellen Sandell (@ellensandell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ellensandell/status/1445228592883920897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Tasmanian health authorities have identified 17 primary close contacts of a Covid-positive Launceston teenager and say the likelihood of further cases is \u8220\'20\'1Cquite high\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abcnews/status/1445224847735287814"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ABC reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am BST\par \par \uc2 New Zealanders are grieving for the end of the country\u8217\'20\'19s Covid elimination strategy and anxious about what the future holds, a day after the prime minister \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2  announced the country would switch to a suppression approach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s kind of a grieving for what we are losing,\u8221\'20\'1D said microbiologist Siouxsie Wiles, one of the pandemic response\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent science communicators. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very clearly losing alert level one, and the freedoms and privileges that come with [it].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/05/anger-and-grief-new-zealanders-fearful-as-covid-elimination-strategy-ends"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anger and grief: New Zealanders fearful as Covid elimination strategy ends}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 I am saddened that I have now lost three birds, but I will regroup behind the ground parrot.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/05/superb-fairywren-pulling-ahead-in-2021-australian-bird-of-the-year-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Superb fairywren pulling ahead in 2021 Australian bird of the year poll}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Frydenberg in isolation after staff member tests positive for Covid\par \par \uc2 The treasurer, \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2 , has just released a statement saying he is in isolation after a staff member tested positive for Covid-19. He has received a negative result, but says he is remaining in isolation until further notice.\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qLisupJoXD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qLisupJoXD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2  (@JoshFrydenberg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoshFrydenberg/status/1445212530700214273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 The Hillsong founder Brian Houston will plead not guilty to charges alleging he concealed child sexual abuse by his late father in the 1970s.\par \par \uc2 The megachurch founder did not appear during a first mention of the case at Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s Downing Centre local court on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Houston\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer told the court Houston would plead not guilty.\par \par \uc2 Read our full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/05/hillsong-founder-brian-houston-pleads-not-guilty-to-concealing-sexual-abuse-charge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillsong founder Brian Houston to plead not guilty to concealing sexual abuse charge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Masks still compulsory for statues.\par \par \uc2 enltrLockdown may be lifting in Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s Latrobe Valley, but the Migrant statue at Morwell\u8217\'20\'19s Immigration Park remains covid safe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gippsnews?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gippsnews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/covid19vic?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #covid19vic}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PYmp0PmMkK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PYmp0PmMkK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jarrod Whittaker (@JarrodWhittaker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JarrodWhittaker/status/1445206772067672068?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 The Greens are going to try to force the House to debate its federal integrity bill when parliament next sits (mid-October), given it passed the Senate more than two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Labor, the Greens and a crossbench coalition have been trying to get the government to bring on a debate about establishing a federal Icac since the election. So far, the government has not budged. And given Scott Morrison \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Barnaby Joyce\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s most recent comments on a federal Icac model, it is unlikely to.\par \par \uc2 Still, Senator \uc2 Larissa Waters\uc2  says it is beyond time for the parliament to debate the matter:\par \par \uc2 The PM\u8217\'20\'19s comments this morning that the NSW Icac assumes guilt before an investigation are patently wrong and are designed to justify his pathetically weak proposal for a toothless body that wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have applied to or stopped many of the scandals we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen plaguing his government.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, the Greens\u8217\'20\'19 bill to establish a strong, independent, effective national integrity commission allows for public hearings, retrospectivity and the ability to investigate anonymous tip-offs, balanced with appropriate safeguards and privacy provisions.\par \par \uc2 It passed the Senate more than two years ago \u8211\'20\'13 the PM just needs to bring it on for debate in the House and the Australian people could have a federal anti-corruption body in place by Christmas.\par \par \uc2 When parliament resumes, the Greens will attempt to force the PM\u8217\'20\'19s hand by moving a concurrence motion, compelling the government to bring on my national integrity commission bill in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 The PM needs to listen to the Australian people and get this done.\par \par \uc2 The Greens senator \uc2 Larissa Waters\uc2 . Photograph: Mick Tsikas/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Thank you Matilda. Another shift that gets you even closer to the blogging hall of fame.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51am BST\par \par \uc2 With that absolutely JUMBO day, I will hand you over to the fantastic Nino Bucci.\par \par \uc2 Stay safe everyone!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50am BST\par \par \uc2 The Morrison government has been accused of demonstrating it is not taking the climate crisis seriously after approving a third new coalmine development in a month shortly before a major international conference on the issue.\par \par \uc2 With global climate talks in Glasgow less than four weeks away, the environment minister, \uc2 Sussan Ley\uc2 , has given a subsidiary of the mining giant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/glencore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Glencore}}}\uc2  the green light to expand the Mangoola mine near Muswellbrook.\par \par \uc2 It means the company can create a new coal pit north of an existing mine to extract of an additional 52m tonnes of the fossil fuel over eight years.\par \par \uc2 The mine had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/apr/26/nsw-planning-body-gives-green-light-to-hunter-valley-coalmine-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  by the NSW Independent Planning Commission in April, less than a month before a state byelection in the Upper Hunter in which the future of the coal industry was a prominent issue.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full report below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/new-coalmine-mangoola-nsw-muswellbrook-approved-australia-environment-minister-sussan-ley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Third new coal project approved by Australian environment minister Sussan Ley in just one month}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrnow *Americans* are doing street protests against Australia's COVID measures.\par \par \uc2 This "Australia has fallen" social media narrative is going bananas in some US anti-COVID/conspiracy circles, after images of protests and police responses recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MzfQsfUb8R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MzfQsfUb8R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Butler (@JoshButler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoshButler/status/1445203692655767552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Dom_Perrottet?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @dom_perrottet}}}\uc2  on your appointment as Premier. I call on the incoming Premier to commit to making no changes that would see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care wound back or restricted during his term. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care was decriminalised in 2019 & we can\u8217\'20\'19t go backwards. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nswpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nswpol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jamal Hakim (he/him/his) (@thejamalhakim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thejamalhakim/status/1445197026103160845?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrGood news! 22 of Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s LGAs have now PASSED 90% first-dose milestone! Bring on those second doses, and watch the immunity soar! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/covid19vic?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #covid19vic}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr Sandro Demaio (@SandroDemaio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SandroDemaio/status/1445190593278185474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian press conference has ended on a sombre note (yes, it\u8217\'20\'19s only just ended), as 24-year-old Will breaks down the struggle, and uncertainty, of living with long Covid.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 Did they give you any indication as to how long this might be your reality for?\par \par \uc2 Will:\par \par \uc2 Well, I think in March last year when I first got it, you know, the nurses said you should be fine in two weeks. And then I called them in two weeks and they said \u8211\'20\'13 right, we should expect it to be next month. Next month... you know.\par \par \uc2 The reality is that I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that we know. On the one hand, that\u8217\'20\'19s really scary because it could be indefinite. I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to be positive and hope that there has been a slightly positive trend over time and there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason that that can\u8217\'20\'19t continue.\par \par \uc2 But I think that we don\u8217\'20\'19t know, and there\u8217\'20\'19s more and more data and evidence and anecdotes coming out every day about how it affects different people for longer periods of time. But I haven\u8217\'20\'19t been given any indication of when it will stop. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know when that will be. I hope that it issoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 And as if Melbourne wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going through enough, now the skyscrapers are falling apart.\par \par \uc2 enltrA window and frame have fallen from high up an Elizabeth Street skyscraper, landing on the footpath. One witness says it shattered just a metre from where a man was standing. Can you spot where it came from? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sILrMa09jQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sILrMa09jQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Paul Dowsley (@paul_dowsley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/paul_dowsley/status/1445198455605915656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Ummm... so this is happening across the pond. Crowds gathering outside the office of the consulate general of Australia in New York to protest.\par \par \uc2 They were shouting \u8220\'20\'1Csave Australia\u8221\'20\'1D, despite the state of New York recording more than 55,000 Covid-19 deaths compared to the entirety of Australia only recording 1,346.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe crowd gathers outside the Consulate General of Australia here in New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g9JVbiEzt5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/g9JVbiEzt5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brendan Gutenschwager (@BGOnTheScene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BGOnTheScene/status/1445126806152089602?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s Covid response deputy secretary, Kate Matson, is asked about the elephant in the room \u8211\'20\'13 on a day of more than 1,700 cases, with more than 38,000 primary close contacts, t ier 2 exposure sites will no longer be listed on the health department\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 The premier said before that our contact tracing is at this stage keeping up. But if we\u8217\'20\'19re relying on people to contact their own close contacts, how is that us keeping up?\par \par \uc2 Matson:\par \par \uc2 As the public health risk changes, the process needs to change... We\u8217\'20\'19 re no longer going for Covid zero. When we were... a few months ago in the outbreak... we would take a really risk averse approach to exposure site management, contact management, etc.\par \par \uc2 So we have changed in the values to deal with the highest risk and that is obviously on primary close contacts and tier one exposure sites... we are focusing on the highest risk of transmission and the most sensitive settings, so we will never lose focus on our most sensitive setting, be it schools, as they go back, or aged care facilities or healthcare facilities.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 The new NSW premier says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t expect any more MPs to leave the state parliament.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 Can you guarantee your colleagues that no more will resign from parliament?\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve had a great opportunity \u8211\'20\'13 like others \u8211\'20\'13 to speak to many colleagues over what has been a very difficult weekend for many.\par \par \uc2 There is strong commitment from colleagues that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expect there to be any more, no.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 OK back to Perrottet, who has been asked if he has spoken to the prime minister since he has been appointed NSW premier. It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that he has had a fairly rocky relationship with Scott Morrison, publicly criticising the commonwealth government and demanding they bring back jobkeeper during the early days of the Sydney lockdown.\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 Look, I have a very constructive relationship with the prime minister. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t spoken to him today, but I will.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve known Scott for many years in the Liberal party. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t see why there could be seen to be an issue if you have a disagreement. Disagreement is good. You want a passionate prime minister. You want a passionate premier.\par \par \uc2 You want passionate treasurers, those who will stand up and fight for their state. And that means, from time to time, you\u8217\'20\'19re not always going to agree. But once you\u8217\'20\'19ve had those discussions, you move on.\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s a passionate guy. And that will, from time to time, lead to disagreements. But disagreements aren\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily a bad thing in their own way.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 Have you spoken to \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  since you\u8217\'20\'19ve been voted in?\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 I haven\u8217\'20\'19t had the chance yet. She messaged me yesterday in relation to wishing me well, and also to pass on to the party room a message, which I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to go into, but which I did today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 OK, remember how I said that \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s partner is in quarantine?\par \par \uc2 I have just been informed that, in fact, his partner is the federal minister for foreign affairs \uc2 Marise Payne\uc2 , and she is in quarantine because she has just come back from the US!\par \par \uc2 Talk about a western Sydney power couple!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , is asked whether the recent CFMEU protests have been superspreader events.\par \par \uc2 There has been a significant uptick in cases in the past week in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 Andrews says it would be hard to know, in part due to the fact anti-vaxxers probably aren\u8217\'20\'19t pro-testing either:\par \par \uc2 If that was the case, it would be somewhat challenging to work out. All I can apply is either facts that I\u8217\'20\'19m briefed and I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a briefing today about any patterns... what I would also say, though, just commonsense tells me that if you\u8217\'20\'19re protesting and you don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that this virus is real, then you\u8217\'20\'19re probably not going to go and get tested. And if you do go and get tested, you may not necessarily participate in the contact tracing process.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that that is an absolute, but that\u8217\'20\'19s what logic tells me. I just encourage everybody to go and get the jab. Get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 More baby questions for Perrottet. (It is a feminist catharsis for me to see male politicians asked these questions.)\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 Can you speak to the sacrifices? You might not be able to coach basketball on the weekends anymore. They might be moments you miss.\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 I have not had those conversations.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 Will it be worth it?\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 The opportunity and be privileged to serve the people of the state is enormous. If I did not believe that I could make the difference to improve the lives of every person in this state then I would not be standing up here today.\par \par \uc2 They are decisions that you contemplate, you speak to your family about. Yes, they will be challenges, I know, with that, and perhaps, disappointments of things, other family events and the time that I may not have, but that will drive me, even more, to make sure that every single hour of my day, when I am at work, is dedicated to the improvement of the lives of every person across the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Surge in cases won't delay Victoria's reopening, premier says\par \par \uc2 Victorian premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  says Victoria is still on track for eased restrictions from late October, despite surging case numbers.\par \par \uc2 He says Victoria is still on track, if not ahead of schedule, to meet its October and November vaccination targets.\par \par \uc2 Victoria has recorded a national record for daily case numbers on Tuesday, with 1,763 new cases.\par \par \uc2 At this stage, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got no advice [that] I would have to alter anything on the roadmap; I want to try and give people as much freedom as fast as I can, as [safely] as possible.\par \par \uc2 But I don\u8217\'20\'19t have any advice that sees us having to alter that.\par \par \uc2 He says today\u8217\'20\'19s increase in case numbers is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery serious\u8221\'20\'1D and claims illegal household visits are contributing to high numbers.\par \par \uc2 Then we can open up, it\u8217\'20\'19s only a few weeks away, so we\u8217\'20\'19ve just got to see this through.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get those vaccination numbers and the protection that comes with that to the highest level we can, and it\u8217\'20\'19s 70 and 80 [%].\par \par \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  speaks to reporters in Melbourne on Tuesday. Photograph: James Ross/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Victorian premier \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  is asked about reports today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heraldsun.com.au/coronavirus/yarra-city-council-slugs-covidhit-cafes-bars-for-outdoor-dining/news-story/e0110132943c0cbd6acc00221e0849bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yarra council in inner city Melbourne wants to charge businesses up to $5,000 a year}}}\uc2  for every car park used for outdoor dining.\par \par \uc2 Andrews says he \u8220\'20\'1Clooks forward to them defending that to their ratepayers\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll leave them to defend that. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that they\u8217\'20\'19ve necessarily done that.\par \par \uc2 So that is a matter for them. I would answer your question this way. We\u8217\'20\'19re not doing that. We\u8217\'20\'19re doing the opposite. We\u8217\'20\'19re providing substantial grants to restaurants, bars, cafes and pubs, to move outside and to have the best experience for their patrons that they possibly can.\par \par \uc2 And the reason for that is that you are at dramatically less risk of spreading this if you are outside in the open air. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more to say quite soon about some further support for that outdoor economy to operate as safely as it possibly can once we get past 70%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s talk about the babies. Perrottet\u8217\'20\'19s many babies, that is.\par \par \uc2 Reporter:\par \par \uc2 You said you were going to be the first premier of families. If you were a female leader, you would be asked how you can manage being premier and also a parent of six children, so I think it is fair to ask you that today. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 Perrottet:\par \par \uc2 Well, it is demanding. I mean, being a father, like being a mother, when you have got family commitments, balancing work and family life is a challenge for every single person right across the state.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, I think what I might lose in time I gain in perspective*, and everyone has the attributes, everyone has their strengths and weaknesses, and I am no different to that, but one thing I do know is that I have a very strong team around me.\par \par \uc2 I have a strong family and I have a strong ministerial team who will ensure that our focus is on the people of NSW, and that we come out stronger on the other side. And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take our state from good to great.\par \par \uc2 And, yes, I have family commitments, but that should not disqualify one from the job. I think it enriches you. It gives you different perspective, and with all the different ministers in the team, I think we set ourselves up to make a real difference to the people of our state.\par \par \uc2 * A line only a male politician could pull off.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrACT COVID-19 update (5 October 2021):\par \par \uc2 ?? New cases today: 33\par \par \uc2 ?? Active cases: 384\par \par \uc2 ?? Total recovered cases: 649\par \par \uc2 ?? Total cases: 1038\par \par \uc2 ?? Negative test results (past 24 hours): 2,909\par \par \uc2 ?? In hospital: 14\par \par \uc2 ?? Lives lost: 5 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uwccC1fmRh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uwccC1fmRh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 ACT Health\uc2  (@ACTHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACTHealth/status/1445189627552296960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am BST\par \par \uc2 No new cases in Tasmania but Launceston told to be on 'high alert'\par \par \uc2 Residents in the north of Launceston are being asked to remain on high alert for Covid symptoms and 19 close contacts are in quarantine after a positive case in the city.\par \par \uc2 Acting premier Jeremy Rockliff said no new cases of the Delta strain had been picked up yet but residents needed to be cautious.\par \par \uc2 It comes after a 15-year-old Tasmanian boy who tested positive for Covid-19 visited an LGA in Launceston with his cousin on Sunday afternoon, breaching home quarantine requirements.\par \par \uc2 Whilst the pair were only at the shop for a few minutes, we have declared the IGA as an exposure site.\par \par \uc2 The boy was not wearing a mask during his visit and people who visited the venue on 113 George Town Road between 2.20 pm and 2.45 pm on Saturday have been asked to get tested and isolated.\par \par \uc2 There are 17 primary close contacts and 35 casual contacts related to the case. All 17 close contacts are in quarantine and nine have returned negative test results and the others are pending.\par \par \uc2 Health authorities warned it could be the middle of October until they know if the close and casual contacts have been infected.\par \par \uc2 It is important we monitor the community now for any signs of Covid.\par \par \uc2 Testing hours have been extended at the Launceston clinic.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Perrottet has been asked about his conservative views and how his Catholic faith will affect the way he runs the state. (He is fairly well known for voting against the decriminalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the bill passed two years ago.)\par \par \uc2 My religious views and my Christian faith is something I am incredibly proud of, as many people across our state are. That is something that is personal to me and personal to many people, and I think that is incredibly important.\par \par \uc2 We live in a very diverse society. I think some of the criticism in relation to that diversity has been unfounded and I am proud to live \u8211\'20\'13 and I love our state and I\u8217\'20\'19d love the diversity* and the multicultural backgrounds and the religious backgrounds \u8211\'20\'13 diversity should be celebrated. It should not be criticised.\par \par \uc2 People should judge people on who they are and what they say, not based on some, not based on some religious element, and I am very proud of the fact that I have a strong Christian faith.\par \par \uc2 Does that in any way take away my capacity to serve as premier? Well, I do not think so, and I think it is a sad thing that some people do, but I think people right across our state, in the main, believe in freedom of religion and freedom of the opportunity to serve in public life regardless of what your ethnic background is, what your religious values are.\par \par \uc2 * He has labelled his Catholic faith in terms of diversity. It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that, as of the 2016 census, 22% of the Australian population is Catholic, the largest religious group, second only to \u8220\'20\'1Cno religion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 ACT records 33 new local Covid-19 cases\par \par \uc2 The ACT numbers are in, and they aren\u8217\'20\'19t great. The territory have recorded 33 local Covid-19 cases. Twenty-eight are linked but only six were in quarantine for their entire infectious period.\par \par \uc2 enltrACT {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/covid19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #covid19}}}\uc2  update: 33 new cases. 28 are linked. Five cases are under early investigation.\par \par \uc2 Six were in quarantine, 14 were partly in the community.\par \par \uc2 14 people are in hospital - five in ICU, three are being ventilated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/covid19act?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #covid19act}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karen Barlow (@KJBar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KJBar/status/1445188879846305801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Perrottet has confirmed that environment minister \uc2 Matt Kean\uc2  will become the new treasurer (which is understood to be a key element of the deal the right of the party made with the moderates to get their man Dom in the top job).\par \par \uc2 Hazzard will remain as health minister.\par \par \uc2 Perrottet did not yet have an answer on who will take over the transport portfolio now that \uc2 Andrew Constance\uc2  is too cool for state politics and is heading for Canberra instead.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 And here is the new deputy Liberal leader (not to be mistaken with the deputy premier, who will be the Nationals leader), \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And oh my Lord, his partner has been in quarantine while all of this has been going on!\par \par \uc2 First and foremost, I would really like to acknowledge and thank my family, my parents, Gary and Leslie, my brother John, for their unwavering support over my time as a member of Parliament and the work that I have done right across western Sydney. T o Marise [Payne], who is currently in isolation, what a time to be doing quarantine. Thank you for being a rock during this period of time and this transition.\par \par \uc2 I also want to say a very big thank you to all of the people of Penrith. Yes, our football team won and we have a lot to celebrate and I would not be here today without your commitment and my passion for this community knows no bounds.\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  will be an outstanding premiere of NSW. He knows how to do the heavy lifting. He knows that you run a budget. This is a team that is focused on everyone across the state. We have been through immense challenges whether it is the city, the coast, the suburbs or the bush, will be focused on the people of NSW, we will come out of this pandemic stronger than ever before and we will get people back in work.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Perrottet says there will be no cabinet reshuffle until the government is through the current reopening.\par \par \uc2 He also says that as well as being an \u8220\'20\'1Cinfrastructure premier\u8221\'20\'1D he will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily premier\u8221\'20\'1D. His focus, he says, will be\u8221\'20\'1Don how we can make life better for working families, living the Liberal values of opportunity, aspiration and hard work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Perrottet will 'continue the plan' for reopening that Berejiklian started\par \par \uc2 One of the big questions now that pro-business Perrottet is leading the state is, of course, will the new premier stick to Berejiklian\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 reopening plan, or throw open the floodgates early?\par \par \uc2 He says that he will continue the reopening process that Berejiklian started.\par \par \uc2 Now, while there are still more challenging days to come, there is light at the end of the tunnel, thanks to the way that everyone across our state has responded.\par \par \uc2 We want NSW to bounce back stronger, safer and more successful than ever before, to get back to the life that we love and the freedoms that we hold dear.\par \par \uc2 As a former treasurer, I know that a strong society needs a strong economy, and that is why our first priority will be to continue the plan that we have started: keeping people safe, opening up the economy and securing our recovery.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 The new NSW premier, \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2 , is speaking now in his first press conference as leader of the state.\par \par \uc2 He has started by publicly stating his support for embattled \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  as she officially resigns as premier and prepares to go before Icac.\par \par \uc2 I want to acknowledge that the events of the last few days have been difficult and I think we all understand why.\par \par \uc2 Unexpected change can bring uncertainty and, sometimes, many, they can feel unsettling. But as hard as it may be, we all have a duty as a state to keep going.\par \par \uc2 Today begins a new chapter for New South Wales, and one that we will all write together. I am honoured that my colleagues have asked me to write that chapter as premier, and I thank them for the confidence that they have put in me.\par \par \uc2 The first thing I want to do today is to acknowledge my predecessor and pay tribute to her, \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 , whose strong and steady leadership has seen us through so many difficult challenges. Everyone would agree that her hard work, tireless dedication and total commitment to her job was second to none. She has been an inspiring role model for many, especially women and migrant communities, and that is just one of the reasons why I believe there has been such an outpouring of support over the last few days.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW has recorded 608 new locally acquired cases of Covid-19 and another seven people have died, as schooling and elective surgery resumes in some areas.\par \par \uc2 The daily case numbers are the lowest since August and it is the fourth day in a row with fewer than 700 cases, reports AAP.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 NSW Health\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dr J eremy McAnulty said in today\u8217\'20\'19s update, there had also been \u8220\'20\'1Cslight decline\u8221\'20\'1D in testing numbers.\par \par \uc2 We really encourage people to come forward for testing as we get closer to more people getting vaccinated in the community.\par \par \uc2 It is really important we all maintain our vigilance for symptoms and come forward for testing so we don\u8217\'20\'19t miss cases.\par \par \uc2 There were 85,642 Covid-19 tests reported to 8pm on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Six men and one woman with Covid-19 have died, bringing the toll for the current outbreak to 385 deaths.\par \par \uc2 Five of the people who died were not vaccinated while two had received one dose of a Covid-19 vaccine.\par \par \uc2 There are 978 people in hospital with Covid-19 in NSW, with 190 in intensive care, and 94 on ventilators.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s current CHO has credited Hajkowicz, who will take over her role from 1 November, for the state only recording seven deaths from Covid-19 throughout the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Young:\par \par \uc2 Every single one of those deaths, I regretted, and we all regret it, but at least it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t more. That was due to the work that he\u8217\'20\'19s done.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 New Zealand reports 24 new local Covid-19 cases\par \par \uc2 New Zealand has announced 24 new community cases of Covid 19 today \u8211\'20\'13 18 in Auckland and six in Waikato.\par \par \uc2 That brings its total outbreak to 1,381. Seven of today\u8217\'20\'19s 24 cases are still unlinked, with health authorities investigating to try and trace them back to existing cases. The country has 32 people hospitalised and seven in ICU.\par \par \uc2 The cases come a day after the prime minister, \uc2 Jacinda Ardern\uc2 , announced a loosening of restrictions in Auckland, the centre of the outbreak: first by allowing outdoor gathering and returning young children to school, and with plans to reopen hospitality and retail businesses in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Ardern announced today that the country would also be introducing vaccine certificates for large-scale events \u8211\'20\'13 and warned those hoping to go to summer festivals that they would need to get vaccinated now. She said the government was also looking at whether to make those certificates compulsory for restaurants, cafes and bars too.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s transport minister, \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2 , fronted the media this morning alongside major infrastructure authority boss Corey Hannett as construction resumes for around 10,000 workers across the state.\par \par \uc2 Most sites will return at 25% capacity today, while some critical projects will be at full capacity after a two-week hiatus over Covid-19 non-compliance.\par \par \uc2 Allan and Hannett were unable to confirm exactly how many workers had been vaccinated since the mandate was introduced, but said of 2,000 workers returning to Metro Tunnel sites, 99% had been vaccinated and 95% of workers at level crossing sites were vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Construction companies require an updated Covid-safe plan to operate, and all workers must have had at least one vaccine dose.\par \par \uc2 Allan:\par \par \uc2 A massive effort has gone into getting the 18,000 strong Big Build workforce vaccinated and project sites ready to return to work in compliance with new construction public health orders... to stay open and continue to hit those roadmap targets, we do need each and every worksite to be Covid-safe, to comply with the rules.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Queensland introduces new chief health officer\par \par \uc2 Queensland is welcoming in a new chief health officer who will take over from \uc2 Dr Jeannette Young\uc2  when she takes over her new role of the governor of Queensland (what a promotion!)\par \par \uc2 Dr Krispin Hajkowicz will take over the role, who has played a large role in Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 management over the past 18 months.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrMinister for Health, Greg Hunt and Department of Health Secretary, Professor \uc2 Brendan Murphy\uc2  will hold a press conference at 12pm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/auspol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #auspol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Political Alert (@political_alert) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/political_alert/status/1445182112861093892?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrDr Young said genomic sequencing from the Fitzgibbon woman in her 50s who tested positive on Monday is similar to Delta clusters in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @MartySilk (@MartySilkHack) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MartySilkHack/status/1445181079397158913?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Queensland premier Annastacia Palaszczuk says the woman who tested positive went straight into hotel quarantine on arrival\par \par \uc2 Luckily, as Victoria is a red zone, everyone else on her flight, Q562, was also headed straight into isolation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Queensland records two local Covid-19 cases\par \par \uc2 OK jumping across the Queensland now (lots of presser on right now).\par \par \uc2 Queensland has recorded two new locally acquired cases.\par \par \uc2 One is a three-year-old girl, a household contact in the aviation cluster.\par \par \uc2 The second is a 19-year-old woman who arrived on a flight from Victoria.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Victorian government will be publishing vaccination data by suburb on its website from today. They\u8217\'20\'19ve identified 27 postcodes with first dose coverage rates of under 75 per cent. They include areas such as Campbellfield, Frankston North, Kensington and St Kilda. Statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CkHIBpQTyy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CkHIBpQTyy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Benita Kolovos (@benitakolovos) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benitakolovos/status/1445178323827527683?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrews:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m also pleased today to be able to announce that round one of the vaccination enhancement grants program for those priority local government areas in Melbourne have been finalised.\par \par \uc2 These are the GP and community pharmacy grants to allow them to employ more staff, expand their hours, rent additional space, fill out additional space. Ultimately, they\u8217\'20\'19re grants that allow them to get more jabs in more arms than would otherwise be the case. Round one has now been finalised.\par \par \uc2 There are 300 GPs and community pharmacists who will be sharing in that $1.5m in additional support. It\u8217\'20\'19s common sense.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely about doing those very practical, very local things that can make a big difference to the number of people who are moving through those settings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria's Latrobe Valley will emerge from lockdown from midnight\par \par \uc2 Andrews says the Latrobe City LGA, a region in Gippsland encompassing the regional city of Traralgon, will come out of its seven-day lockdown from midnight tonight, despite some new cases being recorded in the region today.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m very pleased to be able to inform you, and particularly the people of Latrobe city, that their seven-day lockdown will end at midnight tonight. There are some new cases in Latrobe today.\par \par \uc2 Deputy secretary Kate Mattson can speak to those in a moment, but we feel we have a good understanding of that outbreak, and we can move Latrobe to the regional Victorian settings from midnight tonight. I\u8217\'20\'19m very grateful to everybody across Latrobe city for the contribution they\u8217\'20\'19ve made.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the full, official statement from \uc2 Rob Stokes\uc2 , who has just lost his bid to become NSW premier.\par \par \uc2 Our party room has made their choice, and made it emphatically.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d like to congratulate my great friend \uc2 Dom Perrottet\uc2  on being chosen as our new leader and becoming the NSW premier.\par \par \uc2 Dom has proven himself as an outstanding treasurer and will be a great premier. He has my full support.\par \par \uc2 The community now rightfully expect us to get on with the job we were elected to do and ensure that we recover from the pandemic and regain our freedom.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrews:\par \par \uc2 As you would recall, we received more than 100,000 somewhat unexpected Moderna doses from the commonwealth. We\u8217\'20\'19re grateful to have them. And those appointments are now open.\par \par \uc2 Please \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s no shortage of appointments available right now.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re beyond that kind of supply constraint phase. We\u8217\'20\'19re now into a phase where there are appointments. You can go to more than 55 state hubs. You can go to hundreds and hundreds of community pharmacies. You can go and see your trusted GP and access those vaccines.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrews:\par \par \uc2 83.2% of those over 16 have now received a first dose of a Covid-19 vaccine, 53% have now received a second dose.\par \par \uc2 Those numbers continue to steadily climb, and we\u8217\'20\'19re very grateful to everybody who\u8217\'20\'19s playing their part as we look to get as many Victorians vaccinated as possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , is giving details of the four Covid-19 infected people who died in the last day.\par \par \uc2 I regret to report that four Victorians have lost their lives with Covid-19 \u8211\'20\'13 a man in his 80s from Whittlesea, a woman in her 70s from Hume, a man in his 60s from Whitehorse, and a woman in her 60s from Banyule.\par \par \uc2 We extend our deepest sympathies and our condolences to the friends and family of those four Victorians. This will be a very challenging and difficult time for them.\par \par \uc2 517 people are currently in hospital with Covid-19. 101 of those are in intensive care. 66 are on a ventilator. Of the people in hospital yesterday, 66% were unvaccinated. 28% had one dose. Just 6% were fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 NSW records 608 Covid-19 cases and seven deaths\par \par \uc2 enltrNSW recorded 608 new locally acquired cases of COVID-19 in the 24 hours to 8pm last night.\par \par \uc2 No new cases were acquired overseas. The total number of cases in NSW since the beginning of\par \par \uc2 the pandemic is 65,687. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BzGPYZ3rtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BzGPYZ3rtq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 NSW Health\uc2  (@NSWHealth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHealth/status/1445177169676693505?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The Victorian premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  , is speaking now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights organisation Marie Stopes Australia have released a statement urging the new NSW premier to publically commit to not changing or rolling back any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care laws.\par \par \uc2 The conservative Catholic politician voted against decriminalising access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in NSW, when the law was passed two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Managing director Jamal Hakim said:\par \par \uc2 I want to extend my congratulations to the incoming NSW premier, \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  on his elevation to the role.\par \par \uc2 It is critical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services are not restricted under his leadership.\par \par \uc2 We do not want to see NSW move backwards in relation to sexual and reproductive healthcare provision in the state, particularly in relation to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. We have fought for too long to have this human right put in jeopardy once again.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in NSW is a postcode lottery and funding still needs to be embedded to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services, particularly for women and pregnant people in the regions.\par \par \uc2 Premier Perrottet must commit to making no changes that would see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care wound back or restricted during his term.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 undltr11am\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WhatTimeIsTheVicPresser (@WhatTimeDan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhatTimeDan/status/1445174592809541635?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 We are expecting to hear from the Victorian leaders in about 15 minutes, after recording the highest ever single day of cases for any state in Australia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 And here is the health minister, \uc2 Brad Hazzard\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 I welcome the new premier and he\u8217\'20\'19ll do a great job looking after the people in New South Wales.\par \par \uc2 What happens is we have a premier who will make sure the citizens of the state are looked after. I look forward to that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 And here is the defeated \uc2 Rob Stokes\uc2 , who is taking his loss pretty gracefully.\par \par \uc2 The party room had a democratic vote. I always said I would give people a choice. They have chosen emphatically, democracy is the winner.\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  will be a magnificent premier and he has my undivided loyalty and support. And I will use every ounce of strength in my body to make sure that he is re-elected as premier in NSW when we go to the polls in 2023.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 OK, the people are coming out of the room! Time to hear from the new premier of NSW, \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an honour and absolute privilege to be elected as the parliamentary leader of the Liberal party, the premier of NSW. Alongside my deputy leader, \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I really appreciate the trust my colleagues have put in me today, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll have more to say a bit later in about an hour\u8217\'20\'19s time. Thanks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrTransport Infrastructure Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JacintaAllanMP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JacintaAllanMP}}}\uc2  and Major Infrastructure Infrastructure Authority boss Corey Hannett unable to say exactly how many workers have been vaccinated, as construction opens back up.. some critical projects at 100%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/10NewsFirstMelb?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @10NewsFirstMelb}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/springst?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #springst}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2T9r61OZrl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2T9r61OZrl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Love (@SimoLove) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimoLove/status/1445170564235026434?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 enltrDeputy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWNationals?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NSWNationals}}}\uc2  leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PaulTooleMP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PaulTooleMP}}}\uc2  will hold a standup in Bathurst at 12pm today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Breaking?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Breaking}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mollie Gorman (@_MollieGorman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_MollieGorman/status/1445169891091226625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  will be the new premier of NSW\par \par \uc2 The Liberal party whip, Adam Crouch, has just announced the results of the NSW Liberal party room vote.\par \par \uc2 As expected, \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  will be deputy.\par \par \uc2 Good morning everyone, as the government whip I can confirm that the New South Wales parliamentary Liberal party have met this morning to fill a vacancy for leader.\par \par \uc2 A ballot has been held and I can declare that the honourable \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  has been elected to the leadership position of the NSW Liberal parliamentary party and I can also confirm that the deputy position has been awarded to the honourable \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2 . Thank you all.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Nine news is reporting that Perrottet has won the vote 39 to 5:\par \par \uc2 filtrPerrottet 39 Stokes 5. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/9NewsSyd?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @9NewsSyd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris O'Keefe (@cokeefe9) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cokeefe9/status/1445167714859839488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Scott Morrison has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/gladys-berejiklian-approached-by-senior-liberals-to-run-in-warringah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuelled suggestions Gladys Berejiklian could move to federal politics}}}\uc2  or be given a governmental appointment, saying she has \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot more to contribute\u8221\'20\'1D and can choose \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat she wants to do next\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Despite that encouragement, the prime minister also tempered expectations by noting that the former New South Wales premier would have to \u8220\'20\'1Cdeal with the issues before her\u8221\'20\'1D, in reference to mid-October hearings before the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/independent-commission-against-corruption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Independent Commission Against Corruption}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Berejiklian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/01/nsw-premier-gladys-berejiklian-resigns-after-icac-announces-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stood down as premier on Friday and quit parliament}}}\uc2  after Icac revealed it was investigating whether she had been involved in \u8220\'20\'1Ca breach of public trust\u8221\'20\'1D between 2012 and 2018 because of her relationship with the former Wagga Wagga MP \uc2 Daryl Maguire\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/gladys-berejiklian-approached-by-senior-liberals-to-run-in-warringah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian Australia revealed}}}\uc2  that Berejiklian has been approached by senior Liberals in NSW to run for the federal seat of Warringah against the independent Zali Steggall, who won the normally blue-ribbon seat from Tony Abbott.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full report below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/gladys-berejiklian-has-a-lot-more-to-contribute-scott-morrison-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian has \u8216\'20\'18a lot more to contribute\u8217\'20\'19, Scott Morrison says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Nine news is reporting that NSW Liberal MP Ray Willians has had two inconclusive rapid Covid-19 tests and must now go for a PRC swab.\par \par \uc2 He will however still be able to vote remotely for the new party leader.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\uc2  : Liberal MP Ray Williams has had two inconclusive RATs on arrival at Parliament for the leadership vote and is now being sent for a PCR test. Arrangements being made for him to vote remotely. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/9NewsSyd?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @9NewsSyd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Daniels (@lizziedaniels) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lizziedaniels/status/1445158694660894728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 By the way, we will be hearing from the Queensland premier at 10am AEST, 11am ADST.\par \par \uc2 The state had an unlinked case yesterday, although as the person was double vaccinated and hadn\u8217\'20\'19t appeared to transmit the virus to any of their close contacts the state was not plunged into lockdown.\par \par \uc2 It will be interesting to see how things have panned out with increased testing overnight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 A reminder that when it comes to the bird of the year competition this blog is not a non-partisan, unbiased source. We are FIRMLY team pelican and you should go vote for the majestic creature right now!\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/ng-interactive/2021/sep/27/australian-bird-of-the-year-2021-vote-now-for-your-favourite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian bird of the year 2021: vote for your favourite #birdoftheyear}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voting is beginning any moment in the NSW Liberal party room for their new leader, and therefore the new state premier. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you all the updates as soon as I can.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The body of a man who went missing while swimming at a beach in Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s north has been found, reports AAP.\par \par \uc2 Emergency services were called to Obelisk Beach off Chowder Bay Road, Middle Head, just after 5pm on Monday following reports a swimmer had not resurfaced.\par \par \uc2 A group of people were swimming out to a yacht anchored off the beach when the man, 38, disappeared underwater, NSW police said.\par \par \uc2 Officers from the Marine Area Command attended and conducted a search with the help of PolAir, Marine Rescue and NSW Maritime.\par \par \uc2 Police divers found his body about 8.20pm and he is yet to be formally identified.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrPrime Minister Scott Morrison on whether there will ever be a federal anti-corruption watchdog, like the ICAC in NSW:\par \par \uc2 "I'm sure there are millions of people who've seen what's happened to \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 , they'll understand that's a pretty good call not to follow that model."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @MartySilk (@MartySilkHack) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MartySilkHack/status/1445153071516958720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Australia records no new Covid-19 cases overnight\par \par \uc2 South Australia\u8217\'20\'19s chief health officer, \uc2 Nicola Spurrier\uc2 , told ABC radio in Adelaide this morning that there have been no new Covid-19 cases overnight.\par \par \uc2 Tough new restrictions were introduced for Mount Gambier and two other council areas in South Australia yesterday after a woman in her 40s tested positive to Covid-19. It is believed she spent time in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 The restrictions came into place from 4pm and are expected to be in force for at least seven days.\par \par \uc2 Areas affected include Mount Gambier city, the district council of Grant and Wattle Range council in the state\u8217\'20\'19s south-east.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prime minister accuses Queensland of trying to extort hospital funding\par \par \uc2 The prime minister has accused Queensland of using Covid-19 to \u8220\'20\'1Cextort\u8221\'20\'1D more money for public hospitals, reports AAP.\par \par \uc2 Hospitals are jointly funded by state and federal government, but deputy premier \uc2 Steven Miles\uc2  says the commonwealth has artificially capped spending growth at 6.5%, which could prevent hospitals from being able to meet demand when the state reopens.\par \par \uc2 Prime minister Scott Morrison says there is already enough federal funding for Queensland hospitals, and premier Annastacia Palaszczuk is trying to use state border closures to \u8220\'20\'1Cextort\u8221\'20\'1D more cash.\par \par \uc2 He told Nine\u8217\'20\'19s Today program today:\par \par \uc2 She has to take that up with the Queensland people then. I mean, to go down this point and say: \u8216\'20\'18Well, you know, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to hold the federal government to ransom and seek to extort from them money on the basis of Covid\u8217\'20\'19, I just don\u8217\'20\'19t think is the right way to go.\par \par \uc2 The commonwealth had contributed to half the cost of propping up state and territory health systems against Covid-19, Mr Morrison said, a commitment which totalled about $30 billion nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Of course there are challenges but as a state government, they\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be responsible for their state health system.\par \par \uc2 NSW is getting on with it, so are Victoria and the ACT, so Queensland needs to get on with it.\par \par \uc2 Miles said on Monday every state and territory had asked for extra support for hospitals to deal with Covid-19 and Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s request was not unusual.\par \par \uc2 He said the 6.5% cap on federal spending growth was arbitrary as it did not take into account increased demand due to the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The pandemic will clearly drive demand that is greater than that,\u8221\'20\'1D the deputy premier told reporters.\par \par \uc2 And given that our hospitals are funded as a partnership, we would like the federal government to increase their contribution to that partnership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reminder that we will be finding out the result of the NSW Liberal leadership vote at 10am, where it is likely treasurer Dominic Perrotett will be made the new premier of NSW.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former senior judge Stephen Charles has criticised \uc2 Barnaby Joyce\uc2  for likening the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/new-south-wales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New South Wales}}}\uc2  anti-corruption watchdog to the \u8220\'20\'1CSpanish Inquisition\u8221\'20\'1D, saying the deputy prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery silly\u8221\'20\'1D and showed the federal government had no desire to be held accountable for its own integrity failings.\par \par \uc2 Joyce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/barnaby-joyce-condemns-spanish-inquisition-icac-saying-it-makes-mps-terrified-to-do-their-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led the attacks}}}\uc2  on the \uc2 NSW Independent Commission Against Corruption\uc2  (Icac) on Monday, arguing it was working \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very badly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This is not the great righteous process, it\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit Spanish Inquisition. We elect politicians, not bureaucrats. People should be the final arbiter... The bureaucracy reigns supreme here and politicians are basically terrified to do their job.\par \par \uc2 Joyce was supported by fellow National \uc2 Matt Canavan\uc2 , who said he agreed \u8220\'20\'1Cwith that sentiment\u8221\'20\'1D. The attacks on the commission follow earlier criticisms by former federal attorney general Philip Ruddock and the current NSW health minister, \uc2 Brad Hazzard\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read the full report below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/very-silly-for-barnaby-joyce-to-compare-nsw-icac-to-spanish-inquisition-former-senior-judge-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Very silly\u8217\'20\'19 for Barnaby Joyce to compare NSW Icac to Spanish Inquisition, former senior judge says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 And just like that, we have to extend how far up the graph goes.\par \par \uc2 Here is today\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 number on the Victoria infection graph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/embed/aus/2020/yacht-charter-v19/index.html?key=1BaHphN6yIfVk10EHlOFPlYSq8qLI8IHSiEJLZ2WVuAg&location=docsdata"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victorian case number graph}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Australia has secured 300,000 courses of molnupiravir, an antiviral capsule to treat Covid-19 that could be in use by early 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Morrison government has struck a supply agreement with MSD to provide the oral treatment if it is approved by the \uc2 Therapeutic Goods Administration\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/01/covid-antiviral-pill-halves-hospitalisations-and-deaths-maker-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Molnupiravir has been shown}}}\uc2  to prevent hospitalisation, serious illness and death in Covid patients, although it is still in late-stage clinical trials.\par \par \uc2 It is one of a number of treatments that can make the virus less severe, along with sotrovimab and remdesivir, which are already in use. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2  authorities stress vaccination is still the most effective tool for preventing severe illness.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/05/australia-strikes-deal-for-new-covid-pill-that-could-be-used-in-treatment-by-early-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia strikes deal for new Covid pill that could be used in treatment by early 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of! It seems that \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , WhatsApp and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  are back in business. Well for me at least.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrTwitter has been waiting for this moment when WhatsApp, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  are down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cpAerk0SVT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cpAerk0SVT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pedro Mbugua (@PedroMbugua_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PedroMbugua_/status/1445097450386169858?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 As Australians are waking up this morning, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  is still down across the entire world.\par \par \uc2 The outage is not just affecting \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , but other \uc2 Facebook\uc2 -owned properties including Messenger, \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and WhatsApp.\par \par \uc2 The simplest way to describe what is happening is that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  pushed out an update that is supposed to tell the rest of the internet where to find \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s servers, but effectively deleted all that information, meaning to the internet it looks like \uc2 Facebook\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist at the moment.\par \par \uc2 Normally that is an easy fix, but as my colleague Alex Hern has been tweeting overnight, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  runs everything through its \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , from the sites itself to all the applications and internal infrastructure, so it prevents \uc2 Facebook\uc2  from sending a correction message, and even goes as far as locking \uc2 Facebook\uc2  employees out of the physical building, because their passes no longer work.\par \par \uc2 enltrand the ability to log-in to the system that would send the follow-up message\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 alex hern (@alexhern) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexhern/status/1445130877588082694?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 According to reports, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  has now sent a team over to its servers to manually reset them. So it might be a little while longer before you can return to \uc2 Facebook\uc2  or \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oh and if that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough, Victoria have had another earthquake.\par \par \uc2 enltrA magnitude 3.0 earthquake has been recorded at 7:17am in Rawson, Victoria this morning. So far there are 2 felt reports, and no reports of damage. More info via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeoscienceAus?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GeoscienceAus}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BfEDYfbMOY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BfEDYfbMOY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xO5xxi32fO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xO5xxi32fO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VICSES News (@vicsesnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vicsesnews/status/1445137000214925312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Victoria records 1,763 new Covid-19 cases\par \par \uc2 The Victorian numbers are in and they are not good news.\par \par \uc2 The state has recorded Australia\u8217\'20\'19s highest ever day of Covid cases, with 1,763 new infections.\par \par \uc2 This means Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s peak is now higher than NSW.\par \par \uc2 enltrReported yesterday: 1,763 new local cases and 0 cases acquired overseas.\par \par \uc2 - 35,253 vaccines administered\par \par \uc2 - 62,189 test results received\par \par \uc2 - Sadly, 4 people with COVID-19 have died\par \par \uc2 More later: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OCCFTAtS1P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OCCFTAtS1P}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19Vic?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19Vic}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19VicData?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19VicData}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V9dumLMJ2A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/V9dumLMJ2A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VicGovDH (@VicGovDH)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VicGovDH/status/1445140582205059077?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Up to the new premier to determine' whether NSW sticks to roadmap out of lockdown, Greg Hunt says\par \par \uc2 Now on to the whole NSW situation.\par \par \uc2 Host Lisa Millar:\par \par \uc2 What do you think the new New South Wales premier will do with the state\u8217\'20\'19s roadmap out of lockdown?\par \par \uc2 Hunt:\par \par \uc2 So, all our advice and it will be up to the new premier to determine this, but all our advice is there\u8217\'20\'19s a clear broad commitment to the roadmap right across the NSW government.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re at over 88% first vaccinations. They\u8217\'20\'19re continuing to vaccinate at a higher rate. The cases are coming down. Obviously, no one is out of the woods anywhere yet. But we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the case numbers having more than halved in NSW and I hope the trend can continue as vaccinations are up, cases are down.\par \par \uc2 The public have done a herculean job as we know. I think there\u8217\'20\'19s a strong clear commitment to that roadmap, to the process of protecting the state, protecting the people, but giving people their lives back and the capacity for families to meet for weddings and funerals and people to attend births and to meet with beautiful new grandchildren and to do all the things that underline our humanity.\par \par \uc2 Federal health minister Greg Hunt. Photograph: Mike Bowers/The Guardian\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 So while all of this politics nonsense has been going on, the federal government has invested in a new antiviral pill that has the potential to help stop Covid-19 disease from progressing to its acute and life-threatening stages.\par \par \uc2 Health minister Greg Hunt has been out and about this morning spruiking the government\u8217\'20\'19s purchase and is speaking with ABC News Breakfast now.\par \par \uc2 It is an important step forward. It\u8217\'20\'19s molnupiravir, it\u8217\'20\'19s made by Merck, and it\u8217\'20\'19s an oral pill. The treatments we had until now have had to be done through hospital infusion.\par \par \uc2 We have purchased 300,000 courses. It\u8217\'20\'19s provided to people early after diagnosis if they have risk factors of potentially progressing to hospitalisation.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a five-day course, two pills a day. Critically the clinical trials show it reduces the risk of hospitalisation and death by half.\par \par \uc2 It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t prevent Covid, it\u8217\'20\'19s about treating it, and significantly reducing the risk so it\u8217\'20\'19s a complement to vaccination. And these two things together are all part of the process of protecting Australians and saving lives, but also giving them the pathway back.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The New South Wales treasurer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/dominic-perrottet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Perrottet}}}\uc2 , has emerged as the man most likely to take over as the state\u8217\'20\'19s premier following \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bombshell resignation last week.\par \par \uc2 The treasurer has been working hard on building a profile in recent months (perhaps in the hope of the premier\u8217\'20\'19s job becoming vacant), but despite serving in the NSW government ministry since 2014, for many voters, Perrottet is a largely unknown quantity.\par \par \uc2 So who is the would-be premier of Australia\u8217\'20\'19s largest state?\par \par \uc2 Find out below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/conservative-warrior-economic-reformer-premier-meet-dominic-perrottet-nsws-likely-next-leader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative warrior, economic reformer, premier? Meet Dominic Perrottet, NSW\u8217\'20\'19s likely next leader}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrNSW Government Whip Adam Crouch will announce the new Leader of the Parliamentary Liberal Party at the completion of the Liberal Party Room Meeting, which begins at 10am {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nswpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nswpol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Political Alert (@political_alert)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/political_alert/status/1445132949939109888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 So now that Icac has felled the NSW premier, \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 , attention has turned to the lack of a federal counterpart for the agency.\par \par \uc2 Some say this is proof that a federal Icac is absolutely essential, others say it\u8217\'20\'19s proof that such an agency should never touch the hallowed halls of Canberra\u8217\'20\'19s parliament house.\par \par \uc2 Prime minister Scott Morrison was asked about this while speaking to Sunrise this morning and he was clear that his government wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be considering the NSW Icac model.\par \par \uc2 Host David Koch:\par \par \uc2 New South Wales. It has put a lot of focus from the general public on Icac. Who are they, and who are they responsible to? Who reviews them? Does Icac need to be reformed?\par \par \uc2 Morrison:\par \par \uc2 It is certainly not a model we ever consider at a federal level, anything that has been on display for some time. You have got to have processes that assume people are innocent before they are thought to be guilty. That is a real problem. It is not a model we have ever contemplated going at a federal level.\par \par \uc2 We have a set of arrangements at a federal level that can be built upon, but certainly not going down that path, and I\u8217\'20\'19m sure there are millions of people who are see what has happened to \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  and understand that [it\u8217\'20\'19s] a pretty good call not to follow that model.\par \par \uc2 enltr"It's certainly not a model we'd ever consider at a federal level"\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ScottMorrisonMP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ScottMorrisonMP}}}\uc2  on claims NSW's anti-corruption watchdog wields too much power. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/c9QT4o0mIh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/c9QT4o0mIh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sunrise (@sunriseon7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sunriseon7/status/1445124843951722506?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Berejiklian could make a great prime minister if cleared by Icac, NSW transport minister says\par \par \uc2 Andrew Constance\uc2  has given his former premier, \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 , a massive plug on ABC radio this morning, stating that as long as she can get this whole Icac thing cleared up, she would make a fantastic prime minister.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/gladys-berejiklian-approached-by-senior-liberals-to-run-in-warringah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian Australia revealed yesterday that Berejiklian has been approached by senior Liberals to run for the federal seat of Warringah}}}\uc2 , with some federal MPs stating she was seriously considering the proposal.\par \par \uc2 Constance was asked this morning if he thought she should take up this opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Yeah, absolutely. I think if Glad can get cleared up \u8211\'20\'13 whatever these issues are, through the public hearing process \u8211\'20\'13 I think she\u8217\'20\'19d be unreal.\par \par \uc2 You couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have more hard-working, deeply principled Australian female politician* and \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  so, yeah, if that if that\u8217\'20\'19s an option, why not?...\par \par \uc2 But do I think she\u8217\'20\'19s got the capacity to be prime minister of Australia? You bet.\par \par \uc2 *Umm, mate, did you really need to say \u8220\'20\'1C female politician\u8221\'20\'1D here.\par \par \uc2 A man looks at flowers and signs placed by members of the public outside the local office of former NSW premier \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  on 2 October. Photograph: David Gray/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Prime Minister tells ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kochie_online?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kochie_online}}}\uc2  ? the NSW ICAC is not a model he\u8217\'20\'19s considering for any federal corruption body {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d1hYzSYbyA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d1hYzSYbyA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anna Henderson (@annajhenderson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/annajhenderson/status/1445121111973269511?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outgoing NSW transport minister \uc2 Andrew Constance\uc2  is speaking to ABC radio now about his decision to resign from state politics in order to make a federal run.\par \par \uc2 Constance has defended his choice to leave as the party faces a tremulous leadership change, but said it \u8220\'20\'1Cwould\u8217\'20\'19ve been ideal\u8221\'20\'1D for the deputy premier and Nationals leader \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2  to stick around until the waters calmed.\par \par \uc2 After 18-and-a-half years in state politics and 10-and-a-half years as a cabinet minister, with an incoming premier there\u8217\'20\'19s going to always be a degree of change...\par \par \uc2 Chris Minns\uc2  is saying that it\u8217\'20\'19s selfish [for \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  to resign]. \uc2 Chris Minns\uc2  would do well to look around his own team to see who\u8217\'20\'19s shopping their CVs.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Constance\uc2 . Photograph: Joel Carrett/AAP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrAsks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PatsKarvelas?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PatsKarvelas}}}\uc2  : Should the Deputy Premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2  have stayed on to provide stability?\par \par \uc2 "That would've been ideal."\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewConstance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AndrewConstance}}}\uc2 , outgoing NSW Transport Minister\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 RN Breakfast (@RNBreakfast) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RNBreakfast/status/1445127189410709506?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 4, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Security agencies need stronger oversight: ANU paper\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s national security apparatus has become \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most complex and sophisticated in the world\u8221\'20\'1D but oversight functions have not kept up, according to a paper published today.\par \par \uc2 Dr William A Stoltz, the senior adviser for public policy at the Australian National University\u8217\'20\'19s national security college, believes the Parliamentary Joint Standing Committee on Intelligence and Security (PJCIS) needs more support given the wide remit of its oversight work:\par \par \uc2 The PJCIS is now dealing with arguably the most complex and arcane aspects of government business, especially for members who have had limited previous exposure to law enforcement, security or intelligence issues.\par \par \uc2 For example, recently the committee has been simultaneously considering inquiries into extremism and radicalisation, foreign intelligence collection, access to telecommunications data, the listing of terrorist organisations, the security of critical infrastructure, criminal use of the dark web, oversight reforms, and agencies\u8217\'20\'19 expenditure.\par \par \uc2 In the paper, Stoltz renews calls for the PJCIS to be given the power to commission the inspector-general of intelligence and security to undertake special reviews and investigations \u8220\'20\'1Cso that parliament can gain access to operational insights on its own terms\u8221\'20\'1D. That would ensure that parliamentary representatives \u8220\'20\'1Creceive more information about intelligence activities than what agencies tell them\u8221\'20\'1D. He also says PJCIS members\u8217\'20\'19 staffers should be given high-level security clearances so they can better support MPs and senators to perform their oversight function.\par \par \uc2 Stoltz also proposes the appointment of a \u8220\'20\'1Cminster for intelligence\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cimprove the ability of cabinet to exercise informed, strategic leadership over Australia\u8217\'20\'19s modern intelligence and security enterprise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This role would be performed by an assistant minister or a junior minister. They would not be responsible for approving specific intelligence collection activities, but would advise the cabinet\u8217\'20\'19s national security committee and senior ministers on agency budgets, capabilities, and legislative reforms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning everyone, it\u8217\'20\'19s Matilda Boseley here and we have a jam-packed Tuesday ahead.\par \par \uc2 First up, of course, we have the impending NSW Liberal leadership vote for the new premier taking place today, and it seems almost certain that treasurer \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  will be taking the top job.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/oct/04/conservative-warrior-economic-reformer-premier-meet-dominic-perrottet-nsws-likely-next-leader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Long touted as the premier-in-waiting}}}\uc2 , the treasurer struck a deal with his moderate colleagues over the weekend to make jobs minister \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  his deputy and promote environment minister \uc2 Matt Kean\uc2  to treasurer if they backed him.\par \par \uc2 Former prime minister and Liberal party elder J ohn Howard has also backed Perrottet, saying he is driven and reform-focused.\par \par \uc2 But planning minister \uc2 Rob Stokes\uc2  is refusing to back down, and the big question now is \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat will he do if the vote doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go his way\u8221\'20\'1D. Could this be the fourth byelection the Coalition must contend with out of this shakeup?\par \par \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  leaves his home in Sydney on Tuesday morning. Photograph: Joel Carrett/AAP\par \par \uc2 Down south in Victoria, tradies are starting up their tools as a two-week pause on construction is lifted across Melbourne and other locked-down areas.\par \par \uc2 Construction workers can return to worksites on Tuesday as long as they meet strict safeguards and have at least had their first coronavirus vaccination.\par \par \uc2 The industry-wide mandate, and other restrictions, sparked a protest outside the CFMEU\u8217\'20\'19s Melbourne headquarters two weeks ago, causing the government to announce the sector would down tools for a fortnight-long reset.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s chief health officer, \uc2 Prof Brett Sutton\uc2 , could not say what proportion of the industry is now vaccinated but said tens of thousands of workers have rolled up their sleeves and he was confident the industry had learned the \u8220\'20\'1Chard lesson\u8221\'20\'1D and reflected on compliance issues with masks and tearooms.\par \par \uc2 OK, with that, why don\u8217\'20\'19t we jump into the day?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 2021-10-04T20:27:24Z 2021-10-05T08:00:04Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/477c4854877dafa016efa88dddee87b9902a5210/0_117_5178_3107/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/477c4854877dafa016efa88dddee87b9902a5210/0_117_5178_3107/500.jpg}}}\uc2  An iron ore mine in the Pilbara. The Bathurst MP Paul Toole has confirmed he will run for the NSW Nationals leadership. Sixteen prisoners at the Melbourne Assessment Prison have tested positive for Covid-19. \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  (right) and \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  (left) arrive at Government House in Sydney for Perrottet\u8217\'20\'19s swearing in ceremony as the 46th premier of NSW. The Greens senator \uc2 Larissa Waters\uc2 . \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2  speaks to reporters in Melbourne on Tuesday. Federal health minister Greg Hunt. A man looks at flowers and signs placed by members of the public outside the local office of former NSW premier \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2  on 2 October. \uc2 Andrew Constance\uc2 . \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  leaves his home in Sydney on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211004eha40035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
