\par\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List: new head vows to put Republicans on back foot over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,134 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par 15:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler wants to recruit more women of color to run and engage young people, immigrants and working mothers\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler, the new president of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, the fundraising juggernaut responsible for electing hundreds of \u8220\'20\'1CDemocratic pro-choice women\u8221\'20\'1D, has a warning for Republicans: be ready to defend your opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Butler, a veteran labor leader and Democratic strategist, is the first woman of color to lead the organization, which started in the basement of founder \uc2 Ellen Malcolm\uc2  in 1985 and has grown to become one of the most influential and well-financed political action committees in the country.\par \par \uc2 She begins her tenure at a perilous moment for supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Last month, the supreme court let stand a Texas law that bans abortions after about six weeks, and makes no exceptions for rape or incest. The court will separately hear a case that has the potential to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that legalized the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , Butler said she believes the new extremist restrictions in Texas and those under consideration in several other states would be an \u8220\'20\'1Canimating issue\u8221\'20\'1D for Democrats and women across the country, offering a sharp contrast with Republicans over rights many believed had long been settled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir goal is clear and that is to overturn Roe and take away the rights of women to make their own healthcare decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single candidate running for office must be on the record about where they stand in supporting women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats face a daunting election cycle in 2022, but Butler believes public opinion is on their side.\par \par \uc2 The threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights underscore Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List\u8217\'20\'19s mission to elect Democratic women at every level of government, Butler said. State and local elections are as critical to that fight as defending Democratic majorities in Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a role for everybody to play,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In Butler, Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List has chosen a leader with years of experience organizing Black and Latina women, a record of promoting progressive causes and ties to the highest-ranking woman in American politics. She said she views the role as an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aytlne7LB_s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opportunity}}}\uc2  to follow in her mother\u8217\'20\'19s footsteps while blazing a path for her seven-year-old daughter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a great way to contribute to the movement for justice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand in this moment, probably one of the most important ways to be in this space.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Butler was raised in southern Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 the state that has asked the supreme court to overturn Roe when it hears arguments in the case in December. She attended \uc2 Jackson State University\uc2 , a historically Black college in the state, where she was taught by professors who risked arrest in the struggle for voting rights during the civil rights movement.\par \par \uc2 The experience had a profound influence on her career and her politics, she said. After graduating, she joined the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 , where she was eventually elected to lead SEIU Local 2015, the largest home-care workers union in the country. In that role, and later as president of SEIU California, she spearheaded efforts to address pay inequity for women and successfully advocated for policies like raising the state\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 Before joining Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, Butler worked as a political consultant and was a senior strategist on Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 As president of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, Butler said she hopes to expand its reach beyond Washington DC. Her goal is to leverage the organization\u8217\'20\'19s network of candidates, donors and supporters to build a \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s political power\u8221\'20\'1D movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to build a powerful, more engaged \u8230\'20\'26 and more diverse Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List community,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 For Democratic women running for office, few endorsements are as influential \u8211\'20\'13 or sought after \u8211\'20\'13 as the one offered by Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List. Since its founding, the group has raised hundreds of millions of dollars to help elect Democratic women, from the vice-presidency to city councils.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, it helped power a Democratic takeover of the House in an election cycle that was hailed as the \u8220\'20\'1Cyear of the woman\u8221\'20\'1D. In 2020, a record six women ran for president. All lost, but later that year Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.emilyslist.org/news/entry/emilys-list-endorses-kamala-harris-for-vice-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first-of-its-kind}}}\uc2  endorsement for vice-president.\par \par \uc2 As the organization has grown, so have its critics.\par \par \uc2 With women running for office in greater numbers \u8211\'20\'13 and Democrats broadly united on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List has increasingly found itself in the middle of the party\u8217\'20\'19s internecine fights. Progressives in particular have scrutinized the groups\u8217\'20\'19 decisions to endorse candidates in primary contests involving two or more qualified women.\par \par \uc2 Butler said Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List has no intention of shying away from contested primaries when there\u8217\'20\'19s an opportunity to win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look at multiple women running as a good problem to have and a sign of success,\u8221\'20\'1D Butler said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is to get more Democratic, pro-choice women elected to office. Ultimately, that means helping our candidates win in their primaries and that leads to some tough decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List has also faced criticism that its vetting process \u8211\'20\'13 which requires candidates to demonstrate that they can raise money and run professional campaigns \u8211\'20\'13 can disadvantage women of color, who face higher hurdles to fundraising than white women. Butler said there was more work to do to lift up women of color, who represent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emilyslist/status/1364670810384916482"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 40%}}}\uc2  of the candidates Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List has helped elect.\par \par \uc2 She said Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List was \u8220\'20\'1Cdoubling down\u8221\'20\'1D on its commitment to engage, recruit and support candidates of color as it mobilizes new voices\u8211\'20\'13 young people, immigrants and working mothers, among them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe organization has done incredible work to elect some really great women \u8211\'20\'13 some great women of color,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that there is more that progressive organizations like Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List can do to break down some of those structural barriers so women, and in particular Black and brown women, can move through the political process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At present, Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List is focused on the upcoming elections in Virginia and New Jersey, and the 2022 midterms that will determine control of Congress and statehouses across the country.\par \par \uc2 As for whether 2024 will be the year an American woman finally shatters that \u8220\'20\'1Chighest and hardest glass ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D, Butler said it was far too early to speculate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the mission of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List to elect Democratic pro-choice women at all levels of government,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe presidency should not be the only level of government that remains out of reach.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211005eha5000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
