\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats position themselves as last line of defense for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington DC \par \uc2 1,449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2021\par 13:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Party sees new urgency \u8211\'20\'13 and political opportunity \u8211\'20\'13 amid growing threat to Roe v WadeOpinion: In Texas, flustered \u8216\'20\'18pro-lifers\u8217\'20\'19 are backpedaling\par \par \uc2 Standing on the lawn of the US Capitol, in clear view of the supreme court, a coalition of Democratic women declared Roe v Wade was no longer the law of the land.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half a century after the court established the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it allowed a near-complete ban to stand in Texas, the second-most populous state. Though the 5-4 decision did not address the substance of the Texas law, Democrats warn that it was a mere taste of things to come from the court \u8211\'20\'13 and Republicans who helped expand its conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen this court embraced this shameful Texas law, they brought shame to the \uc2 United States supreme court\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said at a press conference on Friday, ahead of a vote on legislation effectively codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat were they thinking, or were they thinking, or were they just rubber-stamping what they were sent to the court to do?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After her remarks, Pelosi returned to the chamber to preside as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats narrowly approved}}}\uc2  the bill. The vote was largely symbolic \u8211\'20\'13 Republican opposition in the Senate all but ensures the measure will not become law. Yet the Senate majority leader, Chuck Schumer, said he planned to bring it to the floor anyway.\par \par \uc2 The urgent push, however futile, was a reflection of just how powerful Democrats believe the issue could be in coming elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in totally uncharted territory,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cecile Richards, a former president of Planned Parenthood who now co-chairs a Democratic political action committee, American Bridge 21st Century. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a day that people certainly hoped would never come. But that\u8217\'20\'19s where we\u8217\'20\'19re at now and there\u8217\'20\'19s no way to be on the sidelines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Washington and beyond, Democrats are embracing the struggle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , portraying themselves as the last line of defense against further erosion \u8211\'20\'13 or outright abolition \u8211\'20\'13 of a constitutional right many believed settled long ago.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has weighed in, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole of government\u8221\'20\'1D response. The justice department is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/doj-texas-abortion-law-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing}}}\uc2  Texas over its law, which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at roughly six weeks, before most women even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\par \par \uc2 This week, the supreme court announced it would hear oral arguments on 1 December in a case involving a Mississippi law banning abortions after 15 weeks, a direct challenge to Roe. A ruling is expected next year, before the November elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Moments of crisis\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 focus on reproductive rights also reflects shifting political dynamics.\par \par \uc2 Unity on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a relatively recent development for the party. After successive defeats in rural America, and defections among white working class voters, Democrats won majorities in Congress with a coalition of urban and suburban college-educated voters who tend to be more socially liberal.\par \par \uc2 While Americans\u8217\'20\'19 views are notoriously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2019/06/2020-democrats-abortion/590701/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 difficult to survey}}}\uc2 , polling has found that attitudes on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have remained relatively consistent. A solid majority say the procedure should remain legal with some restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_US_092021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent Monmouth University poll}}}\uc2  found that a majority of Americans want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in all or some circumstances. More than six in 10 said they did not want the court to revisit Roe. Among Americans with a college degree, support for keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly legal was even higher.\par \par \uc2 Public opinion hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been a barrier for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, who have aligned with the Republican party to enact laws severely restricting access to the procedure in states across the country. They also made the supreme court a political priority, culminating in a 6-3 conservative majority, led by three appointees of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReproductive justice organizers were effectively out-organized in state legislatures, particularly after the Tea Party wave in 2010, and there really hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been an effective response since then,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a legal historian at Florida State University and author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Abortion-Law-America-Wade-Present/dp/1108498280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  and the Law in America: Roe v Wade to the Present.}}}\uc2  But, she said, that could change as more Americans come to terms with the reality that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now effectively outlawed in a state like Texas.\par \par \uc2 Mobilizing support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights becomes \u8220\'20\'1Ceasier, ironically, in moments of crisis like this because everybody agrees that criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be really bad if you\u8217\'20\'19re on the pro-choice side of the debate\u8221\'20\'1D, Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats say fear of losing Roe is motivating voters beyond their liberal base.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople have always believed that somehow, at the end of the day, no matter what politicians did, that the judicial system would be there to back up women,\u8221\'20\'1D Richards said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat just simply isn\u8217\'20\'19t true any more. Now we actually have to face the consequences of making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the issue is also energizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, activists say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment is a culmination of years of pro-life strategy and the stakes have never been higher,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mallory Quigley, a vice-president of the \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  List. She said her group was already knocking on doors in battleground states including Arizona and Georgia, seeking to mobilize \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life base voters\u8221\'20\'1D as well as those \u8220\'20\'1Cwho can be persuaded to vote for the pro-life candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, Republicans have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=the+hill+republilcan+texas+law&oq=the+hill+republilcan+texas+law&aqs=chrome..69i57j69i64.4214j0j7&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more circumspect}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Chave long been able to talk aggressively about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while knowing that the most aggressive policies would either fail in legislatures or be struck down by the courts\u8221\'20\'1D, said Joshua Wilson, a political scientist at the University of Denver and author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sup.org/books/title/?id=24837"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New States of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Politics}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That certainty is gone now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Roe is overturned or otherwise significantly eroded,\u8221\'20\'1D Wilson said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe GOP will own that change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even as Republicans in states like Florida, Arkansas and South Dakota promise copycat legislation, polling has found that most Americans believe the Texas law goes too far. Particularly objectionable, surveys {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_092021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 , is the failure to include exceptions for rape or incest and a provision effectively deputizing ordinary citizens to bring lawsuits against anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with the potential to earn $10,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s so much at stake\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Democrats face a challenging electoral landscape in 2022 as they seek to defend their fragile majorities in the House and Senate and defy a historical pattern in which the president\u8217\'20\'19s party suffers midterm losses. Whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains front and center in national debate will depend on a number of factors, including the state of the pandemic and the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Elections in Virginia this fall? will provide the first major test of how ?the issue resonates with voters?, particularly ????suburban women who were critical to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats running for statewide office have all seized on the Texas law as a harbinger of what is to come in Virginia if Republicans are elected.\par \par \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2 , a former governor running to recapture the office, is portraying himself as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://terrymcauliffe.com/terry-mcauliffe-pledges-to-stand-as-brick-wall-in-protecting-reproductive-rights-in-virginia-glenn-youngkin-would-usher-in-dangerous-texas-style-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brick wall}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D against efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. His opponent, Glenn Youngkin, hit back at McAuliffe in a digital ad, calling the former governor\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo extreme\u8221\'20\'1D for Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Olivia Gans Turner, president of the Virginia Society for Human Life, said voters who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been mobilizing since 2020, when the Democratic governor, Ralph Northam, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/04/10/politics/virginia-abortion-protections/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed legislation }}}\uc2  that overturned longstanding restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe in Virginia who care about the pro-life issue were already very alert and aware of the stakes,\u8221\'20\'1D Gans Turner said. McAuliffe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cobsession with the subject\u8221\'20\'1D, she said, had helped to put it front and center in a way that she believed would further motivate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents and possibly alienate moderates.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists say fear that Roe is at risk is resonating with voters across Virginia, including with those who may not have previously considered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a priority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so much at stake now that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has opened the floodgates to similar bans across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jamie Lockhart, executive director of Planned Parenthood Advocates of Virginia, which is working to elect Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CA Texas-style ban could easily come to Virginia if Glenn Youngkin is elected governor and Republicans take control of the house of delegates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lockhart said she had observed an increase in enthusiasm among voters and volunteers, some of whom pointed to the Texas law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing on the ground \u8211\'20\'13 the increased level of enthusiasm that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing from from our volunteers and supporters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere absolutely is the potential that Virginians\u8217\'20\'19 support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is the difference-maker in this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210926eh9q000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
