\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden will make \u8216\'20\'18case-by-case\u8217\'20\'19 decision on executive privilege over Capitol riot records \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 8,654 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2021\par 01:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House clarifies earlier comments about subpoenaed documentsMayorkas: no migrants remaining under Del Rio bridge\u8216\'20\'18There will be consequences\u8217\'20\'19 for treatment of Haitians: BidenHouse Democrats vote to establish federal right to abortionSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 White House says Biden will make \u8216\'20\'18case-by-case\u8217\'20\'19 decision on executive privilege\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, we reported that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had decided not to invoke executive privilege over Trump White House documents subpoenaed by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, based on comments White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  made in her daily briefing.\par \par \uc2 But the Biden White House told reporters later in the day that it would make decisions about executive privilege over Trump White House documents \u8220\'20\'1Con a case-by-case basis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki had said earlier today that \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has already concluded it would not be appropriate to assert executive privilege,\u8221\'20\'1D but the White House noted she also said this represented the president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Coverarching view,\u8221\'20\'1D and declined to get into hypotheticals about what the administration would or would not release.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s clarification:\par \par \uc2 The Administration believes strongly in the vital role this Committee is playing and will continue to work closely with it moving forward. Jen was referring to the Administration\u8217\'20\'19s previous decision not to assert executive privilege in the matter of certain former DOJ officials who had been called to testify before Congress. The Administration will determine any future questions of executive privilege involving documents and testimony on a case-by-case basis, as Jen noted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: White House says now that decision on executive privilege for Jan. 6 committee-requested materials and testimony has NOT been made, per source \u8212\'20\'14 Psaki was referring to previous privilege requests.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1441524463804116995?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House: \u8220\'20\'1CJen was referring to the Administration\u8217\'20\'19s previous decision \u8212\'20\'14 will determine any future questions of executive privilege involving documents and testimony on a case-by-case basis, as Jen noted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1441531726539464708?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening Summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re wrapping up our live US politics coverage for tonight. Some highlights from today\u8217\'20\'19s news:\par \par \uc2 * The sham election \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Maricopa county found that Biden defeated Trump by 360 more votes than previously thought. A draft report of the audit\u8217\'20\'19s findings affirmed that Biden won Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county last year. The investigation, which was overseen by a firm whose CEO had promoted lies about election fraud, had attracted many allegations of political bias.\par \par \uc2 * But the lack of substantive findings did not stop the leaders of the \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D from raising unsubstantiated concerns they claimed needed further investigation, even as journalists and officials factchecked their claims in real time.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, experts in US election law and democratic norms warned of the likelihood of attempted \u8220\'20\'1Celection subversion\u8221\'20\'1D from Republicans in 2022 and 2024, and cautioned that \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t have a democracy if one of the two major parties cannot accept an election defeat.\u8221\'20\'1D The current behavior of many Republican politicians was anti-democratic, multiple political scientists cautioned, and \u8220\'20\'1C The US faces a serious risk that the 2024 election, and other future US elections, will not be conducted fairly,\u8221\'20\'1D a leading election law expert said.\par \par \uc2 * House Democrats passed a bill to establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The nearly party-line vote came weeks after a highly controversial six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in Texas, leading to copycat bills in other states. The House-approved legislation is considered dead on arrival in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 * Biden promised there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D for border agents accused of mistreating Haitian migrants. Taking reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions after delivering prepared remarks on vaccination efforts, Biden said the footage of border agents on horseback confronting migrants was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous. I promise you, those people will pay,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 * The homeland security secretary said there are no remaining migrants in the Del Rio border encampment that sparked outcry. Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas also pledged that the findings of the investigation into border agents\u8217\'20\'19 actions toward Haitian migrants would be made public.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 'An existential threat to American democracy.' Experts warn of GOP 'election subversion'\par \par \uc2 The United States faces significant risks to its democracy in the 2022 and 2024 elections, experts on democracy and election law warned at a conference on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have a significant portion of one of the two major political parties that is no longer committed to democratic norms,\u8221\'20\'1D political scientist \uc2 Larry Diamond\uc2 , a fellow at the conservative Hoover Institute, warned as part of a conference on \u8220\'20\'1Celection subversion\u8221\'20\'1D hosted by the \uc2 University of California, Irvine\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are facing an existential challenge to American democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just the crazies that kill democracy, it\u8217\'20\'19s not just the people who storm the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  on 6 January,\u8221\'20\'1D said Steve Levitsky, one of the authors of How Democracies Die. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the mainstream Republican party not breaking with democratic extremists that is most dangerous at this moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US faces a serious risk that the 2024 election, and other future US elections, will not be conducted fairly, and that the candidates taking office will not reflect free choices made by eligible voters under previously announced election rules,\u8221\'20\'1D Rick Hasen, a leading US election law expert and the host of the conference, said.\par \par \uc2 The decision by many Republican politicians to continue to back \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims that he lost because of election fraud, and their continued willingness to undermine confidence in elections rather than admit defeat, was a serious blow to American democracy, Levitsky said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t have a democracy if one of the two major parties cannot accept an election defeat,\u8221\'20\'1D Levitsky said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn most cases where we lose a democracy, you can get it back, but it often takes, ten, fifteen, twenty years,\u8221\'20\'1D he added later. \u8220\'20\'1CBetter to prevalent backsliding than to try to reverse it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Survivors seek healing as first details emerge in Tennessee grocery shooting\par \par \uc2 Two women who had been strangers prior to Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting at a Tennessee supermarket clenched each other\u8217\'20\'19s hands and fought back tears Friday, as they gathered at a vigil to pray for healing from the previous day\u8217\'20\'19s rampage at a \uc2 Kroger\uc2  where the shooter worked, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-crime-shootings-tennessee-e2a9c775a296af80400ce4564f6f6c78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hollie Skaggs and Sara Wiles happened to be running errands at the same \uc2 Kroger\uc2  in Collierville. A day later, after a gunman killed one person and himself and wounded 14 others, Skaggs called Wiles her guardian angel.\par \par \uc2 The gunman worked in a sushi business at the store, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cthird-party vendor\u8221\'20\'1D who worked on a daily basis, police have said. He died of an apparent self-inflicted gunshot wound within a couple of minutes of officers arriving at the \uc2 Kroger\uc2  in the upscale suburb outside of Memphis.\par \par \uc2 The victims included 10 employees and five customers, police said. The shooter, acting alone, did not appear to target anyone specifically as he rampaged through the building on a sunny Thursday afternoon, police said. The entire shooting was over within minutes as first responders swarmed the scene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all want to know the why,\u8221\'20\'1D Collierville Police Chief Dale Lane said of the shooter\u8217\'20\'19s motive. \u8220\'20\'1CBut today, less than 24 hours (after the shooting), we\u8217\'20\'19re not ready to tell you that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A friend of the shooter\u8217\'20\'19s family said his parents were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery upset\u8221\'20\'1D about their son\u8217\'20\'19s involvement and were praying for all the people involved.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not boost our way out of this pandemic,\u8217\'20\'19 CDC official warns\par \par \uc2 The U.S. launched a campaign to offer boosters of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s COVID-19 vaccine to millions of Americans on Friday even as federal health officials stressed the real problem remains getting first shots to the unvaccinated, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-science-business-health-coronavirus-vaccine-9da6d4dab4f3dc0542db951557042ac9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not boost our way out of this pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D warned \uc2 Dr. Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention \u8212\'20\'14 even though she took the rare step of overruling the advice of her own expert panel to make more people eligible for the booster.\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of COVID-19 cases and hospitalizations are among the unvaccinated, Walensky noted. And all three COVID-19 vaccines in the U.S. offer strong protection against severe illness, hospitalization and death despite the extra-contagious delta variant that caused cases to soar. But immunity against milder infection appears to wane months after initial vaccination.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They wasted $6m to tell us what we already knew.\u8217\'20\'19 Reactions to AZ ballot review\par \par \uc2 What did the Arizona Cyber Ninjas review of 2020 election results accomplish?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey wasted nearly $6 million to tell us what we already knew, meanwhile exacerbating an already unhealthy political environment,\u8221\'20\'1D Arizona state Sen. Paul Boyer (R) told The Hill in a text message.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Five takeaways from Arizona's audit results {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0C65VEXfVg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0C65VEXfVg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/meOJoLqWGz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/meOJoLqWGz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Hill (@thehill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill/status/1441535175465136135?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But by other measures, focused on the way the review continues to feed doubt and conspiracy theories about election measures, it may have accomplished a lot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has reportedly been banned from Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Bourg/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRudy is really hurt,\u8221\'20\'1D Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2021/09/24/scoop-fox-to-rudy-youre-banned-494458"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  a source \u8220\'20\'1Cclose to Giuliani\u8221\'20\'1D as saying.\par \par \uc2 According to the website, the prominent Trump ally learned of his expulsion on the eve of the 20th anniversary of the 9/11 attacks, after which, as New York mayor, he became a national figure.\par \par \uc2 Fox News declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Politico quoted its source as saying Giuliani was hurt was \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause he did a big favour for Rupert [Murdoch]. He was instrumental [in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://go.politicoemail.com/?qs=a4d953b906d7f93bed2407da6bc3ff565cc5a93d523e0e683561e40e98c8b11acc742e670aa13d922aa17cbd335d1a65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1996}}}\uc2  ] in getting Fox on Time Warner so it could be watched in New York City.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s apparent expulsion may also be linked to Fox News business. Both network and sometime personal attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/25/dominion-rudy-giuliani-lawsuit-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to Donald Trump}}}\uc2  have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/mar/26/fox-news-sued-dominion-2020-election-voting-fraud-lies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued by Dominion Voter Systems}}}\uc2  over false claims about supposed electoral fraud in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Fox News has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/05/18/998099249/fox-news-moves-to-have-dominion-voting-systems-lawsuit-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  to dismiss, citing first amendment protections of free speech and saying Dominion had not proved \u8220\'20\'1Cactual malice\u8221\'20\'1D in its reporting.\par \par \uc2 A judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.225699/gov.uscourts.dcd.225699.45.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to have the suit dismissed. The former mayor has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/rudy-giuliani-defense-dominion-conspiracy-theories-are-substantially-true-2021-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  his claims about Dominion are \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially true\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/rudy-giuliani-reportedly-banned-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Rudy is really hurt\u8217\'20\'19: Giuliani reportedly banned from Fox News}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 California governor signs bill to replace the term \u8216\'20\'18alien\u8217\'20\'19 in California\u8217\'20\'19s laws\par \par \uc2 News from California:\par \par \uc2 enltrGavin Newsom signs AB1096 by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LuzRivas?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LuzRivas}}}\uc2  to remove and replace the term "alien" in California code.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Newsom calls it "an offensive term for a human being."\par \par \uc2 "By changing this term, we are ensuring California's laws reflect our state's values," he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexei Koseff (@akoseff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/akoseff/status/1441532099186479112?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 In search of fraud, Arizona Cyber Ninjas review found 99 additional votes for Biden\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CCyber Ninjas\u8221\'20\'1D election investigation, which lasted several months, confirmed that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did indeed beat Trump in Maricopa county, the state\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county, Doug Logan, who led the review, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  senate on Friday. In fact, a hand recount found 99 additional votes for Biden and 261 fewer votes for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Logan, the CEO of Cyber Ninjas, a Florida-based firm leading the review, said in a presentation Friday afternoon to the Arizona senate that the discrepancies were \u8220\'20\'1Csmall\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ballots that were provided to us in the coliseum very accurately correlate with the official canvas numbers that came through,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Despite that finding, Logan, who has spread election conspiracy theories, outlined what he claimed were anomalies in the count. Several of them were immediately debunked by Maricopa county officials, who fact-checked his presentation.\par \par \uc2 Shiva Ayyadurai, a failed \uc2 US senate\uc2  candidate who has espoused election conspiracy theories, gave another presentation filled with misrepresentations about the county\u8217\'20\'19s process for verifying signatures.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/republican-audit-arizona-bigger-lead-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republican \u8216\'20\'18audit\u8217\'20\'19 finds even bigger lead for Biden in 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the eve of a Trump rally in Perry, Georgia on Saturday, the Republican official in charge of elections in the state said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to come, and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to say what he\u8217\'20\'19s going to say, but he knows in his heart that he lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/georgia-secretary-state-slams-trump-110000397.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussing}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about election fraud in his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with a conservative newspaper, the Washington Examiner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time we\u8217\'20\'19ve looked into all of these and all of these concerns, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the election fair and square,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat bothers me, and it really should bother everyone, after 10 months since the last ballots were counted, we\u8217\'20\'19re still dealing with this misinformation and disinformation surrounding the elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realLizUSA/status/1438886054380154884/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  released last week, the former president claimed to have found 43,000 \u8220\'20\'1Cinvalid\u8221\'20\'1D ballots in Georgia and told Raffensperger and the governor of Georgia, Brian Kemp, to \u8220\'20\'1Cstart the process of decertifying the election, or whatever the correct legal remedy is, and announce the true winner\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger seems resigned to what is coming in Perry on Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We are not going to win that bullhorn argument,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s now been a call to \u8216\'20\'18Imeach Biden\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 We have all made spelling errors (especially, gentle readers, on this live blog) but some are more awkward than others.\par \par \uc2 enltrLauren Boebert has sent a release calling to impeach Biden, but she has messed up the logo here {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IR3m2QxNFT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IR3m2QxNFT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1441465613684252672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cyber Ninjas \u8216\'20\'18audit\u8217\'20\'19 of AZ election results: \u8216\'20\'18Found nothing, more investigation needed\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live politics coverage from our West Coast bureau in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Guardian voting rights reporter Sam Levine is covering the results of the highly politicized \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election results. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/14/arizona-election-audit-recount-ballots-maricopa-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  carnivalesque, GOP-led Cyber Ninjas review}}}\uc2  of the 2020 ballots ended up confirming Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win in Maricopa county, Arizona, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kjzz.org/content/1719314/arizona-election-audit-confirms-bidens-win-maricopa-county-also-casts-doubts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft of the report obtained by local reporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But in testimony in Arizona right now, people involved in the process are still testifying about supposed \u8220\'20\'1Canomalies\u8221\'20\'1D they found. Sam breaks down why this outcome is concerning:\par \par \uc2 enltr1 of the main talking points of those who supported the AZ review was that there was nothing to fear because it would only assuage concern if it turned up nothing. But the CN draft report shows why that's misleading. The report found nothing, yet says more investigation is needed\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1441491113462976512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCyber Ninjas draft report flags more than 10,300 ppl as potential double voters based on name, and birth year. This is widely known as an unreliable method. It's been shown again and again by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElectProject?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ElectProject}}}\uc2  and others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0UIOboChtl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0UIOboChtl}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j8XrYDAnvy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/j8XrYDAnvy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1441470612145201153?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDr. Shiva says now further auditing is needed of the signature verification process, even as reporters and the county have immediately been able to explain several of the "anomalies" he identified. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/q3STVg8TGg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/q3STVg8TGg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1441506832875278336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Sam has more on the text of the report, as well as the testimony happening now. You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SRL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow him on Twitter for live coverage at @srl}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrLanguage in this section is a microcosm of how the report is creating uncertainty even though CN failed to turn up any evidence of actual fraud. "While it is possible for multiple\par \par \uc2 individuals to share all these details; it is not common, and this list should be fully reviewed."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1441471342881218560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Lois Beckett, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has decided not to invoke executive privilege over Trump White House documents subpoenaed by the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said during her daily briefing, \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has already concluded it would not be appropriate to assert executive privilege.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump had claimed he would use executive privilege to block the committee\u8217\'20\'19s access to documents, but because he is no longer president, he needs Biden\u8217\'20\'19s permission to do so.\par \par \uc2 * Biden promised there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D for border agents accused of mistreating Haitian migrants. Taking reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions after delivering prepared remarks on vaccination efforts, Biden said the footage of border agents on horseback confronting migrants was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous. I promise you, those people will pay,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 * The homeland security secretary said there are no remaining migrants in the Del Rio border encampment that sparked outcry. Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas also pledged that the findings of the investigation into border agents\u8217\'20\'19 actions toward Haitian migrants would be made public.\par \par \uc2 * The sham election \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Maricopa county found that Biden defeated Trump by 360 more votes than previously thought. A draft report of the audit\u8217\'20\'19s findings affirmed that Biden won Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county last year. The investigation, which was overseen by a firm whose CEO had promoted lies about election fraud, had attracted many allegations of political bias.\par \par \uc2 * House Democrats passed a bill to establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The nearly party-line vote came weeks after a highly controversial six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in Texas, leading to copy cat bills in other states. The House-approved legislation is considered dead on arrival in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 Lois will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  will appear on CBS News\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C60 Minutes\u8221\'20\'1D this Sunday, the network just announced.\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2  said Cheney would be speaking to correspondent Lesley Stahl about \u8220\'20\'1Cre-election, her criticism of \uc2 Pres. Trump\uc2  and her family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrEmbattled WY Republican Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  talks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LesleyRStahl?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LesleyRStahl}}}\uc2  about re-election, her criticism of \uc2 Pres. Trump\uc2  and her family on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/60Minutes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @60Minutes}}}\uc2  Sun 7p {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JRpR5N8sGv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JRpR5N8sGv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News PR (@CBSNewsPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNewsPress/status/1441501319580164100?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The interview comes as the Wyoming congresswoman faces a daunting primary race against Trump-backed challenger Harriet Hageman.\par \par \uc2 Cheney is also serving as the vice-chair of the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, which just issued subpoenas to four former Trump aides.\par \par \uc2 Cheney, who supported impeaching Trump for inciting the January 6 insurrection, is one of two Republicans serving on the committee, alongside \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reported on the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s latest round of subpoenas last night:\par \par \uc2 The House select committee scrutinizing the Capitol attack on Thursday sent subpoenas to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and a cadre of top Trump aides, demanding their testimony to shed light on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s connection to the 6 January riot.\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas and demands for depositions marked the most aggressive investigative actions the select committee has taken since it made records demands and records preservation requests that formed the groundwork of the inquiry into potential White House involvement.\par \par \uc2 House select committee investigators targeted four of the closest aides to the former president: deputy White House chief of staff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/20210923%20Scavino%20Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dan Scavino}}}\uc2 , former Trump campaign manager {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/20210923%20Bannon%20Letter_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2 , and the former acting defense secretary\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/20210923%20Patel%20Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kash Patel}}}\uc2  as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/20210923%20Meadows%20Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meadows}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/23/us-capitol-attack-subpoena-mark-meadows-steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House committee on Capitol attack subpoenas Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff and other top aides}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/17/jan-6-probe-request-trump-512430"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has some more details}}}\uc2  on how the process will play out as the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection subpoenas records from the Trump White House:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Archives and Records Administration\uc2  has sent hundreds of pages of documents requested by the Jan. 6 select committee to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team to review, according to a person familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 That move kicks off a process that will result in some tough decisions for Biden \u8217\'20\'19s White House counsel, both politically and legally. That\u8217\'20\'19s because the office will have to decide whether to sign off on any efforts from Team Trump to keep sensitive White House communications from becoming public.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to document after document relevant to the Jan. 6 panel\u8217\'20\'19s expansive request, Biden White House lawyers will likely face the same tough dilemma: They can either send Congress the material over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s objections, entering unprecedented legal territory about the treatment of former presidents; or they can withhold materials from Hill allies, thereby stymieing investigators\u8217\'20\'19 access and potentially generating significant political fallout.\par \par \uc2 And now the White House has indicated Biden is opposed to using executive privilege to block lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 access to subpoenaed documents, likely setting up a historic clash between the current and former presidents.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 During her briefing, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  also called on Republicans to help Democrats in reforming the immigration system, as the Biden administration weathers criticism over its treatment of Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary argued it would take congressional action to substantially improve \u8220\'20\'1Cour broken immigration system,\u8221\'20\'1D saying such action was \u8220\'20\'1Clong overdue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki calls on GOP to help pass a bill to fix "our broken immigration system"\par \par \uc2 "There are a lot of Republicans out there giving speeches about how outraged they are about the situation at the border. Not many who are putting forward solutions or steps that we could take" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AQAW10WMyg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AQAW10WMyg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1441484440828481541?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of Republicans out there giving speeches about how outraged they are about the situation at the border, not many who are putting forward solutions or steps that we could take,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo we\u8217\'20\'19re a little tired of the speeches. We\u8217\'20\'19d like to partner on solutions and working together to address this problem that has not been partisan in the past.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will not invoke executive privilege on January 6 records, Psaki says\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has decided he will not invoke executive privilege to block access to Trump White House records related to the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has already concluded it would not be appropriate to assert executive privilege,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said at her briefing.\par \par \uc2 Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s comments come one day after the House select committee investigating the insurrection issued subpoenas to four former aides of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president responded to the news by claiming he would \u8220\'20\'1Cfight the Subpoenas on Executive Privilege and other grounds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But because Trump is not president anymore, he would need to seek Biden\u8217\'20\'19s permission to prevent lawmakers from gaining access to subpoenaed records. And now Biden is signaling he will not exercise his executive privilege on the matter.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/23/us-capitol-attack-subpoena-mark-meadows-steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House committee on Capitol attack subpoenas Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff and other top aides}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  took over the podium after homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas departed the briefing room.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the timing of the House vote on the bipartisan infrastructure bill, Psaki said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to win the vote when it happens. That\u8217\'20\'19s our objective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, House Democratic leaders are signaling they still plan to bring the bill up for a vote on Monday, as speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  looks to simultaneously advance the reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 enltrModerate Democrats met with House Dem leaders in Pelosi's office for an hour and 15 minutes, and afterward they were was high expectation the vote on the Senate's infrastructure bill would still occur on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "I'm bringing the bill to the floor on Monday," Hoyer told us\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1441482794128101378?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas acknowledged that the footage of border agents on horseback confronting Haitian migrants was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 However, Mayorkas seemed to temper his comments about the images more than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has, saying that he was not willing to \u8220\'20\'1Cpre-judge\u8221\'20\'1D the agents until the investigation into their actions was concluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not conduct ourselves in an immoral way,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said of his department. \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not conduct ourselves in an unethical way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMayorkas: "We do not conduct ourselves in an immoral way. We do not conduct ourselves in an unethical way... We are reuniting families that were separated."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1441478184202129415?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas said there have been 17 expulsion flights to Haiti, carrying about 2,000 people.\par \par \uc2 According to Mayorkas, another 8,000 migrants have voluntarily returned to Mexico. And 5,000 others are being processed by the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas said border officials have been expelling migrants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/apr/21/us-mexico-border-title-42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under Title 42}}}\uc2  when applicable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas also addressed the outrage over footage of border agents on horseback confronting Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 enltr"In the midst of meeting these challenges, we, our entire nation, saw horrifying images that do not reflect who we are, who we aspire to be, or the integrity and values of our truly heroic personnel," DHS Secretary Mayorkas says. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Euj8VzTqpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Euj8VzTqpg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1441473083131547648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the midst of meeting these challenges, we, our entire nation, saw horrifying images that do not reflect who we are, who we aspire to be, or the integrity and values of our truly heroic personnel in the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that those images painfully conjured up the worst elements of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing battle against systemic racism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas noted there is an investigation underway into the agents\u8217\'20\'19 behavior, and they have been reassigned to \u8220\'20\'1Cadministrative duties\u8221\'20\'1D. The department has also ended the use of horse patrol units in Del Rio.\par \par \uc2 The homeland security secretary pledged to make public the findings of the investigation into the agents\u8217\'20\'19 actions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 No migrants remaining under Del Rio bridge, Mayorkas says\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is now holding her daily briefing, and she is joined by homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas provided an update on the situation in the border city of Del Rio, Texas, where many Haitian migrants have been attempting to enter the US in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has faced criticism for the treatment of the Haitians after images showed migrants camping underneath a bridge in the punishing Texas heat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs of this morning, there are no longer any migrants at the camp underneath the Del Rio International Bridge,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden holds first-ever in-person Quad leaders summit\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now holding the first-ever in-person Quad leaders summit at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Biden is joined by Indian Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2  and Australian Prime Minister Scott Morrison.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrives to attend the Quad summit. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 The US president sat down with Modi in the Oval Office this morning, and he will hold a separate meeting with Suga this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Biden also held a one-on-one meeting with Morrison earlier this week, during which the two leaders \u8220\'20\'1Caffirmed their commitment to a free and open Indo-Pacific region,\u8221\'20\'1D per the White House readout of their conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  eyes LA mayoral run\par \par \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2 , a Democratic congresswoman from California, is reportedly planning to run for Los Angeles mayor. The Washington Post first reported the news.\par \par \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2 . Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Although the field is still shaping up, Bass\u8217\'20\'19 national profile and broad popularity would make her a top contender for the position Eric Garcetti is vacating to be ambassador to India.\par \par \uc2 Bass, 67, was on the short list to be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-president. Her name has also come up in discussions of who might replace \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  as House Speaker.\par \par \uc2 In California, she has built a reputation as a progressive and a pragmatist : a community organizer who fought police brutality and addiction in Los Angeles and a practical politician who helped dig the state out of a historical fiscal crisis in 2008.\par \par \uc2 She was elected to Congress in 2010 to lead one of the most diverse districts in California, a constituency in Los Angeles that is 25% white, 25% Black, 40% Latino and 8% Asian American.\par \par \uc2 In the House, she took the lead in pushing for a police reform bill which passed her chamber twice but failed this week after negotiators conceded that Senate Democrats and Republicans would be unable to reconcile their differences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s sad,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the LA Times in an interview published Friday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CBut at this point, I just felt like we were just running around in circles and we were never going to get to yes on anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, she told reporters earlier this week, \u8220\'20\'1Cour sense of urgency remains\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bass urged Biden and his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cuse the full extent of their constitutionally mandated power to bring about meaningful police reform\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In LA, Bass is interested in addressing homelessness and public health in the aftermath of the pandemic, a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Other mayoral candidates include city council member and former state Senate leader \uc2 Kevin de Le\u243\'00\'F3n\uc2 , city attorney \uc2 Mike Feuer\uc2  and council member Joe Buscain.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi determined to pass 'two jobs bills'\par \par \uc2 Telling Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cthat intensity continues\u8221\'20\'1D, the House Speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , has confirmed plans to press ahead with efforts to pass both a bipartisan infrastructure bill and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s huge budget and spending package.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Photograph: Kent Nishimura/Los Angeles Times/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe move forward to pass two jobs bills next week: the Build Back Better Act and the Bipartisan Infrastructure Framework,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi wrote in a widely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/pelosi-aims-pass-infrastructure-safety-net-bills-next-week-democrats-n1280040"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  letter to her party on Friday.\par \par \uc2 On the spending bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/meetings/BU/BU00/20210925/114090/BILLS-117pih-BuildBackBetterAct.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which runs to 2,465 pages}}}\uc2  or more than two War & Peaces if you go by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tableau.uchicago.edu/articles/2013/04/why-read-war-and-peace"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first edition}}}\uc2  of Leo Tolstoy\u8217\'20\'19s voluminous potboiler, Manu Raju of CNN more succinctly reports: \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Democratic leaders emerge from meeting saying they could vote as soon as next week on the reconciliation bill. Rules [committee] could act on Tuesday. [Majority leader Steney] Hoyer will soon announce it\u8217\'20\'19s possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reconciliation is the process by which budgetary legislation can pass the Senate with a simple majority. That chamber is split 50-50, with Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  the deciding vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what version they could bring to floor since Democrats are still in significant disagreement,\u8221\'20\'1D Raju added.\par \par \uc2 He was referring to s plits between moderates and progressives over spending priorities and ambitions, all playing out in a way that a) threatens to tank Biden\u8217\'20\'19s domestic agenda in a bloody tableau of intra-party dysfunction and b) has Republicans rubbing their hands with glee, what with their complete opposition to such plans and also their determination to force a showdown over the debt ceiling and with it a possible government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 In short, Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s right. The intensity will continue.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 An extraordinary confrontation outside the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  today, between the Michigan Democrat \uc2 Debbie Dingell\uc2  and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a far right Republican from Georgia.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bensiegel/status/1441431285642121220"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by Ben Siegel of ABC News, the confrontation developed as Democrats prepared to host a press conference on the Capitol steps about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting to protect them}}}\uc2  in the face of concerted assault from Republican-run states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStand with women,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene shouted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re performative,\u8221\'20\'1D Pete Aguilar, a Democrat from California, replied.\par \par \uc2 Dingell then shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CYou should practice the basic thing you\u8217\'20\'19re taught in church: respect your neighbour!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene shouted back: \u8220\'20\'1CChurch?! Are you kidding me? Try being a Christian and supporting life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dingell responded: \u8220\'20\'1CYou try being a Christian and try treating your colleagues decently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene said: \u8220\'20\'1CWatch your step.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She may have meant it literally, as Dingell briefly and slightly unsteadily stepped down towards her.\par \par \uc2 enltrGreene and Rep. Dingell are now shouting at each other.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou should practice the basic thing you\u8217\'20\'19re taught in church: respect your neighbor!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene: \u8220\'20\'1CChurch?! Are you kidding me? Try being a Christian!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dingell: \u8220\'20\'1CYou try being a Christian and treat your colleagues decently.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5aXtaU1dNK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5aXtaU1dNK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Siegel (@bensiegel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bensiegel/status/1441432103460147204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 If the confrontation was not quite reminiscent of those described in The Field of Blood ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blogs.lse.ac.uk/lsereviewofbooks/2019/12/10/book-review-the-field-of-blood-violence-in-congress-and-the-road-to-the-civil-war-by-joanne-freeman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a well-received book}}}\uc2  by the historian Joanne B Freeman, about brutal spats in Congress in the years before the civil war) it was certainly indicative of the bitter split between most members of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and the US at large.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino\u8217\'20\'19s report on the vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights which preceded the confrontation at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Democrats vote to establish federal right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The sham election \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Maricopa county found that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by 360 more votes than previously thought. A draft report of the audit\u8217\'20\'19s findings affirmed that Biden won Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county last year. The investigation, which was overseen by a firm whose CEO had promoted lies about election fraud, had attracted many allegations of political bias.\par \par \uc2 * Biden pledged that there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D for border agents accused of mistreating Haitian migrants. Taking reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions after delivering prepared remarks on vaccination efforts, Biden said the footage of border agents on horseback confronting migrants was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous. I promise you, those people will pay,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 * House Democrats passed a bill to establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The nearly party-line vote came weeks after a highly controversial six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in Texas, leading to copy cat bills in other states. The House-approved legislation is considered dead on arrival in the evenly controlled Senate.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The debate ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vote was passionate and personal, as was expected for what has become one of the most polarizing issues in American politics.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats recalled the days before 1973, when the supreme court decided Roe v Wade, establishing a legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v Wade was not the beginning of women having abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Congresswoman Jan Schakowsky, a Democrat from Illinois. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was the end of women dying from abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Sylvia Garcia, a Democrat of Texas, waved a wire coat hanger as a symbol of the dangerous \u8211\'20\'13 and sometimes deadly \u8211\'20\'13 methods women would use to attempt an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it was legalized.\par \par \uc2 Republicans rose to denounce the bill, arguing that it would allow \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand\u8221\'20\'1D at every stage of pregnancy, even until birth.\par \par \uc2 The measure \u8220\'20\'1Cisn\u8217\'20\'19t about freedom for women,\u8221\'20\'1D said Congresswoman \uc2 Vicky Hartzler\uc2 , a Republican from Missouri. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about death for babies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats vote to establish federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  voted on Friday to establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , moving swiftly to advance the measure after the supreme court declined to stop a Texas law effectively outlawing the procedure and as they await a separate ruling next year that could further erode access.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, named the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health and Protection Act, is part of the party\u8217\'20\'19s strategy to push back against the rush of state laws restricting abortions and to show their determination to defend reproductive rights, an issue they believe will resonate ahead of the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has urged support for the measure, but Republican opposition in the Senate all but ensures the bill will not reach his desk.\par \par \uc2 With the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , presiding over the vote, the House passed the measure 218-211. All Republicans and one Democrat opposed the bill.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Democrats vote to establish federal right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The scramble to secure a remote connection for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  severely delayed her interview with The View, so the conversation kicked off with about ten minutes left in the show.\par \par \uc2 When the interview finally began, the View hosts pressed Harris on the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal and immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  addresses the U.S. Border Patrol deploying agents on horseback against Haitian migrants at the U.S.-Mexico border: \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should not be treated that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got to do more, no question... Haiti is our neighbor.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ao61DG9zH3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ao61DG9zH3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The View (@TheView) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheView/status/1441435880506396672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked about the alarming footage of border agents on horseback confronting Haitian migrants in Del Rio, Texas, Harris said she was \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged\u8221\'20\'1D by the images.\par \par \uc2 Noting that there is an investigation underway into the border agents\u8217\'20\'19 behavior, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere needs to be consequence and accountability. Human beings should not be treated that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the Biden administration would halt deportation flights to allow those migrants to apply for asylum, Harris deflected, simply saying the US must \u8220\'20\'1Cdo more\u8221\'20\'1D to support Haiti.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris' View appearance disrupted by hosts' positive Covid tests\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 plans to appear in-studio for an interview on The View were scrapped after two of the talk show\u8217\'20\'19s hosts tested positive for coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Moments before the vice-president was supposed to come onstage, it was announced that hosts Sunny Hostin and Ana Navarro had tested positive for Covid.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  Harris: "Sunny [Hostin] and Ana [Navarro] are strong women and I know they're fine, but it really also does speak to the fact that they're vaccinated and vaccines really make all the difference because otherwise we would be concerned about hospitalization and worse." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m5NMwT5dk8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m5NMwT5dk8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The View (@TheView) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheView/status/1441431474704580610?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 So the interview, which was meant to be Harris\u8217\'20\'19 first in-studio conversation since becoming vice-president, was conducted remotely.\par \par \uc2 When the interview finally began, Harris offered her best wishes to Hostin and Navarro, both of whom are fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSunny and Ana are strong women, and I know they\u8217\'20\'19re fine, but it really also does speak to the fact that they\u8217\'20\'19re vaccinated and vaccines really make all the difference because otherwise we would be concerned about hospitalization and worse,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said to applause from the studio audience.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host the first in-person summit of the Quad countries \u8211\'20\'13 the US, India, Japan and Australia \u8211\'20\'13 at the White House on Friday as he ratchets up the reorientation of US foreign policy towards the Pacific and the containment of China.\par \par \uc2 The summit, which will seek to deepen ties within the ad hoc grouping, will take place just nine days after the surprise announcement of the Aukus security agreement between Australia, the UK and US, built around the sharing of nuclear-propulsion technology with Australia for its new submarine fleet.\par \par \uc2 Aukus and an invigorated Quad are the two central pillars of the US president\u8217\'20\'19s signature foreign policy, which some are calling the Biden doctrine: bolstering the world\u8217\'20\'19s democracies against the spread of authoritarianism by building a web of alliances.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/24/joe-biden-quad-summit-contain-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to rally regional support for China containment strategy at Quad summit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden meets with Modi in Oval Office\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now meeting with Indian Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  in the Oval Office, ahead of the first-ever in-person Quad leaders summit this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Welcoming Modi to the White House, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CMr Prime Minister, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to build on our strong partnership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith shared a photo from the two leaders\u8217\'20\'19 meeting:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the Oval Office. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  of India: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Prime Minister, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to build on our strong partnership.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/osICFnI45l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/osICFnI45l}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1441425678755409921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  condemned the sham election \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Arizona as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous attempt by extremist Republicans to undermine our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArizona Republicans \u8212\'20\'14 not to mention their copycats in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, and other states \u8212\'20\'14 have been beholden to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s unhinged conspiracy theories that incited a mob to attack the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and law enforcement,\u8221\'20\'1D DNC spokesperson Ryan Thomas said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Republican peddling election misinformation will have to explain to their constituents why they spent their time undermining democracy on behalf of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  instead of delivering for their constituents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine and Oliver Milman have more details on the sham election \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Arizona:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has repeatedly falsely claimed that he won the election and was a victim of fraud, despite no evidence of this, and state Republicans in Arizona seized upon these lies to demand an audit of vote in Maricopa county.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Maricopa county hired two firms to audit its elections equipment and software, with these reviews finding no problems with the systems reviewed.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/azaudit?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #azaudit}}}\uc2  draft report from Cyber Ninjas confirms the county\u8217\'20\'19s canvass of the 2020 General Election was accurate and the candidates certified as the winners did, in fact, win.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maricopa County (@maricopacounty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maricopacounty/status/1441228176600952839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough for the state senate, controlled by Republicans, however, which hired Cyber Ninjas for the controversial audit.\par \par \uc2 The recounting process was dogged with allegations of ballots being mishandled and cybersecurity concerns, with workers at one point using UV lights to check for bamboo fibers in ballots, part of a conspiracy theory that China had somehow planted votes into Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election. The review concluded in July.\par \par \uc2 While the draft report does not claim that Trump did beat Biden in Arizona, it does criticize the state for the handling and integrity of how the election was run.\par \par \uc2 Maricopa county\u8217\'20\'19s board of supervisors has rejected this, stating on its Twitter feed that the report\u8217\'20\'19s allegations are \u8220\'20\'1Clittered with errors & faulty conclusions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/republican-audit-arizona-bigger-lead-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republican \u8216\'20\'18audit\u8217\'20\'19 finds even bigger lead for Biden in 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed confidence that Democrats will be able to pass both the bipartisan infrastructure bill and the reconciliation package, even as moderates and progressives remain at odds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a process, and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be up and down. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I don\u8217\'20\'19t look at the polls. Not a joke,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd hopefully at the end of the day, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to deliver on what I said I would do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Multiple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/354872/biden-approval-rating-hits-new-low-harris.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2021/09/23/biden-loses-ground-with-the-public-on-issues-personal-traits-and-job-approval/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  have shown that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating is now underwater, as he weathers criticism for everything from the chaotic Afghanistan withdrawal to the possible government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked for his response to criticism that he has not delivered on his campaign promises, as the country faces the possibility of both a government shutdown and an economic default.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRemember I said it\u8217\'20\'19s going to take me a year to deliver everything I\u8217\'20\'19m looking at here,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTake a look at what I inherited when I came into office,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added. \u8220\'20\'1CPart of it is dealing with the panoply of things that landed on my plate. I\u8217\'20\'19m not complaining, it\u8217\'20\'19s just a reality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 'There will be consequences' for treatment of Haitian migrants, Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took several questions from reporters after concluding his prepared remarks on efforts to get more Americans vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, the first question focused on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of Haitian migrants who have recently arrived at the US-Mexican border in large numbers.\par \par \uc2 Biden was asked whether he takes responsibility for border agents\u8217\'20\'19 behavior toward the migrants. Some disturbing footage from Del Rio, Texas, showed border agents on horseback confronting a group of migrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course I take responsibility. I\u8217\'20\'19m president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding that the footage was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous. I promise you, those people will pay,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, pointing to the investigation that is underway. \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden also warned that such behavior was \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csends the wrong message around the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s simply not who we are,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says he will get a booster shot after CDC approves them for high-risk groups\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered remarks this morning on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to boost vaccination rates in the US.\par \par \uc2 The president celebrated the news that the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/cdc-overrides-advisory-panel-pfizer-booster-americans-high-risk-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has officially}}}\uc2  approved \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine booster shots for high-risk populations, including those who are 65 or older.\par \par \uc2 The 78-year-old president said he would be receiving his booster shot \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as I can.\u8221\'20\'1D(Biden received his second \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  dose in January.)\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden says the one-quarter of eligible Americans who haven't gotten a COVID-19 vaccine shot "are causing a lot of damage," blaming them for overcrowding hospitals and putting "our economy at risk."\par \par \uc2 "The refusal to get vaccinated has cost all of us." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xgDWhEkad5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xgDWhEkad5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1441404995207766021?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president also once again urged all eligible Americans to get vaccinated, emphasizing that lower vaccination rates pose a threat to entire communities.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that one-quarter of all eligible Americans have not yet gotten a single vaccine dose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a country as large as ours, that 25% minority can cause an awful lot of damage. And they are causing a lot of damage,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe refusal to get vaccinated has cost all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president is now taking questions from reporters, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats request testimony of CEO who oversaw Arizona 'audit'\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are now requesting the testimony of Doug Logan, the CEO of Cyber Ninjas, which oversaw the sham \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D in Maricopa county.\par \par \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , the chairwoman of the House oversight committee, and Jamie Raskin, the chairman of the subcommittee on civil rights and civil liberties, sent a letter to Logan asking him to appear at a hearing on October 7.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW ??: Chairs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMaloney?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMaloney}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRaskin}}}\uc2  sent a letter to Douglas Logan, CEO of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/CyberNinjas?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #CyberNinjas}}}\uc2 , Inc., requesting his testimony at a hearing on October 7, 2021, regarding Cyber Ninjas\u8217\'20\'19 role in an \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D of 2.1 million ballots cast in Maricopa County, Arizona in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/2020election?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #2020election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oversight Committee (@OversightDems) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OversightDems/status/1441397344168136711?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis request follows your repeated refusal to produce documents requested by the Committee regarding this largely privately funded audit,\u8221\'20\'1D Maloney and Raskin wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result of your obstruction, your participation in a Committee hearing is necessary for the Committee to advance the investigation of the questionable audit your company performed and to examine whether this audit is interfering with Americans\u8217\'20\'19 right to vote free from partisan interference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether Logan, who has expressed support for the baseless conspiracy theory that there was widespread fraud in the 2020 election, will actually appear at the hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Maricopa county \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D was conducted by Cyber Ninjas, a Florida-based cybersecurity firm with little experience in elections.\par \par \uc2 The CEO of Cyber Ninjas, Doug Logan, had previously promoted the baseless conspiracy theory that there was widespread fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2021/03/31/arizona-senate-hires-a-stop-the-steal-advocate-to-lead-2020-election-audit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Arizona Mirror}}}\uc2 , in December 2020, Logan retweeted a tweet from a since-suspended account reading, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m tired of hearing people say there was no fraud. It happened, it\u8217\'20\'19s real, and people better get wise fast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of course, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have presented absolutely no evidence of widespread fraud in the election, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  fairly won.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine and Oliver Milman report:\par \par \uc2 Even though the \u8220\'20\'1Caudit\u8221\'20\'1D was sanctioned by the GOP-controlled Arizona senate, it was funded by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2021/07/28/election-conspiracy-theorist-groups-paid-5-7-million-for-the-arizona-audit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $5.7m}}}\uc2  in outside money, much of which came from conspiracy theorists, including $3.2m from Patrick Byrne, the former CEO of Overstock.com and an additional $1m from a non-profit founded by \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Election experts have widely panned the review, which they say was rooted in shoddy practice around a pre-determined effort to show there was fraud.\par \par \uc2 Ben Ginsberg, a longtime Republican election lawyer, told reporters on Thursday that Trump allies were \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperate for a win\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Maricopa county, he said, they had gotten unprecedented access to look under the hood of an election. If they were not able to prove fraud there, they were unlikely to prove it anywhere else.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of what the report says, Republican efforts to conduct similar reviews are underway. Republicans in both the Wisconsin and Pennsylvania legislatures are moving forward with similar probes in to the 2020 race.\par \par \uc2 And on Thursday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called for a review of the 2020 race in Texas, a state he carried in 2020 by nearly 6 points. Experts worry that the reviews suggest a new normal, where the losers of elections simply refuse to accept the results.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Controversial Arizona 'audit' shows Trump lost by even more votes\par \par \uc2 Greetings, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The highly controversial \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/22/arizona-sham-audit-rumbles-on-but-could-it-backfire-on-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 audit}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D of 2020 ballots has now concluded in Maricopa county, Arizona, and a report was released of its early findings.\par \par \uc2 And that report confirmed what was already known: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s largest county (and the state overall).\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Republic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2021/09/23/arizona-audit-draft-report-confirms-biden-beat-trump-2020/5835521001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The three-volume report by the Cyber Ninjas, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s lead contractor, includes results that show Trump lost by a wider margin than the county\u8217\'20\'19s official election results. The data in the report also confirms that U.S. Sen. Mark Kelly won in the county.\par \par \uc2 The official results are set to be presented to the Senate at 1 p.m. Friday. Several versions of the draft report, titled \u8216\'20\'18Maricopa County Forensic Audit\u8217\'20\'19 by Cyber Ninjas, circulated prematurely on Wednesday and Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The audit was demanded and then promoted by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies, who have continued to peddle the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 And Trump supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/not-just-arizona-republicans-push-more-partisan-election-audits-n1268644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have called}}}\uc2  for similar \u8220\'20\'1Caudits\u8221\'20\'1D in many other US states and counties, almost a year after the election took place.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the Arizona results will discourage some of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s fans from pursuing these sham investigations. But this blogger is skeptical of that.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par 