\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House Democrats vote to establish federal right to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,081 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2021\par 17:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health and Protection Act is part of strategy to push back against rush of state laws but unlikely to advance in Senate\par \par \uc2 House Democrats voted on Friday to establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , moving swiftly to advance the measure after the supreme court declined to stop a Texas law effectively outlawing the procedure and as they await a separate ruling next year that could further erode access.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, named the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health and Protection Act, is part of the party\u8217\'20\'19s strategy to push back against the rush of state laws restricting abortions and to show their determination to defend reproductive rights, an issue they believe will resonate ahead of the 2022 midterm elections. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has urged support for the measure, but Republican opposition in the Senate all but ensures the bill will not reach his desk.\par \par \uc2 With the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , presiding over the vote, the House passed the measure 218-211. All Republicans and one Democrat, congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  of Texas, opposed the bill.\par \par \uc2 The bill is unlikely to advance in the Senate, where Republican opposition is sure to prevent the measure from winning the 60 votes necessary to overcome a filibuster. Nevertheless, the Senate Majority Leader Chuck announced on Friday that he intended to bring the bill to the floor for a vote \u8220\'20\'1Cin the very near future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are currently seeing unprecedented and unconscionable Republican attacks on reproductive rights across the country laced with vicious vigilantism,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a joint statement with Senate sponsors of the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must assert its role to protect the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The near-total party line vote reflects a decades-long shift in the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s embrace of reproductive issues. While Democratic leaders were once reluctant to bring such measures to the floor out of concern for the more socially conservative members of their caucus, nearly every congressional Democrat supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and those who don\u8217\'20\'19t, like Cuellar, have faced increasingly difficult primary challenges.\par \par \uc2 The debate ahead of the vote was passionate and personal, as was expected for what has become one of the most polarizing issues in American politics. Some Democrats recalled the \u8220\'20\'1Cdark ages\u8221\'20\'1D before Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 supreme court decision that established a legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v Wade was not the beginning of women having abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Congresswoman Jan Schakowsky, a Democrat from Illinois. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was the end of women dying from abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Sylvia Garcia, a Democrat of Texas, waved a wire coat hanger as a symbol of the dangerous \u8211\'20\'13 and sometimes deadly \u8211\'20\'13 methods women would use to attempt an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it was legalized.\par \par \uc2 Republicans rose to denounce the bill, arguing that it would allow \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand\u8221\'20\'1D at every stage of pregnancy, even until birth.\par \par \uc2 The measure \u8220\'20\'1Cisn\u8217\'20\'19t about freedom for women,\u8221\'20\'1D said Congresswoman \uc2 Vicky Hartzler\uc2 , a Republican from Missouri. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about death for babies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The legislation would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law and prohibit states from imposing \u8220\'20\'1Cmedically unnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D restrictions that make it difficult to perform and access. It would allow an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after viability \u8211\'20\'13 the point at which a healthy fetus can survive outside the womb, typically between 21 and 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 only in cases where the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health is at risk.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Judy Chu of California, the lead author of the bill, has introduced versions of this legislation in previous cycles. But Democrats moved to vote on it for the first time after the supreme court refused to intervene to block a Texas law that prohibits abortions after a fetal heartbeat is detected, roughly the sixth week of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. The court did not address the constitutionality of the law, but many advocates on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate viewed the decision as a potential sign of how it might rule in a coming challenge to Roe.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law makes no exemptions for pregnancies that are the result of rape or incest. It also effectively deputizes ordinary citizens regardless of where they live to enforce the law, allowing them to collect $10,000 for successfully bring a civil suit against anyone found to \u8220\'20\'1Caid or abet\u8221\'20\'1D an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration sued Texas, arguing that the law is clearly unconstitutional. At least two lawsuits have been filed \u8211\'20\'13 one by a man in Arkansas and another by a man in Illinois \u8211\'20\'13 against a doctor in Texas who published an op-ed claiming to have performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in violation of the new law.\par \par \uc2 Democrats warned of copycat laws popping up in Republican-controlled legislatures across the country. But they are also bracing for a supreme court decision next year, when it will rule on a Mississippi law that seeks to ban most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 a direct challenge to Roe.\par \par \uc2 There is widespread fear among proponents of reproductive rights that the current court, composed of six conservative justices, three of whom \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed to be \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, could further roll back or entirely dismantle Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot rely on Amy Coney Barrett or \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  to confirm our rights for us,\u8221\'20\'1D Chu said at a press conference on Friday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must protect the rights of women and pregnant people in every zip code.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Formidable Republican opposition awaits in the evenly-divided Senate, where it remains unclear if the bill could win the support of all 50 Democrats in the chamber. Two members of the caucus who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, senators Bob Casey of Pennsylvania and Joe Manchin of West Virginia, have not co-sponsored the bill.\par \par \uc2 One of only a few remaining pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans, Senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2021-09-22/sen-susan-collins-says-she-would-oppose-abortion-rights-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the LA Times she opposes th bill and is working with other senators to craft a bill that would \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly would codify Roe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Public opinion polls have consistently found strong support for keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in all or some circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration said it \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly supports\u8221\'20\'1D passage of this bill in light of \u8220\'20\'1CTexas\u8217\'20\'19 unprecedented attack\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur daughters and granddaughters deserve the same rights that their mothers and grandmothers fought for and won\u8212\'20\'14and that a clear majority of the American people support,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a statement of administration policy. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not allow this country to go backwards on women\u8217\'20\'19s equality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210924eh9o002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
