\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bill modeled after Texas ban introduced in Florida\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2021\par 15:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bill gives citizens the right to sue anyone who helps someone who seeks an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as in Texas\par \par \uc2 An anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill that would ban abortions after an embryonic heartbeat is detected, about six weeks, and allow citizens to sue doctors who perform them, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 modeled after Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban SB8}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-religion-us-supreme-court-laws-23c373f3252d511f15ccc170887c30e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was introduced in Florida}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Filed by the Republican representative Webster Barnaby, the bill allows people to sue practitioners and others who aid people seeking abortions up to six months after an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was performed versus only four months allocated in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s SB8. The implications of the bill have alarmed many concerned about the role of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/texas-abortion-vigilantes-sb8-citizens-sue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  vigilante}}}\uc2  lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 Previous attempts to pass such restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in Florida had failed, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to block }}}\uc2  Texas\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law has ignited new attempts to pass anti-choice legislation across the country. In addition to Florida, Republican leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/03/texas-abortion-republicans-six-states-arkansas-florida-indiana-mississippi-north-south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in at least five other states}}}\uc2  have said that they are interested in passing legislation similar to the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/01/democrats-condemn-supreme-court-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely criticized }}}\uc2  decision, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and other Republican lawmakers echoed their support for the bill and interest in replicating it in the Sunshine state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have always fought for unborn babies and their right to life, and the Florida house of representatives has been a national leader in developing pro-life legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Florida house speaker, \uc2 Chris Sprowls\uc2 , via a spokesperson following the supreme court decision. \u8220\'20\'1COur laws have to be strong enough to jump through multiple levels of judicial scrutiny. We look forward to bringing to the floor a bill that saves every unborn life possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barnaby\u8217\'20\'19s office did not return a request for comment from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-texas-florida-laws-ce46baccd56943066d488c218b268bbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Florida Democrats have condemned the new legislation, including the agriculture commissioner, \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , who announced her run for governor of Florida next year against DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill is dangerous, radical, and unconstitutional. The hypocrisy of this attempt by Governor [Ron] DeSantis and Republicans in the state legislature to take away our rights while at the same time preaching \u8216\'20\'18my body, my choice\u8217\'20\'19 when it comes to wearing masks is absolutely disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fried in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210923eh9n0020g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
