\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New Texas law bans  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs after seven weeks pregnancy\b0\par\par\uc2 Melody Schreiber \par \uc2 666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2021\par 15:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s actions sparked outrage from reproductive rights advocates in a state that recently passed another restrictive bill\par \par \uc2 By the end of the year Texas may have even more restrictions on the ability to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its Republican governor, Greg Abbott, quietly signed into law new restrictions banning the mail-order provision of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication seven weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/872/billtext/pdf/SB00004F.pdf#navpanes=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2  prevents providers from prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs more than seven weeks into pregnancy, instead of 10 weeks, the current limit. It takes effect on 2 December.\par \par \uc2 Abbott signed the law with no meaningful fanfare on Friday and news about the event only broke later, triggering outrage from reproductive rights advocates who warned the move was another devastating blow to pregnant people in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-choice politicians in Texas are launching their attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access from every angle imaginable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adrienne Kimmell, Naral Pro-Choice America acting president, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Even before the legislation, known as Senate Bill 4 (SB4), was signed, Texas had some of the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the country amid requirements for a 24-hour waiting period, ultrasound imaging, admitting privileges for doctors, parental consent for minors.\par \par \uc2 Another controversial bill, Senate Bill 8 (SB8), was passed by the Texas legislature in May that sought to stop abortions in the state beyond six weeks, often before many people know they are pregnant. That law effectively rendered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state almost impossible and triggered widespread condemnation when the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused an emergency request}}}\uc2  to block the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe most recent one, in terms of mail-order prescriptions, simply adds one more barrier,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Jones, a professor of political science at Rice University.\par \par \uc2 The sweep of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures will probably prove popular among Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s Republican base, but may not gain wider approval within Texas. About a third of Texans want to see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended entirely, except when pregnancy threatens the life of the pregnant person. But about half of Texans want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain legal, Jones said.\par \par \uc2 Will Metcalf, a Texas state representative, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/willmetcalfTX/status/1432803779804635143?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  last month that the bill sought a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrackdown on unsafe \u8216\'20\'18mail order\u8217\'20\'19 abortions\u8221\'20\'1D and to increase reporting requirements for medical complications. The Texas legislature approved SB4 in a special session ending 2 September.\par \par \uc2 Those who \u8220\'20\'1Cintentionally, knowingly, or recklessly\u8221\'20\'1D violate the law by providing medication through the mail will now face criminal penalties \u8211\'20\'13 as much as $10,000 in fines and two years in prison \u8211\'20\'13 including providers from out of state, the Dallas Morning News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2021/09/20/gov-greg-abbott-signs-more-texas-abortion-restrictions-penalties-into-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the law also applies to international organizations providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication through the mail, such a state-level law could prove difficult to enforce.\par \par \uc2 Soon after SB8 went into effect, there were indications that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/texas-women-are-now-going-online-abortion-pills-info-after-states-new-ban-says-nonprofit-1628243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  self-managed abortions were rising}}}\uc2 , with a sharp increase in traffic to sites providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs in the mail.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court did not block SB8 from going into effect in Texas, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/21a24_8759.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in its decision the challengers raised \u8220\'20\'1Cserious questions\u8221\'20\'1D about the constitutionality of the law. A physician who challenged the law, Alan Braid, is now being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/texas-abortion-law-san-antonio-doctor-sued"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued for providing an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow you actually do have somebody whose rights are being violated, who is being sued for doing something that the supreme court has said is constitutional and legal,\u8221\'20\'1D Jones said. It may prove whether extreme laws such as SB8 and SB4 will stand in higher courts, he said.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and health organizations are working to provide better access to contraception in the wake of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s severe restrictions.\par \par \uc2 People in Texas and other states \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserve access to the full range of reproductive options, which includes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, Angela Maske, who works with the #FreeThePill Youth Council. \u8220\'20\'1CAs we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing these increasing attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, it\u8217\'20\'19s really more important than ever that we improve access to birth control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210922eh9m0018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
