\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump campaign knew voter fraud claims were baseless soon after election loss, says report \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett (now) and Joan E Greve in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 8,044 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2021\par 07:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump has continued to peddle lies about fraud in the 2020 election up until now, almost a year after ballots were castAdam Schiff: Capitol riot committee \u8216\'20\'18going straight to subpoenas\u8217\'20\'19Democrats push Biden\u8217\'20\'19s spending plans while trying to avoid shutdownSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 We are wrapping up another day of US politics coverage. Here are today\u8217\'20\'19s highlights:\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration is facing public criticism from powerful Democrats about its continued use of a Trump-era border policy, Title 42, which denies migrants at the US border the ability to seek asylum. Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , among others, have spoken out against the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s use of Title 42, in the context of a still-unfolding scandal about US Border Patrol treatment of Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expressed her support for a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough investigation\u8221\'20\'1D of the treatment of Haitian immigrants at the US-Mexican border. The vice-president said the footage of US border patrol agents confronting Haitian immigrants on horseback and potentially using whips on them was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should never be treated that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m deeply troubled about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Adam Schiff said the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing straight to subpoenaswhere we think we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with recalcitrant witnesses.\u8221\'20\'1D The Democratic congressman told reporters that he expects some of the panel\u8217\'20\'19s requests to be complied with, but he added, \u8220\'20\'1CWhere we do meet resistance, we intend to push back hard and fast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Newly released court documents show that the Trump campaign knew its allegations against \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  were baseless within weeks of the 2020 election. The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/us/politics/trump-dominion-voting.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign drafted an internal memo on November 19 that debunked election conspiracy theories involving Dominion and its voting machines. And yet, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team continued to peddle the false allegations against Dominion.\par \par \uc2 * Congressional Democrats are facing multiple crises as they attempt to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda. Intraparty divisions remain over both the bipartisan infrastructure bill and the $3.5tn reconciliation package, while lawmakers are trying to simultaneously suspend the debt ceiling and extend government funding past the end of the month. Republicans remain adamant that they will not assist in any effort to increase the debt ceiling, even though Democrats helped them do just that during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 * Biden addressed the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2  and outlined his approach to foreign policy. As the US president receives criticism for his handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal and weathers France\u8217\'20\'19s outrage over a nuclear submarine deal with Australia, Biden promised \u8220\'20\'1Ca new era of relentless diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CUS military power must be our tool of last resort, not our first,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * In response to the ongoing criticism of \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in vaccine misinformation, racist rhetoric, lies about the 2020 election and other crises, M ark Zuckerberg signed off on a plan to insert positive information about the company intoFacebook users\u8217\'20\'19 news\u8217\'20\'19 feeds, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, US medical staff at the front lines of the country\u8217\'20\'19s 1,900 Covid-19 deaths a day, the most since March, are speaking out about the \u8220\'20\'1C heart-wrenching, soul-crushing\u8221\'20\'1D effects of witnessing the deaths of unvaccinated people amid widespread misinformation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Heart-wrenching, soul-crushing\u8217\'20\'19: US COVID-19 deaths are topping 1,900 a day\par \par \uc2 COVID-19 deaths in the U.S. have climbed to an average of more than 1,900 a day for the first time since early March, with experts saying the virus is preying largely on a distinct group: 71 million unvaccinated Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-coronavirus-pandemic-missouri-c4d03a53de4036158fabb0125c4f7b02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The increasingly lethal turn has filled hospitals, complicated the start of the school year, delayed the return to offices and demoralized health care workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr. Dena Hubbard, a pediatrician in the Kansas City, Missouri, area who has cared for babies delivered prematurely by cesarean section in a last-ditch effort to save their mothers, some of whom died. For health workers, the deaths, combined with misinformation and disbelief about the virus, have been \u8220\'20\'1Cheart-wrenching, soul-crushing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Trans youth in Texas show up to testify against third round of anti-trans bills\par \par \uc2 For The 19th, Orion Rummler reports from Texas on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/09/trans-texans-special-session-means-another-fight-to-exist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emotional toll}}}\uc2  of having to advocate against multiple rounds of anti-trans legislation at the state level.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the things they say about trans children, it\u8217\'20\'19s heartbreaking,\u8221\'20\'1D one Texan said.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Doing this work is hard. Have your therapist on speed dial, hard."\par \par \uc2 Trans youth in Texas are fighting off a third round of anti-trans bills this year.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/i_oriion?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @i_oriion}}}\uc2  reports, the cost of that fight, is taking a toll. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3Ujmdx09u3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3Ujmdx09u3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Sosin (@shoeleatherkate) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shoeleatherkate/status/1440355121808830469?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The people showing up to testify at the capitol during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/09/trans-texans-special-session-means-another-fight-to-exist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marathon sessions}}}\uc2  are not necessarily representative of trans Texans and their families overall, Rummler reported.\par \par \uc2 White parents of trans kids are typically the face of the debate over anti-trans legislation, Victoria Kirby York, deputy executive director of the National Black Justice Coalition, told The 19th: \u8220\'20\'1CIt paints a picture of who the harm is hitting that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get at the data.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Project Amplify\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Facebook\uc2  reportedly using news feed to boost pro-\uc2 Facebook\uc2  stories\par \par \uc2 When a plan to use \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s news feed to show users positive content about the company was discussed at a January internal meeting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/technology/zuckerberg-facebook-project-amplify.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several Facebook executives were \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked,\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  signed off on the policy last month, according to the Times, part of what reporters characterized as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/technology/zuckerberg-facebook-project-amplify.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broader shift within Facebook to apologize less}}}\uc2  when faced with evidence of the platform\u8217\'20\'19s role in vaccine misinformation, racist rhetoric, and other democratic crises.\par \par \uc2 enltrFacebook is using its News Feed, the social network's most important digital real estate, to show people positive stories about itself as part of a new initiative approved by \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  and code-named Project Amplify. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iDrzvwenWu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iDrzvwenWu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  (@nytimes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes/status/1440429000384409604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The effort also reportedly focused on cutting down on internal leaks from within the company.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt leaked. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Fg8vuvtAsy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Fg8vuvtAsy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bGqpdlLxQO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bGqpdlLxQO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1440433084915011596?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Gabby Petito confirmed dead of homicide as search for fiance continues\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  says a county coroner has confirmed that human remains found in remote northern Wyoming along the border of Grand Teton national park are those of 22-year-old Gabby Petito, who disappeared while on a cross-country road trip with a fiance who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/gabby-petito-florida-police-search-fiance-brian-laundrie-of-missing-woman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now being sought by authorities}}}\uc2  in Florida.\par \par \uc2 The Teton county coroner, Brent Blue, determined her manner of death was homicide, but did not disclose a cause of death pending final autopsy results, officials said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrTeton County Coroner Dr. Brent Blue confirmed the remains are those of Gabrielle Venora Petito, date of birth March 19, 1999. Coroner Blue\u8217\'20\'19s initial determination for the manner of death is homicide. The cause of death remains pending final autopsy results. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JoHenMZ9UU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JoHenMZ9UU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 FBI\uc2  Denver (@FBIDenver) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBIDenver/status/1440421552042897415?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The national attention to Petito\u8217\'20\'19s disappearance and death has prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insider.com/710-indigenous-people-missing-in-wyoming-where-gabby-petito-disappeared-2021-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broader conversations }}}\uc2  about the ongoing crisis of missing and murdered women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insider.com/710-indigenous-people-missing-in-wyoming-where-gabby-petito-disappeared-2021-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly indigenous women}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Chaotic\u8217\'20\'19 scene as White House aides block questions to Biden about border policies\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  took questions from British reporters during an Oval Office meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but White House aides shut down American reporters\u8217\'20\'19 attempts to ask the president about the US border. The government\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of Haitian migrants at the border has sparked broad condemnation this week.\par \par \uc2 enltrA chaotic scene in the Oval Office today as \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  unexpectedly took questions from British reporters, and White House aides shouted over American reporters as we tried to ask Biden questions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2wus2ilX0F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2wus2ilX0F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Restuccia (@AndrewRestuccia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewRestuccia/status/1440430907261800452?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNot good, folks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9mN15mZL9y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9mN15mZL9y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Seung Min Kim (@seungminkim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/seungminkim/status/1440430677288108044?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden did attempt to answer a reporter\u8217\'20\'19s question, but his answer was \u8220\'20\'1Cundecipherable,\u8221\'20\'1D CBS News reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrCBS News' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @EdOkeefe}}}\uc2  reports that during Pres. Biden's bilateral meeting with British PM \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , U.S. press questions about the southern border were shouted down by White House aides. The president's answer was undecipherable. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MeXVTcFEBX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MeXVTcFEBX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1440432398223622157?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Update: a CBS News reporter tweeted that part of the president\u8217\'20\'19s answer was decipherable once they played the tape back later: \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not justified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: We have played back the tape and part of the president\u8217\'20\'19s answer is decipherable. I asked for his response to the situation on the southern border and he says in part, \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not justified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He is wearing a mask and there is shouting so nothing else is decipherable\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1440438931040784386?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats speak out about Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s use of Trump border policy\par \par \uc2 Powerful Democratic lawmakers have been speaking out about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of Haitian migrants at the border, and prominent celebrities are also highlighting the policy and calling for the Biden administration to change course.\par \par \uc2 enltrNotable seeing Schumer come out so strongly against Title 42 --- and framing it as a Trump policy Biden has chosen to continue. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jWCjEcsSeh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jWCjEcsSeh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hamed Aleaziz (@Haleaziz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Haleaziz/status/1440355393557843974?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe horrible treatment of these innocent Haitian people\u8212\'20\'14who have come to the border fleeing violence and natural disaster\u8212\'20\'14must stop immediately.\par \par \uc2 The Admin must stop these expulsions and end this Title 42 policy at our southern border.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1440384096396472334?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats from Texas and Oregon have also been highlighting the policy, which \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  News immigration reporter Hamed Aleaziz wrote had not previously generated a broad public discussion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTitle 42 has been a policy that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t produced outrage/protest on a wide scale,\u8221\'20\'1D Aleaziz wrote on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden rarely talks about it and his administration discusses it as an unfortunate necessity. Schumer, in this clip, is framing it as a choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAs the son of parents who fled Nazi Germany to find refuge in America, I know the importance of our country remaining a safe and humane haven. Haitian refugees deserve far better than a knee-jerk Title 42 response.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  (@RonWyden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonWyden/status/1440443063705300993?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAsylum is a fundamental human right that the U.S. has suspended for 18 months now.\par \par \uc2 Title 42 has allowed people fleeing desperate situations to be summarily deported without due process.\par \par \uc2 The admin must reverse course or we risk allowing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies to become the default.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Juli\u225\'00\'E1n Castro (@JulianCastro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulianCastro/status/1440116376123891717?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Other prominent Americans, including filmmaker Ava Duvernay, also put a spotlight on Title 42.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHaiti \u8212\'20\'14 the only nation on Earth to free itself from the shackles of slavery and that continues to pay the price for that act \u8212\'20\'14 as the entire world regards it with untold scorn and shame.\u8221\'20\'1D - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SonofBaldwin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SonofBaldwin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  must end Title 42 deportations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kxCXwsY0nu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kxCXwsY0nu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ava DuVernay (@ava) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ava/status/1440329923512528896?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has more background on the policy and its history:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Biden administration is relying on a contested Trump-era policy - based on a public health law known as Title 42 - as it disperses thousands of Haitian migrants along the U.S.-Mexico border. Here's a look at the law and the controversy surrounding it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KV7F4J1Z6q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KV7F4J1Z6q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1440101985739546624?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 After \u8216\'20\'18horrible\u8217\'20\'19 border images, Democrats press administration to end use of Title 42\par \par \uc2 The White House is facing sharp condemnation from Democrats for its handling of the influx of Haitian migrants at the U.S. southern border, after images of U.S. Border Patrol agents on horseback using aggressive tactics went viral this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-del-rio-alejandro-mayorkas-de6e8368484e5a45788c808596a9b4d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In response, Democrats on Capitol Hill are calling on the Biden administration to end its use of a pandemic-era authority to deport migrants without giving them an opportunity to seek asylum in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The provision in question, known as Title 42, was put in place by the Trump administration in March 2020 to justify restrictive immigration policies in an effort to prevent the spread of the coronavirus. But the Biden administration has used Title 42 to justify the deportation of Haitian migrants who in recent days have set up an encampment in and around the small city of Del Rio, Texas. The provision gives federal health officials powers during a pandemic to take extraordinary measures to limit transmission of an infectious disease.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge late last week ruled the regulation was improper and gave the government two weeks before its use was to be halted, but the Biden administration on Monday appealed the decision. Shortly after the judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision on Friday, Homeland Security officials formed a plan to begin immediately turning the groups of Haitian migrants around, working against the clock.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration pushing back on this stay of expulsions is another example of broken promises to treat migrants with respect and humanity when they reach our borders to exercise their fundamental right to asylum,\u8221\'20\'1D said Karla Marisol Vargas, senior attorney with the Texas Civil Rights Project and co-counsel on the litigation.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Mayorkas said he was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrified\u8221\'20\'1D by the images that have spread widely on social media. Some of the mounted agents use their horses to forcibly move and block the migrants, seeming to herd them like animals, and taunt them in at least one instance." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S1znUuxrYN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/S1znUuxrYN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 darlene superville (@dsupervilleap) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dsupervilleap/status/1440406864718487552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/haitian-migrants-texas-del-rio-bridge-expelled-us-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke out earlier}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, saying the photos of the Border Patrol agents\u8217\'20\'19 treatment of migrants left her deeply troubled, and that \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should never be treated that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reflecting the urgency of the political problem for the administration, Homeland Security chief Alejandro Mayorkas also said Tuesday the images \u8220\'20\'1Chorrified\u8221\'20\'1D him, a seeming shift in tone from a day earlier, when he and others were more sanguine about the situation at the border.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics north of Texas flooded with patients after severe state ban\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe journey from Texas \u8211\'20\'13 whose surface area is almost 270,000 square miles \u8211\'20\'13 to other states poses its own challenge. For many, the trip will be impossible. For others, it will be harrowing,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shefali Luthra reports for The 19th}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrAbortion clinics in states north of Texas report seeing **double** the number of patients than before Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8212\'20\'14 and phones \u8220\'20\'1Cringing off the hook.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QuM0iYfFB1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QuM0iYfFB1}}}\uc2  via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/19thnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @19thnews}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shefalil?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @shefalil}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emily Ramshaw (@eramshaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eramshaw/status/1438910112899420161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne minor, who was raped by a family member, traveled eight hours from Galveston to Oklahoma to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the DOJ briefing. \u8220\'20\'1CAnother patient facing violence at the hands of her husband is \u8216\'20\'18discreetly attempting to leave Texas without her husband finding out,\u8217\'20\'19 and is \u8216\'20\'18desperate\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18selling personal items\u8217\'20\'19 to scrape together the funds needed for an out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/abortion-clinics-bordering-texas-are-seeing-double-the-number-of-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics north of Texas flooded with patients after severe state ban }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 New poll shows Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rate has dropped to 31% in Iowa\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Iowa adults disapprove of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s job as president, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/2021/09/21/president-joe-biden-job-approval-rating-plunges-after-afghanistan-covid-surge/8378224002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Des Moines Register poll}}}\uc2 . Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support is now lower than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s worst results in the same poll, the newspaper reported, and his handling of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan has the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/2021/09/21/president-joe-biden-job-approval-rating-plunges-after-afghanistan-covid-surge/8378224002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  lowest approval}}}\uc2  of the issues surveyed.\par \par \uc2 enltrYikes: Biden approval in IOWA down to 31 percent, with 62 percent disapproving, in new Des Moines Register poll.\par \par \uc2 Obama carried Iowa 2x in his presidential campaigns. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UxQre4NAuR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UxQre4NAuR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Kraushaar (@HotlineJosh) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HotlineJosh/status/1440313056072896517?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The mid-September poll surveyed 805 Iowa adults, and has a margin of error of plus or minus 3.5 percentage points, according to the Des Moines Register.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  confirms SEC investigation into sexual misconduct allegations\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live US politics coverage from our West Coast bureau in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  has confirmed an investigation by US regulators following allegations of sexual misconduct and discrimination at one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most high-profile video game companies.\par \par \uc2 The California-based company said on Tuesday that it was complying with a recent \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  subpoena sent to current and former employees and executives and the company itself on \u8220\'20\'1Cemployment matters and related issues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/sep/21/activision-blizzard-confirms-sec-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Activision Blizzard confirms SEC investigation into sexual misconduct allegations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Lois Beckett, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Congressional Democrats are facing multiple crises as they attempt to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda. Intraparty divisions remain over both the bipartisan infrastructure bill and the $3.5tn reconciliation package, while lawmakers are trying to simultaneously suspend the debt ceiling and extend government funding past the end of the month. Republicans remain adamant that they will not assist in any effort to increase the debt ceiling, even though Democrats helped them do just that during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 * Biden addressed the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2  and outlined his approach to foreign policy. As the US president receives criticism for his handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal and weathers France\u8217\'20\'19s outrage over a nuclear submarine deal with Australia, Biden promised \u8220\'20\'1Ca new era of relentless diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CUS military power must be our tool of last resort, not our first,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expressed her support for a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough investigation\u8221\'20\'1D of the treatment of Haitian immigrants at the US-Mexican border. The vice-president said the footage of US border patrol agents confronting Haitian immigrants on horseback and potentially using whips on them was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should never be treated that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m deeply troubled about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Adam Schiff said the select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing straight to subpoenaswhere we think we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with recalcitrant witnesses.\u8221\'20\'1D The Democratic congressman told reporters that he expects some of the panel\u8217\'20\'19s requests to be complied with, but he added, \u8220\'20\'1CWhere we do meet resistance, we intend to push back hard and fast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Newly released court documents show that the Trump campaign knew its allegations against \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  were baseless within weeks of the 2020 election. The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/us/politics/trump-dominion-voting.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign drafted an internal memo on November 19 that debunked election conspiracy theories involving Dominion and its voting machines. And yet, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team continued to peddle the false allegations against Dominion.\par \par \uc2 Lois will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli foreign minister \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2  spoke with House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  about the dust-up over Iron Dome funding in Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 government spending bill, per Walla News.\par \par \uc2 Hoyer reportedly told Lapid that the funding hold-up was \u8220\'20\'1Ctechnical\u8221\'20\'1D and Democratic leaders remain committed to getting the money approved soon.\par \par \uc2 enltrIsraeli foreign minister \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2  spoke to House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  about the hold up in the voting on the Iron Dome funding\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barak Ravid (@BarakRavid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarakRavid/status/1440412581424889857?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats have reportedly stripped $1bn in funding for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Iron Dome defense system from their government spending bill, after progressives expressed criticism of the provision.\par \par \uc2 Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/democrats-iron-dome-government-funding-2e81d2d4-8001-4f97-a4cc-23c1db6b3c17.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 There has never a situation where military aid for Israel was held up because of objections from members of Congress. While the funding will get a vote in its current defense bill, the clash underscores the deep divisions within the Democratic party over Israel....\par \par \uc2 The funding has been a key priority for House Majority Leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  (D-Md.), but its supporters ultimately caved after several progressive members like \uc2 Rep. Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (D-Wash.) threatened to vote against the short-term funding bill, which also includes language to raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The Iron Dome will be included in the final, bipartisan and bicameral fiscal year 2022 Defense bill,\u8217\'20\'19 said a House Appropriations committee spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 Some House Democrats have criticized their progressive colleagues for targeting the Iron Dome spending, arguing that the technology has helped protect civilian lives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever your views on the Israeli-[Palestinian] conflict, using a system that just saved hundreds, if not thousands, of lives as a political chit is problematic,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrIron Dome is a purely *defensive* system \u8212\'20\'14 it protects civilians when hundreds of rockets are shot at population centers. Whatever your views on the Israeli-Pal conflict, using a system that just saved hundreds, if not thousands, of lives as a political chit is problematic. (2/5)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Elissa Slotkin\uc2  (@RepSlotkin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSlotkin/status/1440383924375416844?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  went into Monday\u8217\'20\'19s federal election with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/13/canada-anita-anand-covid-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s highest Covid-19 vaccination rates}}}\uc2 , billions spent on pandemic aid and the hope that he could convert the earned goodwill into a majority government.\par \par \uc2 He fell short of that aim: after a 36-day campaign and a C$610m election, the makeup of parliament remained largely unchanged, with the Liberals holding roughly 158 seats \u8211\'20\'13 short of the 170 needed for a majority.\par \par \uc2 The Liberals received a smaller share of the popular vote than any other winning party in the country\u8217\'20\'19s history \u8211\'20\'13 suggesting the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s popularity is waning, despite his party\u8217\'20\'19s electoral advantages. And while the math in parliament remained largely the same, three of Trudeau\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet ministers didn\u8217\'20\'19t win re-election.\par \par \uc2 Trudeau will be forced to navigate a parliament that he needs to woo in order to survive. But it may yet give him the rare opportunity to pass sweeping, legacy-defining legislation.\par \par \uc2 When he called the election in mid August, Trudeau was asked about his future as party leader if the Liberals once again fell short of majority government. Trudeau declined to answer, but said that more work was required on crucial issues such as child-care and housing, adding that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnowhere near done yet\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to Canadian Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  today after his country\u8217\'20\'19s snap election, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House\u8217\'20\'19s readout of the conversation, Biden congratulated Trudeau on securing another term as prime minister.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe two leaders underscored the strong and deep friendship between the United States and Canada, and discussed their shared commitment to strengthening the resilience and competitiveness of the U.S. and Canadian economies and coordinating on COVID-19 pandemic response,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President expressed to Prime Minister Trudeau his desire to continue working closely and deepening collaboration with Canada \u8211\'20\'13 one of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s top partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Trudeau was able to stay in office, his Liberal party did not meet its goal of securing a majority of parliament seats, meaning the prime minister will still need to work with other parties to advance his agenda.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/canada-justin-trudeau-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trudeau didn\u8217\'20\'19t win the majority but still has chance to pass sweeping legislation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  met with British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  before his afternoon sit-down with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you will discuss with the president, the relationship between our two countries is a long and enduring one, one that we value,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told Johnson.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister added, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a great honor and privilege for me to be here, to meet you for the first time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  greets British PM \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  from her ceremonial office. Harris says she looks forward to the US and UK\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clong-standing\u8221\'20\'1D transatlantic relationship. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/phRGXHUrxx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/phRGXHUrxx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Perry (@tperry518) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tperry518/status/1440395266830462977?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  this afternoon, hours after the US president addressed the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnson shared a photo of himself boarding an \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  train from New York to Washington for the bilateral meeting.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s choice of transportation will likely delight \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/amtrak-joe-brief-history-of-bidens-history-americas-railroad-2021-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amtrak Joe}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the way to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WhiteHouse}}}\uc2  !\par \par \uc2 ???????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vLEUNX2EX5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vLEUNX2EX5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  (@BorisJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BorisJohnson/status/1440375951603298305?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s advisers continued to level false allegations against \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  even after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign had concluded they were baseless.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/us/politics/trump-dominion-voting.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 According to emails contained in the documents, Zach Parkinson, then the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s deputy director of communications, reached out to subordinates on Nov. 13 asking them to \u8216\'20\'18substantiate or debunk\u8217\'20\'19 several matters concerning Dominion. The next day, the emails show, Mr. Parkinson received a copy of a memo cobbled together by his staff from what largely appear to be news articles and public fact-checking services.\par \par \uc2 Even though the memo was hastily assembled, it rebutted a series of allegations that [campaign lawyer Sidney] Powell and others were making in public. It found:\par \par \uc2 * That Dominion did not use voting technology from the software company, \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 , in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 * That Dominion had no direct ties to Venezuela or to [George] Soros.\par \par \uc2 * And that there was no evidence that Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s leadership had connections to left-wing \u8216\'20\'18antifa\u8217\'20\'19 activists, as Ms. Powell and others had claimed.\par \par \uc2 According to the Times, it is unclear whether Trump himself saw the memo at the time. Regardless, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lies about voter fraud have been repeatedly fact-checked by numerous news outlets, and he has continued to spread them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign knew within weeks that election fraud claims were baseless - report\par \par \uc2 Newly released court documents show that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential campaign knew within weeks of the election that accusations against \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  were false.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/us/politics/trump-dominion-voting.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Two weeks after the 2020 election, a team of lawyers closely allied with \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  held a widely watched news conference at the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Washington. At the event, they laid out a bizarre conspiracy theory claiming that a voting machine company had worked with an election software firm, the financier \uc2 George Soros\uc2  and Venezuela to steal the presidential contest from Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 But there was a problem for the Trump team, according to court documents released on Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 By the time the news conference occurred on Nov. 19, Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign had already prepared an internal memo on many of the outlandish claims about the company, \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 , and the separate software company, \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 . The memo had determined that those allegations were untrue.\par \par \uc2 Trump has continued to peddle lies about fraud in the 2020 election up until now, almost a year after ballots were cast.\par \par \uc2 The former president has also extended those baseless claims to more recent elections, claiming they were also tainted by widespread fraud. Trump has, of course, presented absolutely no evidence to support those outlandish allegations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats move forward with plan to vote on infrastructure bill next week\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are moving forward with their plan to vote on the bipartisan infrastructure bill next week, despite pushback from progressive lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  confirmed this morning that the vote on the infrastructure bill will happen next Monday or Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Hoyer added that the lower chamber will vote to advance the $3.5tn reconciliation package \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as it\u8217\'20\'19s ready,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook-pm/2021/09/21/sinema-house-mods-get-their-way-494417"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement marks a defeat for progressives, who have insisted that they will not support the infrastructure bill without receiving assurances about the future of the reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of House progressives have indicated they are willing to block the infrastructure bill if necessary, which could potentially lead to the proposal\u8217\'20\'19s defeat.\par \par \uc2 Given Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 very narrow majority in the House, the future of the infrastructure bill may hang on how many Republicans choose to support it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vaccine mandates for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US military}}}\uc2  are meant to identify \u8220\'20\'1Csincere Christians \u8230\'20\'26 free thinkers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C men with high testosterone levels \u8221\'20\'1D, the Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  claimed on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . Photograph: The Rubin Report\par \par \uc2 Such people, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not love \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and would therefore \u8220\'20\'1Cleave immediately\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the takeover of the US military,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said.\par \par \uc2 The rightwing host has a hugely influential platform, reaching {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2021/08/fox-news-ratings-august-1234825169/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an average 3.3 million viewers}}}\uc2  in August. Despite vaccinations or daily Covid tests being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverdarcy/status/1437858807854608386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 required by Fox News}}}\uc2 , Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s employer, he has consistently cast doubt on vaccines and other measures to combat Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Katie Lane, whose 45-year-old father was not vaccinated and who died of Covid-19 in Washington state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/daughter-blames-tucker-carlsons-misinformation-for-unvaxxed-dads-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  he \u8220\'20\'1Cwatched some \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  videos on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , and some of those videos involved some misinformation about vaccines, and I believe that played a role\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the US death toll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2021/sep/02/covid-19-coronavirus-us-map-latest-cases-state-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed 675,000}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/flu/pandemic-resources/1918-commemoration/1918-pandemic-history.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  toll from the flu pandemic of 1918. The vast majority of hospitalisations and deaths are among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/alabama-population-shrink-first-time-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unvaccinated people}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/sep/21/tucker-carlson-fox-news-us-military-vaccine-mandate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tucker Carlson claims US military vaccine mandate a \u8216\'20\'18purity test\u8217\'20\'19 for \u8216\'20\'18men with high testosterone\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jesse Benton, and Doug Wead, two Republican operatives, have been charged with funneling $ 25,000 from an unnamed Russian to a presidential campaign in 2016.\par \par \uc2 The indictment does not name the campaign but at the time of the alleged contribution, September 2016, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was the Republican nominee for president against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the Associated Press reports, \u8220\'20\'1Caccording to court papers, Wead, 75, of Bonita Springs, Florida, told a Russian foreign national he could meet an unnamed presidential candidate at a political event in exchange for a contribution. It is illegal to solicit campaign contributions from foreigners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US justice department\uc2  alleges that Wead, also an author, and Benton, a former senior aide to the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  of Kentucky, and Senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , from the same state, orchestrated a cover-up of the illegal donation.\par \par \uc2 There is no indication that Trump or other campaign aids knew where the money came from.\par \par \uc2 The AP again: \u8220\'20\'1CBoth men appeared in court on Monday. Benton\u8217\'20\'19s attorney did not immediately return messages seeking comment. Wead attorney Jay Sekulow\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 formerly a lawyer for Trump when he was president \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Csaid Wead pleaded not guilty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last December, Trump pardoned Benton for a 2012 conviction {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumlocalnews.com/nys/binghamton/ap-top-news/2021/09/20/politico-pardoned-by-trump-accused-of-illegal-campaign-scam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for bribery.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schiff: 6 January committee 'going straight to subpoenas'\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, a senior Democratic member of the House select committee investigating the deadly attack on the US Capitol on 6 January, said on Monday the panel was \u8220\'20\'1C going straight to subpoenas where we think we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with recalcitrant witnesses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn some cases, we\u8217\'20\'19re making requests we think will be complied with,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/21/jan-6-investigation-subpoenas-513425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also told reporters}}}\uc2 , as relayed by Politico.\par \par \uc2 The select committee contains only two Republicans : prominent Trump critics \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 . The minority leader, Kevin McCarthy, withdrew co-operation when the speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , rejected his suggestion of panel slots for Jim Jordan of Ohio and Jim Banks of Indiana, key allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jordan in particular has been the focus of reporting on what he knew and when about the 6 January attack, around which five people died and which Trump supporters mounted after a \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D rally near the White House, at which Trump told them to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D in service of his lie that his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the result of electoral fraud.\par \par \uc2 Jordan and other members of Congress including McCarthy are seen as potential witnesses to be called by the 6 January committee.\par \par \uc2 Most observers expect them to fiercely resist such summons. Some have claimed \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/17/jan-6-probe-request-trump-512430"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive privilege}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D may shield Republicans from discussing communications with Trump in January. Schiff, the chair of the House intelligence committee, said such claims were \u8220\'20\'1Cbogus\u8221\'20\'1D and said the Biden justice department is unlikely to approve them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere we do meet resistance, we intend to push back hard and fast,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said, without naming any prospective witnesses. Whether simple Republican refusal to play ball can be overcome without lengthy court battles remains of course to be seen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Sidney Blumenthal\u8217\'20\'19s take on whether Jordan can be compelled to appear before the committee \u8211\'20\'13 informed by events in Virginia and in Congress in the years immediately before the civil war:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/aug/02/want-to-make-jim-jordan-sing-about-the-capitol-attack-ask-jefferson-davis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Want to make Jim Jordan sing about the Capitol attack? Ask Jefferson Davis | Sidney Blumenthal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Congressional Democrats are facing multiple crises as they attempt to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda. Intraparty divisions remain over both the bipartisan infrastructure bill and the $3.5tn reconciliation package, while lawmakers are trying to simultaneously suspend the debt ceiling and extend government funding past the end of the month. Republicans remain adamant that they will not assist in any effort to increase the debt ceiling, even though Democrats helped them do just that during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 * Biden addressed the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2  and outlined his approach to foreign policy. As the US president receives criticism for his handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal and weathers France\u8217\'20\'19s outrage over a nuclear submarine deal with Australia, Biden promised \u8220\'20\'1Ca new era of relentless diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CUS military power must be our tool of last resort, not our first,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expressed her support for a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough investigation\u8221\'20\'1D of the treatment of Haitian immigrants at the US-Mexican border. The vice-president said the footage of US border patrol agents confronting Haitian immigrants on horseback and potentially using whips on them was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should never be treated that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m deeply troubled about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris supports 'thorough investigation' into treatment of Haitian immigrants\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said she supports carrying out a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough investigation\u8221\'20\'1D into the treatment of Haitian immigrants at the US-Mexican border.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s comments come after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/us-begins-deportation-flights-haitians-texas-border-town"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 footage surfaced}}}\uc2  of US border patrol agents rounding up Haitian immigrants on horseback and potentially using whips to push them back as they attempted to enter the country.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  makes first comments on footage of Texas Border Patrol agents using horse lariats to handle Hatian migrants at the border. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/z4cjnKLuaZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/z4cjnKLuaZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Perry (@tperry518) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tperry518/status/1440349631657824261?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked about the footage by a reporter, Harris said the images were \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible,\u8221\'20\'1D and she intends to speak to homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas about the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHuman beings should never be treated that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m deeply troubled about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House has similar criticized the border agents\u8217\'20\'19 behavior, with press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  saying yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think anyone seeing that footage would think it was acceptable or appropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/us-begins-deportation-flights-haitians-texas-border-town"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House criticizes border agents who rounded up migrants on horseback}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine notes, Chuck Schumer \u8217\'20\'19s pledge that Democrats will go it alone on voting rights legislation marks a shift in tone for the Senate majority leader.\par \par \uc2 However, Democrats will still have to contend with the obstacles presented by the Senate filibuster, which seems unlikely to be changed anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 enltrSlight tweak here in Schumer's language around expected GOP blockage on voting rights. Schumer has been saying "all options are on the table" if voting rights bill is blocked - now he's saying Democrats will go at it alone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SKFyTabsyt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SKFyTabsyt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1440330364229091336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer pledges Democrats will 'move on our own' with voting rights, despite filibuster challenges\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  warned that Democrats will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove on our own\u8221\'20\'1D if Republicans continue to block voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer on voting rights: "If Republicans are unwilling to move forward, Democrats will have to move on our own."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1440329596772098063?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the Senate floor moments ago, Schumer pledged that the upper chamber would vote on the Freedom to Vote Act, the compromise voting rights bill unveiled by Democrats last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is my intention to hold a vote for the Freedom to Vote Act here on the Senate floor,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans are unwilling to move forward, Democrats will have to move on our own.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of course, advancing the legislation would almost certainly require altering the Senate filibuster, and a handful of key Democrats, including Joe Manchin, remain opposed to that proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his speech at the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2  meeting, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized the US priority in defending allies and the country\u8217\'20\'19s interests, including in terrorist attacks, but said that while the country is prepared to use force if necessary, the \u8220\'20\'1CUS military power must be our tool of last resort, not our first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt should not be used as an answer to every problem we see around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cbombs and bullets cannot defend against Covid-19 or its future variants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo fight this pandemic, we need a collective act of science and political will. We need to act now to get shots in arms as fast as possible and expand access to oxygen treatments to save lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2021/sep/21/un-general-assembly-joe-biden-jair-bolsonaro-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN: Joe Biden urges leaders to confront \u8216\'20\'18decisive decade for our world\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Haitian migrants at the Mexico-US border in Texas face a ramped-up US exclusion effort, with six expulsion flights to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/haiti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haiti}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. Mexico has begun bussing some away.\par \par \uc2 More than 6,000 had been removed from an encampment at Del Rio, Texas, US officials said on Monday as they defended a strong response that included immediately expelling migrants to their impoverished Caribbean country and faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/us-begins-deportation-flights-haitians-texas-border-town"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticism for using horse patrols}}}\uc2  to stop them entering the town.\par \par \uc2 Some Haitian migrants returned to Mexico, while others struggled to decide where to take their chances.\par \par \uc2 Marie Pierre, 43, stood on the Mexican side of the Rio Grande as night fell, with hundreds of others, unsure what to do.\par \par \uc2 She said border patrol agents separated her from her 19-year-old son in Texas and she didn\u8217\'20\'19t know if he had been deported. She waited for a chance to charge her phone, hoping to get news from family in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/haitian-migrants-texas-del-rio-bridge-expelled-us-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and Mexico expel thousands of Haitians at Del Rio bridge in Texas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, back on Capitol Hill, House Democratic leaders are still expressing optimism about the likelihood of their government spending bill passing the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is our hope that Senate Republicans will also do the right thing and stop playing politics around the debt limit,\u8221\'20\'1D House Democratic caucus chair \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 Jeffries said that \u8220\'20\'1Cat least a handful of Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D have indicated they are open to supporting the proposal, but it will take at least 10 Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D votes to get the bill through the Senate.\par \par \uc2 And Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  remains adamant that he will not support any effort to raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: US is 'opening a new era of relentless diplomacy'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking at the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2 , his first speech as US president.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted the 4.5m people who have died from Covid-19, saying, \u8220\'20\'1COur shared grief is a poignant reminder that our collective future will hinge on our ability to recognize our common humanity, to act together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the clear and urgent choice that we face here at the dawning of what must be a decisive decade for our world. A decade that will quite literally, determine our futures as a global community,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my view, how we answer these questions in this moment, whether we choose to fight for our shared future or not. all reverberate for generations yet to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden briefly addressed the US removal of troops in Afghanistan, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of continuing to fight the wars of the past, we are fixing our eyes and devoting our resources to the challenges that hold the keys to our collective future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re opening a new era of relentless diplomacy of using the power of our development aid to invest in new ways of listing people up around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that the US is turning its focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cregions of the world\u8221\'20\'1D that are most \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequential\u8221\'20\'1D, including the Indo-Pacific region.\par \par \uc2 Read more updates from the \uc2 UN\uc2  in \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s separate live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2021/sep/21/un-general-assembly-joe-biden-jair-bolsonaro-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres tells UN \u8216\'20\'18the world must wake up\u8217\'20\'19 over climate change \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to Politico, House minority whip Steve Scalise said this morning that Republican leadership will be encouraging members to vote against Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 government spending bill.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Whip announced this AM in the GOP conference meeting that they will be whipping against CR/debt limit, sources tell me.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1440315374768066565?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 If all House Republicans oppose the bill, then nearly every Democrat in the chamber will need to support it in order to get it passed.\par \par \uc2 And those hurdles will come before the bill heads over to the evenly divided Senate, where it currently has no path to the 60 votes needed for passage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Rose DeLauro, the Democratic chairwoman of the House appropriations committee, said the spending bill \u8220\'20\'1Cmeets the continuing needs of people who live paycheck to paycheck\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is critical that Congress swiftly pass this legislation to support critical education, health, housing and public safety programs and provide emergency help for disaster survivors and Afghan evacuees,\u8221\'20\'1D DeLauro said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Noting that the bill includes funds for relocating Afghan refugees and responding to natural disasters, DeLauro added, \u8220\'20\'1CBy extending funding through December 3, this legislation will allow Congress to negotiate full-year government funding bills that make historic and transformative investments to benefit working families. As we take that step today, providing help for people in desperate need is a moral imperative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats release text of government spending bill\par \par \uc2 The House appropriations committee has released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://appropriations.house.gov/sites/democrats.appropriations.house.gov/files/documents/Extending%20Government%20Funding%20and%20Delivering%20Emergency%20Assistance%20Act.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the text}}}\uc2  of a bill to keep the government funded past the end of the month and raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 If enacted, the bill would continue government funding through December 3 and suspend the debt ceiling until December 16.\par \par \uc2 The legislation would also invest $28.6bn in natural disaster response and $6.3bn in efforts to relocate Afghan refugees.\par \par \uc2 However, Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has vowed to oppose any effort to raise the debt ceiling, so it remains unclear how this bill could make it through the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details coming up. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are trying to put pressure on Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  over his insistence that Republicans will not help raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderMcConnell}}}\uc2  said: \u8216\'20\'18America can\u8217\'20\'19t default. That would be a disaster.\u8217\'20\'19 Yet, now he and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateGOP}}}\uc2  are trying to force the first-ever default of the U.S.,\u8221\'20\'1D House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll Members must come together in a spirit of bipartisanship to protect the full faith and credit of the U.S.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTwo years ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderMcConnell}}}\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica can't default. That would be a disaster." Yet, now he and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateGOP}}}\uc2  are trying to force the first-ever default of the U.S. All Members must come together in a spirit of bipartisanship to protect the full faith and credit of the U.S.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1440277146006523909?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But McConnell has somewhat of a notorious history for not giving in to pressure campaigns, with his handling of supreme court openings likely being the most famous example of that.\par \par \uc2 And so far, McConnell has given no indication of softening his position on the debt ceiling, even though Democrats helped Republicans raise the debt ceiling while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The intraparty arguments over Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn reconciliation package have raised concerns that the bill, which is considered the lynchpin of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, could fail.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/21/democrats-biden-domestic-agenda-implode-513218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Moderate Senate Democrats Joe Manchin (W.Va.) and Kyrsten Sinema (Ariz.) continue to be a major headache for party leadership\u8217\'20\'19s $3.5 trillion target. The Senate parliamentarian just nixed the party\u8217\'20\'19s yearslong push to enact broad immigration reform. House members may tank the prescription drugs overhaul the party has run on for years. And a fight continues to brew over Sen. Bernie Sanders \u8217\'20\'19 (I-Vt.) push to expand Medicare.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If any member of Congress is not concerned that this could fall apart, they need treatment,\u8217\'20\'19 said \uc2 Rep. Emanuel Cleaver\uc2  (D-Mo.), who warned his party \u8216\'20\'18will pay for it at the polls\u8217\'20\'19 if it fails in enacting Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda. \u8216\'20\'18Our caucus has the feeling of freedom to support or oppose leadership.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats wrestle with multiple challenges as government shutdown looms\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Democrats are trying to put out fires on multiple fronts as they seek to simultaneously advance their economic agenda and avoid a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders are scrambling to get both the bipartisan infrastructure bill and the $3.5tn reconciliation package to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  talks with reporters after a pair of votes at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  yesterday. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 However, progressive lawmakers have threatened to torpedo the infrastructure bill unless they receive guarantees that the reconciliation package will also pass, while moderate Democrats are demanding that the reconciliation package be scaled down.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democratic leaders are also trying to avoid a government shutdown and raise the debt ceiling, essentially daring Republicans to help them do so.\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has insisted that Republicans will not help Democrats with increasing the debt ceiling, even though the two parties acted together to raise the debt ceiling during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/us/politics/debt-ceiling-democrats-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are pairing}}}\uc2  a government spending proposal and a debt ceiling suspension in one bill, meaning the US could face a government shutdown and an economic catastrophe if Republicans follow through on McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s threat.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations over all of those proposals will continue today on Capitol Hill. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210921eh9l001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
