\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House denies \uc2 UN\uc2  chief\u8217\'20\'19s claim of \u8216\'20\'18dysfunctional\u8217\'20\'19 US-China relationship \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now) and Lauren Gambino and Martin Pengelly (earlier) \par \uc2 6,343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2021\par 00:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Our relationship with China is one not of conflict but of competition\u8217\'20\'19US to lift travel ban for vaccinated travelers from UK and most of EUJoe Biden: fate of spending plan with show extent of powerSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today, thanks for following along. Some key links and developments from the day:\par \par \uc2 * The White House responded critically to widely shared images of US border patrol agents in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/us-begins-deportation-flights-haitians-texas-border-town"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rounding up Haitian migrants on horseback}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The US will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/us-travel-ban-lifted-uk-eu-flights-allowed-vaccinated-latest-covid-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lift Covid-19 travel restrictions}}}\uc2  to allow fully vaccinated passengers from the UK and most \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) countries to travel into the country from early November.\par \par \uc2 * Biden will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/biden-un-speech-multilateral-diplomacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make his first speech to the United Nations as president}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, seeking to \u8220\'20\'1Cclose the chapter on 20 years of war\u8221\'20\'1D and begin an era of intensive diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration wants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/biden-administration-us-refugee-cap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly double the number of refugees admitted to the United States}}}\uc2  to 125,000 in the fiscal year starting on 1 October in keeping with a campaign promise, according to a statement from the state department.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and BioNTech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pfizer.com/news/press-release/press-release-detail/pfizer-and-biontech-announce-positive-topline-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Monday children aged five to 11 are on track to receive the two companies\u8217\'20\'19 Covid-19 vaccination by Halloween.\par \par \uc2 * Global financial markets have fallen sharply amid concern over rising inflation and the threat of financial contagion in China\u8217\'20\'19s property sector from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/20/shares-in-chinas-evergrande-plunge-again-as-fears-of-contagion-grow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the debt-stricken developer Evergrande,}}}\uc2  despite a boost from the relaxation of US travel rules.\par \par \uc2 * Alabama is shrinking under the onslaught of Covid-19, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alabamanews.net/2021/09/17/harris-alabama-recorded-more-deaths-than-births-in-2020/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its chief medical officer said}}}\uc2 , as deaths in the state outnumber births for the very first time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Texas doctor who publicly said he had provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the limit set by the state\u8217\'20\'19s new law is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/courts_law/texas-abortion-doctor-sued/2021/09/20/f5ab5c56-1a1c-11ec-bcb8-0cb135811007_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now facing a lawsuit}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post reports that Alan Braid, a physician in San Antonio who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote a column}}}\uc2  saying he had defied Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, is being sued by an Arkansas man who said he wanted to test the constitutionality of the Texas measure. The man bringing the lawsuit is Oscar Stilley, a former lawyer who was convicted of tax fraud in 2012, the Post reported. He is currently on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-doctor-who-performed-abortion-is-sued-in-test-of-new-law-11632176035?st=nsyita2ml2ru6v9&reflink=desktopwebshare_twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 home confinement}}}\uc2  for his previous conviction, the Wall Street Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 In his original column, Braid wrote:\par \par \uc2 I am taking a personal risk. But it\u8217\'20\'19s something I believe in strongly. I have daughters, granddaughters and nieces. I believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an essential part of healthcare. I have spent the last 50 years treating and helping patients. I can\u8217\'20\'19t just sit back and watch us return to 1972.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Braid also wrote about what it was like to work in Texas before Roe v Wade, saying, he had begun his residency in obstetrics and gynecology at a hospital in San Antonio in 1972: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the time, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effectively illegal in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 unless a psychologist certified a woman was suicidal. If the woman had money, we\u8217\'20\'19d refer her to clinics in Colorado, California or New York. The rest were on their own. Some traveled across the border to Mexico.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Texas law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks when most women are not yet aware they are pregnant. The Biden administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/biden-administration-sue-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued over the law}}}\uc2 . The law allows private citizens to file civil complaints against medical providers and others.\par \par \uc2 Our original story on Braid:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/19/texas-doctor-abortion-law-washington-post-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas doctor protests \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law by admitting he carried out procedure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another poll out today shows a majority of US residents support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, with 55% of respondents saying they would oppose the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 enltrA new Yahoo News/YouGov poll reveals that Americans\u8217\'20\'19 views about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain highly complex, although the Roe v. Wade ruling remains popular, while a recent Texas law banning most abortions is not. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oE5liZBXcw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/oE5liZBXcw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yahoo News (@YahooNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YahooNews/status/1440053875034054667?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Yahoo News/YouGov poll of 1,600 adults found that 76% of Democrats support Roe v Wade, and 51% of Republicans support getting rid of it.\par \par \uc2 A Monmouth university {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/20/government-shutdown-democrats-spending-plans-joe-biden-coronavirus-latest-news-us-politics?page=with:block-6148a9848f08001fa2d1fb0a#block-6148a9848f08001fa2d1fb0a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll from earlier}}}\uc2  said that 54% of Americans disagree with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to go into effect.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to raise refugee cap in October\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration plans to raise the cap on refugees admitted to the US to 125,000 in the upcoming fiscal year starting in October, the state department said in a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/biden-seeks-increase-number-refugees-admitted-us-state-department-says-2021-09-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Reuters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement is in line with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign promises to reverse the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 The state department said it would consult with the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  and Congress to raise the cap, which was set at 62,500 for the 2020 fiscal year, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of Afghan refugees are currently waiting at US military bases seeking resettlement in America. Biden has faced intense pressure from immigrants\u8217\'20\'19 rights groups to allow more refugees into the US.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Richard Durbin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/refugees-biden-administration-trump/2021/09/20/55d4e448-1a50-11ec-8380-5fbadbc43ef8_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement to the Washington Post}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I applaud the Biden administration for setting a target of 125,000 refugee admissions in the next fiscal year \u8212\'20\'14 a target my colleagues and I have been advocating for since April. And while I\u8217\'20\'19m disappointed in the projected number of refugees to be admitted this fiscal year, I acknowledge the challenges the Biden administration inherited with the US Refugee Admissions Program due to the anti-immigrant actions of the previous Administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/biden-administration-us-refugee-cap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration seeks to lift US refugee cap to 125,000 beginning 1 October}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hi all \u8211\'20\'13 Sam Levin in Los Angeles taking over our live coverage for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 Covid has now killed roughly as many US residents as the 1918-19 Spanish flu did \u8211\'20\'13 approximately 675,000 people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/science-health-pandemics-united-states-coronavirus-pandemic-c15d5c6dd7ece88d0832993f11279fbb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More from the AP}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The US population a century ago was just one-third of what it is today, meaning the flu cut a much bigger, more lethal swath through the country. But the COVID-19 crisis is by any measure a colossal tragedy in its own right, especially given the incredible advances in scientific knowledge since then and the failure to take maximum advantage of the vaccines available this time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBig pockets of American society \u8212\'20\'14 and, worse, their leaders \u8212\'20\'14 have thrown this away,\u8221\'20\'1D medical historian Dr Howard Markel of the University of Michigan said of the opportunity to vaccinate everyone eligible by now.\par \par \uc2 Like the Spanish flu, the coronavirus may never entirely disappear from our midst. Instead, scientists hope it becomes a mild seasonal bug as human immunity strengthens through vaccination and repeated infection. That could take time.\par \par \uc2 enltrCOVID-19 has now killed about as many Americans as the 1918-19 Spanish flu pandemic did \u8212\'20\'14 approximately 675,000. The 1918-19 influenza numbers are rough guesses. The population of the U.S. at the time was about one-third the size of what it is today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/07AY1140fQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/07AY1140fQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1439990628960591876?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden departs for New York to attend the \uc2 U.N. General Assembly\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Fn0BdGP2dx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Fn0BdGP2dx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ken Thomas (@KThomasDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KThomasDC/status/1440042577214902279?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will make his first speech to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/unitednations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Nations}}}\uc2  as president on Tuesday, seeking to \u8220\'20\'1Cclose the chapter on 20 years of war\u8221\'20\'1D and begin an era of intensive diplomacy, our worlds affairs editor Julian Borger writes.\par \par \uc2 But when he arrives in New York, he will have to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontend with hostility from China, an open rift with France and widespread scepticism among \uc2 UN\uc2  member states over his commitment to multilateralism following disagreements over Israel, a chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/16/stab-in-the-back-french-fury-australia-scraps-submarine-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a nuclear submarine deal that took adversaries and allies by surprise}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read Julian\u8217\'20\'19s preview of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/biden-un-speech-multilateral-diplomacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s UN speech is an opportunity to show \u8216\'20\'18America is back\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 * The US relaxed travel restrictions for fully vaccinated travelers from the UK, \uc2 EU\uc2 , China and several other countries. The announcement comes 18 months after the Trump administration imposed the restrictions to stem the spread of the coronavirus, and as the US faced mounting pressure from foreign leaders to lift the ban.\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court announced that it would hear oral arguments in a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that poses a direct challenge to Roe v Wade. A new national poll found that most Americans do not support overturning the landmark decision.\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  confirmed that Biden is attempting to speak to French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  after a diplomatic spat over the administration\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that the US was forming a new defense alliance with Australia and the UK.\par \par \uc2 * Biden announced new rules to protect federal workers from extreme heat, the biggest weather-related killer in the US.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  announced that they will try to pass a bill to prevent both a government shutdown and a debt-default, as Republicans dig in.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  have announced that legislation to avert a government shutdown will be paired with a measure to avoid a debt default.\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has vowed that Republicans will not cooperate with Democrats to raise or suspend the debt ceiling. Democrats have argued that the vote should not be a partisan one, as they voted to raise the debt limit by trillions of dollars during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The legislation to avoid a government shutdown will also include a suspension of the debt limit through December 2022 to once again meet our obligations and protect the full faith and credit of the United States, \u8221\'20\'1D they said in a joint statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe a suspension of the debt limit through December 2022 would provide an amount of time commensurate with the debt incurred as a result of passing last winter\u8217\'20\'19s bipartisan $908bn emergency Covid relief legislation, which was authored by Republican senators Cassidy, Romney, Portman, Collins and others, and ultimately voted for by more than 40 Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 including Senator McConnell \u8211\'20\'13 and signed into law by the previous president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The government is set to run out of money at the end of the month. Separately, Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said that the US would likely default on its debt sometime in October if action is not taken. Failure to raise the debt limit would \u8220\'20\'1Chave absolutely catastrophic economic consequences\u8221\'20\'1D, Yellen has warned.\par \par \uc2 The bill will also include emergency funding requested by the administration to aid states battered by the recent natural disasters as well as funding to help resettle Afghan refugees.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin told CNN reporter Manu Raju that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to delay a vote on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $3.5tn reconciliation package until 2022, as Axios reported yesterday. But he does support a \u8220\'20\'1Cwait and see\u8221\'20\'1D approach, he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin says Dems will need a lot of "clarity" to get reconciliation bill together by next week --- and calls for a pause. "Let's wait and see whatever we need... The main thing is inflation."\par \par \uc2 But AOC says infra bill is going down on Sept. 27 if reconciliation hasn't passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZoDkCkcx7K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZoDkCkcx7K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1440034736064249865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what I said? I said let\u8217\'20\'19s wait and see whatever we need. We need to have a good idea. The main thing is inflation, if it\u8217\'20\'19s transitory or not, you have a better idea, you know, once we get into it a little bit longer, but right now inflation is still high,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin told CNN.\par \par \uc2 He added that his meeting with Biden last week was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery good\u8221\'20\'1D, but wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say if they were close to a deal. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re just still working through everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the same time, New York congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez told CNN that she would vote against the infrastructure package on 27 September unless the House and Senate passed the much larger reconciliation package, a position she said was shared by as many as 45 members of the progressive caucus. That bill will almost certainly not be ready by the 27 September deadline.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have a very small destructive group of members who want to hold the entire country\u8217\'20\'19s agenda hostage for an arbitrary date,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1440035567861829632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Raju. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is not, it\u8217\'20\'19s not representative of the agenda of the caucus \u8211\'20\'13 is not representative of the agenda of the president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden announces new plan to protect workers from extreme heat\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is putting forward the first federal workplace rules on extreme heat, following a searing summer that has highlighted the dangers of heat, the biggest weather-related killer in the US.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the White House said that \uc2 the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)\uc2 , part of the department of labor, will start a new rule-making process to assign a heat standard for American workers, as well as oversee the enforcement of the new requirement. This will likely take the form of increased breaks or complete work shutdowns when the heat reaches certain thresholds.\par \par \uc2 The White House also said it will look to bolster efforts to improve tree cover in cities and help support cooling centers for people living in places that have to deal with dangerously high temperatures.\par \par \uc2 Around 1,300 people die in the US from excess heat each year, according to the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 , with outdoor workers, such as people who work in construction, at particular risk from high temperatures. Dangerous conditions are becoming more frequent due to the human-caused climate crisis. This summer was marginally hotter than the record Dust Bowl summer of 1936, federal government scientists confirmed last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy administration will not leave Americans to face this threat alone,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, I am mobilizing an all-of-government effort to protect workers, children, seniors, and at-risk communities from extreme heat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki was pressed repeatedly on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy toward Haitian migrants fleeing political instability, natural disaster and poverty.\par \par \uc2 Biden campaigned on a more humanitarian approach to immigration, but his muscular response to stem the crisis at the border has drawn sharp criticism from members of his own party. Psaki stressed that the deportation of Haitian immigrants are consistent with their enforcement policy.\par \par \uc2 She said the message from the administration continues to be \u8220\'20\'1Cnow is not the time to come\u8221\'20\'1D to the US.\par \par \uc2 She called the shocking photos and videos depicting mounted border patrol agents using whips and insulting migrants \u8220\'20\'1Chorrific\u8221\'20\'1D though the \u8220\'20\'1Cfull context\u8221\'20\'1D is missing.\par \par \uc2 enltrWH Press Secretary calls images of what looks like border patrol on horseback rounding up Haitian migrants with whips "horrific" & says this should never happen again.\par \par \uc2 She adds that she needs the "full context" but doesn't think anyone seeing this would see it as "acceptable." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GtaJttBz78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GtaJttBz78}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yamiche Alcindor (@Yamiche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1440011902504013824?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked about the parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that Democrats cannot include provision offering a pathway to citizenship for millions of immigrants, Psaki said Biden remained \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely committed\u8221\'20\'1D to enacting immigration reform. She said the administration would work with Congress on new proposals to ensure this gets done.\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if there is now a recognition that some of the priorities that Biden campaigned on are just not going to happen, Psaki replies: "No."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1440007275498942464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki called the drone strike that mistakenly killed Afghan citizens, including children, a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrific tragedy\u8221\'20\'1D and said Biden supports an swift investigation.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki on drone strike that killed innocent Afghans: "The loss of any civilian life is a tragedy... This was done in error and clearly the investigation that will continue is something the president strongly supports."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1440004632147894276?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a tragedy and every loss is a tragedy and he supports the efforts to move this forward as quickly as possible and to have a thorough investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, summarizing the president\u8217\'20\'19s response to the failure.\par \par \uc2 Officials said an internal review revealed that no Islamic State members were killed as a result of the attack, only civilians.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki previewed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s address at the \uc2 UN\uc2  tomorrow, as the White House defends the president\u8217\'20\'19s credibility as a global leader following the administration\u8217\'20\'19s frantic withdrawal from Afghanistan and a dust up between the US and France, one of America\u8217\'20\'19s oldest allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is going to lay out the case for why the next will determine our future, not just for the United States but for our global community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA central thrust of his remarks will be about \u8220\'20\'1Cimportance of reestablishing our alliances after the last several years,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CRe-establishing alliances doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that you won\u8217\'20\'19t have disagreements.... That is not the bar for having an alliance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19ll also make clear that many of the most pernicious threats facing the global community such as pandemics, climate change, rising authoritarianism, and economic inequality \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot be solved or even addressed through the force of arms\u8221\'20\'1D and must be addressed through collective global action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe will also reaffirm that the United States is not turning inward,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, arguing that the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to withdraw from Afghanistan was not a sign of the US ceding its leadership on the global stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki confirmed that Biden will speak to the French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , in the coming days to \u8220\'20\'1Creaffirm our commitment to working with one of our oldest and closest partners on a range of challenges that the global community is facing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 France recalled its ambassador from the US and Australia last week after Canberra\u8217\'20\'19s surprise decision to cancel an order for French-built submarines and its security pact with Washington and London.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki: The president will speak to President Macron of France in the coming days and I expect he will "reaffirm our commitment to working with one of our oldest and closest partners on the challenges that the global community is facing".\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1440002140345356289?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Responding to a question about the deal, she said the US would not back out of the defense agreement with the UK and Australia.\par \par \uc2 After an \uc2 FDA\uc2  panel endorsed booster shots for Americans 65 and older, Psaki said that Biden will get a third shot and the jab will be on camera, but no date has been set yet. The president, who is vaccinated, is regularly tested for Covid-19 and his most recent test was negative, the press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  pushed back on comments by the UN Secretary-General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2 , who described the US-China relationship as \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely dysfunctional\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur relationship with China is one not of conflict but of competition,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Guterres made the comments during an interview with The Associated Press ahead of the annual \uc2 United Nations\uc2  gathering of world leaders.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 UN\uc2 , Biden will make clear \u8220\'20\'1Cthat he is not looking to pursue a future, a new cold war with any country in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly supports\u8221\'20\'1D a House bill that would protect women\u8217\'20\'19s access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the administration said a Texas law effectively banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 6 weeks \u8220\'20\'1Cblatantly violates existing Supreme Court precedent established under Roe v. Wade nearly half a century ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In light of the law, which the Supreme Court allowed to go into effect, the House is expected to advance legislation designed to stop states from enacting anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures like the one in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The bill is expected to pass the Democratic-controlled House but it faces an uphill battle in the evenly split Senate, where most legislation requires 60 votes. Most Republicans oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and support calls to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the wake of Texas\u8217\'20\'19 unprecedented attack, it has never been more important to codify this constitutional right and to strengthen health care access for all women, regardless of where they live,\u8221\'20\'1D the administration said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to hear Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law case\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to hear oral arguments in a case challenging a Mississippi law that bans most abortions in the state after 15 weeks of pregnancy. The lawsuit is a direct challenge to Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The case will be argued on 1 December.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: The Supreme Court just released its December argument calendar. Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, the term's big \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, will be argued Dec. 1. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zRXC7azbHF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zRXC7azbHF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D4wG3yYSfK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D4wG3yYSfK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1439985310226685956?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, lawyers for Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, the only licensed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility in Mississippi, asked the court to reject the state\u8217\'20\'19s request to \u8220\'20\'1Cjettison a half-century of settled precedent\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that if the law were upheld, the \u8220\'20\'1Cfallout would be swift and certain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The law, known as the Gestational Age Act, passed in 2018 allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks on in cases involving \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergencies or for severe fetal abnormality\u8221\'20\'1D. It contains no exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Under the law, doctors could have their medical licenses suspended or revoked if they perform abortions that do not comply with the law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Will he or won\u8217\'20\'19t he?\par \par \uc2 After an unsuccessful run for Senate and then president of the United States, former Texas congressman \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  may be making a run for governor, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/scoop-beto-plans-texas-comeback-governors-race-33a3ae1a-4c58-4e7a-9e44-26342d3128c9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  in Axios.\par \par \uc2 Though a run is widely expected, \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  has not confirmed his intentions publicly. Nevertheless, the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  is raising speculation further by fundraising off the anonymously-sourced report that he will challenge the Republican governor Greg Abbott next year.\par \par \uc2 enltrHe\u8217\'20\'19s been publicly mum about his plans, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DemGovs?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DemGovs}}}\uc2  are already fundraising off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/axios?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @axios}}}\uc2  reporting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BetoORourke?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BetoORourke}}}\uc2  plans to run for Texas governor. \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  has been getting an earful from TX Dems who want him to take on Abbott. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/q76cPsnP6J"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/q76cPsnP6J}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Garrett Haake\uc2  (@GarrettHaake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GarrettHaake/status/1439975057812598795?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo decision has been made,\u8221\'20\'1D David Wysong, \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former House chief of staff and a longtime adviser told Axios. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has been making and receiving calls with people from all over the state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since his presidential run, \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  has become a prominent voting rights advocate and one of the leading opponents to a sweeping new Texas law that dramatically restricts ballot access. The state also recently passed one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, which could help galvanize Democrats and independents in the state.\par \par \uc2 But the growing humanitarian crisis at the US-Mexico border has motivated conservatives in a state where Republicans still dominate even as changing demographics pave the way for a political shift.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Most Americans do not want the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade, a \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  poll found.\par \par \uc2 The survey also found that a majority of Americans disagree with the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow a Texas law severely restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to go into effect, though there are clear ideological divisions.\par \par \uc2 enltrNATIONAL POLL: 54% of Americans disagree with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  decision to allow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Texas?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Texas}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/abortion?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  law to go into effect, while just 39% agree.\par \par \uc2 Most Democrats (73%) DISAGREE with the decision while most Republicans (62%) AGREE. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Whz60ozSmd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Whz60ozSmd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1439967731395317768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Top line figures from the poll include:\par \par \uc2 * 62% of Americans say the supreme court should leave the 1973 Roe v Wade decision in place, while 31% want to see it revisited.\par \par \uc2 * 54% of Americans disagree with the supreme court decision allowing the Texas law to go into effect while 39% agree.\par \par \uc2 * 70% of Americans disapprove of a provision of the Texas law allowing private citizens to use lawsuits to enforce the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  mandate.\par \par \uc2 * 81% of Americans disapprove of a provision that would award $10,000 to private citizens who successfully file lawsuits against those who perform or assist a woman with getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American public is largely pro-choice, although many would accept some limitations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patrick Murray, director of the independent Monmouth University Polling Institute. \u8220\'20\'1CThis Texas law goes way too far for most people. The \u8216\'20\'18bounty\u8217\'20\'19 aspect in particular seems objectionable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  plays hardball Photograph: Michael Brochstein/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 So much focus and attention is directed at Joe Manchin, the mercurial Senate Democrat who seems to hold the fate of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s entire domestic agenda in his hands. But there\u8217\'20\'19s another key player in this legislative drama: the Arizona senator, Kyrsten Sinema.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2021/09/20/scoop-sinema-issues-ultimatum-to-biden-494397"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , Sinema drove a hard bargain during her meeting with Biden last week, telling the president that she would not support his massive social policy bill if the House delays \u8211\'20\'13 or tanks \u8211\'20\'13 a vote on the infrastructure bill, scheduled for 27 September. Sinema, a first-term Senator who considers the late \uc2 John McCain\uc2  a political influence, played a central role in writing and building partisan support for the infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 Her position is shared by at least one moderate Democrat in the House, Oregon congressman \uc2 Kurt Schrader\uc2 , who told Politico: \u8220\'20\'1CIf they delay the vote \u8211\'20\'13 or it goes down \u8211\'20\'13 then I think you can kiss reconciliation goodbye. Reconciliation would be dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is all part of the very complex legislative dance happening publicly and privately on Capitol Hill this week as Democrats try to steer Biden\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling, two-part economic agenda through both chambers of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Bracketing the terms of debate is an agreement House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  struck with moderates. In exchange for their support advancing a budget blueprint for the reconciliation bill, she promised a vote on the Senate-passed, bipartisan infrastructure bill on 27 September. But progressives say they have the votes to block that bill unless its paired with the larger spending bill. That bill, which is being negotiated with Senate Democrats as part of the special reconciliation process, almost certainly won\u8217\'20\'19t be ready by next week.\par \par \uc2 So what happens? Does Pelosi delay the 27 September vote, as Majority Whip Jim Clyburn suggested is possible, and hope moderates blink? Does she bring the bill to the floor and hope that enough progressives take the \u8220\'20\'1Csomething is better than nothing\u8221\'20\'1D approach and vote for it?\par \par \uc2 All of this is happening as Congress faces a host of other legislative and fiscal deadlines that, if not met, could lead to a government shutdown and/or a debt default.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 A state department official denied that the change in policy was an attempt to mollify Europe following the falling out between the US and France over the Australian submarine deal, which Washington negotiated without Paris\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge, according to a fresh report from our world affairs editor, Julian Borger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C This is really driven by the science of COVID and as more people are being vaccinated around the world, we of course want people to be able to travel more freely,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erica Barks-Ruggles, a senior official in the bureau of international organization affairs. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re really always being driven by the science, and we continue to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barks-Ruggles made the remark during a briefing call with reporters on the coming week\u8217\'20\'19s diplomacy at \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The news that the US was lifting travel restrictions for foreign travelers reportedly took British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  by surprise.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Double jabbed Brits given green light to travel to US from November, White House confirms.\par \par \uc2 But announcement appears to have taken \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  by surprise. He told us on plane not to "hold your breath" US borders would be reopened any time soon. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5siM9O3yjp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5siM9O3yjp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pippa Crerar (@PippaCrerar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PippaCrerar/status/1439958689822216200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden is due to meet with Johnson at the White House tomorrow, after the president\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2 . As part of their meeting, he was expected to push Biden to lift the travel ban, first implemented 18 months ago by the Trump administration to limit the spread of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 But on the plane yesterday, Johnson tempered expectations, telling reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got to warn you, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think this is going to be necessarily fixed this week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Responding on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Johnson said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdelighted\u8221\'20\'1D by the announcement.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am delighted that from November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  is reinstating transatlantic travel so fully vaccinated UK nationals can visit the USA.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a fantastic boost for business and trade, and great that family and friends on both sides of the pond can be reunited once again.\par \par \uc2 ???????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qbVccvEdrm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qbVccvEdrm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  (@BorisJohnson)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BorisJohnson/status/1439970018477891585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 US to relax travel restrictions for fully vaccinated international passengers\par \par \uc2 The US will lift Covid-19 travel restrictions to allow fully vaccinated passengers from the UK, \uc2 EU\uc2 , China, Brazil and several other countries to enter the country from November, the Biden administration announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The decision from the White House will mark the end of a travel ban imposed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  more than 18 months ago in the early stages of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Under the current policy, only US citizens, members of their immediate families, green card holders and those with national interest exemptions (NIE) can travel into the US if they have been in the UK or \uc2 EU\uc2  in the previous two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The change of direction comes at the start of the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  in New York and marks the culmination of weeks of intense diplomacy between Washington, London and Brussels. It also comes days after France recalled its ambassador to the US and Australia in protest over the administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to provide nuclear-powered submarines to Australia.\par \par \uc2 The travel restrictions were increasingly a source of tension between the US and European leaders in particular, after the \uc2 EU\uc2  opened its doors to Americans months ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Lincoln Project has questioned if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/19/beto-orourke-greg-abbott-texas-governor-matthew-mcconaughey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas governor, Greg Abbott}}}\uc2 , used political influence to pull a TV ad criticising his handling of the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 According to a statement issued on Sunday, the group, formed by anti-Trump Republicans, was told the ad, Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s Wall, was being pulled just 10 minutes before it was due to air on \uc2 ESPN\uc2  during a nationally televised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.espn.com/college-football/game/_/gameId/401282202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 football game}}}\uc2  between the University of Texas and \uc2 Rice University\uc2  on Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/tK11VkicTzo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60-second slot}}}\uc2 , which the Lincoln Project said cost $25,000 and was approved by \uc2 ESPN\uc2  lawyers, blames the Republican governor for more than 60,000 Covid deaths in the state, against a backdrop of images of the US southern border wall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Governor Abbott wants to build a new wall, tell him to stop building this one,\u8221\'20\'1D the message says, showing a wall constructed from coffins.\par \par \uc2 Wood from caskets of all the Covid-19 victims in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  would stretch 85 miles, the ad claims. It remains watchable on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were told it was a \u8216\'20\'18university-made decision\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D to pull the ad, the Lincoln Project said in a press release. \u8220\'20\'1CDid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Abbott}}}\uc2  or his allies assert political influence to ensure the advertisement was not broadcast?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abbott and the University of Texas did not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/lincoln-project-ad-greg-abbott-texas-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lincoln Project says ad attacking Greg Abbott pulled from Texas football game}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that nearly 900 state legislators from 45 states have filed a brief with the supreme court, asking it to reject a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban enacted by Mississippi and thereby uphold Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling guaranteeing the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The issue is front and centre at the moment, after the court allowed to stand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/19/texas-doctor-abortion-law-washington-post-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas law}}}\uc2  which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks and allows private citizens to sue providers and those who help them.\par \par \uc2 The court is now dominated 6-3 by conservatives, and whatever justices from either side of the aisle ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-not-partisan-hacks-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-justices-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 ) ritualistically claim to the contrary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/15/amy-barrett-supreme-court-partisan-hacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that imbalance is shaping its view of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 . For progressives, not to the good.\par \par \uc2 Of the 897 state legislators who signed the brief, NBC reported, 895 were Democrats and two independents. The only states not to provide at least one signatory were Mississippi, North Dakota, Oklahoma, Arkansas and Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, on a remarkable and moving intervention in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate this weekend \u8211\'20\'13 from a doctor in Texas:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/19/texas-doctor-abortion-law-washington-post-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas doctor protests \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law by admitting he carried out procedure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 In news sure to be welcomed by parents across the US, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and BioNTech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pfizer.com/news/press-release/press-release-detail/pfizer-and-biontech-announce-positive-topline-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  this morning children aged five to 11 are on track to receive the two companies\u8217\'20\'19 Covid-19 vaccination by Halloween.\par \par \uc2 Albert Bourla\uc2 , chairman and chief executive officer of Pfizer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20210920005452/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hailed}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe first results from a pivotal trial of a Covid-19 vaccine in this age group\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If the regulatory process proceeds as it has for older age groups, authorisation for use would be expected by the end of October. Earlier this month, FDA chief, Dr Peter Marks, told the Associated Press that once \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  turned over results, his agency would evaluate the data \u8220\'20\'1C hopefully in a matter of weeks \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and BioNTech said European and British authorities would also be asked for emergency authorisation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/20/pfizer-covid-vaccine-children-5-to-11-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US children aged 5 to 11 on track to receive Pfizer vaccine by Halloween}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26and welcome to our coverage of the day in US politics.\par \par \uc2 It might not be a very good day for Democrats in Washington, from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the White House down to leaders, at least, in the House and the Senate. It will at least be a very busy one.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday night, the Senate parliamentarian delivered a blow to progressives in the party when she said they could not include a path to citizenship for undocumented migrants in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/19/joe-biden-economic-spending-plan-infrastructure-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the gargantuan spending bill they are hoping to pass via reconciliation}}}\uc2  , meaning by majority alone in the Senate. Majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  indicated he would have another think.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, efforts to keep the party together on that $3.5tn spending package, difficult at the best of times, seem to be fraying quite badly. Senior party figures have indicated a promised House vote on a bipartisan infrastructure deal meant to be paired with the spending bill might be delayed. That would anger progressives, while moderates continue to feel queasy about the bigger spending package.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona, two key moderates in a chamber split 50-50, have doubts about the spending bill and have reportedly voiced them, Manchin to constituents and Sinema to Biden, in the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 On top of all that, there are 10 days left to sort out government funding and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/19/government-shutdown-fears-debt-ceiling-talks-latest-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoid a shutdown}}}\uc2 , while in the Senate the Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , is refusing to play ball on raising the debt limit, which the US must soon do. That\u8217\'20\'19s rather unprecedented but McConnell is gonna McConnell \u8211\'20\'13 the author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2016/06/mitch-mconnell-book-223790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a memoir called The Long Game}}}\uc2  has his eye on the midterms in 2022, as well as beating back/appeasing the Trumpist wave in his own party and keeping hold of the reins.\par \par \uc2 In the midst of all this, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is due to fly to New York for the \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2 , with questions about the rise of China, the withdrawal from Afghanistan and of course much more buzzing around the big modern building on the banks of the rolling East River.\par \par \uc2 Expect a busy day. Here to set you up is Lauren Gambino\u8217\'20\'19s excellent primer on what all the machinations in Congress might mean for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legacy and the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hold on power:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/19/joe-biden-economic-spending-plan-infrastructure-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden knows fate of spending plan will show extent of his power \u8211\'20\'13 and define his legacy }}}\par \par \uc2 2021-09-20T13:10:33Z 2021-09-21T07:28:17Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/ec44003075fe30ab037b1632fb8fa336f5109b1c/0_0_4200_2520/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/ec44003075fe30ab037b1632fb8fa336f5109b1c/0_0_4200_2520/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to tell the \uc2 UN general assembly\uc2  that he is not looking to start a new cold war with any country in the world. Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  plays hardball\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210920eh9k001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
