\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US Covid-19 deaths now same as the 1918-19 flu pandemic\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2021\par 15:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 1,900 people are dying in the US daily on average. Plus, a mountain goat has killed a grizzly bear in CanadaDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing delivered to your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 has now killed as many Americans as the 1918-19 flu pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 more than 675,000.\par \par \uc2 The US population a century ago was just one-third of what it is today, meaning the flu cut a much bigger, more lethal swath through the country. But the Covid-19 crisis is by any measure a colossal tragedy in its own right, especially given the incredible advances in scientific knowledge since then and the failure to take maximum advantage of the vaccines availablee.\par \par \uc2 Like the 1918-19 flu, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/20/covid-19-death-toll-1918-flu-pandemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the coronavirus may never entirely disappear from our midst}}}\uc2 . Instead, scientists hope it will become a mild seasonal bug as human immunity strengthens through vaccination and repeated infection. That could take time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope it will be like getting a cold, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no guarantee,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rustom Antia, a biologist at \uc2 Emory University\uc2 , who suggests an optimistic scenario in which this could happen over a few years.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many people are dying of Covid-19 a day? While the Delta variant-fueled surge in infections may have peaked, US deaths are more than 1,900 a day on average.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will winter bring a new surge? Yes, the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s influential model is projecting an additional 100,000 or so Americans will die of Covid-19 by 1 January.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many people are vaccinated? Just under 64% of the US population have received as least one dose of the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 White House criticizes border agents who rounded up migrants on horseback\par \par \uc2 The White House on Monday responded critically to widely shared images of US border patrol agents in Texas rounding up Haitian migrants on horseback.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , was asked if the use of horses and possibly whips, potent imagery in a country founded on slavery, represented an \u8220\'20\'1Cappropriate tactic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI have seen some of the footage. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have the full context. I can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine what context would make that appropriate. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anyone seeing that footage would think it was acceptable or appropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 6,000 Haitians and other migrants have been removed from the encampment at the Texas border town of Del Rio, other US officials said Monday as they defended their strong response.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has the homeland security secretary,\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas\par \par \uc2 said? Calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cchallenging and heartbreaking situation\u8221\'20\'1D, he issued a stark warning: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you come to the United States illegally, you will be returned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What about the border control agents? Mayorkas and the border patrol chief, Raul Ortiz, said they would look into the agents\u8217\'20\'19 actions but both officials said they saw nothing apparently wrong based on the photos and video.\par \par \uc2 Canada election result: Trudeau wins third term after early vote gamble\par \par \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  has won a third term as Canada\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, with his Liberal party set to capture the most votes in the snap election, a result he called a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear mandate\u8221\'20\'1D to get the country through the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 With results still trickling in late Monday night, Trudeau was on track for another minority government, meaning he will once again need to work with other parties to pass legislation.\par \par \uc2 Elections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/canada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canada}}}\uc2 , which oversees the vote, had previously warned that some results would take days to be finalised as mail-in ballots are counted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have given this government and this parliament clear direction,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau said from Montreal early on Tuesday morning, while acknowledging the decision to hold an early election was deeply unpopular.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Preliminary results indicated his Liberals had won or were leading in 156 seats \u8211\'20\'13 short of the 170 needed for a parliamentary majority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Erin O\u8217\'20\'19Toole\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opposition Conservatives had 121. The result largely mirrored the outcome of the 2019 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The prime minister gambled by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/15/justin-trudeau-canada-snap-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling an election}}}\uc2  in August in the hopes that the government\u8217\'20\'19s pandemic response could boost his party\u8217\'20\'19s power in parliament.\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to hear arguments in Mississippi case that threatens Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  has set a date to hear arguments in a Mississippi case that could overturn Roe v Wade, the near-50-year-old ruling that guarantees a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization will be heard on 1 December. The case concerns a law that bans most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, a direct challenge to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 News of the court date arrived amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/19/texas-doctor-abortion-law-washington-post-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversy over a Texas law, known as SB8}}}\uc2 , which in effect bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks and empowers citizens to sue providers and anyone who helps a woman access their services.\par \par \uc2 A San Antonio doctor who said he had performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defiance of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s new law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/texas-abortion-law-san-antonio-doctor-sued"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been sued}}}\uc2 , setting up a potential test of the legality of the extreme, near-total ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What law does the Mississippi\par \par \uc2 case concern? The law, known as the Gestational Age Act, allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks in cases involving \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergencies or for severe fetal abnormality\u8221\'20\'1D. Like the Texas law, it contains no exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who is the doctor being sued in Texas? It is Dr Alan Braid, who became the first Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider to publicly reveal he violated the law when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wrote an opinion piece in the Washington Post}}}\uc2  over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Phil Valentine, a prominent Tennessee rightwing talk radio host, died of Covid-19 after mocking the vaccine. Meanwhile, media watchdogs suggest some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/21/anti-vax-radio-hosts-dying-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 basic level of responsibility to the public should be required}}}\uc2  to keep a broadcast license.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 10 women and girls are murdered every day in Mexico, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/sep/20/mexico-femicide-women-girls-amnesty-international-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/sep/20/mexico-femicide-women-girls-amnesty-international-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report by by Amnesty International}}}\par \par \uc2 . The scathing study documents the scale of the violence and the disturbing lack of interest on the part of Mexican authorities to prevent or solve the murders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nearly three tonnes of heroin with a street value of $2.7bn\par \par \uc2 from Afghanistan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/india-seizes-27bn-of-heroin-from-afghanistan-at-port"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been seized from a western Indian port}}}\uc2 , officials said. Two Indians were arrested with the heroin, which was kept in two containers marked as talc.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s restaurant industry is largely open for business again but is still struggling with labor shortages. Workers have attributed this to poor pay and working conditions and disrespect from customers \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/sep/21/restaurant-industry-worker-shortage-pay-increase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are demanding better treatment from employers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Biden administration seeks to lift US refugee cap to 125,000\par \par \uc2 from 1 October\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/20/biden-administration-us-refugee-cap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants to nearly double the number of refugees admitted to the US}}}\uc2  to 125,000 in the fiscal year starting on 1 October, in keeping with a campaign promise, according to the state department. The state department will consult with the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  and Congress to lift the cap, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/03/biden-refugee-cap-us-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set at 62,500 for the 2020 fiscal year}}}\uc2 , ending this month. Biden, a Democrat who took office in January, promised to reverse course after his predecessor, the Republican president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , cut the refugee cap to just 15,000, the lowest level in the history of the modern refugee program.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: mountain goat kills attacking grizzly bear with \u8216\'20\'18dagger-like\u8217\'20\'19 horns\par \par \uc2 With their long, sharp claws and frightening speed, few predators in Canada\u8217\'20\'19s wild hinterlands attack as mercilessly as a hungry grizzly bear. But in a rare turn of events, park officials say a mountain goat not only defended itself from becoming a meal, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/20/canada-mountain-goat-grizzly-bear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was able to kill the attacking bear with its \u8220\'20\'1Cdagger-like\u8221\'20\'1D horns}}}\uc2 . The remains of the bear, who weighed only 70kg (154lb), was discovered on 4 September by a hiker near Field, British Columbia. \uc2 Parks Canada\uc2  said the recent forensic necropsy of a female grizzly bear suggested a goat\u8217\'20\'19s horns pierced the bear\u8217\'20\'19s armpits and neck.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: A Black town\u8217\'20\'19s water is more poisoned than Flint\u8217\'20\'19s. In a white town nearby, it\u8217\'20\'19s clean\par \par \uc2 Tap water samples tested in 2018 revealed lead levels of 22 parts per billion \u8211\'20\'13 well over the federal lead action level of 15 parts per billion and higher, even, than the 20 parts per billion nearby Flint averaged at the height of the crisis that made that city a national symbol of environmental injustice. But for the last three years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/21/benton-harbor-michigan-lead-water-poisoned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 neither the city of Benton Harbor, the county, nor the state have taken sufficient action}}}\uc2 . The health risks posed to the residents of this mostly Black, poverty-stricken city \u8211\'20\'13 which also happens to be the corporate headquarters of \uc2 Whirlpool\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are extraordinary. Despite this, as one resident said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like they don\u8217\'20\'19t care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Want more environmental stories delivered to your inbox?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2015/oct/19/sign-up-to-the-green-light-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to our Green Light newsletter}}}\uc2  to get the good, bad and essential news on the climate every week\par \par \uc2 Last thing: \u8216\'20\'18We saw RuPaul in a loincloth and went, \u8220\'20\'1COh my God!\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 RuPaul\u8217\'20\'19s Drag Race, which pits drag queens against one another in a lipstick-smudged, wig-strewn, basque-busting contest with a $100,000 prize, has notched up 13 seasons, won 19 Emmys and attracted guests such as Lady Gaga and Ariana Grande. Countless spin-offs and international iterations include live DragCon events as well as Drag Race UK. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2021/sep/21/fenton-bailey-randy-barbato-producers-rupauls-drag-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We talk to Fenton Bailey and Randy Barbato}}}\uc2 , the duo who took took RuPaul from obscurity to global fame and created a show that combines reality TV, talent contest, sketch comedy, spoof and musical.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Th headline of this article was amended on 21 September 2021 to make clear, as the article text does, that it is the total deaths that are now the same, not the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath rate\u8221\'20\'1D as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210921eh9l0018o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
