\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Guam court clears the way for \u8216\'20\'18tele- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 in boost for reproductive rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Mar-Vic Cagurangan in Guam \par \uc2 830 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par 09:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The island removes requirement for face-to-face consultations, meaning women can be remotely prescribed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication\par \par \uc2 Sarah* found out she was five weeks pregnant earlier this year. For the mother of three, carrying on with the pregnancy was out of the question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy current partner and I are not ready to have a child at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D said the 30-year-old resident of Tamuning, on the western shore of Guam.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s long been separated from her estranged husband, but the divorce process that involves custody over their children remains unresolved in court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPersonally, I am not financially and emotionally ready to have another child,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Guam but it has long been a contentious issue in the predominately Catholic community. Terminating a pregnancy has been difficult and the only doctor who provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  service retired in 2018.\par \par \uc2 But a recent federal court ruling will make it easier for women on the island to obtain an early-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since 2018, Guamanian women seeking to end their pregnancies have mostly resorted to services off the island. Hawaii is the default destination.\par \par \uc2 The Catholic church, however, endorses another alternative, promoting a newly formed local adoption agency that offers to assist women who are burdened with unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdoption was not an option for me either,\u8221\'20\'1D Sarah said. \u8220\'20\'1CGuam is a small community. Everybody knows everybody. Rumours will swirl and people will judge you unkindly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So Sarah spent $3,000 on a two-day trip to Hawaii, which included the plane ticket, lodging, the physician\u8217\'20\'19s fee and the abortive pill prescribed to her at the Planned Parenthood clinic in Honolulu. The clinic offers medication abortions for women who are up to 11 weeks pregnant. Two tablets are prescribed, taken up to 48 hours apart, to terminate the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy the time I travelled to Hawaii, I was already at the stage of pregnancy that qualified for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI took the first pill before I left Hawaii and then took the second pill when I returned to Guam.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, a federal judge issued a ruling removes the need for women like Sarah to travel to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision paves the way for the practice of \u8220\'20\'1Ctele-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in Guam by striking down restrictions that bar offshore physicians from remotely prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and providing medical consultation and guidance through face-to-face videoconferencing.\par \par \uc2 The court ruled women no longer need \u8220\'20\'1Cin person communication\u8221\'20\'1D or individual consultations \u8220\'20\'1Cin a private room\u8221\'20\'1D to obtain a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe undisputed evidence before the court all points to the fact that a live, face-to- face video conferencing is comparable to, and may even have some benefits over, in-person communication,\u8221\'20\'1D the court said.\par \par \uc2 The decision stemmed from a lawsuit filed by Hawaii-based physicians Dr Shandhini Raidoo and Dr Bliss Kaneshiro, who sought to remotely supply \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to women in Guam.\par \par \uc2 While Guam-licensed, the two doctors could not provide the service due to the \u8220\'20\'1Cin-person communication\u8221\'20\'1D requirement of the law.\par \par \uc2 The court noted that Guam\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cin-person\u8221\'20\'1D requirement \u8220\'20\'1Ccreates an extra step in the medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  process\u8221\'20\'1D that reflects the government\u8217\'20\'19s interest in limiting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and imposing its moral stance on \u8220\'20\'1Cpromoting foetal life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lawyer Vanessa Williams, who has been involved in litigation pushing for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Guam, welcomed the federal court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor people in Guam, just like across the United States, having safe, legal access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  means that we can make our own decisions about our lives, our families, and our futures,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Jayne Flores, director of the Bureau of Women\u8217\'20\'19s Affairs, said: \u8220\'20\'1Cwe encourage support for a woman\u8217\'20\'19s choice in deciding what is best for her reproductive health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the move has been welcomed by some, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a contested issue in the US territory.\par \par \uc2 The practice was a criminal offence up until 1978, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was struck down by Roe v Wade. In 1990, however, the Guam Legislature reinstated the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The law did not survive a constitutional challenge.\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since been legal on Guam, the local legislature continued to add layers of requirements and restrictions, including counselling prior to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 From 2008 to 2017, approximately 200 to 300 abortions were performed each year in Guam.\par \par \uc2 While there may be no record of abortions being performed on the island since 2018, one local physician said it was wrong to conclude that women in Guam had no option other than to travel off the island.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are physicians on island who quietly prescribe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to women on Guam,\u8221\'20\'1D said the physician, who requested not to be named. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no records of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a reportable procedure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *Name has been changed to protect identity.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210920eh9k002s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
