\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Texas doctor protests  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law by admitting he carried out procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 626 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par 03:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alan Braid writes column for Washington Post describing the hardships and deaths he has witnessed among patientsTexas law shows fragility of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, say activists\par \par \uc2 Protesting against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas law}}}\uc2  that outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy and empowers citizens to sue providers and anyone who helps them, a San Antonio doctor said he had provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the new legal limit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am taking a personal risk,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alan Braid wrote for the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s something I believe in strongly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have daughters, granddaughters and nieces. I believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an essential part of healthcare. I have spent the last 50 years treating and helping patients. I can\u8217\'20\'19t just sit back and watch us return to 1972.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was the year before Roe v Wade, the supreme court ruling which guaranteed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The court is now dominated by conservatives, after Republicans installed three justices under Donald Trump. Using an emergency \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-law-cruel-partisan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shadow docket}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D ruling, the court allowed the Texas law to stand. Many observers expect it to fully overturn Roe in another case, from Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Saturday was the one-year anniversary of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/18/ruth-bader-ginsburg-supreme-court-justice-dies-aged-87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death}}}\uc2  of the liberal justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , a key moment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  battle. Ginsburg was succeeded by Amy Coney Barrett, a devout Catholic.\par \par \uc2 Marking the anniversary, Cecile Richards, a former head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/18/abortion-rights-campaigner-anniversary-rbg-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Associated Press}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in a post-Roe world \u8230\'20\'26 all it takes is a Republican governor and a Republican legislature. Your state could be exactly the same.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Braid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he had begun work in Texas in a pre-Roe world, starting a residency in obstetrics and gynecology at a hospital in San Antonio in July 1972.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the time, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effectively illegal in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 unless a psychologist certified a woman was suicidal. If the woman had money, we\u8217\'20\'19d refer her to clinics in Colorado, California or New York. The rest were on their own. Some traveled across the border to Mexico.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That year, he said, he saw \u8220\'20\'1Cthree teenagers die from illegal abortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne I will never forget. When she came into the ER, her vaginal cavity was packed with rags. She died a few days later from massive organ failure, caused by a septic infection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Texas law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/text/SB8/id/2395961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB8}}}\uc2 , went into effect this month. Braid said his clinics were represented by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  in a federal lawsuit seeking to stop the law.\par \par \uc2 Braid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  women who come to his clinic often say why they need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re finishing school or they already have three children, they\u8217\'20\'19re in an abusive relationship, or it\u8217\'20\'19s just not time. A majority are mothers. Most are between 18 and 30. Many are struggling financially.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An architect of the Texas bill, the former state solicitor general Jonathan Mitchell, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  women who want to avoid unwanted pregnancy can simply say no to sex.\par \par \uc2 Braid wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CSeveral times a month, a woman confides that she is having the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because she has been raped. Sometimes, she reports it to the police; more often, she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas\u8217\'20\'19s new law makes no exception for rape or incest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Describing how women must again be referred out of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/09/18/texas-abortion-provider-alan-braid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Braid wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, it\u8217\'20\'19s 1972 all over again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that is why, on the morning of 6 September, I provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a woman who, though still in her first trimester, was beyond the state\u8217\'20\'19s new limit. I acted because I had a duty of care to this patient, as I do for all patients, and because she has a fundamental right to receive this care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210919eh9j0012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
