\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Texas anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law shows \u8216\'20\'18terrifying\u8217\'20\'19 fragility of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, say activists\b0\par\par\uc2 Lizzy Davies \par \uc2 1,023 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2021\par 07:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 39\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Campaigners fear ban emboldens anti-choice governments as more aggressive opposition, better organised and funded, spreads from US\par \par \uc2 The new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in Texas is a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying\u8221\'20\'1D reminder of the fragility of hard-won rights, pro-choice activists have said, as they warn of a \u8220\'20\'1Cmore aggressive, much better organised [and] better funded\u8221\'20\'1D global opposition movement.\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice campaigners have seen several victories in recent years, including in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/irish-abortion-referendum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ireland}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Argentina}}}\uc2  and, most recently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/sep/09/mexico-ruling-decriminalise-abortion-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico}}}\uc2 , where the supreme court ruled last week that criminalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unconstitutional. Another is hoped for later this month when the tiny enclave of San Marino, landlocked within Italy, holds a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://timesofmalta.com/articles/view/abortion-debate-splits-san-marino-as-historic-vote-nears.900377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly charged referendum}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law}}}\uc2 , which bans abortions after about six weeks, once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, and does not make exceptions for incest or rape, has sent shock waves around the world, making pro-choice activists realise they can take nothing for granted.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Shaw, head of advocacy at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msichoices.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MSI Reproductive Choices}}}\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CEven though we have seen little gains here and there, in some places, we can never, ever be complacent because we\u8217\'20\'19re only ever really hanging on to these rights by the skin of our teeth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said the Texas law was \u8220\'20\'1Creally terrifying\u8221\'20\'1D because of the emboldening message it sent to other anti-choice governments and organisations, with the fact it had happened in the US giving it \u8220\'20\'1Ca huge weight and legitimacy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is all happening in the context of a rising, much more aggressive, much better organised, better funded and much more legitimised opposition movement than we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen before,\u8221\'20\'1D Shaw said.\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice campaigners say they have faced increasingly vocal opposition from organisations that started on the US religious right but have spread to other countries, such as 40 Days for Life, a group that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2019/apr/08/anti-abortion-activists-harassing-women-at-uk-clinics-during-lent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distributes graphic and misleading leaflets}}}\uc2  to women outside UK \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 Heartbeat International, a conservative US Christian federation, funds and coordinates a network of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy resource\u8221\'20\'1D centres, many of them in sub-Saharan Africa, to provide women with what it calls \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue reproductive help\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a transnational movement now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shaw. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is them [US organisations] exporting their playbooks and their money overseas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights usually happen in countries where other human rights are under threat, according to analysts. Last year, more than 30 countries, many of them led by authoritarian strongmen or rightwing populists, including Belarus, Uganda, Hungary, Egypt and Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s US administration, signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/geneva-consensus-declaration-english.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-binding anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  document}}}\uc2  known as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/22/us-trump-administration-signs-anti-abortion-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Geneva consensus declaration}}}\uc2 . The text was also seen as being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/biden-reverse-anti-abortion-rights-policies-executive-order/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-LGBTQ}}}\uc2 , as most of the signatories had not legalised same-sex marriage and several prosecute their LGBTQ+ citizens.\par \par \uc2 In one of his first acts as president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2021/01/28/memorandum-on-protecting-womens-health-at-home-and-abroad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden removed the US}}}\uc2  from the declaration in January, as well as ending the Mexico City policy, known as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-global-gag-rule-health-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the signatories was Poland, which is one of only three countries to have significantly rolled back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since 2000, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . The other two are Nicaragua and the US.\par \par \uc2 In October last year, Poland\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional tribunal ruled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/22/poland-rules-abortion-due-to-foetal-defects-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminations due to foetal defects were unconstitutional}}}\uc2 . Three months later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/27/poland-to-implement-near-total-ban-on-abortion-imminently"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a near-total ban}}}\uc2  on abortions was imposed. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now only legal in the case of rape, incest or a threat to the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, human rights observers have said that a Nicaraguan law punishing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without any exceptions, passed in 2006, has simply {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2017/07/31/nicaragua-abortion-ban-threatens-health-and-lives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced women}}}\uc2  to seek unsafe backstreet terminations.\par \par \uc2 Marge Berer, coordinator of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.safeabortionwomensright.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Campaign for Women\u8217\'20\'19s Right to Safe \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , said setbacks were all too common, with breakthrough moments often followed by backlashes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy experience of this is one step forward, two steps forward, or one step back, 10 steps back,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd much of it, if not all of it, depends on who is the head of the government of the day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Berer, who has been involved in the pro-choice movement for almost 40 years, said the overall picture was brighter than it had been then: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/report/abortion-worldwide-2017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer deaths}}}\uc2  from unsafe abortions, and many more countries where terminations are legal.\par \par \uc2 But, she added, she was not hugely optimistic about the future. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so much misogyny in the world. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how anybody is going to make that go away,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, that\u8217\'20\'19s the real problem. It\u8217\'20\'19s that when misogyny takes over on a policy level, it\u8217\'20\'19s very nasty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, there is more hope among activists in Latin America, where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/impact/2019/08/the-green-wave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marea verde}}}\uc2 , or green wave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jun/14/argentina-congress-vote-legalise-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has swept through first Argentina}}}\uc2  and, last week, Mexico, where the supreme court struck down a state law that imposed prison terms for having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While it did not automatically legalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the decision is thought to set a binding precedent for the country\u8217\'20\'19s judges.\par \par \uc2 Eugenia L\u243\'00\'F3pez Uribe, regional director of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ippf.org/our-approach/services/Abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Planned Parenthood Federation}}}\uc2 , said the legal change was the result of \u8220\'20\'1C40 years of hard work\u8221\'20\'1D by campaigners, with mass demonstrations, backroom lobbying and \u8220\'20\'1Ca mainstreaming\u8221\'20\'1D of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in public discourse.\par \par \uc2 She said the ability of the Catholic church to tell people what to do when it came to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception had been greatly reduced. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we know from different surveys \u8230\'20\'26 is that in reality Catholics \u8230\'20\'26 feel that this is a private decision that you have to do with your own conscience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As women in Texas bear the brunt of the law brought in by the governor, Greg Abbott, their Mexican allies across the border were planning to take the fight north, she added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8216\'20\'18green wave\u8217\'20\'19 hasn\u8217\'20\'19t reached the United States so this is a very good opportunity for [it] to cross the border of the Rio Grande and go to the United States. We can make it go even further. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been used to thinking about it in Latin America. Now is the time for North America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210918eh9i000p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
