\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US military admits Kabul strike killed 10 civilians and no Islamic State fighters \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 8,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2021\par 00:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Admission marks reversal for Pentagon, which initially defended strikeGeneral says calls to Chinese counterpart \u8216\'20\'18perfectly within the duties\u8217\'20\'19Far-right groups tell supporters planned rally is a government \u8216\'20\'18trap\u8217\'20\'19Biden criticized over crowded migrant camp near Del Rio, TexasSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s biggest stories.\par \par \uc2 * The US military {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/us-military-strike-afghanistan-civilians-islamic-state-pentagon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted}}}\uc2  that its 29 August drone strike in Kabul killed 10 Afghan civilians and no Islamic State fighters. The admission marked a stunning reversal from the military, which had previously defended the integrity of the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CWe now assess that it is unlikely that the vehicle and those who died were associated with Isis-K or were a direct threat to US forces,\u8221\'20\'1D US CENTCOM Commander Gen Kenneth McKenzie said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a mistake, and I offer my sincere apology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * France has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/17/france-recalls-ambassadors-to-us-and-australia-after-aukus-pact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recalled}}}\uc2  its ambassadors to the US and Australia, marking the latest escalation in the country\u8217\'20\'19s public criticism of the Aukus defense deal. \u8220\'20\'1CThis exceptional decision is justified by the exceptional gravity of the announcements made on 15 September by Australia and the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D French foreign minister \uc2 Jean-Yves Le Drian\uc2  said. French officials have said they received no advance warning of the nuclear submarine deal, which contradicted Australia\u8217\'20\'19s earlier promise to buy a French-built fleet of submarines. This is the first time France has recalled its ambassador since the United States\u8217\'20\'19 founding.\par \par \uc2 * An advisory panel at the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  decisively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/fda-pfizer-booster-shots-covid-vaccine-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  against recommending \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine boosters for all fully vaccinated Americans age 16 or older. The panel\u8217\'20\'19s decision likely means the Biden administration will not meet its deadline of making \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  boosters available to all fully vaccinated American adults by next week.\par \par \uc2 * A humanitarian crisis is unfolding in a crowded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/us-mexico-border-texas-migrants-bridge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 migrant camp}}}\uc2  near Del Rio, Texas. As of last night, about 10,000 migrants \u8211\'20\'13 many from Haiti \u8211\'20\'13 were staying under the Del Rio International Bridge as border patrol officials struggled to process the large number of people arriving at the US-Mexican border. The migrants have had infrequent access to food and water as they wait in the punishing Texas heat.\par \par \uc2 * Interest in the far-right \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/justice-for-j6-rally-washington-proud-boys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice for J6}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday seems to be waning, as potential attendees express concern that the event is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrap\u8221\'20\'1D set by law enforcement. The event is being held in support of the pro-Trump insurrectionists who carried out the Capitol attack on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 * A panel of judges in North Carolina permanently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/17/joe-biden-migrant-camp-republicans-democrats-coronavirus-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6144f4268f08001fa2d1d30e#block-6144f4268f08001fa2d1d30e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 voter ID law, saying that it was at least in part motivated by discrimination against Black voters. The 2018 law was enacted after federal courts struck down a 2013 voter ID law, which was found to target Black voters with \u8220\'20\'1Calmost surgical precision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 The White House will host a virtual global Covid-19 summit next week, as the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2  convenes in New York.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that the meeting of world leaders, civil society groups, philanthropists, business leaders, and NGOs will be asked to \u8220\'20\'1Ccommit to a higher level of ambition\u8221\'20\'1D on issues including \u8220\'20\'1Cenhancing equitably access to vaccines\u8221\'20\'1D and boosting supplies of oxygen, tests, drugs and PPE.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will use the summit to call on world leaders to commit to fully vaccinating 70% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s population by September 2022, the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/09/17/biden-pfizer-vaccine-global/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the Washington Post also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/09/17/biden-pfizer-vaccine-global/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the Biden administration was negotiating to purchase 500m more doses of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine to donate to other countries.\par \par \uc2 Biden has faced criticism for promising booster shots to Americans even as much of the world remains unvaccinated. But earlier today, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  declined to approve \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  booster shots for all Americans over 16. It elected instead to recommend the shots only to those over 65 or at high risk of serious infection, including healthcare workers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Kim Willsher {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/17/france-recalls-ambassadors-to-us-and-australia-after-aukus-pact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  from Paris on France\u8217\'20\'19s decision to recall its ambassadors to the US and Australia:\par \par \uc2 It is the first time France has recalled a US ambassador; the two countries have been allies since the American war of independence. France also cancelled a gala due to be held on Friday to commemorate the anniversary of the Battle of Chesapeake Bay, a decisive event in the war, which ended with the French fleet\u8217\'20\'19s victory over the British on 5 September 1781.\par \par \uc2 A White House official told Reuters that the United States regretted the French decision and said Washington had been in close touch with Paris. The official said the United States would be engaged in the coming days to resolve differences between the two countries.\par \par \uc2 Peter Ricketts\uc2 , a former permanent undersecretary at the Foreign Office and former UK ambassador to France, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LordRickettsP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t underestimate reaction in Paris. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just anger but a real sense of betrayal that UK as well as US and Aus negotiated behind their backs for 6 months. I lived the rupture in 2003 over Iraq. This feels as bad or worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After news of the ambassador recall, Lord Ricketts added: \u8220\'20\'1CUnprecedented between allied nations? Interestingly not from UK. A signal Paris regards Washington and Canberra as ringleaders in plot, with London as accomplice. Expect further French measures targeting interests of all three.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/17/france-recalls-ambassadors-to-us-and-australia-after-aukus-pact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 France recalls ambassadors to US and Australia after Aukus pact}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Public health officials in Idaho and parts of Alaska and Montana have approved healthcare rationing in response to the surge of hospitalizations among largely unvaccinated Covid-19 patients, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The rationing process, known as \u8220\'20\'1CCrisis Standards of Care\u8221\'20\'1D, involves a set of legal and ethical guidelines that hospitals follow to determine who receives care when they cannot meet demand.\par \par \uc2 Some forms of rationing have been common during the pandemic, such as the postponement of non-emergency surgeries.\par \par \uc2 But the rationing standards also include a scoring system if hospitals have to determine who should receive a bed or ventilator. The scoring system prioritizes saving the highest number of \u8220\'20\'1Clife-years\u8221\'20\'1D, so younger, healthier people are more likely to qualify for treatment, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 In extreme cases, if the entire state runs out of ventilators, Idaho will implement a \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Universal\uc2  Do Not Resuscitate Order\u8221\'20\'1D, which means that patients who suffer a cardiac arrest will not receive live saving measures, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe situation is dire \u8211\'20\'13 we don\u8217\'20\'19t have enough resources to adequately treat the patients in our hospitals, whether you are there for Covid-19 or a heart attack or because of a car accident,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dave Jeppesen, director of the Idaho Department of Health and Welfare, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://healthandwelfare.idaho.gov/news/idaho-expands-crisis-standards-care-statewide-due-surge-covid-19-patients-requiring-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  announcing the policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur hospitals and healthcare systems need our help. The best way to end crisis standards of care is for more people to get vaccinated. It dramatically reduces your chances of having to go to the hospital if you do get sick from Covid-19. In addition, please wear a mask indoors in public and outdoors when it\u8217\'20\'19s crowded to help slow the spread.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, the chairman of the House permanent select committee on intelligence, has released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://intelligence.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=1157"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on the US military\u8217\'20\'19s admission that it killed 10 Afghan civilians and no Islamic State targets in its 29 August drone strike, including seven children.\par \par \uc2 Schiff, a California Democrat, appeared to suggest that the military had been dishonest in its public statements following the attack, and that there may be investigations to follow:\par \par \uc2 In acknowledging that error, the Department of Defense has taken the first step towards transparency and accountability. And after such a devastating failure - one that, by the Department\u8217\'20\'19s estimate, killed 10 civilians, at least 7 of them children - it cannot be the last step. We need to know what went wrong in the hours and minutes leading up to the strike to prevent similar tragedies in the future.\par \par \uc2 I am also concerned about the accuracy and completeness of public statements made in the immediate aftermath of the strike, and whether those accounted for all of the information possessed by the government at the time. We must assure that the Department examines its actions carefully and objectively, even in the absence of press reports, such as here, which brought this critical mistake to light.\par \par \uc2 This is an area deserving of additional oversight, and along with my colleagues in Congress, the House Intelligence Committee will continue to press for answers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina Republicans rushed through the voter ID measure in a lame duck session in 2018 after voters approved a constitutional amendment to require identification at the polls.\par \par \uc2 The court noted Republicans enacted the measure through an unusual process, moving the bill quickly through the legislature. They did that, the court said, because they had just lost their supermajority in the state legislature and pass the measure while they could still override a veto from governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 The 2018 amendment and law came after a previous 2013 North Carolina voter ID measure was struck down by federal courts. That measure was part of a law that targeted African Americans with \u8220\'20\'1Calmost surgical precision,\u8221\'20\'1D the US court of appeals for the 4th circuit wrote.\par \par \uc2 The 2018 measure expanded the types of photo ID acceptable under the law to include college and government employee IDs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/north-carolina-judges-strike-down-states-voter-id-law/2021/09/17/6918c568-17e1-11ec-a019-cb193b28aa73_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the AP}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judges block North Carolina voter ID law, citing racial discrimination\par \par \uc2 A North Carolina panel of judges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1g3xeOQDgEHtoEfHI4_44zjy4SgzCnKxA/view?usp=sharing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently blocked}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 voter photo identification law on Friday, saying Republican lawmakers were in part motivated by an intent to discriminate against African American voters when they enacted the measure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of this three-judge panel finds the evidence at trial sufficient to show that the enactment of S.B. 824 was motivated at least in part by an unconstitutional intent to target African American voters,\u8221\'20\'1D Superior Court Judge Michael O\u8217\'20\'19Foghludha wrote in a 2-1 decision for a 3-judge panel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of this three-judge panel also finds that the Defendants have failed to prove, based on the evidence at trial, that S.B. 824 would have been enacted in its present form if it did not tend to discriminate against African American voters,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COther, less restrictive voter ID laws would have sufficed to achieve the legitimate nonracial purposes of implementing the constitutional amendment requiring voter ID, deterring fraud, or enhancing voter confidence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a dissenting opinion, Judge Nathaniel Poovey wrote \u8220\'20\'1Cnot one scintilla of evidence was introduced during this trial that any legislator acted with racially discriminatory intent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ruling is almost certain to be appealed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello everyone, this is Julia Carrie Wong in Oakland, California, picking up the blog for the rest of the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, we brought you the news that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  voted not to recommend a third shot of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for most Americans.\par \par \uc2 However, the panel of experts did recommend that people over 65 and at high risk of severe Covid-19 should get a booster shot at least six months after their first doses, my colleagues Jessica Glenza and Eric Berger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/fda-pfizer-booster-shots-covid-vaccine-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This category includes healthcare workers and people at high-risk of \u8220\'20\'1Coccupational\u8221\'20\'1D exposure to Covid.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s recommendations only apply to the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine. Moderna has also applied to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for approval of booster shots.\par \par \uc2 You can read our full report on the latest in the debate over boosters here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/fda-pfizer-booster-shots-covid-vaccine-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FDA advisers vote not to recommend Pfizer booster shots for most Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Julia Carrie Wong, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The US military admitted that its August 29 drone strike in Kabul killed 10 Afghan civilians and no Islamic State fighters. The admission marked a stunning reversal from the military, which had previously defended the integrity of the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CWe now assess that it is unlikely that the vehicle and those who died were associated with ISIS-K or were a direct threat to US forces,\u8221\'20\'1D US CENTCOM Commander Gen Kenneth McKenzie said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a mistake, and I offer my sincere apology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * France has recalled its ambassadors to the US and Australia, marking the latest escalation in the country\u8217\'20\'19s public criticism of the Aukus defense deal. \u8220\'20\'1CThis exceptional decision is justified by the exceptional gravity of the announcements made on 15th September by Australia and the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D French foreign minister \uc2 Jean-Yves Le Drian\uc2  said. French officials have said they received no advance warning of the nuclear submarine deal, which contradicted Australia\u8217\'20\'19s earlier promise to buy a French-built fleet of submarines.\par \par \uc2 * An advisory panel at the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  decisively voted against recommending \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine boosters for all fully vaccinated Americans aged 16 or older. The panel\u8217\'20\'19s decision likely means the Biden administration will not meet its deadline of making \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  boosters available to all fully vaccinated American adults by next week.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration is receiving criticism over a crowded migrant camp near Del Rio, Texas. As of last night, about 10,000 migrants were staying under the Del Rio International Bridge as Border Patrol officials struggled to process the large number of people arriving at the US-Mexican border. The migrants have had infrequent access to food and water as they wait in the punishing Texas heat.\par \par \uc2 * Interest in the far-right \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday seems to be waning, as potential attendees express concern that the event is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrap\u8221\'20\'1D set by law enforcement. The event is being held in support of the pro-Trump insurrectionists who carried out the Capitol attack on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Julia will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about France\u8217\'20\'19s decision to recall its ambassador to the US, Pentagon spokesperson John Kirby noted that defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  spoke to his French counterpart this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI won\u8217\'20\'19t characterize the French side of course, but it was clear from the discussion that there is still much work to do in terms of our defense relationship with France,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said at the Pentagon press briefing today.\par \par \uc2 enltrPentagon Press Sec. John Kirby responds to France recalling its ambassador to the U.S. over the nuclear submarine deal with Australia:\par \par \uc2 "There is still much work to do in terms of our defense relationship with France.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kyQf2yI4M9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kyQf2yI4M9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1438956646642880515?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Other senior US officials have sought to placate France\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the Aukus deal by emphasizing the enduring importance of the alliance between Washington and Paris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe value our relationship and our partnership with France on a variety of issues facing the global community,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would leave it, of course, to our Australian partners to describe why they sought this new technology and why they pursued this technology from the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 France recalls ambassadors to US and Australia in protest of nuclear submarine deal\par \par \uc2 The French government is now recalling its ambassadors to the US and Australia, marking the latest escalation in the country\u8217\'20\'19s public criticism of the newly announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/sep/16/aukus-pact-uk-and-us-battle-to-contain-international-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aukus deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the request of the President of the Republic, I am recalling to Paris without delay our ambassadors to the United States and to Australia for consultations,\u8221\'20\'1D French foreign minister \uc2 Jean-Yves Le Drian\uc2  said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/en/country-files/united-states/events/article/statement-by-jean-yves-le-drian-minister-for-europe-and-foreign-affairs-17-sept"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis exceptional decision is justified by the exceptional gravity of the announcements made on 15th September by Australia and the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 French officials have expressed outrage over the new defense pact between Australia, the UK and the US, which was announced earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 France has said it was given no advance warning of the nuclear submarine deal, which contradicted Australia\u8217\'20\'19s earlier promise to buy a French-built fleet of submarines.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/sep/16/aukus-pact-uk-and-us-battle-to-contain-international-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aukus pact: UK and US battle to contain international backlash}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US will buy hundreds of millions more doses of the Covid-19 \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for donation to increase global vaccine access, the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/09/17/biden-pfizer-vaccine-global/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on Friday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine. Photograph: Robert F Bukaty/AP\par \par \uc2 Citing two unnamed sources familiar with the deal, the Post said the announcement of the additional vaccine purchases will be made next week, lining up with the United Nations general assembly meeting.\par \par \uc2 Details of the plan remain unfinalized, with the White House declining to comment. \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  also did not respond to the Post\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In June, the US agreed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/kyle-defreytag-us-capitol-attack-police-officer-dies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to donate 500m Pfzier vaccine doses }}}\uc2  to 100 countries, a strategy in the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s plan to bolster US soft power and influence that Biden said had been weakened under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Globally, vaccine inequality is an ongoing issue. As of 25 August, of the 4.8bn Covid vaccines delivered, around 75% have been allocated to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/aug/25/the-guardian-view-on-global-vaccine-inequality-unwise-as-well-as-unethical"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 10 countries. }}}\par \par \uc2 A little over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/america-has-wasted-least-15-million-covid-vaccine-doses-march-n1278211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15m Covid vaccine doses have been thrown out}}}\uc2  in the US since 1 March, even as the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/10/first-thing-biden-introduces-vaccine-mandate-for-100-million-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imposes new employment vaccine mandates}}}\uc2  to boost declining vaccination rates. Meanwhile, public health experts estimate that residents in low-income countries will likely have to wait until 2023 to become vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  advisers vote not to recommend \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  booster shots for most Americans\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza and Eric Berger report:\par \par \uc2 Scientific advisers to the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) \uc2 have voted not to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/16/covid-boosters-us-rollout-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommend a third shot}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for Americans older than 16, a potentially significant blow to the Biden administration after it announced a plan to \u8220\'20\'1Cboost\u8221\'20\'1D adults before advisory committees had a chance to review scientific evidence in public.\par \par \uc2 The committee chair, Dr Arnold Monto, a \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  epidemiologist, said he planned to continue deliberations after the vote. Sixteen of 18 advisers opposed the proposal, even as some members believed there is \u8220\'20\'1Ca role\u8221\'20\'1D for a third dose.\par \par \uc2 The decision by the vaccines and related biological products advisory committee is not binding, but the \uc2 FDA\uc2  usually follows its advice.\par \par \uc2 The decision came after significant public scientific dissent regarding a third dose of the vaccine. Much of the data in favor of a third dose came from Israel, while data was sparse on whether a booster could help protect people against hospitalization and death.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are too many questions for me to feel comfortable saying \u8216\'20\'18yes\u8217\'20\'19 to this,\u8221\'20\'1D said A Oveta Fuller, a member and associate professor of microbiology and immunology at the Medical School University of Michigan, summing up the views of several voting members.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/fda-pfizer-booster-shots-covid-vaccine-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FDA advisers vote not to recommend Pfizer booster shots for most Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  apologized for the \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible mistake\u8221\'20\'1D of the August 29 drone strike in Kabul that resulted in the deaths of 10 Afghan civilians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn behalf of the men and women of the Department of Defense, I offer my deepest condolences to surviving family members of those who were killed, including Mr. Ahmadi, and to the staff of Nutrition and \uc2 Education International\uc2 , Mr. Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s employer,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said, referring to one of the victims of the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe apologize, and we will endeavor to learn from this horrible mistake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Austin noted he has ordered a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough review of the investigation just completed by U.S. Central Command\u8221\'20\'1D to more fully examine how this tragedy unfolded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo military works harder than ours to avoid civilian casualties. When we have reason to believe we have taken innocent life, we investigate it and, if true, we admit it,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will do that in this case. We will scrutinize not only what we decided to do -- and not do -- on the 29th of August, but also how we investigated those outcomes. We owe that to the victims and their loved ones, to the American people and to ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 US CENTCOM commander Gen Kenneth McKenzie offered his \u8220\'20\'1Cprofound condolences\u8221\'20\'1D to the families of those killed in the Kabul attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the combatant commander, I am fully responsible for this strike and its tragic outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D McKenzie said at the Pentagon press briefing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US military\u8217\'20\'19s admission comes a week after the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported that the Kabul drone strike had killed an innocent aid worker trying to bring water to his family.\par \par \uc2 The Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/world/asia/us-air-strike-drone-kabul-afghanistan-isis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  last Friday:\par \par \uc2 Military officials said they did not know the identity of the car\u8217\'20\'19s driver when the drone fired, but deemed him suspicious because of how they interpreted his activities that day, saying that he possibly visited an ISIS safe house and, at one point, loaded what they thought could be explosives into the car.\par \par \uc2 Times reporting has identified the driver as Zemari Ahmadi, a longtime worker for a U.S. aid group. The evidence suggests that his travels that day actually involved transporting colleagues to and from work. And an analysis of video feeds showed that what the military may have seen was Mr. Ahmadi and a colleague loading canisters of water into his trunk to bring home to his family.\par \par \uc2 While the U.S. military said the drone strike might have killed three civilians, Times reporting shows that it killed 10, including seven children, in a dense residential block.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 US military admits Kabul strike killed 10 civilians, no Islamic State fighters\par \par \uc2 The US military has admitted that a drone strike in Kabul last month killed 10 Afghan civilians, rather than the Islamic State fighters it was meant to target.\par \par \uc2 The admission marked a severe reversal for the Pentagon, which had initially defended the effectiveness and necessity of the August 29 strike.\par \par \uc2 enltrGen. McKenzie: "I am now convinced that as many as 10 civilians, including up to 7 children, were tragically killed in that strike...it is unlikely that the vehicle and those who died were associated with ISIS-K...I offer my profound condolences." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/w6M4LEbX3b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/w6M4LEbX3b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1438946013931352073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 US CENTCOM Commander Gen Kenneth McKenzie said at a press briefing that as many as seven Afghan children were believed to have been killed in the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMoreover, we now assess that it is unlikely that the vehicle and those who died were associated with ISIS-K or were a direct threat to US forces,\u8221\'20\'1D McKenzie said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a mistake, and I offer my sincere apology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 USCP chief acknowledges 'threats of violence' in association with 'Justice for J6' rally\par \par \uc2 The chief of the US Capitol Police, Tom Manger, acknowledged that law enforcement officials have heard \u8220\'20\'1Cchatter\u8221\'20\'1D of potential violence in Washington in connection to the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere have been some threats of violence associated with this, the events for tomorrow, and we have a strong plan in place to ensure that it remains peaceful and that if violence does occur, that we can stop it as quickly as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Manger said at a press briefing a day before the far-right rally.\par \par \uc2 enltrCapitol Police Chief Tom Manger tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeffpeguescbs?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jeffpeguescbs}}}\uc2  "it's tough to say" if threats of violence for Saturday's rally are credible, but "the chatter that we heard prior to January 6 obviously turned out to be [credible]...so we're not taking any chances" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l2vu0mIQhT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l2vu0mIQhT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1438916221450260482?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the USCP considers the threats of violence to be credible, Manger said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe chatter that we heard prior to January 6 obviously turned out to be -- many of those threats turned out to be credible, so we\u8217\'20\'19re not taking any chances.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The USCP has escalated security protocols around Capitol Hill in anticipation of the rally, which is being held in support of the insurrectionists who carried out the January 6 attack on the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among other measures, the USCP has reinstalled the fencing around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 , which was previously taken down in July.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The secretary of defense, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , has approved a request to place 100 national guards troops on standby ahead of a planned \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally happening in Washington on Saturday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The far-right protest is being staged by a Trump operative, Matt Braynard, and his organization, Look Ahead America. The rally will demand the justice department drop all charges against the almost 600 people arrested in connection with the 6 January Capitol attack, when Trump supporters attacked Congress in an attempt to overturn the election result.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe task force will only be deployed upon request of the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  to help protect the US Capitol building and congressional office buildings by manning building entry points and verifying credentials of individuals seeking access to the building,\u8221\'20\'1D a Pentagon spokesman told the AP.\par \par \uc2 Five people died around the events of 6 January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/kyle-defreytag-us-capitol-attack-police-officer-dies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including a Capitol Hill police officer. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, where the president is expected to spend the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  disembarks Marine One upon arrival at the Gordons Pond in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware. Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 Biden did not take any questions from reporters as he departed Washington and then arrived in Rehoboth, where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/another-biden-backup-in-delaware-with-his-first-presidential-trip-to-rehoboth-beach-home/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 owns a beach house}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  has become the first openly gay governor in the US to marry in office.\par \par \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2 . Photograph: David Zalubowski/AP\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\uc2  governor and Marlon Reis, his partner of 18 years, hosted an intimate traditional-styled Jewish wedding surrounded by close friends, family and their two children, according to a news release this week.\par \par \uc2 The wedding, held on the \uc2 University of Colorado\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Boulder campus, held significant meaning as it marked the 18th anniversary of their first date.\par \par \uc2 The Colorado governor is the first publicly LGBTQ official to get married while in office, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://victoryfund.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ Victory Fund}}}\uc2 . A decade before Polis was elected governor of Colorado, he made history as the first parent in a same-sex relationship elected to the \uc2 United States House of Representatives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe greatest lesson we have learned over the past 18 months is that life as we know it can change in an instant. We are thankful for the health and wellbeing of our family and friends, and the opportunity to celebrate our life together as a married couple,\u8221\'20\'1D Polis and Reis said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/jared-polis-weds-first-same-sex-marriage-sitting-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jared Polis becomes first sitting governor to marry in same-sex wedding}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Milley defends China calls reported in Woodward book\par \par \uc2 Gen Mark Milley, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, has defended phone calls in which, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/sep/14/mark-milley-donald-trump-bob-woodward-nuclear-war-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new book by Bob Woodward and Robert Costa}}}\uc2  of the Washington Post, he reassured his Chinese counterpart that the US would make it through the transition from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  without launching an attack on Beijing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/sep/14/mark-milley-donald-trump-bob-woodward-nuclear-war-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As reported by Woodward and Costa}}}\uc2 , Milley made \u8220\'20\'1Ca pair of secret phone calls\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Gen Li Zuocheng\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One call reportedly took place on 30 October 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 four days before the election. The other took place on 8 January, two days after Trump supporters attacked Congress, seeking to overturn that defeat.\par \par \uc2 In the first call, prompted also by tensions in the South China Sea and over the origins of the coronavirus pandemic, Milley reportedly told Li: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to assure you that the American government is stable and everything is going to be OK. We are not going to attack or conduct any kinetic operations against you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Milley also reportedly told the Chinese general he would warn him if an attack was launched.\par \par \uc2 In the second call, after the Capitol riot, Milley told Li: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are 100% steady. Everything\u8217\'20\'19s fine. But democracy can be sloppy sometimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On a military flight today, Milley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mark-milley-says-calls-to-chinese-general-were-within-his-duties-11631878596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are routine calls in order to discuss issues of the day, to reassure both allies and adversaries in this case, in order to ensure strategic stability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd these are perfectly within the duties and responsibilities of the chairman.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump and his supporters have lashed out over the reported calls, accusing the general of treasonous behaviour. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/15/joe-biden-mark-milley-great-confidence-trump-revelation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden has said}}}\uc2  Milley retains his \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat confidence\u8221\'20\'1D as the most senior US general.\par \par \uc2 On his flight, to Athens on Nato business, Milley told reporters he would be glad to testify about the calls, as he is due to do in the Senate on 28 September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I will go into any level of detail Congress wants to go into,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s another take:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/17/general-milley-cannot-undermine-civilian-authority-the-us-is-not-a-military-junta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 General Milley cannot undermine civilian authority. The US is not a military junta | Lt Col Daniel L Davis (ret)}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justices do not rule according to personal views and are not politicians, the hardline conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/courts_law/justice-clarence-thomas/2021/09/16/d2ddc1ba-1714-11ec-a5e5-ceecb895922f_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: Robert Franklin/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the media makes it sound as though you are just always going right to your personal preference,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wndu.com/2021/09/17/supreme-court-justice-clarence-justice-delivers-speech-notre-dame/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at Notre Dame university}}}\uc2  in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo if they think you are anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or something personally, they think that\u8217\'20\'19s the way you always will come out. They think you\u8217\'20\'19re for this or for that. They think you become like a politician.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a problem. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to jeopardise any faith in the legal institutions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Thomas was one of five conservatives who in an emergency \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/aug/31/supreme-court-us-cases-shadow-docket"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shadow docket}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/21a24_8759.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 let stand}}}\uc2  an extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law from Texas.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights fear the move previews a formal overturning of Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which guarantees the right, through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/01/roe-v-wade-abortion-ruling-what-to-do-world-without"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a case from Mississippi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten to the point where we\u8217\'20\'19re really good at finding something that separates us,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas said.\par \par \uc2 He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not about winning and losing at the court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thomas is only the latest justice to insist members of a court on which liberals are outnumbered 6-3 do not rule according to political beliefs.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the conservative Amy Coney Barrett {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-not-partisan-hacks-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cjudicial philosophies are not the same as political parties\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed the court was \u8220\'20\'1C not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/12/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-511603"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking}}}\uc2  at a Kentucky centre named for \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate leader who defied convention to block \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s third pick to the court, oversaw two picks by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/14/brett-kavanaugh-fbi-investigation-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hugely controversial}}}\uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , then ripped up his own precedent to rush Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation in place of a liberal lion, \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , shortly before the last election.\par \par \uc2 McConnell looked on as Barrett spoke. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1437411575590232069"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 irony}}}\uc2  did not go {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MartinPengelly/status/1437508608632238083"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unnoticed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-justices-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas insists supreme court justices do not rule based on politics}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration is receiving criticism over a crowded migrant camp near Del Rio, Texas. As of last night, about 10,000 migrants were staying under the Del Rio International Bridge as Border Patrol officials struggled to process the large number of people arriving at the US-Mexican border. The migrants have had infrequent access to food and water as they wait in the punishing Texas heat.\par \par \uc2 * An advisory panel at the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  is meeting to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application to make coronavirus vaccine booster shots available to all fully vaccinated Americans aged 16 or older. The Biden administration had originally said \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna booster shots would be available to all adults starting the week of September 20, but now only \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  may be eligible to distribute third doses next week, pending the recommendation of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  panel.\par \par \uc2 * Interest in the far-right \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday seems to be waning, as potential attendees express concern that the event is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrap\u8221\'20\'1D set by law enforcement. The event is being held in support of the pro-Trump insurrectionists who carried out the Capitol attack on January 6.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza and Eric Berger report:\par \par \uc2 Scientific advisers to the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) will debate the safety and efficacy of recommending a booster shot for fully vaccinated Americans who received the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Whatever the outcome of the advisory panel hearings, the recommendation is unlikely to quell dissent about whether the shots are appropriate to prevent mild to moderate illness at a time when most of the world remains unvaccinated, an issue specifically excluded from \uc2 FDA\uc2  deliberations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are committed to focusing on the science,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Peter Marks, director of the Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research at the FDA, at the beginning of the hours-long meeting.\par \par \uc2 He said the group would \u8220\'20\'1Cdrive our decision-making and will carefully consider those data in the context of the clear and obvious public health need to continue slowing the spread of Covid-19, which at this time is leading to the death of close to 2,000 Americans each day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/fda-pfizer-booster-shots-covid-vaccine-advisers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FDA advisers to debate safety of recommending Pfizer booster shots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dr Vivek Murthy, the US surgeon general, noted the final recommendation from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  on booster shots will come next week, after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine advisory panel meets to discuss the proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis process is consistent with what we outlined in August, where our goals were to stay ahead of the virus, to lay out an initial plan based on our clinical judgement and to ultimately ensure that the final plan would be based on the independent assessment and recommendations of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and CDC,\u8221\'20\'1D Murthy said.\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Surgeon General Vivek Murthy says a CDC advisory committee will meet next week to discuss booster shots, "after which the CDC will make their final recommendation." He says the plans for distributing the shots will be "ready to go" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/H87a2BfUQk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/H87a2BfUQk}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/94pJYVccdT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/94pJYVccdT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1438898190091235336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1COur goal then, and now, is to protect the health and well-being of the public. As soon as the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and CDC complete their evaluations, we will be ready to move forward accordingly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Implicitly addressing criticism about why health officials announced the plan for booster shots so early, Murthy said the Biden administration had used the time before the proposal is approved to coordinate with pharmacies, nursing homes and local leaders about administering third doses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe infrastructure that helped deliver more than 200 million first shots will be ready to go to deliver millions of booster shots as well,\u8221\'20\'1D Murthy said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House pandemic response team is now holding a press briefing, as an \uc2 FDA\uc2  advisory board meets to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application to make coronavirus vaccine booster shots available to all Americans aged 16 or older.\par \par \uc2 White House pandemic response coordinator Jeff Zients began the briefing by underscoring the effectiveness of vaccine mandates in boosting vaccination rates.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CVaccination requirements work, and they're good for the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 White House COVID Response Coordinator Jeff Zients {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CuLRH7iutU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CuLRH7iutU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1438896082310815748?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Zients noted that the vaccination rate among \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  employees went from 59% to 90% in just six weeks, after the company announced a vaccine requirement.\par \par \uc2 In the US military, 89% of active-duty troops have now gotten their first shot, up from 76% just three weeks ago, when defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  announced plans to add the coronavirus vaccine to the list of mandated vaccinations for service members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVaccination requirements work, and they\u8217\'20\'19re good for the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D Zients said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  panel meets to discuss plan for \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine booster shots\par \par \uc2 An advisory panel at the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  is meeting today to discuss \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application to make a booster shot of its coronavirus vaccine available to all Americans aged 16 or older.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-science-health-coronavirus-pandemic-1cd1cf6a5c5c02b63f8a7324807a59f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has more details}}}\uc2  on the meeting:\par \par \uc2 The panel, made up of outside experts who advise the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 , weighed a less than clear-cut case: While research suggests immunity levels in those who have been vaccinated wane over time and boosters can reverse that, the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine is still highly protective against severe illness and death, even amid the spread of the highly contagious delta variant.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  experts were scheduled to vote on one basic question: Does the evidence show that a \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  booster would be safe and effective for people 16 and older? In the event of a yes vote, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  is expected to quickly approve boosters for \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shot.\par \par \uc2 But that is just one step in the process. The more thorny question of who should get the shots and when will be debated next week by advisers to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . The CDC generally adopts the recommendations of the group, which sets policy for U.S. vaccination campaigns.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration had originally said that \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccine booster shots would be available to all American adults starting the week of September 20.\par \par \uc2 But now, only \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  may be eligible for approval starting next week, sparking questions about why the president set out the booster shot plan before the proposal was approved by health authorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time we\u8217\'20\'19ve talked about this, we\u8217\'20\'19ve talked about this as based on a thorough review and a thorough process to complete,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s our job to be prepared whenever we can operationalize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Stephanie Kirchgaessner and Jessica Glenza report on the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas:\par \par \uc2 The legal architect of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/185344/20210729162610813_Dobbs%20Amicus%20FINAL%20PDFA.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has argued in a supreme court brief}}}\uc2  that overturning Roe v Wade, the landmark decision which guarantees a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, would compel women to practice abstinence as a way to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrol their reproductive lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  solicitor general Jonathan Mitchell, who played a pivotal role in designing the legal framework of the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, also argued on behalf of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Texas Right to Life that women would still be able to terminate pregnancies if Roe was overturned by traveling to \u8220\'20\'1Cwealthy pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D states like California and New York with the help of \u8220\'20\'1Ctaxpayer subsidies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen can \u8216\'20\'18control their reproductive lives\u8217\'20\'19 without access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; they can do so by refraining from sexual intercourse,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell wrote in the brief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne can imagine a scenario in which a woman has chosen to engage in unprotected (or insufficiently protected) sexual intercourse on the assumption that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be available to her later. But when this court announces the overruling of Roe, that individual can simply change their behavior in response to the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision if she no longer wants to take the risk of an unwanted pregnancy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/texas-abortion-ban-jonathan-mitchell-supreme-court-brief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Overturning Roe v Wade will promote abstinence, says architect of Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  celebrated the news that Republican congressman \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2 , who supported the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment for inciting the Capitol insurrection, will not seek reelection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is no loss for Ohio or our Country and, most importantly, we have a great candidate who was substantially leading Gonzalez in the polls, Max Miller, who I have given my Complete and Total Endorsement,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said in a statement released this morning.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear what polls Trump was referring to, but Gonzalez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/open/2021/07/us-rep-anthony-gonzalez-trumps-trump-backed-challenger-max-miller-in-fundraising.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had raised significantly more money}}}\uc2  than Miller as of July.\par \par \uc2 In a separate statement, Trump added, \u8220\'20\'1C1 down, 9 to go!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That appears to be a reference to the nine other House Republicans who, like Gonzalez, supported Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/16/us/politics/anthony-gonzalez-ohio-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his conversation with the New York Times}}}\uc2 , Republican congressman \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2  described \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Ca cancer for the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitically the environment is so toxic, especially in our own party right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Gonzalez said of his decision not to seek reelection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can fight your butt off and win this thing, but are you really going to be happy? And the answer is, probably not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gonzalez said he did not believe Trump would be elected president again. \u8220\'20\'1CMost of my political energy will be spent working on that exact goal,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio lawmaker also argued that the Republican party had learned the wrong lessons from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CBeyond that, and more importantly, it\u8217\'20\'19s horribly irresponsible and destructive for the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2  said that his political career has impacted the lives of his family members, which was a driving factor in his decision not to seek reelection.\par \par \uc2 The Republican congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/16/us/politics/anthony-gonzalez-ohio-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  that he and his family had to be escorted by two uniformed police officers through the Cleveland airport earlier this year, due to security concerns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s one of those moments where you say, \u8216\'20\'18Is this really what I want for my family when they travel, to have my wife and kids escorted through the airport?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Gonzalez said.\par \par \uc2 Many members of Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2021/06/members-of-congress-are-spending-more-than-ever-on-security/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have spent more money}}}\uc2  on security since the Capitol insurrection, out of concern for their safety.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-impeachment Republican announces he will not run for reelection\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2 , one of ten House Republicans who supported impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the Capitol insurrection, has announced he will not run for reelection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile my desire to build a fuller family life is at the heart of my decision, it is also true that the current state of our politics, especially many of the toxic dynamics inside our own party, is a significant factor in my decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Gonzalez said in a statement released last night.\par \par \uc2 enltrSee my full statement below regarding my decision not to seek re-election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vsggxjD1FI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vsggxjD1FI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Anthony Gonzalez\uc2  (@RepAGonzalez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAGonzalez/status/1438670555922771968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Gonzalez, a former professional football player, had previously been considered a rising star in the Republican party, but Trump has repeatedly attacked the Ohio lawmaker since he cast the impeachment vote in January.\par \par \uc2 The former president has already endorsed one of the candidates who is challenging Gonzalez in the Republican primary, former Trump aide Max Miller.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Far-right groups tell supporters planned Washington rally is a government \u8216\'20\'18trap\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Extremist groups and prominent rightwing figures are warning supporters not to attend a far-right rally in support of the people arrested for participating in the 6 January Capitol attack, calling the event a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrap\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  are bracing for potential violence at the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D protest rally, which is taking place in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC}}}\uc2  on Saturday, and security fencing has gone up once more around the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 But local and federal officials have also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/amp/news/justice-j6-september-18-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that they expect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2021/09/14/january-6-protesters-preparation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no more than 700}}}\uc2  people to attend the protest, a far cry from the estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/dhs-expects-about-700-people-show-pro-trump-d-c-n1279152"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tens of thousands}}}\uc2  of supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who converged on the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  in January.\par \par \uc2 Across rightwing social media platforms, \u8220\'20\'1Cmost people who are talking about the event in any capacity are telling people to steer clear of DC,\u8221\'20\'1D Cassie Miller, a senior research analyst at the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2 , said. \u8220\'20\'1CAny extremist group that\u8217\'20\'19s talking about it is warning people against attending.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The common narrative in rightwing forums is that the rally is \u8220\'20\'1Ca trap that\u8217\'20\'19s been set by federal authorities\u8221\'20\'1D that will leave participants vulnerable to \u8220\'20\'1Csurveillance and arrest\u8221\'20\'1D, Miller said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/justice-for-j6-rally-washington-proud-boys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Far-right groups tell supporters planned Washington rally is a government \u8216\'20\'18trap\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Val Verde county sheriff Joe Frank Martinez said Border Patrol officials are \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelmed\u8221\'20\'1D trying to process the thousands of immigrants waiting near Del Rio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey just can\u8217\'20\'19t process them fast enough, so there\u8217\'20\'19s a backlog of these individuals underneath the bridge,\u8221\'20\'1D Martinez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/09/16/migrants-haitians-del-rio-bridge-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not detained, they\u8217\'20\'19re just gathered there waiting their turn to get processed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The criticism of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy comes as homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas \u8217\'20\'19 chief of staff is stepping own from her role.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/13/dept-of-homeland-security-chief-of-staff-abruptly-resigns-511650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier this week:\par \par \uc2 Karen Olick, chief of staff to Department of Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, announced Monday that she will be leaving for an undisclosed opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Higgins, the current associate director of Refugee, Asylum and International Operations at \uc2 U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services\uc2 , will step in as a temporary chief of staff until a new appointment is made, according to officials in the department. Olick plans to leave DHS at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 In an email, Mayorkas told DHS officials that Olick \u8216\'20\'18has decided to resign her position and pursue new opportunities. We are grateful to Karen for her service during the critical first nine months of the new Administration.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden criticized over crowded migrant camp near Del Rio, Texas\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is receiving severe criticism over a crowded migrant camp that has popped up near the border city of Del Rio, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/hungry-overwhelmed-texas-town-migrants-slip-back-into-mexico-food-2021-09-16/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Thousands of migrants have converged under the bridge that connects Del Rio, Texas and Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s Ciudad Acu\u241\'00\'F1a, creating a makeshift camp with few basic services in intense heat in the latest border emergency facing U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Del Rio mayor Bruno Lozano said that as of early Thursday evening 10,503 migrants were under the Del Rio International Bridge, up from 8,200 in the morning.\par \par \uc2 Food and water has been scarce, around 20 migrants told Reuters, and temperatures have risen to around 99F (37C). Reuters witnessed hundreds of migrants wading through the Rio Grande river and back into Mexico to stock up on essentials they say they are not receiving on the American side.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers are blaming the White House for the alarming conditions of the camp, saying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has failed to develop appropriate immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration is in complete disarray and is handling the border crisis as badly as the evacuation from Afghanistan,\u8221\'20\'1D the Texas governor, Greg Abbott, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The White House will likely be pressed to come up with answers to address the situation today. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/17/us-mexico-border-texas-migrants-bridge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas: thousands gather under border bridge in new migrant crisis for Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210917eh9h001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
