\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s not a Democrat or a Republican thing\u8217\'20\'19: Biden emphasizes need to address climate crisis \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 7,333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2021\par 00:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President echoes his comments from last week after Hurricane IdaCapitol police arrest man with illegal weapons near DNC headquartersAmy Coney Barrett: supreme court \u8216\'20\'18not comprised of partisan hacks\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. Thanks for tuning in.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  surveyed damage from the Caldor fire on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/california-wildfires-biden-trip-climate-crisis-links-extreme-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit to California}}}\uc2  and warned Americans about the devastating effects of the climate crisis. \u8220\'20\'1CThese wildfires are being supercharged by climate change. It isn\u8217\'20\'19t about red or blue states. It\u8217\'20\'19s about fires,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. Biden made a push for his $3.5tn spending plan Congress is debating, which he said includes $8bn to increase wildfire resiliency. Later today he\u8217\'20\'19ll hit the campaign trail with California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who faces a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/california-recall-gavin-newsom-vote-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recall election}}}\uc2  Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  (USCP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/capitol-police-arrest-knives-democratic-national-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested a man}}}\uc2  for illegally carrying weapons near the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington. The man, identified as 44-year-old Donald Craighead of Oceanside, California, was arrested for possession of prohibited weapons after officers found multiple knives in his truck. Craighead\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle was painted with a swastika and other white supremacist symbols. The arrest comes amid intensifying security concerns about the upcoming \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally that is being held in support of Capitol insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 * The USCP warned of \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerning online chatter\u8221\'20\'1D in connection to the far-right rally, which will take place in Washington on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here to protect everyone\u8217\'20\'19s First Amendment right to peacefully protest,\u8221\'20\'1D USCP chief Tom Manger said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CI urge anyone who is thinking about causing trouble to stay home. We will enforce the law and not tolerate violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/antony-blinken-afghanistan-taliban-house-hearing-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  handling of the US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan. House Republicans sharply criticized the execution of the withdrawal mission during a hearing on Capitol Hill this afternoon, but Blinken blamed any issues in the operation on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s deal with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe inherited a deadline. We did not inherit a plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 * Justice Amy Coney Barrett {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-not-partisan-hacks-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the integrity}}}\uc2  of the supreme court, amid widespread criticism of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect. \u8220\'20\'1CMy goal today is to convince you that this court is not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks,\u8221\'20\'1D the conservative justice said during a Sunday event at the McConnell Center at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CJudicial philosophies are not the same as political parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 - Joan E Greve and Dani Anguiano\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Wildfires are being supercharged by climate change,\u8217\'20\'19 Biden says\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese wildfires are being supercharged by climate change. It isn\u8217\'20\'19t about red or blue states. It\u8217\'20\'19s about fires,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CScientists have been warning us for years that extreme weather is going to get more extreme. We\u8217\'20\'19re living it in real time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president made a push for his $3.5tn spending plan Congress is debating, which he said includes $8bn dollars to increase wildfire resiliency. That plan faces skepticism from key centrist Democrats Joe Manchin and Krysten Sinema.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  shakes hands with \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  before speaking about recent wildfires. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 Biden also praised California\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who faces a recall election Tuesday. The two will hit the campaign trail later today. Newsom, who spoke before Biden, warned that California is \u8220\'20\'1Cdealing with extremes the likes of which we\u8217\'20\'19ve never dealt with in our state\u8217\'20\'19s history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks on his administration's response to wildfires\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone in northern California knows the time of the year when you can\u8217\'20\'19t go outside, when the air will be filled with smoke and the sky will turn an apocalyptic shade of orange,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, speaking after the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese fires are a blinking code red for our nation. We know what we have to do and it starts with our firefighters putting their lives on the line in rugged and dangerous conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, referring to his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to raise firefighter pay.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappening Now: President Biden delivers remarks on the Administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to recent wildfires, and how we can strengthen our resilience to climate change and extreme weather. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/058UdtUvQf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/058UdtUvQf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1437555908029124610?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Study finds meat accounts for nearly 60% of all greenhouse gases from food production\par \par \uc2 The global production of food is responsible for a third of all planet-heating gases emitted by human activity, with the use of animals for meat causing twice the pollution of producing plant-based foods, a major new study has found.\par \par \uc2 The entire system of food production, such as the use of farming machinery, spraying of fertilizer and transportation of products, causes 17.3bn metric tonnes of greenhouse gases a year, according to the research. This enormous release of gases that fuel the climate crisis is more than double the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epa.gov/ghgemissions/inventory-us-greenhouse-gas-emissions-and-sinks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entire emissions of the US}}}\uc2  and represents 35% of all global emissions, researchers said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe emissions are at the higher end of what we expected, it was a little bit of a surprise,\u8221\'20\'1D said Atul Jain, a climate scientist at the University of Illinois and co-author of the paper, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/s43016-021-00358-x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published in Nature Food}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis study shows the entire cycle of the food production system, and policymakers may want to use the results to think about how to control greenhouse gas emissions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/13/meat-greenhouses-gases-food-production-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meat accounts for nearly 60% of all greenhouse gases from food production, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says he wants to raise pay for firefighters\par \par \uc2 On a visit to California\u8217\'20\'19s office of emergency services, Biden said he wants to raise pay for firefighters. \u8220\'20\'1CWe owe them,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden, speaking to a packed house, says he wants to raise pay for firefighters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe owe them. We owe them a hell of a lot more\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iUsNMDOHAH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iUsNMDOHAH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lara Korte (@lara_korte) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lara_korte/status/1437534719202062340?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Entry-level federal wildland firefighters earn a base pay below {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/17/mental-health-crisis-spreading-wildfire-fighters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $14 an hour}}}\uc2 , while the same job with \uc2 Cal Fire\uc2 , the state firefighting agency, pays around $26 an hour. The job is risky and physically exhausting, requiring extended time away from home.\par \par \uc2 US Forest Service\uc2  records showed that only half of fire engines were fully staffed at the start of the season, putting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/california-firefighters-stretched-to-limit-as-devastating-blazes-become-the-norm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 additional pressure}}}\uc2  on crews responding to this year\u8217\'20\'19s massive fires.\par \par \uc2 Experts have warned that California\u8217\'20\'19s wildfires, which have destroyed entire towns and killed more than 180 people since 2017, are outpacing government interventions. In June, the Biden administration laid out a plan to step up its investments to combat wildfires, after facing criticism that the federal efforts are under-resourced and understaffed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the eve of California\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial recall election, many voters are signaling that the state\u8217\'20\'19s peculiar recall process needs to change.\par \par \uc2 The recall effort has put governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  in the peculiar position of having to fight for his political future while retaining broad approval among Californians.\par \par \uc2 The campaign to gather signatures to hold a recall picked up steam amid the worst of the state\u8217\'20\'19s pandemic surge \u8211\'20\'13 with recall proponents capitalizing on frustrations over the state policies shutting down schools and businesses, mandating masking and social distancing.\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  takes photos with supporters in Oakland after speaking at a rally ahead of the Republican-led recall election. Photograph: Brittany Hosea-Small/Reuters\par \par \uc2 But in California, no reason is necessary to start a recall petition. The only requirement to put a recall on the ballot is enough voter signatures \u8211\'20\'13 equal to 12% of voters in the last election - including those of voters from at least five counties.\par \par \uc2 So a small, motivated, and angry minority of conservatives were able to create a state-wide referendum on the Democratic governor of an overwhelmingly blue state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the politics of grievance,\u8221\'20\'1D said James Lance Taylor a political scientist at the University of San Francisco. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of the way this whole phenomenon works in California, it is making it possible for a very competent, governor to be removed for no real, legitimate reason.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden arrives in California\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived in California where he was greeted by the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who faces a recall election Tuesday. Biden and Newsom are headed to \uc2 El Dorado county\uc2  where the president will tour areas damaged by the Caldor fire.\par \par \uc2 enltrCalifornia \uc2 Gov. Gavin Newsom\uc2  greets the president on the tarmac at Mather airport in Sacramento county.\par \par \uc2 Biden campaigns for the California governor later tonight \u8212\'20\'14 a day ahead of the recall election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dubtL1VVdZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dubtL1VVdZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Asma Khalid (@asmamk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/asmamk/status/1437532134198034433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Caldor fire has destroyed 782 homes, scorched 342 sq miles and forced the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/30/caldor-fire-california-lake-tahoe-evacuations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evacuation}}}\uc2  of tens of thousands in the Lake Tahoe Basin. The 219,000-acre blaze came within miles of South Lake Tahoe, a popular destination town that is home to more than 20,000 people, and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/11/empty-campgrounds-burned-ski-lifts-will-lake-tahoe-be-a-tourist-destination-once-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised questions}}}\uc2  about the future of such mountain towns.\par \par \uc2 More than 13,000 firefighters are currently battling 15 large wildfires burning in the state. As reported by my colleague Gabrielle Canon, California\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly extreme wildfires are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/california-firefighters-stretched-to-limit-as-devastating-blazes-become-the-norm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stretching firefighters}}}\uc2  to the limit.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 At her Guardian Live discussion with Jonathan Freedland, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  reflected on her win in the popular vote by nearly 3m votes in 2016, when she lost the electoral college by a few tens of thousands in a couple of states. She said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could easily have lost the electoral college despite his 7m margin last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThink about it, you could have someone who wins by nearly 10m votes and still lose the electoral college under our crazy dysfunctional system, which is a remnant of, frankly, compromises with slave states,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think people who study American politics need to realize how insane this whole electoral college is when you talk about a democracy, which is what we\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://escholarship.org/uc/item/6kt7w3ts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  released Monday by the UC Berkeley\u8217\'20\'19s Institute of Governmental Studies, co-sponsored by the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , 75% of registered voters said they wanted to keep their right to remove a statewide official through a recall election.\par \par \uc2 But majorities of voters also proposed reforms to the process. For example, 63% of voters said they would like to see a runoff election in cases where a recall succeeds, but no candidate to replace an official has gained a majority of support.\par \par \uc2 A man casts his vote at the Lincoln Park senior center in Los Angeles, California, ahead of the recall election for \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Photograph: Frederic J Brown/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Currently, even if a hair above 50% of voters choose to remove the governor, the replacement candidate with the most votes automatically becomes governor. In a scenario where 50.1% support removing governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , rightwing radio host Larry Elder \u8211\'20\'13 the leading opponent \u8211\'20\'13 could become governor with just 20% support.\par \par \uc2 A 55% majority also supported the idea of increasing the number of signatures required for a recall, and 59% said that recallers should have to give a reason for wanting to remove an official such as illegal or unethical conduct.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon and happy Monday. Dani Anguiano here taking over \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live US politics coverage for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on his way to California to survey wildfire damage, as the state battles a devastating fire season that is on track to outpace that of 2020, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/30/california-wildfires-north-complex-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state\u8217\'20\'19s worst fire season}}}\uc2  on record.\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to highlight the connection between the climate crisis and the west\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly extreme wildfires as he seeks to rally support for a $3.5tn spending plan Congress is debating.\par \par \uc2 While in California, the president will also campaign with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who faces a recall election Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 More on his visit and the west\u8217\'20\'19s devastating fire season here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/california-wildfires-biden-trip-climate-crisis-links-extreme-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to highlight link between extreme wildfires and climate crisis in trip to California}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Dani Anguiano, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  underscored the urgent need to address climate change while receiving a wildfires briefing in Boise, Idaho. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a Democrat thing, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a Republican thing. It\u8217\'20\'19s a weather thing,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in Boise. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a reality. It\u8217\'20\'19s serious.\u8221\'20\'1D Biden is now traveling to California, where he will get an update on how recent wildfires have impacted the state and then participate in a campaign event with governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  ahead of his recall election tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 * US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  (USCP) arrested a man for illegally carrying weapons near the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington. The man, identified as 44-year-old Donald Craighead of Oceanside, California, was arrested for possession of prohibited weapons after officers found multiple knives in his truck. Craighead\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle was painted with a swastika and other white supremacist symbols. The arrest comes amid intensifying security concerns about the upcoming \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally that is being held in support of Capitol insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 * The USCP warned of \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerning online chatter\u8221\'20\'1D in connection to the far-right rally, which will take place in Washington on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here to protect everyone\u8217\'20\'19s First Amendment right to peacefully protest,\u8221\'20\'1D USCP chief Tom Manger said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CI urge anyone who is thinking about causing trouble to stay home. We will enforce the law and not tolerate violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  defended the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan. House Republicans sharply criticized the execution of the withdrawal mission during a hearing on Capitol Hill this afternoon, but Blinken blamed any issues in the operation on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s deal with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe inherited a deadline. We did not inherit a plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 * Justice Amy Coney Barrett defended the integrity of the supreme court, amid widespread criticism of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect. \u8220\'20\'1CMy goal today is to convince you that this court is not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks,\u8221\'20\'1D the conservative justice said during a Sunday event at the McConnell Center at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CJudicial philosophies are not the same as political parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dani will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  also shared photos of some of the training exercises and briefings the agency has held recently to prepare for the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 According to the USCP statement, the agency has held such meetings over the past month to ensure the highest level of preparation for the far-right rally.\par \par \uc2 The USCP has also been sharing information on the rally with other law enforcement partners in Washington, the agency said.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere are some pictures from our recent training exercises. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GqlHc9jmQl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GqlHc9jmQl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1437490299014684675?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 USCP warns of 'concerning online chatter' around 'Justice for J6' rally\par \par \uc2 The chief of US Capitol Police, Tom Manger, released a statement on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s security preparations for the September 18 \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally, which is being held in support of the insurrectionists who attacked the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  in January.\par \par \uc2 According to the statement, the USCP is aware of \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerning online chatter\u8221\'20\'1D in connection to the rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here to protect everyone\u8217\'20\'19s First Amendment right to peacefully protest,\u8221\'20\'1D Manger said. \u8220\'20\'1CI urge anyone who is thinking about causing trouble to stay home. We will enforce the law and not tolerate violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrUSCP Prepared for September 18 Demonstration: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OT8FHewII9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OT8FHewII9}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iRMz7WlMiO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iRMz7WlMiO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1437488560823808012?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Manger confirmed that the USCP will temporarily reinstall fencing around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  due to concerns about potential threats on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The fencing was taken down in July, six months after the insurrection, but Manger noted it may need to be reinstalled from time to time to protect the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to reassure everyone these are temporary measures to ensure everyone\u8217\'20\'19s safety,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chief Manger. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are extremely grateful for the support we continue to receive from the local community and our Congressional stakeholders as we carry out our critical mission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  is speaking at a Guardian Live event to Jonathan Freedland, and she has been giving her reaction to the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo you ask if I\u8217\'20\'19m surprised or discouraged. I\u8217\'20\'19m neither. I\u8217\'20\'19m not surprised because I\u8217\'20\'19ve been involved in the women\u8217\'20\'19s movement, the civil rights movement. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the forces that are arrayed against progress when it comes to women\u8217\'20\'19s autonomy, when it comes to the advancement of civil and political and economic rights. I know very well that the other side never gives up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are relentless in their view of what is a properly constructed society, and in that view, white men are at the very top and nobody else is even close.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 At a Guardian Live online discussion, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was asked by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jonathan Freedland whether she would have advised \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  not to have gone ahead with the Afghan withdrawal if she had been in the administration.\par \par \uc2 In her reply, Clinton staunchly defended Biden, putting all the blame on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the deal he made with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  in Doha in February 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think he had that choice,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that it was way too far gone, and I respect the decision to leave. In effect, President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hands were tied because the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  had made it very clear, there would be a ceasefire with respect to the American presence in Afghanistan, not only the military but also the civilian presence which was considerable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut if there was any effort to go back on the deal that Trump had made, then that ceasefire would end. And that would have put President Biden in an impossible position because I believe that our casualties, both military and civilian, would have increased dramatically. And it would have required either withdrawing in the face of greater casualties or putting in more troops which there was no appetite for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the House Foreign Affairs Committee, \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2  has pushed back against Republican attacks on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the withdrawal and evacuation.\par \par \uc2 He has pointed repeatedly to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s deal with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  in February 2020, in which the US agreed to withdraw its troops by 1 May this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe inherited a deadline. We did not inherit a plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans attack Blinken over handling of Afghanistan withdrawal\par \par \uc2 Secretary of State \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2  is being lambasted by Republicans at the House Foreign Affairs Committee for the handling of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan and subsequent evacuation.\par \par \uc2 Michael McCaul, the ranking Republican on the committee, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis, in my judgment, is not only disgraceful. It also dishonors the men and women who served our nation so bravely. Mr Secretary, the American people don\u8217\'20\'19t like to lose, especially not to the terrorists, but that is exactly what has happened. This has emboldened the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  and our adversaries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo make matters worse, we abandoned Americans behind enemy lines, we left behind the interpreters who you, Mr Secretary, and the President, both promised to protect. I could summarize this in one word: Betrayal,\u8221\'20\'1D McCaul added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe America I know keeps its promises. The most important promise in our military is no man left behind, no one left behind. But you broke this promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Simone Biles and other Olympians to testify before \uc2 Senate judiciary committee\par \par \uc2 Olympian Simone Biles will testify before the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  on Wednesday in an oversight hearing into the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdereliction of duty\u8221\'20\'1D in its failure to properly investigate the sexual abuse allegations against former \uc2 USA Gymnastics\uc2  national team doctor Larry Nassar.\par \par \uc2 Biles will be joined on the panel by McKayla Maroney, Maggie Nichols, and Aly Raisman . FBI director Christopher Wray and Department of Justice Inspector General Michael Horowitz will also testify.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Olympic and world champion gymnasts Simone Biles, McKayla Maroney, Maggie Nichols, and Aly Raisman to testify at Wednesday's \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  hearing on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 's dereliction of duty in the Nassar case.\par \par \uc2 DOJ IG Horowitz and \uc2 FBI\uc2  Dir. Wray to also testify.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  (@JudiciaryDems) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryDems/status/1437470371742093317?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The hearing comes after Horowitz\u8217\'20\'19s office found that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  made multiple serious failures during its investigation of the allegations against Nasser and failed to treat them with the \u8220\'20\'1Cutmost seriousness and urgency that they deserved and required.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following the release of the report, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  rebuked the involved officers, saying in a statement that their conduct was \u8220\'20\'1Cinexcusable and a discredit to this organization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Based on statements released by members of the committee ahead of the hearing, Wray can expect to face tough questions about what change the department has made to ensure the failures outline in the report do not happen again.\par \par \uc2 Nassar was ultimately convicted in federal and state courts after hundreds of girls and women came forward to publicly accuse him of sexual abuse. He is now serving what will amount to life in prison.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Echoing his comments last week while surveying the damage caused by Hurricane Ida, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized the need to address climate change through his Build Back Better agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a Democrat thing, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a Republican thing. It\u8217\'20\'19s a weather thing,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said while receiving a briefing on wildfires in Boise, Idaho.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a reality. It\u8217\'20\'19s serious. And we can do this. We can do this. And in the process of building back, we can create jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden calls for new jobs and investments to combat wildfires: "It's not a Democrat thing, it's not a Republican thing. It's a weather thing. It's a reality. It's serious." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vPv9CVkRwY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vPv9CVkRwY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TCO7O2XCeo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TCO7O2XCeo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1437484672574005253?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now getting a briefing on wildfires from state and federal officials at the National Interagency Fire Center in Boise, Idaho.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  getting a wildfire briefing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NIFC_Fire?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NIFC_Fire}}}\uc2  in Boise, ID with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovernorLittle?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GovernorLittle}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6xaTaDUiXW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6xaTaDUiXW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meghan Hays (@MegHays46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MegHays46/status/1437479180820639747?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived in Boise, Idaho, where he will receive a briefing from state and federal officials on wildfire preparedness and response efforts.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden arrives in Boise, greeted by the city\u8217\'20\'19s Mayor Lauren McLean {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wUXNKOYvCj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wUXNKOYvCj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mario Parker (@MarioDParker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarioDParker/status/1437476146984062978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 After the briefing, the president will fly on to Sacramento, California, where he will get an update on how the region has been affected by recent wildfires.\par \par \uc2 Biden will also participate in a campaign event this evening with Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , one day ahead of the California recall election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  expressed gratitude for the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  after officers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2021/sep/13/texas-abortion-ruling-supreme-court-biden-wildfire-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-613f63648f08c56a6ed02ab9#block-613f63648f08c56a6ed02ab9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  a man for illegally carrying weapons near the DNC headquarters in Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are thankful for \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  containing this threat, and can\u8217\'20\'19t comment further on the specifics of this ongoing investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D Sam Cornale, the DNC executive director, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDNC employees are real human beings who fight tirelessly for a better America, and their safety, security, and well-being - physical, mental and emotional - are the top priorities of DNC leadership. This suspect\u8217\'20\'19s apparent views are despicable, and violence and white supremacy have no place in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to a source familiar with the situation, there is currently no indication that the incident is \u8220\'20\'1Crelated to any particular interest in the DNC\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The USCP previously said it was unclear whether the man who was arrested, identified as 44-year-old Donald Craighead of Oceanside, California, had been planning to attend the Saturday rally in support of Capitol insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 A hospital in upstate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  will at least temporarily stop delivering babies later this month, after too many employees resigned over a Covid-19 vaccination mandate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are unable to safely staff the service after 24 September,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UlBCWnhLIwA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gerald Cayer}}}\uc2 , chief executive of the Lewis County Health System, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe number of resignations received leaves us no choice but to pause delivering babies at Lewis county general hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid alarm over the highly infectious Delta variant and continued evidence that vaccines are both safe and effective, New York state has required healthcare workers to be vaccinated against Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The mandate makes room for medical exemptions but excludes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crainsnewyork.com/health-care/new-york-nixes-religious-exemption-covid-19-vaccine-mandate-health-care-workers?adobe_mc=MCMID%3D21378480766757417774179795114485939016%7CMCORGID%3D138FFF2554E6E7220A4C98C6%2540AdobeOrg%7CTS%3D1630426930&CSAuthResp=1%3A%3A264630%3A23%3A24%3Asuccess%3A18B36EFE6EF19126F9F5FEA26808FC36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 religious ones}}}\uc2 . Hospitals and nursing homes must comply by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.ny.gov/news/governor-cuomo-announces-covid-19-vaccination-mandate-healthcare-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 27 September}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nearly three-fourths of staff in the Lewis County Health System have received the jab, including 30 employees after the mandate was announced in August.\par \par \uc2 But another 30 have resigned \u8211\'20\'13 21 from clinical areas \u8211\'20\'13 and 165 remain unvaccinated, leaders say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Essential health services are at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D Cayer said. \u8220\'20\'1CNot because of the mandate. The mandate ensures we will have a healthy workforce and that we are not responsible for transmission in or out of our facilities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/new-york-hospital-babies-staff-quit-vaccine-mandate-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York hospital to stop delivering babies as staff quit over vaccine rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will reportedly nominate Georgetown professor Alvaro Bedoya, a leading privacy expert, as a Democratic commissioner at the Federal Trade Commission, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/biden-to-tap-privacy-hawk-for-ftc-post-928e807e-14f0-49ba-9585-50c9df171a04.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, Bedoya would solidify a Democratic majority on the five-person commission \u8211\'20\'13 replacing Rohit Chopra, a Democrat Biden has tapped to head the \uc2 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nomination comes after Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/14/lina-khan-big-tech-ftc-antitrust"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed}}}\uc2  antitrust expert Lina Khan to chair the FTC. Bedoya represents a similarly progressive choice in the privacy space.\par \par \uc2 Bedoya founded the Center on Privacy & Technology at Georgetown and previously worked as chief counsel of the Senate Judiciary privacy subcommittee, specializing in issues surrounding facial recognition and digital surveillance.\par \par \uc2 Progressive nominees at the FTC could make a large impact as Big Tech faces a reckoning from legislators surrounding alleged anticompetitive practices and unabated surveillance technology.\par \par \uc2 The FTC did not respond to request for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 AOC and Manchin square off\par \par \uc2 The New York congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alexandria-ocasio-cortez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez}}}\uc2  has fired back at the West Virginia senator Joe Manchin for referring to her as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe young lady\u8221\'20\'1D, in the latest escalation in a bitter intra-party spat over the size and scale of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 social spending bill.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda depends on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 ability to overcome internal divisions and enact what would be the largest expansion of the social safety net in generations.\par \par \uc2 Manchin is among the chief obstacles to passing the mooted $3.5tn package. He has said he would not support legislation with such a high price tag. In a Sunday appearance on CNN, Manchin ripped progressives for threatening to sink a bipartisan infrastructure bill if he refuses to support the spending package. Singling out Ocasio-Cortez, Manchin responded to her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1433524952083410949?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claim}}}\uc2  that he meets weekly with oil lobbyists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI keep my door open for everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s totally false. And those types of superlatives, it\u8217\'20\'19s just awful. Continue to divide, divide, divide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that young lady that well. I really don\u8217\'20\'19t. She\u8217\'20\'19s just speculating and saying things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Ocasio-Cortez suggested Manchin was attempting to dismiss a fellow member of Congress as a \u8220\'20\'1Cyoung lady\u8221\'20\'1D because he was beginning to feel the pressure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Washington, I usually know my questions of power are getting somewhere when the powerful stop referring to me as \u8216\'20\'18Congresswoman\u8217\'20\'19 and start referring to me as \u8216\'20\'18young lady\u8217\'20\'19 instead,\u8221\'20\'1D the 31-year-old wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CImagine if every time someone referred to someone as \u8216\'20\'18young lady\u8217\'20\'19 they were responded to by being addressed with their age and gender? They\u8217\'20\'19d be pretty upset if one responded with \u8216\'20\'18the old man\u8217\'20\'19, right? Why this kind of weird, patronizing behavior is so accepted is beyond me! \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-aoc-joe-manchin-infrastructure-spending"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Weird, patronizing behavior\u8217\'20\'19: AOC lets rip at Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18young lady\u8217\'20\'19 remark}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  arrested a man for illegally carrying weapons near the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington. The man, identified as 44-year-old Donald Craighead of Oceanside, California, was arrested for possession of prohibited weapons after officers found multiple knives in his truck. Craighead\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle was painted with a swastika and other white supremacist symbols. The arrest comes amid intensifying security concerns about the upcoming \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally that is being held in support of Capitol insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 * Justice Amy Coney Barrett defended the integrity of the supreme court, amid widespread criticism of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect. \u8220\'20\'1CMy goal today is to convince you that this court is not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks,\u8221\'20\'1D the conservative justice said during a Sunday event at the McConnell Center at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CJudicial philosophies are not the same as political parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is traveling to Idaho and California today to receive briefings on wildfire preparedness and response efforts. The president will also attend a campaign event with California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election. The election will be held tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol fencing will go back up later this week, USCP chief confirms\par \par \uc2 The chief of US Capitol Police, Tom Manger, confirmed that the fencing around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  will go back up later this week, as law enforcement officials prepare for the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fence will go up a day or two before, and if everything goes well, it will come down very soon after,\u8221\'20\'1D Manger said on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Capitol Police Chief Tom Manger on security measures for September 18th 'Justice for J6' rally: "The fence will go up a day or two before and if everything goes well, it will come down very soon after." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/olVblOPyEt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/olVblOPyEt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1437448167491002375?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The USCP chief was speaking after briefing congressional leaders about the agency\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Coperational plan\u8221\'20\'1D for security ahead of the rally, which is being held in support of the insurrectionists who carried out the Capitol attack on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey gave us a good briefing,\u8221\'20\'1D Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re handling this in a very professional, thorough way, and I think they\u8217\'20\'19re much better prepared than things were before January 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manger also noted that he will hold a press conference a day or two before the rally to give the public more information about how officers are preparing for the event.\par \par \uc2 The fencing around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/07/09/1014561578/6-months-after-the-insurrection-the-remaining-capitol-fencing-comes-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came down in July}}}\uc2 , six months after the deadly insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Top security officials in Congress are expected to reinstall fencing around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and authorize the use of deadly force ahead of a planned rally by far-right {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  supporters next weekend demanding the release of rioters arrested in connection with the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The officials, however, had no plans so far to request the national guard, and were not pushing for such a request, principally because the threat assessment did not warrant their deployment, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The Justice for J6 rally on 18 September is being organized by the Trump operative Matt Braynard and his organization Look Ahead America. It is being held to demand that the justice department drop charges against nearly 600 people charged in connection with the Capitol attack which the group calls \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-violent protesters\u8221\'20\'1D, despite widespread violence and five deaths during the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The Senate sergeant-at-arms, Lt Gen Karen Gibson, House sergeant-at-arms, Maj Gen William Walker, and US Capitol police chief, Thomas Manger, are expected to approve fencing to form the backbone of their security response, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/12/capitol-fence-congress-january-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top security officials to reinstall Capitol fence ahead of far-right rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The top four congressional leaders -- House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , House minority leader Kevin McCarthy, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer and Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  -- are now receiving a briefing on security preparations for this Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-08-12/rally-for-jailed-jan-6-rioters-prompts-capitol-security-concern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice for J6}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D rally, per CNN.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe big four congressional leaders \u8212\'20\'14 Pelosi, Schumer, McCarthy and McConnell \u8212\'20\'14 all getting briefed now about the security preparations and plans for Sept. 18 rally\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1437438692226908164?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The briefing had been scheduled before the \uc2 US Capitol Police{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2021/sep/13/texas-abortion-ruling-supreme-court-biden-wildfire-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-613f63648f08c56a6ed02ab9#block-613f63648f08c56a6ed02ab9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  officers had arrested a man carrying illegal weapons near the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters early this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the 6 January attack on the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  has instructed telecom and social media companies last week to preserve records of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , according to a source familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The move positions the select committee on the doorstep of the Oval Office as it pursues a far-reaching inquiry into whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  and his White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/capitol-riot-white-house-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped plan or had advance knowledge}}}\uc2  of the insurrection perpetrated by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s supporters.\par \par \uc2 House select committee investigators signaled their intention to examine potential involvement by the Trump White House and House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  when they last week made a series of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/25/capitol-attack-committee-records-requests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 records demands}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/trump-capitol-attack-committee-phone-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 records preservation}}}\uc2  requests for Trump officials connected to the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 In the records preservation requests, the select committee instructed 35 telecom and social media companies to avoid destroying communications logs of several hundred people, including the House minority leader, Kevin McCarthy, and 10 House Republicans, in case it later issues subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/mark-meadows-records-trump-capitol-attack-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff is target of Capitol attack records request}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 There appeared to be more cameras going up around the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  this morning, as law enforcement officials prepare for the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 An NBC News reporter shared a photo of the increased security measures on Capitol Hill:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis morning preparations seem to be underway for heightened security ahead of the planned rally this weekend Sept 18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eFAyxfCbi9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eFAyxfCbi9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Haley Talbot (@haleytalbotnbc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haleytalbotnbc/status/1437413229660151813?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Craighead said he was \u8220\'20\'1Con patrol\u8221\'20\'1D after \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  officers discovered illegal weapons in his vehicle, according to the USCP statement.\par \par \uc2 Craighead also began talking about white supremacist ideology. His pickup truck was painted with a swastika and other white supremacist symbols.\par \par \uc2 The USCP said it was unclear whether Craighead planned to attend the upcoming \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally, which is being held in support of the insurrectionists who carried out the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol Police arrests man near DNC headquarters amid concerns over far-right rally\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  arrested a man early this morning near the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Washington.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscp.gov/media-center/press-releases/uscp-officers-arrest-california-man-bayonet-machete"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  from the USCP, 44-year-old Donald Craighead of Oceanside, California was arrested for possession of prohibited weapons after officers found multiple knives in his truck.\par \par \uc2 enltrUSCP Officers Arrest California Man with Bayonet & Machete: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0mhsoOC8vX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0mhsoOC8vX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9SR1NXsJV6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9SR1NXsJV6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1437423592480911369?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 An officer noticed Craighead\u8217\'20\'19s pickup truck while on patrol around midnight. The vehicle had swastika and other white supremacist symbols painted on it, and it did not have a license plate.\par \par \uc2 When officers looked inside the vehicle, they saw a bayonet and machete, which are illegal in DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is good police work plain and simple,\u8221\'20\'1D USCP chief Tom Manger said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe applaud the officers\u8217\'20\'19 keen observation and the teamwork that resulted in this arrest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The news comes amid intensifying concerns over the upcoming \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally, an event being held in support of the rioters who carried out the Capitol insurrection. The rally is scheduled to take place in Washington on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump refused to condemn Capitol rioters, book says\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump declined her chief of staff\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion she condemn rioters who attacked the US Capitol on 6 January, according to a new book by the spurned aid who also says the former first lady believed her husband\u8217\'20\'19s lie that his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the result of electoral fraud.\par \par \uc2 According to Politico, reporting the first details of the hotly anticipated book, I\u8217\'20\'19ll Take Your Questions Now: What I Saw in The Trump White House, \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2  also compares Melania Trump to Marie Antoinette.\par \par \uc2 The first lady was like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe doomed French queen\u8221\'20\'1D, Grisham reportedly writes. \u8220\'20\'1CDismissive. Defeated. Detached.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Politico reported that on 6 January, as Trump supporters attempted to violently overturn the election, Grisham texted Melania Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you want to tweet that peaceful protests are the right of every American, but there is no place for lawlessness and violence?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A minute later, \u8220\'20\'1CMelania replied with a one-word answer: \u8216\'20\'18No.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/13/melania-trump-stephanie-grisham-capitol-attack-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania Trump refused to condemn rioters who attacked Capitol, book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden heads to Idaho and California for wildfire briefing and recall event\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just boarded Air Force One to travel to Boise, Idaho, where the president will receive a briefing on wildfire preparedness and response efforts.\par \par \uc2 After the briefing, Biden will fly on to Sacramento, California, where he will receive an update on how recent wildfires have affected the region.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden boards AF1 for his first trip to the West Coast, which will take him to Boise, Idaho for a briefing on wildfires & Sacramento, Calif. to survey wildfire damage, before heading to Long Beach to campaign for Calif. Gov. Gavin Newsom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bh00LMfOny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bh00LMfOny}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexandra Jaffe (@ajjaffe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ajjaffe/status/1437408733806608397?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the trip, President Biden will see firsthand the significant physical, human, and economic costs of wildfires,\u8221\'20\'1D a White House official told the press pool.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs one in three Americans are impacted by the increasing frequency of ferocity of extreme weather events, he will reiterate the message he shared on the east coast last week: the climate crisis is code red.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This evening, the president will participate in a campaign event with California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election.\par \par \uc2 The election will be held tomorrow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/california-recall-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Recent polls}}}\uc2  indicate the Democratic governor has mitigated the threat of being removed from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The cloud-based software giant \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  is offering to help relocate employees out of Texas following the state\u8217\'20\'19s enactment of its extreme new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly personal issues\u8221\'20\'1D that the law creates, a message to the company\u8217\'20\'19s entire workforce sent late on Friday said any employee and their family wishing to move elsewhere would receive assistance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COhana if you want to move we\u8217\'20\'19ll help you exit TX. Your choice,\u8221\'20\'1D the Salesforce chief executive, \uc2 Marc Benioff\uc2 , said in a tweet featuring a CNBC article about the offer, and using a term common in Hawaii for \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In its message to workers, \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , which is headquartered in California, did not directly mention Texas, where about 2,000 of its 56,000 global workers are based, or take a stance on the law. But its intention was clear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are incredibly personal issues that directly impact many of us \u8211\'20\'13 especially women,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/11/salesforce-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Salesforce offers to help staff leave Texas as \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law takes effect}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Amy Coney Barrett spoke on Sunday at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://louisville.edu/mcconnellcenter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McConnell Center}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2 , a venue created by and named for \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican leader in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, McConnell ruthlessly blocked \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s final pick for the court, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , claiming it was too close to an election and the next president should decide.\par \par \uc2 Between 2017 and 2020, McConnell shepherded through three picks made by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Barrett was the last \u8211\'20\'13 in place of \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , a heroine to US liberals \u8211\'20\'13 shortly before an election Trump lost.\par \par \uc2 McConnell, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2021/09/12/justice-amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-decisions-arent-political/8310849002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisville Courier-Journal}}}\uc2  reported, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2021/09/12/justice-amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-decisions-arent-political/8310849002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  Barrett for not trying to \u8220\'20\'1Clegislate from the bench\u8221\'20\'1D and for being from \u8220\'20\'1CMiddle America\u8221\'20\'1D. Barrett is from Indiana and, unlike the other eight justices, did not attend Harvard or Yale.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barrett defends integrity of the court after widely criticized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Amy Coney Barrett defended the integrity of the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest court yesterday, almost two weeks after she and four of her conservative colleagues allowed a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy goal today is to convince you that this court is not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks,\u8221\'20\'1D Barrett {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2021/09/12/justice-amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-decisions-arent-political/8310849002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  during a Sunday event at the McConnell Center at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJudicial philosophies are not the same as political parties,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing: Sometimes, I don\u8217\'20\'19t like the results of my decisions. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not my job to decide cases based on the outcome I want.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett speaks to an audience at University of Louisville McConnell Center. Photograph: Timothy D Easley/AP\par \par \uc2 Barrett was confirmed to the supreme court just days before the 2020 presidential election, even though Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  had refused to consider \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court nominee in 2016 because it was an election year.\par \par \uc2 Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation shifted the ideological balance of the court, given that she replaced the late liberal justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 . That shift enabled the 5-4 ruling in the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s Louisville appearance was picketed by protesters who expressed outraged over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision. One of the protesters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2021/09/12/justice-amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-decisions-arent-political/8310849002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Louisville Courier Journal}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWith what\u8217\'20\'19s been happening in Texas, I don\u8217\'20\'19t want it to spread to Kentucky. \u8230\'20\'26 And so, we\u8217\'20\'19re just coming to let Mitch know how a lot of citizens feel about this issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210913eh9d001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
