\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden tells Republicans threatening to sue over vaccine mandate: \u8216\'20\'18Have at it\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington (earlier) and Gabrielle Canon in Los Angeles (now) \par \uc2 8,401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2021\par 00:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 South Carolina and Arizona governors decry \u8216\'20\'18big government overreach\u8217\'20\'19 after president orders larger businesses to demand employees be vaccinated\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for me tonight. Thanks for reading along! Here\u8217\'20\'19s some of what we covered:\par \par \uc2 * New details uncovered by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  suggest that the US military mistakenly killed civilians and children with a drone officials claimed had taken out Islamic State militants. The target, now identified as Zemari Ahmadi, was a US aid group worker and reportedly was distributing water to neighbors, not transporting weaponry or explosives.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration appealed a ruling from a US district court judge who put the Daca program on pause in July.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Department of Education\uc2  is investigating Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban on mask mandates in schools, citing its potential for discrimination against students with disabilities. The agency is also investigating five other states with similar rules.\par \par \uc2 * Jacob Chansley \u8212\'20\'14 the so-called QAnon Shaman \u8212\'20\'14 will have to await sentencing for his part in the Capitol Riot after a federal judge denied his request for pre-trial release. Chansley, who was pictured wearing horns on his head as he stormed the building, pleaded guilty to obstructing an official proceeding last week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/jacob-chansley-us-capitol-attack-pleads-guilty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Capitol rioter photographed wearing horns pleads guilty}}}\par \par \uc2 * A federal appeals court struck down Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, ruling that the ban on the procedure after a fetal heartbeat can be detected \u8212\'20\'14 near the six-week mark \u8212\'20\'14 was \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutionally unsound\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 See you next time! Until then:\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a3PWIGfB6Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a3PWIGfB6Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ladies and gentlemen, the weekend ?? (@CraigWeekend) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigWeekend/status/1436466515608432645?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law was blocked by a federal appeals court today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opn.ca6.uscourts.gov/opinions.pdf/21a0215p-06.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling that the measure was \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutionally unsound\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The law banned abortions after a fetal heartbeat can be detected, which typically occurs around 6 weeks into the pregnancy \u8212\'20\'14 often before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough this circuit\u8217\'20\'19s recent\u8212\'20\'14and alarming\u8212\'20\'14decisions have broadened the extent to which the government may impede a person\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to choose whether to carry a pregnancy to term, the law remains clear that if a regulation is a substantial obstacle to a woman seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is invalid,\u8221\'20\'1D the court said in the ruling.\par \par \uc2 enltrAppeals court strikes down Tennessee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, with Judge Thapar (a Trump appointee) writing lengthy partial dissent taking aim at Roe v. Wade: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bZqizndvtJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bZqizndvtJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/J1kcQRDBMn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/J1kcQRDBMn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1436388167616188416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a huge win for pregnant people in Tennessee,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rabia Muqaddam, staff attorney at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we are relieved that the court has reinstated a full block on these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, we must remain vigilant,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, noting that a case that makes it before the conservative-majority supreme court could overturn Roe v. Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must act swiftly to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and declare \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans like these illegal by passing the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The decision follows last week\u8217\'20\'19s controversial ruling from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  over a similar law in Texas, that granted victory to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates and allowed the law to be enforced.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-greg-abbott-texas-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC on Texas governor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18disgusting\u8217\'20\'19 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  remarks: \u8216\'20\'18He is not familiar with a female body\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The man known as the \u8220\'20\'1CQAnon Shaman\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 who was pictured during the Capitol riot with his face painted underneath a fur hat adorned with horns \u8212\'20\'14 has been denied temporary release.\par \par \uc2 Jacob Chansley pleaded guilty to obstructing an official proceeding last week and asked to be freed from prison while he awaits sentencing. Today, a federal judge denied that request in a 9-page order, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cno condition or combination of conditions would ensure that he would not flee\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr"there is no doubt that he is a mascot for thee QAnon movement. Hundreds of attendees joined Chansley's September 3, 2021 plea-agreement hearing on the public access line, and at least once this Court's proceedings where interrupted with shouts of 'Freedom!\u8217\'20\'19" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1iAfHIldKa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1iAfHIldKa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1436432898958188546?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Chansley was diagnosed with transient schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, depression and anxiety during his pretrial detention, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-judge-denies-capitol-rioters-request-temporary-release-prison-2021-09-10/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . He faces between 41 and 51 months in prison.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Department of Education\uc2  to investigate Florida mask mandate\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban on mask mandates in schools \u8212\'20\'14which penalizes school systems that require students to mask-up to stop the spread of Covid \u8212\'20\'14 is now under investigation by the \uc2 US Department of Education\u8217\'20\'19s Office for Civil Rights\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The order, which was issued by Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and is currently being challenged in court, will be evaluated by the federal agency for whether it fails to meet the needs of students with disabilities.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The civil rights arm of the \uc2 U.S. Department of Education\uc2  opens investigation into Florida\u8217\'20\'19s mask mandate ban in schools.\par \par \uc2 More on that announcement here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gBhhxjHxoi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gBhhxjHxoi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ana Ceballos (@anaceballos_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/anaceballos_/status/1436447086627758099?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 At the end of August, the agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/news/press-releases/department-educations-office-civil-rights-opens-investigations-five-states-regarding-prohibitions-universal-indoor-masking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it was launching directed investigations into whether 5 states \u8212\'20\'14 Iowa, Oklahoma, South Carolina, Tennessee, and Utah \u8212\'20\'14 were discriminating against students with disabilities with their anti-mask-mandate orders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department has heard from parents from across the country \u8211\'20\'13 particularly parents of students with disabilities and with underlying medical conditions \u8211\'20\'13 about how state bans on universal indoor masking are putting their children at risk and preventing them from accessing in-person learning equally,\u8221\'20\'1D said US Secretary of Education \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2  in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s simply unacceptable that state leaders are putting politics over the health and education of the students they took an oath to serve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Florida was initially left off the list because its order wasn\u8217\'20\'19t being enforced, the result of a ruling from Circuit Judge John C. Cooper last month, that the state couldn\u8217\'20\'19t continue penalizing schools. Earlier today however, Florida was granted approval to start enforcing the order again while the appeals process continues. The investigation announcement from the Department of Education came just hours after the appeals court decision was issued.\par \par \uc2 In a letter s ent to the Florida Department of Education Commissioner \uc2 Richard Corcoran\uc2  today, the agency wrote that it \u8220\'20\'1Cis concerned that Florida\u8217\'20\'19s policy requiring public schools and school districts to allow parents to opt their children out of mask mandates may be preventing schools in Florida from meeting their legal obligations not to discriminate based on disability and from providing an equal educational opportunity to students with disabilities who are at heightened risk of severe illness from COVID-19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zebras may still on the loose in the suburbs of Washington DC, but at least one thing is now clear \u8212\'20\'14 Democratic Congresswoman \uc2 Eleanor Holmes Norton\uc2  did not set them free.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy alibi is solid\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/eleanor-holmes-norton-zebras_n_613b7828e4b0628d095ae4fe?ncid=engmodushpmg00000004"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the Huffington Post, noting that she was home enjoying time with family last weekend when the striped equines began their adventure.\par \par \uc2 enltrFive zebras are on the loose in Prince George\u8217\'20\'19s Co. right now!\par \par \uc2 Nearby resident Paul Curling shared this video of a zebra seen from his backyard.\par \par \uc2 Animal services says they escaped from a farm last week near Duley Station Road in Upper Marlboro.\par \par \uc2 The farm has a permit for them. ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dY7XDx6vfx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dY7XDx6vfx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Roussey (@tomroussey7news) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tomroussey7news/status/1435675637289738244?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The DC delegate was accused by a member of the public as commentary about her battle to make DC a state.\par \par \uc2 From HuffPost:\par \par \uc2 Norton said a member of the public accused her of letting the zebras free by pointing out that she has historically valued the principle of \u8220\'20\'1Cconsent of the governed,\u8221\'20\'1D or the philosophy that a government\u8217\'20\'19s right to use state power is justified only when consented to by the people or society over which that political power is exercised.\par \par \uc2 Norton said it\u8217\'20\'19s true that she values that philosophy, particularly in her fight for D.C. statehood. She added that she opposes unnecessary fences, too.\par \par \uc2 For those reasons, Norton said, she can see why someone would accuse her of setting the zebras free. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can understand why the charge was made,\u8221\'20\'1D said the D.C. delegate. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope the owners find the zebras and that all involved live long, full lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/10/zebras-escape-maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Escaped zebras bamboozle Maryland officials: \u8216\'20\'18They\u8217\'20\'19re just too fast\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has challenged the ruling by a US District judge in Texas, who found the Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals program (or DACA) to be unlawful.\par \par \uc2 In July, Judge \uc2 Andrew Hanen\uc2  ruled against the Obama-era program and barred the government from approving new applications. Current participants were allowed to continue as litigation progressed.\par \par \uc2 Today the Biden Administration\u8217\'20\'19s filed a notice to appeal, according to CNN, moving on previous comments from the president that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot letting this go\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey come here with really no choice and they\u8217\'20\'19re good, good people,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said during a CNN townhall of the hundreds of thousands of people participating in the program, referred to as Dreamers.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/18/daca-dreamers-us-immigration-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Explainer: what is Daca and who are the Dreamers?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle Canon here, taking you through the news for the rest of the afternoon from the west coast.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/world/asia/us-air-strike-drone-kabul-afghanistan-isis.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  has shed light on an American drone strike in Afghanistan \u8212\'20\'14 one of the last fired in the war that stretched over 20 years \u8212\'20\'14 and raised new questions about whether it was justified.\par \par \uc2 The missile launched at a vehicle by the US military killed 10 people in Kabul on August 29, including 7 children, according to the report. Reporters also discovered that officials did not identify who the driver before firing, even though they later alleged the target taken out was ISIS affiliated.\par \par \uc2 Now revealed to be Zemari Ahmadi, a US aid group worker, interviews and surveillance footage reviewed by the \uc2 NYT\uc2  suggests he may have been taking colleagues to and from work when he died in the blast, and that the large containers identified in his car were filled with water to be distributed to neighbors.\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 NYT\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 According to one of Mr. Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s passengers, a colleague who regularly commuted with him, the ride home was filled with their usual laughing and banter, but with one difference: Mr. Ahmadi kept the radio silent, as he was afraid of getting in trouble with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHe liked happy music,\u8221\'20\'1D the colleague said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat day, we couldn\u8217\'20\'19t play any in the car.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ahmadi dropped off his three passengers, and then headed for his home near the airport. \u8220\'20\'1CI asked him to come in for a bit, but he said he was tired,\u8221\'20\'1D the last passenger said.\par \par \uc2 Although U.S. officials said that at that point they still knew little about Mr. Ahmadi\u8217\'20\'19s identity, they had become convinced that the white sedan he was driving posed an imminent threat to troops at the airport.\par \par \uc2 When Mr. Ahmadi pulled into the courtyard of his home \u8212\'20\'14 which officials said was different than the alleged ISIS safe house \u8212\'20\'14 the tactical commander made the decision to strike his vehicle, launching a Hellfire missile at around 4:50 p.m.\par \par \uc2 Although the target was now inside a densely populated residential area, the drone operator quickly scanned and saw only a single adult male greeting the vehicle, and therefore assessed with \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable certainty\u8221\'20\'1D that no women, children or noncombatants would be killed, U.S. officials said.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/world/asia/us-air-strike-drone-kabul-afghanistan-isis.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Gabrielle Canon, will take over for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Republican leaders are threatening lawsuits over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to order employers with 100 or more workers to establish vaccine mandates or require regular coronavirus testing. The proposal is part of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new six-pronged strategy to boost vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Americans when he was elected that he would not impose vaccine mandates. He lied,\u8221\'20\'1D said Republican National Committee chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhen his decree goes into effect, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  will sue the administration to protect Americans and their liberties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden responded to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 threats of lawsuits with this message: \u8220\'20\'1CHave at it.\u8221\'20\'1D While visiting a middle school in Washington this morning, the president said, \u8220\'20\'1CI am so disappointed that, particularly some Republican governors, have been so cavalier with the health of these kids, so cavalier with the health of their communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * A Florida appeals court handed Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  a victory in his battle to ban mask mandates in schools. After a county court judge blocked the controversial policy from going into effect earlier this week, the appeals court ruled that the ban could be implemented as the case makes its way through the legal system.\par \par \uc2 * Another 21 US citizens left Afghanistan today, as the Biden administration continues its efforts to evacuate Americans even after the military mission in Kabul formally ended last week. A spokesperson for the National Security Council said the Americans left Afghanistan \u8220\'20\'1Cboth on a chartered \uc2 Qatar Airways\uc2  flight from Kabul and via overland passage to a neighboring country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * US-bound flights carrying Afghan refugees were temporarily paused after four cases of measles were detected among the passengers. The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , said the flights were paused \u8220\'20\'1Cout of an abundance of caution,\u8221\'20\'1D and the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  are now contact-tracing the cases.\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The thorn in Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s side has been Leon county court judge John Cooper, who first ruled for a group of parents on 2 September that the governor\u8217\'20\'19s order banning school mask mandates overstepped his constitutional authority.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Cooper lifted the automatic stay on his own ruling that came into effect when DeSantis appealed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUpon our review of the trial court\u8217\'20\'19s final judgment and the operative pleadings, we have serious doubts about standing, jurisdiction and other threshold matters,\u8221\'20\'1D today\u8217\'20\'19s appeals court ruling stated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese doubts significantly militate against the likelihood of the appellees\u8217\'20\'19 [parents\u8217\'20\'19] ultimate success in this appeal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In plain English, it means DeSantis has the authority to at least try to ban mask mandates in schools while the case works its way further through the court system, although the districts are unlikely to comply.\par \par \uc2 And in a further twist on Friday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  promised to pick up the tab for any financial penalties DeSantis imposes on the defiant districts through a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/news/press-releases/us-department-education-announces-new-grant-program-provide-funding-school-districts-being-penalized-implementing-covid-safety-measures?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal grant program}}}\uc2  by the department of education.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be thanking districts for using proven strategies that will keep schools open and safe, not punishing them,\u8221\'20\'1D education secretary \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida appeals court gives DeSantis a win in effort to ban school mask mandates\par \par \uc2 A Florida appeals court on Friday tilted the pendulum back towards the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/08/florida-mask-mandate-schools-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crusade to permanently ban school districts from imposing mask mandates}}}\uc2  on students and staff.\par \par \uc2 The panel of three judges - two of them appointed by the previous Republican governor \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , and the other by DeSantis himself - overturned a district court judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling from two days earlier that prevented the state from penalizing districts with such mandates.\par \par \uc2 Their decision effectively clears the way for the \uc2 Florida department of education\uc2  to resume its withholding of state funds from districts that continue to defy the governor.\par \par \uc2 So far 13 districts, covering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/25/florida-schools-mask-mandates-coronavirus-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 2.8m school-age students}}}\uc2 , have mask mandates, with only a medical opt-out, and are not expected to change course despite today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 The see-saw legal battle centers on DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 30 July executive order that sought to make mask mandates illegal, and a subsequent lawsuit filed by a group of concerned parents claiming their children would suffer \u8220\'20\'1Cirreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D as a result.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/25/florida-schools-mask-mandates-coronavirus-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Half of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 2.8m public school students now face mask mandates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has not yet gotten his third coronavirus vaccine shot, even though he received his second dose in January, according to \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Health experts are recommending Americans seek a vaccine booster eight months after their second shot, meaning the president should be getting his third dose soon.\par \par \uc2 Asked if and when Biden might get his booster shot, Psaki said, \u8220\'20\'1CHe will. He has not yet gotten it yet. We\u8217\'20\'19ll wait until it\u8217\'20\'19s widely available, which we expect to be soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki says President Biden will get a COVID vaccine booster shot, but "we'll wait until it's widely available, which we expect to be soon" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8Dkty38jZD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8Dkty38jZD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1436417331958255617?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 One reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is considering requiring coronavirus vaccinations for domestic flights in the US.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary did not rule out the possibility, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are always looking at more we can do to protect and save lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has already mandated mask usage for flights, trains and public transportation to limit the spread of the virus from traveling.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  confirmed that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Chinese President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  spoke for more than 90 minutes yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the two leaders had discussed coronavirus and its origins, the press secretary confirmed they had, but she did not offer any details on their comments.\par \par \uc2 The White House released a readout of the conversation yesterday, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThe two leaders had a broad, strategic discussion in which they discussed areas where our interests converge, and areas where our interests, values, and perspectives diverge. They agreed to engage on both sets of issues openly and straightforwardly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has previously accused the Chinese government of withholding vital information on the origins of coronavirus, which was first detected in Wuhan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 One reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether the White House was concerned that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new vaccination policies could drive the country further apart, particularly considering Republican governors have threatened to sue over the president\u8217\'20\'19s proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, we do see some loud, vocal opponents of what the president announced yesterday,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not a surprise. It\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate. It\u8217\'20\'19s disappointing. It\u8217\'20\'19s sad, because ultimately these steps will save lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked why Biden changed his mind on vaccine mandates from earlier this year, Psaki said the administration did not anticipate the high level of vaccine opposition once the treatments were deemed safe and made easily available.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 US-bound flights for Afghan refugees 'temporarily paused' due to measles cases\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her (twice-delayed) daily briefing with reporters, and she was asked about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/us-afghan-evacuee-flights-halted-from-two-key-bases/600095828/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  that health concerns have stalled US-bound flights for Afghan refugees.\par \par \uc2 Psaki confirmed that some Afghan refugees\u8217\'20\'19 planes have been \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporarily paused\u8221\'20\'1D because of four diagnosed cases of measles among the passengers.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary noted that refugees coming to the US are required to have their measles vaccination, and she said the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  has already started contact-tracing the cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s violent crackdown on protests against their hardline rule has already led to four documented deaths, according to a \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights official who said the group had used live ammunition, whips and batons to break up demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 Ravina Shamdasani, the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rights spokesperson, told a briefing in Geneva that it had also received reports of house-to-house searches for those who participated in the protests.\par \par \uc2 The protests against the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to power, many of which have been led by women fearful of their status under the Islamist group, have been the target of violence in a number of locations and were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/taliban-ban-protests-and-slogans-that-dont-have-their-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally banned this week}}}\uc2  without prior authorisation by the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new interior ministry.\par \par \uc2 Describing the crackdown on dissent as \u8220\'20\'1Csevere\u8221\'20\'1D, Shamdasani also described how journalists covering the demonstrations had faced intimidation, including in one case the threat of \u8220\'20\'1Cbeheading\u8221\'20\'1D, apparently a reference to an incident in which two Afghan journalists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/09/violent-attacks-on-afghan-journalists-by-taliban-prompt-growing-alarm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were detained, flogged and threatened}}}\uc2  earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/10/at-least-four-killed-in-taliban-crackdown-on-protests-says-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least four killed in Taliban crackdown on protests, says UN}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says 21 US citizens left Afghanistan today\par \par \uc2 Another 21 US citizens left Afghanistan today as evacuation efforts continue, according to a new statement from the National Security Council.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday the \uc2 United States government\uc2  facilitated the additional departures of U.S. citizens and lawful permanent residents both on a chartered \uc2 Qatar Airways\uc2  flight from Kabul and via overland passage to a neighboring country,\u8221\'20\'1D NSC spokesperson \uc2 Emily Horne\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Qatar Airways\uc2  flight held 19 U.S. citizens and the party traveling overland included two U.S. citizens and 11 lawful permanent residents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The news comes as the Biden administration has continued to coordinate the evacuation of Americans out of Afghanistan, even though the US military formally ended its mission in Kabul last week.\par \par \uc2 Another chartered \uc2 Qatar Airways\uc2  plane carrying American citizens left Kabul yesterday, which marked the first US-facilitated evacuation flight since the mission concluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s departures demonstrate how we are giving Americans clear and safe options to leave Afghanistan from different locations,\u8221\'20\'1D Horne said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to provide proven options for leaving. It is up to Americans who remain whether they choose to take them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/10/afghanistan-flight-kabul-doha-lands-foreign-passengers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan flight carrying more than 100 foreign passengers lands in Doha}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The sombre ceremonies that take place in New York, Pennsylvania and on the outskirts of Washington every September 11 to mark the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/september11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2001 terrorist attacks}}}\uc2  will take on an extra significance on Saturday morning, as America commemorates the 20th anniversary of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/09/al-qaida-the-terror-group-that-learned-the-secret-of-longevity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 al-Qaida hijackings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/children-september-11-anniversary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 family members}}}\uc2  of the nearly 3,000 victims killed on that day are expected to gather in downtown Manhattan, in a field in Shanksville, and at the Pentagon, where the terrorists crashed the passenger jets they had seized that morning.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will visit all three sites, and will be joined at Ground Zero in New York by \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , whom he served for two terms as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Small memorial ceremonies will be held across the US, and millions are expected to tune in to coverage that will blanket the TV networks throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/10/biden-obama-9-11-anniversary-terror-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden and Obama to attend memorials marking 20th anniversary of 9/11}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arkansas gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , who previously served as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, has released her first television ad, which is entitled \u8220\'20\'1CWho We Are\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll never forget being a student at Little Rock Central High and watching my dad - a Republican governor - and \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  - a Democrat president - hold open the doors for the Little Rock Nine, doors that forty years earlier had been closed to them because they\u8217\'20\'19re Black,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders says in the ad.\par \par \uc2 The Little Rock Nine were a group of Black children who integrated Central high school in 1957. The governor of Arkansas at the time, Orval Faubus, brought in national guard members to block their enrollment.\par \par \uc2 The nine Black students were eventually allowed into the high school with the assistance of \uc2 US Army\uc2  troops, as a violent white mob hurled threats and racist slurs at the children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood triumphed over evil,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders says of the Little Rock Nine in her ad. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is who we are. The radical left wants to teach our kids America is a racist and evil country, but Arkansans are generous, hard-working people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ad concludes with Sanders vowing to \u8220\'20\'1Cdefend our freedom and champion good schools, higher paying jobs, and a better life for all\u8221\'20\'1D. It will debut tomorrow during the Arkansas vs. Texas college football game.\par \par \uc2 To learn more about the Little Rock Nine, read this 2017 piece from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/sep/24/little-rock-arkansas-school-segregation-racism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Little Rock Nine: the day young students shattered racial segregation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor who was once one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s most vocal cheerleaders, urged Republicans to move past the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lies about winning the 2020 election during a stinging speech on Thursday night in California.\par \par \uc2 Using the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  presidential library in Simi Valley as a symbolic backdrop, Christie slammed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing insistence that the election was stolen from him, and told the in-person gathering of party donors: \u8220\'20\'1CWe deserve much better than to be misled by those trying to acquire or hold on to power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  participates in a discussion about his new book at the Washington Post in 2019. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The speech was one of the most damning to date by former allies of Trump, though Christie refrained from mentioning him by name. Instead, he attacked the cult of conspiracy that Trump has fueled with his false election claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to renounce the conspiracy theorists and the truth deniers. The ones who know better and the ones who are just plain nuts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christie, who was a Trump advisor in both the 2016 and 2020 presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to give our supporters facts that will help them put all those fantasies to rest. We need to quit wasting our time, our energy and our credibility on claims that won\u8217\'20\'19t ever convince anyone of anything. Pretending we won when we lost is a waste of time and energy and credibility.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is widely expected to announce he will be running for the White House again in 2024, has embarked on a nationwide tour of sporadic rallies at which he regularly repeats the debunked claims that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 Appearing to address Republican supporters who attend Trump\u8217\'20\'19s events, Christie added: \u8220\'20\'1CNo man, no woman, no matter what office they\u8217\'20\'19ve held or wealth they\u8217\'20\'19ve acquired, are worthy of blind faith or obedience,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe deserve much better than to be misled by those trying to acquire or hold on to power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats held a conference call today to discuss the $3.5tn spending package, as committees work through their components of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the first time women have had so much leverage in this debate,\u8221\'20\'1D speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said on the call, according to a source familiar with the conversation. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the first time children have had so much leverage in this debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker thanked the committee chairs for \u8220\'20\'1Call of their great work getting us to this place,\u8221\'20\'1D and she expressed confidence that the committees would conclude their work by September 15.\par \par \uc2 However, disagreements remain over the topline cost of the legislation. Moderate Democrats, including senators Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , have insisted on a less expensive bill, while progressives are adamant that $3.5tn is the floor for the cost of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Students age 12 and older in the Los Angeles public school system soon must be vaccinated to attend classes on campus under one of the toughest anti-Covid mandates enacted in the nation.\par \par \uc2 Parent Rosa Vargas and her son, 9th grade student Victor Loredo, 14, walk home after getting tested at a \uc2 Los Angeles Unified School District\uc2  COVID-19 testing and vaccination site in East Los Angeles Thursday, April 15, 2021. \uc2 California Gov. Gavin Newsom\uc2  is urging all schools in the state to reopen, saying there are no health barriers to getting children back into classrooms and ending distance learning. Photograph: Damian Dovarganes/AP\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 The board of the \uc2 Los Angeles Unified School District\uc2  voted Thursday to require students age 12 and up to be fully vaccinated with those who take part in sports and other extracurricular activities receiving both of two shots by the end of October and all others by Dec. 19.\par \par \uc2 Students who can\u8217\'20\'19t show proof of vaccination won\u8217\'20\'19t be permitted to have in-person learning following the end of winter break on Jan. 11 unless they have a medical or other exemption.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis action is not about violating anybody\u8217\'20\'19s rights,\u8221\'20\'1D school board member Monica Garcia said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis action is about doing our job to be able to offer public schools that children can come to school and be safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The nation\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest school district was the largest in the U.S. to issue such a mandate. Nearby Culver City Unified School District imposed a similar policy last month for the 7,000-student district.\par \par \uc2 New York City\u8217\'20\'19s school system, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest, has only mandated vaccinations for 20,000 student athletes in certain sports considered at high risk of spreading the virus, including wrestling.\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles Unified, which has 630,000 students, has moved more aggressively than most districts in enacting COVID-19 safety measures. It tests all students and employees every week, requires masking indoors and outdoors and has ordered employees to be vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 The district was among the last of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest school districts to reopen to classroom instruction last spring. The teachers union opposed the move for months, citing health concerns.\par \par \uc2 The union applauded the new mandate, which it sought after teachers were ordered to get the shots.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  may authorize Covid-19 vaccine for kids based on two months of safety data\par \par \uc2 Parents and educators eager for health regulators to get a shift on with the process of approving Covid-19 vaccinations for children of various ages may be encouraged by news this afternoon that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  may authorize Covid-19 vaccine for kids based on two months of safety data.\par \par \uc2 In this file photo children arrive for class on the first day of school reopening on December 7, 2020 in the Brooklyn borough of New York City. - New York announced a vaccine mandate for all public school staff, including teachers and principals, on August 23, 2021 as the city escalates attempts to slow the spread of the hyper-contagious Delta variant. Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that:\par \par \uc2 U.S. heath regulators said children in clinical trials testing COVID-19 vaccines should be monitored for at least two months for side effects, suggesting that the agency is considering a quicker path to authorize the shot for emergency use than full approval.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Food and Drug Administration\uc2  said on Friday it was looking to complete the data review as quickly as possible, likely in a matter of weeks rather than months.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  granted full approval last month for the use of \uc2 Pfizer Inc\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine in people over the age of 16 based on a six-month follow-up from the trial. The shot was authorized in December for emergency use based on a shorter, two-month follow up.\par \par \uc2 The agency is under pressure to approve a vaccine for children below 12 years of age amid a surge in infections fueled by the spread of the Delta coronavirus variant, which has disrupted the reopening of schools.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and partner \uc2 BioNTech SE\uc2  as well as Modern a Inc are racing to submit clinical data seeking regulatory approval for their vaccines in children below 12 years of age.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 /BioNTech\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine has been currently authorized for children aged 12 to 15 in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  said it expects to report data needed for approval in five and 11 year olds sometime this month and could potentially submit an application for emergency use shortly after. The drugmaker said data for kids aged two and under five could arrive soon after.\par \par \uc2 For children between six months and two years, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  has said it could have a safety and immunogenicity data as early as October or November.\par \par \uc2 Moderna on Thursday said it has fully enrolled participants in a trial testing its shot in children between six and 11 years and that it was still conducting dose selection studies for younger age groups.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Igor Fruman, a former associate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2 , told a New York court hearing today that he will plead guilty to one criminal count in a campaign finance case.\par \par \uc2 Fruman is a former associate of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , the Republican most recently known as a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a 2020 election quasi-conspiracy theorist and the subject of a federal investigation and better known previously a legitimate presidential candidate and mayor of New York City.\par \par \uc2 Activist with Rise and Resist follow Igor Fruman, right, as he arrived in Federal court in Manhattan with his attorney Todd Blanche today. Fruman, a businessman who helped \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in his effort to dig up dirt on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Ukraine, was scheduled to appear in court for an expected guilty plea in a case involving allegations of illegal campaign. Photograph: Mary Altaffer/AP\par \par \uc2 The Reuters news agency reports that Fruman worked to collect damaging information about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  before he became US president.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani has not been charged or accused of criminal wrongdoing, the wire service notes.\par \par \uc2 CNBC reported that Fruman pleaded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/rudy-giuliani-associate-igor-fruman-likely-plead-guilty-wednesday-n1277486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guilty Friday to soliciting campaign contributions from a foreign national}}}\uc2  nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/oct/10/rudy-giuliani-associates-trump-campaign-finance-violations-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two years after}}}\uc2  being charged with crimes that included making illegal donations to a pro-Trump political action campaign.\par \par \uc2 CNBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/09/10/rudy-giuliani-associate-igor-fruman-set-to-plead-guilty-in-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further reported}}}\uc2  that:\par \par \uc2 Fruman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/11/04/giuliani-associate-lev-parnas-will-comply-with-house-impeachment-probe.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his business partner Lev Parnas,}}}\uc2  a co-defendant in the same case, had worked with Giuliani in an effort to dig up damaging information about President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Ukraine when Biden had emerged as a leading challenger to then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The change-of-plea hearing in Manhattan federal court came as Giuliani, who has acted as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney, faces an ongoing criminal investigation by the U.S. Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office for the Southern District of New York.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, who denies any wrongdoing, served two terms as mayor of New York after heading that same prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 office for years.\par \par \uc2 The Ukraine-born Fruman was originally charged with 10 crimes.\par \par \uc2 But in court Friday, he agreed to plead guilty only to a single count related to soliciting U.S. campaign contributions from a foreign national as part of what prosecutors said was a bid to get state-issued recreational marijuana business licenses for a cannabis venture that ultimately never got off the ground.\par \par \uc2 Fruman said the money was solicited from a foreign businessman who was interested in investing in the cannabis company that Fruman and others were pursuing.\par \par \uc2 The campaign donations were earmarked for government officials, both Republican and Democrat, in states moving to legalize marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI deeply regret my actions and apologize to the court and the \uc2 United States government\uc2  for this conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D Fruman told Judge J. Paul Oetken, after admitting that he had known such campaign donations from foreigners were illegal under American law.\par \par \uc2 Fruman\u8217\'20\'19s plea came in an agreement with prosecutors that led to the other charges being dropped, but he has not agreed to a deal that would compel him to cooperate with federal prosecutors in any ongoing investigation.\par \par \uc2 His sentencing was scheduled for Jan. 21, and he remains free on bond. The plea agreement stipulates that federal sentencing guidelines suggest that Fruman receive a prison term of between three years and three years and 10 months.\par \par \uc2 But Oetken is not bound by those guidelines.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Republican leaders are threatening lawsuits over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to order employers with 100 or more workers to establish vaccine mandates or require regular coronavirus testing. The proposal is part of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new six-pronged strategy to boost vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Americans when he was elected that he would not impose vaccine mandates. He lied,\u8221\'20\'1D said Republican National Committee chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhen his decree goes into effect, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  will sue the administration to protect Americans and their liberties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden responded to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 threats of lawsuits with this message: \u8220\'20\'1CHave at it.\u8221\'20\'1D While visiting a middle school in Washington this morning, the president said, \u8220\'20\'1CI am so disappointed that, particularly some Republican governors, have been so cavalier with the health of these kids, so cavalier with the health of their communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden also offered reassurance to parents who are worried about the safety of schools as the Delta variant continues to spread. \u8220\'20\'1CI want folks to know that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be okay. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be okay,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at Brookland middle school in DC. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what it takes to keep our children safe and our schools open. And we have the tools to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Jared Golden of Maine has expressed concern about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plan to order employers with 100 of more workers to establish vaccine mandates or require regular coronavirus testing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter stating this summer that it is not the role of the federal government to institute vaccine mandates, I am frustrated that the Biden Administration has abruptly announced a vaccine and testing mandate for businesses with more than 100 employees,\u8221\'20\'1D Golden said in a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pressherald.com/2021/09/09/members-of-maines-congressional-delegation-react-to-presidents-sweeping-vaccination-mandate/?rel=related"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per the Portland Press Herald}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I personally think getting vaccinated against COVID-19 is a good thing to do, I am generally skeptical of blanket mandates from the federal government and I am particularly concerned about the negative pressure the president\u8217\'20\'19s mandate may put on an already challenging labor market in Maine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Golden represents a district that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won in 2020, and he has occasionally broken with his party on some major proposals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-coronavirus-pandemic-house-elections-portland-bills-eb17ca63bb929e314399e16576f5d91c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $1.9tn coronavirus relief bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melody Schreiber reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 As universities and colleges in the United States open for the fall semester, even those institutions requiring masks and vaccinations are grappling with unexpectedly high rates of Covid.\par \par \uc2 In one high-profile example, the \uc2 University of Delaware\uc2  sent a message to faculty this week, instructing them not to let students know if their classmates test positive for Covid-19 even though cases are rising on campus.\par \par \uc2 If a student notifies an instructor that they have Covid-19, the instructor is now not allowed to notify the rest of the class they came in contact with a positive case.\par \par \uc2 Instead, instructors should tell students that \u8220\'20\'1Cgiven the current incidence of Covid-19 on campus, we should assume that we may have contact with individuals who are shedding Covid-19, perhaps unknowingly,\u8221\'20\'1D the email said.\par \par \uc2 One professor, who asked to withhold her name to protect her job, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  that she understood the policy as she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to reveal sensitive health information about some students to others. However, she said, she was concerned that current contact-tracing strategies would not be enough to control the spread of Covid on campus.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/10/covid-coronavirus-us-colleges-fall-semester"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m nervous\u8217\'20\'19: US colleges wrestle with Covid safety as fall semester begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden responds to Republicans threatening lawsuits over vaccine policies: 'Have at it'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took a couple questions from reporters after concluding his prepared remarks at Brookland Middle School in Washington.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked the president how he responds to Republican governors who have threatened to file lawsuits over his new vaccination policies, including his plan to order employers with 100 or more workers to establish vaccine mandates or require regular coronavirus testing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHave at it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden replied.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I am so disappointed that, particularly some of the Republican governors, have been so cavalier with the health of these kids, so cavalier with the health of their communities. We're playing for real here, this isn't a game," President Biden says. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EW7LfGtyJa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EW7LfGtyJa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1436340803169882120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so disappointed that, particularly some Republican governors, have been so cavalier with the health of these kids, so cavalier with the health of their communities,\u8221\'20\'1D the president added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re playing for real here, this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a game. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t know of any scientist out there in this field that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think it makes considerable sense to do the six things I\u8217\'20\'19ve suggested.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several Republican governors and the \uc2 Republican National Committee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/10/biden-vaccine-mandate-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live?page=with:block-613b5ac78f088f2a91a7fc63#block-613b5ac78f088f2a91a7fc63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have indicated}}}\uc2  they will file lawsuits to prevent Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies from going into effect, arguing that his plan is an overreach of federal authority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  offered reassurance to parents who are nervous that their children\u8217\'20\'19s schools will be repeatedly closed because of the spread of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want folks to know that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be okay. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be OK,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at Brookland middle school in Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what it takes to keep our children safe and our schools open. And we have the tools to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"I want folks to know we're going to be ok," President Biden says. "We know what it takes to keep our children safe and our schools open. And we have the tools to do it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EclFprHNrv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EclFprHNrv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1436338975967518721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden noted he laid out a new strategy yesterday to boost vaccinations and limit the spread of coronavirus, which will help keep schools open in a safe manner.\par \par \uc2 The president encouraged parents to vaccinate children who are eligible to get the vaccine, meaning those who are at least 12 years old.\par \par \uc2 Biden then invited the students of Brookland Middle School to \u8220\'20\'1Ca special visit at the White House\u8221\'20\'1D once they get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to get in trouble with the Secret Service and everybody else,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how we\u8217\'20\'19re going to mechanically do it, but I assume the buses can get you to the White House. And if we can\u8217\'20\'19t get you all in one room, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be out in the Rose Garden or out in the back there and maybe let you fly the helicopters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was introduced by one of Brookland Middle School\u8217\'20\'19s students, a young boy named Elijah Poole who discussed the difficulties of trying to get educated amid the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Once the president started speaking, he thanked Elijah for his kind introduction, and he noted that he could not have delivered such a speech when he was in eighth grade because he spoke with a stutter at the time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I am amazed when I see young women and men like you, who stand up and speak with such grace and ease,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really impressive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is speaking at Brookland Middle School about the need to protect children from coronavirus in the classroom.\par \par \uc2 The first lady, who is an educator herself, talked about how thrilled she is to be back in the classroom with her students. (Tuesday marked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/07/us/politics/jill-biden-teaching.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first day back}}}\uc2  at Northern Virginia Community College.)\par \par \uc2 Biden addressed how difficult the past year and a half have been for parents whose children could not go to school because of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CParents, this is hard, but you\u8217\'20\'19re doing your best,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The first lady also expressed her thanks to teachers who have continued to share lessons with their students over the past year and a half, under extremely trying circumstances.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith all my heart, thank you for being the heroes that we needed,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bidens visit DC school to discuss Covid safety for students\par \par \uc2 Joe and Jill Biden have just arrived at Brookland Middle School in Washington, where they will discuss safety protocols to protect students from coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden and the First Lady visit with 6th grade students. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0dlixF1AnX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0dlixF1AnX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Scott (@rachelvscott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelvscott/status/1436330788447006724?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president and the first lady were greeted at the school by education secretary \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 , DC mayor Muriel Bowser, DC public schools chancellor Lewis Ferebee and principal Kerry Richardson.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliver remarks about how the Administration is helping to keep students safe in classrooms,\u8221\'20\'1D according to his official schedule.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite the threat of lawsuits from a number of Republican leaders, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that at least one Republican governor is actually welcoming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new vaccination policies.\par \par \uc2 enltrI appreciate the President\u8217\'20\'19s continued prioritization of vaccination and the country\u8217\'20\'19s recovery as we move forward. As Vermont\u8217\'20\'19s experience shows, vaccines work and save lives. They are the best and fastest way to move past this pandemic. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xqNC0GXELq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xqNC0GXELq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Phil Scott\uc2  (@GovPhilScott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovPhilScott/status/1436093027748040704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI appreciate the President\u8217\'20\'19s continued prioritization of vaccination and the country\u8217\'20\'19s recovery as we move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Phil Scott\uc2 , the Republican governor of Vermont, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Vermont\u8217\'20\'19s experience shows, vaccines work and save lives. They are the best and fastest way to move past this pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vermont has one of the highest vaccination rates in the country, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2020/us/covid-19-vaccine-doses.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 87.5%}}}\uc2  of adults already having received at least one vaccine dose.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , striving to restore public confidence in his handling of the pandemic, announced new vaccination mandates on Thursday for 100 million workers, about two-thirds of the American labour force.\par \par \uc2 Channeling national frustration as the virus surges back, the US president adopted his sternest tone yet in reprimanding the tens of millions of Americans who are still not vaccinated against the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can and we will turn the tide of Covid-19,\u8221\'20\'1D he said firmly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19ll take a lot of hard work and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to take some time. Many of us are frustrated with the nearly 80 million Americans who are still not vaccinated even though the vaccine is safe, effective and free.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech in the state dining room of the White House, against a backdrop of \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s portrait and with watching reporters crammed tightly, was seen as a high-profile attempt to claw back momentum and offer reassurance to Americans feeling despair about whether the pandemic will ever end.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  has also said it plans to file a lawsuit over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new vaccine policy for private-sector employers.\par \par \uc2 enltrJoe Biden told Americans when he was elected that he would not impose vaccine mandates. He lied.\par \par \uc2 When his decree goes into effect, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  will sue the administration to protect Americans and their liberties. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XinwFw4bam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XinwFw4bam}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  (@GOPChairwoman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPChairwoman/status/1436118614504050692?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Americans when he was elected that he would not impose vaccine mandates. He lied. Now small businesses, workers, and families across the country will pay the price,\u8221\'20\'1D RNC chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  said in a statement released yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike many Americans, I am pro-vaccine and anti-mandate. Many small businesses and workers do not have the money or legal resources to fight Biden\u8217\'20\'19s unconstitutional actions and authoritarian decrees, but when his decree goes into effect, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  will sue the administration to protect Americans and their liberties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When he announced his new pandemic response strategy yesterday, Biden indicated he was ready for a fight over his proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line: We\u8217\'20\'19re going to protect vaccinated workers from unvaccinated co-workers,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican governors threaten lawsuits over Biden's vaccine mandate\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  outlined his new strategy to boost coronavirus vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant, which has caused an increase in case numbers across the country.\par \par \uc2 One of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s initiatives involves ordering the Labor Department to direct businesses with more 100 workers to establish vaccine mandates or require employees to undergo regular coronavirus testing.\par \par \uc2 And some Republican governors are already pushing back against the president\u8217\'20\'19s policy.\par \par \uc2 enltrRest assured, we will fight them to the gates of hell to protect the liberty and livelihood of every South Carolinian.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gov. Henry McMaster\uc2  (@henrymcmaster) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/henrymcmaster/status/1436074995374039045?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American Dream has turned into a nightmare under President Biden and the radical Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D South Carolina governor \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRest assured, we will fight them to the gates of hell to protect the liberty and livelihood of every South Carolinian.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arizona governor \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  threatened to fight the policy in court, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly the kind of big government overreach we have tried so hard to prevent in Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 now the Biden-Harris administration is hammering down on private businesses and individual freedoms in an unprecedented and dangerous way. This will never stand up in court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210910eh9a0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
