\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says \u8216\'20\'18we can and we will turn the tide on Covid-19\u8217\'20\'19 in White House speech \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 7,897 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2021\par 00:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President asks unvaccinated Americans: \u8216\'20\'18What more do you need to see?\u8217\'20\'19Administration sues Texas over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawBlow to US gun control efforts as Biden withdraws ATF nominationBiden to mandate Covid vaccinations for all federal workers \u8211\'20\'13 reportsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  laid out his new strategy to combat the spread of coronavirus. The White House has said the president will outline six steps to boost vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant. Biden announced coronavirus vaccination requirements for all federal workers, and a new Labor Department rule compelling private employers to adopt similar vaccination policies.\par \par \uc2 * The justice department filed a lawsuit against Texas over its six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a week after the supreme court declined to block the law\u8217\'20\'19s implementation. \u8220\'20\'1CThe act is clearly unconstitutional under longstanding supreme court precedent,\u8221\'20\'1D attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said at a press conference this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * Biden confirmed he will withdraw the nomination of \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 . Chipman had attracted intense criticism from Republicans and a handful of Democrats for his advocacy work with the gun control group Giffords. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the White House is in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussions\u8221\'20\'1D with Chipman to find another role for him in the administration.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  signaled she is ready for a fight following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of one of her primary opponents, Harriet Hageman. After Trump mocked Cheney as the \u8220\'20\'1Cnumber one provider of sound bites\u8221\'20\'1D for Democrats, the Republican congresswoman replied, \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s a sound bite for you: Bring it.\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney has repeatedly criticized Trump over his lies about fraud in the 2020 election, and she supported his impeachment for inciting the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 * A charter flight carrying US citizens out of Kabul has safely landed in Qatar, the White House said. The flight\u8217\'20\'19s departure was facilitated by the \uc2 US government\uc2 , as the Biden administration continues its efforts to evacuate American citizens out of Afghanistan, even after the military formally ended its Kabul mission last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 A third of the female service members in the air force and space force say they\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced sexual harassment, according to a new study.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 The review, done by the Air Force inspector general concluded that minorities and women are underrepresented in leadership and officer positions, particularly at the senior levels, and get promoted less frequently. It echoed many of the findings of an initial review, released last December, which found that Black service members in the Air Force are far more likely to be investigated, arrested, face disciplinary actions and be discharged for misconduct.\par \par \uc2 The two reviews into racial, ethnic and gender disparities across the Air Force and Space Force broadly confirm that biases exist, but the data does not fully explain why. The studies also reflect broader campaigns within the \uc2 Defense Department\uc2  and the Biden administration to root out extremism and racism.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has declared domestic extremism an urgent national security threat and the \uc2 Defense Department\uc2  is working to identify extremist behavior and eliminate it from the force. Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , earlier this year, ordered military leaders to spend a day talking to their troops about extremism in the ranks, after a number of former and current military members took part in the assault on the U.S. Capitol in January.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will visit California on Monday, stopping in Sacramento to survey wildfire damage and then Long Beach to campaign with governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  against the recall election.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was in California yesterday campaigning for Newsom, returning to her home county of Alameda to rally voters. Newsom, a Democrat who won office by historic margins, remains popular and appears poised to maintain his seat per recent polls and early returns. But Democrats in California and DC are taking no chances - escalating efforts to help Newsom maintain his place at the helm of the most populous US state.\par \par \uc2 Californians have already started voting, and nearly a third have returned their ballots so far. The deadline to return ballots or vote in person is 14 September, the day after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/16/californias-governor-recall-election-is-heating-up-heres-what-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s governor recall election is heating up. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you need to know}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden withdraws pick to run firearms agency after \uc2 NRA\uc2  pressure\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a Thursday afternoon statement that he was no longer proposing \uc2 David Chipman\uc2 , a 25-year veteran of the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2  (ATF) who has worked to tighten gun laws, as the agency\u8217\'20\'19s next director, confirming an earlier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/chipman-atf-withdraw/2021/09/09/d5804a3a-1108-11ec-a511-cb913c7e5ba0_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post report.}}}\par \par \uc2 The gun reform group Brady says Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to bow to \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  (\uc2 NRA\uc2 ) pressure and withdraw his nominee, a strong gun control advocate, to lead the agency enforcing federal firearms laws is \u8220\'20\'1Ca shameful day for our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/24/nra-republicans-david-chipman-guns-atf-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported in July}}}\uc2  that Chipman\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, which Biden announced in April, was in trouble, stalled by opposition from pro-gun Republicans in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  and targeted by the \uc2 NRA\uc2  and industry lobbyists.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/david-chipman-atf-biden-nomination-withdrawal-nra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden withdraws pick to run firearms agency after NRA pressure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the tools. Now we just have to finish the job,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his concluding remarks.\par \par \uc2 More details of his pandemic plan will be revealed in the coming weeks, he said. He ended his speech with a whisper: \u8220\'20\'1CGet vaccinated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He did not take questions from the press.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president said he will also enact measures to disincentivize those seeking to undermine vaccine and masking mandates.\par \par \uc2 Implicitly referring to leaders like Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.edweek.org/leadership/florida-governor-threatens-to-withhold-salaries-of-school-leaders-who-impose-mask-mandates/2021/08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to withhold salaries}}}\uc2  from school board members and superintendents in districts with mask mandates, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CTalk about bullying in schools.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, local school officials are trying to keep children safe in a pandemic while their governor picks a fight with them and even threatens their salaries or their jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 If teachers\u8217\'20\'19 pay is withheld by states, the federal government will step in to pay it, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI promise you, I will have your back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president also said that the TSA will double fines for passengers who refuse to wear masks. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd by the way, show some respect,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy message to unvaccinated Americans is this: what more is there to wait for? What more do you need to see?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve made vaccinations free, safe and convenient.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been patient but our patience is wearing thin and your refusal has cost all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an overview of vaccination stats across the US:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/us-vaccine-distribution-tracker-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US vaccine distribution: track your state's progress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key points: Biden's pandemic plan\par \par \uc2 * The Labor Department will require all employers with more than 100 employees to ensure their workers are vaccinated or tested weekly. Employers must also provide paid time off to allow workers to get vaccinated. This will affect more than 80 million workers in private sector businesses. Companies that do not comply could face fines of up to nearly $14,000 per violation.\par \par \uc2 * Workers in healthcare settings that receive Medicaid or Medicare reimbursement must be vaccinated , a move that applies to 50,000 providers and covers more than 17 million healthcare workers .\par \par \uc2 * All federal government workers, as well as employees of contractors that do business with the federal government, must get vaccinated, or regularly tested.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in a tough stretch and it could last for awhile,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, stressing that the Delta variant had complicated the US recovery.\par \par \uc2 Stressing that vaccines protect people from hospitalizations and deaths from the Delta variant, he called the surge in cases a pandemic of the unvaccinated.\par \par \uc2 A quarter of adults still haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten any vaccine shot, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat 25% can cause a lot of damage, and they are,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He implicitly called out the Republicans who are hindering a vaccination push - calling the behavior \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden explains Covid-19 strategy\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can and will turn the tide of Covid-19,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking from the White House, Biden started by recapping progress made so far in getting Americans vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the tools to combat the virus if we come together and use those tools,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, acknowledging frustrations with the 80m who are unvaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon lay out his new strategy to combat the spread of coronavirus. The White House has said the president will outline six steps to boost vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant. Biden is expected to announce he is requiring coronavirus vaccinations for all federal workers, without the option to undergo regular testing instead of getting vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 * The justice department filed a lawsuit against Texas over its six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a week after the supreme court declined to block the law\u8217\'20\'19s implementation. \u8220\'20\'1CThe act is clearly unconstitutional under longstanding supreme court precedent,\u8221\'20\'1D attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said at a press conference this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * Biden confirmed he will withdraw the nomination of \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 . Chipman had attracted intense criticism from Republicans and a handful of Democrats for his advocacy work with the gun control group Giffords. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the White House is in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussions\u8221\'20\'1D with Chipman to find another role for him in the administration.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  signaled she is ready for a fight following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of one of her primary opponents, Harriet Hageman. After Trump mocked Cheney as the \u8220\'20\'1Cnumber one provider of sound bites\u8221\'20\'1D for Democrats, the Republican congresswoman replied, \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s a sound bite for you: Bring it.\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney has repeatedly criticized Trump over his lies about fraud in the 2020 election, and she supported his impeachment for inciting the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 * A charter flight carrying US citizens out of Kabul has safely landed in Qatar, the White House said. The flight\u8217\'20\'19s departure was facilitated by the \uc2 US government\uc2 , as the Biden administration continues its efforts to evacuate American citizens out of Afghanistan, even after the military formally ended its Kabul mission last week.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis suffers legal defeat over anti-riot law\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been another busy day in court for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s litigious Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who followed up yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s rebuff by a federal judge over his ban on mask mandates in schools with another defeat on Thursday - this time over his flagship anti-riot law.\par \par \uc2 US district court judge Mark Walker, in a 90-page ruling, determined that the state\u8217\'20\'19s HB 1, which DeSantis signed into law in April, is unconstitutional. Touted by the governor as a means of enhancing public safety and clamping down on mob violence in the wake of protests nationwide in the wake of the murder of George Floyd, the law created, among other provisions, a new crime of \u8220\'20\'1Cmob intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D and protected motorists who hit protestors during a riot.\par \par \uc2 Walker, however, was not impressed with the language contained in the law. \u8220\'20\'1C[Its] new definition of \u8216\'20\'18riot\u8217\'20\'19 both fails to put Floridians of ordinary intelligence on notice of what acts it criminalizes, and encourages arbitrary and discriminatory enforcement, making this provision vague to the point of unconstitutionality,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 His temporary injunction effectively prohibits enforcement of the law while legal challenges to it make their way through the courts.\par \par \uc2 If DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s recent actions are anything to go by, it won\u8217\'20\'19t be long before the issue is back in the courtroom. On Thursday, DeSantis filed an emergency appeal to reverse Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s mask mandate ruling, asserting a \u8220\'20\'1Chigh likelihood\u8221\'20\'1D of winning the case on appeal, and claiming that the court of district judge John Cooper \u8220\'20\'1Cabused its discretion\u8221\'20\'1D by lifting a stay the governor had previously won that halted Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s earlier order freeing school districts to require masks.\par \par \uc2 A decision is likely within the next few days.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  sharply criticized the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law this afternoon, as the vice-president met with reproductive health providers and patients to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Harris noted many US states beyond Texas have enacted restrictive laws that have made it extremely difficult to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, underscoring the need for a robust response to such policies.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  makes first on camera comments about the DOJ lawsuit filed against the state of Texas following TX Senate Bill 8. Harris says the DOJ understands that the TX law is \u8220\'20\'1Cpatently unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LUJrAxibQp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LUJrAxibQp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Perry (@tperry518) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tperry518/status/1436060223911890952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 United States department of justice\uc2  has spoken loudly in saying that this law is patently unconstitutional,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said of the new federal lawsuit against Texas.\par \par \uc2 Asked what other steps the Biden administration can take to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the vice-president said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to codify Roe v Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group NARAL praised the Biden administration for filing a lawsuit against Texas over its six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are pleased to see the Biden administration taking action to fight for Texans\u8217\'20\'19 reproductive freedom by filing a lawsuit to block SB 8\u8212\'20\'14the harshest and most extreme ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country,\u8221\'20\'1D NARAL acting president Adrienne Kimmell said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: Texas is the tip of the iceberg. This lawsuit sends a strong message to anti-choice lawmakers across the country who are racing to enact copycat versions of SB 8 in their own states. The threat to the future of safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looming larger than ever, and safeguarding reproductive freedom requires bold and immediate action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  noted the justice department is seeking a preliminary injunction to prevent enforcement of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, out of concern for private citizens acting as \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty hunters\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure the statute is respected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department of justice has a duty to defend the Constitution of the United States and to uphold the rule of law,\u8221\'20\'1D the attorney general said at his press conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we fulfill that duty by filing the lawsuit I have just described.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  whether he expected the justice department to file additional lawsuits against states threatening to pass laws similar to Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe additional and further risk here is that other states will follow similar models with respect not only to this constitutional right but theoretically against any constitutional right,\u8221\'20\'1D the attorney general said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo if another state uses the same kind of provisions to deprive its citizens of their constitutional rights, and in particular to deprive their citizens of the ability to seek immediate review, we will bring the same kind of lawsuit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration sues Texas over six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is suing Texas over its six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which went into effect last week after the supreme court declined to block the law\u8217\'20\'19s implementation.\par \par \uc2 enltrGarland says Texas' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is "clearly unconstitutional" and the state doesn't dispute that. He says the ban creates "bounty hunters" who can file lawsuits "to prevent women from exercising their constitutional rights by thwarting judicial review for as long as possible" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jPwMJHFf02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jPwMJHFf02}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1436044985984499716?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  confirmed the news at a press conference this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe act is clearly unconstitutional under longstanding supreme court precedent,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general warned that the law \u8220\'20\'1Cdeputizes all private citizens, without any showing of personal connection or injury, to serve as bounty hunters\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure the law is respected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe obvious and expressly acknowledged intention of this statutory scheme is to prevent women from exercising their constitutional rights by thwarting judicial review for as long as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had previously promised that he would pursue a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government effort\u8221\'20\'1D to respond to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, specifically looking at what tools the justice department may have to push back against the Texas law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Charter flight from Kabul safely lands in Qatar, White House says\par \par \uc2 A charter flight carrying American citizens out of Kabul has now safely landed in Qatar, the White House said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 The flight\u8217\'20\'19s departure was facilitated by the \uc2 US government\uc2 , as the Biden administration continues its efforts to evacuate American citizens out of Afghanistan, even after the military formally ended its Kabul mission last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Taliban\uc2  have been cooperative in facilitating the departure of American citizens and lawful permanent residents on charter flights from HKIA,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Emily Horne\uc2 , a spokesperson for the National Security Council, said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue these efforts to facilitate the safe and orderly travel of American citizens, lawful permanent residents, and Afghans who worked for us and wish to leave Afghanistan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how many US citizens were on the charter flight and how many Americans remain in Afghanistan. \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 , the White House chief of staff, said on Sunday that there were roughly 100 Americans still in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  hinted that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be pursuing actions to put pressure on major employers to set coronavirus vaccine requirements for their workers.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked the White House press secretary at her briefing, \u8220\'20\'1CCan the Department of Labor or anybody else compel major employers, large employers, to force the vaccine mandates on their employees?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki replied, \u8220\'20\'1CYes. Stay tuned. More to come this afternoon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: "Can the Department of Labor or anybody else compel major employers, large employers, to force the vaccine mandates on their employees?"\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 : "Yes. Stay tuned. More to come this afternoon." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yRbPtR0ZVi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yRbPtR0ZVi}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HsNZGEDUWb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HsNZGEDUWb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1436036364257185797?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to deliver a speech on his new strategy to boost coronavirus vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant in about two hours.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to sign an executive order requiring coronavirus vaccinations for all federal workers, without a testing alternative to opt out of the mandate.\par \par \uc2 Some major private-sector employers, including \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 United Airlines\uc2 , have already established vaccine mandates for their workers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal workers will have 75 days to get fully vaccinated under Biden's new policy\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  offered some details on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech this afternoon, in which he will outline his new strategy to boost coronavirus vaccinations and limit the spread of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary said federal workers will have 75 days to get fully vaccinated under an executive order that Biden will sign later today.\par \par \uc2 enltrFederal employees will have about 75 days to get fully vaccinated under the executive order Biden will sign Thursday, Psaki says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jYfQW3U8gY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jYfQW3U8gY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jNVpgN4qng"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jNVpgN4qng}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg Quicktake (@Quicktake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Quicktake/status/1436029455462551559?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki noted the vaccine order will include \u8220\'20\'1Climited exceptions for legally recognized reasons,\u8221\'20\'1D such as religious objections and disabilities that prevent vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 Biden announced in July that federal workers would be required to get vaccinated or undergo regular coronavirus testing, but the newest order will not include a testing option.\par \par \uc2 Psaki confirmed that federal workers who do not comply with the vaccination mandate will go through the \u8220\'20\'1Cstandard HR process,\u8221\'20\'1D which could include facing \u8220\'20\'1Cprogressive disciplinary action\u8221\'20\'1D. She later added that employees could potentially be terminated if they do not get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 One reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  intends to name another nominee to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 , now that \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nomination has been withdrawn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe certainly would at an appropriate time,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a timeline on that at this point in time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Psaki previously noted, there has only ever been one Senate-confirmed ATF director in the history of the bureau, so it will likely be extremely difficult to get any nominee confirmed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing, and she was asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to withdraw the nomination of \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  as the head of the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe always knew this would be challenging,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said of the decision, noting that there has only ever been one Senate-confirmed ATF director in the history of the bureau.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the president continues to have a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat deal of respect\u8221\'20\'1D for Chipman, and she added that the White House is engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussions\u8221\'20\'1D with Chipman about a future role in the administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden withdraws Chipman's nomination to lead ATF\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has officially confirmed he is withdrawing \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes after Republicans and the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  launched a campaign to block the confirmation of Chipman over his advocacy work for the gun control group Giffords.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 David Chipman\uc2  spent 25 years in distinguished service to our country as an ATF agent,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe would have been an exemplary Director of the ATF and would have redoubled its efforts to crack down on illegal firearms traffickers and help keep our communities safe from gun violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, Republicans in Congress have made clear that they intend to use gun crime as a political talking point instead of taking serious steps to address it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that at least one senator who caucuses with Democrats, Angus King of Maine, had signaled some concerns about Chipman\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as well, making his confirmation very unlikely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince taking office, my Administration has taken numerous steps to combat gun violence, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to use every tool at our disposal to fight gun violence and keep Americans safe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am grateful for Mr. Chipman\u8217\'20\'19s service and for his work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 On East 26th Street in Reserve, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2 , sits a family house constructed from the bottom up with bricks and mortar, plywood and cement.\par \par \uc2 Robert Taylor built this family home in stages, using paychecks from the three jobs he worked and assistance from the Farmers Home Association, the now defunct federal government agency that assisted low-income rural communities to buy land.\par \par \uc2 Taylor would set aside money each week to buy studs and bricks. Parts of the house would arrive on the back of a truck, ready to be assembled.\par \par \uc2 It took three years to complete the first floor, and by 1968 Robert Taylor was ready to move in with his wife and four children. He became the first on his mother\u8217\'20\'19s side of the family to own a home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my entire life,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI put everything into it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As an afternoon thunderstorm echoed across the nearby levees, Robert Taylor, 79 years old, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/hurricane-ida-rebuilding-fund-for-robert-taylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned this week}}}\uc2  to what remained of his house. Even in a neighborhood decimated by the storm, the destruction to Taylor\u8217\'20\'19s house stood out as particularly pronounced.\par \par \uc2 Read \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/hurricane-ida-louisiana-robert-taylor-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He \u8216\'20\'18put everything\u8217\'20\'19 into his Louisiana home. Hurricane Ida destroyed it in one day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The weekly number of US jobless claims has hit a pandemic low of 310,000, mitigating some fears of potential layoffs due to the elevated number of coronavirus cases as the Delta variant spreads.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-health-pandemics-coronavirus-pandemic-economy-7df212b86c19811dff9d2f0a0f7b6ab2?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s report from the Labor Department showed that jobless claims dropped from a revised total of 345,000 the week before. And at their current pace, weekly applications for benefits are edging toward their pre-pandemic figure of roughly 225,000.\par \par \uc2 But the spread of the delta variant this summer has put renewed pressure on the economy and the job market. On Wednesday, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  reported that U.S. economic activity \u8216\'20\'18downshifted\u8217\'20\'19 in July and August, in part because of a pullback in dining out, travel and tourism related to concerns about the delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Still, the ongoing drop in applications for unemployment aid \u8212\'20\'14 six declines in the past seven weeks \u8212\'20\'14 indicates that most companies are holding onto their workers despite the slowdown. That trend should help sustain the economic rebound through the current wave of infections.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the report in a new statement, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the ongoing impact of the Delta variant, the evidence is clear: the Biden plan is working, we are seeing real results, and the American economy is on the move again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melody Schreiber writes\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The US has far too many cases of the coronavirus to see an end to the pandemic, \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , director of the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/fauci-no-control-covid-a2572210-dbdb-48b0-aa2e-92e8e9fcd69a.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Axios in an interview published Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe endgame is to suppress the virus,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we\u8217\'20\'19re still in pandemic mode, because we have 160,000 new infections a day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The seven-day average of new cases declined slightly from the previous week, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#trends_dailycases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 140,000 cases}}}\uc2 , although it\u8217\'20\'19s possible reported case numbers are low given two holidays this week. Rates this high make it impossible to return to some semblance of normal life, Fauci said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a country of our size, you can\u8217\'20\'19t be hanging around and having 100,000 infections a day. You\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get well below 10,000 before you start feeling comfortable,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/anthony-fauci-comments-covid-19-cases-high-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Not even modestly good control\u8217\'20\'19: Fauci says US Covid cases 16 times too high to end pandemic}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration plans to sue Texas over the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which amounts to a near total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-prepares-to-sue-texas-over-abortion-law-11631151641?mod=e2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the justice department could file a lawsuit on Thursday, just over a week after the law came into effect.\par \par \uc2 Senate Bill 8, pushed through by Texas\u8217\'20\'19 Republican-dominated legislature, bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks. Most women are not aware they are pregnant as early as that time.\par \par \uc2 According to the Journal the justice department will argue that the law, which offers no exceptions for rape or incest, \u8220\'20\'1Cillegally interferes with federal interests\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the US attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/doj-texas-abortion-law-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the justice department would \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect those seeking to obtain or provide reproductive health services\u8221\'20\'1D, under a federal law known as the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances.\par \par \uc2 Garland said that law would be enforced \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to protect the constitutional rights of women and other persons, including access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/biden-administration-sue-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration plans to sue Texas over near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the supreme court justice many liberals wish would retire so \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democratic-held Senate could replace him, thereby at least delaying the calamity which would be conservatives gaining an even stronger grip on the court than the 6-3 advantage they already hold, will give a TV interview this weekend. To Fox News Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The show announced the interview, with anchor Chris Wallace, today.\par \par \uc2 Breyer, 83 