heney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarriet is a fourth-generation daughter of Wyoming, a very successful attorney, and has the support and respect of a truly great U.S. Senator, Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s own \uc2 Cynthia Lummis\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in his endorsement of Hageman.\par \par \uc2 But when contacted to confirm the endorsement, Lummis would not definitively say whether she had offered her support to Hageman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you, I\u8217\'20\'19ve known Harriet Hageman for decades. She is a fabulous choice for President Trump \u8212\'20\'14 and I\u8217\'20\'19m just leaving it at that,\u8221\'20\'1D Lummis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/campaigns/cynthia-lummis-declines-to-address-trump-claim-that-she-is-joining-him-in-opposing-liz-cheney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Washington Examiner}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTake my statement at face value. That\u8217\'20\'19s all I\u8217\'20\'19m saying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been widely expected to endorse one of \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s primary rivals, given that the two have repeatedly clashed since the then-president incited the Capitol insurrection on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Cheney supported Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment following the insurrection, and she is now one of just two Republicans, along with \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , serving on the House select committee investigating the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s repeated criticism of Trump and his lies about fraud in the 2020 election ultimately led to her losing her position as the House Republican conference chairwoman earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Despite the attacks from Trump and his allies, Cheney has given no indication that she plans to walk away from her reelection race next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they think that they are going to come into Wyoming and make the argument that the people of Wyoming should vote for someone who is loyal to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over somebody who is loyal to the Constitution, I welcome that debate,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney told the \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8221\'20\'1D show in May.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cheney responds to Trump's endorsement of primary rival: 'Bring it'\par \par \uc2 Republican congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  signaled she is ready for a fight after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  endorsed her primary rival, Harriet Hageman.\par \par \uc2 The former president announced his widely expected endorsement this morning, saying Hageman is \u8220\'20\'1Call in for America First\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly endorse Republican House of Representatives Candidate Harriet Hageman from Wyoming who is running against warmonger and disloyal Republican, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarriet has my Complete and Total Endorsement in replacing the Democrats number one provider of sound bites, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About twenty minutes after Trump issued his endorsement, Cheney responded over \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s a sound bite for you: Bring it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s a sound bite for you: Bring it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VmET1JUs12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VmET1JUs12}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@Liz_Cheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1435985804665442307?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Tim Kaine sent his best wishes to \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  after she revealed that she had been treated for breast cancer earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  is one of my best friends in the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D Kaine said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe works hard with her head up and a smile on her face. Anne and I are thinking of Amy and her family today and are so glad she is doing well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAmy Klobuchar is one of my best friends in the Senate. She works hard with her head up and a smile on her face. Anne and I are thinking of Amy and her family today and are so glad she is doing well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Mf10su8Gvy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Mf10su8Gvy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Kaine (@timkaine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/timkaine/status/1435969655290548226?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar reveals she was treated for breast cancer earlier this year\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  has revealed that she was treated for breast cancer earlier this year and is now doing well.\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar, who also ran for president last year, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@Amy_Klobuchar/statement-from-senator-amy-klobuchar-975260e9de8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medium post}}}\uc2  that she was diagnosed with Stage 1A breast cancer after a February mammogram showed abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after that, the Minnesota senator underwent a lumpectomy at the Mayo Clinic to remove the cancer.\par \par \uc2 enltrI wanted to share an update about my health. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0yGWuw4OKV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0yGWuw4OKV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  (@amyklobuchar)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amyklobuchar/status/1435932792240676878?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn May, I completed a course of radiation treatment, and after additional follow-up visits, it was determined in August that the treatment went well,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course this has been scary at times, since cancer is the word all of us fear, but at this point my doctors believe that my chances of developing cancer again are no greater than the average person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar sought the Democratic presidential nomination last year and turned in stronger-than-expected performances in Iowa and New Hampshire. But she dropped out before Super Tuesday following a lackluster showing in South Carolina, and she then endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar has represented Minnesota in the Senate since 2007, and she serves as chairwoman of the Senate rules committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former Trump White House press secretary \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 , also a former top aide to former first lady Melania Trump, has written a book.\par \par \uc2 According to Axios, which broke the news having noticed an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  page for the title, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll Take Your Questions Now: What I Saw in The Trump White House will be published on 5 October by \uc2 Harper Collins\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 . Photograph: Carlos Barr\u237\'00\'EDa/Reuters\par \par \uc2 No news yet of what might be in the highly guarded tome, but cynical observers might suggest it being highly guarded is rather appropriate, given that Grisham proved highly guarded in the company of reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/magazine/2020/04/14/short-strange-tale-trumps-former-press-secretary-stephanie-grisham/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 while she was White House press secretary}}}\uc2  and indeed barely took any questions: she did not host a single press room briefing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/stephanie-grisham-out-as-white-house-press-secretary-after-eight-months-during-which-she-held-no-regular-news-briefings/2020/04/07/6d93b7aa-75bd-11ea-87da-77a8136c1a6d_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in her nine months on the job}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Grisham stayed in the White House after relinquishing the press secretary role, ultimately resigning on 6 January this year, the day Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters stormed the US Capitol in an attempt to overturn his election defeat.\par \par \uc2 According to Axios, a source close to Grisham said she \u8220\'20\'1Cknows where all the bodies are buried because she buried a lot of them herself \u8230\'20\'26 [she] has receipts... she was a press person and it was her job to make sure she knew what was happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The reporter Jonathan Swan \u8211\'20\'13 he of the famous interview with Trump last summer and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2020/aug/05/who-is-jonathan-swan-the-reporter-who-grilled-trump-and-what-do-kangaroos-have-to-do-with-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looks of bewilderment and skepticism}}}\uc2  that were swiftly, inevitably memed \u8211\'20\'13 adds that a former West Wing source said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I heard this, all I could think about was Stephanie surrounded by a lake of gasoline, striking a match with a grin on her face.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough water on earth to contain the fire she could set to all of Trump world, including parts like the first lady\u8217\'20\'19s orbit, which not many people are in a position to illuminate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to articulate how much anxiety this is going to cause.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has contacted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s spokeswoman, Liz Harrington, to see if he has any comment.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not particularly hard to articulate how much interest Grisham\u8217\'20\'19s book will cause as publication day nears, whether it turns out scoop-filled or a damp squib.\par \par \uc2 This summer saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jul/17/donald-trump-books-leonnig-rucker-bender-wolff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a huge crop of Trump books}}}\uc2  with attendant scoops and reviews. Many observers said most such books were relatively lacking in scoop, the territory having been strip-mined since Michael Wolff birthed a genre with Fire and Fury in 2018.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that books about Melania, and indeed press coverage of them \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/02/melania-trump-new-book-roger-stone-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tend to be eagerly read}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jul/17/donald-trump-books-leonnig-rucker-bender-wolff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A madman with millions of followers\u8217\'20\'19: what the new Trump books tell us}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House plans to withdraw Chipman's nomination to run ATF - reports\par \par \uc2 The White House plans to withdraw \uc2 David Chipman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/chipman-atf-withdraw/2021/09/09/d5804a3a-1108-11ec-a511-cb913c7e5ba0_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/09/white-house-withdraw-atf-nominee-510811"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chipman had faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/24/nra-republicans-david-chipman-guns-atf-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intense criticism}}}\uc2 , mostly but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/08/03/biden-aft-nominee-resistance-king-502341"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not entirely}}}\uc2  from Republicans, over his advocacy work with the gun control group Giffords.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced Chipman\u8217\'20\'19s nomination {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/08/joe-biden-gun-violence-executive-actions-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in April}}}\uc2 , as part of a broader strategy to crack down on gun violence in the US.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/09/white-house-withdraw-atf-nominee-510811"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2 , the White House has offered Chipman a role at the Justice Department, so he will still likely be a member of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report from July on efforts by Republicans and the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  to block Chipman\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/24/nra-republicans-david-chipman-guns-atf-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NRA and Republicans out to hobble Biden\u8217\'20\'19s choice for top gun law role}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dani Anguiano reports on the coronavirus surge in Medford, Oregon:\par \par \uc2 There was a time earlier this summer when April Rivera and the staff at the drive-through Covid testing site in southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/oregon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oregon}}}\uc2  where she worked had considered closing their doors because demand was so low.\par \par \uc2 Now, hundreds of patients are lining up at the Asante Rogue regional medical center\u8217\'20\'19s testing site in Medford every day, filling the temporary drive-through in a strip mall parking lot. Even the national guard has been called in to help. Some patients are arriving so sick they\u8217\'20\'19ve been taken away in ambulances while still in line.\par \par \uc2 Despite the widespread availability of vaccines, this region of Oregon is in the grip of an intense Covid-19 surge that has filled local hospitals to capacity, overwhelmed healthcare workers and killed 37 people in the last two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Last month, cases in the Medford area in Jackson county were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wweek.com/news/state/2021/08/25/covid-infections-are-rising-faster-in-southwest-oregon-than-anywhere-else-in-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing faster}}}\uc2  than anywhere else in the US, driven by the hyper-contagious Delta variant and a low vaccination rate.\par \par \uc2 On Friday afternoon at the drive-through testing site, under a thick haze of wildfire smoke, a steady stream of patients waited in their cars to receive tests.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/oregon-hospital-coronavirus-unvaccinated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inside an Oregon hospital amid an \u8216\'20\'18absolutely stunning\u8217\'20\'19 Covid surge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to mandate coronavirus vaccinations for all federal workers - reports\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is reportedly expected to announce today that he will require all federal workers to get vaccinated against coronavirus, without any testing option to opt out of the mandate.\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/09/politics/joe-biden-covid-speech/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Among the steps the President will take is signing an executive order requiring all federal workers be vaccinated against Covid-19, with no option of being regularly tested to opt out of the requirement, according to a source familiar with the plans.\par \par \uc2 The President will also sign an executive order directing the same standard be extended to employees of contractors who do business with the federal government. The Department of Defense, the Department of Veterans Affairs, \uc2 Indian Health Service\uc2  and \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  will also complete their previously announced vaccination requirements, which the White House estimates covers 2.5 million workers.\par \par \uc2 Biden announced in July that federal workers would be required to attest to being vaccinated or receive regular coronavirus tests to limit the spread of coronavirus in government workplaces.\par \par \uc2 However, the president has been under intense pressure to ramp up vaccine requirements as coronavirus case numbers have climbed due to the spread of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melody Schreiber reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 As millions of children head back to school across the US, health experts are highlighting a troubling trend: hundreds of thousands of them are testing positive for Covid.\par \par \uc2 More than 250,000 children had new cases in the last week of August, the \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aap.org/en/pages/2019-novel-coronavirus-covid-19-infections/children-and-covid-19-state-level-data-report/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a report published on Tuesday. That\u8217\'20\'19s the highest weekly rate of new pediatric cases since the pandemic began, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a 10% increase in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 With slightly more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#trends_dailycases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1m}}}\uc2  new Covid cases reported in the US during that period, that means one of every four new cases in the country was among children.\par \par \uc2 Children\u8217\'20\'19s hospitals are straining under the spike in cases. About 2,500 children were hospitalized with Covid-19 in the week up to 6 September, which is also more than ever before, data from the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#new-hospital-admissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A total of 750,000 children tested positive between 5 August and 2 September, the AAP said. In the same time period, 54,859 children were admitted to hospitals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#new-hospital-admissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the CDC.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of the pandemic, 5 million children in the US have tested positive for Covid-19 and at least 444 have died, the AAP said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/09/covid-19-cases-children-surging-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid cases among children are surging in the US as students head back to school}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melody Schreiber reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Charlaine was skeptical of the vaccines at first. She wondered how they were created so quickly, and she was wary of the long history of medical experimentation and disregard for Black people like her in the United States.\par \par \uc2 But then Charlaine, a nurse in a neonatal intensive care unit, thought about the disparate health outcomes for people of color in the pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 and knew that she might not receive the same level of care as others if she got sick.\par \par \uc2 She did her research and determined that the mRNA vaccines, which became available to health workers late last year, are safe and effective. Charlaine, who asked to use only her first name to protect her job, got her vaccine in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere we have this virus that is killing, maiming, debilitating people, and I knew that if I was in a position of being sick, I would be treated differently and probably not survive. So that was one layer of protection that I wanted to give myself,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A year and a half into the pandemic, healthcare workers are exhausted, burned out and worried that the worst is far from over. Amid that stress, much attention has been focused on nurses who haven\u8217\'20\'19t received the vaccine, even though the majority of these essential workers have been inoculated. That has left many nurses feeling betrayed, both by their unvaccinated patients and by public perception.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/us-nurses-vaccinated-vaccine-hesitant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Most nurses are vaccinated \u8211\'20\'13 so why do people think health workers are vaccine hesitant? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to outline new strategy to combat Delta variant of coronavirus\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver a speech today on \u8220\'20\'1Chis robust plan to stop the spread of the Delta variant and boost COVID-19 vaccinations,\u8221\'20\'1D according to his official schedule.\par \par \uc2 The White House has said the president will outline six steps to get the virus under control, as case numbers have climbed in recent weeks due to the spread of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  deliver remarks in honor of labor unions during an event in the East Room of the White House. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to lay out these six steps tomorrow because we have more work to do, and we are still at war with the virus and with the Delta variant,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether average Americans\u8217\'20\'19 daily lives would be affected by the president\u8217\'20\'19s new strategy, Psaki replied, \u8220\'20\'1CIt depends on if you\u8217\'20\'19re vaccinated or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of now, 75% of US adults have received at least one vaccine dose, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations_vacc-total-admin-rate-total"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But many Americans, namely children, are still not eligible to get vaccinated, leaving many questions about how schools can remain open in communities with high levels of coronavirus spread. Biden will likely address that very issue this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 2021-09-09T13:34:19Z 2021-09-10T00:49:33Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/fce32644446498bff0ce2b9da91b9ef1be2896d4/0_133_4000_2401/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/fce32644446498bff0ce2b9da91b9ef1be2896d4/0_133_4000_2401/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Biden delivers remarks on his plan to stop the spread of the Delta variant and boost Covid-19 vaccinations, in the State Dinning Room of the White House on Thursday. \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  deliver remarks in honor of labor unions during an event in the East Room of the White House.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210909eh99001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
