\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House derides Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s vow to \u8216\'20\'18eliminate\u8217\'20\'19 rape amid criticism of Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 7,179 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2021\par 00:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  scorns Texas governor\u8217\'20\'19s defense of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banAlexandria Ocasio-Cortez calls Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8216\'20\'18disgusting\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * The White House derided governor Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate\u8221\'20\'1D rape in Texas amid widespread outcry over the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. \u8220\'20\'1CIf Governor Abbott has a means of eliminating all rapists or all rape from the United States, then there\u8217\'20\'19d be bipartisan support for that,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said at her daily briefing. She added that the unrealistic nature of Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s promise underscores \u8220\'20\'1Cwhy women in Texas should have access to healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez similarly mocked Abbott for his \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D of basic biology, after the Texas governor incorrectly said women would have a full six weeks to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (In reality, women are already four weeks pregnant by the time they miss a period.) \u8220\'20\'1CI find Governor Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez told CNN last night. \u8220\'20\'1CHe speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not just ignorance. It\u8217\'20\'19s ignorance that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The city of Richmond officially removed a statue of Confederate general Robert E Lee. The statue, whose pedestal had become covered in Black Lives Matter graffiti to protest its presence in the city, had stood in Richmond for 131 years.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  traveled to California to campaign alongside governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election. The vice-president headlined a Bay Area rally ahead of the election, which will be held on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised unions and reflected upon the loss of AFL-CIO president \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2  at a White House event to mark Labor Day. Speaking two days after the country celebrated Labor Day, Biden thanked union leaders and members for consistently supporting him throughout his political career. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen unions win, workers across the board win. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18whistleblower\u8217\'20\'19 website forced offline\par \par \uc2 Troubles are mounting for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  website used to report violators of the state\u8217\'20\'19s extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation after the site was forced offline by two different web hosting platforms.\par \par \uc2 The site ProLifeWhistleblower.com was removed from its original web host by the provider GoDaddy on Friday before being suspended by its new host, an agency known for providing services to far-right groups .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor all intents and purposes it is offline,\u8221\'20\'1D Ronald Guilmette, a web infrastructure expert, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey are having technical difficulties. My personal speculation is that they are going to have trouble keeping it online moving forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of Tuesday, ProLifeWhistleblower.com redirects to Texas Right to Life\u8217\'20\'19s main website.\par \par \uc2 Created by Texas Right to Life, an evangelical Christian group, the site allowed people to anonymously submit information about potential violations of the new law \u8211\'20\'13 which makes it illegal to help women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the sixth week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/texas-abortion-whistleblower-website-forced-offline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8216\'20\'18whistleblower\u8217\'20\'19 website forced offline }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Revealed: LAPD officers told to collect social media data on every civilian they stop\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2  police department (LAPD) has directed its officers to collect the social media information of every civilian they interview, including individuals who are not arrested or accused of a crime, according to records shared with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Copies of the \u8220\'20\'1Cfield interview cards\u8221\'20\'1D that police complete when they question civilians reveal that LAPD officers are instructed to record a civilian\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and other social media accounts, alongside basic biographical information. An internal memo further shows that the police chief, Michel Moore, told employees that it was critical to collect the data for use in \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestigations, arrests, and prosecutions\u8221\'20\'1D, and warned that supervisors would review cards to ensure they were complete.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/lapd-social-media-monitoring-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 documents}}}\uc2 , which were obtained by the not-for-profit organization the Brennan Center for Justice, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/analysis-opinion/lapd-documents-reveal-use-social-media-monitoring-tools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised concerns about civil liberties}}}\uc2  and the potential for mass surveillance of civilians without justification.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are real dangers about police having all of this social media identifying information at their fingertips,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Levinson-Waldman, a deputy director at the Brennan Center, noting that the information was probably stored in a database that could be used for a wide range of purposes.\par \par \uc2 The Brennan Center conducted a review of 40 other police agencies in the US and was unable to find another department that required social media collection on interview cards (though many have not publicly disclosed copies of the cards). The organization also obtained records about the LAPD\u8217\'20\'19s social media surveillance technologies, which have raised questions about the monitoring of activist groups including Black Lives Matter.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/revealed-los-angeles-police-officers-gathering-social-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: LAPD officers told to collect social media data on every civilian they stop}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 US\u8217\'20\'19s wealthiest 1% are failing to pay $160bn a year in taxes, report finds\par \par \uc2 The wealthiest 1% of Americans are responsible for more than $160bn of lost tax revenue each year, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/featured-stories/the-case-for-a-robust-attack-on-the-tax-gap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new report}}}\uc2  from the US treasury.\par \par \uc2 Natasha Sarin, deputy assistant secretary for economic policy, said: \u8220\'20\'1CA well-functioning tax system requires that everyone pays the taxes they owe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the treasury report, the wealthiest 1% of US taxpayers are responsible for an estimated $163bn in unpaid tax each year, amounting to 28% of the \u8220\'20\'1Ctax gap\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sarin said that tax gap \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe difference between taxes that are owed and collected\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Caround $600bn annually and will mean approximately $7tn of lost tax revenue over the next decade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  proposes closing the tax gap by empowering the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  (\uc2 IRS\uc2 ) to more aggressively pursue unpaid taxes, at a cost of $80bn and in the process helping fund the president\u8217\'20\'19s ambitious domestic economic agenda.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress and lobbyists for business are united in opposition to the proposal to shore up tax enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sheer magnitude of lost revenue is striking,\u8221\'20\'1D Sarin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/featured-stories/the-case-for-a-robust-attack-on-the-tax-gap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt is equal to 3% of GDP, or all the income taxes paid by the lowest earning 90% of taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/us-wealthiest-responsible-yearly-160bn-lost-tax-revenue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US\u8217\'20\'19s wealthiest 1% are failing to pay $160bn a year in taxes, report finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has asked officials appointed to military academy advisory boards by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to resign, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 The 11 officials include former counselor to Trump Kellyanne Conway, former press secretary \uc2 Sean Spicer\uc2  and former national security adviser HR McMaster.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal \u8220\'20\'1Cwas to ensure you have nominees and people serving on these boards who are qualified to serve on them and who are aligned with our core values,\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Former Office of Management and Budget director \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2  on the Naval Academy\u8217\'20\'19s board said he would not resign, noting that appointees usually serve for three years. \u8220\'20\'1CNo. It\u8217\'20\'19s a three year term,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/russvought/status/1435634747854688262"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he tweeted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden vowed to make racial justice the heart of his agenda \u8211\'20\'13 is it still beating?\par \par \uc2 Defying the punishing August heat, the \uc2 Rev Al Sharpton\uc2  recently led a gathering thousands strong through the streets of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital on the 58th anniversary of the March on Washington, when \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  delivered his immortal I Have a Dream speech on that day in 1963.\par \par \uc2 Now, as then, there was an urgency to their march. In statehouses across the country, Republicans are proposing \u8211\'20\'13 and passing \u8211\'20\'13 new voter restrictions that activists say amount to the greatest erosion of voting rights since the Voting Rights Act was passed in 1965, a crowning achievement of the civil rights movement.\par \par \uc2 Speaking near the White House, Sharpton recalled \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/29/us/politics/joe-biden-speech-transcript.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victory-night promise}}}\uc2  to lead the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat battle\u8221\'20\'1D for racial justice. The time to fight had come, the reverend told Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou said the night you won that Black America had your back, and that you were going to have Black Americans\u8217\'20\'19 backs,\u8221\'20\'1D Sharpton said. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, Mr President, they\u8217\'20\'19re stabbing us in the back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since taking office, Biden has placed racial justice at the center of his governing agenda, embedding language that promotes equity into his executive orders, policy proposals and public speeches. \u8220\'20\'1CThe dream of justice for all will be deferred no longer,\u8221\'20\'1D he vowed in his inauguration address. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can deliver racial justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet the escalating fight over voting rights underscores the difficulty Biden faces in his efforts to advance racial equity. It is an issue that is critical to his legacy but one that faces a myriad of political and legal obstacles. From voting rights to policing reform to helping Black farmers and other critical issues, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s racial justice agenda has suffered a wide array of setbacks and delays during his first year in office.\par \par \uc2 Despite controlling the White House and Congress, Democrats have yet to pass a pair of federal elections bills that are the centerpiece of the party\u8217\'20\'19s strategy for beating back the sweep of new voting restrictions in Republican-led states.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/joe-biden-racial-justice-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden vowed to make racial justice the heart of his agenda \u8211\'20\'13 is it still beating?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The White House derided governor Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate\u8221\'20\'1D rape in Texas amid widespread outcry over the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. \u8220\'20\'1CIf Governor Abbott has a means of eliminating all rapists or all rape from the United States, then there\u8217\'20\'19d be bipartisan support for that,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said at her daily briefing. She added that the unrealistic nature of Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s promise underscores \u8220\'20\'1Cwhy women in Texas should have access to healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez similarly mocked Abbott for his \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D of basic biology, after the Texas governor incorrectly said women would have a full six weeks to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (In reality, women are already four weeks pregnant by the time they miss a period.) \u8220\'20\'1CI find Governor Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez told CNN last night. \u8220\'20\'1CHe speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not just ignorance. It\u8217\'20\'19s ignorance that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The city of Richmond officially removed a statue of Confederate general Robert E Lee. The statue, whose pedestal had become covered in Black Lives Matter graffiti to protest its presence in the city, had stood in Richmond for 131 years.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  traveled to California to campaign alongside governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election. The vice-president headlined a Bay Area rally ahead of the election, which will be held on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised unions and reflected upon the loss of AFL-CIO president \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2  at a White House event to mark Labor Day. Speaking two days after the country celebrated Labor Day, Biden thanked union leaders and members for consistently supporting him throughout his political career. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen unions win, workers across the board win. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Texas state senator Wendy Davis, who famously staged an hours-long filibuster in 2013 to protest another restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, criticized governor Greg Abbott \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd comment\u8221\'20\'1D that he will \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate\u8221\'20\'1D rape in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow in the world are you going to do that? And if you have a magic formula for it, why haven\u8217\'20\'19t you done it already?\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. Greg Abbott (R-TX) suggested 'eliminating rape' as a solution to helping rape and incest victims who could be effected by Texas' restrictive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill. "If you have a magic formula for it, why haven't you done it already?" Fmr. Texas State Sen. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/wendydavis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @wendydavis}}}\uc2  responds. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bN1oJKKhcj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bN1oJKKhcj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ayman Mohyeldin Reports (@AymanMSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AymanMSNBC/status/1435690633344266242?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Davis also noted that Texas had the largest backlog of untested rape kits a few years ago, with more than 20,000 kits sitting on shelves.\par \par \uc2 She added that Texas juries are currently allowed to consider the behavior of the rape victim in determining the guilt of an alleged rapist, making it even less likely that victims will feel comfortable bringing criminal charges against their attackers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the entire comment is just absolutely absurd and in no way should it deflect from the crisis that we have in our state right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said. \u8220\'20\'1CAlmost all of our providers have stopped providing abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris criticizes Abbott as she campaigns for Newsom in California\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  criticized Greg Abbott \u8217\'20\'19s defense of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as the vice-president campaigned for governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  in California this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she saw Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments about the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban while watching the morning news today, likely referring to the Republican governor\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate all rapists from the streets of Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris responds to Abbott: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9juO1dlGNo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9juO1dlGNo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1435697038444965895?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The vice-president condemned Abbott for \u8220\'20\'1Carrogantly\u8221\'20\'1D dismissing the concerns of rape survivors, who may now be forced to carry pregnancies to term because of the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to speak those words that were empty words, that were false words, that were fueled with not only arrogance but bravado \u8211\'20\'13 that is not who we want in our leaders,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want in our leaders someone like \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who always speaks the truth on behalf of all the people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom is facing a September 14 recall election, although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/california-recall-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent polls}}}\uc2  have shown a majority of California voters oppose removing the governor from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has lost another legal battle in his campaign to prevent schools from implementing mask mandates.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/florida-mask-mandate-ban-ron-desantis-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A Florida judge ruled on Wednesday that the state cannot enforce a ban on public schools mandating the use of masks to guard against the coronavirus, while an appeals court sorts out whether the ban is ultimately legal.\par \par \uc2 The Leon county circuit judge, John C Cooper, lifted an automatic stay of his decision last week that the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and education officials exceeded their authority by imposing the blanket ban through executive order and hitting pro-mask local school boards with financial penalties.\par \par \uc2 Cooper said the overwhelming evidence before him in a lawsuit by parents challenging the DeSantis ban is that wearing masks does provide some protection for children in crowded school settings, particularly those under 12 for whom no vaccine yet exists.\par \par \uc2 The case will next go before an appellate court in Tallahassee, and DeSantis has expressed confidence that his team will ultimately win the legal fight, despite widespread criticism over the mask mandate ban.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/florida-mask-mandate-ban-ron-desantis-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blow to DeSantis as judge rules Florida cannot enforce mask mandate ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked for the White House\u8217\'20\'19s response to the \uc2 World Health Organization{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/health/2021/09/08/covid-vaccine-masks-mandates-cdc/5760439001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for}}}\uc2  a moratorium on coronavirus vaccine booster shots through the end of the year to help get more doses to lower-income countries.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki says the WHO's call to halt Covid booster shots is a "false choice," saying the U.S. will continue to donate vaccines to countries while providing a third dose to Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LQiW1PKObS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LQiW1PKObS}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ghj4HjJaHH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ghj4HjJaHH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg Quicktake (@Quicktake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Quicktake/status/1435683171387969539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur view is that this is a false choice,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said, noting the US has shared about 140 million vaccine doses with more than 90 countries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, the president and this administration has a responsibility to do everything we can to protect people in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd as our health advisers have recommended additional booster shots, we are working to implement that. Our view is we can do both.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The daily White House press briefing has now concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 One reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether average Americans\u8217\'20\'19 daily lives will be affected by the pandemic-related initiatives that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to outline tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt depends on if you\u8217\'20\'19re vaccinated or not,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are six steps the president is announcing. There will be new components.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech tomorrow comes amid concerns that travel over Labor Day weekend may cause a surge in coronavirus infections in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Psaki mocks Abbott's pledge to 'eliminate' rape amid criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked for her response to Texas governor Greg Abbott \u8217\'20\'19s latest defense of the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in his state.\par \par \uc2 Asked yesterday why rape and incest victims should be forced to carry a pregnancy to term, Abbott pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate all rapists from the streets of Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIf Governor Abbott has a means of eliminating all rapists or all rape from the U.S. then there\u8217\'20\'19d be bipartisan support for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WH Press Sec. \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  responds to Gov. Greg Abbott (R-TX) defending 6-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban by claiming he\u8217\'20\'19ll "eliminate all rapists\u8221\'20\'1D from Texas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oY5D1c3ojN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oY5D1c3ojN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1435679934383538183?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, if Governor Abbott has a means of eliminating all rapists or all rape from the United States, then there\u8217\'20\'19d be bipartisan support for that,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut given there has never in the history of the country, in the world been any leader who\u8217\'20\'19s ever been able to eliminate rape, eliminate rapists from our streets, it\u8217\'20\'19s even more imperative -- it\u8217\'20\'19s one of the many reasons I should say, not the only reason -- why women in Texas should have access to healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Progressive congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/08/texas-abortion-comments-aoc-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-6138b65f8f08d78b49870973#block-6138b65f8f08d78b49870973"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has similarly mocked}}}\uc2  Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments, accusing the Republican governor of endangering Texans through his \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , has now taken over the podium in the briefing room, and she kicked off her comments by previewing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks on the coronavirus pandemic tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Psaki noted Biden is meeting with members of the White House pandemic response team today in preparation for his speech tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 In the speech, Biden will lay out \u8220\'20\'1Csix steps to stop the spread of Delta and increase vaccinations,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. She noted the president\u8217\'20\'19s latest initiatives will build upon policies he has enacted over the past few months.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brian Deese, the director of the National Economic Council, noted that major poultry and beef suppliers saw record of near-record profits in the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, consumers are dealing with disproportionate price increases in those sectors, which account for half of the overall recent rise in grocery prices.\par \par \uc2 Deese said the Biden administration is looking closely at what may be motivating these price increases to ensure that companies are not taking advantage of consumers amid a global pandemic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing, and she is joined by agriculture secretary Tom Vilsack and Brian Deese, the director of the National Economic Council.\par \par \uc2 Deese discussed the recent increase in the cost of groceries, and he noted that much of the rise is due to the higher prices of beef, poultry and pork.\par \par \uc2 Due to the the level of corporate consolidation in those industries, Deese expressed concern about the possibility of \u8220\'20\'1Cpandemic profiteering\u8221\'20\'1D by companies as Americans pay more at their supermarkets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas: how the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban empowers anti-choice citizens to sue\par \par \uc2 Marie Solis writes for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Last week, the most severe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction in the country became law in Texas. SB8 is a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which amounts to more or less an outright ban, since many people don\u8217\'20\'19t know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant until after the six-week mark. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the state have estimated that the law bans somewhere between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/courts_law/texas-six-week-abortion-ban/2021/09/01/e53cf372-0a6b-11ec-a6dd-296ba7fb2dce_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85% and 90%}}}\uc2  of the procedures they provide.\par \par \uc2 But perhaps the most shocking part of the law is how it\u8217\'20\'19s enforced: SB8 is enforced not by the state attorney general or other government officials, but by private citizens, who are encouraged to snitch on people who violate the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban by filing civil lawsuits against them. (And they are promised a minimum of $10,000 in \u8220\'20\'1Cdamages\u8221\'20\'1D if they win the suit \u8211\'20\'13 what \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters are calling a \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty\u8221\'20\'1D.) The threat of litigation and financial ruin has forced clinics across the state to comply with the law, even though its core principle \u8211\'20\'13 banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is still unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 This legal mechanism has made it impossible for reproductive rights groups to pre-empt the law, since they can\u8217\'20\'19t name the typical state enforcers as the defendants in their suits. The supreme court has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/02/sonia-sotomayor-dissent-texas-abortion-ban-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to intervene}}}\uc2 , arguing in a Wednesday night {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/06/supreme-court-trump-texas-abortion-law-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shadow docket decision}}}\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers didn\u8217\'20\'19t sufficiently address the \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplex and novel antecedent procedural questions\u8221\'20\'1D in their emergency appeal.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  spoke with Rupali Sharma, senior counsel and director at the Lawyering Project, who explained the legal mechanism that has allowed SB8 to go into effect and, as a practical matter, ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/texas-abortion-vigilantes-sb8-citizens-sue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  vigilantes: how the ban empowers anti-choice citizens to sue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  is bracing for potential violence on September 18, when far-right protesters are expected to arrive in Washington for a rally in support of the January 6 insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/08/politics/capitol-hill-security-september-18-rally/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement officials are bracing for potential clashes and unrest during an upcoming right-wing rally in Washington, DC, as violent rhetoric surrounding the September 18 event has increased online and counter protests are being planned for the same day, according to an internal Capitol Police memo reviewed by CNN.\par \par \uc2 The latest intelligence report on the \u8216\'20\'18Justice for J6\u8217\'20\'19 rally \u8212\'20\'14 which aims to support insurrectionists charged in the Capitol riots \u8212\'20\'14 notes that online chatter in support of the event started increasing after the officer who fatally shot rioter Ashli Babbitt went public with his identity in a recent interview with NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Lester Holt.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been a noticeable uptick in violent rhetoric around the event and heated discussions centered on Babbitt\u8217\'20\'19s shooting on social media and discussion boards, according to the memo. The document warns that many individuals may also see September 18 as a \u8216\'20\'18Justice for Ashli Babbitt\u8217\'20\'19 rally, which could be cause for concern, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not unreasonable to plan for violent altercations. There\u8217\'20\'19s also been additional discussions of violence associated with the event, with one online chat suggesting violence against Jewish centers and liberal churches while law enforcement is distracted that day.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Capitol security protocols in preparation for the rally, House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  told reporters earlier today, \u8220\'20\'1CWe intend to have the integrity of the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  be intact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C \uc2 Taliban\uc2  government fails inclusivity test \u8221\'20\'1D seems a little bit like \u8220\'20\'1CPope found to be Catholic\u8221\'20\'1D as news lines go, but there it is on the wires after comments from the secretary of state, \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2 , today, the day the new government of Afghanistan was announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re assessing the announcement but despite professing that a new government would be inclusive, the announced list of names consists exclusively of individuals who are members of the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  or their close associates, and no women,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken told reporters earlier, adding that the Biden administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned by the affiliations and track records of some of those individuals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As Reuters reports, Blinken and his German counterpart \uc2 Heiko Maas\uc2  today \u8220\'20\'1Cconvened a virtual meeting of 22 foreign ministers plus officials from Nato, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the United Nations. Blinken said all those in the meeting agreed on the need to hold the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  accountable before giving the new government legitimacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Taliban\uc2  seek international legitimacy and support. Any legitimacy, any support, will have to be earned,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a report from Peter Beaumont:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/afghan-women-to-be-banned-from-playing-sport-taliban-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghan women to be banned from playing sport, Taliban say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lee statue removed in Richmond\par \par \uc2 For 131 years it loomed over Richmond, once the capital of America\u8217\'20\'19s slave-owning south, sending a chilling message about the resilience of white supremacy to generations that passed beneath.\par \par \uc2 But at 8.55am on Wednesday, daylight reappeared between a giant statue of Confederate general Robert E Lee and its granite pedestal, now covered with Black Lives Matter graffiti. In warm sunshine the towering sculpture was hoisted by work crews and lowered to the ground {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/08/robert-e-lee-statue-confederate-general-richmond-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid cheers, songs and whoops from a watching crowd}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A statue of Confederate general Robert E Lee is removed in Richmond, Virginia. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 No one believed that the final humbling of insurrectionist Lee or the removal of a bronze monument, albeit one of the biggest to the Confederacy, was going to fix systemic racism overnight. But in the moment there was elation after a decades-long campaign galvanised by racial justice protests that followed the police killing of George Floyd in faraway Minneapolis last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a beautiful day for democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said a 47-year-old man who gave his name as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/usarmyoverlord"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rig}}}\uc2  and carried a monochrome version of the Stars and Stripes that bore the words \u8220\'20\'1CBlack Lives Matter and a raised fist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for us to be honest about our history. Germany has zero statues of Hitler or Rommel. They learned the lesson and we have not learn the lesson: we cannot coddle white supremacy in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Darren Soto\uc2 , a Florida Democrat, announced this morning that he has tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDarrenSoto/status/1435601648102084612"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful to only have mild symptoms, which I credit to the vaccine. I am currently self-isolating and working remotely. I encourage everyone to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GetVaccinated?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GetVaccinated}}}\uc2  to save lives!\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis morning I also received monoclonal antibody treatment to further reduce potential symptoms. This treatment is helpful but not a substitute for the Covid-19 vaccine. I encourage everyone to get vaccinated as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The running tally of members of Congress to have contracted breakthrough cases of Covid-19 after vaccination: six House members, four senators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/08/politics/darren-soto-tests-positive-covid/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Breakthrough cases remain very rare. The vast majority of hospitalisations and deaths from Covid-19 in the US are among unvaccinated people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez mocked Greg Abbott for his \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D of basic biology, after the Texas governor defended the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban by incorrectly saying women would have a full six weeks to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (In reality, women are already four weeks pregnant by the time they miss a period.) \u8220\'20\'1CI find Governor Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez told CNN last night. \u8220\'20\'1CHe speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not just ignorance. It\u8217\'20\'19s ignorance that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is traveling to California to campaign alongside governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election. The vice-president will headline a Bay Area rally ahead of the election, which will be held on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised unions and reflected upon the loss of AFL-CIO president \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2  at a White House event to mark Labor Day. Speaking two days after the country celebrated Labor Day, Biden thanked union leaders and members for consistently supporting him throughout his political career. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen unions win, workers across the board win. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his remarks on labor unions, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  noted that his wife, Jill Biden, is a member of the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , the largest teachers\u8217\'20\'19 union in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd by the way, of course, I sleep with an NEA member every night,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president then highlighted the first lady\u8217\'20\'19s return to the classroom yesterday. Jill Biden had her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/jill-biden-returns-classroom-working-first-lady-n1278586"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first day back}}}\uc2  at Northern Virginia Community College on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After concluding his prepared remarks, Biden stepped into the crowd to say hi to some of the union leaders and members who attended the White House event. He did not appear to take any questions from reporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  subtly mocked his predecessor, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in his remarks praising unions to mark the country\u8217\'20\'19s celebration of Labor Day this week.\par \par \uc2 Discussing the health of the US economy, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, the stock market\u8217\'20\'19s gone up exponentially since I\u8217\'20\'19ve been president. You haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard me say a word about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump famously touted the strength of the stock market as an indication of the success of his economic agenda, but he insisted he bore no responsibility for the markets\u8217\'20\'19 decline after the coronavirus pandemic started.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden praises unions and remembers Trumka to mark Labor Day\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking at the event to honor unions at the White House, after the US celebrated Labor Day earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The president asked for a moment of silence to recognize the essential workers and union leaders who had died in the past year and a half, including the late AFL-CIO president \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden holds a moment of silence at the White House honoring union and essential workers who died of COVID-19 and \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2 , the AFL-CIO president who died last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Nj065CIsxp}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tn1fALLOUp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tn1fALLOUp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1435635486991785992?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden emphasized that unions would \u8220\'20\'1Calways be welcome\u8221\'20\'1D in the White House as long as he is president, and he thanked union leaders and members for their support over his political career.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen unions win, workers across the board win. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CFamilies win. Communities win. America wins. We grow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler, who recently took over as the head of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  after the death of \uc2 Richard Trumka\uc2 , received a standing ovation when she spoke at the labor event.\par \par \uc2 Shuler called for the passage of the PRO Act to protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize. The legislation has already passed the House, but it currently has no path forward in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Labor secretary \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2  is now speaking at the White House event to honor union leaders, after the US recognized Labor Day earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Walsh and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  received a standing ovation from attendees as they kicked off the event in the East Room.\par \par \uc2 Walsh told the crowd that Biden said to labor leaders backstage before the event, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is labor\u8217\'20\'19s house.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow often do you hear that?\u8221\'20\'1D the labor secretary said to more applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to soon deliver remarks on labor unions at the White House, following the country\u8217\'20\'19s celebration of Labor Day on Monday. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 enltrWaiting for President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  to give remarks on labor unions before a masked audience at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WhiteHouse}}}\uc2  today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/azYyGPL5pr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/azYyGPL5pr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nikki Schwab (@NikkiSchwab) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikkiSchwab/status/1435627544259309582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is convening an expanded group of western nations to set a framework for cooperation with the new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taliban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban}}}\uc2  government, amid fears that isolating the militant group could backfire.\par \par \uc2 The meeting on Wednesday, chaired by the US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2 , and the German foreign minister, \uc2 Heiko Maas\uc2 , faces an all-male, Pashtun-dominated caretaker government that has ignored calls to form an inclusive administration.\par \par \uc2 The virtual meeting, convening as many as 20 nations, will run through a familiar set of conditions for cooperation with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , including free movement for Afghan and foreign nationals who wish to leave, protection of rights for women and a commitment to protect aid workers.\par \par \uc2 The meeting is likely to discuss the terms for giving humanitarian aid, after the \uc2 UN\uc2  warned this week that the Afghan economy was on the brink of collapse.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/us-led-meeting-set-out-framework-taliban-cooperation-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-led meeting to set out framework for Taliban cooperation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to return to in-person arguments next month\par \par \uc2 The supreme court intends to return to hearing in-person arguments starting next month, although the court is still restricting public access to the building.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-courts-coronavirus-pandemic-3d8f33e6db3d31e09ff102b7d6ccf285"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The high court announced Wednesday that the justices plan to return to their majestic, marble courtroom for arguments beginning in October, more than a year and a half after the in-person sessions were halted because of the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The court said that oral arguments scheduled for October, November and December will be in person but that: \u8216\'20\'18Out of concern for the health and safety of the public and Supreme Court employees, the Courtroom sessions will not be open to the public.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The court said that while lawyers will no longer argue by telephone, the public will continue to be able to hear the sessions live.\par \par \uc2 The court had been hearing arguments by phone since the start of the pandemic, leading to some very comical moments where justices forgot to unmute themselves for questioning.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I'm sorry, Chief. I did it again." - Justice Sotomayor, after a silence in which she apparently forgets to unmute herself during the second telephone oral argument at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Todd Ruger (@ToddRuger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ToddRuger/status/1257677284699443202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2020}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was asked about Capitol security ahead of the \u8220\'20\'1CJustice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally, which is being held in support of the insurrectionists who carried out the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe intend to have the integrity of the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  be intact,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said of the rally, which will be held on September 18. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going into any specifics in that regard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerPelosi}}}\uc2  on security measures for upcoming September 18th "Justice for J6\u8221\'20\'1D rally: "We intend to have the integrity of the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  be intact."\par \par \uc2 Full video here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IEDhE2Vp4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IEDhE2Vp4k}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WgTwEClUDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WgTwEClUDF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1435614402246500356?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi went on to criticize congressional Republicans who have downplayed the violence of the January 6 insurrection, which resulted in several deaths.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven after all of that, a majority of the Republicans in the House voted not to accept the certification of the electoral college,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now these people are coming back to praise the people who were out to kill -- out to kill members of Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said congressional Democrats have \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral options\u8221\'20\'1D to raise the debt ceiling and will not be including it in their $3.5tn spending package.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t be putting it in reconciliation,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi told reporters at her weekly press conference.\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders have repeatedly said that Congress should be able to raise the debt ceiling in a bipartisan fashion, as lawmakers did when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans have insisted they will not help raise the debt ceiling, despite the severe economic risk of not doing so. Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has demanded that Democrats include a debt ceiling hike in their reconciliation bill, which will not require any Republican support to pass.\par \par \uc2 The debt ceiling is one of many issues that Congress will have to tackle when members return from their August recess later this month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is now holding her weekly press conference, as Congress prepares to return to session after its August recess.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker began her comments by listing some of the country\u8217\'20\'19s recent extreme weather events, including Hurricane Ida, and emphasizing the need to address the climate crisis through national legislation.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Mother Nature is not happy with us": Pelosi calls for Congress to pass bipartisan initiatives addressing the climate crisis, but says "the fossil fuel industry weighs in very heavily with some of the people on the other side of the aisle" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vk4cxpmoKo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vk4cxpmoKo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1435607700625399816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMother Nature is not happy with us in terms of how we recognize that challenges face us,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CClimate crisis is real. Human behavior has an impact on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The press conference comes one day after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  toured neighborhoods in New Jersey and New York that have been severely impacted by flooding from Ida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe got to listen to the scientists and the economists and the national security experts,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in Queens yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey all tell us this is code red; the nation and the world are in peril. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not hyperbole. That is a fact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris travels to California to campaign with Newsom\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is traveling to California today to campaign with Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who is facing the threat of a recall election.\par \par \uc2 Harris will headline a rally for Newsom in the Bay Area, ahead of the Tuesday election.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  boards Air Force Two prior to departure from Joint Base Andrews in Maryland. Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The vice-president had originally been scheduled to campaign with Newsom late last month, but she canceled her appearance because of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/26/afghanistan-large-explosion-hits-entry-gate-kabul-airport"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terrorist attack}}}\uc2  at the Kabul airport.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , said yesterday that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will also travel to California \u8220\'20\'1Cearly next week\u8221\'20\'1D to campaign with Newsom.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/california-recall-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Recent polls}}}\uc2  indicate Newsom has mitigated the threat of being recalled since last month, when surveys showed Californians were evenly split on whether to remove the governor from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 United Nations human rights monitors have strongly condemned the state of Texas for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which they say violates international law by denying women control over their own bodies and endangering their lives.\par \par \uc2 In damning remarks to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , Melissa Upreti, the chair of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/issues/women/wgwomen/pages/wgwomenindex.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN\u8217\'20\'19s working group on discrimination against women and girls}}}\uc2 , criticized the new Texas law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/text/SB8/id/2395961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 8}}}\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1Cstructural sex and gender-based discrimination at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She warned that the legislation, which bans abortions at about six weeks, could force \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers underground and drive women to seek unsafe procedures that could prove fatal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis new law will make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsafe and deadly, and create a whole new set of risks for women and girls. It is profoundly discriminatory and violates a number of rights guaranteed under international law,\u8221\'20\'1D the human rights lawyer from Nepal said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/un-experts-condemn-texas-anti-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN experts condemn Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law as sex discrimination \u8216\'20\'18at its worst\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Kari Paul reports:\par \par \uc2 Troubles are mounting for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  website used to report violators of the state\u8217\'20\'19s extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation after the site was forced offline by two different web hosting platforms.\par \par \uc2 The site ProLifeWhistleblower.com was removed from its original web host by the provider GoDaddy on Friday before being suspended by its new host, an agency known for providing services to far-right groups .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor all intents and purposes it is offline,\u8221\'20\'1D Ronald Guilmette, a web infrastructure expert, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey are having technical difficulties. My personal speculation is that they are going to have trouble keeping it online moving forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of Tuesday, ProLifeWhistleblower.com redirects to Texas Right to Life\u8217\'20\'19s main website.\par \par \uc2 Created by Texas Right to Life, an evangelical Christian group, the site allowed people to anonymously submit information about potential violations of the new law \u8211\'20\'13 which makes it illegal to help women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the sixth week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, internet users have protested against the site by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-tiktok-reddit-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flooding it with false reports}}}\uc2 , memes and even porn in the hopes of rendering it less effective.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/texas-abortion-whistleblower-website-forced-offline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8216\'20\'18whistleblower\u8217\'20\'19 website forced offline }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 AOC mocks Abbott's 'deep ignorance' of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after defending six-week ban\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Democrats across the country remain outraged by the Texas law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a point at which many women don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Asked yesterday about why rape or incest victims would be forced to carry a pregnancy to term, Republican governor Greg Abbott replied that women still had six weeks to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate all rapists from the streets of Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Responding to Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments last night, Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez noted that by the time a woman misses a period, she is already four weeks pregnant. So it is not true that a woman has six weeks to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr"He speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it's not just ignorance. It's ignorance that's hurting people."\par \par \uc2 Democratic Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez slams Texas's GOP Gov. Abbott for defending the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law by saying he's working to "eliminate all rapists." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lAGG731QGP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lAGG731QGP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anderson Cooper 360\u176\'00\'B0 (@AC360) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AC360/status/1435401902393544707?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find Governor Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez said.\par \par \uc2 The progressive congresswoman also noted that many rape victims are assaulted by people they know and often choose not to bring criminal charges against their perpetrators, underscoring the unrealistic nature of Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate\u8221\'20\'1D rapists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not just ignorance. It\u8217\'20\'19s ignorance that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting people,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez said.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 2021-09-08T13:40:30Z 2021-09-09T00:21:42Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/20ad95414dc6666580eed3846168fe04e19daf54/0_169_5117_3072/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/20ad95414dc6666580eed3846168fe04e19daf54/0_169_5117_3072/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the White House press secretary, on Wednesday. A statue of Confederate general Robert E Lee is removed in Richmond, Virginia. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  boards Air Force Two prior to departure from Joint Base Andrews in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210908eh98001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
