\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden administration sues Texas over \u8216\'20\'18clearly unconstitutional\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 748 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2021\par 22:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detectedKamala Harris says reproductive rights are \u8216\'20\'18non-negotiable\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration sued Texas on Thursday over the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which amounts to a near total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling the law \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , said the law that went into effect last week after the supreme court refused to block it and bans almost all abortions in the state was one \u8220\'20\'1Call Americans should fear\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Senate bill 8, pushed through by Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature, bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks. Most women are not aware they are pregnant as early as that time.\par \par \uc2 The justice department decided to argue that the law, which offers no exceptions for rape or incest, \u8220\'20\'1Cillegally interferes with federal interests\u8221\'20\'1D, the Wall Street Journal first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-prepares-to-sue-texas-over-abortion-law-11631151641?mod=e2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Later on Thursday, Vice-President Kamala Harris said the right of women to make their own choices on reproductive rights and decisions about \u8220\'20\'1Ctheir own bodies\u8221\'20\'1D was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot negotiable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and her support for the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade decision}}}\uc2  from 1973, which paved the way for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal across the US, was \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 VP Kamala Harris voiced her support to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive health providers during a meeting Thursday to discuss the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe right of women to make decisions about their own bodies is not negotiable,\u8221\'20\'1D she said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iRtofLrmRW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iRtofLrmRW}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg Quicktake (@Quicktake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Quicktake/status/1436067541110099969?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 On Monday Garland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/doj-texas-abortion-law-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the justice department would \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect those seeking to obtain or provide reproductive health services\u8221\'20\'1D, under a federal law known as the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances.\par \par \uc2 Garland said that law would be enforced \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to protect the constitutional rights of women and other persons, including access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/08/texas-abortion-vigilantes-sb8-citizens-sue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 incentivizes any private citizen}}}\uc2  to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or anyone deemed to have helped a women get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  contravening the law. It came into effect on 1 September, and survived an emergency appeal to the supreme court, which voted 5-4 to allow the law to remain in force.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, when announcing the lawsuit, Garland said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe act is clearly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and said that it failed to give women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  their constitutional right \u8220\'20\'1Cat the very moment they need it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And he added that the \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of scheme\u8221\'20\'1D that Texas has devised and other states want to follow, where the public enforces the law as a way to avoid legal challenge, and allows individuals to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or those helping a woman obtain the service, was designed to \u8220\'20\'1Cnullify the constitution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the new law and reaffirmed the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CThis extreme {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  law blatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v Wade and upheld as a precedent for nearly half a century,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has since been under pressure to act, with Democrats on the House judiciary committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/uploadedfiles/2021-09-07_hjc_dems_to_ag_garland.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing to Garland}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, although many experts believe that winning the lawsuit will be a challenge for the federal government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department of Justice cannot permit private individuals seeking to deprive women of the constitutional right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to escape scrutiny under existing federal law simply because they attempt to do so under the color of state law,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote the Democratic members of Congress, who include \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 , representative for Washington, and Val Demings, from Florida.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law is the strictest legislation enacted against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the United States since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark Roe v Wade decision in 1973. At least 12 other states have enacted bans early in pregnancy, but all have been blocked from going into effect.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers have said the law will probably force many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Texas to ultimately close. Women\u8217\'20\'19s rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fear}}}\uc2  the conservative-dominated supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s lack of action over the law could signal the start of the unravelling of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Harris said on Thursday that no legislative body had the right to circumvent the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who was speaking to reporters at a meeting with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and patients, said the right of women to make decisions about their own bodies was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot negotiable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210909eh990020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
