\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 AOC on Texas governor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18disgusting\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  remarks: \u8216\'20\'18He is not familiar with a female body\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 887 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2021\par 13:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Congresswoman explains basic biology to Greg Abbott after he claimed six weeks was ample time to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Democrats including the New York congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez have decried Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ignorance\u8221\'20\'1D after the Texas governor inaccurately defended his state\u8217\'20\'19s new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, saying that it does not require victims of rape and incest to carry pregnancies to term because it provides ample time for a person to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2 , which took effect on 1 September, is the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure in the US and essentially bans most abortions, offering no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Asked by a reporter on Tuesday why he would \u8220\'20\'1Cforce a rape or incest [survivor] to carry a pregnancy to term\u8221\'20\'1D, Abbott denied that was the case, saying the law \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t require that at all because, obviously, it provides at least six weeks for a person to be able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AC360/status/1435401902393544707?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1435401902393544707%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bostonglobe.com%2F2021%2F09%2F08%2Fnation%2Fdisgusting-aoc-criticizes-governor-abbott-over-defense-texas-abortion-law%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusting\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI do know that he is not familiar with a female or menstruating person\u8217\'20\'19s body because if he [was], he would know you don\u8217\'20\'19t have six weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cortez went on to explain the basic biology surrounding pregnancies, and that many pregnancies are often undetected at six weeks. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CIn case no one has informed him before in his life, six weeks pregnant means two weeks late on your period. And two weeks late on your period, for any person with a menstrual cycle, can happen if you\u8217\'20\'19re stressed, if your diet changes, or for really no reason at all. So you don\u8217\'20\'19t have six weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cortez added: \u8220\'20\'1CHe speaks from such a place of deep ignorance, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not just ignorance. It\u8217\'20\'19s ignorance that\u8217\'20\'19s hurting people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulianCastro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Juli\u225\'00\'E1n Castro}}}\uc2 , a former Democratic presidential candidate and mayor of San Antonio, tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CGreg Abbott is lying. Many women don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant by the six-week mark when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is outlawed in this bill. Rape and incest victims would be forced to carry a pregnancy to term at that point \u8211\'20\'13 or face civil lawsuits for getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While defending the radical new law and its lack of exemptions for victims of sexual violence, the governor also vowed to purge the state of all rape and sexual assault.\par \par \uc2 Abbott said: \u8220\'20\'1CRape is a crime and Texas will work tirelessly to make sure that we eliminate all rapists from the streets of Texas by aggressively going out and arresting them and prosecuting them and getting off the streets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , mocked those comments at a briefing on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, if Governor Abbott has a means of eliminating all rapists or all rape from the United States, then there\u8217\'20\'19d be bipartisan support for that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  state senator Wendy Davis, who memorably staged an hours-long filibuster in 2013 to protest another restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, also derided the \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd comment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow in the world are you going to do that? And if you have a magic formula for it, why haven\u8217\'20\'19t you done it already?\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 And the Texas state representative Gene Wu mocked Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s answers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeneforTexas/status/1435426312861085696?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweeting}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Abbott had a solution to end all rape and he sat on it until now? Does it involve a horse dewormer?\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/jul/16/huge-study-supporting-ivermectin-as-covid-treatment-withdrawn-over-ethical-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ivermectin,}}}\uc2  an anti-parasitic drug mostly used on animals that has been falsely promoted by rightwing figures worldwide for treating Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, the \uc2 Texas department of public safety{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dps.texas.gov/sites/default/files/documents/crimereports/19/cit2019.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2  more than 14,650 cases of rape, constituting nearly a quarter of all violent crimes across the state. Fewer than 3,900 people were arrested for rape and other sexual offenses.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez fired back at Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s comments about eradicating rapists, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of people who are raped or are sexually assaulted are assaulted by someone that they know. These aren\u8217\'20\'19t just predators that are walking around the streets at night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez, who in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/01/aoc-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-sexual-assault-survivor-capitol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  revealed}}}\uc2  that she is a sexual assault survivor, went on to say: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen something like that happens, it takes a very long time \u8230\'20\'26 for any victim to come forward. Second of all, when a victim comes forward, they don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily want to bring their case into the carceral system. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want to re-traumatize themselves by going to court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily want to report a family friend to a police precinct, let alone in the immediate aftermath of the trauma of sexual assault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the US\u8217\'20\'19s most radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law continue to face backlash, the Department of Justice on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/doj-texas-abortion-law-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  vowed}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect the constitutional rights of women and other persons, including access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joan E Greve contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Information and support for anyone affected by rape or sexual abuse issues is available from the following organizations. In the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rainn.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rainn}}}\uc2  offers support on 800-656-4673. In the UK, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rapecrisis.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rape Crisis}}}\uc2  offers support on 0808 802 9999. In Australia, support is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1800respect.org.au/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1800Respect}}}\uc2  (1800 737 732). Other international helplines can be found at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210908eh980028p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
