\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden surveys Hurricane Ida damage and warns \u8216\'20\'18climate change was here\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 7,379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2021\par 00:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden to tour neighborhoods affected by last week\u8217\'20\'19s huge stormAbbott says \u8216\'20\'18election integrity is now law in the state of Texas\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  toured New Jersey and New York neighborhoods impacted by Hurricane Ida. Delivering remarks in Queens, the president said the dangerous flooding caused by Ida demonstrated the threat that climate change poses. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are beginning to realize this is much, much bigger than anyone was willing to believe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in Queens. \u8220\'20\'1CEven the climate skeptics are seeing that this really does matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration requested $30bn in additional funding to respond to natural disasters and resettle Afghan refugees. As Congress prepares to craft a short-term continuing resolution to keep the government funded past the end of the month, the administration asked for $24bn to respond to Hurricane Ida and other recent extreme weather events, while also requesting $6.4bn to process and transport Afghan refugees who fled their country last month.\par \par \uc2 * Republican governor Greg Abbott signed a highly controversial voting bill in Texas. The law will prohibit 24-hour and drive-through voting, making it even harder to access the ballot box in a state that already has some of the most burdensome voting requirements in the country. The signing of the bill ends a weeks-long standoff between Democratic and Republican state legislators over the proposal.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said she disagreed with Democratic senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s call for a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations over the $3.5tn spending package. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, obviously I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty excited about where we are. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s working very hard. The committees are doing their work. We\u8217\'20\'19re on a good timetable.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin penned an op-ed last week expressing concern about the price tag of the budget bill, raising concerns that it will not pass the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 An editorial co-published by more than 200 medical and health journals asserting that global heating will cause \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic harm to health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(21)01915-2/fulltext#%20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 editorial}}}\uc2  said that the climate crisis was the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest threat to global public health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe science is unequivocal; a global increase of 1.5C above the preindustrial average and the continued loss of biodiversity risk catastrophic harm to health that will be impossible to reverse,\u8221\'20\'1D it reads. \u8220\'20\'1CIndeed, no temperature rise is \u8216\'20\'18safe\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Authors of the piece included the editors the Lancet and the New England Journal of Medicine.\par \par \uc2 They mentioned both direct and indirect health risks brought on by global heating. Increasingly severe heat and higher temperatures have triggered \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased dehydration and renal function loss, dermatological malignancies, tropical infections, adverse mental health outcomes, pregnancy complications, allergies, and cardiovascular and pulmonary morbidity and mortality\u8221\'20\'1D, they said.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, the effects of climate change on agriculture will drive up malnutrition, they said. And the loss of biodiversity will increase the chance of pandemics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are united in recognising that only fundamental and equitable changes to societies will reverse our current trajectory,\u8221\'20\'1D the authors wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Larry is expected to send rip currents along the East Coast, but isn\u8217\'20\'19t expected to make landfall.\par \par \uc2 enltrHurricane {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Larry?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Larry}}}\uc2  Advisory 29: Large Larry Still a Major Hurricane. Likely to Produce Dangerous Swells Over the Western Atlantic Coast This Week. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VqHn0u1vgc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VqHn0u1vgc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 National Hurricane Center (@NHC_Atlantic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NHC_Atlantic/status/1435345647205371908?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The storm intensified to a category 3 hurricane on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A number of hurricanes and tropical storms have been battering the US and Caribbean. In addition to Ida, there was Julian and Kate \u8211\'20\'13 as well as Tropical Storm Fred and Hurricane Grace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, the evidence is clear: Climate change poses an existential threat to our lives, to our economy,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said today, after surveying the damage from Ida. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the threat is here; it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to get any better. The question: Can it get worse? We can stop it from getting worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court rules criminal penalties for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unconstitutional\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court has struck down a state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, ruling that criminal penalties for terminating pregnancies are unconstitutional, in a decision which advocates say provides a path to decriminalisation across the country.\par \par \uc2 The ruling contrasts sharply with recent actions in the United States to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 most notably across the border from Coahuila in Texas, where legislation \u8211\'20\'13 upheld by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after about six weeks of pregnancy}}}\uc2  and allows citizens to pursue legal actions against women seeking a termination.\par \par \uc2 In a unanimous 10-0 ruling, Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s top court ordered the northern state of Coahuila to remove sanctions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its criminal code \u8211\'20\'13 with several justices arguing the prohibitions on voluntarily interrupting a pregnancy violated women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to control their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not about the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said justice Luis Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Aguilar, who wrote the court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion for overturning the Coahuila law. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s rather the right to decide of women and persons able to gestate to make decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision continues a trend in Latin America towards decriminalization as women waving green handkerchiefs have thronged the streets across the continent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/14/argentina-abortion-legalized-latin-america-reform"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to demand action on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  access and gender violence.\par \par \uc2 Mexico follows Argentina, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers voted in December to decriminalise \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  during the first 14 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling continues a trend from Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court to rule in favour of petitions brought by women seeking abortions for health reasons or due to sexual assault.\par \par \uc2 It also turns back a spate of state-level attempts over the past dozen years to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/jul/29/abortion-banned-controversial-mexican-state-governor-veracruz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrict \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  through constitutional amendments.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/07/mexico-abortion-law-struck-down-supreme-court-penalties-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court rules criminal penalties for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  unconstitutional}}}\par \par \uc2 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The children of 9/11: haunted by their fathers\u8217\'20\'19 last hours, some dread the anniversary\par \par \uc2 Robyn Higley has always hated September. It\u8217\'20\'19s the month when everything bad happens, when her spirits, generally so bright and bubbly the rest of the year, grow bleak and deflated.\par \par \uc2 She feels sad in September. Though she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t fully understand why.\par \par \uc2 As the 20th anniversary of 9/11 approaches, she knows that this September is going to be worse than even the 19 others she has lived through. The media will endlessly reprise that terrible day, there will be an outpouring of patriotic fervor and emoting, and she will be even more on show than in previous years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not like it all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYes I get it, the 20th is a big thing. But there\u8217\'20\'19s so much expectation of how I\u8217\'20\'19m supposed to feel. People expect this grieving little girl who\u8217\'20\'19s so heartbroken. But I\u8217\'20\'19m almost 20 years old, I\u8217\'20\'19m grown up now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s complicated being Robyn Higley around 9/11. How should she grieve for the father whom she never met? What should she make of the label that has been pinned to her throughout her life \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1C9/11 baby\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 when she herself was not even there on that tragic day?\par \par \uc2 On 11 September 2001 her father, Robert Higley \u8211\'20\'13 Robbie as he was known to all \u8211\'20\'13 went to work on the 92nd floor of the south tower of New York\u8217\'20\'19s World Trade Center. An insurance executive, he had started a new job three months before and was excited that day to have been asked to step up as acting manager.\par \par \uc2 When the north tower was struck at 8.46am, Robbie called his wife Vycki and told her that something had happened in the other building but that he was fine. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an agonizingly short conversation when I look back on it now,\u8221\'20\'1D Vycki Higley said.\par \par \uc2 It took Vycki time to piece together what happened next. Her husband helped evacuate 12 of his colleagues, ushering them into an elevator that was one of the last to reach the ground floor before United Airlines flight 175 slammed into the south tower at 9.03am.\par \par \uc2 Robbie didn\u8217\'20\'19t make it out. He chose not to get into the elevator because he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo the managerial thing\u8221\'20\'1D, Vycki said, and make sure everyone else was all right.\par \par \uc2 Vycki was left a widow on 9/11, a single mother caring for her four-year-old daughter Amanda. She was also heavily pregnant with Robyn.\par \par \uc2 By the time Robyn was born seven weeks later, on 3 November 2001, the \u8220\'20\'1C9/11 baby\u8221\'20\'1D was already a celebrity. Such was the level of interest in her as a newborn victim of the twin towers attacks that a camera crew from ABC News\u8217\'20\'19 20/20 was present in the delivery room at her birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was hilarious,\u8221\'20\'1D Robyn said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen my mom went into labour she got to the hospital and found ABC News already waiting for her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robyn Higley is one of 105 children who were in the womb when their fathers were killed in the terrorist attacks in New York, Washington and Shanksville, Pennsylvania. As a member of this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/aug/15/20-years-after-the-world-trade-center-attacks-what-are-the-children-of-911-doing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exceptionally rarified club}}}\uc2 , she entered the world and grew up in an environment in which her identity had already been set for her.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/children-september-11-anniversary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The children of 9/11: haunted by their fathers\u8217\'20\'19 last hours, some dread the anniversary}}}\par \par \uc2 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly 300% more Covid patients in US hospitals at weekend than a year ago\par \par \uc2 The number of Covid-19 patients in hospitals across the US this Labor Day weekend was nearly 300% higher than this time last year, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/map.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2 . The average number of deaths was over 86% higher than the same period last year.\par \par \uc2 The surge in patients comes as the highly contagious Delta variant continues to spread across the US, and coincided with a weekend that saw a spike in travel. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/video/surge-in-covid-labor-day-travel/#x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2 , more than 3.5 million people travelled across the country on Friday and Saturday for the Labor Day holiday, despite the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recommendation for unvaccinated people to refrain from traveling.\par \par \uc2 Hospitalizations and deaths are a lagging indicator of Covid spread, so the impact of people\u8217\'20\'19s travels this week will not be clear right away, but the agency is continuing to advise caution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have actually articulated that people who are fully vaccinated and who are wearing masks can travel,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/wi/milwaukee/news/2021/09/03/cdc-safety-and-health-tips-traveling-labor-day-weekend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , director of the CDC, last week. \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough given where we are with disease transmission right now, we would say that people need to take their own \u8211\'20\'13 these risks \u8211\'20\'13 into their own consideration as they think about traveling,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 This past weekend saw 1.146m weekly cases, compared with 287,235 last year. Despite the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/us/covid-cases.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decline}}}\uc2  in cases in certain states including Florida, other states such as Idaho are seeing hospitals begin to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-health-public-health-coronavirus-pandemic-idaho-db21f9a14254996144e78aafb1518259"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ration}}}\uc2  healthcare amid patient surges.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/us-covid-patients-hospitals-surge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly 300% more Covid patients in US hospitals at weekend than a year ago}}}\par \par \uc2 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  toured New Jersey and New York neighborhoods impacted by Hurricane Ida. Delivering remarks in Queens moments ago, the president said the dangerous flooding caused by Ida demonstrated the threat that climate change poses. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are beginning to realize, this is much, much bigger than anyone was willing to believe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in Queens. \u8220\'20\'1CEven the climate skeptics are seeing that this really does matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration requested $30bn in additional funding to respond to natural disasters and resettle Afghan refugees. As Congress prepares to craft a short-term continuing resolution to keep the government funded past the end of the month, the administration asked for $24bn to respond to Hurricane Ida and other recent extreme weather events, while also requesting $6.4bn to process and transport Afghan refugees who fled their country last month.\par \par \uc2 * Republican governor Greg Abbott signed a highly controversial voting bill in Texas. The law will prohibit 24-hour and drive-thru voting, making it even harder to access the ballot box in a state that already has some of the most burdensome voting requirements in the country. The signing of the bill ends a weeks-long standoff between Democratic and Republican state legislators over the proposal.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said she disagreed with Democratic senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s call for a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations over the $3.5tn spending package. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, obviously I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty excited about where we are. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s working very hard. The committees are doing their work. We\u8217\'20\'19re on a good timetable.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin penned an op-ed last week expressing concern about the price tag of the budget bill, raising concerns that it will not pass the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  criticized lawmakers who have pushed back against his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to respond to the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Queens after touring hurricane-impacted neighborhoods in New York and New Jersey, Biden said that witnessing the devastation from the storm was \u8220\'20\'1Can eyeopener\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people who stand on the other side of the fences, who don\u8217\'20\'19t live there, who are yelling that we\u8217\'20\'19re interfering with free enterprise by doing something about climate change \u8212\'20\'14 they don\u8217\'20\'19t live there. They don\u8217\'20\'19t understand,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president called on Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , who spoke before him, to help him get his Build Back Better agenda through Congress to ensure the nation is better prepared for extreme weather events like hurricanes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe nation and the world are in peril. That\u8217\'20\'19s not hyperbole. That is a fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve been warning us that extreme weather would get more extreme over the decade, and we\u8217\'20\'19re living it in real time now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After concluding his prepared remarks, Biden wrapped up the event without taking questions from reporters.\par \par \uc2 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden emphasizes danger of climate crisis after touring Ida-impacted neighborhoods\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s response to Hurricane Ida and other extreme weather events, which have become more intense and more frequent because of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting upon his tour of Ida-impacted neighborhoods in New Jersey and New York, Biden noted he also visited Louisiana last week to see how the hurricane devastated that state. The president will soon travel to California to witness the effects of recent wildfires as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are beginning to realize, this is much, much bigger than anyone was willing to believe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in Queens. \u8220\'20\'1CEven the climate skeptics are seeing that this really does matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now holding an event in Queens, New York, to outline his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to respond to Hurricane Ida and other extreme weather events, which have become more common because of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 The first speaker at the event was \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , who took over as New York governor late last month, after \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  stepped down over allegations of sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 Hochul introduced herself by saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m New York state governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , and this is my second week on the job.\u8221\'20\'1D That line got some laughs from the small assembled crowd in Queens.\par \par \uc2 Hochul noted that the rainfall caused by Ida broke a record that had been set just 10 days earlier. \u8220\'20\'1CLadies and gentlemen, that is the definition of a climate crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are experiencing a climate crisis as we speak.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now touring a neighborhood in Queens, New York, that was severely impacted by the flooding from Hurricane Ida last week.\par \par \uc2 The president was joined on the tour by Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer and progressive congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, among others.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to soon deliver remarks on hurricane response efforts, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taliban\uc2  name all-male Afghan cabinet including minister wanted by \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Emma Graham-Harrison and Akhtar Mohammad Makoii report:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taliban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban}}}\uc2  have announced an all-male caretaker government including an interior minister wanted by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , on a day when at least two people were killed by violent policing of street protests against the new authorities.\par \par \uc2 The leadership unveiled on Tuesday is drawn entirely from \uc2 Taliban\uc2  ranks, despite promises of an inclusive cabinet, and many of its senior figures are on \uc2 UN\uc2  sanctions lists, which is likely to complicate the group\u8217\'20\'19s search for international recognition.\par \par \uc2 Afghanistan will once more be officially known as an Islamic emirate, as it was under \uc2 Taliban\uc2  rule in the 1990s, and its chief, Hibatullah Akhundzada, will be supreme leader.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  have also brought back the ministry for promotion of virtue and prevention of vice, a notorious enforcement body that was one of the most hated institutions when they last controlled Afghanistan. Its main function was to police the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2001/nov/18/terrorism.afghanistan2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme interpretation}}}\uc2  of Islamic law.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister will be Mullah Mohammad Hassan Akhund, one of the founding members of the group who was close to its original leader, one-eyed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/jul/30/mullah-omar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mullah Mohammed Omar}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/07/taliban-name-afghanistans-new-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban name all-male Afghan cabinet including minister wanted by FBI}}}\par \par \uc2 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden went back to work today, while her husband the president toured the flood-hit north-east.\par \par \uc2 The first lady spent months teaching writing and English remotely before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s return to teaching in person at Northern Virginia Community College, where she has worked since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Biden, 70, is the first first lady to leave the White House to log hours at a full-time job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTeaching,\u8221\'20\'1D she has said, \u8220\'20\'1Cisn\u8217\'20\'19t just what I do. It\u8217\'20\'19s who I am.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the subject, from David Smith in Washington:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/24/jill-biden-first-lady-outside-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jill Biden gives quiet lesson in juggling first lady role with outside job}}}\par \par \uc2 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 One New Jersey family told the president that they lost all their belongings after their home burned and exploded following the flooding from Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 The couple were able to escape the home with their infant daughter, but they now must rebuild from scratch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank God you\u8217\'20\'19re safe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the family.\par \par \uc2 President Biden met with a NJ family whose home burned and exploded after the flooding. They escaped with their infant daughter but lost all their belongings. Watch short video clip of their visit. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hn0orAUwc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hn0orAUwc6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kelly O'Donnell (@KellyO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellyO/status/1435316705593593860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  toured one of the neighborhoods in Manville, New Jersey, that was severely impacted by flooding from Hurricane Ida last week.\par \par \uc2 The president was seen shaking hands and chatting with residents who had been forced to remove belongings from their homes because of flood damage.\par \par \uc2 President Biden tours Hurricane Ida damage in Manville, NJ.\par \par \uc2 Full video here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4Rs7mycXRT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4Rs7mycXRT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a8xiS0I896"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a8xiS0I896}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1435313590404268032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls on Congress to approve $24bn in funds for disaster response after Ida\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is calling on Congress to appropriate more funds for disaster response and Afghan refugee resettlement in its short-term continuing resolution.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/omb/briefing-room/2021/09/07/delivering-for-the-american-people-and-meeting-urgent-needs-in-the-new-fiscal-year/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new statement}}}\uc2 , the acting director of the Office of Management and Budget, Shalanda Young, acknowledged that Congress likely have to pass a continuing resolution to keep the government funded past the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, we are also calling on Congress to include additional funding in a CR to help address two other urgent needs: responding to recent and ongoing natural disasters, and meeting our commitments to our Afghan allies and partners,\u8221\'20\'1D Young said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpecifically, we urge Congress to appropriate over $14 billion as part of a CR to address the natural disasters that occurred prior to Hurricane Ida. We fully expect that Hurricane Ida will significantly increase the need for further disaster response funding, by at least $10 billion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Young also requested $6.4bn in funds to \u8220\'20\'1Cmeet our commitments to Afghan allies and partners,\u8221\'20\'1D as the \uc2 US government\uc2  seeks to resettle tens of thousands of Afghan refugees.\par \par \uc2 If approved, the funds would support refugee processing centers overseas and cover transportation costs as approved Afghans make their way to the US.\par \par \uc2 Young\u8217\'20\'19s statement comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tours neighborhoods in New Jersey and New York that were severely impacted by flooding caused by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The restrictive new Texas voting law is not the only piece of Lone Star legislation attracting condemnation today.\par \par \uc2 United Nations human rights monitors have strongly condemned the state for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which they say violates international law by denying women control over their own bodies and endangering their lives.\par \par \uc2 In damning remarks to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , Melissa Upreti, the chair of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/issues/women/wgwomen/pages/wgwomenindex.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN working group on discrimination against women and girls}}}\uc2 , criticized the new Texas law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/text/SB8/id/2395961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB8}}}\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1Cstructural sex and gender-based discrimination at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She warned that the legislation, which bans abortions at about six weeks, could force \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers underground and drive women to seek unsafe procedures that could prove fatal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis new law will make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsafe and deadly, and create a whole new set of risks for women and girls. It is profoundly discriminatory and violates a number of rights guaranteed under international law,\u8221\'20\'1D the human rights lawyer from Nepal said.\par \par \uc2 Upreti, one of five independent experts charged by the \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights council in Geneva to push for elimination of discrimination against women and girls around the world, was also sharply critical of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week the court\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/06/supreme-court-trump-texas-abortion-law-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided by a 5-4 vote}}}\uc2  to allow the Texas law to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 go ahead}}}\uc2 , despite its blatant disregard of the court\u8217\'20\'19s own 1973 ruling legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe law and the way it came about \u8211\'20\'13 through the refusal of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to block it based on existing legal precedent \u8211\'20\'13 has not only taken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  backward, but in the eyes of the international community, it has taken the entire country backward,\u8221\'20\'1D Upreti said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/un-experts-condemn-texas-anti-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN experts condemn Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law as sex discrimination \u8216\'20\'18at its worst\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden in Jersey: 'Climate change was here'\par \par \uc2 A long way from Texas in New Jersey, of course, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is still touring areas hit by flooding unleashed by the remnants of Hurricane Ida last week.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a taste of what the president said just now in New Jersey: \u8220\'20\'1C For decades, scientists have warned of extreme weather \u8230\'20\'26 and climate change was here. And we\u8217\'20\'19re living through it now. We don\u8217\'20\'19t have any more time \u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re at one of those inflection points where we either act, or we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna be in real, real trouble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19ll find receptive audiences for such rhetoric in Jersey and across the Hudson River in New York, where he\u8217\'20\'19s due to speak later today. State and local leaders have been very clear about what such extreme weather events mean about the new normal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our southern bureau chief, Oliver Laughland, reporting on the fallout from Hurricane Ida further south, in Louisiana:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/i-dont-have-a-choice-hurricane-ida-leaves-devastated-louisiana-communities-struggling-with-new-reality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a choice\u8217\'20\'19: Hurricane Ida leaves devastated Louisiana communities struggling with new reality}}}\par \par \uc2 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Statements are coming in from opponents of the new Texas voting law. Here are some edited versions of some of them:\par \par \uc2 * Derrick Johnson, president, National \uc2 Association for the Advancement of Colored People\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CBlack votes were suppressed today. Texas governor Greg Abbott has intentionally signed away democracy for so many. We are disgusted. This voter suppression bill is undemocratic, unAmerican and even violates core conservative principles. While Greg Abbott and many other governors have confirmed over and over how far they are willing to go to attack Black voters, we will continue to fight twice as hard to defend the right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nina Perales\uc2 , vice-president of litigation, Mexican American Legal Defense and Educational Fund: \u8220\'20\'1CSB1 will reduce voter participation and discriminate on the basis of race, and for those reasons it should be struck down in court. In addition to making voting more difficult for all voters, SB1 is aimed directly at Latinos and Asian Americans with specific provisions that cut back on assistance to limited English-proficient voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Former Texas congressman and presidential candidate \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Abbott is restricting the freedom to vote for millions of Texans. Instead of working on issues that actually matter, like protecting school kids from Covid or fixing our failing electrical grid, Abbott is focused on rigging our elections and implementing extreme, right-wing policies. Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s agenda of criminalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , permit-less carry, anti-mask mandates and voter suppression is killing Texans and limiting their voting rights to elect more responsible leaders.\par \par \uc2 * Claudia Yoli Ferla, executive director, MOVE Texas Action Fund: \u8220\'20\'1CHistory will remember this period as one of democracy in distress; as an era during which our sacred freedom to vote endured unrelenting assault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Republican governor Greg Abbott signed a highly controversial voting bill in Texas. The law will prohibit 24-hour and drive-thru voting, making it even harder to access the ballot box in a state that already has some of the most burdensome voting requirements in the country. The signing of the bill ends a weeks-long standoff between Democratic and Republican state legislators over the proposal.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrived in New Jersey to tour neighborhoods impacted by Hurricane Ida, which caused widespread flooding in the Northeast last week. The president is now receiving a briefing from local leaders on hurricane response efforts, and he will later deliver a speech in Queens, New York, on how his administration is working to better prepare for extreme weather, which has become more common because of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said she disagreed with Democratic senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s call for a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations over the $3.5tn spending package. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, obviously I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty excited about where we are. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s working very hard. The committees are doing their work. We\u8217\'20\'19re on a good timetable.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin penned an op-ed last week expressing concern about the price tag of the budget bill, raising concerns that it will not pass the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine has more details on the Texas voting law:\par \par \uc2 The signing of the bill marks the end of a weeks-long standoff between Democrats and Republicans over the legislation.\par \par \uc2 In late May, Democrats walked out of the legislature, denying Republicans the necessary quorum to pass the initial version of the bill, which would have made it easier for judges to overturn elections and restricted early voting on Sundays, a day traditionally used by African American churches to encourage people to vote.\par \par \uc2 Republicans subsequently cut both provisions from the bill. But before a new version could be considered in a July special session, Democrats in the state house left the state and flew to Washington DC, again denying Republicans a quorum to proceed with legislation.\par \par \uc2 While the Democrats in Washington lobbied federal lawmakers to pass federal voting restrictions, state senator Carol Alvarado undertook a 15-hour filibuster on the senate floor to try and block the measure.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, after Abbott called a second special session to consider the measure, the house speaker, Dade Phelan, signed civil arrest warrants for the Democrats who refused to show up at the capitol (no one was ultimately arrested). But slowly, a trickle of Democrats began to return to the capitol, giving Republicans a majority, and enraging Democrats who wanted to continue to stay away.\par \par \uc2 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports:\par \par \uc2 The voting restrictions will only add to those already in place in Texas, which has some of the most burdensome voting requirements in the US and was among the states with the lowest voter turnout in 2020.\par \par \uc2 The Texas house of representatives gave its approval to a final form of the measure on Tuesday, 80-41. The senate quickly followed with an 18-13 vote Tuesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The bill, nearly identical to a measure that passed the legislature last week, would prohibit 24-hour and drive-thru voting \u8211\'20\'13 two things officials in Harris county, home of Houston, used for the first time in 2020.\par \par \uc2 It would also prohibit election officials from sending out unsolicited applications to vote by mail, give poll watchers more power in the polling place and provide new regulations on those who assist voters.\par \par \uc2 Here is \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report from last week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/texas-legislature-voting-restrictions-bill-final-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas legislature gives final approval to sweeping voting restrictions bill}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Abbott signs highly controversial voting bill in Texas\par \par \uc2 Republican governor Greg Abbott as just signed a highly controversial bill to place new restrictions on voting access in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElection integrity is now law in the state of Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said after signing the bill, which voting right advocates have said unfairly targets people of color.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Greg Abbott (R-TX) signs restrictive voting bill SB1 into law, despite House Democrats fleeing state in attempts to stop its passage:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElection integrity is now law in the state of Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iViAQZZ6SB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iViAQZZ6SB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1435277355610746885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Texas legislature gave its final approval to the bill last Tuesday, after Democrats delayed the passage of the proposal for weeks by fleeing the state.\par \par \uc2 The law will prohibit 24-hour and drive-thru voting and place new restrictions on who can assist people as they seek to cast their ballots, making Texas one of the hardest places to vote in the country.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jason Miller, a former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has released a statement in response to reports that he was detained by authorities in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis afternoon my traveling party was questioned for three hours at the airport in Brasilia, after having attended this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s CPAC Brasil Conference. We were not accused of any wrongdoing, and told only that they \u8216\'20\'18wanted to talk,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Miller.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe informed them that we had nothing to say and were eventually released to fly back to the United States. Our goal of sharing free speech around the world continues!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Miller previously served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson, but he now runs the company Gettr, a social media platform designed for conservatives.\par \par \uc2 According to earlier reports, Miller was detained by Brazilian authorities to answer questions over his alleged anti-democratic activities in the country.\par \par \uc2 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden arrives in New Jersey to receive briefing and tour Ida-affected neighborhoods\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived at Central Jersey Regional Airport in Hillsborough Township for a briefing and a tour of neighborhoods impacted by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 The president was greeted by New Jersey governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  and his wife, Tammy Murphy, as well as three Democratic House members from the state -- \uc2 Tom Malinowski\uc2 , \uc2 Frank Pallone\uc2  and \uc2 Bonnie Watson Coleman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden will soon receive a briefing on hurricane response at the Somerset County Emergency Management Training Center before touring a neighborhood in Manville, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 The president will then travel on to Queens, New York, to deliver remarks on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to better prepare for and respond to hurricanes, which have become more frequent and more intense due to the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin wrote a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/manchin-pelosi-biden-3-5-trillion-reconciliation-government-spending-debt-deficit-inflation-11630605657"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal op-ed}}}\uc2  last week calling for a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in advancing the spending package.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile some have suggested this reconciliation legislation must be passed now, I believe that making budgetary decisions under artificial political deadlines never leads to good policy or sound decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said in the op-ed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI, for one, won\u8217\'20\'19t support a $3.5tn bill, or anywhere near that level of additional spending, without greater clarity about why Congress chooses to ignore the serious effects inflation and debt have on existing government programs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rebuilding our crumbling physical infrastructure \u8211\'20\'13 roads, bridges, water systems \u8211\'20\'13 is important. Rebuilding our crumbling human infrastructure \u8211\'20\'13 health care, education, climate change \u8211\'20\'13 is more important. No infrastructure bill without the $3.5 trillion reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@SenSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1433572638014640128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, the leftwing chairman of the Senate budget committee, responded to Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s warning in kind, threatening to torpedo the bipartisan infrastructure bill if the spending package is not approved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRebuilding our crumbling physical infrastructure \u8211\'20\'13 roads, bridges, water systems \u8211\'20\'13 is important,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CRebuilding our crumbling human infrastructure \u8211\'20\'13 healthcare, education, climate change \u8211\'20\'13 is more important. No infrastructure bill without the $3.5tn reconciliation bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Congress prepares to return from its August recess, Democratic leaders are scrambling to figure out how to advance both bills, which encompass much of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda. If centrists and progressives don\u8217\'20\'19t reach an agreement, both proposals may fail.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/biden-democrats-brewing-battle-budget-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to referee Democrats in brewing battle over $3.5tn budget bill}}}\par \par \uc2 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi disagrees with Manchin over $3.5tn spending package\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said she did not agree with Democratic senator Joe Manchin \u8217\'20\'19s call for a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations over the $3.5tn budget bill due to concerns about deficit spending.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, obviously I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty excited about where we are. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s working very hard. The committees are doing their work. We\u8217\'20\'19re on a good timetable. And I feel very exhilarated by it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi this AM in Capitol: \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, I don't agree\u8221\'20\'1D when I asked her about Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s call to take a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D on $3.5T bill. She also said: \u8220\'20\'1Cwhy?\u8221\'20\'1D when asked about lowering price tag. Asked about Manchin and Sinema: \u8220\'20\'1CWell you have to go talk to the Senate about that\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XnH7d8TLB5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XnH7d8TLB5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1435252892835983362?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A CNN reporter asked Pelosi whether she believed the topline cost of the final bill would be less than $3.5tn because of the criticism from Manchin and fellow Democratic senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, you have to go talk to the Senate about that,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we\u8217\'20\'19re going to pay for as much of it as possible, and it will have far less impact on the national debt than the Republican 2017 tax scam.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will head to California \u8220\'20\'1Cearly next week\u8221\'20\'1D to campaign with governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said moments ago.\par \par \uc2 Newsom is facing a difficult recall election in California, and a number of prominent Democrats have been offering their assistance as the governor fights to remain in office.\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is also scheduled to travel to her home state of California tomorrow to campaign with Newsom.\par \par \uc2 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , there are now less than 100 Americans remaining in Afghanistan who still need to be evacuated.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is receiving regular updates from his national security team as the administration works to evacuate all US citizens seeking to leave Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The Kabul evacuation mission formally ended last week, but Biden pledged the US would continue to work past the deadline to help all Americans still in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now gaggling with reporters aboard Air Force One en route to New Jersey and New York, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will tour neighborhoods affected by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 Psaki confirmed that the president will use the tour as an opportunity to highlight how average Americans are being affected by extreme weather, which has intensified due to the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet, Biden said of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to Hurricane Ida, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working around the clock to ensure impacted areas have the support they need to recover and rebuild.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m on my way to New Jersey and New York to meet with local officials and survey the damage from Ida. We\u8217\'20\'19re working around the clock to ensure impacted areas have the support they need to recover and rebuild.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1435249187076165636?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another White House reporter asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  whether he planned to meet with any of the Afghan refugees who have come to the US since the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  takeover.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, they\u8217\'20\'19re all over the country, and I\u8217\'20\'19m sure I\u8217\'20\'19ll be seeing some of them. And they\u8217\'20\'19re welcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The US military evacuated more than 65,000 Afghans out of the country last month, and tens of thousands of them have already arrived in America.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he plans to meet Afghan refugees, President Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CThey are all over the country. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure I will be seeing some of them\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lMJCXogkRw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lMJCXogkRw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Raquel Kr\u228\'00\'E4henb\u252\'00\'FChl (@Rkrahenbuhl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Rkrahenbuhl/status/1435245637495296002?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now en route to New Jersey and New York, where he will tour neighborhoods affected by Hurricane Ida and deliver remarks on hurricane preparedness.\par \par \uc2 President Biden getting on Air Force One for his trip to survey Ida storm damage in NJ/NY. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZNLFyFTDuD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZNLFyFTDuD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eugene Daniels (@EugeneDaniels2) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EugeneDaniels2/status/1435242722038849536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president took a couple questions from reporters before boarding Air Force One. Asked what he wants to see on his trip today, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m hoping to see the things we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be able to fix permanently with the bill that we have in for infrastructure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another reporter asked Biden how he will get all congressional Democrats on board with his infrastructure proposals, as progressives and centrists argue over the price tag of the $3.5tn spending package.\par \par \uc2 The president replied with a quote from the musical \u8220\'20\'1CAnnie\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CThe sun\u8217\'20\'19s going to come out tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress will return from its summer recess later this month, and some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are already gearing up for a political fight \u8211\'20\'13 with each other.\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers are looking to pass their $3.5tn spending package, after the House and the Senate approved the blueprint for the budget bill last month. The ambitious legislation encompasses much of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, including proposals to expand access to affordable childcare, invest in climate-related initiatives and broaden Medicare coverage.\par \par \uc2 But to get the bill passed, Democrats will first need to reach an agreement on the cost of the legislation. Centrist Democrats, including Senators Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin, have expressed concern about the bill\u8217\'20\'19s $3.5tn price tag, while progressives have indicated they will fiercely oppose any attempt to cut funding in the proposal.\par \par \uc2 With his entire economic agenda hanging in the balance, Biden will need to convince the two fractious wings of his party to come together and pass a comprehensive spending package. And given Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 extremely narrow majorities in both the House and the Senate, there is virtually no room for error.\par \par \uc2 Despite warning signs of intra-party friction over the cost of the budget bill, congresswoman Suzan DelBene, who chairs the centrist New Democrat Coalition, said the House\u8217\'20\'19s focus right now should still be on the content of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think discussion of a number is more distracting when the focus really needs to be on, what is the substance going to be of this legislation?\u8221\'20\'1D DelBene told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf we have strong legislation the people support, I think we can find the path forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/07/biden-democrats-brewing-battle-budget-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to referee Democrats in brewing battle over $3.5tn budget bill}}}\par \par \uc2 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his trip to New Jersey and New York, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will underscore how the climate crisis is affecting average Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden will highlight how one in three Americans have been impacted by severe weather events in recent months, and that no one is immune from climate change,\u8221\'20\'1D a White House official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/07/politics/joe-biden-hurricane-ida-new-york-new-jersey/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe will speak about the economic impacts of extreme weather, while driving home the urgent need for key investments to fight climate change and in resilient infrastructure, critical investments included in the President\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip comes as Congress prepares to return from its August recess and take up the bipartisan infrastructure bill and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn spending package, which the president has argued will make the country better prepared for extreme weather events.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 As they sifted through the wreckage of their childhood home in Mount Airy, Louisiana, members of the Robinson family were hunting for memories.\par \par \uc2 They came in the form of a dozen family photo albums, somehow preserved amid the rubble. There was nothing much else to salvage as most of the house was destroyed. It had been in the family for generations, built and preserved with toil and hard work.\par \par \uc2 Judy Robinson, 70, had raised her two children here, working as a plant operator at a nearby \uc2 Marathon Oil\uc2  refinery and then living on income support as a retiree.\par \par \uc2 Her daughter, Gayle Robinson, struggled as she watched Judy\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to seeing home for the first time since Hurricane Ida struck seven days ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen her look how she looked,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, outside in the oppressive heat. \u8220\'20\'1CConfused. Lost for words. It\u8217\'20\'19s like someone threw a grenade into the house.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As cable news channels pivoted away from Ida\u8217\'20\'19s destruction in south-east {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  over the weekend, the storm only a week into history, thousands of people, including the Robinson family, were still coming to terms with a new reality.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/i-dont-have-a-choice-hurricane-ida-leaves-devastated-louisiana-communities-struggling-with-new-reality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a choice\u8217\'20\'19: Hurricane Ida leaves devastated Louisiana communities struggling with new reality}}}\par \par \uc2 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to tour New York and New Jersey neighborhoods affected by Ida\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to New York and New Jersey today to tour neighborhoods affected by Hurricane Ida, which hit the US last week.\par \par \uc2 The president will receive a briefing on hurricane response from local leaders in Hillsborough Township, New Jersey, and tour a neighborhood in Manville, New Jersey, before delivering remarks in Queens, New York.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit comes after the hurricane caused widespread flooding in the New York metropolitan area, leading to at least 50 deaths from Virginia to Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to deliver remarks on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to prepare for and respond to hurricanes, which are becoming more intense and more common due to the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 While touring hurricane-impacted Louisiana last week, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CHurricane Ida is another reminder that we need to be prepared for the next hurricane and superstorms that are going to come, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to come more frequently and more ferociously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/06/biden-visit-new-york-new-jersey-hurricane-ida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to visit New York and New Jersey reeling from deadly storms}}}\par \par \uc2 2021-09-07T13:36:29Z2021-09-08T07:22:12Z{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/277bbe9f84882ed8b60722544b297f90d4486a74/0_21_3500_2101/500.jpgJoe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/277bbe9f84882ed8b60722544b297f90d4486a74/0_21_3500_2101/500.jpgJoe}}}\uc2  Biden, along with Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez and Chuck Schumer, tours a neighborhood affected by Hurricane Ida in Queens, New York.Joe Biden is greeted by New Jersey Governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  and others as he arrives for briefing about the impact of Hurricane Ida.The flooded area of Southwest Hoboken, New Jersey, after a night of high winds and rain from the remnants of Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210907eh97001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
