\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UN\uc2  experts condemn Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law as sex discrimination \u8216\'20\'18at its worst\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 913 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2021\par 11:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: human rights lawyer criticizes the supreme court and says new law will \u8216\'20\'18make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsafe and deadly\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 United Nations human rights monitors have strongly condemned the state of Texas for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , which they say violates international law by denying women control over their own bodies and endangering their lives.\par \par \uc2 In damning remarks to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , Melissa Upreti, the chair of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/issues/women/wgwomen/pages/wgwomenindex.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN\u8217\'20\'19s working group on discrimination against women and girls}}}\uc2 , criticized the new Texas law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/text/SB8/id/2395961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 8}}}\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1Cstructural sex and gender-based discrimination at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She warned that the legislation, which bans abortions at about six weeks, could force \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers underground and drive women to seek unsafe procedures that could prove fatal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis new law will make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsafe and deadly, and create a whole new set of risks for women and girls. It is profoundly discriminatory and violates a number of rights guaranteed under international law,\u8221\'20\'1D the human rights lawyer from Nepal said.\par \par \uc2 Upreti, one of five independent experts charged by the \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights council in Geneva to push for elimination of discrimination against women and girls around the world, was also sharply critical of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week the court\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/06/supreme-court-trump-texas-abortion-law-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided by a five to four vote}}}\uc2  to allow the Texas law to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 go ahead}}}\uc2 , despite the provision\u8217\'20\'19s blatant disregard of the court\u8217\'20\'19s own 1973 ruling legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe law and the way it came about \u8211\'20\'13 through the refusal of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to block it based on existing legal precedent \u8211\'20\'13 has not only taken Texas backward, but in the eyes of the international community, it has taken the entire country backward,\u8221\'20\'1D Upreti said.\par \par \uc2 Reem Alsalem, the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s special rapporteur on violence against women, advising and reporting to the Human Rights Council and its member states on the issue, was also scathing of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow the Texas law to stand. She accused the five rightwing justices who formed the majority \u8211\'20\'13 and who include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2020/09/26/trump-legacy-supreme-court-422058"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all three of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointees}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 of exposing women to potential violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThrough this decision the \uc2 supreme court of the United States\uc2  has chosen to trample on the protection of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights, thereby exposing them and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  service providers to more violence,\u8221\'20\'1D Alsalem told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Women of color, those with low incomes and from other vulnerable groups would bear the brunt of the crackdown, she pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Alsalem singled out as especially egregious the element of the Texas law that makes abortions all but impossible even for women who become pregnant because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.expressnews.com/news/legislature/article/Anti-abortion-laws-used-to-exempt-cases-of-rape-16434785.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rape and incest}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat exacerbates their trauma as well as mental and physical suffering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  joined the three justices on the liberal wing of the supreme court in dissenting against the majority\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to block the Texas law, with all four {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071#block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issuing strong statements}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under SB 8, some 7 million Texan women are estimated to be at risk of losing access to legal abortions. Health clinics offering the service have already begun to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/08/texas-planned-parenthoods-abortion-law-turning-away-patients/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turn patients away}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SB 8 bans all abortions after initial cardiac activity can be detected in the fetus, usually at around six weeks of pregnancy. Legislation to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  so early are often evocatively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/05/abortion-doctors-fetal-heartbeat-bills-language-misleading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 but misleadingly}}}\uc2  called heartbeat bills, even though at that stage the heart has not yet formed.\par \par \uc2 The cut-off is so early that many women would not be aware that they are even pregnant, and up to 90% of all terminations in the state are expected to blocked.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade led the way to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the stage where a fetus can survive outside the womb, typically around 24 weeks into the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Another contentious aspect of the new Texas law is that it transfers responsibility for enforcing the new rules from state officials to ordinary citizens who are encouraged to sue anyone who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2021/09/texas-ban-abortion-fund-lawsuit.html#:~:text=On%20Sept.%201%2C%20a%20new,of%20%2410%2C000%20plus%20attorneys'%20fees."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Caids\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cabets\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with bounties of $10,000 and their legal fees paid if the lawsuit succeeds.\par \par \uc2 Under international law, governments are allowed to regulate voluntary terminations of pregnancy. But they are not allowed to do so in ways that jeopardize the lives or women, subject them to physical or mental pain or suffering, discriminate against them or arbitrarily interfere with their privacy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/Documents/Issues/Women/WRGS/SexualHealth/INFO_Abortion_WEB.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Human rights bodies}}}\uc2  have long acknowledged that denying women access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by criminalizing the practice or by erecting other hurdles can in certain circumstances amount to cruel, degrading and inhumane treatment. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have even been likened by international bodies to a form of torture.\par \par \uc2 In 2015 the \uc2 UN\uc2  working group on discrimination against women conducted an official visit to the US to probe the position and treatment of women in American society.\par \par \uc2 In their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.refworld.org/docid/5800dd4a4.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 final report}}}\uc2 , the human rights experts expressed regret that American women have \u8220\'20\'1Cseen their rights to sexual and reproductive health significantly eroded\u8230\'20\'26 Ever-increasing barriers are being created to prevent their access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Upreti told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  that since that visit, the situation in the US had deteriorated further.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe notified the US administration that the imposition of new barriers to access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services constitutes discrimination under international law, yet the retrogression has continued,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 8 September 2021 to include Reem Alsalem\u8217\'20\'19s official title.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210907eh97000me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
