\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Observer view on the Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Observer editorial \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2021\par 05:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The insidious oppression of women across the world must not be ignored\par \par \uc2 Last Wednesday, a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was implemented in Texas. Women are now prevented from getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  six weeks after conception (a point at which many women do not even realise they are pregnant), even in cases of rape or incest. It is the latest, and most extensive, erosion of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights that has long been championed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/may/20/observer-view-on-abortion-donald-trump-gag-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US religious right}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/02/sonia-sotomayor-dissent-texas-abortion-ban-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the words of}}}\uc2  Justice Sonia Sotomayer \u8211\'20\'13 in a dissenting opinion to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow the law to be implemented while its constitutionality is determined in the coming years \u8211\'20\'13 it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbreathtaking act of defiance of the constitution\u8230\'20\'26 and of the rights of women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The consequences for women living in the second most populous state in the US will be devastating. It is estimated the law will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent 85%}}}\uc2  of Texan women who want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from accessing one in the state; for the vast majority of these women who cannot afford the time and resources required to travel out of state, this means they will be unable to access safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. In a shocking contravention of their human rights, women with unwanted pregnancies will be forced to carry them to term and undergo the danger and trauma of childbirth.\par \par \uc2 A wealth of international {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evidence}}}\uc2  shows the futility of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; rates are no lower in countries where it is illegal or severely restricted, but many more women die as a result of being forced to seek illegal and unsafe procedures. The only way to effectively reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates is by expanding women\u8217\'20\'19s access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.everydayhealth.com/birth-control/politics-birth-control-access-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contraception,}}}\uc2  yet conservatives in the US have consistently sought to limit their access to free birth control.\par \par \uc2 The way that Texas legislators have sought to get around the unconstitutionality of their ban is chilling in the extreme. Rather than leaving enforcement of the ban up to the state, the legislation allows anybody in the world to sue those involved in providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care or practical support to women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for at least $10,000 plus legal costs.\par \par \uc2 The law is framed so broadly that anyone who could be construed to have aided a woman in getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 from a friend offering advice to a taxi driver picking them up for an appointment \u8211\'20\'13 could fall foul of these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/08/impact-texas-abortion-ban-20-fold-increase-driving-distance-get-abortion?gclid=Cj0KCQjwssyJBhDXARIsAK98ITTS-TBgMm3RtDiBMhWoB4T3EqI32P8_W_ulH6gep5aFEoBINfMbX6YaAmjcEALw_wcB#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provisions}}}\uc2 . This is an insidious and misogynist way of targeting women and the support networks they need to rely on if they find themselves needing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The consequences are likely to extend far beyond Texas: Republicans in six more states are preparing to rush through bills based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/03/texas-abortion-republicans-six-states-arkansas-florida-indiana-mississippi-north-south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas law}}}\uc2 . And the anti-women\u8217\'20\'19s rights majority that now exists on the supreme court puts a woman\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional right}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , established back in 1973, at risk.\par \par \uc2 The patriarchal forces that seek to control women and their bodies are embedded everywhere\par \par \uc2 It is perhaps tempting to look at the dire situation facing women in Afghanistan, where the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s takeover has put women in extreme mortal danger, and feel uncomplicated relief that in liberal democracies such as the United States women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms will never face the same extraordinary level of threat from male fundamentalists. Yet the Texas ban \u8211\'20\'13 and threats to women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms from authoritarian leaders within {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-europe-55838210"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the EU}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 highlight that taking the hard-fought gains of second-wave feminists for granted is risky in the extreme.\par \par \uc2 Civil rights struggles rarely stand still: history shows us that momentous achievements, such as the popular vote to legalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ireland in 2018, are often punctuated with periods where recently won rights are eroded. Women across the world continue to be oppressed on the basis of their reproductive biology: the patriarchal forces that seek to control women and their bodies are embedded everywhere. Preventing things from slipping backwards, let alone achieving progress, is a fight in and of itself.\par \par \uc2 Here in the United Kingdom, women enjoy a better range of legal protections than in the US, where there is no right to paid time off work after having a baby or universal access to free childcare or healthcare. But in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/cbp-8909/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Northern Ireland}}}\uc2 , women are still struggling to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services despite \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being legalised almost two years ago. A woman is killed by a man every three days, yet there remains a huge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensaid.org.uk/womens-aid-responds-to-the-governments-funding-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shortfall}}}\uc2  in domestic abuse services for women who experience male violence, while the women\u8217\'20\'19s prison estate is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/feb/28/to-expand-womens-prisons-is-idiotic-and-inhumane-we-should-phase-them-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filled with}}}\uc2  domestic abuse survivors. Rape convictions are at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2020/jul/30/convictions-fall-record-low-england-wales-prosecutions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic low}}}\uc2 , effectively decriminalising male violence against women.\par \par \uc2 Those women considered by men to be past their sexual prime face a particularly toxic blend of sexism and ageism in workplaces, in their communities and in our public discourse.\par \par \uc2 The Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban shows how vulnerable women\u8217\'20\'19s rights can be even in the richest liberal democracies. In societies such as the US and the UK, women have immeasurably more freedom than they did a century ago and still do in many parts of the world. Yet there is nowhere in the world where women are truly free from the burden of patriarchal oppression. We ignore that at our peril.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210908eh95002s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
