\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden signs order on declassification of \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 9/11 documents \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin and Lauren Aratani and Martin Pengelly \par \uc2 9,895 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2021\par 00:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Attorney general must release documents over the next six monthsUS adds 235,000 jobs in August amid Delta surgeBiden urges Congress to \u8216\'20\'18finish the job\u8217\'20\'19 on passing his economic agendaIda death toll in north-east nears 50Trump \u8216\'20\'18about ready to announce\u8217\'20\'19 2024 run, says Jim JordanSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today, thanks for following along. Some key links from the day:\par \par \uc2 * Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/03/texas-abortion-republicans-six-states-arkansas-florida-indiana-mississippi-north-south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaders in at least six US states}}}\uc2  are rushing to follow the lead of Texas in adopting an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Biden and top Democrats are scrambling for a strategy to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-biden-democrats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counter Republican restrictions}}}\uc2  on women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights amid the fallout from the new Texas law.\par \par \uc2 * The man who was photographed inside the US Capitol during the 6 January insurrection wearing a horned headdress and furs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/jacob-chansley-us-capitol-attack-pleads-guilty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The US economy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/sep/03/us-jobs-report-august-2021-hiring-delta-variant-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added just 235,000 jobs in August, a sharp drop from preceding months}}}\uc2 , as employers cut back hiring plans amid the spread of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 * Hurricane Ida hit a heavily industrialized region hard shortly after it was revealed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/louisiana-cancer-alley-hurricane-ida-st-james-parish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearby steel plant pumped sulphur gas in atmosphere for six years}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Biden has announced the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-fbi-release-files-september-11-investigation-saudi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wholesale review and declassification of files from the investigation into the 9/11 attack}}}\uc2 , in response to intense pressure from Congress and victims\u8217\'20\'19 families currently suing Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 * Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/florida-covid-ron-desantis-appeals-mask-ruling-record-covid-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed a mask mandate ruling}}}\uc2  as the state\u8217\'20\'19s Covid deaths set a record.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 More on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to LaPlace, Louisiana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/climate-change-dfc998fa74455e28bb43ff66dd7c00b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Giant trees knocked sideways. Homes boarded up with plywood. Off-kilter street signs.\par \par \uc2 Less than a week after Hurricane Ida battered the Gulf Coast, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  walked the streets of a hardhit Louisiana neighborhood on Friday and told local residents, \u8220\'20\'1CI know you\u8217\'20\'19re hurting, I know you\u8217\'20\'19re hurting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden pledged robust federal assistance to get people back on their feet and said the government already had distributed $100 million directly to individuals in the state in $500 checks to give them a first slice of critical help. Many people, he said, don\u8217\'20\'19t know what help is available because they can\u8217\'20\'19t get cellphone service.\par \par \uc2 Residents welcomed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presence, one of them drawing a sign with his last name and a heart for the dot on the \u8220\'20\'1Ci.\u8221\'20\'1D They laughed and posed for selfies.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  talks with a resident as he tours a neighborhood impacted by Hurricane Ida. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Uber and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  have said they would cover legal expenses of their drivers if they were sued under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s new extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which allows suits to be brought against people who transport patients to clinics.\par \par \uc2 enltrBoth Uber and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  now announcing they will be covering any legal fees of ridershare drivers if they were to be sued under Texas' new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law SB8 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gwAEsCnCK4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gwAEsCnCK4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Salvador Hernandez (@SalHernandez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SalHernandez/status/1433898017958940672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-where-to-get-abortion-legally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purposefully broad}}}\uc2  and allows private citizens to bring suits against anyone who potentially \u8220\'20\'1Caided or abetted\u8221\'20\'1D someone accessing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, as my colleague outlined in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-where-to-get-abortion-legally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explainer}}}\uc2 . If plaintiffs are successful, they receive $10,000 and have legal fees reimbursed.\par \par \uc2 Lyft{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/09/03/1034140480/lyft-and-uber-will-pay-drivers-legal-fees-if-theyre-sued-under-texas-abortion-la"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Drivers are never responsible for monitoring where their riders go or why. Imagine being a driver and not knowing if you are breaking the law by giving someone a ride. Similarly, riders never have to justify, or even share, where they are going and why. Imagine being a pregnant woman trying to get to a healthcare appointment and not knowing if your driver will cancel on you for fear of breaking a law. Both are completely unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 GoDaddy boots Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  'whistleblower' website\par \par \uc2 The new \u8220\'20\'1Cwhistleblower\u8221\'20\'1D website of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Texas Right to Life briefly went down today after GoDaddy, which was hosting the site, said it violated its rules:\par \par \uc2 enltrGoDaddy is cutting off Texas Right to Life\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18whistleblowing\u8217\'20\'19 website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DruFn0Tj28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DruFn0Tj28}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eo3Fd0TzaX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eo3Fd0TzaX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Verge (@verge) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/verge/status/1433876233071124481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 My colleague Kari Paul reported on Thursday that pro-choice users on TikTok and Reddit had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-tiktok-reddit-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a guerrilla effort to fight Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions}}}\uc2  by flooding the online tip website that encouraged people to report potential violations of the law.\par \par \uc2 GoDaddy said the \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life whistleblower\u8221\'20\'1D website violated numerous provisions of its terms of service, including the rule that says sites \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not collect or harvest (or permit anyone else to collect or harvest) any user content... or any non-public or personally identifiable information about another user or any other person or entity without their express prior written consent\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2021/9/3/22656196/godaddy-texas-right-for-life-abortion-whistleblowing-site"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Verge reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The site was down earlier this afternoon. Visitors to the website saw an \u8220\'20\'1CAccess Denied\u8221\'20\'1D page. A GoDaddy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/03/technology/texas-abortion-law-website-tiktok.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spokesperson told the New York Times}}}\uc2  that it had given the website a 24-hour notice about the takedown.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  "whistleblower" website went down today after GoDaddy said it violated terms of services, and after users flooded it with fake tips. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cC8awzYVoy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cC8awzYVoy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levin (@SamTLevin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamTLevin/status/1433920734410117121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 One TikTok user went viral after they said they had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@travelingnurse/video/7003093359573110021?is_copy_url=1&is_from_webapp=v1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 submitted 742 fake reports}}}\uc2  of the governor, Greg Abbott, getting illegal abortions. More on the digital campaign against the site and the new law here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-tiktok-reddit-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TikTokers flood Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  whistleblower site with Shrek memes, fake reports and porn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger has the full story on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order to declassify the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 9/11 records:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced the wholesale review and declassification of files from the investigation into the 9/11 attack, in response to intense pressure from Congress and victims\u8217\'20\'19 families currently suing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the 20th anniversary of 9/11 approaches, the American people deserve to have a fuller picture of what their government knows about those attacks,\u8221\'20\'1D an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/09/03/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-the-executive-order-directing-declassification-review-of-documents-related-to-the-september-11-2001-terrorist-attacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2  issued on Friday said.\par \par \uc2 It said the full record would be disclosed in tranches over the coming six months \u8220\'20\'1Cexcept when the strongest possible reasons counsel otherwise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The order said that while the \u8220\'20\'1Cindiscriminate\u8221\'20\'1D release of information could jeopardise national security and the ability to prevent future attacks, a better balance had to be struck between transparency and accountability.\par \par \uc2 It said \u8220\'20\'1Cinformation should not remain classified when the public interest in disclosure outweighs any damage to the national security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-fbi-release-files-september-11-investigation-saudi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden tells FBI to release files on 9/11 investigation \u8211\'20\'13 and possible Saudi links}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two major US insurers have agreed to cover the living expenses for residents in Louisiana who evacuated their homes before they were under mandatory evacuation orders, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/09/03/hurricane-ida-insurance-companies-heed-biden-call-to-help-victims-cover-more-costs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNBC}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The White House had urged the companies not to deny policyholders based on technicalities, and it appears that \uc2 Allstate\uc2  and \uc2 USAA\uc2  are confirming that they will cover the expenses.\par \par \uc2 enltrScoop: After Biden called on them to "do the right thing," 2 of the the country's biggest insurers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Allstate?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Allstate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USAA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USAA}}}\uc2  have agreed to cover living expenses for ppl who evacuated voluntarily in Louisiana from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ida?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ida}}}\uc2 , not just mandatory evacs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bY2voixKxf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bY2voixKxf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christina Wilkie (@christinawilkie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/christinawilkie/status/1433873181388034049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Gabrielle Cannon reports from the wildfires in northern California, where extreme conditions are making the blazes exponentially worse:\par \par \uc2 Before the ravenous Caldor fire laid siege to South Lake Tahoe, California\u8217\'20\'19s top firefighting priority lay just to the north, where the Dixie fire scorched more land than any other single fire in state history. Together, the two behemoths have already blackened more than 1m acres (4,000 sq km) along the Sierra Nevada range. And fire season in the American west is just heating up.\par \par \uc2 The climate crisis has helped create extreme fire emergencies, with huge, rapid-moving blazes tearing through a hot, parched landscape at lightning speed. Fires have hopped granite summits firefighters had hoped would slow their spread. Blazes have displayed erratic burn behavior, making their movements hard to predict.\par \par \uc2 The extreme conditions raise fresh questions about the ability of the country\u8217\'20\'19s firefighting forces to control an emergency that has grown exponentially bigger year after year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/california-firefighters-stretched-to-limit-as-devastating-blazes-become-the-norm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California firefighters \u8216\'20\'18stretched to limit\u8217\'20\'19 as devastating blazes become the norm}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden addresses hurricane relief efforts in Louisiana\par \par \uc2 Hi all - Sam Levin here in Los Angeles, taking over our live coverage for the day.\par \par \uc2 Biden is now in LaPlace, Louisiana, and has just spoken about the US response to Hurricane Ida. He said the disaster was a reminder of the worsening hurricane threats in the US:\par \par \uc2 Superstorms are going to come, and they are going to come more frequently and more ferociously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said crews from 32 different states were working to restore power: \u8220\'20\'1CI know you\u8217\'20\'19re all frustrated.\u8221\'20\'1D The president also said he was working to pressure the cellphone companies to restore service, noting that some residents were unaware of the services available to them due to lack of service.\par \par \uc2 The president further noted that some insurance companies were trying to unjustly deny claims of hurricane victims, based on technicalities:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m calling on private insurance companies: Don\u8217\'20\'19t hide behind the fine print... Pay what you owe your customers! Help those in need. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we should all be doing now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s earlier coverage from New Orleans where residents have struggled without power for days:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/new-orleans-hurricane-ida-power-outage-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel abandoned\u8217\'20\'19: New Orleanians swelter through days without power}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 A man in Mississippi who served 23 years in prison before charges were dropped is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mississippitoday.org/2021/09/03/curtis-flowers-doug-evans-mississippi-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing}}}\uc2  the district attorney who continued to prosecute his case despite multiple mistrials.\par \par \uc2 Curtis Flowers, 51, was released from prison in September after the attorney general of Mississippi dropped charges against Flowers after reviewing evidence from the case. Flowers was originally charged with murdering four people at a furniture store in Winona, Mississippi. Flowers\u8217\'20\'19 case was prominently featured in the investigations podcast \u8220\'20\'1CIn the Dark\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, the \uc2 US Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2019/jun/22/curtis-flowers-conviction-supreme-court-removal-of-black-jurors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that the district attorney, Doug Evans, who continued to prosecute Flowers\u8217\'20\'19 case made sure to keep African Americans off the jury of his trials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 A parent of an elementary school student in Tucson, Arizona threatened to call the local authorities and conduct a \u8220\'20\'1Ccitizen\u8217\'20\'19s arrest\u8221\'20\'1D of the school\u8217\'20\'19s principal because of the school\u8217\'20\'19s virus protocols.\par \par \uc2 The principal of Mesquite Elementary School called the father on Thursday telling him his son was to stay home for at least a week to quarantine after coming in close contact with someone who tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Later that morning, the man walked into the school with his son and two other mans carrying zip ties and confronted the principal on the quarantine policy.\par \par \uc2 The Tucson police department said that they responded to the incident, but it is unclear if any charges were made, according to the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the most powerful tools as adults is the behavior that we model to young people \u8211\'20\'13 and the behavior that was modeled today makes me really sad,\u8221\'20\'1D John Carruth, the superintendent of the school\u8217\'20\'19s district told the Post.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Civil rights groups have filed two new federal lawsuits challenging the sweeping new election restrictions Texas Republicans approved earlier this week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/sites/default/files/2021-09/2021-9-3%20Doc%201%20Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One suit}}}\uc2 , filed by a coalition of Texas civic action groups as well as a former poll worker and Harris county election administrator, argues that the law is intentionally designed to discriminate against minority voters. It also says the law violates the First Amendment\u8217\'20\'19s free speech protections as well as the equal protection guarantee of the 14th amendment along with the Voting Rights Act and the Americans with Disabilities Act.\par \par \uc2 A second federal suit, filed by \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , Texas Civil Rights Project, and Disability Rights Texas, makes similar claims.\par \par \uc2 Among the provisions the suit challenges are those that allow poll watchers increased movement at the polls, something it says could lead harassment of voters of color at the polls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShould poll watchers engage in behavior that intimidates or harasses voters or election workers, including hovering over them or trailing voters through the polling place, election workers run the risk of criminal prosecution if they attempt to stop such behavior. The risk of such intimidation has historically been and will continue to be higher for voters of color,\u8221\'20\'1D it says.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in federal court in San Antonio, also challenges provisions in the law that impose new requirements on those who assist voters, including an oath in which they are required to affirm the voter asked them for assistance and that they understand the voter\u8217\'20\'19s ballot may not be counted if they are ineligible for assistance. Assistors may also swear that they did not \u8220\'20\'1Cpressure\u8221\'20\'1D the voter for assistance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis additional language will cause assistors to question every voter\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18need\u8217\'20\'19 for assistance, which further invades the voter\u8217\'20\'19s privacy and opens assistors to the threat of prosecution for any misstep,\u8221\'20\'1D the suit says. \u8220\'20\'1CThis additional language will cause assistors to question every voter\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cneed\u8221\'20\'1D for assistance, which further invades the voter\u8217\'20\'19s privacy and opens assistors to the threat of prosecution for any misstep.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The groups are also challenging a new prohibition blocking election officials from soliciting vote by mail applications. The law, the suit says, chills the speech of officials like plaintiff Isabel Longoria, the Harris County election administrator, from encouraging people to vote by mail.\par \par \uc2 Several more suits are expected in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2  has been speaking to reporters about Afghanistan, once more defending the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s record on the withdrawal, and in particular on the evacuation of Afghans who had worked with or for the US military or government and are entitled to special immigration visas (SIVs).\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the week, state department officials admitted that a majority of SIV applicants had been left behind. Blinken was less definitive on that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf the roughly 124,000 people who\u8217\'20\'19ve been evacuated, the vast majority, 75-80% are Afghans at risk. And of those, some significant number will be SIVs either people who already hold an SIV visa or those who are actually in the pipeline, some number will be potential P1 (first priority) or P2 refugees and some other number will be Afghans at risk, who may not fit into any of those categories,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Blinken will fly to Doha and then to Ramstein Air base in Germany, to meet refugees and the US officials dealing with their processing.\par \par \uc2 In terms of getting vulnerable Afghans out of the country, he said the US had shared detailed \u8220\'20\'1Ca tremendous amount of very detailed information\u8221\'20\'1D about Kabul airport with other capitals, with the aim of getting it back up and running as soon as possible, and was looking at land routes out of the country, \u8220\'20\'1Cas well as making sure that we have very clear and precise plans to help people, as as necessary, use those routes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 A judge in Buffalo, New York will allow Byron Brown to run in the city\u8217\'20\'19s mayoral election, though he was defeated in the primary election by India Walton, a self-declared socialist candidate.\par \par \uc2 The judge, US district court judge John Sinatra, has ordered the Erie County Board of Elections to put Brown\u8217\'20\'19s name on the ballot as an independent in the November general election. Brown has served as mayor for four terms.\par \par \uc2 Walton, a nurse and community organizer, said that is considering an appeal of the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling was a travesty and mockery of justice,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Buffalo News. \u8220\'20\'1CThe hearing should never have proceeded.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walton said that the lawsuit shows that Brown \u8220\'20\'1Cis a true sore loser\u8221\'20\'1D and that she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think \u8220\'20\'1Cvoters are going to be fooled.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With no Republican challengers in the race, Walton was sure to win the general election in November, which would have made her the first socialist mayor of a major US city in decades.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden orders declassification of documents from \uc2 FBI\uc2  9/11 investigation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just announced that he signed an executive order today that will declassify documents related to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation of 9/11, a little over a week before the 20th anniversary of the attack.\par \par \uc2 Biden said he is directing the justice department to oversee a declassification review of documents related to the investigation. The order requires the attorney general to release the declassified documents over the next six months.\par \par \uc2 Families of 9/11 victims are currently suing the Saudi Arabian government in a federal court in New York for alleged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/24/september-11-former-saudi-officials-questioned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 involvement}}}\uc2  in the attack and have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/fbi-offer-documents-families-9-11-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  they want information about who financed and supported the attacks. They have said that an earlier offer from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to release some documents from investigation have not gone far enough and demanded a more comprehensive declassification review.\par \par \uc2 Families of victims have put pressure on Biden to undergo a declassification review, saying that if he took no object, they would \u8220\'20\'1Cpublicly stand in objection to any participation by his administration in any memorial ceremony of 9/11\u8221\'20\'1D, the group said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Biden expressed sympathy for the families of victims, saying that the administration \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue to engage respectfully with members of this community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI welcome their voices and insight as we chart a way forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a statement Friday, Biden announces he's signed an Executive Order directing the DOJ to oversee a declassification review of documents related to the 9/11 attacks requiring AG Merrick Garland "to release the declassified documents publicly over the next six months." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XZxW9LZLpk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XZxW9LZLpk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DJ Judd (@DJJudd) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DJJudd/status/1433858263066583045?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group of parents in Iowa are filing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/2021/09/03/iowans-disabilities-sue-kim-reynolds-over-mask-mandate-ban-schools-covid-department-of-education/5711038001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  against the state for its ban on mask mandates, says the law discriminates against students with disabilities that make them more susceptible to Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs in the case are asking the federal judge to block the ban on mask mandates and order to allow the states to allow mandates.\par \par \uc2 Like many Republican governors across the country, Iowa governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  signed an order banning masks in May, arguing that she does not believe in government mandates.\par \par \uc2 Heather Preston, a mother in Des Moines whose child has a rare organ disorder who makes him at risk of serious illness if he gets Covid-19, said in a statement that the lack of a mandate is a serious safety threat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor my son, going to school where not everyone is wearing masks puts him at huge risk. Meanwhile, because of his needs, he needs to be learning in person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/manchin-pelosi-biden-3-5-trillion-reconciliation-government-spending-debt-deficit-inflation-11630605657"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  in the Wall Street Journal published yesterday, Democratic senator Joe Manchin said that he will not pass the $3.5tn spending bill that progressive members of the party want to pass through reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 Manchin said that Democrats looking to pass the bill have \u8220\'20\'1Cno regard to rising inflation, crippling debt or the inevitability of future crises.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s some of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s Democrats have not responded in kind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Northeast is flooded after torrential rain. The West Coast is on fire. The Gulf is still reeling from the hurricane,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted the House Progressive Caucus yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is not time to pause or pull back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Northeast is flooded after torrential rain.\par \par \uc2 The West Coast is on fire.\par \par \uc2 The Gulf is still reeling from the hurricane.\par \par \uc2 This is no time to pause or pull back. We need to pass the President's Build Back Better agenda and invest in urgent climate action NOW. Lives are at stake.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Progressive Caucus (@USProgressives) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USProgressives/status/1433547064244424710?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 It seems that the White House is taking a less aggressive approach toward convincing Manchin and other moderate Democrats, saying in a statement that Manchin is \u8220\'20\'1Can important partner to our administration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president firmly believes that critical investment in our future should be paid for and if we do, economists tell us that they should not increase the inflation risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KJP46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KJP46}}}\uc2  on the Manchin op-Ed: \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Manchin is an important partner to our administration. The president firmly believes that critical investment in our future should be paid for and if we do, economists tells us that they should not increase the inflation risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Epstein (@jeneps) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeneps/status/1433843733947195392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 This is Lauren Aratani taking over for Martin Pengelly.\par \par \uc2 Ethics watchdog group Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington (CREW) filed a complaint against House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and US representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  for allegedly violating House rules by threatening companies who comply with records requests issued by the House committee investigating the January 6 Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf these companies comply with Democrat order to turn over private information, they are in violation of federal law and subject to losing their ability to operate in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy wrote in a statement on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIf companies still choose to violate federal law, a Republican majority will not forget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on Democrats asking companies to violate federal law: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XELEVNbx65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XELEVNbx65}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@GOPLeader) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPLeader/status/1432820807684739073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 31, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Greene echoed this statement in an interview, saying that if companies \u8220\'20\'1Cgo along with this, they will be shut down and that\u8217\'20\'19s a promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In its complaint, CREW has asked the congressional ethics office whether McCarthy and Greene violated House rules by threatening companies\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMcCarthy and Greene are transparently trying to thwart the Select Committee by illegally threatening companies with reprisals if they comply with the committee\u8217\'20\'19s proper and lawful requests \u8211\'20\'13 quite possible to protect themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D said Noah Bookbinder, president of CREW, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizensforethics.org/legal-action/legal-complaints/crew-files-ethics-complaint-against-kevin-mccarthy-marjorie-taylor-greene/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was revealed on Monday that the House committee has asked telecommunication companies like \uc2 AT&T\uc2  and \uc2 Verizon\uc2  to preserve records of Republican House members, including Greene and McCarthy for the investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 This is Martin Pengelly, handing the controls to Lauren Aratani with a few highlights of the morning in US politics:\par \par \uc2 * In remarks at the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6132345e8f0830dd895ff04b#block-6132345e8f0830dd895ff04b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden said}}}\uc2 disappointing August job numbers were the result of the surge in cases of the Delta variant of the coronavirus. He also championed his infrastructure and budget plans, which must still find a way through Congress, as a way to ensure that the economic recovery from Covid does not falter.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613243b98f0830dd895ff1c9#block-613243b98f0830dd895ff1c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that senior US health officials have told the White House to scale back plans to offer vaccine booster shots this month, given a lack of relevant data.\par \par \uc2 * Biden also attacked the stringent and controversial anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law passed in Texas and effectively OK-d by the supreme court as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613239318f083528f0f533b8#block-613239318f083528f0f533b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost un-American}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and said he wanted to examine the \u8220\'20\'1Cpossibilities within the existing law, to have the justice department look and see whether are the things that can be done\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * In Congress, Democrats who control the Senate judiciary committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6132254c8f08bf4765a44924#block-6132254c8f08bf4765a44924"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  they would investigate the growing use of the \u8220\'20\'1C shadow docket \u8221\'20\'1D by the conservative-run supreme court, to deal with rulings expeditiously and without full hearings.\par \par \uc2 * The president then left for Louisiana, where he was scheduled to see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-61322f238f083528f0f532fe#block-61322f238f083528f0f532fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 damage done by Hurricane Ida}}}\uc2  last weekend and meet people still without power as a result of the historic storm. \uc2 Entergy\uc2 , a power supplier, said power would be restored for most but not all by midweek next week.\par \par \uc2 * In the north-east, states continued to count the cost of flooding and tornadoes unleashed by the remnants of Ida on Wednesday night. The death toll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613218ed8f08bf4765a44852#block-613218ed8f08bf4765a44852"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nudged 50}}}\uc2 , or by some counts passed it. Leaders including New York City mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  and New York governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  warned that such evidence of the quickening climate crisis meant much more needed to be done to cope with future floods.\par \par \uc2 * Biden\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, said the US expects to admit more than 50,000 people{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6132497e8f083528f0f53532#block-6132497e8f083528f0f53532"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 airlifted from Kabul}}}\uc2  after Afghanistan fell to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  last month. At the same time, a new Washington Post poll showed Biden still underwater with the public about his handling of the US withdrawal, despite strong public support for ending the near-20-year war.\par \par \uc2 And finally\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-61323bef8f0830dd895ff108#block-61323bef8f0830dd895ff108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Iowa}}}\uc2 , a reporter released hidden-camera video of the Ohio congressman Jim Jordan telling Republicans: \u8220\'20\'1C President Trump, he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna run again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much more to come, no doubt. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Some light reading in the meanwhile:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/trump-loyalists-doctors-ministers-reawaken-america-tour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump loyalists team up with anti-vax doctors for \u8216\'20\'18health and freedom\u8217\'20\'19 tour}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 How does someone in Texas get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now and what\u8217\'20\'19s next?\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of people in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  can effectively no longer access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state after it banned the procedure except in the earliest weeks of pregnancy often before most know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 In a 5-4 vote on Wednesday, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  refused to block the law, which permits private citizens to enforce the ban and possibly collect $10,000 if they win a case against a person helping someone obtain the medical procedure.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you should know about the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-where-to-get-abortion-legally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How does someone in Texas get an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  now and what\u8217\'20\'19s next?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas, said this morning the US expects to admit more than 50,000 people airlifted from Kabul after Afghanistan fell to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has said around 124,000, including US citizens, permanent residents and Afghans who worked with the US and other countries after the invasion in 2001, were brought out of Kabul before the military withdrew.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Mayorkas said more than 40,000 have arrived in the US so far, about 25% citizens or permanent residents and the rest special immigrant visa recipients or people considered \u8220\'20\'1Cvulnerable\u8221\'20\'1D under \uc2 Taliban\uc2  rule. That group includes women, children, and members of civil society, Mayorkas said.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas said all those entering the US were undergoing security screening and vetting and being tested for Covid-19 and offered a vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Amid political battle over the withdrawal from Afghanistan, some on the hard right of the Republican party have opposed admission to the US for Afghan refugees or claimed the Biden administration is not vetting such admissions properly.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/post-abc-poll-biden-afghanistan/2021/09/02/5520cd3e-0c16-11ec-9781-07796ffb56fe_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll from the Washington Post and ABC News}}}\uc2  on Friday put support for the US withdrawal at 78% but approval for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of it at 26%. That contributed to a slide in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s overall job approval rating, which stood at 44% with 51% disapproving.\par \par \uc2 The poll also found that 68% of respondents approved of taking in refugees from Afghanistan after security screening. Among Republicans, 56% supported taking such refugees in.\par \par \uc2 Further reading:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/03/afghanistan-women-defiant-amid-taliban-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18No fear, we are united\u8217\'20\'19: Afghan women defiant amid Taliban crackdown}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Solnit: Texas is part of a bigger Republican war\par \par \uc2 The American right has been drunk on its freedom from two kinds of inhibition since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared to guide them into the promised land of their unleashed ids.\par \par \uc2 One is the inhibition from lies, the other from violence. Both are ways members of civil society normally limit their own actions out of respect for the rights of others and the collective good. Those already strained limits have snapped for leading Republican figures, from \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  on Fox News to Ted Cruz in the Senate and for their followers. We\u8217\'20\'19ve watched those followers gulp down delusions from Pizzagate to QAnon to covid-denialism to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies. And rough up journalists, crash vehicles into and wave weapons at Black Lives Matter and other antiracist protestors at least since Charlottesville, menace statehouses, issue threats to doctors and school boards testifying about public health, and plot to kidnap \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, for imposing Covid-prevention protocols.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  that the rightwing supreme court just smiled upon, despite its violation of precedent, seethes with both violence and lies. The very language of the law is a lie\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/03/republicans-texas-abortion-right-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans seethe with violence and lies. Texas is part of a bigger war they\u8217\'20\'19re waging | Rebecca Solnit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Capitol rioter known as the \u8220\'20\'1CQAnon Shaman\u8221\'20\'1D will plead guilty to charges stemming from his role in the 6 January assault, his attorney has said.\par \par \uc2 Jacob Chansley shot to a dubious sort of fame around the deadly attack by Trump supporters, after he was pictured inside the Capitol and the Senate chamber wearing cod-Native American headgear.\par \par \uc2 He is among more than 600 participants in the riot, around which five people died, to have been arrested and charged.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/qanon-shaman-capitol-attack-guilty-plea_n_61311a2be4b0eab0ad95c891"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HuffPost}}}\uc2 , Chansley\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Albert Watkins, said he had reached a plea deal over charges which include obstructing an official proceeding and civil disorder.\par \par \uc2 Watkins also said Chansley had \u8220\'20\'1Cgenuine mental health issues\u8221\'20\'1D which \u8220\'20\'1Crendered [him] more vulnerable to the propaganda of the day\u8221\'20\'1D, but now sought \u8220\'20\'1Cto be accountable for [his] actions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jacob Chansley seen in Phoenix, Arizona last November. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters\par \par \uc2 QAnon is an antisemitic conspiracy theory which holds that the world is controlled by a cabal of cannibalistic paedophiles, against whom \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is waging a heroic battle.\par \par \uc2 In his statement to HuffPost, Watkins said Chansley was \u8220\'20\'1Ca long-avowed and practicing shaman\u8221\'20\'1D who has now \u8220\'20\'1Crepudiated the \u8216\'20\'18Q\u8217\'20\'19 previously assigned to him and requests future references to him be devoid of use of the letter \u8216\'20\'18Q\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/25/qanon-conspiracy-theory-explained-trump-what-is"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 QAnon explained: the antisemitic conspiracy theory gaining traction around the world}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House may scale back booster shot plans \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 On the subject of Covid-19, the Delta variant and booster shots, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was for a bit at the White House earlier, at least in blaming economic problems on Delta and unvaccinated people, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/03/us/coronavirus-booster-shots.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2  that top health officials have told the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/03/us/coronavirus-booster-shots.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there may not be enough data to recommend booster shots just yet}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The administration had planned to offer booster shots to the general public later this month but the Times reported that on Thursday, the officials advised a delay.\par \par \uc2 Janet Woodcock, acting commissioner of the Food and Drug Administration, and \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, reportedly told White House Covid co-ordinator Jeffrey Zientz their agencies may be able recommend boosters by late September \u8211\'20\'13 but only for certain recipients of the FDA-approved \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech vaccine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has increased its death toll from Hurricane Ida in the north-eastern US to 49 \u8211\'20\'13 various counts are difficult to monitor, and some sources have put it well above 50.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on his way to Louisiana, where Ida made landfall last weekend as one of the most powerful storms ever to hit the US. Power remains out there for millions \u8211\'20\'13 and won\u8217\'20\'19t be back, and then not for all, until the middle of next week, power supplier \uc2 Entergy\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the north-east, remnants of Ida arrived with torrential rain on Wednesday night. At least 25 people died in New Jersey and 16 in New York, with deaths also recorded in Maryland, Pennsylvania and Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , the governor of New Jersey, has said at least six people are missing in the state.\par \par \uc2 Further reading:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/03/big-oil-hurricane-ida-flood-victims-thoughts-prayers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are big oil companies sending to Hurricane Ida flood victims? 'Thoughts and prayers'}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jordan: Trump 'about ready to announce' 2024 run\par \par \uc2 Lauren Windsor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawindsor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a reporter}}}\uc2  who specialises in catching conservatives in unguarded moments, has posted video of a conversation with the Ohio Republican Jim Jordan in Iowa this week, in which he indicates that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will soon announce a run for president in 2024.\par \par \uc2 In the shaky video, Jordan is seen to say: \u8220\'20\'1C President Trump, he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna run again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked, \u8220\'20\'1CYou think so?\u8221\'20\'1D Jordan says: \u8220\'20\'1CI know so. Yeah, I talked to him yesterday. He\u8217\'20\'19s about ready to announce after all of this craziness in Afghanistan...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jordan agrees with a questioner who says Biden should \u8220\'20\'1Cfucking resign, pardon my French\u8221\'20\'1D, as the president is \u8220\'20\'1C really bad, really bad, so \u8230\'20\'26 thank you for coming \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Jordan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613212798f0830dd895fedfa#block-613212798f0830dd895fedfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  that he made the remarks. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the video:\par \par \uc2 enltrEXCLUSIVE-->\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan: President Trump, he's gonna run again.\par \par \uc2 Pete: You think so?\par \par \uc2 Jordan: I know so. Yeah, I talked to him yesterday. He's about ready to announce after all of this craziness in Afghanistan... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ndogdm7Ipl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ndogdm7Ipl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Windsor (@lawindsor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawindsor/status/1433800993603530755?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A Trump run would seem to have a decent chance of success, given his domination of the Republican party, which has taken up his lies about electoral fraud causing his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and which has put its shoulder to the wheel against investigations of Trump supporters\u8217\'20\'19 deadly assault on the US Capitol on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Other claimants to the throne, should all this prove to be bluff and bluster, include the Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Nikki Haley, once UN ambassador under Trump but someone who seems to go in and out of favour with the former president \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/570574-trump-on-nikki-haley-every-time-she-criticizes-me-she-uncriticizes-me-about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as he has also noticed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law 'un-American', DoJ will study response\par \par \uc2 A reporter catches Biden at the podium with a question about the assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Texas, via a new law which the conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  allowed to stand.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to talk about these things from Louisiana,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have continued to be a strong supporter of Roe v Wade, No1,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, referring to the 1973 supreme court ruling which safeguards the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the most pernicious thing about the Texas law is it sort of creates a vigilante system where people get rewards to go out [and sue people for aiding or arranging abortions].\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I know this sounds ridiculous, it is almost un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden also says he wants to examine the \u8220\'20\'1Cpossibilities within the existing law, to have the justice department look and see whether are the things that can be done, that can limit the independent action of individuals and enforce federal and state law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know enough to give you an answer yet,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve asked that to be checked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And with that the president is off to Louisiana to tour the damage done by Hurricane Ida, shouted questions about the withdrawal from Afghanistan following in his wake.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not always easy, this presidenting lark.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-biden-democrats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats rush to find strategy to counter Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden continues to describe his wish for the wealthy to \u8220\'20\'1Cjust pay a fair share\u8221\'20\'1D, while continuing to do well as the economy recovers, and for \u8220\'20\'1CCongress to finish the job and come through for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His final appeal is for Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cstick together\u8221\'20\'1D while pursuing economic growth, and to make a \u8220\'20\'1Cgiant step forward in the fight against climate change, a crisis made more evident than ever by the death and destruction caused by extreme weather just these past few days\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s heading for Louisiana, where power remains out to millions after Hurricane Ida hit last weekend, and leaving the north-east coast, where the death toll from the storm\u8217\'20\'19s remnants, which hit on Wednesday, is approaching or even past 50, depending on who\u8217\'20\'19s count you use.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'no question' Delta variant behind poor jobs numbers\par \par \uc2 Speaking about the disappointing jobs numbers for August \u8211\'20\'13 as America prepares for the Labor Day holiday \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  insists: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is an economic recovery that is durable and strong. The Biden plan is working.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Graeme Wearden of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  business desk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/sep/03/service-sector-china-uk-us-jobs-payroll-markets-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe US added just 235,000 new jobs in August, a sharp and disappointing slowdown in hiring. That\u8217\'20\'19s much weaker than expected, as the Delta variant of Covid-19 hit America\u8217\'20\'19s economy last month.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wall Street, in the aftermath of the jobs report, markets opened poorly.\par \par \uc2 Biden adds: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I know some want to see a larger number today and so did I, what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this year is a continued growth, month after month in job creation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He does admit that work needs to be done, including on combating the Delta variant of the coronavirus, which has driven a surge in cases and deaths from Covid-19 widely seen to have contributed to the disappointing jobs numbers.\par \par \uc2 Biden thinks so: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no question the Delta variant is why today\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report isn\u8217\'20\'19t stronger,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 He also says too many people are still unvaccinated. The vast majority of hospitalisations and deaths in states struggling with Delta are among the unvaccinated. Many such states are run by Republicans opposed to public health measures and mandates.\par \par \uc2 Biden also calls for Congress to \u8220\'20\'1C finish the job of passing my economic agenda \u8221\'20\'1D. There are all sorts of roadblocks in the way of his infrastructure and budget plans, which are caught in crossfire between progressives and moderates in the Democratic party and, in the case of the budget plan, uniform opposition from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about good paying jobs for ordinary people,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says. \u8220\'20\'1CBlue collar workers, jobs at a prevailing wage not $15 an hour but 20 or 30, but for the carpenters and pipe fitters, plumbers, electrical workers and so many others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We\u8217\'20\'19ll combat climate change by building our clean energy future,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden adds, topically as he prepares to visit Louisiana to meet victims of Hurricane Ida, promising to create \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of jobs and building windmills and solar panels all around the country and transferring that energy transmitted to parts that don\u8217\'20\'19t have that capacity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also promises taxes will not go up on ordinary Americans, and that big corporations should \u8220\'20\'1Cpay their fair share \u8230\'20\'26 and it comes up to billions of dollars if they pay\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe wealthy people aren\u8217\'20\'19t paying taxes they owe,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says, after briefly evoking the spectre of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe other guy\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his predecessor in the Oval Office. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna change that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomebody\u8217\'20\'19s gotta pay,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, hoping through such forceful words, of course, not to pay too heavily politically if the economic recovery should falter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 New Orleans will have power back by Wednesday, says supplier\par \par \uc2 In Louisiana, which Hurricane Ida hit first as one of the most powerful storms ever to make landfall in the US, power supplier \uc2 Entergy\uc2  has said power should be restored to almost all of New Orleans by Wednesday, 10 days after Ida destroyed the city\u8217\'20\'19s electric gird.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 Not every customer will have power back, \uc2 Entergy\uc2  said. Customers with damage where power enters their home will need to fix it themselves, and there could be some smaller areas that take longer. And there still is no concrete promise of when the lights will come back on in the parishes east and south of New Orleans, which were battered for hours by winds of 100mph or more.\par \par \uc2 The company asked for patience, acknowledging the heat and misery in Ida\u8217\'20\'19s aftermath.\par \par \uc2 In New York City, \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  has been addressing the fallout from flooding in which 11 people died as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/02/flooding-deaths-north-east-us-rain-storms-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the remnants of Ida battered the north-east}}}\uc2  on Wednesday night and Thursday morning. Many of those killed were in basement apartments, unable to get out as flash floods hit.\par \par \uc2 De Blasio\uc2  observed a moment of silence, thanked everyone who has worked to recover, then stressed again that \u8220\'20\'1Cno one projected\u8221\'20\'1D the record rainfall in an hour that hit the city, smashing a record set only weeks before during Tropical Storm Henri.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThings we are told will happen once a century are now happening regularly and they are getting worse,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 De Blasio\uc2  said, pointing an acceptance of the reality of the climate crisis in states like New York which is not necessarily shared elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, we\u8217\'20\'19re still waiting for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s due to speak about the disappointing jobs report, which seems a result of the pandemic and the Delta variant surge, before he flies out to Louisiana to visit people hit by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 And here he comes\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the last of the US troops took off from Kabul on Tuesday, Jonathan Freedland spoke to Thomas Kean. Kean co-wrote the 9/11 commission report, detailing who was to blame for the events of September 11, and making recommendations to prevent a subsequent attack.\par \par \uc2 In the latest episode of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Politics Weekly podcast, Kean shares his thoughts on the end of America\u8217\'20\'19s longest war:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 : 'tyrants' force people to make fake vax cards\par \par \uc2 The act of buying a fake vaccination card, according to \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  of Fox News, is \u8220\'20\'1Can act of desperation by decent, law-abiding Americans who have been forced into a corner by tyrants\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . Photograph: Richard Drew/AP\par \par \uc2 As opposed to an act to get round vaccination requirements at businesses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/23/fox-news-covid-vaccination-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Fox News}}}\uc2  which do not wish to help spread the coronavirus and add to a US death toll of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2021/sep/02/covid-19-coronavirus-us-map-latest-cases-state-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 643,000}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In New York, 15 people were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/08/31/us/manhattan-charges-covid-vaccine-card-scheme/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  this week over a scheme to make and sell fake vaccination ID and to fraudulently enter people into the New York vaccinations database.\par \par \uc2 Cyrus Vance Jr\uc2 , the Manhattan district attorney, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes are too high to tackle fake vaccination cards with whack-a-mole prosecutions \u8230\'20\'26 Making, selling, and purchasing forged vaccination cards are serious crimes with serious public safety consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson disagrees. On his primetime show on Thursday night, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThese arrests will be used to justify digital health passports for the entire American population.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As opposed to that section of the American population {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/23/fox-news-covid-vaccination-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which works for Fox News}}}\uc2 , which as was widely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/19/media/fox-vaccine-passport/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  in July, has \u8220\'20\'1Cdeveloped a secure, voluntary way for employees to self-attest their vaccination status\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Carlson said Vance was lying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBuying a fake vaccination card is not a, quote, \u8216\'20\'18serious crime,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1C It\u8217\'20\'19s not even close to a serious crime. Buying a fake vaccination card is an act of desperation by decent, law-abiding Americans who have been forced into a corner by tyrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what\u8217\'20\'19s a serious crime? Forcing Americans to take drugs they don\u8217\'20\'19t need or want. That\u8217\'20\'19s a very serious crime. And let\u8217\'20\'19s hope, in the end, someone is punished for it, severely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson also said health workers who have refused to be vaccinated had \u8220\'20\'1Cin good conscience \u8230\'20\'26 risked their careers to preserve their right to bodily autonomy and now they\u8217\'20\'19re in jail for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson is of course {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/aug/31/fox-news-tucker-carlson-revolt-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a controversy magnet by design}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/23/fox-news-covid-vaccination-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News backs Covid vaccination \u8211\'20\'13 a pity no one told Tucker Carlson}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Of interest in the case of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/185188/20210729091216198_19-1392%20Amicus%20Brief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an amicus brief}}}\uc2  filed with the supreme court in the case of a restrictive Mississippi law yet to be considered is co-signed by all the usual suspects when it comes to possible 2024 ambitions \u8211\'20\'13 bar one.\par \par \uc2 The brief was filed by \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , governor of South Carolina, and co-signed by \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  of Alabama, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  of Arizona, \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  of Arkansas, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida, Brian Kemp of Georgia, \uc2 Brad Little\uc2  of Idaho, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  of Iowa, \uc2 Michael Parson\uc2  of Missouri, \uc2 Greg Gianforte\uc2  of Montana, \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  of Oklahoma, and Greg Abbott of Texas.\par \par \uc2 Missing from that list \u8211\'20\'13 some of whom, looking at you, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , seem more likely to run for the Republican presidential nomination if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t than others \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/30/south-dakota-governor-troops-mexico-border-kristi-noem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem of South Dakota}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Noem is being advised by none other than \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , once Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager and still someone close to the Trump inner circle. Noem is someone very much mentioned whenever speculation about 2024 raises its ugly head. This blogger wonders, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613212798f0830dd895fedfa#block-613212798f0830dd895fedfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apropos}}}\uc2  of Jim Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s mention of Reynolds of Iowa as a possible Trump running mate yesterday, whether Noem might be a prospective VP pick too.\par \par \uc2 Republican governors who did not sign the brief in the Mississippi case include \uc2 Phil Scott\uc2  of Vermont, \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2  of Massachusetts and \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  of Maryland \u8211\'20\'13 popular governors in charge of blue or Democratic states. Hogan is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jul/28/larry-hogan-maryland-governor-interview-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very much considering a run}}}\uc2  in 2024 \u8230\'20\'26 if it would in all likelihood be a run, in a party fully prostrate before Trump, wildly unlikely to succeed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jul/28/larry-hogan-maryland-governor-interview-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'A bigger tent message': Larry Hogan on Trump and his own White House ambitions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Durbin: Senate panel will investigate supreme court 'shadow docket'\par \par \uc2 News from the Senate, where Dick Durbin, the Illinois Democrat who chairs the judiciary committee, has announced a hearing on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s use of the \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow docket\u8221\'20\'1D to rule on hugely consequential cases as if by stealth, \u8220\'20\'1Cparticularly its order permitting Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions to take effect this week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For more on the shadow docket, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-61320e2e8f083528f0f53093#block-61320e2e8f083528f0f53093"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  block published at 8.40am}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no date for a hearing yet, but in a statement from Democrats on the judiciary committee, Durbin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/press/dem/releases/senate-judiciary-committee-to-examine-the-texas-abortion-ban-and-the-supreme-courts-abuse-of-its-shadow-docket"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court must operate with the highest regard for judicial integrity in order to earn the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust. This anti-choice law is a devastating blow to Americans\u8217\'20\'19 constitutional rights \u8211\'20\'13 and the court allowed it to see the light of day without public deliberation or transparency.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis anti-choice law is a devastating blow to Americans' constitutional rights\u8212\'20\'14and SCOTUS allowed it to see the light of day without public deliberation or transparency. The \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  must examine the conservative Court\u8217\'20\'19s abuse of the shadow docket. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YhE6uNPIV1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YhE6uNPIV1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Dick Durbin (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1433781404312215553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt a time when public confidence in government institutions has greatly eroded, we must examine not just the constitutional impact of allowing the Texas law to take effect, but also the conservative court\u8217\'20\'19s abuse of the shadow docket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s midnight order calls into question the consequences of the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s increased use of the \u8216\'20\'18shadow docket\u8217\'20\'19 in judicial review, which can hinder public confidence and leave lower courts in the dark about how to apply the court\u8217\'20\'19s precedent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Justice Kagan wrote in her dissent, \u8216\'20\'18the majority\u8217\'20\'19s decision is emblematic of too much of this court\u8217\'20\'19s shadow docket decision-making \u8211\'20\'13 which every day becomes more un-reasoned, inconsistent, and impossible to defend.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jordan hints Trump will announce 2024 run soon\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will announce a run for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawindsor/status/1433587340702851074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 any day now}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, the Ohio congressman and prominent Trump supporter Jim Jordan reportedly said in Iowa on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Jordan denied he made the comment to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theundercurrent.tv/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Undercurrent}}}\uc2 , a liberal website.\par \par \uc2 The reporter who said he did, Lauren Windsor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawindsor/status/1433646393386807297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  a still of Jordan talking and wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t both be right. See for yourself, video coming tomorrow \u8230\'20\'26 stay tuned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The still was taken from a similar angle to that with which Windsor recently caught the Wisconsin senator Ron Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://madison.com/wsj/news/local/govt-and-politics/sen-ron-johnson-nothing-obviously-skewed-about-2020-election-results/article_993349c6-b643-5741-a44d-24323ad51de0.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitting there was no voter fraud}}}\uc2  in his state at the 2020 election, and that Trump simply lost.\par \par \uc2 Still, Trump refuses to admit that and while repeatedly lying about electoral fraud has repeatedly stoked speculation that he will mount an attempt to take back the White House. In his first four-year term, he was impeached twice amid unprecedented scandal, rancour, chaos and, at its end, outright insurrection against the peaceful transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 Jordan, as it happens, is one of a number of senior Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/aug/02/want-to-make-jim-jordan-sing-about-the-capitol-attack-ask-jefferson-davis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweating over moves by the House committee}}}\uc2  investigating the deadly 6 January assault on the US Capitol, including a request that phone companies preserve records which may shed definitive light on who talked to Trump and when that day. Kevin McCarthy, the House Republican leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/02/politics/kevin-mccarthy-preserve-phone-records/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is also under scrutiny}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and has threatened phone companies with retribution if they comply.\par \par \uc2 As it also happens, Jordan hinted at an imminent Trump announcement elsewhere during his Iowa trip. Speaking at a Dallas county Republican party dinner in West Des Moines on Thursday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcci.com/article/ohio-rep-jim-jordan-teases-donald-trump-run-in-2024-during-trip-to-iowa/37468512#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KCCI Des Moines reported}}}\uc2 , Jordan said he spoke to Trump on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m convinced he\u8217\'20\'19s going to, you know, he\u8217\'20\'19s thinking about this fine governor you have [\uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 ] as part of that amazing ticket,\u8221\'20\'1D Jordan said.\par \par \uc2 A GOP official later said Trump would travel to Iowa, the first state to vote, very soon. Earlier this week, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/live/?v=524216302211545&ref=watch_permalink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told rightwing radio host Todd Starnes}}}\uc2  he would soon stage more political rallies, adding: \u8220\'20\'1C We\u8217\'20\'19re going to Iowa. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to Georgia. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to some others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s grip on the Republican party, a second presidential candidacy would likely blow other hopefuls, Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida and former Trump UN ambassador Nikki Haley prominent among them, out of the political water.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are doing their best to be prepared. On Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/heeding-steve-bannons-call-election-deniers-organize-to-seize-control-of-the-gop-and-reshape-americas-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica came out with a striking report}}}\uc2  about efforts, driven by former White House strategist and far-right gadfly \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cseize control of the GOP from the bottom up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In short, Bannon, who Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/20/donald-trump-pardons-steve-bannon-amid-last-acts-of-presidency-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardoned on federal fraud charges}}}\uc2 , thinks Trump lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause the Republican party sold him out\u8221\'20\'1D and is therefore pushing a takeover of precinct-level Republican operations by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Such workers can have an outsized effect on how elections are run, including playing a role in polling day operations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/heeding-steve-bannons-call-election-deniers-organize-to-seize-control-of-the-gop-and-reshape-americas-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica said}}}\uc2  it \u8220\'20\'1Ccontacted GOP leaders in 65 key counties, and 41 reported an unusual increase in signups since Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s campaign began. At least 8,500 new Republican precinct officers (or equivalent lowest-level officials) joined those county parties. We also looked at equivalent Democratic posts and found no similar surge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/03/trump-loyalists-doctors-ministers-reawaken-america-tour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump loyalists team up with anti-vax doctors for \u8216\'20\'18health and freedom\u8217\'20\'19 tour}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Per the disappointing jobs report ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/03/joe-biden-louisiana-texas-abortion-afghanistan-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613217f78f08bf4765a44840#block-613217f78f08bf4765a44840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see block at 8.55am}}}\uc2  ), and ahead of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remarks on the subject at 10am ET, I should add that \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Graeme Wearden knows a lot more about all this than me and is running our business blog, here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/sep/03/service-sector-china-uk-us-jobs-payroll-markets-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US added just 235,000 new jobs in August amid Delta variant surge \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ida death toll in north-east nears 50\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press puts the death-toll in the north-east from Hurricane Ida at 48, two higher than I had in my intro.\par \par \uc2 Two more deaths are reported in New Jersey, the state which has paid the highest price in lives after being hit by tornadoes at one end and flooding at the other.\par \par \uc2 Late on Thursday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  declared federal disasters for New Jersey and New York, freeing up aid.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in all affected states said the search for victims and the process of identifying the dead was not over.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s new governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , came into the job in the aftermath of Tropical Storm Henri, which was briefly a hurricane, and now continues in the aftermath of Ida.\par \par \uc2 She said on Thursday the region should follow extensive work in the aftermath of Superstorm Sandy, which battered the north-east in 2012, with more work to prepare for more frequent flash-flooding inland, as the climate crisis takes hold.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne thing I want to make clear,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1C We\u8217\'20\'19re not treating this as if it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen again for 500 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The August jobs numbers are out and they are not as good as expected. As I am not in any even remote meaning of the term a business journalist I will note that Biden is due to make remarks about the numbers at 10am ET, then offer you Reuters\u8217\'20\'19 take:\par \par \uc2 US job growth slowed more than expected in August amid a softening in demand for services and persistent worker shortages as Covid-19 infections soared, but the pace was enough to sustain the economic expansion.\par \par \uc2 Non-farm payrolls increased by 235,000 jobs last month after surging 1.053m in July, the US labor department said in its closely watched employment report on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The unemployment rate fell to 5.2% from 5.4% in July. It has, however, been understated by people misclassifying themselves as being \u8220\'20\'1Cemployed but absent from work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters had forecast non-farm payrolls increasing by 728,000 and the unemployment rate falling to 5.2%. Payrolls estimates ranged from as low as 375,000 to as high as 1.027m.\par \par \uc2 The initial August payrolls print has undershot expectations and been slower than the three-month average job growth through July over the last several years, including in 2020. August payrolls have been subsequently revised higher in 11 of the last 12 years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Reliable Sources has a handy roundup of headlines in the Texas press concerning the draconian anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law passed in the state and, via the Jack Ryan-esque {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/us/politics/supreme-court-shadow-docket-texas-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shadow Docket}}}\uc2 , not stopped by \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Austin American-Statesman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/story/opinion/editorials/2021/09/01/texas-abortion-ban-uses-harassment-bypass-rule-law-austin-american-statesman-editorial/5668857001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went with}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CTexas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban uses harassment to bypass the rule of law\u8221\'20\'1D; the Houston Chronicle opinion pages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/opinion/letters/article/Opinion-Hello-Texas-The-Wild-West-called-they-16429340.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plumped for}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CHello, Texas? The Wild West called, they want their laws back\u8221\'20\'1D; and the Fort Worth Star-Telegram {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.star-telegram.com/opinion/editorials/article253944998.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chose}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CConservatives used to hate frivolous lawsuits. Now, Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law invites them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the words of a far greater man than me, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wdEcO8_2Kl8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Morris}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThose are the headlines. God I wish they weren\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/us/politics/supreme-court-shadow-docket-texas-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interesting piece on the Shadow Docket}}}\uc2 , which it says is made up of \u8220\'20\'1C emergency petitions that often yield late-night decisions issued with minimal or no written opinions \u8221\'20\'1D, thereby departing from usual practice including oral arguments before the court, and which the conservative-dominated panel is using with increased frequency to decide matters of huge importance.\par \par \uc2 In her dissent to the unsigned opinion on the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, the liberal justice Elena Kagan said the practice \u8220\'20\'1Cevery day becomes more unreasoned, inconsistent and impossible to defend \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Steve Vladeck, a law professor at the University of Texas at Austin who has studied the Shadow Docket and testified about it, told the Times: \u8220\'20\'1CIf they are going to issue rulings that profoundly change the law, I think they have an obligation to write and to explain why they are doing it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This law has set off a five-alarm fire among liberals and supporters of women\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/supreme-court-abortion-texas-mississippi-democrats-49018174-7b2b-4e4c-b416-8d41867cd8c6.html?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that the Biden White House is ready to go into battle, seeing a hot issue for the midterms next year. Referring to the portions of the Texas law which allow people to sue anyone they suspect of even aiding an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior White House aide said: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to see the GOP defend the idea that your nosy neighbour can sue your aunt for driving you to the hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell on how Congress sees the issue:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/texas-abortion-law-biden-democrats-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats rush to find strategy to counter Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 and welcome to another day\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of politics in the US, which means the politics of the Afghanistan withdrawal and the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill and more but also of course means coverage of the ongoing fallout from Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 One of the most powerful storms ever to hit the US hammered New Orleans and left people dead in Louisiana and Mississippi, then drenched the north-east on Wednesday, killing as many as 46 people, predominantly in flash-floods. Reports out of New York, a city of basement apartments which some found impossible to escape, were appalling and moving both.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will visit Louisiana today, touring and talking in LaPlace and Lafourche. Millions are still without power.\par \par \uc2 The nearest deaths to Washington on Wednesday were in Maryland \u8211\'20\'13 New Jersey, New York and Pennsylvania suffered most \u8211\'20\'13 but Biden is, obviously, keenly aware of the national picture.\par \par \uc2 At the White House on Thursday, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe past few days of Hurricane Ida and the wildfires in the west and the unprecedented floods in New York and New Jersey is yet another reminder that the climate crisis is here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Someone should probably {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1433544610513657857"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tell Fox News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrJust check out this chyron -- alongside footage of NYC facing a historic flood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/knEr09bXPY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/knEr09bXPY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Baragona (@justinbaragona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1433544610513657857?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden will leave the White House for Louisiana at 10.30am \u8211\'20\'13 after giving remarks about the latest jobs numbers \u8211\'20\'13 and he\u8217\'20\'19ll speak again at 2.35pm.\par \par \uc2 Brian Stelter of CNN, meanwhile, makes a reasonable point about media focus on the storm in the north-east: \u8220\'20\'1CNational news outlets based in NY and DC are often accused of an east coast bias. And those complaints have a lot of merit. But not on Thursday. Ida\u8217\'20\'19s aftermath was deadlier in the north-east than the south, so the extensive coverage was entirely warranted...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s plenty more going on, of course, so stay with us.\par \par \uc2 Further reading, about where Biden\u8217\'20\'19s going:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/new-orleans-hurricane-ida-power-outage-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel abandoned\u8217\'20\'19: New Orleanians swelter through days without power}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210903eh93001uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
