\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republicans in six states rush to mimic Texas anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law\b0\par\par\uc2 Samira Sadeque in New York \par \uc2 503 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2021\par 17:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 North Dakota, South Dakota, Mississippi, Indiana, Arkansas and Florida eye similar measures to new Texas ban after six weeks\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders in as many as six US states are rushing to follow the lead of Texas in adopting an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  that critics, including Joe Biden, have slammed as unconstitutional and built to encourage vigilantism among the public.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are bracing to resist a flurry of initiatives from Florida to North Dakota in the wake of the new Texas law, the most extreme in the US, which the conservative majority on the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to block}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the law went into effect in Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  past six weeks}}}\uc2  of a pregnancy, including for victims of incest or rape, and giving any private citizen the option to sue someone providing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or anyone even believed to be peripherally assisting someone to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Within a day of the law going into effect, six other states \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncadvertiser.com/news/article/Lawmaker-North-Dakota-may-use-Texas-abortion-law-16431357.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Dakota}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-religion-us-supreme-court-laws-23c373f3252d511f15ccc170887c30e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2021/09/02/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court-indiana-ban-womens-rights/5703329001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/02/texas-abortion-law-private-right-to-sue-509244?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida, South Dakota and Arkansas}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have said they are looking to adopt a similar ban, according to numerous reports.\par \par \uc2 An Arkansas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocate told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  on Friday she was prepared to fight such a law if it were to happen in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLegislation that mirrors Texas\u8217\'20\'19s new law will harm pregnant Arkansans in need of abortions and we will not stand for it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ali Taylor, co-founder and president of the Arkansas \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Support Network. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight is far from over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added that if such legislation were pass, her organization would continue providing access to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its clients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will include helping people access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Arkansas before six weeks and helping people go out of state when they are past the [legislative] gestation limit,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be intimidated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kristin Ford, acting vice-president of communications and research at Naral Pro-Choice America , condemned the way the six states scrambled to consider the legislation with such urgency after the Texas law went into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the most acute and urgent threat to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Roe was decided half a century ago,\u8221\'20\'1D she told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , referring to the landmark Roe v Wade US supreme court decision in 1973 that effectively made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal nationwide and established the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus is viable outside the womb, typically around 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Ford said this was a product of increasingly radicalized rightwing rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe radical right has been working for decades to decimate reproductive freedom and halt social progress,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut they don\u8217\'20\'19t represent the values of Americans, eight in 10 of whom support safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and pushing these heinous laws flies in the face of public opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Pew Research Center{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/05/06/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  from May, about 59% of Americans say they support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210903eh93002mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
