\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden condemns \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18unprecedented assault\u8217\'20\'19 on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2021\par 16:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President denounces justices for failing to block Texas banVows to \u8216\'20\'18ensure women have access to safe and legal abortions\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Thursday, saying it had delivered \u8220\'20\'1Can unprecedented assault on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right\u8221\'20\'1D in a rebuke of its decision not to consider a Texas law that effectively bans abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law, one of the most restrictive abortions bans in the US in five decades, had been in effect for nearly 24 hours when the court delivered a 5-4 decision late on Wednesday that denied an emergency appeal from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 All three justices appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , along with two of the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative members, voted to deny the appeal.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/09/02/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-supreme-court-ruling-on-texas-law-sb8/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Biden pledged his administration would act to \u8220\'20\'1Censure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions\u8221\'20\'1D as protected by the landmark Roe v Wade ruling in 1973.\par \par \uc2 He said the new legislation empowered private citizens in Texas to sue healthcare providers, family members supporting a woman exercising her right to choose after six weeks, or \u8220\'20\'1Ceven a friend who drivers her to a hospital or clinic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt unleashes unconstitutional chaos and empowers self-anointed enforcers to have devastating impact,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president said he would direct the Office of the White House Counsel to \u8220\'20\'1Claunch a whole-of-government effort to respond to the decision\u8221\'20\'1D, including directing the federal justice and health departments to see \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat legal tools we have to insulate women and providers from the impact of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s bizarre scheme\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The decision from the majority appeared to shock even fellow supreme court justices. \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , who voted against the majority, called the decision \u8220\'20\'1Ca breathtaking act of defiance \u8211\'20\'13 of the constitution, of this court\u8217\'20\'19s precedent and of rights of women seeking abortions throughout Texas\u8221\'20\'1D in her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/21a24_8759.pdf#page=7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissenting opinion}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When given the chance to act on a \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional law engineered to prohibit women from exercising their constitutional rights and evade judicial scrutiny,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Ca majority of the justices have opted to bury their heads in the sand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Signed in May by the Texas governor, Greg Abbott, the law prohibits abortions once embryonic cardiac activity is detected by medical professionals, usually around six weeks of pregnancy. Reproductive health experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimate}}}\uc2  that the ban will prevent 85% of pregnant women, particularly low-income women, from getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, which has a population of 29 million.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s denial of the appeal calls into question the future of Roe v Wade, which has affirmed a person\u8217\'20\'19s right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until \u8220\'20\'1Cviability\u8221\'20\'1D of a fetus, usually in the third trimester of pregnancy. When its next term starts in October, the court is expected to decide on a law in Mississippi that bans abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The laws from Texas and Mississippi are just two of dozens of laws that have been passed in recent years that severely restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in conservative states.\par \par \uc2 States were emboldened to create anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation with the presidency of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his appointment of three conservative justices \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 who have indicated they do not believe the constitution protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas law was specifically crafted to evade the judicial scrutiny other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws have received because of Roe v Wade protections. Instead of having the government outright restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it relies on private citizens to carry out the ban. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/text/SB8/id/2395961"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2  allows private citizens to sue not only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers but also anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 a wide-ranging net meant to deter anyone from even assisting a women from getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the threat of legal action. The law does not make any exception for cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats, including Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, have said that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision emphasizes the need to abolish the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/30/what-is-filibuster-meaning-republicans-blocking-biden-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibuster}}}\uc2 , which allows a minority of 41 US senators to block a vote on most legislation. The debate over the filibuster has divided Democrats since the start of the year, when the party declared a majority in Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats can either abolish the filibuster and expand the court, or do nothing as million of people\u8217\'20\'19s bodies, rights and lives are sacrificed for far-right minority rule,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1433283680181620739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1433283680181620739%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehill.com%2Fhomenews%2Fhouse%2F570505-ocasio-cortez-scrapping-filibuster-over-abortion-rights-shouldnt-be-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a difficult decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The night before the law went into effect, some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers reported carrying out abortions until midnight, with their waiting rooms full of patients trying to get abortions while the procedure was still legal.\par \par \uc2 One clinic in Fort Worth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/09/abortion-texas-whole-womans-clinic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carried out}}}\uc2  67 abortions in 17 hours, with doctors working from 7am into the late evening.\par \par \uc2 The next day, the parking lot of the clinic was empty, Marva Sadler, senior director of clinical services at Whole Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dfw.cbslocal.com/video/5952791-fort-worth-abortion-clinic-tells-some-clients-theyll-need-to-go-out-of-state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a local TV news station. Sadler said some women had to be turned away because ultrasounds detected cardiac activity and made them ineligible for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Talking to women who the clinic had to turn away, \u8220\'20\'1Cmost of them this morning told us it\u8217\'20\'19s not about the finances of getting to another state, it\u8217\'20\'19s the day off of work, it\u8217\'20\'19s finding someone to take care of their children and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D Sadler said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s impossible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the supreme court justices who denied the appeal said that their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/21a24_8759.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cis not based on any conclusion about the constitutionality of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law\u8221\'20\'1D, it will probably encourage other states to pass similar laws designed to skirt judicial scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law] promises an alternative to that typical path that pro-life laws go down,\u8221\'20\'1D John Seago, legislative director for Texas Right to Life, an organization that helped craft the legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6093905/texas-abortion-ban-abortion-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Time. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a valid public policy tool and we\u8217\'20\'19re excited to see how it works.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a press briefing on Thursday, the White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , said Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cof course worried that other states \u8230\'20\'26 will copycat these steps that happened in Texas\u8221\'20\'1D and said the White House was acting \u8220\'20\'1Cas quickly as possible to see what our options are\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh92002mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
