\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden vows to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights after \u8216\'20\'18devastating\u8217\'20\'19 Texas ruling \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano in Portland (now) and Joanna Walters in New York (earlier) \par \uc2 9,286 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2021\par 00:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President pledges to launch \u8216\'20\'18whole-of-government effort\u8217\'20\'19Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  sides with liberal minority in 5-4 voteRead Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s scathing dissent on Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * West Virginia Democratic Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613138918f0830dd895fe2ca#block-613138918f0830dd895fe2ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisting}}}\uc2  that there should be a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in the progress through Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, specifically the passage of his $3.5tn tax and spending budget package.\par \par \uc2 * Some Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a#block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are saying}}}\uc2  the supreme court has effectively already overturned Roe v Wade after the conservative majority ruled to allow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, the most extreme in the US, to stand.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d#block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2 , the US president said, for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking \u8230\'20\'26 to see what steps the federal government can take to ensure that women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  have access to safe and legal abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Chief justiceJohn Roberts and all three liberal associate justices of the supreme court, Elena Kagan, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , penned dissents to the ruling last night. Each had hugely important points to make. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071#block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s language}}}\uc2  was the most blistering, calling the Texas law \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and the court\u8217\'20\'19s order to allow it \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll from sudden heavy rains and flooding in the US north-east is continuing to climb.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/02/flooding-deaths-north-east-us-rain-storms-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 40 people died}}}\uc2 , with at least 23 dead in New Jersey, after the remnants of Hurricane Ida brought extreme weather to the region.\par \par \uc2 * The6 January House committee wants to preserve Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s phone records. The committee tasked with investigating the deadly Capitol attack has asked telecommunications companies to preserve records belonging to the House minority leader and other House Republicans.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says the Biden administration will use \u8216\'20\'18every lever\u8217\'20\'19 to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to consider a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  law that effectively bans abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joanna Walters and Dani Anguiano\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 White House will use \u8216\'20\'18every lever\u8217\'20\'19 to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said the Biden administration will use \u8220\'20\'1Cevery lever\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cdefend the right to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to consider a Texas law that effectively bans abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe will use every lever of our Administration to defend the right to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14and to strengthen that right. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5WQAM7DNag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5WQAM7DNag}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1433566167134842885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement released Thursday afternoon, the vice-president vowed the administration would act after the justices \u8220\'20\'1Ceffectively allowed a bounty law to go into effect in Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is not the last word on Roe v Wade, and we will not stand by and allow our nation to go back to the days of back-alley abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Changing winds offer hope as firefighters battle blaze near Lake Tahoe\par \par \uc2 With winds finally turning in their favor, firefighters are throwing all their resources into boxing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  blaze burning mere miles from Lake Tahoe and neighboring Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Three days of fiercely gusting winds had driven the Caldor fire east through the rugged Sierra {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2 , forcing tens of thousands of people from the region of forests, mountain hamlets, resorts and alpine lakes.\par \par \uc2 A firefighter lights a backfire to stop the Caldor fire from spreading near South Lake Tahoe. Photograph: Jae C Hong/AP\par \par \uc2 Overnight, thousands of firefighters from around the US battled the blaze, which by Thursday morning stretched across roughly 210,259 acres (850 sq km), and achieved 25% containment.\par \par \uc2 Winds were expected to calm heading into the weekend, although the humidity remained low and the eastern side of the vast wildfire was still burning trees and running through explosively dry grasslands into areas hard for firefighters to reach, authorities said. The blaze was also throwing sparks that caught trees and created spot fires up to a mile ahead of the main wall of flames.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/caldor-fire-california-lake-tahoe-winds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Caldor fire: changing winds offer hope as firefighters battle blaze near Lake Tahoe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former US ambassador directed business to Trump hotel\par \par \uc2 Kelly Craft\uc2  steered government business to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Washington hotel while serving as the US ambassador to Canada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/zacheverson/2021/09/02/trumps-ambassador-craft-steered-us-government-business-to-her-boss-hotel/?sh=6f27176d2f8f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forbes reported Thursday.}}}\par \par \uc2 In November 2018, Craft emailed a staffer about staying at the Trump hotel for a conference in Washington DC, emails released by the state department show. In the first half of 2018, she stayed at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hotel at least three times while in DC for government business.\par \par \uc2 Craft, who later served as ambassador to the UN under Trump, previously faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/19/trump-un-pick-kelly-craft-ambassador-canada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congressional scrutiny}}}\uc2  after spending more than half her time as ambassador to Canada away from her post.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Virginia court rules state can remove Robert E Lee statue\par \par \uc2 The Virginia supreme court has cleared the path for the state to remove a statue of Robert E Lee in Richmond. The large monument to the Confederate general, which stood for over a century, became a center of protest after the death of George Floyd.\par \par \uc2 The ruling came in after lawsuits filed by residents who attempted to block removal of the 21ft bronze equestrian sculpture, which shows Lee in military attire atop a 40ft pedestal.\par \par \uc2 The statue of Confederate General Robert E Lee on Monument Avenue in Richmond. Photograph: Steve Helber/AP\par \par \uc2 More on the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/statue-confederate-general-robert-e-lee-virginia-removed-court-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Statue of Confederate Gen Robert E Lee in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s capitol can be removed, court rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 6 January House committee seeks to preserve Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s phone records\par \par \uc2 The committee tasked with investigating the deadly Capitol attack has asked telecommunications companies to preserve records belonging to the House minority leader and other House Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/02/politics/kevin-mccarthy-preserve-phone-records/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s name was included along with several other lawmakers and hundreds of others. The California Republican on Tuesday said that any company that complied with such a request from the committee would be \u8220\'20\'1Cin violation of federal law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf companies still choose to violate federal law, a Republican majority will not forget and will stand with Americans to hold them fully accountable under the law,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy, along with Jim Jordan, the top Republican on the House judiciary committee, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/capitol-riot-white-house-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already expected to face scrutiny}}}\uc2  over phone calls to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hi folks. Dani Anguiano here taking over \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of US political news for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 The death toll from the unexpected heavy rain and flooding brought by remnants of Hurricane Ida is continuing to climb. \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , the New Jersey governor, has reported at least 23 state residents died in the storm.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am saddened to report that, as of right now, at least 23 New Jerseyans have lost their life to this storm.\par \par \uc2 The majority of these deaths were individuals who got caught in their vehicles by flooding and were overtaken by the water.\par \par \uc2 Our prayers are with their family members.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  (@GovMurphy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovMurphy/status/1433538547307487237?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 At least 12 people died in New York City, police said. Officials have said many of those killed were trapped in basement apartments that filled with water.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively afternoon and my colleague on the US west coast, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dani-anguiano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dani Anguiano}}}\uc2 , will now take over the blog and bring you any remaining developments in US political news for the next few hours, so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Main events today so far:\par \par \uc2 * West Virginia Democratic Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-613138918f0830dd895fe2ca#block-613138918f0830dd895fe2ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisting}}}\uc2  today that there should be a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in the progress through Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, specifically the passage of his $3.5 trillion tax and spending budget package.\par \par \uc2 * Some Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a#block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are saying}}}\uc2  that the supreme court has effectively already overturned Roe v Wade after the conservative majority ruled to allow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, currently the most extreme in the US, to stand.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke of the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130f79f8f083528f0f52296#block-6130f79f8f083528f0f52296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unimaginable damage}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D caused by the aftermath of Hurricane Ida coming ashore on the Gulf coast last weekend and now causing flooding as far north as New York, so far.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d#block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2 , the US president said, for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking \u8230\'20\'26 to see what steps the federal government can take to ensure that women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  have access to safe and legal abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Chief JusticeJohn Roberts and all three liberal associate justices of the Supreme Court, Elena Kagan, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , penned dissents to the ruling last night. Each had hugely important points to make. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071#block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s language}}}\uc2  was the most blistering, calling the Texas law \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and the court\u8217\'20\'19s order to allow it \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrat Manchin calls for "pause" in Biden budget bill\par \par \uc2 West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  is insisting today that there should be a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic pause\u8221\'20\'1D in the progress through Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, specifically the passage of his $3.5 trillion tax and spending budget package.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin digs in against $3.5 trillion plan. "Yet some in Congress have a strange belief there is an infinite supply of money to deal with any current or future crisis, and that spending trillions upon trillions will have no negative consequence for the future. I disagree."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1433509319920734212?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This endangers the flagship budget legislation that Democratic leaders plan to push through Congress this fall (bypassing the filibuster in the Senate so that Republicans can\u8217\'20\'19t block it).\par \par \uc2 But the conservative-leaning Democrat said at a chamber of commerce event in West Virginia yesterday - and in an opinion piece in the Wall Street Journal (subscription) today that the specter of rising inflation and a bloated national debt mean not only applying the brakes but also devising a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificantly smaller\u8221\'20\'1D package.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy placing a strategic pause on this budgetary proposal, by significantly reducing the size of any possible reconciliation bill to only what America can afford and needs to spend, we can and will build a better and stronger nation for all our families,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said in the WSJ.\par \par \uc2 Manchin yesterday called on Democrats to \u8220\'20\'1Chit the pause button\u8221\'20\'1D on the legislation, citing what he thinks are more important concerns, such as the issue of national security in the wake of the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s takeover of Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s sit back. Let\u8217\'20\'19s see what happens. We have so much on our plate,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The Dems will need every single one of its US Senators to vote for the legislation, with the chamber tied 50-50 with the Republicans and vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  able to cast a deciding vote as president of the Senate, with the passage bypassing the filibuster obligation because it involves budgetary legislation.\par \par \uc2 But Manchin is right now against.\par \par \uc2 enltrManchin: "I, for one, won\u8217\'20\'19t support a $3.5 trillion bill, or anywhere near that level of additional spending, without greater clarity about why Congress chooses to ignore the serious effects inflation and debt have on existing government programs."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1433510541201379329?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 A former Georgia prosecutor has been indicted today on misconduct charges alleging she used her position to shield the men who chased and killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ahmaud-arbery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ahmaud Arbery}}}\uc2  from being charged with crimes immediately after the shootings.\par \par \uc2 A mural of Ahmaud Arbery in Brunswick, Georgia. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The AP writes:\par \par \uc2 A grand jury in coastal Glynn County indicted former Brunswick Judicial Circuit District Attorney Jackie Johnson on charges of violating her oath of office and hindering a law enforcement officer.\par \par \uc2 Arbery was killed Feb. 23, 2020, after a white father and son, Greg and Travis McMichael, armed themselves and pursued the 25-year-Black man in a pickup truck after spotting him running in their neighborhood outside the coastal city of Brunswick.\par \par \uc2 A neighbor, William \u8220\'20\'1CRoddie\u8221\'20\'1D Bryan joined the chase and took cellphone video of Travis McMichael shooting Arbery at close range with a shotgun. The McMichales said they believed Arbery was a burglar and that he was shot after attacking Travis McMichael with his fists.\par \par \uc2 Police did not charge any of them immediately following the shooting, and the McMichaels and Bryan remained free for more than two months until the \uc2 Georgia Bureau of Investigation\uc2  took over the case. All three were charged with murder in May 2020 and face trial this fall.\par \par \uc2 Greg McMichael had worked as an investigator in Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s office and left her a cellphone message following the shooting.\par \par \uc2 The indictment says Johnson showed \u8220\'20\'1Cfavor and affection\u8221\'20\'1D toward Greg McMichael in the investigation and interfered with police officers at the scene by \u8220\'20\'1Cdirecting that Travis McMichael should not be placed under arrest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson has insisted she did nothing wrong, saying she immediately recused herself from the case because Greg McMichael was a former employee. She recommended an outside prosecutor, Waycross Judicial Circuit District Attorney George Barnhill, who was appointed to the case and concluded no charges were warranted. Barnhill later stepped aside after Arbery\u8217\'20\'19s family noted he had a son working for Johnson as an assistant prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Johnson lost reelection last year, and blamed the controversy over Arbery\u8217\'20\'19s death for her defeat. She did not immediately return a phone message seeking comment Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court allowing a new Texas law that bans most abortions is the biggest curb to the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in decades, and Republicans in other states are already considering similar measures.\par \par \uc2 The law prohibits abortions once medical professionals can detect cardiac activity, usually around six weeks before some women know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant, The Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Courts have blocked other states from imposing similar restrictions, but Texas\u8217\'20\'19 law differs significantly because it leaves enforcement up to private citizens through civil lawsuits instead of criminal prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The AP writes further:\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know about the new Texas law that took effect Tuesday, which already has \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in neighboring states reporting a surge in the number of Texas women seeking the procedure:\par \par \uc2 WHAT DOES THE TEXAS LAW DO?\par \par \uc2 It allows any private citizen to sue Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who violate the law, as well as anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D a woman getting the procedure. The law does not make exceptions for rape or incest. The person bringing the lawsuit who needs to have no connection to the woman getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is entitled to at least $10,000 in damages if they prevail in court.\par \par \uc2 HOW MANY PEOPLE COULD BE AFFECTED BY THE TEXAS LAW?\par \par \uc2 The new Texas law could affect thousands of women seeking abortions, though precise estimates are difficult. In 2020, Texas facilities performed about 54,000 abortions on residents. More than 45,000 of those occurred at eight weeks of pregnancy or less. Some of those abortions still could have been legal under the new law, if they occurred before cardiac activity was detected.\par \par \uc2 HOW IS THE TEXAS LAW DIFFERENT FROM THOSE IN OTHER STATES THAT HAVE TRIED TO RESTRICT \b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  EARLY IN PREGNANCY?\par \par \uc2 The key difference is the enforcement mechanism. The Texas law relies on citizens suing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers over alleged violations. Other states sought to enforce their statutes through government actions like criminal charges against physicians who provide abortions.\par \par \uc2 Texas is one of 14 states with laws either banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely or prohibiting it after eight weeks or less of pregnancy. The rest have all been put on hold by courts. Most recently, a court halted a new Arkansas law that would have banned all abortions unless necessary to save the life of the mother in a medical emergency. Other states with blocked laws banning abortions early in pregnancy are Alabama, Georgia, Iowa, Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, Missouri, North Dakota, Ohio, South Carolina, Tennessee and Utah.\par \par \uc2 HOW DID THE TEXAS \b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LAW COME ABOUT?\par \par \uc2 Texas has long been a major battleground over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and access, including a 2013 law that closed more than half of the 40-plus \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the state before it was blocked by the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Emboldened by victories in the 2020 elections, Republicans responded with a hard-right agenda this year that included loosening gun laws and further tightening what are already some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s strictest voting rules. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups say the new law was in response to frustration over prosecutors refusing to enforce other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions already on the books.\par \par \uc2 Before Republican Gov. Greg Abbott signed the law in May, voters in Lubbock, Texas, approved an ordinance similarly intended to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the city by allowing family members to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats have promoted Republican congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  to become vice chair of the specially-convened committee investigating the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 Capitol insurrection}}}\uc2  by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , left, and \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , right, in foreground, after the first hearing of the House Select committee to investigate the January 6 attack on the U.S. Capitol, on Capitol Hill in Washington, in July. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 The move places her in a leadership spot on the panel, even as some Republicans are threatening to oust her from the GOP party conference for participating, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Cheney, who has become a fierce critic of former Trump, has remained defiant amid the criticism from her own party, insisting that Congress must probe the Capitol attack, in which hundreds of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters violently pushed past police, broke into the building and interrupted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certification of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election victory}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press further reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe owe it to the American people to investigate everything that led up to, and transpired on, January 6th,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney, Republican of Wyoming, said in a statement as Democrats announced her promotion on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be deterred by threats or attempted obstruction and we will not rest until our task is complete.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s appointment as vice chairwoman comes amid an effort by some Republicans to oust Cheney and congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , Republican of Illinois, from the GOP conference because they accepted their appointments to the panel from House Speaker and top Democrat \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . A draft letter by Arizona Rep. Andy Biggs to Republican Leader Kevin McCarthy obtained by The Associated Press calls Cheney and Kinzinger \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo spies for the Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D whom Republicans cannot trust to attend their private meetings.\par \par \uc2 Biggs, chairman of the conservative House Freedom Caucus, is calling on the conference to change its rules to state that any Republican who accepts a committee assignment or serves on a committee without a recommendation from GOP leadership \u8220\'20\'1Cshall immediately cease to be a Member of the Conference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the committee has met privately, Cheney has worked closely with Democrats in determining the direction of the probe. The committee\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, Mississippi Representative \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , said in the statement announcing Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s appointment that Democrats are \u8220\'20\'1Cfortunate to have a partner of such strength and courage\u8221\'20\'1D and that Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s insights have shaped the early work of the panel.\par \par \uc2 Cheney \u8220\'20\'1Chas demonstrated again and again her commitment to getting answers about January 6th, ensuring accountability, and doing whatever it takes to protect democracy for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, McCarthy has issued a veiled threat to telecom and social media companies who comply with committee requests to turn over records that illuminate what certain politicians may have been saying in the run up to and during the insurrection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://us.cnn.com/2021/08/31/politics/mccarthy-january-6-committee-records-requests-warning/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN has reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 We mentioned earlier that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t specifically link climate change with the extreme weather that\u8217\'20\'19s exacerbating storms in the south and east and wildfires in the west, when he spoke at the White House earlier.\par \par \uc2 But it would be remiss of us not to point out that he did mention his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/us-senate-passes-bipartisan-infrastructure-bill-biden-schumer-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infrastructure plans}}}\uc2 , which include measures to mitigate the effects of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 The president said:\par \par \uc2 When Congress returns this month, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to press for their action on my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/us-senate-passes-bipartisan-infrastructure-bill-biden-schumer-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Build Back Better plan}}}\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s going to make historic investments in electrical infrastructure, modernizing our roads, bridges, our water systems, sewer and draining systems, electric grids and transmission lines, and make them more resilient to these superstorms and wildfires and floods that are going to happen with increasing frequency and ferocity.\par \par \uc2 At the White House briefing a little earlier, press sec \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked if the extreme weather events had changed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s view on action needed on carbon reduction to combat global heating.\par \par \uc2 Psaki pointed out that: \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s reaffirmed with his his commitment today to getting his Build Back Better agenda passed, which has a huge focus on addressing the climate crisis and taking a number of steps, including investing in resiliency for infrastructure, also setting ambitious goals and taking policy steps to reach those.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-controlled House of Representatives plans to debate and vote on legislation aimed at stopping states from enacting tough anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations like the one in Texas, Speaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi}}}\uc2  said today.\par \par \uc2 Speaker Pelosi holding a press conference on Capitol Hill last month with leaders of the Poor People\u8217\'20\'19s Campaign. Photograph: Lenin Nolly/NurPhoto/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 But the bill\u8217\'20\'19s prospects in the Senate are slim unless this is the hill the Biden White House chooses to kill the filibuster on.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Texas law}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1Cdelivers catastrophe to women in Texas, particularly women of color and women from low-income communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said in a statement that a Democratic bill would be brought before the full House after September 20, when its recess is scheduled to end.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters news agency adds:\par \par \uc2 Most legislation requires the support of at least 60 lawmakers to advance in the Senate. The House Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 measure, the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, would likely struggle to get 10 votes among Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Most Republicans oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the most divisive issues in the United States, and many have urged the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark decision making it a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 The Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act has been introduced in Congress multiple times since 2013 but never advanced in either the House or Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is now briefing the media. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is busy simultaneously (but in another room) talking with Jewish religious leaders to celebrate the beginning of the season of Jewish high holidays.\par \par \uc2 White House Press Briefing with \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  yesterday. Photograph: Michael Brochstein/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Psaki is now speaking to the point that the US president made earlier, on the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come into effect}}}\uc2  in Texas this week, with the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  refusing the block it.\par \par \uc2 Biden said earlier that he was directing the Office of the White House Counsel \u8220\'20\'1Cto launch a whole-of-government effort to respond to this decision [by Scotus], looking...to see what steps the federal government can take to ensure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki just said, in response to a question, that the impact of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last night\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  requires immediate processes to get underway, effectively, to figure out if there is any recourse by the administration.\par \par \uc2 She added that he has asked his team \u8220\'20\'1Cto determine what if any steps can be taken here to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, and access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if the White House was surprised by the supreme court ruling last night, Psaki said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know the make-up of the court, but we try to stay away from predictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supported-group-fertilization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arch-conservative}}}\uc2  selection to replace the late liberal champion \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , tipped the court to a swing-proof conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  is regarded as a more moderate conservative, but even if he sides with the three liberal justices on the bench, as he did last night on the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, those four are no match for Barrett, \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  when those conservatives opine as a bloc.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  on Amy Coney Barrett:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supported-group-fertilization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: Amy Coney Barrett supported group that said life begins at fertilization}}}\par \par \uc2 And this:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett signed newspaper ad that called Roe v Wade 'barbaric'}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 This is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/09/new-york-city-storm-flooding-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second time in recent weeks}}}\uc2  that subway stations and streets have been submerged in New York city as flooding and heavy rain impacting the city and the wider US north east region have killed more than 20 people.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has pledged to tackle climate change but this week it was also being criticized by environmental groups after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/biden-administration-takes-steps-resume-oil-gas-drilling-auctions-2021-08-31/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resuming drilling auctions for oil and gas exploration.}}}\par \par \uc2 Four environmental groups have filed a lawsuit in Washington federal court challenging the decision to hold the offshore auction, alleging the underlying environmental analysis was flawed and violated federal law, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration has folded to the oil industry... ignoring the worsening climate emergency we face,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brettny Hardy, an attorney with \uc2 Earthjustice\uc2 , which filed the lawsuit on behalf of the groups.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 The morning has been dominated by reaction to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  decision last night, refusing to block an extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in Texas. And there has also been a lot of attention by leaders from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on down on the devastation caused by a storm system spawned by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have lots more US politics news going forward. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is due to brief the media at 2pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Here are the main points so far today:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a#block-6131040b8f083528f0f5238a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decry}}}\uc2  supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusal to block}}}\uc2  Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme anti- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  after issuing an emergency opinion last night.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke of the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130f79f8f083528f0f52296#block-6130f79f8f083528f0f52296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unimaginable damage}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D caused by the aftermath of Hurricane Ida coming ashore on the Gulf coast last weekend and now causing flooding as far north as New York, so far.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d#block-6130f1988f083528f0f5222d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2 , the US president said, for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking \u8230\'20\'26 to see what steps the federal government can take to ensure that women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  have access to safe and legal abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2 , a former acting solicitor general of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130e76b8f0830dd895fdde7#block-6130e76b8f0830dd895fdde7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on}}}\uc2  Congress to act immediately over the Scotus majority-conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  not to block the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Chief JusticeJohn Roberts and all three liberal associate justices of the Supreme Court, Elena Kagan, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , penned dissents to the ruling last night. Each had hugely important points to make. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071#block-6130d6e98f083528f0f52071"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s language}}}\uc2  was the most blistering, calling the Texas law \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and the court\u8217\'20\'19s order to allow it \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats decry supreme court refusal to block Texas's extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law after issuing an emergency opinion\par \par \uc2 Many are saying that the supreme court has effectively already overturned Roe v Wade after the conservative majority ruled to allow the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, currently the most extreme in the US, to stand.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law bans almost all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy and, given that about nine of of 10 abortions are performed after six weeks and many don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they are pregnant before that, it more or less bans abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 Judges in Texas did not stop the law taking effect and an appeal from the pro-choice side to the supreme court failed last night. The law not just imposes a ban but allows ordinary citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and anyone allegedly \u8220\'20\'1Caiding and abetting\u8221\'20\'1D, such as someone who drives someone to a clinic, although it does not allow the suing of the patient themself.\par \par \uc2 New York progressive congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez said on \uc2 twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans promised to overturn Roe v Wade, and they have. Democrats can either abolish the filibuster and expand the court, or do nothing as millions of peoples\u8217\'20\'19 bodies, rights, and lives are sacrificed for far-right minority rule. This shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a difficult decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublicans promised to overturn Roe v Wade, and they have.\par \par \uc2 Democrats can either abolish the filibuster and expand the court, or do nothing as millions of peoples\u8217\'20\'19 bodies, rights, and lives are sacrificed for far-right minority rule.\par \par \uc2 This shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a difficult decision. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GcEjkxt3gs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GcEjkxt3gs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1433283680181620739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 She means the Biden administration should decide to expand the supreme court beyond the nine-member bench, so that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could pick more liberals and get them seated on the court to provide a liberal majority there. Right now there are five arch conservatives and three liberals, so even if chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  sides with the liberals, as he did last night, it does not stop the will of the conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Democrats wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to get approval to expand the court through the narrowly-balanced \uc2 US Senate\uc2  without destroying the filibuster, a rule that means a majority of 60 is needed to approve things, while the Democrats only have 50 Senators and the Republicans have 50.\par \par \uc2 Freshman progressive congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  of New York backed up AOC on \uc2 twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrFor 48 years, Roe v. Wade has been the law of the land in America.\par \par \uc2 Republicans on the Supreme Court just effectively struck it down. They\u8217\'20\'19re not playing by the rules, and it\u8217\'20\'19s time for the President and Senate to act to save lives.\par \par \uc2 Expand the Court. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gptdYm4E7P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gptdYm4E7P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  (@JamaalBowmanNY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamaalBowmanNY/status/1433393742640291843?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 He later added:\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublicans are quick to talk about \u8220\'20\'1Cindividual liberties\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom,\u8221\'20\'1D but remain relentless on legislating what decisions people are allowed to make about their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  (@JamaalBowmanNY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamaalBowmanNY/status/1433414539253530628?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is urging insurance companies not to hold back on paying out to people engulfed by flooding as a result of the storms unleashed by Hurricane Ida, across a huge swath of the US, after the tempest came ashore at the weekend near New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 The US president is calling on the corporations to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo the right thing\u8221\'20\'1D and not to refuse to pay out for relocation costs based on \u8220\'20\'1Cfine print\u8221\'20\'1D such as whether a state or locality ordered a mandatory evacuation or urged voluntary evacuation, pointing out that often there isn\u8217\'20\'19t time to upgrade an evacuation announcement to a mandatory order, before a tempest hits.\par \par \uc2 And he pointed out that sometimes staying at home instead of evacuating can mean the difference between life and death, so it\u8217\'20\'19s not exactly voluntary.\par \par \uc2 Biden said he spoke earlier today to New York state\u8217\'20\'19s new governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , and New Jersey governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  and would soon be talking with Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2  (all Democrats) about the terrible impact the storm had on their states last night and the continued effects today.\par \par \uc2 enltrFollowing the stunning flooding, New York Gov. Kathy Hochul says she just got off the phone with President Biden and he told he\u8217\'20\'19d approve \u8220\'20\'1Cany declaration\u8221\'20\'1D she needs.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1433440260743221250?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Rivers around Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Philadelphia are so swollen that the city is hamstrung by major flooding in the region today.\par \par \uc2 Last night the National Weather Service issued a flash flood emergency warning for all five boroughs of New York City: Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx and Staten Island.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the first time that such a warning has ever been issued for the city. People were trapped in the subways\u8221\'20\'1D and had to be rescued by firefighters, he said.\par \par \uc2 The death toll in the New York region has now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/new-york-flooding-state-of-emergency-ny-city-flash-flood-nyc-hurricane-ida-remnants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risen to 14}}}\uc2 . The death toll in the US Gulf area so far is six. All from the same storm.\par \par \uc2 Biden also noted that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/caldor-fire-california-lake-tahoe-winds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 massive Caldor wildfire}}}\uc2  burning in California and into Nevada \u8220\'20\'1Cis one of the few fires that has ever burned from one side of Sierra Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s mountain range to the other. So far it has burned more than 200,000 acres.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Disappointingly, he did not take the opportunity to address the role the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  is playing in making these extreme weather events such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/hurricane-ida-aftermath-climate-change-making-hurricanes-devastating/story?id=79727034"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hurricanes}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/opinion/story/2021-09-01/tahoe-caldor-wildfire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fires}}}\uc2  more devastating and more frequent.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez just retweeted this:\par \par \uc2 enltrI never want to hear anyone say that a Green New Deal is too expensive ever again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AAO6Xo26OO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AAO6Xo26OO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr. Lucky Tran (@luckytran) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/luckytran/status/1433268106495991811?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe nation is here to help\u8221\'20\'1D those who have fallen victim to the storms unleashed by Hurricane Ida.\par \par \uc2 First responders pull residents in a boat following flooding in Mamaroneck, New York, that trapped people. Photograph: Mike Segar/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Buildings have been ripped apart and floods have inundated areas from Louisiana to New York.\par \par \uc2 Boats are going house to house in parts of Pennsylvania right now rescuing people. Maryland and New Jersey saw tornadoes twisting through and New York city was under a rare tornado warning for a while last night.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s widely acknowledged now that the climate crisis is leading to more extreme weather hitting the world more often, including in the US. From the floods caused by Ida to the drought and high temperatures fueling humungous wildfires out west, climate change is upping extreme weather in the US from coast to coast.\par \par \uc2 The US president just said that rain was falling in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Central Park last night at the rate of three inches per hour at a certain stage. More rain fell during the storm, which lasted for about 12 hours, in New York than normally falls in the whole of September, Biden pointed out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks of "devastation" from storm unfolding from Hurricane Ida\par \par \uc2 The US president is speaking now on the historic northeast US flooding caused last night by the huge storm that howled in across Pennsylvania, New Jersey and New York and had started in the US Gulf as Hurricane Ida that hit Louisiana as a Category four and then downgraded to a still-destructive storm.\par \par \uc2 Biden said that Hurricane Ida, which hit at the weekend, was the fifth largest in US recorded history.\par \par \uc2 Biden pointed out that the winds \u8220\'20\'1Cliterally cause the Mississippi River to change course\u8221\'20\'1D temporarily as a result of the massive winds.\par \par \uc2 He said there were winds believed to have gusted up to 170mph, causing \u8220\'20\'1Cunimaginable damage\u8221\'20\'1D and cause such damage that it slowed rescue and clear-up efforts.\par \par \uc2 The president is going to New Orleans and other parts of Louisiana tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement from moments ago on the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to block the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law now in effect in the US, in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  strongly support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The US president and vice president have called on Congress to codify the rights afforded by Roe v Wade, to protect them from action in the courts. Photograph: Chris Kleponis/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling overnight is an unprecedented assault on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rights under Roe v. Wade, which has been the law of the land for almost fifty years. By allowing a law to go into effect that empowers private citizens in Texas to sue health care providers, family members supporting a woman exercising her right to choose after six weeks, or even a friend who drives her to a hospital or clinic, it unleashes unconstitutional chaos and empowers self-anointed enforcers to have devastating impacts.\par \par \uc2 Complete strangers will now be empowered to inject themselves in the most private and personal health decisions faced by women. This law is so extreme it does not even allow for exceptions in the case of rape or incest. And it not only empowers complete strangers to inject themselves into the most private of decisions made by a woman\u8212\'20\'14it actually incentivizes them to do so with the prospect of $10,000 if they win their case.\par \par \uc2 For the majority to do this without a hearing, without the benefit of an opinion from a court below, and without due consideration of the issues, insults the rule of law and the rights of all Americans to seek redress from our courts. Rather than use its supreme authority to ensure justice could be fairly sought, the highest Court of our land will allow millions of women in Texas in need of critical reproductive care to suffer while courts sift through procedural complexities.\par \par \uc2 The dissents by Chief Justice Roberts, and Justices Breyer, Sotomayor, and Kagan [note: which you can read in earlier posts in today\u8217\'20\'19s blog] all demonstrate the error of the Court\u8217\'20\'19s action here powerfully.\par \par \uc2 While the Chief Justice was clear to stress that the action by the Supreme Court is not a final ruling on the future of Roe, the impact of last night\u8217\'20\'19s decision will be immediate and requires an immediate response. One reason I became the first president in history to create a Gender Policy Council was to be prepared to react to such assaults on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. Hence, I am directing that Council and the Office of the White House Counsel to launch a whole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking specifically to the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  and the Department of Justice to see what steps the Federal Government can take to ensure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions as protected by Roe, and what legal tools we have to insulate women and providers from the impact of Texas\u8217\'20\'19 bizarre scheme of outsourced enforcement to private parties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are waiting for Joe Bide n to make public remarks on the aftermath of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/new-orleans-hurricane-ida-power-outage-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Ida}}}\uc2 , which has sent a storm rampaging across a huge swath of the US, causing death and suffering from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/new-orleans-hurricane-ida-power-outage-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  to Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/new-york-flooding-state-of-emergency-ny-city-flash-flood-nyc-hurricane-ida-remnants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey and New York}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president is running behind schedule on this, as is very common for him. In the meantime he put out a statement on the Supreme Court emergency opinion just before midnight last night that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block an extreme law in Texas}}}\uc2  that came into effect on September 1 and bans almost all abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 This is seen as opening a very obvious path for the court to overturn the landmark 1973 ruling in Roe v Wade that essentially legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in the US for the first time.\par \par \uc2 Biden said of the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority opinion: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the majority to do this without a hearing, without the benefit of an opinion from a court below, and without due consideration of the issues, insults the rule of law and the rights of all Americans to seek redress from our courts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/09/02/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-supreme-court-ruling-on-texas-law-sb8/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full statement}}}\uc2  and we\u8217\'20\'19ll spell out more of it in the next post.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden pledges action to stop Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 The US president just spoke and said that the White House is pushing for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking \u8230\'20\'26 to see what steps the federal government can take to ensure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yesterday Biden was looking to Congress to solve this, in the face of the failure to do so by the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 . But clearly the pressure is building on the administration after last night\u8217\'20\'19s Scotus decision not to block the Texas law.\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking from Biden:\par \par \uc2 "I am directing that Council and the Office of the WH Counsel to launch a whole-of-government effort to respond to this decision, looking \u8230\'20\'26 to see what steps the Federal Gov't can take to ensure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1433450949079670794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  referred in his tweet last night to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/outlook/2021/06/07/roe-abortion-congress-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion piece}}}\uc2  he wrote for the Washington Post in June and gives good context to his call for Congress to act.\par \par \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  speaks to the media outside the Supreme Court in 2018 after arguing against the Trump administration in a case. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 Congress passing a law that enshrines the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in legislation, if possible, would certainly be a faster and maybe less controversial approach than Biden trying to expand the supreme court to engineer a new liberal majority on the bench.\par \par \uc2 Katyal wrote the piece in June, when Scotus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/17/abortion-case-supreme-court-threatens-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to consider}}}\uc2  in its next term, which begins in October, what at that point was the most significant major challenge to US reproductive rights, saying it would consider a case where the state of Mississippi wants to enforce a ban on almost all abortions after the 15th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi case was to be the first on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come before the court since the confirmation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/19/amy-coney-barrett-william-barr-book-deals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  on the eve of the election last year. She is a devout Catholic and gave conservatives on the court a 6-3 majority.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi case could lead to the landmark Roe v Wade precedent being gutted after nearly half a century.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  law, enacted in 2018, was blocked by lower courts as inconsistent with supreme court precedent that protects the right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the foetus can survive outside the womb. The block was appealed to Scotus.\par \par \uc2 Then came this week\u8217\'20\'19s Texas shock and everything changed. However, Katyal is consistent in his argument in that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/outlook/2021/06/07/roe-abortion-congress-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post piece}}}\uc2  that:\par \par \uc2 Congress can, right now, by simple majority vote, protect those rights and nullify any threat posed by the Mississippi case or any other....because the Constitution says that federal law reigns supreme over state laws, this insight also means that Congress can sweep away state laws that conflict with federal protections. Congress uses this power of \u8220\'20\'1Cpreemption\u8221\'20\'1D all the time \u8212\'20\'14 blocking states from having their own food and drug laws, employment rules, banking regulations and the like. Congress also frequently passes legislation to guarantee rights. Indeed, almost all of the major civil rights protections you have at your job or at restaurants or in hotels are guaranteed by Congress, not the courts or the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 That is because the Constitution restricts only governments, not private individuals or corporations.\par \par \uc2 Congress has a bill before it that would capitalize on this insight and statutorily guarantee the reproductive rights recognized by the Supreme Court since 1973. Called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/senate-bill/1645/cosponsors?searchResultViewType=expanded"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act}}}\uc2  and sponsored by senators including Kyrsten Sinema (D-Ariz.), Charles E. Schumer (D-N.Y.), Tim Kaine (D-Va.) and \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  (D-Minn.), it would codify the rights [on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] two generations have taken as part of American life....\par \par \uc2 Some in the Senate would try to filibuster the legislation, claiming 60 votes, not 50, is needed to pass it. But if there is ever a piece of legislation that merits a departure from the filibuster, this is pretty much it. Recall that it was the Republicans in the Senate who bypassed the filibuster when they confirmed President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s three nominees to the Supreme Court, including Barrett.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former acting solicitor general calls for Congress to act immediately to codify Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into legislation\par \par \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2 , a former acting solicitor general of the US, and a professor in national security law at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 , in Washington, DC, tweeted early this morning shortly after the Scotus (\uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2 ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  not to block the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  , calling on Congress to act.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongress should tmrw pass legislation to codify Roe. SCOTUS powerless to stop it. If try filibuster, great arg to get rid of it. Trump nuked filibuster for S Ct. If 50 is good enough to confirm a justice for life&against Roe... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/prjHTyUrA5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/prjHTyUrA5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1433289147289149442?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Elena Kagan was solicitor general before she was tapped by \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  to join the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Katyal urges the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  right now to take up legislation that would codify the rights afforded by the Roe v Wade landmark 1973 decision that essentially legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in the US for the first time.\par \par \uc2 But as we see, that constitutional right is constantly under attack from the political right, both with restrictive state laws and with appeals to the supreme court that aim to reduce the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  further and further and ultimately overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 So Katyal (and president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ) is freshly urging Congress to act.\par \par \uc2 This article from New York magazine\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecut.com/2019/10/what-does-codify-roe-v-wade-mean-from-democratic-debate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Cut explains}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Codifying Roe v. Wade would take the question of safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s hands by passing legislation in Congress that guarantees women in every state the right to unfettered access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. This would protect the right to choose even in the event that Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Finally, Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the most centrist liberal, if you like, on the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 , also wrote a dissenting opinion to the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s last night after the court refused to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme law banning most abortions and encouraging the public to sue providers and \u8220\'20\'1Cabettors\u8221\'20\'1D of the service.\par \par \uc2 Breyer has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jun/16/stephen-breyer-supreme-court-retirement-legal-scholars-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under pressure to retire}}}\uc2  so that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can have his best chance of successfully picking a liberal replacement without running into schemes by the Republicans to block the confirmation of his choice. But Breyer has indicated that that is not about to happen.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the court\u8217\'20\'19s oldest justice, at age 83.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the oldest member of the supreme court bench at 83. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Last night he joined the dissenters in opposing the majority and expressing his view on their decision.\par \par \uc2 He, as had been mentioned by other dissenters, talks about the effort by the Texas state legislature to insulate its law from judicial review by \u8220\'20\'1Cdelegating\u8221\'20\'1D to the general public the power to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, which critics slam as sanctioning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fee7f8f083528f0f51524#block-612fee7f8f083528f0f51524"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vigilantism}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bryer wrote last night:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI recognize that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law delegates the State\u8217\'20\'19s power to prevent abortions not to one person (such as a district attorney) or to a few persons (such as a group of government officials or private citizens) but to any person.\par \par \uc2 But I do not see why that fact should make a critical legal difference. That delegation still threatens to invade a constitutional right, and the coming into effect of that delegation still threatens imminent harm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice Elena Kagan, on the liberal wing of the supreme court, brought up the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s opinion last night in the context of two landmark cases - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  from 1973 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/17/abortion-case-supreme-court-threatens-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood v Casey}}}\uc2  from 1992.\par \par \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  Justices (L-R) Elena Kagan, \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  arrive for the inauguration of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Washington on January 20. To the right is Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Reynolds/EPA\par \par \uc2 Roe was the milestone that for the first time lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being a legal right across the United States. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/505/833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1992 case}}}\uc2  was a key reaffirmation by the court of the constitutional right afforded by Roe.\par \par \uc2 The court found that individual US states may not impose an \u8220\'20\'1Cundue burden\u8221\'20\'1D on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the stage where the fetus is considered viable (which differs from state to state but has typically been around six months).\par \par \uc2 Kagan also echoed Sotomayor in calling the Texas law \u8220\'20\'1Cpatently unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D and decried the rushed case. Kagan points out that the court majority has not tried to dispute that the Texas law contravenes constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 In her fierce dissent last night, she said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout full briefing or argument, and after less than 72 hours\u8217\'20\'19 thought, this Court greenlights the operation of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s patently unconstitutional law banning most abortions.\par \par \uc2 The Court thus rewards Texas\u8217\'20\'19s scheme to insulate its law from judicial review by deputizing private parties to carry out unconstitutional restrictions on the State\u8217\'20\'19s behalf.\par \par \uc2 As of last night, and because of this Court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Texas law prohibits abortions for the vast majority of women who seek them\u8212\'20\'14in clear, and indeed undisputed, conflict with Roe and Casey.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor says court order is 'stunning' in her dissent, Texas law 'flagrantly unconstitutional'\par \par \uc2 The reaction to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s majority decision last night by the court\u8217\'20\'19s dissenting justices was interesting in that all four of the judges regarded as the liberal wing issued statements and so did the chief justice.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  poses during a group photo in Washington DC, in April. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dissent was characteristically blistering.\par \par \uc2 She wrote:\par \par \uc2 The Court\u8217\'20\'19s order is stunning. Presented with an application to enjoin a flagrantly unconstitutional law engineered to prohibit women from exercising their constitutional rights and evade judicial scrutiny, a majority of Justices have opted to bury their heads in the sand.\par \par \uc2 Last night [Tuesday], the Court silently acquiesced in a State\u8217\'20\'19s enactment of a law that flouts nearly 50 years of federal precedents.\par \par \uc2 Today [just before midnight on Wednesday], the Court belatedly explains that it declined to grant relief because of procedural complexities of the State\u8217\'20\'19s own invention....\par \par \uc2 Because the Court\u8217\'20\'19s failure to act rewards tactics designed to avoid judicial review and inflicts significant harm on the applicants and on women seeking abortions in Texas, I dissent. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  issued a firm dissent to the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s opinion on the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  (L) is greeted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the president arrived to deliver his first address to a joint session of Congress in the House chamber of the US Capitol in Washington, DC, in April. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe statutory scheme before the Court is not only unusual, but unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 The [Texas state] legislature has imposed a prohibition on abortions after roughly six weeks, and then essentially delegated enforcement of that prohibition to the populace at large.\par \par \uc2 The desired consequence appears to be to insulate the State from responsibility for implementing and enforcing the regulatory regime.\par \par \uc2 Although the Court does not address the constitutionality of this law, it can of course promptly do so when that questions is properly presented,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts wrote last night\par \par \uc2 Roberts has sided with the liberal wing of the court before and that has been enough to stop the conservative supreme court judges from having their way - such as a few years ago when he was instrumental in protecting the Affordable Care Act (aka Obamacare), where the federal government helped millions more Americans get health insurance cover.\par \par \uc2 But now, since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  replaced the late liberal \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  with arch Christian conservative Amy Coney Barrett just before the presidential election last year, that \u8216\'20\'18wing\u8217\'20\'19 of the court now has a swing-proof majority.\par \par \uc2 The opinion issued by the court last night was a so-called emergency opinion - it fell outside of the normal supreme court season, which begins again in October, and there were not oral arguments presented to the court.\par \par \uc2 This was an opinion requested and delivered in matter of a few days.\par \par \uc2 So Roberts is hinting that the court is not necessarily done with this case. Meanwhile, however, the law goes into effect in Texas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  refuses to block Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US live blog readers, the politics news landscape has been very lively overnight despite Congress not being in session, and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a dramatic day so please tune in and stick with us as we bring you all the developments pronto.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overnight handed down an unsigned opinion that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not block the new law}}}\uc2  that went {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into effect}}}\uc2  in Texas yesterday that bans almost all abortions and offers the public the right to sue anyone providing the service or anyone allegedly \u8220\'20\'1Caiding and abetting\u8221\'20\'1D in the provision of that service.\par \par \uc2 It is the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  consolidated a swing-proof ultra-conservative majority on the court after liberal \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s death just before the election last year. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  swung behind the liberal minority on the nine-member bench last night but it was not enough to override the conservatives and the opinion was handed down by five supporters versus four dissenters.\par \par \uc2 There were some blistering written dissents, calling the decision \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D. Yesterday \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the law in Texas was blatantly unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have all the fall-out here. This is seen as almost the final straw to the supreme court overturning the 1973 Roe v Wade landmark ruling that led to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becoming a legal right nationwide in the US.\par \par \uc2 Also on our docket today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is due to make public remarks at 11.40 ET on the aftermath of Hurricane Ida, with other leaders already talking about how the climate crisis is driving more extreme weather.\par \par \uc2 * Ida drenched and battered New York and New Jersey last night with excessive wind and rain and tornadoes, causing loss of life and the governor of New Jersey calling his state the most vulnerable to climate change in the US. Louisiana remans underwater and many, many without power after Ida made landfall as a Category 4 hurricane at the weekend.\par \par \uc2 * This as the climate crisis is also driving the fierce record wildfires out west, with the Lake Tahoe fire in California, in particular, raging there.\par \par \uc2 * Republican leadership is shrieking about efforts by the special House committee (led by Democrats) to obtain social media records about what politicians were up to in the lead up to the insurrection at the US Capitol by extremist Trump supporters, and threatening retaliation against the media companies. We\u8217\'20\'19ll get into all that.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh9200235\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
