\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 How does someone in Texas get an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  now and what\u8217\'20\'19s next?\b0\par\par\uc2 Amanda Holpuch in New York \par \uc2 1,001 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 18:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The supreme court refused to block the ban \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what you should know about the most restrictive US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of people in Texas can effectively no longer access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state after it banned the procedure except in the earliest weeks of pregnancy often before most know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 In a 5-4 vote on Wednesday, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  refused to block the law, which permits private citizens to enforce the ban and possibly collect $10,000 if they win a case against a person helping someone obtain the medical procedure.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you should know about the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US:\par \par \uc2 How does someone legally access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas now?\par \par \uc2 To obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas under the law, a person would have to realize they are pregnant very early in gestation.\par \par \uc2 The law bans abortions once a medical professional can detect cardiac activity in an embryo, usually in the first five to six weeks of a pregnancy. Cardiac activity does not confirm the pregnancy is viable and is detected with advanced technology before a heart is formed.\par \par \uc2 The law includes a narrow exemption for \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergencies\u8221\'20\'1D but there is not an exemption for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 How early is five to six weeks in a pregnancy?\par \par \uc2 Doctors start the pregnancy clock from the day of a person\u8217\'20\'19s last menstrual period. So, someone with an average 28-day menstrual cycle would be considered four weeks pregnant the first day they missed their period.\par \par \uc2 That leaves a two-week window to confirm the pregnancy and make a decision about how to manage it \u8211\'20\'13 though many women have irregular periods, which would shrink that window. Others don\u8217\'20\'19t track their cycle or can\u8217\'20\'19t easily afford the cost of a pregnancy test or doctor\u8217\'20\'19s appointment.\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and reproductive rights groups said 85% to 90% of the procedures happen there after the sixth week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 A full-term pregnancy is 39 weeks. Before the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Texas, Roe v Wade stopped laws that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus is viable outside the womb, generally regarded as 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 What makes this law different from other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions?\par \par \uc2 Crucially, it has survived a challenge in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court. The supreme court has previously blocked states from banning abortions before a pregnancy is viable but let this one through in a decision just before midnight on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Other laws which prohibit abortions after six weeks have passed but were blocked in court before they went into effect.\par \par \uc2 This law is also unique in that it is being enforced by individuals, not government officials, which makes it more difficult to challenge in court.\par \par \uc2 Individuals can enforce this law?\par \par \uc2 Yes. Private citizens, including people who live outside Texas, can sue anyone they think may have \u8220\'20\'1Caided or abetted\u8221\'20\'1D someone getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks. If they win the suit, they get $10,000 and their legal fees are covered. It\u8217\'20\'19s intentionally broad and could penalize family and friends who drive people to appointments or help pay for transportation there.\par \par \uc2 In a federal lawsuit challenging the law, a coalition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and reproductive rights groups said the law \u8220\'20\'1Cplaces a bounty on people who provide or aid abortions, inviting random strangers to sue them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Who is harmed most by this?\par \par \uc2 The effects of this law will not be felt equally.\par \par \uc2 Researchers at the University of Texas said the law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would particularly affect Black patients}}}\uc2  and people living on low incomes. The main reasons Texans are already delayed in obtaining the procedure are because they need to find the money to pay for it, they live far from the facility and time constraints for travel to the procedure because of work, school and childcare.\par \par \uc2 When access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bixbycenter.ucsf.edu/sites/bixbycenter.ucsf.edu/files/Abortion%20restrictions%20risk%20women%27s%20health.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it is likely}}}\uc2  unsafe abortions increase. Each year, between 4.7% and 13.2% of maternal deaths are attributed to unsafe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/preventing-unsafe-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the World Health Organization (WHO)}}}\uc2 . The WHO said nearly every death and disability from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be prevented through sex education, contraception and access to safe abortions.\par \par \uc2 Will people leave Texas to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 It was already difficult to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas and in its neighboring states. Those few clinics in outside states have said they are already seeing an increase in people booking medical appointments.\par \par \uc2 But again, the people who have the means to easily leave the state are the least likely to need the medical procedure. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are collecting money to help women make the journey, but it is no small endeavor. As well, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds could be targeted by this law.\par \par \uc2 Texas is nearly three times the size of the UK and if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasmonthly.com/the-daily-post/how-big-is-texas-compared-to-other-land-masses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its boundaries were overlaid on Europe,}}}\uc2  Paris, Amsterdam, Prague and Florence could all be in the state\u8217\'20\'19s geography.\par \par \uc2 What happens next?\par \par \uc2 Multiple lawsuits are still pending in Texas and civil disobedience is in full force, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/barbieBHG/status/1433148458693767177"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests under way}}}\uc2  and donations pouring into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TEAFund"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  funds}}}\uc2  and reproductive rights groups. The Texas-based immigration legal services group Raices said it would continue to fund and support access to abortions. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to send a very clear message: Raices will not obey this archaic and sexist law,\u8221\'20\'1D said the group\u8217\'20\'19s CEO and president, Jonathan Ryan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.raicestexas.org/2021/09/01/raices-vows-to-disobey-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doing about this?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/09/02/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-supreme-court-ruling-on-texas-law-sb8/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The president said on Thursday}}}\uc2  that he was directing the White House gender policy council to respond to this decision with help from the health department and the justice department \u8220\'20\'1C??to ensure that women in Texas have access to safe and legal abortions\u8221\'20\'1D. The speaker of the House, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said when Congress returns from recess, Democrats will introduce a reproductive health bill, but it is extremely unlikely that would pass in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh9200335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
