\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  view on the Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban: this is not the end\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 707 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 18:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to block the law marks a grave blow to the freedom and safety of women\par \par \uc2 The cruel, vindictive and dangerous law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that has taken effect in Texas}}}\uc2  is much more than the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in the United States. To many, it understandably feels like the beginning of the end \u8211\'20\'13 denying women the rights enjoyed under the landmark Roe v Wade ruling, which established that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal before the foetus is viable outside the womb, at around 24 weeks. It will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/25/anti-abortion-movement-bullish-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further embolden}}}\uc2  the religious right. Though polling suggests the majority of Americans believe that terminations should be legal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-supreme-court-declines-block-texas-abortion-ban-2021-09-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in most or all cases}}}\uc2 , this is already the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/07/state-policy-trends-midyear-2021-already-worst-legislative-year-ever-us-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worst ever legislative year}}}\uc2  for restrictions.\par \par \uc2 But it is better understood as the end of the beginning. The right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has, in practice, been systematically dismantled through methods ranging from intimidation to cynical regulation. This moment is the culmination of the first stage in a decades-long war on the rights of women, made possible by Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointment of judges known to support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/tracking-trump/policy/federal-judges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricting reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . A divided supreme court refused to block the legislation while the legal battle over it plays out.\par \par \uc2 This is a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, with an exemption only for medical emergencies. The six-week limit in practice applies not from fertilisation, but from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/courts_law/texas-six-week-abortion-ban/2021/09/01/e53cf372-0a6b-11ec-a6dd-296ba7fb2dce_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six weeks after a woman\u8217\'20\'19s last period}}}\uc2 , used by doctors to date pregnancies \u8211\'20\'13 when most women will not even know they are pregnant. Up to 90% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s procedures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/us/supreme-court-texas-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 happened after that time}}}\uc2 . International evidence, and America\u8217\'20\'19s own past, testifies that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2007/10/12/world/12abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not stop abortions}}}\uc2 . It will push them underground, endangering women\u8217\'20\'19s health and lives. It is an attack on the rights of all women, but above all will punish those who are poor and black, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already struggled to access services}}}\uc2  and will not be able to travel outside the state easily. It will hurt women who want to control their own bodies, including survivors of incest, rape and abuse.\par \par \uc2 Many states have enacted similar laws, which have been blocked. But this one is especially egregious. It has used the architecture of the state to promote the rule of the mob. It prohibits officials from enforcing it, instead deputising ordinary citizens to sue anyone for suspected violations. While designed this way to make legal challenges harder, it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sifill_LDF/status/1433061003516862467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part of the broader turn of Trump Republicans}}}\uc2  towards vigilantism and away from democratic institutions. By promising a $10,000 bounty to anyone who sues successfully, it encourages the greedy as well as vindictive ex-partners and zealots to act. Not only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, but anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids and abets\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is liable; it appears that even someone who drives a woman to a clinic could be targeted. There is no redress against malicious suits, even in cases where the plaintiff has a past history of similar claims. The result is that doctors and providers who comply with the law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AshaRangappa_/status/1433120423365918720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can still be put out of business}}}\uc2  by vexatious claims.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s blistering dissent attacked the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s inaction in the face of \u8220\'20\'1Ca breathtaking act of defiance \u8211\'20\'13 of the constitution, of this court\u8217\'20\'19s precedents and of rights of women seeking abortions throughout Texas\u8221\'20\'1D. But she is in the minority as the court prepares to rule on a separate case \u8211\'20\'13 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions after 15 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 which anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists see as a chance to overturn Roe v Wade. If that happens, bans will automatically come into force under trigger statutes enacted by multiple states. Others would be able to enforce pre-Roe v Wade bans that remain on their books.\par \par \uc2 This law, like the wider anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive, hurts women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom, their health and even their lives. It has been achieved through the relentless efforts of activists who are not merely egging on but also funding others around the world. Meeting and defeating these challenges will require an equally committed, comprehensive and ambitious campaign. The opponents of women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom will not stop. Defenders cannot either. This law will galvanise them.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh92002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
