\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Most extreme  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law in US takes effect in Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,309 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 16:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 27\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  fails to act to block near-total ban that allows private citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers\par \par \uc2 The most radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US has gone into effect, despite legal efforts to block it.\par \par \uc2 A near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas empowers any private citizen to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who violates the law, opening the floodgates to harassing and frivolous lawsuits from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vigilantes that could eventually shutter most clinics in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will be thrown into absolute chaos,\u8221\'20\'1D says Amanda Williams, executive director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support group the Lilith Fund, a plaintiff in the suit that challenged the law. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, many people who need access the most will slip through the cracks, as we have seen over the years with the relentless attacks here in our state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unbelievable that Texas politicians have gotten away with this devastating and cruel law that will harm so many.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senate Bill 8, ushered through the Republican-dominated Texas legislature and signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into law}}}\uc2  by the Republican governor, Greg Abbott, in May, bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks, and offers no exceptions for rape or incest. Texas is the first state to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this early in pregnancy since Roe v Wade, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last-minute efforts to halt it}}}\uc2  through an appeal to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  by Tuesday did not succeed.\par \par \uc2 While a dozen other states have passed similar so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills, they have all been blocked by the courts. The Texas version is novel in that it is intentionally designed to shield government officials from enforcement, and thus make legal challenges more difficult to secure. It instead incentivizes any private citizen in the US to bring civil suit against an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The law \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately and catastrophically reduces \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Texas\u8221\'20\'1D, say state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, and will probably force many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to ultimately close. It will prevent the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  majority of Texas women}}}\uc2  (85%) from accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, as most are not aware they are pregnant as early as six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden condemned the new law and reaffirmed the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CThis extreme {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  law blatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v Wade and upheld as a precedent for nearly half a century,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood, which operates 11 clinics in the state, and Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health clinics told the Guardian they would comply with the extreme law despite the fact that it is contrary to their best medical practices. In the days leading up to the law\u8217\'20\'19s enactment, Texas clinics say they have been forced to turn away patients who need \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care at the law\u8217\'20\'19s cutoff point this week and into the near future.\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  physicians in Texas have opted to discontinue offering services, choosing to avoid the potential risk of frivolous and costly lawsuits. For instance, most of the physicians across the four Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health clinics in Texas will not continue care to prevent jeopardizing their livelihoods, said the clinic founder, Amy Hagstrom Miller.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are all going to comply with the law even though it is unethical, inhumane and unjust,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Ghazaleh Moayedi, a Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider and OB-GYN, said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt threatens my livelihood and I fully expect to be sued. But my biggest fear is making sure the most vulnerable in my community, the Black and Latinx patients I see, who are already most at risk from logistical and financial barriers, get the care they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The law will force most patients to travel out of state for care, increasing the driving distance to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic twentyfold \u8211\'20\'13 from an average of 12 miles to 248 miles one-way, nearly 500 miles round-trip, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/08/impact-texas-abortion-ban-20-fold-increase-driving-distance-get-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2  found. And that is only if patients have the resources to do so, including time off work, ability to pay for the procedure, and in some cases childcare.\par \par \uc2 Providers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund support groups \u8211\'20\'13 who help finance travel, lodging and direct service for low-income women through donations \u8211\'20\'13 have spent months scrambling to coordinate with out-of-state clinics, including in New Mexico and Colorado, to ensure patients receive timely care when SB8 goes into effect. Last year, the state was offered a glimpse of what would happen if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care ceased: when the state barred most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures amid the Covid-19 pandemic in March 2020, the number of patients who traveled out of state for care {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/fullarticle/2774731?guestAccessKey=1a9d0b9c-7889-460f-839e-326b29d61634&utm_source=For_The_Media&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=ftm_links&utm_content=tfl&utm_term=010421#note-JLD200123-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jumped nearly 400%}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -seeking women are expected to be delayed until later in pregnancy and others will be forced to carry pregnancy to term or try to end their pregnancies without medical oversight, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers caution. As with most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, low-income women and women of color will bear the greatest burden under SB8.\par \par \uc2 Physicians are not the only ones that could be targeted under SB8: a breathtakingly wide range of people and groups, including clinic nurses, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund workers, domestic violence and rape crisis counselors, or even a family member who offers a car ride to the clinic could now face suit from strangers. Those who sue can collect a minimum of $10,000 if they win, but if providers are legally successful they cannot recoup any legal payment. The law, say providers, will spur \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty hunters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The law\u8217\'20\'19s radical legal provision is the first of its kind in the country.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s major anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby group, Texas Right to Life, have already helped empower anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to enforce the law by creating a website that invites \u8220\'20\'1Cwhistleblowers\u8221\'20\'1D to report violations of SB8. (In response, pro-choice advocates have flooded the digital entry forms with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adubs80/status/1428835376895041538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 satirical information}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, funds and clergy members, represented by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 , and \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/texas-abortion-ban-lawsuit-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2  against SB8 in July, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/WWH-v.-Jackson-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2  that the law would \u8220\'20\'1Ccreate absolute chaos in Texas and irreparably harm Texans in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A preliminary injunction hearing was originally set for Monday 30 August in federal court. However, the largely conservative fifth circuit court of appeals cancelled the hearing on Sunday afternoon and denied the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 request to allow the district court to block the law. Providers then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed to the US supreme court}}}\uc2  for emergency relief.\par \par \uc2 But the court failed to act before the law took effect on Wednesday, allowing it to proceed. While the nation\u8217\'20\'19s high court, which now holds a strong anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  contingent, plans to consider a Mississippi 15-week ban that could test Roe v Wade during the next term, its lack of action in the Texas case signals the possible early unraveling of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Texas is already one of the most difficult states in the US in which to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a slew of state laws pushed by the Republican-dominated legislature over the past decade, including a 24-hour waiting period, a 20-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, restrictions on telemedicine, and a prohibition on private and public insurance. It is home to the highest number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5972217/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  deserts}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 cities in which an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -seeking patient must travel at least 100 miles for care \u8211\'20\'13 in the country.\par \par \uc2 Following the passage of a 2013 multi-part law known as House Bill 2, roughly half of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics shuttered \u8211\'20\'13 dropping from 40 to less than 20. While the law was eventually struck down by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 2016, many clinics were unable to reopen. Large swaths of the state \u8211\'20\'13 including the Panhandle and west Texas \u8211\'20\'13 are without an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, forcing women to travel great distances for care.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210901eh91001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
