\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: The radical near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho \par \uc2 1,220 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 11:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US has gone into effect, with the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  refusing to block itDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gone into effect in Texas}}}\uc2 , with the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  voting 5-4 last night to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deny the emergency appeal }}}\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 The ban empowers any private citizen living in Texas or elsewhere to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who violates the law, opening providers to frivolous lawsuits from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vigilantes that could eventually shutter most clinics in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The law prohibits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before most know that they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 and offers no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A dozen other states have passed similar \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills that have been blocked by the courts. The Texas version was designed to incentivize private citizens to bring a civil suit against an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure, making legal challenges more difficult to secure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  have been lambasting the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/01/democrats-condemn-supreme-court-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over its silence on the Texas law}}}\uc2 . Biden said the law \u8220\'20\'1Cblatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Eight dead amid \u8216\'20\'18historic\u8217\'20\'19 New York flooding caused by remnants of Hurricane Ida\par \par \uc2 The National Weather Service (\uc2 NWS\uc2 ) has issued its first ever flash flood emergency warning for the city of New York, as the remnants of Hurricane Ida brought heavy rain that flooded subway lines and streets in Manhattan, Brooklyn and New Jersey. The storm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/new-york-flooding-state-of-emergency-ny-city-flash-flood-nyc-hurricane-ida-remnants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed seven people in New York City and one in Passaic, New Jersey}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With temperatures close to 100F and a heat advisory in place for much of southern Louisiana, many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/new-orleans-hurricane-ida-power-outage-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remain without power and a means to stay cool}}}\uc2  after Hurricane Ida swept through earlier this week. New Orleans is offering a number of mobile cooling stations, including a fleet of air-conditioned buses parked across the city. But with power restored to just 11,500 customers in a city of 400,000 \u8211\'20\'13 and nearly a million homes and businesses in Louisiana still without power, alongside 32,000 more in neighboring Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s not nearly enough. There is still no timeline for a full restoration of power.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the remnants of Hurricane Ida prompted the evacuations of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/hurricane-ida-louisiana-food-water-heat-electricity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands of people in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , after water reached dangerous levels at a dam near Johnstown.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The National Weather Service confirmed at least one tornado in a southern New Jersey county just outside Philadelphia, with rubble and roofs torn from buildings.\par \par \uc2 Sackler family to pay $4.5bn to settle opioid claims\par \par \uc2 A US federal bankruptcy judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/purdue-pharma-sackler-family-settlement-judge-approves-opioid-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conditionally approved yesterday a potential $10bn plan}}}\uc2  submitted by the OxyContin maker \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  to settle a litany of lawsuits over its role in the opioid crisis that has killed a half-million Americans over the past two decades.\par \par \uc2 A part of that plan includes the Sackler family giving up ownership of the company and contributing $4.5bn, in exchange for freeing them from any future lawsuits over opioids.\par \par \uc2 Colorado grand jury indicts five over Elijah McClain\u8217\'20\'19s death\par \par \uc2 Elijah McClain, a 23-year-old Black man, had been walking home in the city of Aurora, Colorado in August 2019 when a 911 caller reported that he looked suspicious. His encounter with police and paramedics left him in a coma, and he died six days later.\par \par \uc2 A grand jury has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/elijah-mcclain-colorado-grand-jury-indicts-five-over-black-mans-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted three police officers and two paramedics}}}\uc2  over his death, charging them with manslaughter and criminally negligent homicide. Video of the encounter leading to his death went viral, showing the police officers who responded to the call putting him in a chokehold as he pleaded for his life, trying to explain to them that \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just different\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Further investigation found that the paramedics who treated him during the encounter injected him with a large amount of the sedative agent ketamine \u8211\'20\'13 more than 1.5 times the dose for his weight.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A shooting at a North Carolina high school has left one student dead, authorities said. The shooter, believed to also be a student, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/north-carolina-school-shooting-leaves-one-dead-with-suspect-at-large"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is in custody}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Staggering wealth inequality in the US is heaping long-term harm on minority children, with Black children having access to just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/inequality/2021/sep/02/us-wealth-inequality-black-hispanic-children"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1 cent for every dollar}}}\uc2  enjoyed by their white counterparts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The podcaster Joe Rogan has contracted Covid-19 and is taking ivermectin, a drug used to deworm horses that health officials have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/joe-rogan-covid-ivermectin-horse-drug-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly warned people not to take for coronavirus}}}\uc2 . Rogan is \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most consumed media products on the planet\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , and has significant influence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Afghan refugees have begun arriving in the US, exhausted but relieved, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/afghan-refugees-arrive-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uncertain about what the future holds}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: 99% of people arrested by a Beverly Hills \u8216\'20\'18safe streets\u8217\'20\'19 unit were Black\par \par \uc2 A new civil rights lawsuit filed against the wealthy \uc2 California city of Beverly Hills\uc2  alleges that out of 106 people arrested by a Beverly Hills police \u8220\'20\'1Csafe streets\u8221\'20\'1D taskforce, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/beverly-hills-police-taskforce-lawsuit-racial-profiling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 105 were Black}}}\uc2  and one was a dark-skinned Latino person. The lawsuit was filed by a couple on vacation in Beverly Hills last September who had been riding a scooter when police detained them \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout any reasonable suspicion or probable cause\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: redeeming Juul\par \par \uc2 Juul, the e-cigarette maker known for pushing their sweet candy-like flavors, is at the center of a string of lawsuits for knowingly addicting a generation to nicotine. At least 68 deaths have been linked to these black pods, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , and more than 2,800 lung injuries in the US. Yet Juul may also be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/sep/02/juul-fda-appeal-e-cigarettes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the best tools to quit smoking}}}\uc2 . Can the company redeem itself?\par \par \uc2 Climate Check: black mayonnaise\par \par \uc2 After years of neighborhood activism, officials have begun excavating the century of toxic sludge hiding in the Gowanus Canal in Brooklyn, New York \u8211\'20\'13 sludge that has colloquially become known as \u8220\'20\'1Cblack mayonnaise\u8221\'20\'1D. To the neighborhood\u8217\'20\'19s dismay, however, the cleanup efforts began not out of duty or honor \u8211\'20\'13 but because officials want to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/02/gowanus-canal-brooklyn-new-york-toxic-cleanup-epa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 build a mega-development}}}\uc2  atop the toxic chemicals.\par \par \uc2 Want more environmental stories delivered to your inbox?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2015/oct/19/sign-up-to-the-green-light-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to our Green Light newsletter}}}\uc2  to get the good, bad and essential news on the climate every week\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: the power of no\par \par \uc2 From Naomi Osaka to Simone Biles, this was the year of strong women being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/the-power-of-no-how-to-build-strong-healthy-boundaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unafraid of saying no}}}\uc2 . This is a practice that we all need to learn, experts and therapists say. \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a society that does not glorify choosing yourself. It is not honored,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nedra Tawwab, a relationship therapist and author of the book Set Boundaries, Find Peace: A Guide to Reclaiming Yourself. \u8220\'20\'1CBut when your life is impacted by not having healthy boundaries for yourself, we need to pay attention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in Touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh92001mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
