\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Thursday briefing: Fuel poverty fears as energy costs rise\b0\par\par\uc2 Warren Murray \par \uc2 1,775 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 05:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Average household bill expected to climb more than \u163\'00\'A3100 \u8230\'20\'26 despair over Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law \u8230\'20\'26 and a return to school in the time of Covid\par \par \uc2 Top story: \u8216\'20\'18Exposed to fossil fuel price swings\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Hello, Warren Murray here to open up shop.\par \par \uc2 Household energy bills are to rise after the electricity market price passed the \u163\'00\'A3100-a-megawatt-hour mark for the first time since the market was formed in 1990. The industry regulator \uc2 Ofgem\uc2  is raising the cap on default energy deals for the coming winter by more than 12%. The increase is expected to push about 500,000 households into fuel poverty, according to campaigners, reigniting calls for a social energy tariff.\par \par \uc2 It means 11m households with direct debit bills will be asked to pay an average of \u163\'00\'A31,138 for a dual-fuel energy bill, an increase of \u163\'00\'A3139. For another 4m households that use prepayment meters, the average bill will climb from \u163\'00\'A31,156 to \u163\'00\'A31,309. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is not a lot we can do in the short term as Britain is particularly exposed to fossil fuel price swings,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Iain Staffell from \uc2 Imperial College London\uc2 , whose analysis of the energy market found Britain needs to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/sep/02/uk-energy-bills-to-rise-after-record-wholesale-electricity-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduce its reliance on fossil fuels to be spared the effects of price swings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A particularly cold winter across Europe and Asia has left global gas storage levels depleted this year, while in Brazil dry weather forced more reliance on gas instead of hydroelectric power. In the summer, much of the northern hemisphere faced exceptionally hot weather \u8211\'20\'13 with \u8220\'20\'1Cheat domes\u8221\'20\'1D forming over North America, Greenland, southern Europe and Siberia \u8211\'20\'13 which fuelled increased demand for gas power plants to generate electricity for air conditioning.\par \par \uc2 * * *\par \par \uc2 More privacy for kids on net \u8211\'20\'13 Sweeping regulations governing how online services treat children\u8217\'20\'19s data come into effect today. The Age Appropriate Design Code mandates websites and apps to take the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest interests\u8221\'20\'1D of their child users into account or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/sep/02/uk-childrens-digital-privacy-code-comes-into-effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face fines of up to 4% of annual global turnover}}}\uc2 . Unless they can prove their service is not used at all by children, companies now must make their entire offering compatible with the code, or attempt to identify younger users and treat them with care. The code prohibits \u8220\'20\'1Cnudge\u8221\'20\'1D techniques encouraging children to give up too much of their privacy; calls on companies to minimise data they collect about children; and requires them to offer children maximum privacy by default. In the weeks leading up to the code\u8217\'20\'19s enforcement, TikTok, \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  have all been tightening up privacy for children.\par \par \uc2 * * *\par \par \uc2 Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law \u8216\'20\'18extreme\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 The most radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US has gone into effect, despite legal efforts to block it. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total ban in Texas}}}\uc2  empowers any private citizen to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, opening the floodgates to harassing lawsuits from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vigilantes. It bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks, and offers no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Texas is the first state to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this early in pregnancy since Roe v Wade, and last-minute efforts to halt it through an appeal to the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/us-supreme-court-refuses-to-block-radical-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not succeed}}}\uc2 . While a dozen other states have passed similar so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills, they have all been blocked by the courts. The Texas version is designed to make legal challenge more difficult. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the new law and reaffirmed the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThis extreme Texas law blatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v Wade and upheld as a precedent for nearly half a century.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * * *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Caught out\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 The UK Foreign Office warned less than four weeks before Kabul fell that the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  could return rapidly to power, it has emerged. \uc2 Dominic Raab\uc2 , the foreign secretary, has told MPs he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2021/sep/01/dominic-raab-uk-intelligence-said-kabul-unlikely-to-fall-this-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believed the Afghan capital would remain safe until next year}}}\uc2  based on an assessment by the joint intelligence committee, a view he said was widely shared by Nato allies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2021/sep/01/afghanistan-dominic-raab-answers-five-questions-mps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a two-hour grilling}}}\uc2 , he admitted the UK had been \u8220\'20\'1Ccaught out and surprised by the scale and speed of the fall of Kabul\u8221\'20\'1D. The Afghan female TV presenter who interviewed a \uc2 Taliban\uc2  official live on air has ended up fleeing the country, saying from Qatar that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/female-tv-anchor-who-interviewed-taliban-official-ends-up-having-to-flee-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the militants don\u8217\'20\'19t accept women as humans}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Reporters Sans Fronti\u232\'00\'E8res\uc2  says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/afghanistan-only-handful-of-female-journalists-still-working"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer than 100 of Kabul\u8217\'20\'19s 700 female journalists are still working}}}\uc2  as they are forced out of jobs and told to stay at home despite \uc2 Taliban\uc2  promises to respect their rights. Raab has flown out on a visit to neighbouring countries of Afghanistan amid efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2021/sep/01/dominic-raab-to-visit-afghanistans-neighbours-amid-refugee-efforts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 help those left behind by the airlift from Kabul}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * * *\par \par \uc2 Sacklers settle \u8211\'20\'13 A US judge looks set to approve a potentially $10bn settlement over the opioid crisis. The OxyContin maker, \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , will be reorganised under a board appointed by public officials and will funnel its profits into government-led efforts to prevent and treat opioid addiction. Under the settlement with victims and thousands of state and local governments, the once-celebrated Sackler family will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/purdue-pharma-sackler-family-settlement-judge-approves-opioid-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hand over their company and contribute $4.5bn to be freed from any future lawsuits over opioids}}}\uc2 . The settlement includes a compensation fund for some victims of drug addiction. Most US states have sued Purdue, claiming its marketing of OxyContin contributed to an epidemic of more than 500,000 deaths in the US. Some have been attributed to OxyContin and other prescription opioids, though most are from illicit forms such as heroin and illegal fentanyl. The crisis crushed the reputation of the philanthropic Sacklers, whose name was once emblazoned on the walls of museums and universities around the world.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus podcast: Covid and the start of school\par \par \uc2 With ministers promising a return to normal in classrooms, it\u8217\'20\'19s a tough time to be a teacher \u8211\'20\'13 but with new information constantly emerging on vaccines for children, and the pandemic not yet over, it\u8217\'20\'19s a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2021/sep/02/the-big-coronavirus-questions-as-a-new-school-term-begins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tough time for parents and pupils too}}}\uc2 . Jules White and Nicola Davis have done their homework.\par \par \uc2 Lunchtime read: That time I kicked Jackie Chan\u8217\'20\'19s butt\par \par \uc2 The kung fu goddess Michelle Yeoh talks about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/sep/02/michelle-yeoh-marvel-shang-chi-legend-ten-rings-kung-fu-crazy-rich-asians-jackie-chan-butt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her most eye-popping stunts}}}\uc2 , her yearning to do another Crazy Rich Asians and her outrageously enjoyable new Marvel movie, Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings.\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Sarah Storey has completed a journey she began 29 years ago, winning her 17th gold medal to become, outright, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/02/sarah-storey-wins-historic-17th-paralympic-gold-medal-great-britain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most successful British Paralympian of all time}}}\uc2 . The 43-year-old Storey won the women\u8217\'20\'19s C4-5 road race with her ParalympicsGB teammate Crystal Lane-Wright claiming silver.\par \par \uc2 Gareth Southgate has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/sep/01/gareth-southgate-urges-england-avoid-swanning-around-after-euros-run-hungary-world-cup-qualifier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for focus and humility}}}\uc2  when England visit Hungary in World Cup qualifying on Thursday night, telling his team not to start \u8220\'20\'1Cswanning around\u8221\'20\'1D after their exploits at Euro 2020. Ollie Pope and Chris Woakes are in line for England recalls while off-spinner Ravichandran Ashwin is poised to return for India {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/unpredictable-series-england-india-seeking-stabilty-fourth-test-the-oval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the fourth Test at the Oval}}}\uc2  that starts on Thursday. England\u8217\'20\'19s women reclaimed Fortress Chelmsford with a vengeance, hitting their highest T20 score against New Zealand \u8211\'20\'13 184 for four \u8211\'20\'13 before bowling out their opponents for 138 in 18.5 overs to finish with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/tammy-beaumont-powers-england-to-comfortable-t20-win-over-new-zealand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a huge 46-run win}}}\uc2 . Cristiano Ronaldo struck twice in the dying minutes to give Portugal a 2-1 win over the Republic of Ireland after John Egan\u8217\'20\'19s opener put the Irish on course for what would have been a famous and deserved victory. In Copenhagen, Denmark scored two early goals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/sep/01/denmark-scotland-world-cup-2022-qualifier-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to beat Scotland 2-0}}}\uc2  in their World Cup qualifier.\par \par \uc2 British No 1 Dan Evans defeated home hope Marcos Giron 6-4, 7-6 (3), 2-6, 6-3 at the US Open and will face Alexei Popyrin as he aims to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/dan-evans-overcomes-marcos-giron-and-rain-delays-to-make-us-open-third-round"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reach the fourth round at Flushing Meadows for the first time}}}\uc2 . The probability that a contaminated pork burrito led to the US Olympic 1500m medal prospect Shelby Houlihan\u8217\'20\'19s failed drugs test is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery close to zero\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/cas-say-close-to-zero-probability-shelby-houlihan-failed-drugs-test-due-to-burrito"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court of arbitration for sport has ruled}}}\uc2 . Rory McIlroy has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/rory-mcilroy-sad-to-see-fan-behaviour-towards-bryson-dechambeau-golf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered public support}}}\uc2  to the much-maligned Bryson DeChambeau, saying it is \u8220\'20\'1Csad to see\u8221\'20\'1D widespread criticism of the American golfer. And the former world champion Kimi R\u228\'00\'E4ikk\u246\'00\'F6nen has confirmed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/01/kimi-raikkonen-announces-retirement-from-f1-at-end-of-the-season"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will retire from Formula One}}}\uc2  at the end of the season.\par \par \uc2 Business\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks have risen as investors wait for US jobs data that might influence when the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  starts to wind down its stimulus. Shanghai, Tokyo and Hong Kong, which are the bulk of Asian market capitalisation, advanced. South Korea and Sydney declined. The FTSE looks like opening just a few points lower while the pound is sitting on $1.377 and \u8364\'20\'AC1.163 as we publish.\par \par \uc2 The papers\par \par \uc2 Our Guardian print edition leads today with \u8220\'20\'1CForeign Office warned of rapid takeover by \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Also on the front page: the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/i-pray-they-are-alive-afghans-headed-to-us-think-of-families-left-behind"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new hopes and old fears of Afghan families}}}\uc2  headed for the US; and people with poor immunity will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/britons-with-severely-weakened-immune-system-to-receive-third-covid-jab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered a third Covid jab but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t count as a booster}}}\uc2 .The Mirror hits on the right language for that last one: \u8220\'20\'1CTop-up jabs for 500,000\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Times says \u8220\'20\'1CThird jab for vulnerable \u8211\'20\'13 but no mass rollout yet\u8221\'20\'1D while the Telegraph has \u8220\'20\'1CScientists told to give older adults booster jabs\u8221\'20\'1D (as well as the top-ups for the immuno-compromised). The Mail is insistent: \u8220\'20\'1CNow give Britain the booster it needs!\u8221\'20\'1D, accusing health officials of \u8220\'20\'1Cdithering over whether all over-50s should get the extra shot\u8221\'20\'1D. The Express has eyes elsewhere: on Matt Hancock\u8217\'20\'19s romantic life but also \u8220\'20\'1COutrage over prescription \u8216\'20\'18tax on sick\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D as analysis by \uc2 Age UK\uc2  suggests proposals to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/sep/02/scrapping-free-prescriptions-for-over-60s-could-have-devastating-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise the free prescription age from 60 to 66}}}\uc2  could have a devastating impact on the health of tens of thousands of older people.\par \par \uc2 The Metro has \u8220\'20\'1CPiers in the clear\u8221\'20\'1D after the TV watchdog said himself was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/sep/01/ofcom-clears-piers-morgan-over-meghan-good-morning-britain-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed to criticise Meghan, the Duchess of Sussex}}}\uc2 . The i leads on the Afghan war and \uc2 Dominic Raab\uc2  with \u8220\'20\'1CUK cabinet ministers at war in Afghan blame game\u8221\'20\'1D while for something different the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  splashes with \u8220\'20\'1CUK draws up plan to shift Trident subs abroad if Scotland secedes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  Morning Briefing is delivered to thousands of inboxes bright and early every weekday. If you are not already receiving it by email, you can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2016/mar/01/the-morning-briefing-start-the-day-one-step-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For more news: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Get in Touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210902eh92000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
