\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden condemns Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law that \u8216\'20\'18blatantly violates\u8217\'20\'19 constitution \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh, Joanna Walters and Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 6,080 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 00:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Supreme court fails to act to block restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\u8216\'20\'18It is unbelievable that Texas politicians have gotten away with this\u8217\'20\'19Capitol attack inquiry to investigate Trump White House\u8217\'20\'19s role\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that the Biden administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fdf0c8f0830dd895fd097#block-612fdf0c8f0830dd895fd097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in \u8220\'20\'1Cno rush\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to acknowledge officially the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  as the governing authority in Afghanistan. The defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fb5fb8f083528f0f5121c#block-612fb5fb8f083528f0f5121c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke of}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Csolemn\u8221\'20\'1D time for the department in the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  released a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859#block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticizing}}}\uc2  the Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  that went into effect today and affirming the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support of Roe v Wade. Senior Democrats in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fa0618f0830dd895fccbf#block-612fa0618f0830dd895fccbf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slammed}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  for not taking up an appeal to consider the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, letting the law go into effect though it virtually bans all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 The Capitol Police\uc2  Department is \u8220\'20\'1Cclosely monitoring\u8221\'20\'1D a rally planned in support of the 6 January insurrectionists, chief Tom Manger said in a statement. Lawmakers continue the process of investigating the deadly 6 January storming of the capitol. Congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , chair of the House select committee investigating the Capitol attack, is seeking to expand an inquiry into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s role in the insurrection\par \par \uc2 * New York governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , in one of her first major moves as the state\u8217\'20\'19s new governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/news/coronavirus/ny-democrats-call-on-hochul-to-extend-eviction-ban-set-to-expire-tuesday/3248532/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for lawmakers to return to Albany for a special session to extend the state\u8217\'20\'19s eviction moratorium. State lawmakers are expected to start a special session at noon today with the goal of extending the moratorium, currently set to expire at midnight, through mid-January.\par \par \uc2 * The Caldor Fire is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/01/weather/us-western-wildfires-wednesday/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing in}}}\uc2  on Lake Tahoe, threatening over 34,000 structures in the popular resort town. Meanwhile, people in Louisiana are still reeling from the aftermath of Hurricane Ida, dealing with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-08-30/new-orleans-levees-withstood-hurricane-ida-as-electricity-failed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stifling heat}}}\uc2  as blackouts continue in New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joanna Walters, Lauren Aratani and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Firefighters battling a ferocious wildfire in the Lake Tahoe Basin are facing critical hours as they work to prevent the flames from reaching a resort city at the southern tip of the lake.\par \par \uc2 Crews gained ground on the behemoth blaze raging on the California-Nevada border, officials said Wednesday, despite dry gusty conditions and difficult terrain.\par \par \uc2 The Caldor fire did not make as strong a push toward Tahoe as it did the previous day, said the operations section chief, Tim Ernst, as winds came up less strong than expected and bulldozers made progress creating fire lines.\par \par \uc2 But with forecasters warning that there will be swirling, gusty winds all Wednesdaycrews face a hard fight to keep the fire from reaching homes in the town of South Lake Tahoe in California and expanding into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Caldor fire was 3 miles (5km) outside South Lake Tahoe by Tuesday afternoon, \uc2 Cal Fire\uc2  battalion chief Henry Herrera told \uc2 KGO-TV\uc2 . A day earlier, roughly 22,000 residents jammed the city\u8217\'20\'19s main artery for hours after they were ordered to leave as the fire advanced.\par \par \uc2 Pushed by strong winds, the Caldor fire has expanded in recent days. Stephen Vollmer, a fire behavior analyst for the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (\uc2 Cal Fire\uc2 ), said embers were being cast up to a mile out in front of the fire, creating new ignition points, including in some parts of the dense forest that have not burned since 1940 or before.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/caldor-fire-lake-tahoe-wildfires-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Firefighters in make-or-break fight to keep Caldor fire from Lake Tahoe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Open season on media\u8217\'20\'19: journalists increasingly targeted at Los Angeles protests\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles has seen volatile protests almost every weekend this summer over trans rights, political opposition to masks and vaccines, and the recall of the Democratic governor. At least seven journalists have been physically assaulted while covering these rallies, six of them by rightwing demonstrators.\par \par \uc2 Attacks on the press are just one part of escalating rightwing street violence in the city, which has included multiple stabbings, people being sprayed in the face with bear Mace, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/pkbxmg/breast-cancer-patient-attacked-anti-mask-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assault on a breast cancer patient}}}\uc2  outside a clinic, and repeated physical brawls with leftwing protesters in the streets. In another sign of growing tensions, protesters rallying against vaccine mandates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-08-30/covid-vaccination-foes-protest-homes-of-two-l-a-city-council"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed up}}}\uc2  at the homes of two Los Angeles city council members on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Several Los Angeles journalists said the violence was like nothing they had seen before, and that some of the attacks had taken place with police officers standing nearby.\par \par \uc2 The Los Angeles police department and the Los Angeles county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s department did not respond to requests for comment about whether there had been any arrests so far in any of the incidents, even as some of the journalists have publicly identified the people they believe attacked them and at least three have made official police reports.\par \par \uc2 The documentary film-maker Rocky Romano said he was hit over the head with a lead-filled baton at an anti-trans protest on 3 July while wearing a vest clearly marked \u8220\'20\'1Cpress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/los-angeles-protest-journalists-attacked-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Open season on media\u8217\'20\'19: journalists increasingly targeted at Los Angeles protests}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  are monitoring 18 September rally at US Capitol\par \par \uc2 The Capitol Police\uc2  Department is \u8220\'20\'1Cclosely monitoring\u8221\'20\'1D a rally planned in support of the 6 January insurrectionists, chief Tom Manger said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/capitol-siege-887b2b3a4bcc3c667858765b1281c959"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  on what officials are expecting at the 18 September rally:\par \par \uc2 Far right extremist groups like the Proud Boys and Oath Keepers are planning to attend a rally later this month at the U.S. Capitol that is designed to demand \u8220\'20\'1Cjustice\u8221\'20\'1D for the hundreds of people who have been charged in connection with January\u8217\'20\'19s insurrection, according to three people familiar with intelligence gathered by federal officials.\par \par \uc2 As a result, \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  have been discussing in recent weeks whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/capitol-siege-959046e70443c6137975be5ba78746e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the large perimeter fence }}}\uc2  that was erected outside the Capitol after January\u8217\'20\'19s riot will need to be put back up, the people said.\par \par \uc2 The officials have been discussing security plans that involve reconstructing the fence as well as another plan that does not involve a fence, the people said. They were not authorized to speak publicly and spoke to The Associated Press on condition of anonymity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/16:43%20https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-dc-wire-only-on-ap-capitol-siege-government-and-politics-455d7f1c758a2177f9bf68ca96c3dc87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The decision on whether or not to erect the fence again}}}\uc2  will likely be considered by the Capitol Police Board, according to a House aide familiar with the matter and granted anonymity to discuss it. No decisions have been made. The board consists of the Sergeant at Arms of the \uc2 U.S. House of Representatives\uc2 , the Sergeant at Arms and Doorkeeper of the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 , and the Architect of the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 This rally comes at the heels of two bomb threats near the capitol, and as lawmakers continue the process of investigating the deadly 6 January storming of the capitol. Congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , chair of the House select committee investigating the Capitol attack, is seeking to expand an inquiry into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s role in the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood slams "vigilante" effect of new Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban law\par \par \uc2 Erica Sackin, political communications director of women\u8217\'20\'19s health services and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider Planned Parenthood, said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new law in Texas}}}\uc2  risks promoting vigilantism from the public.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood members march in the \u8220\'20\'1CHometown Heroes\u8221\'20\'1D Ticker Tape Parade in New York City in July. Healthcare Workers, first responders and essential workers were honored for their service during the Covid-19 pandemic. Photograph: Ron Adar/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Critics argue that it sets a dangerous precedent beyond just \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  - imagine if anyone could sue anyone over a constitutional right they simply didn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with.\par \par \uc2 Sackin told CNN a little earlier: \u8220\'20\'1CWe gave never seen a law like this one before. This \u8216\'20\'18sue thy neighbor\u8217\'20\'19 provision means that it\u8217\'20\'19s not just going to be impossible for people to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it really creates, almost, this vigilante, where they can go after anyone they suspect of having helped someone to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Alisyn Camerota asked Sackin what she thought, given that Texas Republican governor Greg Abbott is fond of banning mask mandates and isn\u8217\'20\'19t in favor of vaccination mandates and argues that Texans and not state government should decide their own best practices, yet has egged on the state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Sackin said: It\u8217\'20\'19s really hard to hear something like that coming out of his mouth, especially when we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at what this law means for people across Texas. Right now patients are scared, parents are worried, patients can\u8217\'20\'19t make the most personal decision about if and when they want to become a parent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they even are going to be able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all it\u8217\'20\'19s going to mean driving hundreds of miles out of state, if they an afford it, and that includes not just the drive, that includes accommodation, funding an appointment, taking time off of work, finding childcare, so really the layers and layers of restrictions on getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas are unbelievable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sackin said Planned Parenthood would continue to fight and were waiting for the Supreme Court \u8220\'20\'1Cto hopefully weigh in\u8221\'20\'1D adding \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are deeply disappointed that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t take any action overnight...but it\u8217\'20\'19s still possible they will take action and allow some emergency relief, because of how much harm this law will cause.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sackin warned, however, that the move in Texas by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  forces was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust one piece of an agenda we are seeing across the country\u8221\'20\'1D to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  inaccessible.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively afternoon and my colleague on the US west coast, Maanvi Singh, will now take over the blog and bring you any remaining developments in US political news for the next few hours, so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 So far:\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that the Biden administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fdf0c8f0830dd895fd097#block-612fdf0c8f0830dd895fd097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in \u8220\'20\'1Cno rush\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to acknowledge officially the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  as the governing authority in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 * The defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fb5fb8f083528f0f5121c#block-612fb5fb8f083528f0f5121c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke of}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Csolemn\u8221\'20\'1D time for the department in the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  released a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859#block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticizing}}}\uc2  the Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  that went into effect today and affirming the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 * Senior Democrats in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fa0618f0830dd895fccbf#block-612fa0618f0830dd895fccbf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slammed}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  for not taking up an appeal to consider the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, letting the law go into effect though it virtually bans all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Paxton Smith, who stealthily used her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/02/texas-valedictorian-graduation-speech-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 valedictorian address}}}\uc2  at her Dallas high school in June to rail against Texas\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban legislation, spoke out today to call the passing of the law and the failure by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to intervene \u8220\'20\'1Cheart-wrenching\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Paxton Smith at her high school graduation in Dallas in June. Photograph: Courtesy Paxton Smith\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very sad to see, and it is so heart-wrenching that so many people in Texas have had a fundamental human right taken away from them today,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/01/us/paxton-smith-reacts-to-texas-abortion-law-trnd/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Smith}}}\uc2 , who is studying at the University of Texas.\par \par \uc2 She told CNN:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very upset that this law has been able to go into effect, and I know a lot of people share that sentiment and the idea that if we do face ourselves with an unplanned pregnancy then that life-changing decision... is no longer up to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think a lot of times some of the most important voices in the issue are not listened to,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt deeply affects every person differently and very personally... and I think that\u8217\'20\'19s something that needed to be talked about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith said that the new law \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinitely\u8221\'20\'1D made her question whether she wanted to live in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI worry about my rights in a state where the value of my voice and the value of what happens with my life and with my body if I get pregnant are not taken into account.\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s valedictorian speech garnered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/littlewhitty/status/1399982526396043264"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millions of views}}}\uc2  on social media and won praise from politicians such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1400127800288419840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/betoorourke/status/1400151466531344388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read an interview she did with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  at the time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/05/paxton-smith-abortion-ban-speech-texas-valedictorian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/05/paxton-smith-abortion-ban-speech-texas-valedictorian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People were excited\u8217\'20\'19: Paxton Smith on her valedictorian speech for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says "no rush" to recognize \uc2 Taliban\uc2  as leaders of Afghanistan\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  mentioned once again this afternoon that the Biden administration is not in a hurry to acknowledge officially the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  as the governing authority in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 But that very obviously is not ruling out a future formal recognition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no rush to recognize, from the US or any country around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said at the media briefing earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Taliban\uc2  soldiers talk to each other, in Kabul, Afghanistan, earlier today. Photograph: Wana News Agency/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Asked if and how that might change, Psaki said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt will depend very much on their behavior.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US brought many Afghan allies out of the country in its huge airlift, but the majority of those who applied for visas and expected to be evacuated because they had worked alongside Americans in the last 20 years ended up being left behind when the last US military plane left shortly after midnight local time on 31 August, the deadline the Biden administration had agreed with the Taliban for the US to leave Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the handful of American citizens left behind who want to leave will be evacuated, echoing what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/joe-biden-afghanistan-speech-us-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden said yesterday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/joe-biden-afghanistan-speech-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden sets himself apart by placing Afghanistan blame at predecessors\u8217\'20\'19 feet}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  just responded to another question from the press at the media briefing about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Texas law}}}\uc2  banning almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an extreme threat,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press sec said, noting that the law allows for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe offering of $10,000 to someone who reports someone who is going to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so of course it\u8217\'20\'19s of great concern [but] it\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time there have been efforts by some in the country to prevent a woman having a right to choose\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are strongly in support of the legal right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, afforded by the 1973 Roe supreme court ruling, being codified via federal legislation.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve called on Congress to do that, she said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Ccodifying Roe v Wade as the law of the land is something Congress can do\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When then asked if the Biden administration had any intention of taking specific action, Psaki said: \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot speak to anything to do with the department of justice, they are independent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris put out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/01/22/statement-from-president-biden-and-vice-president-harris-on-the-48th-anniversary-of-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  about this on their first full day in office, on 22 January, on the 48th anniversary of the landmark 1973 supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 They said at the time:\par \par \uc2 In the past four years, reproductive health, including the right to choose, has been under relentless and extreme attack. We are deeply committed to making sure everyone has access to care \u8211\'20\'13 including reproductive health care \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of income, race, zip code, health insurance status, or immigration status.\par \par \uc2 The Biden-Harris Administration is committed to codifying Roe v. Wade and appointing judges that respect foundational precedents like Roe.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is holding a press conference right now, starting off with the White House\u8217\'20\'19s rebuke of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s focus is to reiterate our deep commitment to the constitutional right established by Roe v Wide\u8230\'20\'26 and to continue to call for the codification of Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Psaki also responded to a question on concerns that the White House prematurely decided that American adults should be eligible for booster Covid-19 vaccines. Psaki said that health officials such as \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  and \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) head \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  have \u8220\'20\'1Creviewed mountains and mountains of available data on vaccine effectiveness and made a clinical judgment that boosters would be needed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere will still be a final piece of this process that will be seen through,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said regarding further plans the White House will release on how booster shots will be rolled out by 20 September.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A summer camp and men\u8217\'20\'19s conference hosted by an Illinois church has been linked to 180 confirmed and probable Covid-19 cases, the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/wr/mm7035e4.htm?s_cid=mm7035e4_w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Tuesday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agency noted that the events did not require vaccinations or testing. The camp was a five-day overnight church camp for high-school-aged teenagers and a two-day men\u8217\'20\'19s conference. The events took place in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 Among the 122 confirmed cases, 85% of the people were not vaccinated while 15% were fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis investigation underscores the impact of secondary SARS-CoV-2 transmission during large events such as camps and conferences when Covid-19 prevention strategies, including vaccination, masking, physical distancing and screening testing, are not implemented,\u8221\'20\'1D the CDC said in its report.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was a remarkable moment at the end of the Pentagon briefing. Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  and Gen Mark Milley were asked about the pain and anger of veterans seeing 20 years of fighting end in defeat and retreat.\par \par \uc2 Austin talked about everyone understanding and accepting the emotions of others. Milley was more direct, and talked about his own feelings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo you asked me where my pain and anger comes from?\u8221\'20\'1D he replied to the CNN journalist who asked the question. \u8220\'20\'1CI have all those same emotions and I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the secretary does and anyone who\u8217\'20\'19s served. And I commanded troops. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t born a four-star general. I have walked the patrols and been blown up and shot and RPG-ed and everything else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DAnd my pain and anger comes from the same as grieving families, the same as those soldiers that are on the ground,\u8221\'20\'1D Milley said, adding that he had visited wounded service members at Walter Reed hospital last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is tough stuff. War is hard. It\u8217\'20\'19s vicious, it\u8217\'20\'19s brutal, it\u8217\'20\'19s unforgiving. And yes, we all have pain and anger, and when we see what has unfolded over the last 20 years and over the last 20 days, that creates pain and anger. Mine comes from 242 of my soldiers killed in action over 20 years in Iraq and Afghanistan. So yeah, I have that. But I\u8217\'20\'19m a professional soldier. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to contain my pain and anger and continue to execute my mission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Pentagon, Gen Mark Milley addressed Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s drone strike, which is believed to have killed at least 10 Afghan civilians, including seven children under the age of 11.\par \par \uc2 Milley insisted that the intelligence continued to show that the target was an Islamic State car bomb.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the time, and I think this is still valid, we had very good intelligence that Isis-K was preparing a specific type of vehicle at a specific type location. We monitored that through various means, and all of the different criteria were being met. We went through the same level of rigor that we\u8217\'20\'19ve done for years, and we took a strike,\u8221\'20\'1D Milley said.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSecondly, we know that there were secondary explosions,\u8221\'20\'1D the general went on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause there were secondary explosions, there\u8217\'20\'19s a reasonable conclusion to be made that there were explosives in that vehicle. The third thing is we know from a variety of other means that at least one of those people that were killed was an Isis facilitator.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Milley took a step towards acknowledging the civilian casualties. \u8220\'20\'1CSo were there others killed? Yes, there are others killed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. But added: \u8220\'20\'1CWho they are they? We don\u8217\'20\'19t know. We\u8217\'20\'19ll try to sort through all that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a telling exchange, Gen Mark Milley, chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, was asked what it was like having to coordinate with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  during the evacuation after fighting with them for long.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn war, you do what you must, in order to reduce risk to the mission and the force, not what you necessarily want to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Milley said.\par \par \uc2 Asked if it was possible that the US might cooperate with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  in operations against the \uc2 Islamic State Khorasan\uc2  Province (ISKP), he replied: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At that point, defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , interjected quickly: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to tell you that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything that we can to make sure we remain focused on ISIS-K [Pentagon-speak for ISKP]. We understand that network and at the time of our choosing, in the future, we\u8217\'20\'19ll hold them accountable for what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Addressing reporters in the Pentagon, defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  also made it clear he was well aware of the bitter criticism coming from war veterans for the chaos surrounding the evacuation of Afghan interpreters and other employees.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/majority-of-interpreters-other-u-s-visa-applicants-were-left-behind-in-afghanistan-official-says-11630513321?page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting today}}}\uc2  that most of those eligible for special immigration visas were left behind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will always be proud of the part that we played in this war,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expect Afghan war veterans to agree any more than any other group of Americans. I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard strong views from many sides in recent days. And that\u8217\'20\'19s vital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s democracy. That\u8217\'20\'19s America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top defense officials speak on Afghanistan: 'Proud' and 'solemn' time for defense department\par \par \uc2 The defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , is making his first major appearance since the evacuation of Kabul, Afghanistan alongside the chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, General Mark Milley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy time for all of us in this department. A proud one and a solemn one too,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have concluded our historic evacuation operation, and ended the last mission of the US war in Afghanistan. America\u8217\'20\'19s longest war has come to a close.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs both a secretary and as a veteran..my thoughts have been with the brave Americans who stood up to serve after al-Qaida attacked us on September 11 2001.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick summary of everything that\u8217\'20\'19s happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 * With a Texas law banning most abortions, Democrats have slammed the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  for not taking up an appeal that would have at least temporarily blocked the law. In a statement, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said the court allowed the law to go into effect \u8220\'20\'1Cunder the cover of darkness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Without mentioning the Supreme Court specifically, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  criticized the Texas law as one that \u8220\'20\'1Cblatantly violates\u8221\'20\'1D constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 * New York lawmakers are meeting this afternoon in a special session to extend the state\u8217\'20\'19s eviction moratorium, which is set to expire at midnight.\par \par \uc2 * A Black high school principal in Texas was abruptly suspended from his job after parents accused him of promoting critical race theory, which one parent called a \u8220\'20\'1Cconspiracy theory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more live updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Texas was working until 11:59pm last night, right up until the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law would go into effect on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have staff and doctors providing abortions in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 still at this hour \u8211\'20\'13 and they are all in to provide care until 11:59 tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health last night. \u8220\'20\'1COur waiting rooms are filled with patients and their loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Marva Sadler, senior director of clinical services at Whole Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/08/31/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Tribune}}}\uc2  that the clinics were \u8220\'20\'1Cengulfed\u8221\'20\'1D with over 100 patients who were scrambling to undergo procedures at the Fort Worth clinic before Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The clinic was one of the plaintiffs who filed an appeal to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  against the state ban, saying in a court filing that the law \u8220\'20\'1Cunquestionably contravenes this Court\u8217\'20\'19s precedent and will cause clear harm\u8221\'20\'1D and said that law is \u8220\'20\'1Csomething that has never been allowed to occur in any other state of the nation in the decades since Roe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Clinics, including Whole Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/08/31/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  that they may have to close and turn patients away starting Wednesday with the law in effect.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden blasts Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, says it \u8216\'20\'18blatantly violates\u8217\'20\'19 Constitution\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just released a statement criticizing the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that went into effect today and affirming the White House\u8217\'20\'19s support of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis extreme Texas law blatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v. Wade and upheld as a precedent for nearly half a century,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COutrageously, it deputizes private citizens to bring lawsuits against anyone who they believed has helped another person get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which might even include family members, health care workers, front desk staff at a health clinic, or strangers with no connection to the individual.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a new statement, President Biden lambasts the Texas law that went into effect overnight banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state after six weeks, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D and a blatant violation of constitutional right established under Roe v. Wade. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3AR8IHMl96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3AR8IHMl96}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Betsy Klein (@betsy_klein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/betsy_klein/status/1433101777243676682?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has joined the number of Democrats specifically criticizing the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  for allowing the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to go into effect today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the cover of darkness, by choosing to do nothing, the Supreme Court allowed an unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas to go into effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton tweeted. \u8220\'20\'1CTheir decision doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the fact that reproductive rights are human rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrUnder the cover of darkness, by choosing to do nothing, the Supreme Court allowed an unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas to go into effect last night.\par \par \uc2 Their decision doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the fact that reproductive rights are human rights. We'll fight for them. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hp1N6G2S3M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/hp1N6G2S3M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  (@HillaryClinton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1433093747856789504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers say Supreme Court could have stalled Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers are criticizing the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  for not taking up an appeal to consider the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, letting the law go into effect though it virtually bans all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Supreme Court allowed the law to go into effect \u8211\'20\'13 effectively ending Roe v Wade protections in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joaquin Castro\uc2 , a US representative from Texas, said in a Tweet.\par \par \uc2 enltrTexas GOP banned all abortions after about 6 weeks, before many even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant, and the Supreme Court allowed the law to go into effect\u8212\'20\'14effectively ending Roe v. Wade protections in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Congress must act. All women have a constitutional right to full health care.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joaquin Castro\uc2  (@JoaquinCastrotx) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoaquinCastrotx/status/1433084927940104198?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn refusing to intervene last night, the Supreme Court tipped the scales of justice in favor of one of the most draconian state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in history,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , chair of the House Oversight Committee, wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairwoman-maloney-s-statement-on-supreme-court-inaction-allowing-texas-6-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe Supreme Court has put the health and safety of Texas \u8211\'20\'13 especially people with lower incomes and people of color \u8211\'20\'13 in jeopardy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cori Bush, a US representative from Missouri, said in a Tweet that \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is health care and [the bill] in Texas, combined with the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s inaction, is a disgrace to our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court can end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights tonight, without any oral arguments. They\u8217\'20\'19re hoping we don\u8217\'20\'19t notice,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted Senator Mazie Hirono yesterday.\par \par \uc2 enltrThat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case you think the Supreme Court will use to take down Roe next year? It might not matter. The Court can end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights tonight, without any oral arguments. They're hoping we don't notice. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2A4LUkT6pU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2A4LUkT6pU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Mazie Hirono (@maziehirono) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maziehirono/status/1432775696619909124?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 31, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court is set to take on a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in its next term, which begins in October. The Mississippi law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 A high school principal in Texas was suspended after parent criticism that he was promoting critical race theory, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/09/01/texas-principal-critical-race-theory/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 James Whitfield, principal of Colleyville Heritage High School, was initially the target of a heated school board meeting in July where one man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.star-telegram.com/news/local/article253238543.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  Whitfield of promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cthe conspiracy theory of systemic racism\u8221\'20\'1D. Though school board policy barred direct attacks against individuals, the man named Whitfield throughout the meeting.\par \par \uc2 After several weeks of controversy, Whitfield, who is Black, was suspended by the school district.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was not given any clear reasoning behind the decision and was not given a timetable regarding further steps,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitfield told the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CI was simply told that it was in the best interest of the school district.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Across the country, conservatives have spent the last year railing against critical race theory, though what ideas their anger is directed toward is largely undefined. In June, Texas governor Greg Abbott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/06/15/abbott-critical-race-theory-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  a bill that dictates what students in the state must be taught. Opponents of the bill say that it limits honest conversations about race in America and will make teachers shy away from discussing sensitive topics in the classroom.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York State Assembly holds special session to extend eviction moratorium\par \par \uc2 New York governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , in one of her first major moves as the state\u8217\'20\'19s new governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/news/coronavirus/ny-democrats-call-on-hochul-to-extend-eviction-ban-set-to-expire-tuesday/3248532/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for lawmakers to return to Albany for a special session to extend the state\u8217\'20\'19s eviction moratorium.\par \par \uc2 State lawmakers are expected to start a special session at noon today with the goal of extending the moratorium, currently set to expire at midnight, through mid-January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going to exacerbate what is already a crisis in terms of the homelessness problem. We are not going to allow people who through no fault of their own lost income, are not able to pay and are facing eviction,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/news/coronavirus/ny-democrats-call-on-hochul-to-extend-eviction-ban-set-to-expire-tuesday/3248532/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at a press conference Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s Congressional delegation sent a letter to Hochul Monday urging her to extend the moratorium.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe joined the New York delegation to urge Gov. Hochul to extend the NY eviction ban. This would protect families while the State resolves the delay in issuing rent relief. NY landlords & renters are eligible for $2B in aid - the state has distributed just several hundred million. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gDhk5dFwfl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gDhk5dFwfl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez (@RepAOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAOC/status/1432372766519570438?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 US Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/aug/27/us-supreme-court-blocks-biden-eviction-moratorium"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  the Biden administration from enforcing a temporary ban on evictions, allowing evictions across the country to resume. Along with New York, other states like California, Maryland and New Jersey have put in place their own temporary ban on evictions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Markwayne Mullin, a Republican US representative from Oklahoma, reportedly threatened the Tajikistan ambassador and his staff for not assisting him in transferring cash into the country, with the ultimate goal of going into neighboring Afghanistan to rescue five Americans, a woman and her four children, who are stuck in the country.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/mullin-afghanistan-trip/2021/08/31/62f63bb0-0a90-11ec-a256-709238a1404d_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 , Mullin planned to hire a helicopter for the operation and called the Tajikistan embassy for help. Embassy officials rejected his request, denying that they would break the country\u8217\'20\'19s laws on cash limits to help him visit the country. The representative became outraged, demanding to know the names of the staff members who he was speaking to.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon earlier had denied Mullin\u8217\'20\'19s request to travel to Afghanistan given the dangerous conditions in the country. Two other Congress members have taken unauthorized trips to Afghanistan, \uc2 Seth Moulton\uc2 , a Democrat from Massachusetts and Peter Meijer, a Republican from Michigan. The Pentagon and State Department have criticized these operations as PR stunts that take away resources from strained departments during a time of crisis.\par \par \uc2 House leaders \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy have spoken against lawmakers traveling to the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re putting yourself \u8211\'20\'13 not just yourself, but you\u8217\'20\'19re putting Americans in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way, if the military has to protect you, which they will do,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two top officials at the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) have reportedly resigned over frustrations toward the White House \u8217\'20\'19s handling of Covid-19 vaccine booster shots. The officials worked in the Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research, the agency\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine department.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement last month that Americans will be eligible for a booster shot has frustrated \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulators who are scrambling to organize data that clearly demonstrates the benefits of a booster shot and come up with a solid rollout plan by 20 September, the date when the administration said booster shots will become available.\par \par \uc2 Paul Offit, an infectious disease expert who is on the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine advisory committee told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/08/31/biden-booster-plan-fda-508149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  that the booster plan is more the White House\u8217\'20\'19s than the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s. \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration has kind of backed themselves up against the wall a little bit here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 FDA commissioner \uc2 Janet Woodcock\uc2  sent a memo yesterday to \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulators yesterday emphasizing that she understands that work is \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplex and the days are long\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Cwill hopefully one day allow us to fully put Covid-19 behind us and better prepare us for future challenges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law goes into effect in Texas\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to the politics live blog.\par \par \uc2 The most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law since Roe v Wade will go into effect today in Texas, making illegal abortions once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, typically six weeks after conceptions. The law offers no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The law allows any private citizen to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, leaving clinics in the state vulnerable to lawsuits. Multiple challenges against the law were brought to court but have so far seen no actions. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has not acted on an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeal}}}\uc2  made against the law. The court is expected to take up a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in its next term, though its lack of action around this Texas law signals the risk Roe v Wade is in with the court\u8217\'20\'19s anti-choice majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will be thrown into absolute chaos,\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda Williams, executive director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support group the Lilith Fund, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unbelievable that Texas politicians have gotten away with this devastating and cruel law that will harm so many.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an eye out for reactions to this new law. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today.\par \par \uc2 * A law that restricts voting by mail and empowers poll watchers is headed to the desk of Texas governor Greg Abbott after it passed the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature. Abbott has indicated he plans to sign the legislation into law.\par \par \uc2 * The debate over mask mandates in schools continues as Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2  announced yesterday that K-12 schools must mandates masks.\par \par \uc2 * The Caldor Fire is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/01/weather/us-western-wildfires-wednesday/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing in}}}\uc2  on Lake Tahoe, threatening over 34,000 structures in the popular resort town. Meanwhile, people in Louisiana are still reeling from the aftermath of Hurricane Ida, dealing with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-08-30/new-orleans-levees-withstood-hurricane-ida-as-electricity-failed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stifling heat}}}\uc2  as blackouts continue in New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more live updates.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210901eh91002ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
