\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morning mail: Indigenous vaccination rates lag, Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban, hospital pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Parkin \par \uc2 1,406 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2021\par 21:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thursday : Western Australian regions have lowest Covid vaccination rates. Plus: camera discovery reveals climber\u8217\'20\'19s last images before fatal avalanche\par \par \uc2 Good morning. WA\u8217\'20\'19s premier has locked horns with his federal counterparts, Texas has ushered in radical new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, and \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2  is facing fresh scrutiny over the allocation of federal grant funding.\par \par \uc2 Covid vaccination rates among Indigenous Australians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/datablog/ng-interactive/2021/sep/02/indigenous-vaccination-rates-lag-in-almost-every-region-of-australia-new-figures-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are lagging badly}}}\uc2 , with new figures showing that across large swathes of Western Australia less than 10% of Aboriginal adults are fully vaccinated. Meanwhile, WA premier \uc2 Mark McGowan{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/sep/01/furious-mark-mcgowan-accuses-morrison-government-of-mission-to-bring-covid-into-wa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has accused the Morrison government}}}\uc2  of being \u8220\'20\'1Con [a] mission to bring Covid into Western Australia\u8221\'20\'1D, responding angrily to a warning from the federal attorney general, Michaelia Cash, that the legal basis for state border closures would diminish as vaccination rates increased. Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s premier, \uc2 Daniel Andrews\uc2 , has suggested restrictions could ease in September as the state approaches 70% vaccination rates, despite a continued uptick in new cases in both Victoria and New South Wales.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all but banned in Texas}}}\uc2 , after last minute attempts in the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to halt radical new legislation failed. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said the bill that passed the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus?page=with:block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859#block-612fa9688f08bf4765a42859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blatantly violates the constitutional right}}}\uc2  established under Roe v. Wade\u8221\'20\'1D, with pro-choice activists claiming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US\u8217\'20\'19s second most populous state will be \u8220\'20\'1Cthrown into absolute chaos\u8221\'20\'1D. The new legislation bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, normally around six weeks, with no exceptions for victims of either rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The energy minister, \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2 , and resources minister, \uc2 Keith Pitt\uc2 , are facing scrutiny from a Senate inquiry, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/sep/02/angus-taylor-and-keith-pitt-asked-by-senate-inquiry-chair-to-explain-dealings-with-firm-awarded-beetaloo-gas-grants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freedom of information documents revealed}}}\uc2  a company with close Liberal-party links received $21m in federal grants, having asked for information regarding \u8220\'20\'1Celigibility criteria\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Capplication process\u8221\'20\'1D well before the program guidelines were officially released. Empire Energy\u8217\'20\'19s managing director has said the company followed \u8220\'20\'1Cdue and proper process at all times\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Australia\par \par \uc2 News Corp co-chairman \uc2 Lachlan Murdoch\uc2  has been called before a Senate inquiry,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/sep/02/lachlan-murdoch-asked-to-appear-at-parliamentary-inquiry-into-youtubes-suspension-of-sky-news-australia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to explain his editorial direction}}}\uc2  of Sky News Australia, following the broadcaster\u8217\'20\'19s temporary banning by \uc2 YouTube\uc2  for alleged misinformation regarding Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Leading Australian scientists and engineers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/02/australia-has-technology-to-cut-emissions-now-and-coalition-should-embrace-it-scientists-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have urged the Morrison government}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget on with it\u8221\'20\'1D when it comes to emissions reductions, stating that \u8220\'20\'1Cmature, low-carbon technology\u8221\'20\'1D already exists to curb high-emitting industrial sectors.\par \par \uc2 An independent scientific panel found that Adani\u8217\'20\'19s conservation plans for the endangered black-throated finch were \u8220\'20\'1Csuperficial\u8221\'20\'1D, a fact the Queensland government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/sep/02/buried-queensland-government-report-found-adani-plan-to-protect-black-throated-finch-was-superficial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to keep secret}}}\uc2 , despite originally commissioning the study.\par \par \uc2 The world\par \par \uc2 Women will not feature in the cabinet or other top positions within the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new government,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/women-can-continue-working-in-afghan-government-say-taliban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a senior spokesperson has confirmed}}}\uc2 , despite claiming positions would be filled \u8220\'20\'1Con merit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Salman Rushdie has made a deal to publish his next work of fiction as a serialised novella on the subscription newsletter platform Substack. \u8220\'20\'1CI got very attracted to the idea recently, in this strange year and a half, of trying out things I\u8217\'20\'19ve never done before,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/sep/01/i-guess-im-having-a-go-at-killing-it-salman-rushdie-to-bypass-print-and-publish-next-book-on-substack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said when the deal was announced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Israel has dubbed a US plan to reopen its Jerusalem consulate as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bad idea\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Historically a base for diplomacy with Palestinian authorities, President Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/01/israel-us-plan-reopen-jerusalem-consulate-bad-idea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has pledged to reopen the consulate}}}\uc2  as part of ongoing support for a two-state solution.\par \par \uc2 A leading \uc2 Opec\uc2  member has urged fellow oil producers to contemplate \u8220\'20\'1Cenergy transition\u8221\'20\'1D, by embracing renewable energy and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/01/opec-member-urges-oil-producers-to-focus-more-on-renewable-energy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving away from fossil fuel dependency}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest known triceratops skeleton, Big John, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/sep/01/big-john-largest-known-triceratops-skeleton-goes-on-display-before-auction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is set to go under the hammer}}}\uc2  at an auction house in France. Painstakingly put together from over 200 bones, the 2.6m and over 700kg \u8220\'20\'1Cmiracle of nature\u8221\'20\'1D is expected to fetch \u8364\'20\'AC1.5m.\par \par \uc2 Recommended reads\par \par \uc2 Two decades ago Richard Stiles escaped an avalanche in New Zealand, but friend Steve Robinson wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so lucky. Now the rediscovery of a missing backpack containing a roll of film has revealed Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s last mountain ascent before he died. \u8220\'20\'1CTwenty-four years ago, Robinson and his friend Richard Stiles were having a breather on the side of the mountain when an enormous block of ice crashed into the snow and set off an avalanche. Stiles leaped out of the way and survived, but could see no sign of Robinson \u8211\'20\'13 or his backpack. Until he saw those pictures on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  on Saturday night,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/02/photos-from-beyond-the-grave-camera-discovery-reveals-climbers-last-images-before-fatal-avalanche"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Tory Shepherd}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Australian economy is nearly 10% bigger than it was at this stage one year ago. But before you reach for the champagne, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/grogonomics/2021/sep/02/australias-economy-looks-better-than-a-year-ago-but-sadly-we-arent-out-of-the-covid-woods-yet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Jericho cautions}}}\uc2 , a Covid buffeting still looms. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you consider that during the mining boom years the highest annual GDP growth ever reached was 4.9%, you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to have a degree in economics to know something is amiss \u8211\'20\'13 because we sure as heck are not in a boom right now.\u8221\'20\'1D And while a post-lockdown correction is definitely at play, a fall in government investment incentives puts a load of pressure on private sector investment to fuel future growth.\par \par \uc2 When it hit the shelves in 2018, Boy Swallows Universe was an instant Australian literary sensation. And when playwright Tim McGarry broached the subject of adapting the novel for the stage with author Trent Dalton, he received succinct feedback: \u8220\'20\'1Cgood luck to you, mate\u8221\'20\'1D. But shorn from its initial six and a half hours, McGarry has woven a multilayered tapestry, befitting the novel\u8217\'20\'19s own complexity and chutzpah, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2021/sep/02/swing-for-the-fence-bringing-boy-swallows-universe-to-the-stage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Stafford writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve featured in plenty of other people\u8217\'20\'19s ten funniest things on the internet, but now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2021/sep/02/aunty-donna-the-funniest-things-i-have-ever-seen-on-the-internet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it\u8217\'20\'19s the turn of Aunty Donna}}}\uc2  to share with us their favourite online funnies. So if you like beer, women and big shiny trucks \u8211\'20\'13 or just premium prices \u8211\'20\'13 take a gander.\par \par \uc2 Listen\par \par \uc2 Hospitals at breaking point. As the Delta strain endures, some of New South Wales\u8217\'20\'19 largest hospitals are approaching the stage where staff exhaustion is beginning to compromise patient care. On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2021/sep/02/inside-the-nsw-hospitals-at-breaking-point"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this episode of Full Story}}}\uc2 , reporter Elias Visontay hears from doctors, nurses and patients on the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Full Story is Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s daily news podcast. Subscribe for free on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/au/podcast/full-story/id1482061243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Apple Podcasts}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open.spotify.com/show/7GJod4EyoLywB1AW6zrSHh?si=mbMJnUPiSO2snfF0jNw7jw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Spotify}}}\uc2  or any other podcasting app.\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Australia and New Zealand meet once again, with the Bledisloe already decided. But, the third Test in Perth is anything but a dead rubber, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/sep/02/bledisloe-cup-finale-anything-but-a-dead-rubber-in-rugby-championship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bret Harris explains}}}\uc2 , because it doubles as a Rugby Championship match \u8211\'20\'13 a competition Australia could yet win.\par \par \uc2 Due to a Covid-related anomaly, the Socceroos road to Qatar 2022 will now continue in Qatar. And with Australia losing home advantage a well-drilled Chinese opponent looms as just one potential banana-skin in Group B, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/sep/02/world-cup-socceroos-road-to-qatar-starts-in-qatar-but-anything-can-happen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Duerden writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Premier League transfer window has closed. And while big ticket signings such as Cristiano Ronaldo and Romelu Lukaku have dominated the headlines, for many clubs quiet and steady work away from the limelight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/sep/01/transfer-window-verdict-how-every-premier-league-club-fared"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been the story}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Media roundup\par \par \uc2 Police have fined nine men as part of their investigations into illegal parties in Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s eastern suburbs that have led to dozens of Covid-19 cases, the SMH reports. The widow of former deputy prime minister Tim Fischer has accused the Coalition of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theaustralian.com.au/nation/coalition-has-made-a-mess-of-ndis-says-judy-fischer/news-story/dd46f37c24d93d2a1073bd2c14f162c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grossly mismanaging the NDIS}}}\uc2 , reports the Australian. And, a hospital accused in Queensland parliament of providing substandard care was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.couriermail.com.au/news/queensland/documents-reveal-bosses-were-aware-of-unsafe-practices-at-hospital/news-story/0b01a3daae2c6b130572d58ce67c22c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned of declining standards}}}\uc2  by a whistleblowing doctor nearly a year ago, the Courier Mail writes.\par \par \uc2 Coming up\par \par \uc2 The World University Rankings will be released.\par \par \uc2 A sentence hearing will take place for UTS professor Dianne Jolley, who was found guilty of sending herself fake letters.\par \par \uc2 And if you\u8217\'20\'19ve read this far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re calling it a nanogenerator, and according to Swiss scientists it could just be the breakthrough technology that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/01/hi-tech-wooden-flooring-can-turn-footsteps-into-electricity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foot-powers an energy revolution}}}\uc2 . By turning humble wooden floorboards into a nanocrystal and silicone-coated electricity generator, researchers are hoping simply walking around one\u8217\'20\'19s apartment or house could be enough to power household utilities. But with the technology only at proof-of-concept stage, they\u8217\'20\'19ve been keen to stress: it\u8217\'20\'19s still one step at a time.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive the Guardian Australia morning mail to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210901eh91003pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
