\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Democrats condemn supreme court for failing to block Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 661 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2021\par 20:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Critics denounce law as unconstitutional and a threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s health\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats across the country are condemning the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  over its silence on Texas\u8217\'20\'19s latest and most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to date after it came into effect on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The so-called \u8220\'20\'1CHeartbeat Act\u8221\'20\'1D, which was signed into law by Greg Abbott, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, in May, bans abortions at six weeks and does not make exceptions for incest and rape. Furthermore, it empowers private citizens to sue any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who violates the law.\par \par \uc2 Texas is the first state to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this early in pregnancy since Roe v Wade, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last-minute efforts to halt it}}}\uc2  through an appeal to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  by Tuesday did not succeed, as \uc2 the Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats including Joe Biden and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  have criticized the supreme court for not taking up an appeal that would have at least temporarily blocked the law. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/betsy_klein/status/1433101777243676682?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, Biden criticized the law, saying that it \u8220\'20\'1Cblatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v Wade and upheld as precedent for nearly half a century\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Texas law will significantly impair women\u8217\'20\'19s access to the healthcare they need \u8230\'20\'26 And outrageously, it deputizes private citizens to bring lawsuits against anyone who they believe has helped another person get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  also lambasted the court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1433093747856789504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1433093747856789504%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2021%2Fsep%2F01%2Ftexas-abortion-law-afghanistan-latest-news-joe-biden-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  saying on Twitter,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the cover of darkness, by choosing to do nothing, the supreme court allowed an unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas to go into effect last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir decision doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the fact that reproductive rights are human rights. We\u8217\'20\'19ll fight for them,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 The New York representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, who in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/01/aoc-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-sexual-assault-survivor-capitol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that she is a survivor of sexual assault, responded to the law and the supreme court by tweeting a video clip of her speaking against \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to the court in 2018 amid his denials of sexually assaulting Christine Blasey Ford, a California professor, when she was 15 years old and he was 17.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1433113302662516736?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CAmong many other warnings, survivors warned that sexual assault is about abuse of power, & a judge credibly accused of such shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be trusted w the rights of the vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow Roe is upended. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not going anywhere. This is a fight for our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Joaqu\u237\'00\'EDn Castro\uc2 , a congressman from Texas, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court allowed the law to go into effect \u8211\'20\'13 effectively ending Roe v Wade protections in Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D He urged Congress to act, emphasizing that all women have a constitutional right to complete healthcare.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , Democratic chair of the House oversight committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/news/press-releases/chairwoman-maloney-s-statement-on-supreme-court-inaction-allowing-texas-6-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CIn refusing to intervene last night, the supreme court tipped the scales of justice in favor of one of the most draconian state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in history.\u8221\'20\'1D Maloney accused the court of putting the health and safety of Texans, particularly those with lower income and people of color, in jeopardy.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, Senator Mazie Hirono of Hawaii {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maziehirono/status/1432775696619909124?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court can end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights tonight, without any arguments. They\u8217\'20\'19re hoping we don\u8217\'20\'19t notice.\u8221\'20\'1D She added the hashtag \u8220\'20\'1C#BansOffOurBodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A preliminary injunction hearing was originally set for 30 August in federal court. However, the largely conservative fifth circuit court of appeals cancelled the hearing on Sunday afternoon and denied the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 request to allow the district court to block the law. Providers then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed to the US supreme court}}}\uc2  for emergency relief.\par \par \uc2 The court failed to act before the law took effect on Wednesday, allowing it to proceed.\par \par \uc2 As Democrats denounce the supreme court over its silence, the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest court is set to take on a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in its next term, which begins in October. The Mississippi law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210901eh91003h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
