\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US leaves Afghanistan after 20 years\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho \par \uc2 1,292 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 August 2021\par 12:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The last evacuation flight out of Kabul airport marked the end of the US\u8217\'20\'19s longest war, leaving Afghanistan to its fateDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The last evacuation flight flew out of Kabul airport just before midnight local time in Afghanistan, marking the end of the US\u8217\'20\'19s nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/pentagon-kabul-drone-strike-islamic-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20-year occupation of the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In total, 2,461 American service members and civilians were killed and more than 20,000 were injured in the country\u8217\'20\'19s longest war, along with nearly 50,000 Afghan civilians and 70,000 Afghan soldiers and police who are estimated to have died in the violence since 2001. This number includes the 13 American service members and 70 Afghans killed after an airport attack by the \uc2 Islamic State Khorasan\uc2  Province (ISKP).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the last 24 hours, about 1,000 Afghans were evacuated who had worked for or with the US. The total civilian evacuation carried out this month was 123,000 \u8211\'20\'13 79,000 of which were flown out by the US military, including 6,000 US nationals.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 100 Americans remain in Afghanistan who wanted to leave but were unable to get out. The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  has pledged to allow anyone with valid documents to leave after the 31 August deadline.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The last two Americans to step off the tarmac in Kabul were the acting US ambassador, Ross Wilson, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/31/last-man-out-the-haunting-image-of-americas-final-moments-in-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maj Gen Christopher Donahue of the 82nd Airborne Division}}}\uc2 , the US commander who oversaw the evacuation operation.\par \par \uc2 As the last US military transport aircraft lifted off from Kabul airport, \uc2 Taliban\uc2  fighters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/31/gunfire-fills-the-air-in-kabul-as-taliban-celebrate-airport-takeover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired celebratory gunfire through the air }}}\uc2  and moved quickly to seize the airport. \uc2 Taliban\uc2  fighters wearing \uc2 US army\uc2  uniforms entered a former US military hangar and inspected US military helicopters, making an inventory of equipment left behind, video shot by a reporter for the LA Times showed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 For many American veterans who fought in Afghanistan, there are feelings of loss, devastation and anger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/31/us-veterans-afghanistan-fall-taliban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watching the country fall again to Taliban rule}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but not surprise.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Western powers have been forced to accept the reality of the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s control of Afghanistan in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/30/western-powers-back-watered-down-un-draft-on-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  standing behind a watered-down UN resolution}}}\uc2  that fails to spell out any consequences for the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . The resolution says it \u8220\'20\'1Cexpects\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  to honor a commitment to allow Afghans to leave the country and \u8220\'20\'1Crequests\u8221\'20\'1D that Kabul airport be securely reopened,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s next? The ISKP may now work to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/aug/31/afghanistan-islamic-state-divisions-taliban-kabul-bombing-kabul-bombing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 split the Taliban into rival factions}}}\uc2 , hoping that one of these factions will then ally with them.\par \par \uc2 For more Afghanistan news, follow the liveblog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2021/aug/31/afghanistan-live-news-kabul-taliban-biden-final-us-flight-military-forces-leave-airport-islamic-state-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least two killed and more than 1m without power after Hurricane Ida\par \par \uc2 At least two people were killed in the chaos of Hurricane Ida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/hurricane-ida-latest-new-orleans-louisiana-power-outages-death-toll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 150mph monster storm}}}\uc2  that was the most powerful ever to hit Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 John Bel Edwards\uc2 , and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said they expected the death toll to rise, with scores of coastal Louisiana residents trapped by flood waters and pleading to be rescued.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ida knocked out power for the entire city of New Orleans after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/hurricane-ida-new-orleans-damage-katrina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crucial transponder }}}\uc2  was toppled into the Mississippi River. Authorities estimate that more than a million homes and businesses across Louisiana are without power, and that it could be weeks before the power grid is repaired.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Without power, some are now left without food or water for several days and are left waiting and hoping for the best as rescuers survey the damages.\par \par \uc2 Oregon counties request refrigerated trucks for bodies as Covid overwhelms morgues\par \par \uc2 Two Oregon counties are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/oregon-coronavirus-deaths-hospitals-morgues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running out of space to hold bodies }}}\uc2  amid a surge in Covid-19 cases that is overwhelming the state\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare system. Local hospitals, funeral homes and crematoriums are either \u8220\'20\'1Cat the edge of crisis capacity daily\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistently at or exceeding their capacity\u8221\'20\'1D for body storage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the past two weeks, we have had more new positive cases than the first 10 months of the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D the Tillamook county board of commissioners said.\par \par \uc2 California wildfire forces unprecedented evacuation of Tahoe tourist town\par \par \uc2 Thousands of residents have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/30/caldor-fire-california-lake-tahoe-evacuations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced to evacuate}}}\uc2  the popular tourist town of South Lake Tahoe as the Caldor fire draws closer. Ash rained down as the long lines of cars trying to evacuate gridlocked the roads and brought traffic to a standstill.\par \par \uc2 The Caldor fire, which broke out on 14 August, has so far burned 277 sq miles and more than 650 structures have been destroyed. At least 20,000 more structures are under threat. Three first responders have been injured in the blaze, along with two civilians.\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers ask supreme court to halt unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 In a last-ditch effort to stop a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that allows any individual the right to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who violates the extreme law, Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are asking the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/texas-abortion-law-sb8-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block the unprecedented measure}}}\uc2  that goes into effect tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Signed into law by the Republican governor, Greg Abbott, in May, the law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected \u8211\'20\'13 typically about six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and offers no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 In other news\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats are pushing what may be their last chance to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/democrats-voting-rights-senate-bill-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold off voter suppression efforts by Republicans}}}\uc2 , with Democratic party members saying their control of both the House and Senate is at stake if they do not pass new legislation to protect elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jury selection begins today in the trial of the Theranos founder, Elizabeth Holmes, who is is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/aug/30/elizabeth-holmes-trial-jury-selection-begins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with six counts of fraud}}}\uc2  and faces up to 20 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Native American tribes will continue to enforce mask mandates in states with bans on school mask mandates, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/native-american-tribes-mask-mandates-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  asserting their powers as sovereign nations}}}\uc2  to defy the orders.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Opponents of California\u8217\'20\'19s recall of \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  have raised $62.2m to keep him in office\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, is facing a recall election in a few weeks. Those in favor of the recall, however, have only raised $8m, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/california-governor-recall-election-gavin-newsom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he has raised nearly eight times that}}}\uc2 . Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s huge fundraising advantage guarantees absolutely nothing, however, as recalls do not allow the incumbent to face off directly with his opponents.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: how the US created a world of endless war\par \par \uc2 The new kind of US war is not defined by death, but by control by domination and surveillance. While it centers itself on a near complete immunity from harm for the American side and unprecedented care when it comes to killing people on the other, with fewer captives mistreated and fewer civilians dead than in the past, the US\u8217\'20\'19s military operations have become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/31/how-the-us-created-a-world-of-endless-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more expansive in scope and perpetual in time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate Check: selfie stations in national parks\par \par \uc2 US national parks were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/aug/31/us-national-parks-crowd-control-strategies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overrun with visitors this summer}}}\uc2 , with many forced to close their gates with parking filled up. With these visitors came graffiti, trash and reckless behavior. Park officials are brainstorming ways to manage the crowds and preserve these public lands. One tactic: selfie stations to encourage people to take photos in one place instead of another.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: a sea shanty\par \par \uc2 One of the few things that Covid-19 did not shut down in Ireland over the past year and a half was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/travel/2021/aug/31/in-ireland-lockdown-has-made-us-fall-in-love-with-the-sea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appreciation of the sea}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a huge explosion in open-water swimming,\u8221\'20\'1D says Elaine Mullan, of Waterford Sports Partnership.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in Touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210831eh8v001p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
