\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers ask supreme court to halt unprecedented  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 570 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2021\par 20:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights and Planned Parenthood turn to justices in final bid to block near-total ban\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/WWH-v.-Jackson-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking the US supreme court}}}\uc2  to block a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that allows any individual the right to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who violates the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/aug/30/abortion-law-federal-court-decision-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme law}}}\uc2 , a final effort to stop the unprecedented measure from taking effect on Wednesday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Signed into law}}}\uc2  by the Republican governor, Greg Abbott, in May, Senate bill 8 bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected \u8211\'20\'13 typically around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and offers no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The appeal to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s high court comes after the largely conservative fifth circuit court of appeals on Sunday afternoon cancelled a federal district court preliminary injunction hearing on the law scheduled for Monday. Plaintiff attorneys, including the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , Planned Parenthood and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , who are representing more than 20 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and assistance fund groups in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/texas-abortion-ban-lawsuit-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit filed in July}}}\uc2 , requested the fifth circuit block the law itself, but that was denied. They are now asking the supreme court to stop the law or to at least allow district court proceedings to continue so that they can still secure an injunction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn less than two days, Texas politicians will have effectively overturned Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s cruel, unconscionable, and unlawful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unlike other so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills passed in a dozen other states and blocked by the courts, the Texas version largely shields state officials from enforcement. Instead, it empowers any private citizen in the US \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of their connection to the patient \u8211\'20\'13 to bring civil suit against not only an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider but anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure, a stunningly large pool of potential legal targets that could include clinic staff, rape crisis counselors, physicians, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund workers or simply a friend or family member who drives a patient to the clinic.\par \par \uc2 While those who sue can collect a minimum of $10,000 if they are successful, those unjustly sued cannot recover legal fees. The law\u8217\'20\'19s radical legal provision is the first of its kind in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians are empowering extremists to use lawsuits to harass and intimidate anyone who helps someone get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kamyon Conner, executive director of Texas Equal Access Fund, a plaintiff in the lawsuit challenging SB8.\par \par \uc2 Medical professionals, attorneys, and reproductive rights groups have warned that if the law goes into effect it will drastically upend the legal and healthcare landscape in Texas. The majority of Texas women (85%) will not be able to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as most aren\u8217\'20\'19t aware they are pregnant before the six-week cutoff, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Policy Evaluation Project}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf permitted to take effect, SB 8 would immediately and catastrophically reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Texas [...] and likely force many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics ultimately to close,\u8221\'20\'1D providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/WWH-v.-Jackson-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in their request for emergency relief from the supreme court. \u8220\'20\'1CPatients who can scrape together resources will be forced to attempt to leave the state to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and many will be delayed until later in pregnancy. The remaining Texans who need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to remain pregnant against their will or to attempt to end their pregnancies without medical supervision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210830eh8u0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
