\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden predicts \u8216\'20\'18infrastructure decade\u8217\'20\'19 as Senate passes bipartisan bill \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 8,128 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2021\par 00:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bill passes in 69-30 vote, with 19 Republicans supporting planPresident says of Cuomo resignation: \u8216\'20\'18I respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision\u8217\'20\'19Infrastructure bill lauded as a victory for bipartisanship \u8211\'20\'13 but is it?Cuomo resigns in wake of damning report on sexual harassmentNew York governor\u8217\'20\'19s resignation will take effect in 14 days\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  announced his resignation a week after the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office released a report saying the governor had sexually harassed at least 11 women. In a prepared statement today, Cuomo continued to defend his actions, but he said he now considered his resignation to be in the best interest of the state. \u8220\'20\'1CThe best way I can help now is if I step aside and let government get back to governing. And therefore, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ll do,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuomo said, noting the resignation will take effect in 14 days.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  welcomed the governor\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, after the president called for Cuomo to step down last week. \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and I respect the decision he made,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate passed the bipartisan infrastructure bill in a vote of 69 to 30. The legislation now heads to the House, where it may face resistance from some progressive lawmakers. If enacted, the bill would invest $550bn in new federal funds for roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 * Biden praised the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the infrastructure bill, describing the bipartisan deal as proof that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy can still work\u8221\'20\'1D. Speaking at the White House this afternoon, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CAfter years and years of infrastructure week, we\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of an infrastructure decade that I truly believe will transform America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Senate voted along party lines to start debate on the $3.5tn reconciliation bill, which Democrats plan to pass without any Republican support. The vote-a-rama on the bill is now under way in the Senate, and it may continue into the early hours of Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  is suing two far-right news networks, One America News (OAN) and Newsmax, for spreading lies about fraud in the 2020 election. In its lawsuits, Dominion accused the networks of having \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured, endorsed, repeated, and broadcast a series of verifiably false yet devastating lies\u8221\'20\'1D that caused irreparable harm to the company. Dominion is seeking billions of dollars in damages to make up for lost profits and other costs incurred as the company has fought these election lies.\par \par \uc2 * The House will return to session 23 August and will likely work on HR 4, the \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  Voting Rights Act. The act would restore protections of the Voting Rights Act, gutted by the supreme court in 2013. Meanwhile, a court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.txcourts.gov/supreme/orders-opinions/2021/august/august-10-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  a restraining order that protected Texas lawmakers from being arrested after they fled the state in July to stop a Republican effort to enact new voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 * Several of Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional, a federal judge ruled on Tuesday. US district court judge Sarah Evans Barker issued a permanent injunction against a ban on telemedicine consultations between doctors and women seeking abortions. The judge also ruled against state laws mandating in-person examinations by a doctor before medication abortions and against a requirement that women seeking abortions be told human life begins when the egg is fertilized.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve, Dani Anguiano and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 US urged to fast-track vaccine approval for children under 12 as cases rise\par \par \uc2 As Covid cases among children continue to rise in the US due to spread of the Delta variant, experts are urging the federal government to fast-track vaccine approval for those under the age of 12.\par \par \uc2 New {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://services.aap.org/en/pages/2019-novel-coronavirus-covid-19-infections/children-and-covid-19-state-level-data-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data analysis from the American Academy of Pediatrics}}}\uc2  (AAP) indicated that children accounted for 15% of new cases reported last week, with a total of almost 94,000 cases. There was a 4% increase in child cases over the past two weeks, the AAP found.\par \par \uc2 While children still make up a small fraction of hospitalized Covid patients, up to 1.9% in states reporting such data, there is anecdotal evidence in areas that have seen a significant Covid surge in recent weeks that more children are being admitted for care.\par \par \uc2 In Louisiana, which saw a significant surge of 16,000 new Covid cases and 50 deaths over the weekend as the Delta variant rips through the region, pediatricians in New Orleans expressed concerns about an uptick in child Covid admissions.\par \par \uc2 Dr Mark Kline, chief of Children\u8217\'20\'19s Hospital New Orleans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wdsu.com/article/new-orleans-louisiana-children-sick-covid-19-unvaccianted-adults-responsible/37259391#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told local news}}}\uc2  that outpatient Covid positivity rates had risen from 1% a month ago to 20%. The hospital was treating 18 child Covid inpatients with six in intensive care. There were three on ventilators, including a three month old baby, Kline told WDSU News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is heartbreaking, honestly, to take care of potentially dying children,\u8221\'20\'1D Kline told the news channel. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of this was likely unnecessary if we as adults did what we needed to do and get the vaccine. We could have protected these children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Louisiana has one of the lowest rates of vaccination in the US with just 37% of the state fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/us-covid-vaccine-children-under-12-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US urged to fast-track vaccine approval for children under 12 as cases rise}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge rules against Indiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\par \par \uc2 Several of Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional, a federal judge ruled Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The US district court judge Sarah Evans Barker issued a permanent injunction against a ban on telemedicine consultations between doctors and women seeking abortions. The judge also ruled against state laws mandating in-person examinations by a doctor before medication abortions and against a requirement that women seeking abortions be told human life begins when the egg is fertilized.\par \par \uc2 Attacks on reproductive rights in the US have accelerated in the last decade with Republicans using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressive}}}\uc2  new tactics to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists continuing to gain ground on the right.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jul/23/abortion-us-supreme-court-mississippi-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged the supreme court}}}\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade, which legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, and a federal judge blocked an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/21/arkansas-abortion-ban-federal-judge-blocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas law}}}\uc2  banning nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives will likely take up another voting rights bill\par \par \uc2 The House will return to session 23 August and will likely work on HR 4, the \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  Voting Rights Act, \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , the House majority leader, wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.majorityleader.gov/content/dear-colleague-august-work-period"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to colleagues. The act would restore protections of the Voting Rights Act, gutted by the supreme court in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The news comes as top Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are expected to make another attempt to push for voting rights legislation before the chamber leaves Washington for a summer recess.\par \par \uc2 Read more on Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/senate-democrats-push-voting-rights-legislation-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Democrats poised for voting rights push to counter Republican restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas supreme court rules Democrats who left state to block voting restrictions can be arrested\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.txcourts.gov/supreme/orders-opinions/2021/august/august-10-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  a restraining order that protected the lawmakers from being arrested after they fled the state in July to stop a Republican effort to enact new voting restrictions. By fleeing the state, Democratic lawmakers denied the Republican-led legislature the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/16/texas-democrats-jolted-voting-rights-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quorum needed}}}\uc2  to proceed with the bill.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision means that those who have returned to the state can be detained and forcibly brought to the state capitol to re-establish quorum, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/08/10/texas-greg-abbott-democrats-special-session/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more about the fight over Texas voting restrictions here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/16/texas-democrats-jolted-voting-rights-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18??I think it kicked ass\u8217\'20\'19: how Texas Democrats fought for voting rights by fleeing the state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I still feel it isn\u8217\'20\'19t real\u8217\'20\'19: Gold Rush town residents reckon with wildfire devastation\par \par \uc2 The $1tn infrastructure bill that passed the Senate takes some steps toward addressing the climate crisis and building resiliency \u8211\'20\'13 through environmental activists and progressive Democrats say it falls short. In California, where global heating has helped fuel extreme wildfires, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dani-anguiano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dani Anguiano}}}\uc2  reports on the devastation of the Dixie fire:\par \par \uc2 After weeks of fire, smoke and warnings, Kimberly Price\u8217\'20\'19s beloved hometown had run out of time.\par \par \uc2 With wind driving the Dixie fire directly into Greenville, Price\u8217\'20\'19s longtime partner, John Hunter, told her she needed to leave. Price, 58, had spent most of her life in the close-knit Sierra Nevada community. She couldn\u8217\'20\'19t bear the thought of leaving, but the flames were everywhere.\par \par \uc2 She made Hunter promise he would follow, and then she left Greenville, driving away from the home she had bought from her grandparents, with the butterfly bushes and cherry trees she carefully tended, away from the house where her granddaughters had spent their whole lives, away from the storage unit that held handmade Christmas ornaments and her mother\u8217\'20\'19s belongings, and away from the 92-year-old hardware store that Hunter owned.\par \par \uc2 Within an hour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/05/california-dixie-fire-greenville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most of it was gone}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Flames overtook the Gold Rush town of 1,000 people last week, destroying homes and much of the area\u8217\'20\'19s historic downtown: a hotel, a bar and the Hunter Ace Hardware store. Like Paradise and Berry Creek before it, Greenville became another northern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  town devastated by fire.\par \par \uc2 Firefighters are still battling to contain the blaze that leveled much of Greenville. The Dixie fire has grown into the largest single wildfire recorded in California history.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the fire kept pushing through forestlands, as fire crews tried to protect rural communities from the flames. The clearing of thick smoke along one edge of the fire allowed aircraft to join nearly 6,000 firefighters in the fight.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/greenville-california-wildfire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I still feel it isn\u8217\'20\'19t real\u8217\'20\'19: Gold Rush town residents reckon with wildfire devastation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  clarified the president\u8217\'20\'19s earlier comments praising \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legacy as governor.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a reporter had asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to assess Cuomo \u8217\'20\'19s decade-long career as governor. \u8220\'20\'1CI thought he\u8217\'20\'19s done a hell of a job \u8211\'20\'13 and both on everything from access to voting to infrastructure to a whole range of things. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s so sad,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden responded.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @potus}}}\uc2  responded to a specific question today about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYGovCuomo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NYGovCuomo}}}\uc2  work on infrastructure. He also made clear it was right for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYGovCuomo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NYGovCuomo}}}\uc2  to step down, reiterated his support for women who come forward, and made clear you can\u8217\'20\'19t separate personal behavior from other work.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1425194084780679170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki clarified that while Biden praised Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s work on infrastructure, in light of revelations that the New York governor had sexually harassed women, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can\u8217\'20\'19t separate personal behavior from other work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  announced his resignation a week after the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office released a report saying the governor had sexually harassed at least 11 women. In a prepared statement today, Cuomo continued to defend his actions, but he said he now considered his resignation to be in the best interest of the state. \u8220\'20\'1CThe best way I can help now is if I step aside and let government get back to governing. And therefore, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ll do,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuomo said, noting the resignation will take effect in 14 days.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  welcomed the governor\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, after the president called for Cuomo to step down last week. \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and I respect the decision he made,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate passed the bipartisan infrastructure bill in a vote of 69 to 30. The legislation now heads to the House, where it may face resistance from some progressive lawmakers. If enacted, the bill would invest $550bn in new federal funds for roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 * Biden praised the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the infrastructure bill, describing the bipartisan deal as proof that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy can still work\u8221\'20\'1D. Speaking at the White House this afternoon, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CAfter years and years of infrastructure week, we\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of an infrastructure decade that I truly believe will transform America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Senate voted along party lines to start debate on the $3.5tn reconciliation bill, which Democrats plan to pass without any Republican support. The vote-a-rama on the bill is now underway in the Senate, and it may continue into the early hours of Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  is suing two far-right news networks, One America News (OAN) and Newsmax, for spreading lies about fraud in the 2020 election. In its lawsuits, Dominion accused the networks of having \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured, endorsed, repeated, and broadcast a series of verifiably false yet devastating lies\u8221\'20\'1D that caused irreparable harm to the company. Dominion is seeking billions of dollars in damages to make up for lost profits and other costs incurred as the company has fought these election lies.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Klein reports on Kathy Hochul, who will soon become governor of New York:\par \par \uc2 When the New York governor, \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , leaves office in 14 days time after resigning over allegations that he sexually harassed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-sexual-harassment-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 11 women}}}\uc2 , the state will finally get its first female governor.\par \par \uc2 Lieutenant Governor Kathy Hochul, 62, has served in her post since 2015. Now, she will take over as New York\u8217\'20\'19s top politician in just two weeks time, Cuomo announced suddenly on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Hochul, considered a centrist Democrat, got her start in politics working in local government, serving in offices like Eerie county clerk before winning a special election for state congress in her hometown district. However, her time as a congresswoman was short-lived, and she lost to Republican \uc2 Chris Collins\uc2  the following year.\par \par \uc2 As lieutenant governor, the Buffalo-raised politician has rarely sought the spotlight and maintained a characteristic distance from her boss. In recent months, as scrutiny around Cuomo intensified over his treatment of women and accusations that his administration intentionally downplayed the true number of New York nursing home deaths during the Covid-19 pandemic, Hochul further separated herself from him.\par \par \uc2 She called his behavior toward women \u8220\'20\'1Crepulsive\u8221\'20\'1D in the wake of a report from the state attorney general released last week, which detailed allegations that he had sexually harassed 11 women.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/09/kathy-hochul-new-york-lieutenant-governor-andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kathy Hochul: the lieutenant governor taking over for Cuomo}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James, whose office oversaw the investigation into the sexual harassment allegations against \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , said the governor\u8217\'20\'19s resignation ends a \u8220\'20\'1Csad chapter\u8221\'20\'1D for the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday closes a sad chapter for all of New York, but it\u8217\'20\'19s an important step towards justice,\u8221\'20\'1D James said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, closes a sad chapter for all of New York, but it\u8217\'20\'19s an important step towards justice.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1425144148936507396?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The attorney general added, \u8220\'20\'1CI thank Governor Cuomo for his contributions to our state. The ascension of our Lieutenant Governor, Kathy Hochul, will help New York enter a new day. We must continue to build on the progress already made and improve the lives of New Yorkers in every corner of the state. I know our state is in good hands with Lieutenant Governor Hochul at the helm, and I look forward to continuing to work with her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hochul is expected to formally become governor in two weeks, when Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s resignation takes effect. She will be the first woman to ever serve as the governor of New York.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to assess \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decade-long career as governor, as he prepares to step down in the wake of 11 women accusing him of sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of his personal behavior or what he\u8217\'20\'19s done as a governor?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s he done as a governor,\u8221\'20\'1D the reporter replied.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought he\u8217\'20\'19s done a hell of a job \u8211\'20\'13 and both on everything from access to voting to infrastructure to a whole range of things. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s so sad,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @edokeefe}}}\uc2  his assessment of \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 's tenure as governor of New York: "He's done a hell of a job \u8212\'20\'14 on everything from access to voting to infrastructure to a whole range of things. That's why it's so sad." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ea8wIVnL34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ea8wIVnL34}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m3rcWFJ1xQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m3rcWFJ1xQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1425180580858191875?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Moments later, another reporter pressed Biden on whether Cuomo could have truly done \u8220\'20\'1Ca hell of a job\u8221\'20\'1D as governor when he has been accused of sexually harassing nearly a dozen women and breaking laws in the process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou asked two different questions,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. The president underscored the importance of believing the women whose allegations were substantiated by the investigation conducted by the office of the New York attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was asked a specific question,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding that he was not generally attempting to separate Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s personal behavior from his gubernatorial record.\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kaitlancollins}}}\uc2  to President Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CCan you really say that [Gov. Cuomo] has done \u8216\'20\'18a hell of a job\u8217\'20\'19 if he\u8217\'20\'19s accused of sexually harassing women on the job?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G6tjrhn2At"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/G6tjrhn2At}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1425182427220164608?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taking additional questions from reporters, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery concerned\u8221\'20\'1D about the potential spread of coronavirus among children who are too young to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason children are becoming infected is because, in most cases, they live in low vaccination rate states and communities, and they\u8217\'20\'19re getting it from unvaccinated adults. That\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so, my plea is to those who are not vaccinated: Think about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden says he's "very concerned" about children catching COVID and it's "disingenuous" that governors accusing him of government overreach are threatening school officials who enforce protocols. He says he's "checking" if he has power to intervene in states like Texas and Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vqQFRA7kD4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vqQFRA7kD4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1425180183544451081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president also argued that there is a logical inconsistency among Republican lawmakers who are criticizing his administration for alleged federal overreach by encouraging mask usage and simultaneously threatening to retaliate against schools that implement mask mandates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find that totally counterintuitive and, quite frankly, disingenuous,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president did not specifically name \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , but the comment appeared to be a direct rebuke of the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 'I respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision,' Biden says of Cuomo resignation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is taking a few questions from reporters after wrapping up his prepared remarks on the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the bipartisan infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 And \u8211\'20\'13 no surprise here \u8211\'20\'13 the first question was about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response to \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he will step down as governor of New York.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden on \uc2 Gov. Andrew Cuomo\uc2  (D-NY) resignation:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision and I respect the decision he made.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ikwcXplzHU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ikwcXplzHU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1425177454029774849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision, and I respect the decision he made,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president had previously called on Cuomo to resign, after the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office released a report saying the governor had sexually harassed at least 11 women and violated state and federal law in doing so.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  described the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the infrastructure bill as proof that bipartisanship is still possible, even in today\u8217\'20\'19s bitterly divided Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the Republicans who supported this bill, you showed a lot of courage,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of the 19 Republican senators who voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on the infrastructure proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have and no doubt you will disagree with me on many issues, but where we can agree, we should. And here on this bill, we proved that we can still come together to do big things, important things, for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president thanked Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  for supporting the bill, and he credited majority leader Chuck Schumer for his \u8220\'20\'1Cmasterful\u8221\'20\'1D handling of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we proved that democracy can still work,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden celebrates Senate passage of infrastructure bill: 'We\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of an infrastructure decade'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the bipartisan infrastructure bill, thanking the 69 members of both parties who ensured the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s advancement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter years and years of infrastructure week, we\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of an infrastructure decade that I truly believe will transform America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltr"After years and years of infrastructure week, we're on the cusp of an infrastructure decade that I truly believe will transform America," President Biden says after the Senate passed an infrastructure bill. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W4Ce5smERA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W4Ce5smERA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1425173443021086721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 That line was, of course, a reference to the Trump administration repeatedly announcing \u8220\'20\'1Cinfrastructure week\u8221\'20\'1D but failing to ever actually sign any infrastructure bills.\par \par \uc2 The legislation still needs to pass the House before it reaches Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk, and the president emphasized the importance of giving final approval to the bill, which would invest $550bn in new federal funds for roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 About an hour and a half after the scheduled start time, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have arrived for their event to celebrate the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the bipartisan infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president spoke first, saying the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage demonstrated the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s commitment to working \u8220\'20\'1Con behalf of the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we move one step closer to making a once-in-a-generation investment in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will mean people in our nation won\u8217\'20\'19t have to drink water from lead pipes or go to a fast-food parking lot to get high-speed Internet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will soon deliver remarks at the White House on the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the $1.2tn bipartisan infrastructure bill earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Among the White House officials attending the event are Shalanda Young, the acting director of the Office of Management and Budget, and senior presidential adviser \uc2 Steve Ricchetti\uc2 , who helped negotiate the bipartisan agreement.\par \par \uc2 The event was scheduled to begin over an hour ago, but as is often the case with Biden, we are still waiting to start. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  on Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 latest effort to advance voting rights legislation:\par \par \uc2 Top {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  in the Senate are poised to make another attempt to push through voting rights legislation before the chamber leaves Washington for a summer recess, in a sign of their determination to counter a wave of Republican-led ballot restrictions across the nation.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer is expected to reintroduce Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 marquee election reform bill known as the For the People Act, with additional votes on one measure to end partisan gerrymandering and another measure to tighten campaign spending, sources said.\par \par \uc2 None of the measures, for which Schumer hopes to schedule votes immediately after the Senate takes up the $3.5tn budget blueprint for infrastructure, is expected to garner any Republican support and will thus likely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/22/voting-rights-bill-joe-biden-senate-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow the demise of the For the People Act}}}\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 The move by Senate Democrats will encourage voting rights activists, who have watched with alarm that the issue appeared to have taken a back seat as protracted negotiations over the $1tn bipartisan infrastructure package consumed the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Yet in the face of united Republican opposition, the endgame for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 even as they scramble to enact voting rights legislation to roll back a wave of GOP ballot restrictions in time for the 2022 midterm elections \u8211\'20\'13 remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/senate-democrats-push-voting-rights-legislation-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Democrats poised for voting rights push to counter Republican restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now that the bipartisan infrastructure bill has passed the Senate, civil rights leaders are calling on Democrats to act with the same kind of urgency when it comes to voting rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe White House must now prioritize voting rights legislation with the same level of urgency and commitment as the bipartisan infrastructure bill. Time is running out. The infrastructure of our own democracy, the heart and soul of America, is crumbling before our very eyes,\u8221\'20\'1D NAACP president Derrick Johnson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must protect the American people\u8217\'20\'19s sacred right to vote by any means possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 two voting rights bills, the For the People Act and the \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  Voting Rights Act, have stalled in the Senate because of a Republican filibuster.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate votes along party lines to begin debate on $3.5tn reconciliation bill\par \par \uc2 The Senate may have been able to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/aug/10/us-senate-bipartisan-infrastructure-bill-schumer-house-pelosi-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-61129f7f8f089093df87a23e#block-61129f7f8f089093df87a23e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass the $1.2tn infrastructure bill}}}\uc2  in a bipartisan fashion, but the upper chamber quickly reverted back to its partisan ways once that vote was over.\par \par \uc2 In a 50-49 vote that fell along party lines, the Senate voted to start debate on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn reconciliation bill, which covers many of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure initiatives not included in the bill passed today.\par \par \uc2 enltrAgreed to, 50-49: Motion to proceed to Cal. #122, S.Con.Res.14, FY2022 Budget Resolution.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1425138484466094084?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was in the Senate chamber in case she needed to cast a tie-breaking vote to start debate on the bill, but that was not necessary because Republican \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2  was absent for the vote. (Rounds is at the Mayo Clinic with his wife as she receives cancer treatment.)\par \par \uc2 The vote-a-rama on the bill has now begun, with Republicans prepared to offer potentially hundreds of amendments to the spending package, forcing Democrats to take votes on everything from climate policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The vote-a-rama session could continue into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1425150301447892997"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early hours of Wednesday morning}}}\uc2 , but ultimately Democrats do not need any Republican votes to advance the reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 enltrVote Update: the Senate will shortly proceed to up to 4 votes in relation to the following amendments to S.Con.Res.14, FY2022 Budget Resolution:\par \par \uc2 1. Barrasso #3055\par \par \uc2 2. Carper #3330\par \par \uc2 3. Thune #3106\par \par \uc2 4. \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  #3317\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1425147639406997504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/local/state/2021/08/09/florida-gov-desantis-threatens-salaries-school-superintendents-school-board-members-mask-mandates/5544903001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to take away teachers\u8217\'20\'19 salaries in his state if they enforce the mandatory wearing of masks as children come back to school.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is \u8220\'20\'1Clooking at options\u8221\'20\'1D to get around that situation if the governor carries out this threat, White House press sec \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has indicated today.\par \par \uc2 Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  briefing the media at the White House today. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The state could defund the salaries of district superintendents and county school board members who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/2021/08/09/leon-school-superintendent-mask-mandate-florida-tallahassee-schools-covid-temporary-surge/5536387001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mandate mask wearing in schools}}}\uc2 , according to a statement from DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 office yesterday, the Tallahassee Democrat newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/local/state/2021/08/09/florida-gov-desantis-threatens-salaries-school-superintendents-school-board-members-mask-mandates/5544903001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that federal funds distributed to cope with the coronavirus pandemic as a result of the American Rescue Plan signed into law by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  early in his administration included money for schools.\par \par \uc2 But she added that those funds had not been distributed in Florida by the state government. Without saying directly that the White House and the administration will look at ways of ensuring that funding gets to what she described as \u8220\'20\'1Celigible schools\u8221\'20\'1D she said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are looking at our options\u8221\'20\'1D in relation to efforts to ensure teachers do not have their pay cut if they enforce mask-wearing in the classroom to keep children safe from Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus is raging in Florida as a result of the Delta variant and children\u8217\'20\'19s hospitals are under pressure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 'This is a story about courageous woman' - White House on Cuomo quitting\par \par \uc2 The first question to press sec \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was, of course, about the announcement from New York\u8217\'20\'19s three-term, Democratic governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  about an hour ago that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/andrew-cuomo-resigns-sexual-harassment-intimidation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he is resigning}}}\uc2  after a report by the state attorney general found he sexually harassed 11 women.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  announces he will resign. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  led the calls last week from the Democratic establishment for Cuomo to resign after NY attorney general Letitia James announced the findings of a five-month investigation.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the US president had not spoken to Cuomo since then and the White House had not been given a heads-up that the governor was about to announce this morning - at around the exact time the Senate was passing the infrastructure bill, that he was stepping aside.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a story about courageous woman who told their stories\u8221\'20\'1D after the investigation by the AG, she said.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to talk a little later about the infrastructure bill. Psaki has not said if he will address the Cuomo situation. But, of course if journalists get a chance to ask him about it they surely will.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the administration looked forward to working with New York\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor Kathy Hochul, who will now step into Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s shoes and become the first woman to run the state.\par \par \uc2 enltrI agree with Governor Cuomo's decision to step down. It is the right thing to do and in the best interest of New Yorkers.\par \par \uc2 As someone who has served at all levels of government and is next in the line of succession, I am prepared to lead as New York State\u8217\'20\'19s 57th Governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kathy Hochul (@LtGovHochulNY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LtGovHochulNY/status/1425134938450444299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is now beginning her media briefing. She started by praising the passing of the infrastructure bill in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  about an hour ago.\par \par \uc2 She said US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is paying attention to the bipartisan aspect of the bill, after 19 Republicans joined the entire Democratic caucus in the upper chamber to pass the $1tr bill.\par \par \uc2 But she pointed out that even more importantly, the administration believes the legislation will \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliver huge benefits\u8221\'20\'1D to people in the US, creating \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added that the legislation was expected to benefit the environment and deliver clean drinking water and high speed internet to more Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  announced his resignation a week after the New York attorney general released a report saying the governor had sexually harassed at least 11 women. In a prepared statement today, Cuomo continued to defend his actions, but he said he now considered his resignation to be in the best interest of the state. \u8220\'20\'1CThe best way I can help now is if I step aside and let government get back to governing. And therefore, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ll do,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuomo said, noting the resignation will take effect in 14 days.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate passed the bipartisan infrastructure bill in a vote of 69 to 30. The legislation now heads to the House, where it may face resistance from some progressive lawmakers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who has wholeheartedly endorsed the bill, will deliver remarks on the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s Senate passage this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  is suing two far-right news networks, One America News (OAN) and Newsmax, for spreading lies about fraud in the 2020 election. In its lawsuits, Dominion accused the networks of having \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured, endorsed, repeated, and broadcast a series of verifiably false yet devastating lies\u8221\'20\'1D that caused irreparable harm to the company. Dominion is seeking billions of dollars in damages to make up for lost profits and other costs incurred as the company has fought these election lies.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cuomo resigns in wake of damning report on sexual harassment\par \par \uc2 The New York governor, \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , has resigned following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-sexual-harassment-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an investigation}}}\uc2  by the state attorney general that found he sexually harassed multiple women, most of whom worked for him, and also retaliated after some made complaints.\par \par \uc2 Delivering a prepared statement today, Cuomo continued to defend his actions, but he said he now considered his resignation to be in the best interest of New Yorkers and the state government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe best way I can help now is if I step aside and let government get back to governing. And therefore, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ll do,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuomo said, noting the resignation will take effect in 14 days.\par \par \uc2 enltr"The best way I can help now is if I step aside and let government get back to governing. And therefore, that's what I'll do," New York Gov. Cuomo says. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z1edfCJa3z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z1edfCJa3z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1425127074621267973?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Democratic governor had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/biden-cuomo-white-house-sexual-harassment-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost the support}}}\uc2  of the party establishment, with J oe Biden calling on Cuomo to resign and similar demands issued by House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , both of New York\u8217\'20\'19s US Senators \u8211\'20\'13 one of whom is Senate majority leader C huck Schumer \u8211\'20\'13 two Democratic New York congressmen, New York City mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  and a host of Republicans in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s own No 2, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/09/kathy-hochul-new-york-lieutenant-governor-andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York lieutenant governor, Kathy Hochul}}}\uc2 , had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LtGovHochulNY/status/1422631646080155649"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called his conduct}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Crepulsive and unlawful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His political future was dangling by a thread amid moves to impeach the governor and force him from office by the New York legislative assembly in the state capital of Albany.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/andrew-cuomo-resigns-sexual-harassment-intimidation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Cuomo resigns in wake of damning report on sexual harassment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks on the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the bipartisan infrastructure bill at 1:30 pm ET, the White House has just announced.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who presided over the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s final vote on the bipartisan bill, is also expected to speak, according to the White House\u8217\'20\'19s updated schedule for the day.\par \par \uc2 The president has already offered a full endorsement of the infrastructure bill, and he will likely call on the House to quickly pass it once members return from their recess next month. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nineteen Senate Republicans and all 50 Senate Democrats supported the final passage of the $1.2tn bipartisan infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 Here are the names of the 19 Republicans who voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on the bill, including Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrHere are the 19 Republican Senators who voted YES on the bipartisan infrastructure bill:\par \par \uc2 Blunt\par \par \uc2 Burr\par \par \uc2 Capito\par \par \uc2 Cassidy\par \par \uc2 Collins\par \par \uc2 Cramer\par \par \uc2 Crapo\par \par \uc2 Fischer\par \par \uc2 Graham\par \par \uc2 Grassley\par \par \uc2 Hoeven\par \par \uc2 McConnell\par \par \uc2 Murkowski\par \par \uc2 Portman\par \par \uc2 Risch\par \par \uc2 Romney\par \par \uc2 Sullivan\par \par \uc2 Tillis\par \par \uc2 Wicker\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1425122869479153664?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate passes bipartisan infrastructure bill in 69-30 vote\par \par \uc2 Well, it is finally and truly infrastructure week: the Senate has officially passed the bipartisan infrastructure bill in a vote of 69 to 30. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  presided over the vote.\par \par \uc2 Minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  was among the 19 Senate Republicans who joined Democrats to get the bill across the finish line. The legislation required a simple majority to pass the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 enltrPassed, 69-30: Cal. #100, H.R.3684, Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act, as amended.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1425122680815169538?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The bill now heads to the House, where it may face resistance from progressive lawmakers, some of whom have indicated they will not support the legislation without guarantees about the future passage of the $3.5tn reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already indicated he wholeheartedly supports the bipartisan infrastructure bill, which would invest $550bn in new federal funds for roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to soon deliver some kind of official response to the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has officially voted in favor of the bipartisan infrastructure bill, joining at least a dozen other Republican senators.\par \par \uc2 Other members of the Senate Republican leadership team, including \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  and \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , have already voted against the bill.\par \par \uc2 The vote is still open, and the bill currently has 63 \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D votes, which is more than enough to ensure its passage. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bipartisan infrastructure bill has enough votes to pass Senate\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan infrastructure bill now has enough votes to pass the Senate, although the count will not be official until the vote is gaveled out.\par \par \uc2 As of now, 55 senators have voted in support of passing the legislation, which would invest $550bn in new federal funds for roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects. A simple majority was needed to pass the bill\par \par \uc2 A number of Senate Republicans have voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on the bill, but at least two members of the Republican leadership team -- \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  and \uc2 John Thune\uc2  -- have opposed the legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate holds final vote on bipartisan infrastructure bill\par \par \uc2 The Senate is now holding its final vote on the bipartisan infrastructure bill, which is expected to pass with support from members of both parties.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also important to remember that the bill only needs a simple majority to pass, now that the legislation has cleared all possible procedural hurdles.\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW VOTING: Passage of Cal. #100, H.R.3684, Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act, as amended.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1425114013202006017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cuomo attorney blames controversy on 'media frenzy' after report corroborated harassment claims\par \par \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney, Rita Glavin, is now holding another press conference about the sexual harassment allegations against the New York governor.\par \par \uc2 Glavin held the press conference from the governor\u8217\'20\'19s New York City office, and she spoke while sitting in front of a state seal, even though she is the external lawyer for Cuomo.\par \par \uc2 Glavin began the press conference by attacking the credibility of the 11 women who have accused Cuomo of sexual harassment, and she blamed the widespread calls for his resignation on a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedia frenzy\u8221\'20\'1D around the allegations.\par \par \uc2 enltrCuomo's outside attorney, Rita Glavin, is appearing live from the governor's NYC office, in front of the state seal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DhkvHAyj0I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DhkvHAyj0I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Campbell (@JonCampbellGAN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonCampbellGAN/status/1425110795864711180?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about the veracity and the credibility about a report that is being used to impeach and take down an elected official,\u8221\'20\'1D Glavin said.\par \par \uc2 Of course, this \u8220\'20\'1Cmedia frenzy\u8221\'20\'1D picked up after the office of the New York attorney general, Letitia James, released the findings of an investigation that concluded Cuomo had sexually harassed at least 11 women and violated state and federal law in the process.\par \par \uc2 In response to that report, many members of Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s own party, including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , have called on the governor to step down.\par \par \uc2 So it seems pretty clear that it is not simply members of the media who are concerned about the allegations against Cuomo.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority whip \uc2 John Thune\uc2  told Capitol Hill reporters that he will vote against the bipartisan infrastructure bill today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just not fully paid for,\u8221\'20\'1D Thune said, per NBC News.\par \par \uc2 enltrThune is a NO on the bipartisan infrastructure bill, he tells reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just not fully paid for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Did Trump have influence? \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a factor,\u8221\'20\'1D Thune says.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julie Tsirkin (@JulieNBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulieNBCNews/status/1425104955560636435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The news is not the biggest surprise, considering Thune also voted against advancing the bill in a procedural vote on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Despite opposition from members of Senate Republican leadership, the bill should still have enough bipartisan support to pass the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  sues OAN and Newsmax over election lies\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  is suing two far-right news networks, One America News (OAN) and Newsmax, for their coverage of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In its lawsuits, Dominion accused the networks of having \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured, endorsed, repeated, and broadcast a series of verifiably false yet devastating lies\u8221\'20\'1D that caused irreparable damage to the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COAN helped create and cultivate an alternate reality where up is down, pigs have wings, and Dominion engaged in a colossal fraud to steal the presidency from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by rigging the vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Dominion said in its OAN lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Dominion is also suing Patrick Byrne, the former chief executive of Overstock.com. The company accused Byrne of amplifying lies about widespread fraud in the presidential election, harming Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s reputation.\par \par \uc2 Dominion is seeking billions of dollars in damages to make up for lost profits and other costs incurred as the company has fought these election lies.\par \par \uc2 The company has already filed lawsuits against some Trump allies, including \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell, for their roles in spreading the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/04/dominion-trump-disinformation-fox-news-sidney-powell-giuliani-mike-lindell-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominion: will one Canadian company bring down Trump's empire of disinformation?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  climate report raises pressure on Biden to seize a rare moment\par \par \uc2 A stark \uc2 UN\uc2  report on how humanity has caused unprecedented, and in some cases \u8220\'20\'1Cirreversible\u8221\'20\'1D, changes to the world\u8217\'20\'19s climate has heaped further pressure on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  to deliver upon what may be his sole chance to pass significant legislation to confront the climate crisis and break a decade of American political inertia.\par \par \uc2 The US president said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/aug/09/humans-have-caused-unprecedented-and-irreversible-change-to-climate-scientists-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the release on Monday of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change report}}}\uc2  showed that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to tackle the climate crisis. The signs are unmistakable. The science is undeniable. And the cost of inaction keeps mounting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IPCC report}}}\uc2 , developed over the past eight years by scientists who combed over more than 14,000 studies, shows that the US, like the rest of the world, is running out of time to avoid disastrous climate impacts, with a critical global heating threshold of 1.5C to be breached far earlier than previously expected, potentially within a decade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a future problem, it\u8217\'20\'19s a problem now. I\u8217\'20\'19m literally seeing climate change out of my window, climate change is in my lungs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Linda Mearns, an IPCC report co-author located in Boulder, Colorado, which has been baked in extreme heat and wildfire smoke in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Mearns, who has been involved in IPCC reports since 1990, said the latest iteration was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery through and disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D and demanded a strong response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what will be required for people to get it, but my hope is that it will galvanize everyone in Glasgow to meet their agreements,\u8221\'20\'1D she added in reference to \uc2 UN\uc2  climate talks between world leaders in October.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/10/un-climate-report-joe-biden-us-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN climate report raises pressure on Biden to seize a rare moment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2 , who was also part of the initial bipartisan group that negotiated over the infrastructure bill, said he now opposes the legislation as well.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the infrastructure bill: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NEvcFvHiZx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NEvcFvHiZx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2  (@SenatorRounds) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorRounds/status/1425087121044484105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Rounds noted he will not be present for today\u8217\'20\'19s vote, as he is traveling to the Mayo Clinic with his wife as she receives cancer treatments.\par \par \uc2 But the South Dakota Republican said he would vote against the bill if he were in Washington today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor months, I have been working with my colleagues to negotiate bipartisan infrastructure legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Rounds said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, as this framework progressed out of our bipartisan working groups to the Senate floor, it became evident that the legislation in its final form included several progressive mandates and federal funding clawbacks that I believe go too far.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 One curious aspect of the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations over the bipartisan infrastructure bill has been how many Republicans have essentially ignored \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s criticism of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody will ever understand why [Senate minority leader] \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  allowed this non-infrastructure bill to be passed. He has given up all of his leverage for the big whopper of a bill that will follow,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement this morning.\par \par \uc2 The former president has issued similar statements in recent weeks, urging Republican senators to vote against the infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 But his demands don\u8217\'20\'19t seem to be having much of an impact, as the bill is expected to pass with the support of roughly 20 Republican senators.\par \par \uc2 However, some Senate Republicans are clearly a bit more wary of going against Trump to support the bill. Senators \uc2 Jerry Moran\uc2  and \uc2 Todd Young\uc2 , who are both up for reelection next year, have announced they will oppose the bill, even though they supported the initial framework for the legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  praised the bipartisan infrastructure bill as a historic piece of legislation that will help America strengthen its roads, bridges and broadband access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a big day,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s looking good. What we see in today\u8217\'20\'19s bitterly divided Washington is Republicans and Democrats coming together with the president to say, \u8216\'20\'18We need to do this.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"There are more steps to go, but very encouraged by the dynamics here and, of course, looking forward to seeing that officially clear the floor," Transportation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretaryPete?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecretaryPete}}}\uc2  Buttigieg says about the infrastructure bill. "This is good policy and it's good funding." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2ve3YK2khS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2ve3YK2khS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 New Day (@NewDay) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewDay/status/1425063126622478348?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 CNN anchor John Berman asked Buttigieg about what he would say to progressive Democrats in the House who have indicated they will only vote for the bill if they receive assurances about the future passage of the $3.5tn reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is good policy, and it\u8217\'20\'19s good funding,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg replied. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about here represents the most significant infrastructure funding that we\u8217\'20\'19ve done in my lifetime, and then some.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg noted that the Biden administration strongly supports the reconciliation package as well, but he added, \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill, if you just look at it, is going to do a lot for this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate expected to pass bipartisan infrastructure bill this morning\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is expected to hold its final vote on the bipartisan infrastructure bill this morning, and the legislation will likely pass with support from members of both parties.\par \par \uc2 The final vote comes after months of negotiating over the bill, which would invest $550bn in new federal funds in roads, bridges and other physical infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already endorsed the bill, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant long-term investment in our infrastructure and competitiveness in nearly a century\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The exterior of the US Capitol is seen as Senate works to advance the bipartisan infrastructure bill. Photograph: Sarah Silbiger/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 However, the bill still faces a long road to passage in the House, where Democrats have just a three-seat majority.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , has indicated she does not want to hold a vote on the bipartisan bill until the chamber can also take up the $3.5tn reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats released their blueprint for the reconciliation bill yesterday, but much work remains to be done on the massive spending package.\par \par \uc2 So although the bipartisan infrastructure bill will likely clear a key hurdle this morning, there are more challenges ahead before the legislation can actually become law.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210810eh8a001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
