\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Federal judge blocks Arkansas law banning nearly all abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang and agencies \par \uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2021\par 14:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law, which was set to take effect on Friday, was approved by Republican-led legislature and signed by \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\par \par \uc2 A federal judge on Tuesday blocked a law passed in Arkansas that would ban nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 The law, which was set to take effect on Friday, had been approved by Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-led legislature and signed by the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, US district judge Kristine Baker issued a preliminary injunction, temporarily halting the law in its tracks, in a win for pro-choice supporters, while a lawsuit against its constitutionality proceeds.\par \par \uc2 The law would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arkleg.state.ar.us/Bills/Detail?id=SB6&ddBienniumSession=2021%2F2021R&Search="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ban}}}\uc2  clinical providers from carrying out abortions \u8220\'20\'1Cexcept to save the life of a pregnant woman in a medical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D. It also does not provide exceptions for pregnancies occurring through incest or rape or involving fetal anomalies.\par \par \uc2 Violators were set to face fines up to $100,000 and as much as 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Baker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-arkansas-19e3447f0987257a24bf3639ff7dd539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  criticized}}}\uc2  the law as \u8220\'20\'1Ccategorically unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D since it would ban abortions before the fetus is considered viable.\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson, who signed the bill into law in March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/03/21/politics/arkansas-asa-hutchinson-abortion-law-supreme-court-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI signed it because it is a direct challenge to Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s landmark precedent that established a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in 1973.\par \par \uc2 Arkansas already has some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/04/2021-track-become-most-devastating-antiabortion-state-legislative-session-decades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research organization that supports reproductive rights, Arkansas has already enacted 20 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions this year, the most in a single state since a record set by Louisiana in 1978.\par \par \uc2 Baker ruled that the law meant that women in Arkansas \u8220\'20\'1Cface an imminent threat to their constitutional rights\u8221\'20\'1D and would \u8220\'20\'1Csuffer irreparable harm without injunctive relief\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  (ACLU) and Planned Parenthood, which both sued to stop the law, praised Baker\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re relieved that the court has blocked another cruel and harmful attempt to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and intrude on Arkansans\u8217\'20\'19 deeply personal medical decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D ACLU of Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Holly Dickson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-arkansas-19e3447f0987257a24bf3639ff7dd539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-arkansas-19e3447f0987257a24bf3639ff7dd539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he hoped}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  would ultimately take the case.\par \par \uc2 In May, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to take up}}}\uc2  a case from Mississippi involving the question of whether states can ban abortions before a fetus can survive outside the womb. The move could significantly alter nearly five decades of rulings on the procedure and is being called one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/17/abortion-case-supreme-court-threatens-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most consequential \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  cases}}}\uc2  since Roe because it flies in the face of precedent.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210726eh7q002y2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
