\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Mississippi urges \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn Roe v Wade in  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  case\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 652 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2021\par 14:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 State argues that constitution does not support right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Court likely to hear the case this fall and rule in spring\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  should overturn its landmark 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, instead letting states decide whether to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus can survive outside the womb, the state of Mississippi argued in papers filed on Thursday with the court.\par \par \uc2 The filing came as one reproductive rights advocate warned that she believed half of US states would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether if Roe versus Wade was overturned, as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremists gain ground}}}\uc2  and Republican-dominated state legislatures continue their work of recent years to strip back a woman\u8217\'20\'19s choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the Constitution, may a State prohibit elective abortions before viability? Yes. Why? Because nothing in constitutional text, structure, history, or tradition supports a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the Mississippi attorney general, Lynn Fitch, and four of her attorneys wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/context/mississippi-s-supreme-court-brief-dobbs-v-jackson-women-s-health-organization/d59fcfd4-b8ec-42a8-b8e1-e54755fbd4f6/?itid=lk_inline_manual_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the brief}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The arguments are a direct challenge to the central finding of the court\u8217\'20\'19s 1973 Roe versus Wade decision and its 1992 decision in a Pennsylvania \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 Both rulings said states may not put an undue burden on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before viability. The Mississippi attorneys argue that the rulings are \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi case is the first big \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights test in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jul/09/post-trump-supreme-court-appears-willing-to-embrace-judicial-activism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court reshaped}}}\uc2  with three conservative justices nominated by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A 6-3 conservative majority on the nine-strong bench, with the three Trump nominees, said in May that the court would consider arguments over a Mississippi law that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks. Justices are likely to hear the case this fall and could rule on it in the spring.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court, at the end of its first term with a 6-3 conservative majority, in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/17/us-supreme-court-obamacare-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided to uphold}}}\uc2  the Obama administration\u8217\'20\'19s Affordable Care Act, in a significant ruling. Next term, which begins in October, crucial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and gun rights cases will be before the court.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2  is president and CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights, a national reproductive rights advocacy group based in New York, which is defending Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in its challenge of the 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 She said on Thursday that half of the states are poised to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether if Roe v Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s brief reveals the extreme and regressive strategy, not just of this law, but of the avalanche of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions that are being passed across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir goal is for the supreme court to take away our right to control our own bodies and our own futures \u8211\'20\'13 not just in Mississippi, but everywhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in several states have been pushing laws designed to challenge Roe v Wade, including bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the first sign of a fetal pulse is detected, which can be as early as six weeks, before many women realize they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 A federal district judge on Tuesday blocked an Arkansas law that would ban most abortions, ruling that the law is \u8220\'20\'1Ccategorically unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D because it would ban the procedure before the fetus is considered viable.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi 15-week law was enacted in 2018, but was blocked after a federal court challenge. The state\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, remains open and offers abortions up to 16 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 More than 90% of abortions in the US take place in the first 13 weeks of pregnancy, according to federal data.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi clinic has presented evidence that viability is impossible at 15 weeks, and an appeals court said that the state \u8220\'20\'1Cconceded that it had identified no medical evidence that a fetus would be viable at 15 weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210726eh7q002xw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
