\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Most unvaccinated Americans unlikely to get shots, poll finds, as Delta spreads \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett and Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 7,310 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2021\par 00:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 16% say they will get the vaccine, according to AP pollKay Ivey says it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18time to start blaming the unvaccinated\u8217\'20\'19 for rise in casesCovid cases likely to accelerate through summer, new forecasts sayPhiladelphia health officials recommend masks in public indoor settings\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from the Guardian US politics liveblog, here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * A new poll from the Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research found that among American adults who have not yet received a vaccine, 35% say they probably will not, and 45% say they definitely will not.\par \par \uc2 * The White House faced a raft of questions about how to vaccinate more Americans. Right now, about half the total population is vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 * New York City Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  called on private employers, and particularly private hospitals, to consider mandating their employees to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 * Republican lawmakers are also under increasing pressure to encourage their base to get vaccinated, though some experts worry vaccine hesitancy may have already hardened to opposition.\par \par \uc2 * An exasperated Republican Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  said it may be time to start \u8220\'20\'1Cblaming\u8221\'20\'1D unvaccinated people for the rise in the variant.\par \par \uc2 * Finally, Mississippi filed a supreme court brief urging the nine-member bench to overturn Roe v Wade. If that happened, advocates believe half of states would move to outlaw the healthcare procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Cameras, computer modeling, drones: the higher-tech ways to fight fires\par \par \uc2 As dozens of wildfires continue to burn in across the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-science-government-and-politics-fires-environment-and-nature-1d413a10fb7d69badd6430cea4a50825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press has a new report}}}\uc2  out on the new technology that firefighters are using to fight increasingly ferocious blazes. The AP writes:\par \par \uc2 As drought- and wind-driven wildfires have become more dangerous across the American West in recent years, firefighters have tried to become smarter in how they prepare.\par \par \uc2 That includes using new fire behavior computer modeling that can help assess risks before fires start, then project their path and growth.\par \par \uc2 When \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical weather\u8221\'20\'1D is predicted \u8212\'20\'14 hot, dry winds or lightning storms \u8212\'20\'14 the technology, on top of hard-earned experience, allows California planners to pre-position fire engines, bulldozers, aircraft and hand crews armed with shovels and chain saws in areas where they can respond more quickly.\par \par \uc2 In another effort to catch fires quickly, what once were fire lookout towers staffed by humans have largely been replaced with cameras in remote areas, many of them in high-definition and armed with artificial intelligence to discern a smoke plume from morning fog. There are 800 such cameras scattered across California, Nevada and Oregon, and even casual viewers can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.alertwildfire.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remotely watch}}}\uc2  wildfires in real time.\par \par \uc2 Fire managers also routinely summon military drones from the National Guard or Air Force to fly over fires at night, using heat imaging to map their boundaries and hot spots. They can use satellite imagery to plot the course of smoke and ash.\par \par \uc2 On the topic of old-school firefighting technology, our wildfires correspondent Gabrielle \uc2 Canon\uc2  recently spent some time in one of those aforementioned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/03/wildfire-lookout-california-mt-tamalpais"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lookout towers}}}\uc2 . The one she visited is in Marin county, in northern California, and was built almost 100 years ago. Volunteers still spend long hours there, gazing out, looking for a telltale spark.\par \par \uc2 Check out that feature below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/03/wildfire-lookout-california-mt-tamalpais"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wildfire watchmen: the mountain tower where lookouts spot blazes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, my colleague Jewel Wicker covered a new report from the Brennan Center for Justice that found at least 18 states in the US have enacted laws that restrict voting access. The study describes the onslaught as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most aggressive in more than a decade of tracking state voting laws\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The report comes after Republicans in the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/22/voting-rights-bill-joe-biden-senate-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the For the People Act,}}}\uc2  a major bill that would have shored up voting rights, and Democratic lawmakers in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/16/texas-democrats-jolted-voting-rights-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staged a high profile walkout}}}\uc2  from the state legislature in an effort to thwart new voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 At a vigil for lawmaker and civil rights activist John Lewis, attendees urge passage of the For the People Act. Photograph: Alex Wong/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Wicker writes:\par \par \uc2 The report found that the 30 laws that have been passed since 1 January \u8220\'20\'1Cmake mail voting and early voting more difficult, impose harsher voter ID requirements, and make faulty voter [roll] purges more likely, among other things\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The laws were among the more than 400 bills introduced in 49 states during this year\u8217\'20\'19s legislative session that would make voting more difficult.\par \par \uc2 Such proliferating and restrictive legislation contrasted sharply, however, with the report\u8217\'20\'19s finding that no states produced evidence of widespread fraud in the 2020 elections, despite continued claims by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , backed by numerous Republican leaders, that he was not beaten by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the race to the White House.\par \par \uc2 In fact, officials at local, state and national level declared last November\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/13/us-election-most-secure-history-voter-fraud-false-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most secure election}}}\uc2  in US history, while Trump fought in vain through the courts to overturn the result.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/23/us-voting-rights-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and check out all of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-fight-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting rights coverage here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/23/us-voting-rights-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting curbs enacted in 18 US states this year despite none finding widespread fraud}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , delivered an update today on US efforts to share its Covid vaccine doses with other countries around the world. The news comes as domestic vaccination rates stagnate and the White House ramps up its efforts to fight vaccine hesitancy.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  says the United States has shipped 22 million doses of the coronavirus vaccine to other countries this week.\par \par \uc2 The total was a weekly record as vaccines went to 23 countries. Psaki says the recipients included Pakistan, Vietnam, Guatemala, Panama, Senegal, Cameroon and Morocco, among other nations. By this weekend, roughly 80 million doses in total will have shipped from the United States to other countries.\par \par \uc2 Psaki stressed at Friday\u8217\'20\'19s White House news briefing that the United States is \u8220\'20\'1Cdonating more to the world than any other country.\u8221\'20\'1D Still, there is a global vaccine gap between wealthier nations and poorer ones, a reflection of the economic might of American and European countries as well as the pressure to address the needs of domestic populations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amid growing concerns about rising Covid-19 cases across the US, reporter Erin McCormick took a closer look at one state experiencing an alarming spike: California.\par \par \uc2 The Golden State has had some of the strictest lockdowns during the pandemic, and now has some of the highest vaccination rates. But just over a month after the governor lifted the last of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Covid restrictions, case numbers are climbing, and some counties are bringing back mask mandates.\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles is now requiring masks to be worn indoors again, even for those who have been fully vaccinated. Photograph: Mario Anzuoni/Reuters\par \par \uc2 She writes:\par \par \uc2 In Los Angeles, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://publichealth.lacounty.gov/phcommon/public/media/mediapubhpdetail.cfm?prid=3250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 county figures show}}}\uc2  that Covid-19 infections have increased twentyfold in a month. In San Francisco, they\u8217\'20\'19ve almost tripled in two weeks and, overall, California\u8217\'20\'19s hospitalization numbers have increased by 58%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/us/covid-cases.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to New York Times data.}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite the fact that California is one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s most vaccinated states, experts blame the highly contagious Delta variant for a new surge that has disrupted businesses\u8217\'20\'19 and politicians\u8217\'20\'19 plans to celebrate the state\u8217\'20\'19s reopening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPrimarily we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing infections in the unvaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 George Rutherford\uc2 , an epidemiologist at the University of California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/san-francisco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Francisco}}}\uc2 , citing earlier statistics from Los Angeles which found 99.6% of new cases there were in the unvaccinated. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the Delta variant\u8217\'20\'19s extra strength.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2020/us/covid-19-vaccine-doses.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times figures}}}\uc2  showing nearly 77% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s adults having gotten at least one shot of vaccine, that leaves plenty of unprotected people to transmit the virus, Rutherford said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/22/california-covid-cases-mask-requirements"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/22/california-covid-cases-mask-requirements"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California sees a sharp increase in Covid cases and a return to mask mandates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 After arrest in Los Angeles, Trump inauguration chair ordered freed on $250m bail\par \par \uc2 The chair of the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inaugural committee was ordered freed Friday on $250m bail to face charges he secretly worked as an agent for the the United Arab Emirates to influence Trump\u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy, the Associated Press reports.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/elections-north-america-donald-trump-ap-top-news-paul-manafort-6dd33b4234634079821e5825f112e85b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tom Barrack, 74, }}}\uc2  will be subject to electronic monitoring and largely confined to his residence after he is arraigned Monday in a New York courtroom. He was arrested Tuesday in Los Angeles near his home.\par \par \uc2 Barrack is expected to plead not guilty to conspiring to influence US policy on the UAE\u8217\'20\'19s behalf during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 campaign and while Trump was president. Barrack, the founder of private equity firm \uc2 Colony Capital\uc2 , was among three men charged in the case.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors said Barrack used his long personal friendship with Trump to benefit the UAE without disclosing his ties to the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrLongtime Trump associate \uc2 Tom Barrack\uc2 , who was indicted on charges of illegal foreign lobbying, has been freed on $250 million bail {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nEJjEfb3eU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nEJjEfb3eU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CNN Breaking News (@cnnbrk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cnnbrk/status/1418647035507625984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fact-checking claims about HIPAA and vaccination status\par \par \uc2 As various public figures invoke a federal medical records privacy law to explain why they will not comment if they have received the Coronavirus vaccine, journalists are providing a fact-check about why that claim...just does not make sense!\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is not, dear reader, HIPAA -- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aznpzk6XFf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aznpzk6XFf}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KCqgYs6XFf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KCqgYs6XFf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 city nolan (get your ??!!!) (@ndhapple) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ndhapple/status/1418674156732833794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Aishvarya Kavi\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/hipaa-law.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 succinct HIPAA explainer}}}\uc2  is worth a read.\par \par \uc2 enltrNo, HIPAA doesn't make it illegal to ask someone if they've been vaccinated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oypbFt6Awo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/oypbFt6Awo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aishvarya Kavi (@AishvaryaKavi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AishvaryaKavi/status/1418363931781894150?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll: 45% of Americans without Covid vaccine say they \u8216\'20\'18definitely\u8217\'20\'19 wont get it\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live US politics coverage from our Los Angeles office.\par \par \uc2 Most Americans who haven\u8217\'20\'19t been vaccinated against COVID-19 say they are unlikely to get the shots and doubt they would work against the aggressive delta variant despite evidence they do, according to a new poll that underscores the challenges facing public health officials amid soaring infections in some states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-science-health-government-and-politics-coronavirus-pandemic-36ea18ee3a3397da7edd5b8249f0e477"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among American adults who have not yet received a vaccine, 35% say they probably will not, and 45% say they definitely will not, according to a poll from The Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research. Just 3% say they definitely will get the shots, though another 16% say they probably will.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more, 64% of unvaccinated Americans have little to no confidence the shots are effective against variants \u8212\'20\'14 including the delta variant that officials say is responsible for 83% of new cases in the U.S. \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/europe-coronavirus-vaccine-health-coronavirus-pandemic-lifestyle-f7a991223769d8c98d3fc1d03968f560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite evidence that they offer strong protection}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House faced questions on Covid-19, mayors push for vaccine and mask mandates\par \par \uc2 Today had a front and center focus on Covid-19, as cases attributed to the contagiousness of the Delta variant rise across the south and midwest.\par \par \uc2 * The White House faced a raft of questions about how to vaccinate more Americans. Right now, about half the total population is vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 * New York City Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  called on private employers, and particularly private hospitals, to consider mandating their employees to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 * Republican lawmakers are also under increasing pressure to encourage their base to get vaccinated, though some experts worry vaccine hesitancy may have already hardened to opposition.\par \par \uc2 * An exasperated Republican Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  said it may be time to start \u8220\'20\'1Cblaming\u8221\'20\'1D unvaccinated people for the rise in the variant.\par \par \uc2 * Finally, Mississippi filed a supreme court brief urging the nine-member bench to overturn Roe v Wade. If that happened, advocates believe half of states would move to outlaw the healthcare procedure.\par \par \uc2 A man wears an American flag face mask on a street in Hollywood, California, after the indoor mask mandate returned to Los Angeles. With the Delta variant pushing US Covid cases back up, fully vaccinated people are wondering whether they need to start masking indoors again. Covid vaccines remain extremely effective against hospitalization and death. Photograph: Robyn Beck/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s go back to Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s surprising brief to the supreme court, in which it argued the nine-member bench should overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade, decided in 1973, is a landmark decision that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point a fetus can survive outside the womb. That point is widely regarded as roughly 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 In October, the court will consider a Mississippi law that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks. Even taking up the case has signaled the court, which leans conservative, could intend to reconsider foundational aspects of the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jul/23/abortion-us-supreme-court-mississippi-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi urges US supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade in \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the Constitution, may a State prohibit elective abortions before viability? Yes. Why? Because nothing in constitutional text, structure, history, or tradition supports a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the Mississippi attorney general, Lynn Fitch, and four of her attorneys wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/context/mississippi-s-supreme-court-brief-dobbs-v-jackson-women-s-health-organization/d59fcfd4-b8ec-42a8-b8e1-e54755fbd4f6/?itid=lk_inline_manual_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the brief}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That push to invalidate Roe, and move \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the states, was one reproductive rights advocates said they had been warning about for years. If the justices overturn Roe, reproductive rights advocates expect almost half the states to immediately outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s brief reveals the extreme and regressive strategy, not just of this law, but of the avalanche of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions that are being passed across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights, which is arguing the case before the court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir goal is for the supreme court to take away our right to control our own bodies and our own futures \u8211\'20\'13 not just in Mississippi, but everywhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most women of reproductive age live in states that are hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a common health procedure, most often performed very early in pregnancy. Nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2017/abortion-common-experience-us-women-despite-dramatic-declines-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one-in-four women}}}\uc2  who live in the US will have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by age 45.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we saw in the White House press briefing, one of the most closely watched statistics in the last few days is the number of vaccinations distributed daily.\par \par \uc2 There is some anecdotal evidence to suggest that the increase in cases attributed to the Delta variant may encourage people to get vaccinated. The hope, as this tweet shows, is that we could begin to see a slight increase in daily vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe number of people getting the first dose of a COVID-19 vaccine is no longer decreasing and may even be showing signs of increasing slightly, in the face of growing cases, hospitalizations, and deaths. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W0SXWcSdRN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/W0SXWcSdRN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WvIqPGvxdw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WvIqPGvxdw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Larry Levitt (@larry_levitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/larry_levitt/status/1418657764310540292?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor calls on employers to "mandate" vaccines\par \par \uc2 In other \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  news, the mayor is urging private city employers to require their employees to get a Covid-19 vaccination.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the de Blasio administration announced workers at the city\u8217\'20\'19s public hospitals would need to get vaccinated or get a weekly Covid-19 PCR test. This takes the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s urging one step further, after he said he felt the city had done everything possible in \u8220\'20\'1Cpurely voluntary\u8221\'20\'1D terms.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m calling upon all New York City employers, including our private hospitals, to move immediately to some form of mandate,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 de Blasio{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wnyc.org/story/ask-mayor-0722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on WNYC}}}\uc2 ... Whatever the maximum you feel you can do, any form of mandate, including the type we\u8217\'20\'19re doing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The mayor said he was frustrated in particular that New Yorkers, who are eligible to be vaccinated in their homes as part of the distribution drive, had not had better uptake.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s time for more mandates,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 People wear masks around Times Square, as cases of the infectious coronavirus Delta variant continue to rise in New York City. Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t have to testify in a judicial inquiry into the 2014 police chokehold death of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/21/eric-garner-police-chokehold-firing-pantaleo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Garner}}}\uc2 , a judge ruled today, dashing a long-running quest by Garner\u8217\'20\'19s relatives to have the mayor questioned under oath.\par \par \uc2 Memorial for Eric Garner in Staten Island, New York\par \par \uc2 People attend a memorial event for Eric Garner, who was killed by New York City police in 2014, in Staten Island, New York, U.S., July 17, 2021. Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Garner\u8217\'20\'19s death, on 17 July 2014, became a focal point for national conversations on race and policing. Garner\u8217\'20\'19s last words, \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t breathe\u8221\'20\'1D, were chanted by protesters across the US, and echoed in many protests in the years since.\par \par \uc2 They were also among the last words of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2  when he was murdered by then-police officer Derek Chauvin in 2020.\par \par \uc2 The police officer implicated in Garner\u8217\'20\'19s death was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jul/16/eric-garner-death-new-york-no-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never charged}}}\uc2  with a crime. Supporters and relatives of Garner have fought a prolonged battle for full accountability for Garner\u8217\'20\'19s killing.\par \par \uc2 The officer, Daniel Pantaleo, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/19/eric-garner-daniel-pantaleo-nypd-officer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was fired}}}\uc2  in 2019.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Associated Press reported that in addition to \uc2 De Blasio\uc2  being excused:\par \par \uc2 Judge Erika Edwards also excused Police Commissioner \uc2 Dermot Shea\uc2 , the city\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical examiner and other high-ranking current and former city officials from testifying, ruling that other witnesses have more direct knowledge of the case.\par \par \uc2 Edwards ordered 13 witnesses to testify in the inquiry, scheduled to start Oct. 25, including the \uc2 NYPD\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief spokesperson, the head of its internal affairs unit and the president of the police officers union.\par \par \uc2 Four officers and four sergeants who were involved in Garner\u8217\'20\'19s arrest were also ordered to testify, but not the officer who placed Garner in the chokehold, Daniel Pantaleo. The \uc2 NYPD\uc2  fired him in 2019 after a department disciplinary trial.\par \par \uc2 Garner\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Gwen Carr, and sister, Ellisha Flagg Garner, allege that \uc2 de Blasio\uc2  and other city officials neglected their duties in their handling of Garner\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 Carr said in a statement Friday that she was disappointed that \uc2 de Blasio\uc2  and Shea won\u8217\'20\'19t have to testify, but heartened that the judge is forcing the city to turn over troves of previously undisclosed documents related to his July 17, 2014, death.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been seven years since Eric was murdered, and in spite of what Mayor \uc2 de Blasio\uc2  has said to me personally or to New Yorkers, he and other top city officials are still blocking transparency but now the court has ordered them to finally turn over information,\u8221\'20\'1D Carr said.\par \par \uc2 The Garner inquiry is focused on several main issues, including the factors leading to his stop, arrest and the use of force, whether officers lied on official documents, the leak of Garner\u8217\'20\'19s arrest history and medical conditions, and allegations that officers failed to provide Garner with medical care.\par \par \uc2 The city sought to cancel the judicial inquiry, but a state appeals court ruled last week that Garner\u8217\'20\'19s death was the \u8220\'20\'1Crare case in which allegations of significant violations of duty\u8221\'20\'1D warranted such a review.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to nominate Caroline Kennedy, daughter of the late president \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2 , as the American ambassador to Australia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/23/politics/biden-caroline-kennedy-australia/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2  this afternoon, citing three unidentified people familiar with the process.\par \par \uc2 Caroline Kennedy presents the 2017 Profile in Courage Award to former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  during a ceremony at the John F. Kennedy Library in Boston, Massachusetts, May 2017. Photograph: Brian Snyder/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The White House did not immediately return a request for comment on the report.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy threw her support behind Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential campaign in February of that year, writing that the former vice president was more prepared for the job than his rivals.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy previously served as US ambassador to Japan under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first female US ambassador to Japan, Kennedy was an early and prominent supporter of Obama in his initial quest for the presidency in 2008, and also campaigned for him.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports:\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s appointment to Australia reflects the high priority the Biden administration is placing on the Asia-Pacific as it deals with an increasingly assertive China in the region and on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 The US and Australia share close trade ties and a robust military relationship, fighting side by side in every major conflict since World War I.\par \par \uc2 The two countries are also members of the \u8220\'20\'1CFive Eyes alliance,\u8221\'20\'1D an intelligence sharing arrangement between the English speaking democracies of the US, Australia, Canada, New Zealand and the UK.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, Kennedy would come to the job with prior experience specific to the region. A graduate of \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  Law School, Kennedy served as ambassador to Japan from 2013 to 2017 as an Obama administration appointee.\par \par \uc2 In Tokyo, Kennedy worked on military and trade, among other issues, and became the second US ambassador to attend an annual memorial service marking the US atomic bombing of Hiroshima.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s billionaire ally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/may/29/close-friend-trump-thomas-barrack-alleged-tax-evasion-italy-sardinia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas Barrack}}}\uc2  has reached a deal with prosecutors that will allow for his release from custody while he awaits trial on federal charges including illegal foreign lobbying, a prosecutor said during a court hearing today.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Barrack\uc2 . Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Barrack played a leading role in the Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential inauguration events in 2017 and was arrested in California earlier this week on charges of acting as an unregistered agent of a foreign government, specifically the United Arab Emirates.\par \par \uc2 A seven-count indictment was unveiled in federal court after an announcement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/former-advisor-presidential-candidate-among-three-defendants-charged-acting-agents-foreign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Department of Justice,}}}\uc2  which also charged Barrack, 74, with obstruction of justice and making multiple false statements during a June 20, 2019, interview with federal law enforcement agents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Questions to White House about the push to get more Americans vaccinated\par \par \uc2 This press conference was really an ongoing series of questions about Covid, how to get more people vaccinated, and about an increase in cases in low-vaccination states.\par \par \uc2 Psaki has just gotten a question about how to coordinate with Republican governors who have criticized the administration strategy to combat Covid, including with vaccines.\par \par \uc2 She said the reasons people might not have been vaccinated range from \u8220\'20\'1Cmisinformation, some of it is fear, some of it is time, some of it is they are young and they may feel they are Superman or Superwoman,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur objective to communicate to people this is not a political issue, the virus does not discriminate between political party affiliation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki. \u8220\'20\'1CWe rely on and we\u8217\'20\'19re funding and empowering local trusted voices who aren\u8217\'20\'19t seen through a political prism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  speaks at a press briefing at the White House in Washington, Friday, 23 July 2021. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now we\u8217\'20\'19re onto another question about the Covid-19 forecasting we mentioned earlier, with the potential for an October peak in new cases. Psaki said encouraging vaccination is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most powerful role he can play\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even more on vaccinations here \u8211\'20\'13 Psaki is asked how to get more people vaccinated amid the frustration expressed by Republican Alabama Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe always knew it would be harder as more people got vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the stage we\u8217\'20\'19re in now, but we also believe there is still opportunity... to get more people vaccinated there are a range of factors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Factors contributing to more people getting vaccinate might be the role of the Delta variant, \u8220\'20\'1Cfears of the transmissibility of the Delta variant, family members who are getting sick and getting hospitalized,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki.\par \par \uc2 Psaki also confirmed the purchase of another 200 million \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made that purchase,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki. \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line, we\u8217\'20\'19ve always prepared for every scenario\u8221\'20\'1D. Those vaccines are to be delivered in the fall 2021 and spring 2022, and would potentially be used for either booster shots or vaccinations for children younger than 12.\par \par \uc2 Currently, children younger than 12 are not eligible for Covid-19 vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 In another Covid question, Psaki is asked whether more testing would help reduce Covid transmission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The president] relies on the guidance of his health and medical experts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today, Mississippi filed paperwork with the Supreme Court asking it to overturn a decision that provided Americans with the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point a fetus can live outside the womb.\par \par \uc2 That decision, called Roe v Wade, is under threat from a Mississippi law before the court.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are supporters, the president is a supporter, of preserving Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a filing, Mississippi said Roe v Wade and decision that flow from it are, \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/07/23/1019746478/on-abortion-mississippi-swings-for-the-fences-asks-the-supreme-court-to-reverse-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR reported}}}\uc2 , and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe conclusion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a constitutional right has no basis in text, structure, history or tradition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now, we have a question about whether the president is safe while traveling the country.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said federal Covid-19 guidelines say, \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re vaccinated you\u8217\'20\'19re very much protected from severe illness from the virus, and the president will continue to be a model in following those guidelines\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the federal government should take a harsher tone with unvaccinated people, citing Republican Alabama Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments about people who have not yet been vaccinated, Psaki said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think our role is to place blame, what we can do is release accurate information,\u8221\'20\'1D said Psaki.\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re a young person, you may think you\u8217\'20\'19re superman or super woman and immune from getting the virus \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s not true, that is not accurate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Psaki also said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe understand her frustration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here we go \u8211\'20\'13 at the top Psaki said the Biden-Harris administration has \u8220\'20\'1Cshipped a record number of doses to a record number of countries,\u8221\'20\'1D including 22 million doses to 23 countries including many African and Latin American countries.\par \par \uc2 And the first question is about Covid-19, vaccine hesitancy, and that AP poll we just mentioned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue our efforts to go community by community, case by case to convey the accurate information about the efficacy of vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  speaks at a press briefing in the White House Press Briefing Room. Photograph: Michael Brochstein/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll shows challenge of convincing people to get vaccinated\par \par \uc2 A new poll from the Associated Press underscores the challenges public health officials face in trying to get people vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 The poll shows most Americans who haven\u8217\'20\'19t been vaccinated against the coronavirus say they are unlikely to get the shots. About 16% say they probably will get the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Most also doubt they would work against the aggressive delta variant, despite evidence they do. Those findings underscore the challenges facing public health officials as soaring infections in some states threaten to overwhelm hospitals.\par \par \uc2 The poll conducted by The Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research found 35% of adults who have not yet received a vaccine say they probably will not, and 45% say they definitely will not.\par \par \uc2 That means \u8220\'20\'1Cthat there will be more preventable cases, more preventable hospitalizations and more preventable deaths,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dr. Amesh Adalja\uc2 , an infectious disease specialist at Johns Hopkins University.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s daily briefing is expected to start any minute. Here a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a9Ae_BmS8yE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestream of the briefing}}}\uc2  to follow along.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Long-range Covid forecast predicts peak in October\par \par \uc2 Ahead of White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s briefing, expected just at 12:30pm ET, let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the latest long-range coronavirus forecasts released by the Covid-19 Scenario Modeling Hub.\par \par \uc2 These models pull together multiple mathematical projections on detailing how the coronavirus might spread. On Thursday, they released a new data. The forecasts are, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2021/07/22/1019475669/delta-variant-will-drive-a-steep-rise-in-covid-deaths-model-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR rightly put it, deflating}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s going on in the country with the virus is matching our most pessimistic scenarios,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sph.unc.edu/adv_profile/justin-lessler-phd/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Lessler}}}\uc2 , an epidemiologist at the University of North Carolina who helps run the modeling hub, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2021/07/22/1019475669/delta-variant-will-drive-a-steep-rise-in-covid-deaths-model-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe might be seeing synergistic effects of people becoming less cautious in addition to the impacts of the delta variant.\par \par \uc2 In the most likely scenario, the Delta variant is 60% more transmissible than earlier strains of Covid-19, and 70% of the American public is vaccinated. Should that be the case, scientists expect Covid-19 cases to peak in October, with roughly 60,000 new cases per day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2021/07/22/1019475669/delta-variant-will-drive-a-steep-rise-in-covid-deaths-model-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to NPR}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a point of comparison, during the peak of the pandemic in winter 2021, about 250,000 people per day were diagnosed with Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 enltrListen to the latest episode of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 's Politics Weekly Extra podcast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamTLevin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SamTLevin}}}\uc2  gives details on the anti-trans bills being pushed by Republican legislators across the country, and we hear from one of the trans kids affected by those proposals. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tTYgFZfkos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tTYgFZfkos}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1418597514203258882?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dr Peter Hotez\uc2 , a vaccine researcher and the dean of the national school of tropical medicine at Baylor University, is one of the loudest proponents of vaccination in the US.\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/health/article/Dr-Peter-Hotez-Delta-variant-like-nothing-16332812.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Houston Chronicle}}}\uc2 , he again urged people to get vaccinated. In Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/us-vaccine-distribution-tracker-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 43% of the total population}}}\uc2  is fully vaccinated, below the national average of 49%.\par \par \uc2 When you\u8217\'20\'19ve got this as the dominant variant, if you\u8217\'20\'19re unvaccinated and you\u8217\'20\'19ve been lucky enough not to get COVID so far, you have to recognize there\u8217\'20\'19s a good chance your luck\u8217\'20\'19s about to run out, and you will likely get get COVID. You should get vaccinated yesterday, right? This is not the time to wait, because the spread of delta is accelerating very quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Health authorities in Philadelphia are strongly recommending everyone \u8211\'20\'13 including vaccinated people \u8211\'20\'13 wear masks in public, indoor settings. The recommendation came after health authorities saw a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/philly-issues-new-face-mask-recommendations-amid-rise-in-covid-cases-child-hospitalizations/?utm_campaign=sproutsocial&utm_content=1626978281&utm_medium=post&utm_source=facebook,twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 small but disturbing}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D increase in hospitalizations among children, according to radio station WHYY.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKids under 12 cannot yet be vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D said acting health commissioner Dr Cheryl Bettigole, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need you to step up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) guidance says vaccinated people do not need to mask because they are at low risk of transmitting or contracting Covid-19, but recommends people who are immune-compromised or have underlying health conditions continue to mask.\par \par \uc2 The CDC\u8217\'20\'19s guidelines, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/daily-life-coping/participate-in-activities.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found here}}}\uc2 , have been the subject of intense criticism as local health authorities chart the rise of Covid-19 cases associated with the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 A supervisor at a Philadelphia summer camp opens the door to Ferko playground. An outbreak of Covid-19 has forced Philadelphia summer camps to operate at limited capacity. Photograph: Hannah Beier/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Tokyo Olympics opening ceremony comes to an end, First Lady Jill Biden cheers from the stands. On Saturday, she is expected to attend the USA v France women\u8217\'20\'19s 3x3 basketball game and the USA v Nw Zealand women\u8217\'20\'19s soccer game.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  stands to cheer as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TeamUSA?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TeamUSA}}}\uc2  enters the arena. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XM0xiSzqxb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XM0xiSzqxb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Bennett (@KateBennett_DC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateBennett_DC/status/1418564786510467072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst Lady {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DrBiden}}}\uc2  will attend the following Olympic events in Tokyo on Saturday, per the White House:\par \par \uc2 - USA v France women's 3x3 basketball game\par \par \uc2 - Various swimming races\par \par \uc2 - USA v New Zealand women's soccer game\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Monica Alba (@albamonica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/albamonica/status/1418589321431498753?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The bust of a man who was a Confederate general, Ku Klux Klan leader and slave trader was removed from the Tennessee state capitol this morning, a year after the governor said it was high time it was gone.\par \par \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  had been immortalized at the Tennessee capitol in Nashville since the late 1970s.\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: Crews are starting the process of removing the \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  bust from the capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WKRN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WKRN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GMN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GMN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8HwOG3zsoY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8HwOG3zsoY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Palazzo WKRN (@JuliaPalazzoTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaPalazzoTV/status/1418554095602970625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Tennessean{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tennessean.com/story/news/politics/2021/07/22/tennessees-nathan-bedford-forrest-bust-come-down-after-vote/8042280002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The State Building Commission on Thursday gave approval for the relocation of the Forrest bust to the Tennessee State Museum, a final step in a process that has taken more than a year since Gov. Bill Lee first said it was time for the statue to be moved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a year long journey, and this is an appropriate step in that process,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee said prior to the Building Commission meeting Thursday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s most important to me that we followed the process. We talked about that from the very beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Members of the legislative Black Caucus gathered outside the hearing room, and then by the bust, after the vote to celebrate.\par \par \uc2 The Tennessee lieutenant governor Randy McNally, who is also the state senate speaker, had voted against the removal of the bust of Forrest and accused the left of demanding that people \u8220\'20\'1Ckneel at the altar of political correctness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 State Representative London Lamar, left, sings with activist Justin Jones in front of the \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  bust in the Tennessee State Capitol yesterday. Jones led protests over the summer of 2020 to have the bust removed and this followed decades-long efforts to remove the bust of the Confederate general and early \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  leader. Photograph: George Walker IV/AP\par \par \uc2 Wheeled away.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe bust of Confederate Gen. and KKK leader \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  is off its pedestal and being wheeled out of the Tennessee Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dgAg4isvxw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dgAg4isvxw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natalie Allison (@natalie_allison) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/natalie_allison/status/1418558930834366464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers are under increasing pressure to tell their constituents Covid-19 vaccines are safe and effective amid spread of the new, more contagious Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 vaccines are highly effective against the Delta variant, and remain the single most tool available to prevent infection with the highly contagious disease.\par \par \uc2 However, more than a year of mixed messages and misinformation have experts worried Republican\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 vaccine messages will be, at best, muddled, and that skepticism has hardened among the Republican base.Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 In recent news conferences and statements, some prominent Republicans have been imploring their constituents to lay lingering doubts aside. In Washington, the so-called Doctors Caucus gathered at the Capitol for an event to combat vaccine hesitancy. And in Florida, Republican \uc2 Gov. Ron DeSantis\uc2  this week pointed to data showing the vast majority of hospitalized Covid-19 patients hadn\u8217\'20\'19t received shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese vaccines are saving lives,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis, who recently began selling campaign merchandise mocking masks and medical experts.\par \par \uc2 The outreach comes as Covid-19 cases have nearly tripled in the US over the last two weeks, driven by the explosion of the new delta variant, especially in pockets of the country where vaccination rates are low. Public health officials believe the variant is at least twice as contagious as the original version, but the shots appear to offer robust protection against serious illness for most people.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, nearly all Covid-19 deaths in the U.S. are now people who haven\u8217\'20\'19t been vaccinated. Nonetheless, just 56.2% of Americans have received at least one vaccine dose, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Overall, only 51% of Republicans said in mid-June that they had received at least one vaccine dose, versus 83% of Democrats, according to an AP-NORC poll. And many appeared to have made up their minds. Forty-six percent of those who had not been vaccinated said they definitely would not. Among Republicans, even more 53% said they definitely wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t; just 12% said they were planning to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think they\u8217\'20\'19ve finally realized that if their people aren\u8217\'20\'19t vaccinated, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get sick, and if their people aren\u8217\'20\'19t vaccinated, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get blamed for Covid outbreaks in the future,\u8221\'20\'1D said GOP pollster Frank Luntz, who has been working with the Biden administration and public health experts to craft effective messaging to bring the vaccine hesitant off the fence.\par \par \uc2 But Luntz, who conducted another focus group Wednesday evening with vaccine holdouts, said there has been a discernible shift in recent weeks as skepticism has calcified into hardened refusal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe hesitation has transformed into opposition. And once you are opposed, it is very hard to change that position. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 For months now, many conservative lawmakers and pundits have been actively stoking vaccine hesitancy, refusing to take the shots themselves or downplaying the severity of the virus. Republican governors have signed bills protecting the unvaccinated from having to disclose their status and tried to roll back mask mandates. And on social media, disinformation has run rampant, leading President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to claim platforms like \uc2 Facebook\uc2  were \u8220\'20\'1Ckilling people\u8221\'20\'1D a claim he later walked back.\par \par \uc2 At a recent conservative gathering, attendees cheered the news that the Biden administration was falling short of its vaccination goals. Invoking the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious-disease expert, \uc2 Dr. Anthony Fauci\uc2 , \uc2 Rep. Lauren Boebert\uc2 , R-Colo., warned, the government: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t come knocking on my door with your Fauci Ouchie! You leave us the hell alone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 But there were signs that messaging was changing this week, as conservative leaders advocated for the shots. On Fox News, host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  implored his viewers to \u8220\'20\'1Cplease take Covid seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D saying, \u8220\'20\'1CEnough people have died.\u8221\'20\'1D Iowa Sen. Chuck Grassley on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  encouraged \u8220\'20\'1CALL eligible Iowans/Americans to get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Delta variant scares me so I hope those that haven\u8217\'20\'19t been vaccinated will reconsider,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Rep. Steve Scalise, the House Republican whip, distributed pictures of himself receiving his first dose of the vaccine last weekend after months of holding out.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , a polio survivor who has consistently advocated on behalf of the COVID-19 shots, this week urged the unvaccinated to ignore \u8220\'20\'1Call these other voices that are giving demonstrably bad advice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the news conference convened by House GOP leaders on Thursday highlighted Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 competing messages on the virus.\par \par \uc2 Initially billed as an event where Republican doctors in Congress would address the rapidly spreading delta variant, the group instead spent most of its time railing against China and making unverified claims that the coronavirus came from a lab leak in Wuhan, a theory initially popular in far-right circles but now being seriously considered by scientists. They also attacked Democrats, including House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and the Biden administration, for not doing more to get to the bottom of the lab leak theory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is, Why are Democrats stonewalling our efforts to uncover the origins of the COVID virus?\u8221\'20\'1D said New York Rep. Elise Stefanik, the No. 3 Republican in the House.\par \par \uc2 Eric Ward, a senior fellow at the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2  who studies extremism, blamed vaccine reluctance on \u8220\'20\'1Cnearly a year-and-a-half of right-wing rage machine rhetoric.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven conservative leaders now are having a hard time figuring out how to rein in what had primarily been a propaganda campaign, and they are now realizing their constituencies are particularly vulnerable,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  has joined a growing chorus of Republicans urging people to get vaccinated. According to local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkrg.com/news/its-time-to-start-blaming-the-unvaccinated-gov-ivey-on-rise-in-covid-19-cases-low-vaccination-rate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TV station WKRG}}}\uc2 , she told a press conference Thursday:\par \par \uc2 The new cases of Covid are because of unvaccinated folks. Almost 100% of the new hospitalizations are with unvaccinated folks. And the deaths are certainly occurring with the unvaccinated folks. These folks are choosing a horrible lifestyle of self-inflicted pain,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gov. Ivey.\par \par \uc2 When asked how the state can get more shots into the arms of residents, Ivey did not hold back her displeasure with the lack of success previous plans have had.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know, you tell me. Folks are supposed to have common sense. But it\u8217\'20\'19s time to start blaming the unvaccinated folks, not the vaccinated folks. It\u8217\'20\'19s the unvaccinated folks that are letting us down,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve done all I know how to do. I can encourage you to do something but I can\u8217\'20\'19t make you take care of yourself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alabama Governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2  showed her vaccine card after she received her second Covid-19 vaccine shot at Baptist Medical Center South in Montgomery, Ala., Tuesday, 12 Jan, 2021. Photograph: Mickey Welsh/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee removes capital bust of "brutal" Confederate general and KKK leader\par \par \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s building commission has voted 5-2 to remove a bust of a confederate general with a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrutal\u8221\'20\'1D reputation from the capital building.\par \par \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  was one of the first grand wizard\u8217\'20\'19s of the KKK. During the Civil War, Bedford had a \u8220\'20\'1Creputation for killing Black soldiers after they had surrendered\u8221\'20\'1D, local news station {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newschannel5.com/news/nathan-bedford-forrest-bust-could-be-removed-from-capitol-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WTVF reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Before the bust was removed, a sign was placed at the base of the pedestal, \u8220\'20\'1CThank you to all the protesters who made this happen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: Crews are starting the process of removing the \uc2 Nathan Bedford Forrest\uc2  bust from the capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WKRN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WKRN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GMN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GMN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8HwOG3zsoY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8HwOG3zsoY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Palazzo WKRN (@JuliaPalazzoTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaPalazzoTV/status/1418554095602970625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Happy Friday, and welcome to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s politics liveblog.\par \par \uc2 Much of the world is watching the opening of the Tokyo Olympic ceremony ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2021/jul/23/tokyo-olympics-2020-games-live-opening-ceremony-build-up-time-when-how-where-to-watch-tv-japan-olympic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow live here}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 The summertime tradition, already delayed one year by the global Covid-19 pandemic, begins as Americans are increasingly warned about a rise in cases tied to the highly contagious Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) head \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2  warned Americans are in \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/22/us-covid-cases-rise-delta-variant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another pivotal moment}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in the pandemic. The most powerful tool to prevent infection \u8211\'20\'13 vaccines \u8211\'20\'13 are now at hand, but daily distribution rates have plateaued.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkrg.com/news/its-time-to-start-blaming-the-unvaccinated-gov-ivey-on-rise-in-covid-19-cases-low-vaccination-rate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Alabama governor Kay Ivey}}}\uc2  joined a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2021/07/fox-news-conservatives-vaccines-sean-hannity/619510/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing chorus}}}\uc2  of conservatives urging their base to get vaccinated. Republicans have been among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/coronavirus-covid-19/dashboard/kff-covid-19-vaccine-monitor-dashboard/?utm_source=web&utm_medium=trending&utm_campaign=COVID-19-vaccine-monitor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most vaccine resistant}}}\uc2  group in the country.\par \par \uc2 * Covid-19 forecasts released Thursday evening found new Covid-19 cases will probably accelerate through the summer and peak in October, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2021/07/22/1019475669/delta-variant-will-drive-a-steep-rise-in-covid-deaths-model-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dispiriting new projection}}}\uc2  about cases driven by the Delta variant among the unvaccinated. Reminder : vaccines are highly effective against the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210723eh7n001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
