\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Pivotal moment\u8217\'20\'19: CDC chief issues stark warning over surge in Delta Covid variant \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Daniel Strauss \par \uc2 5,668 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 July 2021\par 00:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senators say \uc2 FBI\uc2  gathered over 4,500 tips but failed to follow them upNancy Pelosi rejects Jim Jordan and Jim Banks for inquiry roleWhite House in talks with CDC about updating masking guidance\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f9d7098f08bb57f5f7ce70#block-60f9d7098f08bb57f5f7ce70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that the country is at a \u8220\'20\'1Cpivotal\u8221\'20\'1D moment in fighting the spread of Covid-19. Walensky, speaking at a briefing on Thursday, said of the Delta variant is \u8220\'20\'1Cis one of the most infectious respiratory viruses we know of and that I have seen in my 20-year career\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f9962d8f085dcd6b595b7d#block-60f9962d8f085dcd6b595b7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floated}}}\uc2  appointing congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois to the committee charged with investigating the 6 January mob attack on the Capitol. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll see\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said, adding \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s not even bipartisan; it\u8217\'20\'19s nonpartisan. It\u8217\'20\'19s about seeking the truth and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we owe the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi also said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f980ef8f085dcd6b5959dc#block-60f980ef8f085dcd6b5959dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to have congressman Jim Banks and Jim Jordan on the panel investigating the mob attack.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2#block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it would impose new sanctions on Cuban regime officials. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just the beginning \u8211\'20\'13 the United States will continue to sanction individuals responsible for oppression of the Cuban people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general urged the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong\u8221\'20\'1D. In a new brief, she asked the court to allow a controversial law that bans abortions after 15 weeks to go into effect in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Nowhere is safe\u8217\'20\'19: heat shatters vision of Pacific north-west as climate refuge\par \par \uc2 The recent heatwave that broiled the US Pacific north-west not only obliterated temperature records in cities such as Seattle and Portland \u8211\'20\'13 it also put a torch to a comforting bromide that the region would be a mild, safe haven from the ravages of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Unprecedented temperatures baked the region three weeks ago, part of a procession of heatwaves that have hit the parched US west, from Montana to southern California, over the past month. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/28/portland-seattle-heatwave-heat-dome-temperatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cheat dome\u8221\'20\'1D that settled over the area}}}\uc2  saw Seattle reach 108F (42.2C), smashing the previous record by 3F (1.7C), while Portland, Oregon, soared to its own record of 116F (46.7C). Some inland areas managed to get up to 118F (47.8C).\par \par \uc2 The conditions in a corner of the US known for its moderate, often lukewarm, summers bewildered residents.\par \par \uc2 Roads cracked and buckled in the heat, power cables melted, restaurants shut down. Hospitals suddenly found themselves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/wr/mm7029e1.htm?s_cid=mm7029e1_w&utm_campaign=Hot%20News&utm_medium=email&_hsmi=141769208&_hsenc=p2ANqtz--W5hrfaGsPG7DBBAuWjgBXdaYrBQmfDhMLKsoBgJobzxiKSzA5J07jfPlyIueHzRiQMMBwmsZ5xIW3Jh15ubpre5uKQwFPnoCE9u03RLOmfopom1I&utm_content=141769208&utm_source=hs_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmed}}}\uc2 , with several hundred people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/pacific-northwest-heatwave-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believed to have died in the heat}}}\uc2 . Slightly north, off the coast of Vancouver, an estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/jul/08/heat-dome-canada-pacific-northwest-animal-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1 billion marine creatures perished}}}\uc2 , as helpless mussels and clams cooked in their own shells.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe saw the forecasts and it was hard to believe as we don\u8217\'20\'19t really have heatwaves like that. In Seattle it\u8217\'20\'19s usually so overcast during June we call it Juneuary,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kristie Ebi, an epidemiologist at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2  who knew the heatwave was serious when she woke up at 6am with the temperature already at 80F (26C). \u8220\'20\'1CYou see the heatwaves hit other places and you know it\u8217\'20\'19s bad but there\u8217\'20\'19s not the sense of urgency until it hits you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An old joke in Seattle is that you will know more people with a boat than people with air conditioning and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/data/seattle-is-a-lot-more-air-conditioned-than-it-used-to-be/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest figures show}}}\uc2  just 44% of households in the city are fitted with air conditioning. The Pacific north-west\u8217\'20\'19s image as a place of rugged natural beauty, comfortable climes and forward-thinking politics has helped draw plenty of newcomers \u8211\'20\'13 Seattle was the fastest-growing major US city {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/data/surprise-seattle-was-the-fastest-growing-big-u-s-city-in-2020/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but the freakish heatwave has provided a sobering reality check to its blossoming status as a refuge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of people moving up from California with the idea there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of natural amenities and a lot of cheap space but all of these factors are changing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jesse Keenan, an expert in climate adaptation at Tulane University. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s becoming less affordable and is increasingly burdened by forest fires, terrible smoke, flash floods and these heatwaves that suddenly make things a matter of life or death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Pacific north-west {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nca2018.globalchange.gov/chapter/24/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has heated up by an average of 2F (1.1C) over the past century}}}\uc2 , with growing wildfires, failing coastal fisheries, receding snowpack and increasing heat taking its toll upon a region historically unprepared for such extremes. The recent heatwave would have been \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually impossible\u8221\'20\'1D without human-induced climate breakdown, scientists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/science-environment-57751918"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/21/pacific-northwest-heatwave-dome-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Nowhere is safe\u8217\'20\'19: heat shatters vision of Pacific north-west as climate refuge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s too late\u8217\'20\'19: US doctor says dying patients begging for Covid vaccine\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sarah-betancourt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah Betancourt}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 What the \uc2 US government\uc2  is calling \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/16/covid-19-us-delta-variant-unvaccinated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the pandemic of the unvaccinated}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D is playing out in painful ways as some realize too late that they wish they had had the shot, while others hold out even as they suffer in hospital amid a national surge of new Covid-19 infections, primarily caused by the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 At least 99% of those in the US who died of coronavirus in the last six months had not been vaccinated, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), has said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile vaccination rates have slowed down nationwide and are especially low in some of the more conservative, southern parts of the country, despite more than 610,000 people in the US dying of the virus since the pandemic hit in early 2020.\par \par \uc2 In places such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama}}}\uc2 , only 33% of people who can receive the vaccine had been fully vaccinated, as of 20 July.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, a doctor in a Birmingham, Alabama, hospital, Brytney Cobia, said that all but one of her Covid patients at Grandview medical center didn\u8217\'20\'19t receive the vaccine, with the one who had expected to make a full recovery after receiving oxygen, she told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2021/07/im-sorry-but-its-too-late-alabama-doctor-on-treating-unvaccinated-dying-covid-patients.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Birmingham News}}}\uc2 . Several others are dying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m admitting young, healthy people to the hospital with very serious Covid infections,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Cobia in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the last things they do before they\u8217\'20\'19re intubated is beg me for the vaccine. I hold their hand and tell them that I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, but it\u8217\'20\'19s too late,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, referring to patients who have to be put on a ventilator.\par \par \uc2 Alabama public health officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsfa.com/2021/07/13/unvaccinated-make-up-96-alabama-covid-19-deaths-since-april/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently reported}}}\uc2  96% of Alabamians who have died of Covid since April were not fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Among the people succumbing to the deadly disease are those who are increasingly catching the Delta variant of the coronavirus, which is far more contagious than the original.\par \par \uc2 The variant now makes up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/20/delta-variant-us-covid-increase-cdc-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 83% of new cases}}}\uc2  in the US, according to Walensky.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a dramatic increase, up from 50% for the week of July 3,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/22/us-coronavirus-covid-unvaccinated-hospital-rates-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s too late\u8217\'20\'19: US doctor says dying patients begging for Covid vaccine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My savings were gone\u8217\'20\'19: millions who lost work during Covid faced benefit system chaos\par \par \uc2 Unemployed workers are pushing for reforms and changes to America\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment insurance system after millions of workers experienced severe problems in receiving benefits throughout the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Workers across America faced long delays in receiving unemployment benefits as state systems were quickly overwhelmed with the mass influx of applications that caused months-long backlogs. Meanwhile, workers who made errors on their applications, had missing records or had their claims flagged had their benefits stopped \u8211\'20\'13 and often had difficulty restarting them once problems were resolved.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2021-06-25/u-s-unemployment-at-least-9-million-americans-didn-t-receive-any-benefits#:~:text=They're%20three%20of%20at,U.S.%20Department%20of%20Labor%20data."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 9 million Americans}}}\uc2  are estimated to have lost work due to the pandemic but received no unemployment benefits.\par \par \uc2 Sharon Corpening, 60, a freelance writer in Roswell, Georgia, lost all her work contracts when the pandemic shutdowns occurred throughout the US in March last year.\par \par \uc2 As a gig worker, Corpening\u8217\'20\'19s initial unemployment application was denied by the \uc2 Georgia department of labor\uc2 , until the Cares Act provided pandemic unemployment assistance for gig workers a few weeks later. She spent weeks trying to process her application and encountered issues with the unemployment website, and would sit on the phone for hours daily failing to reach a service representative.\par \par \uc2 Like thousands of Americans having trouble with their unemployment applications, Corpening joined a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  group and got involved in helping others through the unemployment process, advocating for systemic reforms and countering narratives that try to portray unemployed workers as \u8220\'20\'1Clazy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot wanting to work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Corpening took offense at these characterizations and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/21/us-unemployment-benefits-pandemic-cut-republican-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push}}}\uc2  from Republican governors to prematurely cancel federal unemployment benefits while unemployment systems remain broken.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have people who applied eight months ago who have not received a dime,\u8221\'20\'1D said Corpening. \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia is one of the 26 states that cut off federal benefits, and a week out I will tell you all my bank accounts are overdrawn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The impacts were detrimental to workers around the US, who fell behind on rent or mortgage or car payments, experienced utility shutoffs and relied on food banks and assistance programs to feed themselves and their families.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the mass unemployment caused by the pandemic, several organizations, including the Economic Policy Institute and National Employment Law Project, created a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unemployment-insurance-reform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report }}}\uc2  with unemployed workers outlining reforms needed to fix the widespread issues to unemployment insurance that were exposed by Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/22/unemployment-systems-reform-pandemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My savings were gone\u8217\'20\'19: millions who lost work during Covid faced benefit system chaos}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mississippi attorney general urges supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general urged the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong\u8221\'20\'1D. She asked the court to allow a controversial law that bans abortions after 15 weeks to go into effect in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conclusion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a constitutional right has no basis in text, structure, history, or tradition,\u8221\'20\'1D said attorney general Lynn Fitch in a brief.\par \par \uc2 The court will hear arguments on 15 weeks ban in the fall, when the new conservative iteration of the court will decide whether Americans have the right to end pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution does not protect a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Fitch wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution\u8217\'20\'19s text says nothing about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nothing in the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s structure implies a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or prohibits states from restricting it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on the case, from my colleague Jessica Glenza:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Alarm bells are ringing\u8217\'20\'19: activists brace for US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case that could rip up precedent}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for me. I\u8217\'20\'19m passing the blogging baton over to my capable colleague Maanvi Singh on the west coast. To review, here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Dr Rochelle Walensky{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f9d7098f08bb57f5f7ce70#block-60f9d7098f08bb57f5f7ce70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that the country is at a \u8220\'20\'1Cpivotal\u8221\'20\'1D moment in fighting the spread of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f9962d8f085dcd6b595b7d#block-60f9962d8f085dcd6b595b7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floated}}}\uc2  appointing congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois to the committee charged with investigating the 6 January mob attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2#block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it would impose new sanctions on Cuban regime officials.\par \par \uc2 * Pelosi also said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f980ef8f085dcd6b5959dc#block-60f980ef8f085dcd6b5959dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to have congressman Jim Banks and Jim Jordan on the panel investigating the mob attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the director of the Centers for Disease Control, warned that the US is at a \u8220\'20\'1Cpivotal moment in this pandemic\u8221\'20\'1D because of the spread of variants of Covid-19, my colleague Joanna Walters writes.\par \par \uc2 Walensky made the comments amid increasing numbers of cases across the country and as lawmakers and public figures urge Americans with increasing urgency to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Inside the White House there is reportedly an ongoing debate over whether to start a new push urge to Americans to wear masks like in the earlier days of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Walensky, speaking at a briefing on Thursday, said of the Delta variant of Covid that it \u8220\'20\'1Cis one of the most infectious respiratory viruses we know of and that I have seen in my 20-year career\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are at another pivotal moment in this pandemic, with cases rising again and some hospitals reaching their capacity in some areas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/22/us-covid-cases-rise-delta-variant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US in \u8216\'20\'18another pivotal moment\u8217\'20\'19 as Delta variant drives surge in Covid cases}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the chief medical adviser to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , praised Republicans who have been encouraging Americans to get vaccinated. He made those comments in an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/technology/564394-fauci-praises-gop-encouraging-vaccines-a-very-good-thing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill}}}\uc2  newspaper.\par \par \uc2 In particular Fauci praised Congressman Steve Scalise of Louisiana, a member of House Republican leadership, for encouraging Americans to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was very pleased to hear Congressman Scalise... make that statement about vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci told The Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was very helpful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fauci also said \u8220\'20\'1CI think when they see a Republican leader like Congressman Scalise lean strongly towards people getting vaccinated, I think that\u8217\'20\'19s a very positive thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press pool has passed along the guest list for the bill signing, which should start soon. It\u8217\'20\'19s a long list:\par \par \uc2 * The Vice President\par \par \uc2 * The Second Gentleman\par \par \uc2 * Associate Attorney General Vanita Gupta\par \par \uc2 * Acting Assistant Attorney General Amy Solomon, \uc2 Office of Justice Programs\uc2 , DOJ\par \par \uc2 * Kristina Rose, Director, Office for Victims of Crime, DOJ\par \par \uc2 * Maryland Attorney General \uc2 Brian Frosh\par \par \uc2 * Virginia Attorney General \uc2 Mark Herring\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\par \par \uc2 * Senator Richard Blumenthal\par \par \uc2 * Senator Shelley Capito\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Joni Ernst\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\par \par \uc2 * Senator Amy Klobuchar\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Patrick Leahy\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Cynthia Lummis\par \par \uc2 * Senator Lisa Murkowski\par \par \uc2 * Senator \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\par \par \uc2 * Representative Deborah Dingell\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\par \par \uc2 * Representative Ann McLane Kuster\par \par \uc2 * Representative James Langevin\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Lucy McBath\par \par \uc2 * Representative Gwen Moore\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\par \par \uc2 * Representative Mary Gay Scanlon\par \par \uc2 * Representative Jackie Speier\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Ann Wagner\par \par \uc2 * Representative \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even as some of the most famous Republicans in the country urge Americans to get vaccinated, half of all Republicans in the House of Representatives won\u8217\'20\'19t say whether they\u8217\'20\'19ve been vaccinated or not. That\u8217\'20\'19s according to a new report from CNN:\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of House Republicans still won\u8217\'20\'19t say publicly whether they are vaccinated against Covid-19, even as new cases rise nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Some of the 97 Republicans who aren\u8217\'20\'19t sharing their vaccination status told CNN they don\u8217\'20\'19t have a responsibility to model behavior to their constituents.\u8221\'20\'1DI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s anybody\u8217\'20\'19s damn business whether I\u8217\'20\'19m vaccinated or not,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican Rep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/07/politics/chip-roy-democratic-obstruction-2022/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chip Roy}}}\uc2  of Texas told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is ridiculous, what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing. The American people are fully capable of making an educated decision about whether they want to get the vaccine or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over the past few months, CNN has sent multiple inquiries to members of Congress and reviewed public statements but is unable to confirm the vaccination status of almost half the Republican conference.\par \par \uc2 Still a few of them offered some explanations during hallway interviews with CNN this week.\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Rep Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida told CNN \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s very nosy of you,\u8221\'20\'1D when CNN started asking about his vaccination status, but the congressman cut off the question before it got to whether or not he was vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/22/politics/house-republicans-vaccination-rates/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 President Biden is due soon to deliver remarks at a bill signing for \u8220\'20\'1CH.R. 1652, the VOCA Fix to Sustain the Crime Victims Fund Act of 2021\u8221\'20\'1D as the White House press pool noted earlier today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Sheldon Whitehouse of Rhode Island, one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f99c878f08bb57f5f7cb81#block-60f99c878f08bb57f5f7cb81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signatories of a letter}}}\uc2  expressing concern to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  about its investigation into now supreme court justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 . Whitehouse\u8217\'20\'19s tweets illustrate the sense of dissatisfaction he and the other Democratic senators feel about the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to tips about Kavanaugh and its probe of his past conduct years before he became a judge.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis long-delayed answer confirms how badly we were spun by Director Wray and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in the Kavanaugh background investigation and hearing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x24NcE3KtC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/x24NcE3KtC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1418241007985078279?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIt confirms my suspicions that the \u8220\'20\'1Ctip line\u8221\'20\'1D was not real and that \uc2 FBI\uc2  tip line procedures were not followed. There are \uc2 FBI\uc2  tip line procedures. They were not followed.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1418241008958115850?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSo when Wray said they followed procedures, he meant the \u8220\'20\'1Cprocedure\u8221\'20\'1D of doing whatever Trump White House Counsel told them to do. That\u8217\'20\'19s misleading as hell.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1418241009880862720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNo wonder so many witnesses were so frustrated when they tried to bring evidence forward. I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard tales that even \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents not in on the scam sent info to the \u8220\'20\'1Ctip line.\u8221\'20\'1D That must feel like a burn.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1418241011776724993?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrVictims don\u8217\'20\'19t always get redress, but their serious allegations deserve serious investigation, not a \u8220\'20\'1Ctip line\u8221\'20\'1D garbage chute to a White House Counsel desperate to cover up the facts.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1418241012741332996?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration just released a new statement confirming earlier reports about incoming sanctions on new sanctions targeting specific Cuban regime officials.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the key passage:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, my Administration is imposing new sanctions targeting elements of the Cuban regime responsible for this crackdown\u8212\'20\'14the head of the Cuban military and the division of the \uc2 Cuban Ministry of the Interior\uc2  driving the crackdown\u8212\'20\'14to hold them accountable for their actions. This is just the beginning\u8211\'20\'13the United States will continue to sanction individuals responsible for oppression of the Cuban people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden formally announces new sanctions on Cuban officials. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/91pvvjE2Ro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/91pvvjE2Ro}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1418267844941336582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about the president\u8217\'20\'19s filibuster comments last night \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  digressed. First she said that the Senate makes the decisions on the filibuster. She said that Biden was only addressing what the process would look like to change the filibuster and not weighing in one way or another.\par \par \uc2 But she also said she Biden\u8217\'20\'19s position had not changed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat he was referring to was simply to what that process would look like,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said, going on to say that Biden would \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to advocate for the For the People Act...and the John Lewis Voting Rights Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s in reference to two major voting rights bills Democrats want to pass into law. Psaki stressed though that Biden did not want to weigh in closely on Senate procedure though.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe alone doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a role in making these changes in the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  just said there would be more from the State Department and the Treasury Department on the sanctions against Cuban officials later today.\par \par \uc2 Background on that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/22/covid-coronavirus-cdc-us-politics-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2#block-60f990e58f08bb57f5f7cab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s daily press briefing is under way and commerce department secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2  is addressing the country\u8217\'20\'19s semiconductor chip shortage.\par \par \uc2 enltrCommerce Sec. \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 : "I am engaging almost daily with industry" on the chips shortage. "We are working as hard as we can to get the House to pass the CHIPS Act, and we're planning ways to invest the $52 billion..We need to incentivize the manufacture of chips in America." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t5ZFsAjdno"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/t5ZFsAjdno}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christina Wilkie (@christinawilkie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/christinawilkie/status/1418252764203950090?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The country\u8217\'20\'19s semiconductor chip shortage is an ongoing problem that nevertheless has been under the radar to much of the population.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe chip shortage could fairly be described as a crisis\u8212\'20\'14millions of willing consumers unable to buy, thousands of dealerships going broke because they have no inventory, hundreds of plants slowing or stopping new vehicle production. It\u8217\'20\'19s a huge news story\u8212\'20\'14and hugely undercovered.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Alberta (@TimAlberta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TimAlberta/status/1418205988365033476?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats criticize inquiry into \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  in new letter\par \par \uc2 A number of Senate Democrats are questioning the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of tips into \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  during the now Supreme Court justice\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation process. Per The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Nearly three years after Justice \uc2 Brett M. Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/06/us/politics/brett-kavanaugh-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tumultuous confirmation}}}\uc2  to the Supreme Court, the F.B.I. has disclosed more details about its efforts to review the justice\u8217\'20\'19s background, leading a group of Senate Democrats to question the thoroughness of the vetting and conclude that it was shaped largely by the Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 In a letter dated June 30 to two Democratic senators, Sheldon Whitehouse of Rhode Island and Chris Coons of Delaware, an F.B.I. assistant director, Jill C. Tyson, said that the most \u8220\'20\'1Crelevant\u8221\'20\'1D of the 4,500 tips the agency received during an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/05/us/politics/trump-kavanaugh-fbi.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation into Mr. Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s past}}}\uc2  were referred to White House lawyers in the Trump administration, whose handling of them remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 The letter left uncertain whether the F.B.I. itself followed up on the most compelling leads. The agency was conducting a background check rather than a criminal investigation, meaning that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe authorities, policies, and procedures used to investigate criminal matters did not apply,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/210721_FBI%20Kavanaugh%20Follow-up%20Letter1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  from the senators to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/news/release/after-new-details-on-kavanaugh-investigation-surface-senators-call-on-fbi-for-answers-on-handling-of-tip-line"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  from Whitehouse\u8217\'20\'19s office on the letter:\par \par \uc2 Washington, DC \u8211\'20\'13 Senators Sheldon Whitehouse (D-RI), Chris Coons (D-DE), Dick Durbin (D-IL), \uc2 Patrick Leahy\uc2  (D-VT), Richard Blumenthal (D-CT), Mazie Hirono (D-HI), and \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  (D-NJ) wrote to FBI Director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  last evening requesting additional information on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2018 supplemental background investigation of Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 . The senators\u8217\'20\'19 request follows a letter from the Bureau to Whitehouse and Coons revealing new details on the Kavanaugh background investigation, including that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  gathered over 4,500 tips in relation to the investigation without any apparent further action by \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigators. The Bureau also confirmed that tips from the tip line were instead provided to the Trump White House Counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office, where their fate is unknown.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  of Wyoming, who is on the panel to investigate the 6 January mob attack, thinks it would be a good idea for Congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois, another outspoken anti-Trump Republican, to join the panel.\par \par \uc2 enltrPelosi mulls adding more anti-Trump Republicans to Jan. 6 investigation\par \par \uc2 Cheney tells me - Kinzinger would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous addition to the committee. I think ultimately it's up to the speaker, but I would certainly support it\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rVJkzpTBSm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rVJkzpTBSm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1418229840336105482?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi is weighing her options. She said as much during a news conference on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll see\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said, adding \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s not even bipartisan; it\u8217\'20\'19s nonpartisan. It\u8217\'20\'19s about seeking the truth and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we owe the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration to impose sanctions on Cuban officials\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is planning on imposing new sanctions on Cuban officials who are directly linked to human rights violations in the country, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/biden-cuba-sanctions/2021/07/22/b058c69c-ea93-11eb-8950-d73b3e93ff7f_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/biden-cuba-sanctions/2021/07/22/b058c69c-ea93-11eb-8950-d73b3e93ff7f_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Imposed under the Global Magnitsky Act, the sanctions will initially affect what officials said were a small number of individuals from \uc2 Cuba\u8217\'20\'19s Interior Ministry\uc2  and military forces.\par \par \uc2 The measures come as President Biden faces increasing pressure from Congress, activist groups and Cuban Americans to take decisive action in support of the protesters.\par \par \uc2 The administration had been making its way toward implementing a new policy toward Cuba that would reverse many of the actions taken by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to restrict travel, trade and other forms of outreach. The Obama administration had expanded contacts when it reestablished diplomatic relations with Havana in 2015.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions come during ongoing unrest and amid protests in Cuba. The Cuban government has sought to organize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-business-health-cuba-caribbean-9ed6c6dd50ddb764a482099e44cdc25c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counter protests}}}\uc2  as well.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has also looked into taking steps to increasing staffing at its Cuban embassy, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-government-and-politics-cuba-f458659bb747b26f7306a7773c272dfc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives just passed legislation increasing the number of Afghan interpreters who have helped U.S. troops to immigrate to the United States.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Crow takes a victory lap here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/isBk2O3Tgr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/isBk2O3Tgr}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X2b3EdIf0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X2b3EdIf0e}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1418227081595457536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a move the Biden administration has acted on in increasing urgency.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's the OMB Statement of Administration Policy in support of Rep. Jason Crow's legislation to streamline the Special Immigrant Visas program for Afghans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6p0Vtcmi4F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6p0Vtcmi4F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1417221694901653506?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/22/us/politics/afghans-interpreters-visas-house.html?smid=tw-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 Luke Broadwater:\par \par \uc2 Under the legislation, applicants would no longer have to provide a sworn statement that they faced a specific threat or proof that they held a \u8220\'20\'1Csensitive and trusted\u8221\'20\'1D job. Instead, the measure would in effect stipulate that any Afghan who helped the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  by definition faces retribution, and should be able to apply for a visa.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last night \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  quashed any question that he\u8217\'20\'19s moving on abolishing the filibuster. Speaking at a CNN townhall in Cincinnati the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/07/21/biden-nothing-done-filibuster-abolished-500502"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no reason to protect it other than you\u8217\'20\'19re going to throw the entire Congress into chaos and nothing will get done. Nothing at all will get done. And there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot at stake. The most important one is the right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued \u8220\'20\'1CWouldn\u8217\'20\'19t my friends on the other side love to have a debate about the filibuster instead of passing the recovery act?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments come amidst increasing pressure from progressives to gut the filibuster. But the president is not alone in being a holdout. Senators Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona and Joe Manchin of West Virginia, two of the most moderate Democrats in Congress, have been outspoken holdouts as well.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s despite arguments from other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/07/10/clyburn-biden-filibuster-election-reform-499051"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 influential Democrats}}}\uc2  to at least allow a workaround for voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the committee investigating 6 January, the chairman of the committee, Congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  of Mississippi, said it\u8217\'20\'19s possible that Congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois could join the panel.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  says that adding \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  to the Jan. 6 select committee has been discussed with the speaker\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know it's been discussed,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson told me\par \par \uc2 He says if Pelosi signs off, Kinzinger will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcome addition\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1418219148174249986?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger is one of the most outspoken opponents of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the House of Representatives. He\u8217\'20\'19s also a staunch ally of Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the target of much of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s fury these days.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi has also floated bringing on former Congressman Denver Riggleman of Virginia as an adviser.\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerPelosi}}}\uc2  and Dems considering inviting former GOP Rep. Denver Riggleman to serve as 1/6 select committee adviser, per sources familiar. W/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rickklein?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rickklein}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Siegel (@bensiegel)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bensiegel/status/1418210599855529985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi says it would be 'ridiculous' to include Republican duo\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has gotten push back in some quarters for blocking two Republicans from joining the select committee charged with investigating the 6 January mob attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, speaking at a press conference today, pushed back on that criticism. She said it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D to include them on the committee.\par \par \uc2 enltr"ridiculous to put them on a committee seeking the truth," Pelosi says of Banks and Jordan.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Allen (@jonallendc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonallendc/status/1418214121791758336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says she excluded 2 GOP members from the January 6th committee over \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D statements. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TMud4fqzTD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TMud4fqzTD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1418216081622241280?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 More background {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/21/us/politics/jim-banks-jim-jordan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal got its hands on a memo from attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  reinforcing guidelines for the department of justice\u8217\'20\'19s investigations, a move that is clearly in contrast to how critics saw the work of the department under the last administration. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Journal\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-department-underscores-independence-from-white-house-11626910625?st=p4itc32wsvn58uu&reflink=desktopwebshare_twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In a memo addressed to all department personnel, Mr. Garland said the Justice Department \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not advise the White House concerning pending or contemplated criminal or civil law enforcement investigations or cases unless doing so is important for the performance of the President\u8217\'20\'19s duties and appropriate from a law enforcement perspective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The memo said those limits\u8212\'20\'14which it said didn\u8217\'20\'19t apply to matters of national security or foreign relations\u8212\'20\'14were necessary to \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote and protect the norms of Departmental independence and integrity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That language closely tracked a 2009 memo issued by then-Attorney General \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 , which remained in effect throughout the Trump presidency, according to a former Justice Department official. But Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated public comments and criticism about pending criminal investigations and cases involving his allies\u8212\'20\'14some of which the Justice Department appeared to heed\u8212\'20\'14led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  to stress restoring independence to the department in his successful campaign for the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no uniform consensus among Republican governors (who control the majority of governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansions) over what to do about the coronavirus pandemic. In Missouri for instance, Governor Mike Parsons {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kmbc.com/article/missouri-gov-mike-parson-announces-be-a-mo-vip-winner-covid-19-vaccine-incentive-program/37094312#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled}}}\uc2  a new set of incentives for people to get vaccinated, following the example of other Republican governors like West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Jim Justice or Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But in Texas, Governor Greg Abbott, who is up for reelection, is refusing to impose a statewide mask mandate even though cases are on the rise. Via the Texas Tribune:\par \par \uc2 Gov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/directory/greg-abbott/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Abbott}}}\uc2  says he will not impose another statewide mask mandate, despite COVID-19 cases being on the rise again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be no mask mandate imposed, and the reasons for that are very clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.click2houston.com/news/local/2021/07/21/despite-rise-in-covid-19-cases-gov-greg-abbott-says-he-will-not-impose-another-mask-mandate-in-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told KPRC-TV in Houston}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are so many people who have immunities to COVID, whether it be through the vaccination, whether it be through their own exposure and their recovery from it, which would be acquired immunity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It would be \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate to require people who already have immunity to wear a mask,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Tribune\uc2  also notes that as of Sunday, just 43 percent of Texans were vaccinated. That\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mayoclinic.org/coronavirus-covid-19/vaccine-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well behind}}}\uc2  other states in the region and across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a rare sign of the times and specific moment for Trump supporters: former Senator \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  of Kansas, the former Republican presidential nominee, who endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  now says the 45th president lost fair and square to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s the key line from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2021/07/22/98-bob-dole-reckons-legacy-trump-ponders-future-gop/7995412002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA Today report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe lost the election, and I regret that he did, but they did,\u8221\'20\'1D Dole said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe had \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  running all over the country, claiming fraud. He never had one bit of fraud in all those lawsuits he filed and statements he made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Trumper,\u8221\'20\'1D Dole said at one point during the conversation. But he added at another, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sort of Trumped out, though.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House considers new masking push\par \par \uc2 Goodmorning, Daniel Strauss here. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get started.\par \par \uc2 At the White House, officials are debating whether to urge Americans to wear masks more often to curb the spread of coronavirus. That\u8217\'20\'19s according to a new report in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/biden-masks-delta-covid/2021/07/21/cba29774-ea3a-11eb-8950-d73b3e93ff7f_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  detailing the still preliminary deliberations:\par \par \uc2 The talks are in a preliminary phase and their result could be as simple as new messaging from top White House officials. But some of the talks include officials at the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  who are separately examining whether to update their masking guidance, according to a Biden administration aide and a federal health official.\par \par \uc2 Officials cautioned that any new formal guidance would have to come from the CDC, and they maintained that the White House has taken a hands-off approach with the agency to ensure they are not interfering with the work of scientists. But the high-level discussions reflect rising concerns across the administration about the threat of the delta variant and a renewed focus on what measures may need to be reintroduced to slow its spread.\par \par \uc2 Those discussions come as governors across the country offer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/05/vaccine-us-states-america-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly creative}}}\uc2  means to incentivizing people to get vaccinated against the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Some of the most high profile -and at times bombastic- Republican figures in recent days have begun urging Americans to get vaccinated as well, amidst the ongoing spread of deadlier coronavirus variants. Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida made one such plea earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 enltr"These vacines are saving lives"\par \par \uc2 In his most direct effort to encourage people to get vaccinated, Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said 95% of the new COVID cases are those who are not vaccinated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3RzHYEH1mI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3RzHYEH1mI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Angel (@NewsGuyGreg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsGuyGreg/status/1417911400589058049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 21, 2021}}}\uc2  2021-07-22T13:16:52Z 2021-07-23T00:13:01Z https://media.guim.co.uk/51e5f367fb6987417d5b15ff27bb71426a9ce144/0_0_3500_2101/500.jpg \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , director of the CDC, has warned of a \u8216\'20\'18pivotal moment\u8217\'20\'19 amid Covid.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210722eh7m001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
