\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get this done\u8217\'20\'19: Biden on Capitol Hill to push infrastructure package \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 8,567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2021\par 00:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President to discuss massive $3.5tn plan over lunch with DemocratsSenate minority leader McConnell hits back at Biden on voting rights\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was on Capitol Hill for a meeting to discuss Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan. The president attended the Senate Democratic caucus\u8217\'20\'19 weekly policy lunch this afternoon, one day after majority leader Chuck Schumer announced an agreement on the spending proposal. Speaking to reporters just before the lunch started, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get this done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Schumer acknowledged it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Clong\u8221\'20\'1D road to passing the $3.5tn proposal. Senate Democrats still need to hammer out the details of the spending package and get the entire caucus on board before they can move forward. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are going to get this done because we so fervently believe that we must make average American lives a whole lot better,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 * Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  dismissed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Republican voting restrictions, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/democrats-voting-rights-us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts warn}}}\uc2  that the US is facing a potential democratic crisis. The Republican leader specifically mocked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the voting restrictions and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 election represent \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant test of our democracy since the civil war\u8221\'20\'1D, as the president said in Philadelphia yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat utter nonsense,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be laugh-out-loud funny if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so completely and totally irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The select committee investigating the 6 January insurrection announced it will hold its first hearing later this month. On 27 July, the panel will hear first-hand testimony from some of the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  and DC Metropolitan police Department officers who defended the Capitol as pro-Trump insurrectionists stormed the building. House minority leader Kevin McCarthy has still not named anyone to the committee, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether he will do so before the hearing occurs.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration said it will start evacuating at-risk Afghans by the end of the month. The announcement from \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  comes as the US military continues its withdrawal operation and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  makes territorial advances across Afghanistan. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason that we are taking these steps is because these are courageous individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to make sure we recognize and value the role they\u8217\'20\'19ve played over the last several years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Where key Senate moderates stand on the $3.5tn budget resolution\par \par \uc2 Jon Tester, Montana: \u8220\'20\'1CThe price tag is a lot of money but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t scare me, it\u8217\'20\'19s just how it\u8217\'20\'19s being spent. There are plenty of needs out there, we just have to figure out how it\u8217\'20\'19s being spent,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, according to the Hill.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , West Virginia: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re anxious to basically review it. They worked hard on it, we want to see it. Also I\u8217\'20\'19ve been very clear that I want to see the pay-fors and make sure that whatever we do is globally competitive,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema, Arizona: \u8220\'20\'1CKyrsten is committed to working with her colleagues and the administration on ways to create jobs and expand economic opportunities in Arizona and communities across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThose conversations are ongoing and she will give careful consideration to any idea that can strengthen Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s economy and help Arizona families get ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  failed in investigating serious sexual abuse allegations against Larry Nasser, the former USA Gymnastics coach, the Justice department\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general has said.\par \par \uc2 The investigation was \u8220\'20\'1Cinexcusable and a discredit\u8221\'20\'1D to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the department\u8217\'20\'19s watchdog said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 The inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation was spurred by allegations that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  failed to promptly address complaints made in 2015 against Nassar. \uc2 USA Gymnastics\uc2  had conducted its own internal investigation and then the organization\u8217\'20\'19s then-president, Stephen Penny, reported the allegations to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s field office in Indianapolis. But it took months before the bureau opened a formal investigation.\par \par \uc2 At least 40 girls and women said they were molested over a 14-month period while the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was aware of other sexual abuse allegations involving Nassar. Officials at \uc2 USA Gymnastics\uc2  also contacted \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials in Los Angeles in May 2016 after eight months of inactivity from agents in Indianapolis.\par \par \uc2 The inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s office found that \u8220\'20\'1Cdespite the extraordinarily serious nature\u8221\'20\'1D of the allegations against Nassar, \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials in Indianapolis did not respond with the \u8220\'20\'1Cutmost seriousness and urgency that they deserved and required.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When they did respond, the report said, \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials made \u8220\'20\'1Cnumerous and fundamental errors\u8221\'20\'1D and also violated bureau policies. Among the missteps was a failure to conduct any investigative activity until more than a month after a meeting with \uc2 USA Gymnastics\uc2 . Agents interviewed by phone one of three athletes, but never spoke with two other gymnasts despite being told they were available to meet.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/jul/14/larry-nassar-watchdog-report-justice-department-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Inexcusable\u8217\'20\'19: FBI badly mishandled Larry Nassar case, DoJ watchdog says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opinion: How have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first six months been? Our panelists weigh in \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2 : \u8216\'20\'18The biggest potential disaster? Voting rights\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Six months in, it looks like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has a good chance of getting America back to where it was before the pandemic. Covid-19 is in retreat. So far, almost half of the adult population has been fully vaccinated. The economy is roaring back \u8211\'20\'13 still 7m jobs short of where it was in January 2020 but on track to return to the starting gate by the end of the year. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Rescue Plan\u8221\'20\'1D is a major success.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear Biden will get America back to where it was before Trump. His initial slew of executive orders erased most of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive orders, but he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet demolished all of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cruel immigration policies. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s xenophobic rhetoric is gone but Biden hasn\u8217\'20\'19t repaired relations with China. Many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs are still in place. And even with a bare Democratic majority in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s little chance Congress will repeal all of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax cuts for corporations and the wealthy.\par \par \uc2 What about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s big plans to remake America? Depending on your point of view, they\u8217\'20\'19re either on hold or stalled. He\u8217\'20\'19ll likely get bipartisan support for over half a trillion dollars of new spending for \u8220\'20\'1Chard\u8221\'20\'1D infrastructure. That\u8217\'20\'19s not nothing. Beyond that, it\u8217\'20\'19s anyone\u8217\'20\'19s guess what Senate Democrats will agree to on legislation covering childcare, the environment, and healthcare and education that can circumvent a Republican filibuster\par \par \uc2 Bhaskar Sunkara: \u8216\'20\'18Biden is thinking big \u8211\'20\'13 but hasn\u8217\'20\'19t delivered yet\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The good news is that six months into the Joe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2 , he\u8217\'20\'19s delivered on one of his main campaign pitches and restored a sense of \u8220\'20\'1Cnormalcy\u8221\'20\'1D to the country. After four years of mercurial rule by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the White House has become a more predictable place.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the bad news too. Since the old \u8220\'20\'1Cnormal\u8221\'20\'1D wasn\u8217\'20\'19t delivering for millions of working-class Americans.\par \par \uc2 Biden has shown a willingness to think big, but he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t delivered on structural reforms like a $15 minimum wage and a Pro Act meant to help restore trade union density. He\u8217\'20\'19s institutionally constrained by hostile forces within his own party and has been forced to make do with a slim congressional majority, but unless he finds a way to use his political power to overcome some of those barriers, he\u8217\'20\'19ll find himself in an even more difficult position after the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Kate Aronoff: \u8216\'20\'18Biden needs to act on climate now\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not in an enviable position. Besides a Republican party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/07/politics/chip-roy-democratic-obstruction-2022/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hell bent}}}\uc2  on stopping any good things from happening, \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 both of them right-leaning Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 can decide on whatever makes it through a 50-50 senate. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s American Jobs Plan is drastically out of step with what the climate crisis demands, but even that faces major headwinds within our antebellum political system all but built to keep public opinion \u8211\'20\'13 that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dataforprogress.org/blog/2021/4/19/voters-support-green-new-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supports}}}\uc2  a Green New Deal and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/science/2020/06/23/two-thirds-of-americans-think-government-should-do-more-on-climate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stricter regulations}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 from being translated into law.\par \par \uc2 Whatever happens in Congress, though, Biden has a range of as-of-yet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/day-one-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unexplored tools}}}\uc2  at his disposal to start reducing emissions tomorrow. The \uc2 Office of the Comptroller of the Currency\uc2 , \uc2 Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation\uc2  and \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which jointly regulate the banking sector \u8211\'20\'13 could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizen.org/wp-content/uploads/Climate-Financial-Reg-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise capital requirements}}}\uc2  for institutions that invest in fossil fuels, helping stem the flow of Wall Street cash into coal, oil and gas. By declaring a climate emergency, Biden could reinstate the ban on crude oil exports, which have ballooned by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.greenpeace.org/usa/news/report-reinstating-the-crude-oil-export-ban-could-cut-global-emissions-as-much-as-181-million-tons/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 750%}}}\uc2  since rules restricting them were quietly peeled back in 2015. Ending drilling on federal lands \u8211\'20\'13 well within the purview of the Interior Department \u8211\'20\'13 could eliminate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/fossil-fuel-extraction-on-public-lands-produces-one-quarter-of-u-s-emissions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a quarter}}}\uc2  of US emission.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jul/14/joe-biden-first-six-months-panelists-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How have Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first six months been? Our panelists weigh in | Robert Reich, Geoffrey Kabaservice, Bhaskar Sunkara, Theodore R Johnson, Kate Aronoff and Valerie Rawlston Wilson}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is meeting today with General Austin \u8220\'20\'1CScott\u8221\'20\'1D Miller \u8211\'20\'13 who until recently was the top US general in Afghanistan \u8211\'20\'13 to thank him \u8220\'20\'1Cfor his extraordinary service\u8221\'20\'1D, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the final commander of the Resolute Support Mission, General Miller oversaw the vast majority of our drawdown from Afghanistan, which is a particularly vulnerable period for our troops,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThat this drawdown has been conducted in such an orderly and safe way is a testament to General Miller\u8217\'20\'19s leadership, and the President looks forward to personally thanking him later today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US withdrawal process from Afghanistan now nearly complete, according to US Central Command. The Biden administration has also announced an \u8220\'20\'1COperation Allies Refuge\u8221\'20\'1D to evacuate Afghani people who assisted US troops and therefore risk retaliation by staying in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wildfires tear through nearly 1m acres in US west as 16,000 firefighters battle onslaught\par \par \uc2 Wildfires burning across the US west have engulfed nearly a million acres and drawn in about 16,000 firefighters and workers to battle the blazes. The onslaught comes as the region reels from intense drought and deadly heatwaves amplified by the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe amount of fire, where they\u8217\'20\'19re burning, and just the intensity of them is very concerning,\u8221\'20\'1D said Faith Kearns, a scientist at the California Institute for Water Resources.\par \par \uc2 The fast-moving Bootleg fire in southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/oregon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oregon}}}\uc2  has burned more than 200,000 acres. It has already destroyed several homes and threatens thousands more, as officials warn that tinder-dry conditions and high temperatures could exacerbate the situation on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Al Lawson, the fire incident commander, warned responders: \u8220\'20\'1CAs you go out there today \u8211\'20\'13 adjust your reality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not seen a fire move like this, in these conditions, this early in the year. Expect the fire to do things that you have not seen before,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Mark Enty, a spokesman for the North-west Incident Management Team working to contain the fire, said the Bootleg fire had doubled in size each day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s sort of like having a new fire every day,\u8221\'20\'1D Enty said.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/wildfires-us-north-west-threaten-native-american-tribal-lands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wildfires tear through 1m acres in US west as 16,000 firefighters battle onslaught}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has approved of Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 The budget agreement \u8220\'20\'1Cwould grow the middle class, generate strong economic growth, and create millions of jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In a meeting with the Dems, the president \u8220\'20\'1Calso discussed how the means for funding these critical investments is popular with the American people, who know that the wealthiest individuals and corporations often pay a lower tax bill than teachers and firefighters\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement said. And he \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly hit on how the effects of climate change are undeniable, and that the public is demanding action that the budget resolution will deliver\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Crucial moderates will have to get on board in order for Democrats to pass the $3.5tn plan via the budget reconciliation process, circumventing the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Speaker Nancy Pelos i, who will have to shepherd the package through the House, said she approved of it: \u8220\'20\'1CThis budget agreement is a victory for the American people, making historic, once-in-a-generation progress for families across the nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was on Capitol Hill for a meeting to discuss Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan. The president attended the Senate Democratic caucus\u8217\'20\'19 weekly policy lunch this afternoon, one day after majority leader Chuck Schumer announced an agreement on the spending proposal. Speaking to reporters just before the lunch started, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get this done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Schumer acknowledged it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Clong\u8221\'20\'1D road to passing the $3.5tn proposal. Senate Democrats still need to hammer out the details of the spending package and get the entire caucus on board before they can move forward. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are going to get this done because we so fervently believe that we must make average American lives a whole lot better,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 * Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  dismissed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Republican voting restrictions, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/democrats-voting-rights-us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts warn}}}\uc2  that the US is facing a potential democratic crisis. The Republican leader specifically mocked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the voting restrictions and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 election represent \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant test of our democracy since the civil war\u8221\'20\'1D, as the president said in Philadelphia yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat utter nonsense,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be laugh-out-loud funny if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so completely and totally irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The select committee investigating the 6 January insurrection announced it will hold its first hearing later this month. On 27 July, the panel will hear first-hand testimony from some of the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  and DC Metropolitan police Department officers who defended the Capitol as pro-Trump insurrectionists stormed the building. House minority leader Kevin McCarthy has still not named anyone to the committee, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether he will do so before the hearing occurs.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration said it will start evacuating at-risk Afghans by the end of the month. The announcement from \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  comes as the US military continues its withdrawal operation and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  makes territorial advances across Afghanistan. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason that we are taking these steps is because these are courageous individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to make sure we recognize and value the role they\u8217\'20\'19ve played over the last several years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly attack}}}\uc2  on the US Capitol on 6 January, the chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, Gen Mark Milley, told aides the US was facing a \u8220\'20\'1CReichstag moment\u8221\'20\'1D because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was preaching \u8220\'20\'1Cthe gospel of the F\u252\'00\'FChrer\u8221\'20\'1D, according to an eagerly awaited book about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last year in office.\par \par \uc2 The excerpts from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jul/13/rudy-giuliani-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I Alone Can Fix This}}}\uc2 , by Carol Leonnig and Philip Rucker, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2021/07/i-alone-can-fix-it-mark-milley-likened-trump-to-hitler.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by New York magazine}}}\uc2  on Wednesday. The authors\u8217\'20\'19 employer, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jul/13/rudy-giuliani-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first extract from the book}}}\uc2  a day earlier. It will be published next week.\par \par \uc2 Milley\u8217\'20\'19s invocation of Germany under the Third Reich follows a report in another book, Frankly, We Did Win This Election, by Michael C Bender, that Trump told his chief of staff, \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/donald-trump-hitler-michael-bender-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hitler did a lot of good things}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump denies having made the remark.\par \par \uc2 Leonnig and Rucker report that Milley spoke to an \u8220\'20\'1Cold friend\u8221\'20\'1D, who warned the general that Trump and his allies were trying to \u8220\'20\'1Coverturn the government\u8221\'20\'1D in response to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory, which Trump falsely maintains was the result of electoral fraud.\par \par \uc2 Milley is reported to have said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey may try, but they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to fucking succeed. You can\u8217\'20\'19t do this without the military. You can\u8217\'20\'19t do this without the CIA and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19re the guys with guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/donald-trump-reichstag-moment-general-mark-milley-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top US general warned of \u8216\'20\'18Reichstag moment\u8217\'20\'19 in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s turbulent last days}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with a bipartisan group of mayors and governors to discuss the bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 Among the attendees are New Jersey governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  and Illinois governor JB Pritzker, both Democrats, as well as Vermont governor \uc2 Phil Scott\uc2 , a Republican.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meet with a bipartisan group of city and state political leaders. Photograph: Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The meeting comes one day after a bipartisan group of more than 350 US mayors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usmayors.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/USCM-FINAL-Mayors-Letter-on-Bipartisan-Infrastructure-Framework-071321-FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a letter}}}\uc2  indicating their support for the framework.\par \par \uc2 Taking a couple questions from reporters, Biden said he believed there may be some \u8220\'20\'1Cslight adjustments\u8221\'20\'1D to the pay-fors in the infrastructure plan, but he said the proposal was in \u8220\'20\'1Cgood shape\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked if simultaneously pursuing the bipartisan bill and the separate Democrats -only reconciliation package might jeopardize either proposal, Biden replied, \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s the only way to get it done is having those two tracks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  announced her appointees to the January 6 select committee earlier this month, after the chamber voted in favor of forming the panel.\par \par \uc2 In addition to Republican \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , Pelosi named Democrats \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2 , \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , Stephanie Murphy, Pete Aguilar, Adam Schiff and \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2  to the committee. Thompson, who chairs the House homeland security committee, will serve as chairman.\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy strongly opposed the formation of the select committee, and he has not yet appointed anyone to serve on the panel. The Republican leader said yesterday that he had not yet decided whether he would do so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t made a decision yet, even to appoint,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m discussing it with my members. I have a real concern, the scope of what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, because Pelosi was given more spots to fill than McCarthy, the committee already has a quorum to begin holding hearings. The first one is now set to take place in about two weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 select committee to hold hearing with Capitol Police officers\par \par \uc2 The select committee formed to investigate the January 6 insurrection at the Capitol has just announced it will hold its first hearing later this month.\par \par \uc2 On July 27, the committee will hear first-hand testimony from some of the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  and DC Metropolitan Police Department officers who defended the Capitol and lawmakers as pro-Trump insurrectionists stormed the building.\par \par \uc2 enltrJan. 6 Select Committee announces its first hearing - July 27 with USCP and MPD {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y1SP5njs5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Y1SP5njs5a}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1415396309838729222?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy has still not named anyone to the panel, but speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has already appointed enough members to form a quorum.\par \par \uc2 Although McCarthy has not chosen his appointees, the committee will include at least one Republican member: congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who was tapped by Pelosi.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has sent a letter to her caucus members praising Senate Democrats $3.5tn plan to invest in \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In her \u8220\'20\'1CDear Colleague\u8221\'20\'1D letter to fellow House Democrats, Pelosi said the plan indicates the final bill \u8220\'20\'1Cwill contain many of House Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 top priorities, including transformative action on the investments needed to confront the climate crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis budget agreement is a victory for the American people, making historic, once-in-a-generation progress for families across the nation,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Member can be proud of the priorities that this budget commits to \u8211\'20\'13 and every Member should know that we will fight to ensure that our priorities become law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi added that House committees \u8220\'20\'1Cstand ready to work with the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D as Democrats begin the long process to turn the $3.5tn plan into an actual bill that can be passed via reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A cluster of midwestern and southern states have emerged as a new center of Covid-19 outbreaks, as the highly transmissible Delta variant sweeps across poorly vaccinated populations in the US.\par \par \uc2 The news marks a potentially serious setback for the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to curb and control the pandemic as the Delta variant \u8211\'20\'13 which has wreaked havoc in the UK and elsewhere \u8211\'20\'13 is starting to spread more widely in America.\par \par \uc2 It also comes as life in much of the US has started to return to near normal, with many Covid-19 restrictions having been lifted, and as the vaccination program has slowed down.\par \par \uc2 Rates of Covid-19 cases in Kansas, Oklahoma, Missouri, Arkansas, Louisiana and Mississippi are among the highest in the country, and their vaccination rates among the lowest. Covid also appears to be gaining ground in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/06/delta-variant-infections-us-west-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American west}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even so, overall numbers of new Covid-19 cases are low. New infections are less than one-10th the average daily rate at the height of the pandemic in January, even as they have doubled in the last two weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not where we were in April 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr David Dowdy, an associate professor of epidemiology at Johns Hopkins University and an expert in infectious diseases. Nevertheless, he said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen those counts can go up substantially and quickly, so we need to be cautious but without panicking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/us-delta-variant-coronavirus-covid-vaccine-divide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delta variant gains ground in US as outbreaks highlight vaccine divide}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Well, that was quick: the White House has already released one of the videos that pop star Olivia Rodrigo recorded to encourage young people to get vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter if you\u8217\'20\'19re young and healthy,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodrigo says in the video. \u8220\'20\'1CGetting the vaccine is about protecting yourself, your friends and your family. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOlivia Rodrigo is at the White House today to meet with President Biden and Dr. Fauci and discuss the importance of young Americans getting vaccinated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s95KtOkrsF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/s95KtOkrsF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1415381245459054593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this afternoon, Rodrigo made an appearance in the White House briefing room, and she told reporters she was \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond honored and humbled\u8221\'20\'1D to assist the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s vaccination outreach efforts.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Rodrigo would also meet with \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  this afternoon. One White House staffer already shared a photo of Rodrigo with Fauci:\par \par \uc2 enltrvaccines are ~good 4 u~ and all that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TRHypbsPzo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TRHypbsPzo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Clarke Humphrey (@chumphrey46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chumphrey46/status/1415376874419724290?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  left Capitol Hill after meeting with Senate Democrats for about 45 minutes to discuss their $3.5tn plan to invest in \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reporters shouted questions at the president as he prepared to depart, and he said in response, \u8220\'20\'1CGreat to be home. Great to be back with my colleagues. I think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With that, Biden left to return to the White House, where he will soon meet with a bipartisan group of mayors and governors to discuss the separate bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden departs lunch with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateDems?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateDems}}}\uc2  : "Great to be home. Great to be back with my colleagues. I think we're going to get a lot done." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ogNpziq6ys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ogNpziq6ys}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1415374108448206852?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House to start evacuating at-risk Afghans\par \par \uc2 Jenn Psaki announced earlier at the White House that the US will start evacuating from Afghanistan individuals at risk because they worked for the \uc2 US government\uc2  as translators and in other roles.\par \par \uc2 As Reuters puts it: \u8220\'20\'1Cthe evacuation, Operation Allies Refuge, is set to start during the last week of July. Fighting between US-backed Afghan forces and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  has surged in recent weeks, with the militants gaining territory and capturing border crossings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason that we are taking these steps is because these are courageous individuals. We want to make sure we recognize and value the role they\u8217\'20\'19ve played over the last several years,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has set a formal end to the US military mission in Afghanistan for 31 August. The general leading the mission, Austin Miller, relinquished command on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said she could not provide specifics on the numbers of Afghans who will be in the initial evacuation flights \u8220\'20\'1Cfor operational and security reasons\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A US official, speaking on condition of anonymity, said the initial evacuation will include about 2,500 people and that they likely will be housed in US military facilities while their visa applications are processed. A final decision has not been made on the specific bases to be used, the official said.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the objective is to get \u8220\'20\'1Cindividuals who are eligible relocated out of the country\u8221\'20\'1D in advance of the withdrawal of US troops at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our latest report on the situation in Afghanistan ahead of the US withdrawal, which will come almost 20 years after troops first landed:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/14/taliban-claim-afghan-border-crossing-with-pakistan-in-major-gain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban claim Afghan border crossing with Pakistan in major gain}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Tuesday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://house.texas.gov/members/member-page/?district=52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas Democrat}}}\uc2  who fled the state for Washington DC in an attempt to stop a restrictive voting rights law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/14/fox-news-host-texas-democrat-james-talerico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged a Fox News host}}}\uc2  to say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The host, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2019/feb/11/germs-are-not-real-fox-news-host-pete-hegseth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Hegseth}}}\uc2 , would not.\par \par \uc2 James Talarico, a representative from the Austin area, was one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/texas-democrats-voting-exodus/2021/07/13/f391dc9e-e3ce-11eb-a41e-c8442c213fa8_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50}}}\uc2  Texas Democrats who fled to Washington DC. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/13/texas-governor-arrest-democrat-voting-restrictions-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatic move}}}\uc2  was made to deny Republicans a quorum to pass legislation which critics say restricts ballot access among communities likely to vote Democratic.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  gave a major speech on voting rights in Pennsylvania, demanding of Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/13/joe-biden-republicans-voting-rights-philadelphia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHave you no shame?\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\par \par \uc2 Later, Hegseth accused Talarico of being used \u8220\'20\'1Cas a prop or puppet\u8221\'20\'1D by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  in Washington.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m an eighth-generation Texan,\u8221\'20\'1D Talarico said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve only been in DC twice in my life \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m a former middle-school teacher who ran for office just to try to make my community better and I swore an oath when I first got elected two years ago to uphold the constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution of the United States, and also the constitution of the great state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 . And after our former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started his big lie that the election was stolen. Republican legislators in capitols across the country started \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hegseth interrupted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow did you make this about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 20 seconds?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked.\par \par \uc2 Talarico was happy to explain:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/14/fox-news-host-texas-democrat-james-talerico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Did Donald Trump lose?\u8217\'20\'19 Fox News host won\u8217\'20\'19t answer Texas Democrat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on Capitol Hill for a meeting to discuss Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan. The president will attend the Senate Democratic caucus\u8217\'20\'19 weekly policy lunch, as senators await more details on the plan, which was announced last night. It\u8217\'20\'19s still unclear whether the more moderate members of the caucus, such as \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , will support the plan, which includes the Medicare expansion that progressives demanded.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer acknowledged it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Clong\u8221\'20\'1D road to passing the $3.5tn proposal. Senate Democrats still need to hammer out the details of the spending package and get the entire caucus on board before they can move forward. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are going to get this done because we so fervently believe that we must make average American lives a whole lot better,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 * Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  dismissed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Republican voting restrictions, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/democrats-voting-rights-us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts warn}}}\uc2  that the US is facing a potential democratic crisis. The Republican leader specifically mocked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the voting restrictions and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 election represent \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant test of our democracy since the Civil War,\u8221\'20\'1D as the president said in Philadelphia yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat utter nonsense,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be laugh-out-loud funny if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so completely and totally irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden arrives on Capitol Hill to discuss $3.5tn 'human infrastructure' plan\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived on Capitol Hill for his meeting on the $3.5tn infrastructure plan that Senate Democrats announced last night.\par \par \uc2 The president will attend the Senate Democratic caucus\u8217\'20\'19 weekly policy lunch, as senators await more details on the \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D bill.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna get this done!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden arriving at the Capitol to push infrastructure bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NZuSsVrFkV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NZuSsVrFkV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1415360037204135939?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden entered the Capitol walking next to Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer, and the longtime former senator joked that this was his \u8220\'20\'1Chomecoming\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As reporters shouted questions at him about the spending proposal, Biden simply replied, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get this done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer needs all 50 Democratic senators to support the plan in order to vote it out of the Senate, and some moderates in the caucus, including \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , have not yet indicated whether they will support the proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about Olivia Rodrigo \u8217\'20\'19s plans at the White House today, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the pop star will meet with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary reiterated that the White House will put out a video of Rodrigo encouraging young people to get vaccinated, although she did not offer an expected release time for the video.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said Rodrigo\u8217\'20\'19s visit was the latest effort by the White House to \u8220\'20\'1Cmeet people where they are\u8221\'20\'1D as officials try to increase coronavirus vaccination rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will say, not every 18-year-old uses their time to come do this, so we appreciate her willingness to,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 After Olivia Rodrigo left the White House briefing room (much to the disappointment of this blogger), \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  took questions about Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D package.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked Psaki what are \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmust-haves\u8221\'20\'1D for the bill, as Senate Democrats start to hammer out the details of the spending package.\par \par \uc2 Psaki deflected that question, saying she did not want to negotiate from the briefing room podium. She did reiterate Bernie Sanders \u8217\'20\'19 description of the bill as \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric,\u8221\'20\'1D and she said the framework outlined by Senate Democrats is \u8220\'20\'1Creflective of the president\u8217\'20\'19s priorities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Noting Biden will be on Capitol Hill today, Psaki said, \u8220\'20\'1CNow he\u8217\'20\'19s going to engage; he\u8217\'20\'19s going to advocate with members; he\u8217\'20\'19s going to advocate with the American people and communicate and sell the package about why it needs to go forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Olivia Rodrigo encourages vaccinations in White House briefing room\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is holding her daily briefing with reporters, and she was joined by a very special guest: pop star Olivia Rodrigo.\par \par \uc2 The actress and singer was at the White House to record videos to encourage younger Americans to get vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Stepping up to the White House briefing room podium, Rodrigo said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond honored and humbled\u8221\'20\'1D to assist the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s vaccination outreach efforts.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Rodrigo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Olivia_Rodrigo}}}\uc2  statement on importance of youth vaccination: "It's important to have conversations with friends and family members encouraging all communities to get vaccinated." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/anXxJKnRZP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/anXxJKnRZP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1415353134986276872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important to have conversations with friends and family members encouraging all communities to get vaccinated and actually get to a vaccination site, which you can do more easily than ever before,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodrigo said.\par \par \uc2 Rodrigo is also expected to meet today with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser.\par \par \uc2 (And you\u8217\'20\'19re welcome for sparing you any \u8220\'20\'1CDrivers License\u8221\'20\'1D puns because they have all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KJP46/status/1415352782475902981"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already been made}}}\uc2  today.)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine provides some insightful analysis of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s voting rights speech yesterday:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/13/joe-biden-republicans-voting-rights-philadelphia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave his most muscular defense}}}\uc2  of the right to vote yet on Tuesday, but offered few specifics on how Democrats could overcome Republican efforts to stymie federal voting reform.\par \par \uc2 Coming after some activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/28/biden-democrats-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned}}}\uc2  how seriously the White House was taking the issue, an impassioned speech in Philadelphia marked a clear escalation of the president\u8217\'20\'19s defense of voting rights. Bluntly calling out lies about the 2020 election as \u8220\'20\'1Cjust that, a big lie\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden denounced \u8220\'20\'1Can assault on democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s an unfolding assault taking place in America today, an attempt to suppress and subvert the right to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But the most significant part of the speech lay in what he did not say. Biden did not mention the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/13/house-democrats-senate-filibuster-exception-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibuster}}}\uc2 , the Senate rule under which 60 votes are required to proceed on legislation.\par \par \uc2 Republicans used the rule last month to block sweeping voting rights reform. While the filibuster is in place, Democrats have virtually no chance of passing any such bill.\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia, Biden made it clear he was not giving up on federal voting rights legislation. But he did not lay out a pathway. Even as he denounced \u8220\'20\'1Cpeddlers of lies\u8221\'20\'1D who he said were damaging democracy, he appeared to remain convinced Republicans could be persuaded to sign on to legislation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/13/joe-biden-voting-rights-filibuster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden defends voting rights \u8211\'20\'13 but no word on ending the filibuster}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  also mocked the Texas Democratic legislators who fled the state to block Republican voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic lawmakers left Austin on Monday to break quorum on the Texas House\u8217\'20\'19 special legislative session, thus preventing Republicans from advancing their voting bill.\par \par \uc2 But McConnell questioned the legislators\u8217\'20\'19 true intentions in coming to Washington as they try to run out the clock on the 30-day special session.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn reality, they\u8217\'20\'19ve just come here to Washington to snap selfies, bask in the limelight and beg Senate Democrats to take over Texas elections,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said on the Senate floor this morning. \u8220\'20\'1COnce again, this outrage is completely phony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic legislators met with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  yesterday, and they have pleaded with Senate Democrats to pass national voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here in DC, our nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital, because we want to protect the civil right to vote for millions of Texans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Texas state representative Rhetta Bowers at a press conference yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t stay here indefinitely to run out the clock to stop Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 anti-voter attacks. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we need Congress to act now to pass the For the People Act. Texas Democrats will do everything in our power to fight back. But we need Congress to act now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/12/democrats-texas-voting-rights-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why did Democratic lawmakers flee Texas over voter restrictions?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 McConnell mocks Biden's criticism of voting restrictions as experts warn of democratic crisis\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  dismissed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s fiery criticism of Republican voting restrictions as \u8220\'20\'1Cutter nonsense\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Republican leader specifically mocked Biden for referring to the voting restrictions and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant test of our democracy since the Civil War\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat utter nonsense,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said in a Senate floor speech. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be laugh-out-loud funny if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so completely and totally irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  walks to the Senate floor in the US Capitol. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/EPA\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s comments came one day after Biden delivered a speech in Philadelphia condemning Republican efforts to restrict access to the ballot box and emphasizing the need to pass national voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 21st century Jim Crow assault is real,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unrelenting, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to challenge it vigorously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting rights experts have echoed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s concerns, warning that the Republican restrictions and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D could threaten the very foundation of American democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a ticking timebomb,\u8221\'20\'1D Wendy Weiser, the director of the democracy program at the Brennan Center for Justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/democrats-voting-rights-us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian in May}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brennan Center has called for the passage of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 two major voting rights bills, the For the People Act and the \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  Voting Rights Act, which remain stalled in the Senate because of a Republican filibuster.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be a significant failure if [Congress] doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass these two pieces of major voting legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Weiser said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be a significant failure for the country, for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read all of \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s voting rights coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-fight-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 For $12, you can buy a red beverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.winred.com/ron-desantis/storefront/drink-a-beer-red-beverage-cooler-set-of-2/details/?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=071321_koozie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cooler}}}\uc2  imprinted with the words: \u8220\'20\'1CHow the hell am I going to be able to drink a beer with a mask on?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those with deeper pockets can be the proud owner of a $21 T-shirt stamped with the map of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and the logo \u8220\'20\'1CLove My Gov\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CKeep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  Free\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But perhaps the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.winred.com/ron-desantis/storefront/?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=071221_keepfloridafreelaunch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merchandise}}}\uc2  with the best sales potential are the drink koozies and T-shirts that say \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Fauci My Florida\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The slogan , first reported by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/07/13/desantis-fauci-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 , is the brainchild of the team around \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican governor of Florida who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/05/08/politics/desantis-presidential-run-democrats-midterms/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hoping}}}\uc2  he can ride \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s coattails all the way to the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The phrase is a dig at \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the chief White House medical adviser who because of his cautionary approach to the deadly coronavirus and mask-wearing has become a popular punch-bag for Republicans. There is no road that leads to conservative supremacy, it seems, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t run over America\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious diseases expert.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/florida-ron-desantis-digs-fauci-merchandise-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Covid cases rise in Florida, Governor DeSantis digs at Fauci with merchandise}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 fundraising arm raised $45.4 million over the last three months, marking a quarterly record for the group as Republicans seek to flip control of Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-government-and-politics-house-elections-bf36b4f16d1211c2c11bc161d824553b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 That total was bolstered by $20.1 million raised in June, the highest ever monthly off-year total, according to numbers shared with The Associated Press before a public filing deadline.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee last week announced that it had raised $14.4 million in June, bringing its second-quarter total to about $36.5 million \u8212\'20\'14 its best ever for that stretch.\par \par \uc2 The large sums signal that excitement is high among donors to both parties as they prepare for what is expected to be a contentious midterm election season.\par \par \uc2 Republicans only need to flip a handful of seats in the House to take back control of the chamber, and redistricting and historical trends may help them achieve that goal.\par \par \uc2 Historically, the president\u8217\'20\'19s party loses congressional seats in the midterms after his election. Republicans also have the ability to redraw congressional district lines in dozens of states, following the 2020 census.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Olivia Rodrigo has arrived at the White House to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/14/joe-biden-senate-democrats-human-infrastructure-live-latest?page=with:block-60eef8038f080074230bf1e4#block-60eef8038f080074230bf1e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record videos}}}\uc2  encouraging young people to get vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 An AP reporter captured this picture of the pop star entering the West Wing:\par \par \uc2 enltrOlivia Rodrigo enters the West Wing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5IAEZRYhGa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5IAEZRYhGa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Zeke Miller\uc2  (@ZekeJMiller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZekeJMiller/status/1415325522314371072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pop star Olivia Rodrigo is coming to the White House today to encourage younger Americans to get vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COlivia Rodrigo is stopping by the White House today with a clear message to young people: get vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the best way to keep yourself and your loved ones safe from the dangerous new COVID-19 variants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOlivia Rodrigo is stopping by the White House today with a clear message to young people: get vaccinated. It\u8217\'20\'19s the best way to keep yourself and your loved ones safe from the dangerous new COVID-19 variants. Head to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4MYpWqXVVo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4MYpWqXVVo}}}\uc2  to find a clinic near you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1415316454791172096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A White House official confirmed Rodrigo\u8217\'20\'19s visit yesterday, saying she will \u8220\'20\'1Crecord videos about the importance of young people getting vaccinated, including answering important questions young people have about getting vaccinated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The videos will be shared on Rodrigo\u8217\'20\'19s social media channels, which collectively have more than 28 million followers.\par \par \uc2 She is expected to meet with Biden and \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, during her visit.\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s partnership with Rodrigo comes as data shows young Americans between the ages of 18 and 29 are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/young-americans-arent-getting-vaccinated-jeopardizing-covid-19-fight-11625995802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly less likely}}}\uc2  to be vaccinated than their older counterparts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer acknowledges 'long' road ahead on passing infrastructure bill\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer praised the \u8220\'20\'1Clandmark agreement\u8221\'20\'1D reached by Democratic members of the budget committee last night to produce the $3.5tn infrastructure plan.\par \par \uc2 Schumer said the agreement would \u8220\'20\'1Cpave the way for historic legislation later this year called the American Jobs and Families Plan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVery simply, this budget resolution will allow us to pass the most significant legislation to expand support and help American families since the New Deal - since the New Deal,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Chuck Schumer: "Last night the Senate Democratic majority on the Budget Committee reached a landmark agreement on a $3.5 trillion budget resolution." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W22LNfPmO9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/W22LNfPmO9}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A6w8w7S9D4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A6w8w7S9D4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Hill (@thehill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill/status/1415316692662689793?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Democratic leader also acknowledged that much work remains to be done before the bill reach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s desk. The president will be on Capitol Hill today to talk to senators about the plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know the road ahead is going to be long. There are bumps along the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are going to get this done because we so fervently believe that we must make average American lives a whole lot better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer plans to pass the bill using reconciliation, meaning Democrats will not need to gain any Republican support to approve the plan, but some moderate Senate Democrats have not yet indicated whether they are in favor of the proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin reserves judgment on infrastructure plan for now\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  has issued a statement on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan, which was released last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know my Democratic colleagues on the budget committee have worked hard and I look forward to reviewing their agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D the West Virginia senator said.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the \uc2 Senate Budget Committee\uc2 's $3.5 trillion infrastructure package: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qstcR85flP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qstcR85flP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (@Sen_JoeManchin)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sen_JoeManchin/status/1415310987348037633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m also very interested in how this proposal is paid for and how it enables us to remain globally competitive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will reserve any final judgment until I\u8217\'20\'19ve had the opportunity to thoroughly evaluate the proposal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In order to get the infrastructure package through the Senate, majority leader Chuck Schumer will need the support of every member of the Democratic caucus.\par \par \uc2 All eyes will be on Manchin and fellow moderate Kyrsten Sinema as they review the details of the plan, which they will have a chance to do at today\u8217\'20\'19s policy lunch with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Manchin has previously indicated he wants the infrastructure plan to be fully financed, so the pay-fors in the bill could determine whether or not he supports it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood files lawsuit against Texas\u8217\'20\'19 extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Mary Tuma reports from Austin, Texas:\par \par \uc2 In a highly anticipated move, Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/WWH-v.-Jackson-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a federal lawsuit}}}\uc2  on Tuesday against the state\u8217\'20\'19s draconian six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Senate Bill 8 that would empower private citizens to enforce the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Texas legislature\u8217\'20\'19s well-documented hostility to the rights of pregnant people has gone to a new extreme,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the lawsuit, filed by groups including Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2 , along with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support fund groups, doctors, health clinic staff, and clergy members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenate Bill 8 flagrantly violates the constitutional rights of Texans seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and upends the rule of law in service of an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which offers no exception for rape or incest, bars the procedure when embryonic cardiac activity is detected, which is around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before most women even know they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 amounting to a near-total ban.\par \par \uc2 It also allows any private citizen, including anti-choice activists unrelated to the patient, the right to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, rather than tasking the state with enforcement.\par \par \uc2 In fact, any person that \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, such as a friend or family member that pays for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a sexual assault counselor who calls a clinic on behalf of a patient, could be targeted, potentially opening the floodgates to harassing lawsuits that could push \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics into forced closure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unthinkable that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists could be allowed to stand in the way of people accessing essential health care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melaney A Linton, president of Planned Parenthood Gulf Coast.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/texas-abortion-ban-lawsuit-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood files lawsuit against Texas\u8217\'20\'19 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans wasted no time in criticizing Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 $3.5tn proposal, arguing that the plan would cause prices to rise in the US.\par \par \uc2 Congressman Jason Smith, the top Republican on the House budget committee, directly tied the new proposal to the labor department\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-prices-consumer-prices-7c0dceffdbd50a8b1b888af5d3b922ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest report}}}\uc2  showing inflation growth hit a 13-year high last month.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe very same day we find out that inflation growth is the highest it's been in 10 years, Washington Democrats are celebrating trillions more in spending. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i8XVVyW0sx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/i8XVVyW0sx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Jason Smith (@RepJasonSmith) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJasonSmith/status/1415161151080517633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe very same day we find out that year over year inflation growth is the highest it\u8217\'20\'19s been in over 10 years, Democrats are proposing throwing trillions more of inflation fueled logs on the fire,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe political leaders in Washington and President Biden are failing the working class families who can least afford it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But again, Democrats do not need any Republican support to pass their reconciliation bill. They simply need all Senate Democrats and almost all House Democrats to vote in favor of the package -- although that will likely be hard enough on its own.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will also meet this afternoon with a bipartisan group of governors and mayors to discuss the importance of passing the bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressional leaders have a long to-do list for the month of July. They are hoping to turn the bipartisan framework into a bill and get it passed, while also advancing their reconciliation package to cover more of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative priorities.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer has already warned that the upper chamber\u8217\'20\'19s work may spill over into the August recess, which would irritate members on both sides of the aisle.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to his Democratic colleagues last week, Schumer warned, \u8220\'20\'1CPlease be advised that time is of the essence and we have a lot of work to do. Senators should be prepared for the possibility of working long nights, weekends, and remaining in Washington into the previously-scheduled August state work period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senators will likely discuss the timeline for passing the two infrastructure bills when Biden visits Capitol Hill today for Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 weekly policy lunch.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to visit Capitol to discuss Democrats' $3.5tn infrastructure plan\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel from the White House to Capitol Hill today to attend the Senate Democratic caucus\u8217\'20\'19s weekly lunch.\par \par \uc2 The discussion among the president and senators will focus on the $3.5tn \u8220\'20\'1Chuman infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D plan that Democrats released last night.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer said Biden would attend the lunch \u8220\'20\'1Cto lead us on to getting this wonderful plan\u8221\'20\'1D passed.\par \par \uc2 Flanked by senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , left, senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , second from left, and senator \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2 , right, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer offers remarks during a press conference. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very proud of this plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know we have a long road to go. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get this done for the sake of making average Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives a whole lot better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats plan to pass the plan using reconciliation, meaning they can pass the package with a simple majority and do not need any Republican support.\par \par \uc2 But the proposal still has some roadblocks ahead. The overall price tag is much less than the $6tn that progressive senators Bernie Sanders, who chairs the budget committee, had pushed for.\par \par \uc2 However, the proposal also includes a Medicare expansion to include dental, vision and hearing benefits, which has been a top priority for progressives.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Schumer will need to keep all members of the Senate Democratic caucus on board to get the bill passed. Today marks the first test of whether they can do so. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 2021-07-14T13:33:07Z 2021-07-15T00:07:55Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/1d11e17be4bb6a0ef9dcc201039dd764d82158db/0_234_6999_4199/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/1d11e17be4bb6a0ef9dcc201039dd764d82158db/0_234_6999_4199/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Biden with Chuck Schumer on Wednesday. Schumer joked that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s meeting on Capitol Hill represented a \u8216\'20\'18homecoming\u8217\'20\'19. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meet with a bipartisan group of city and state political leaders. Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  walks to the Senate floor in the US Capitol. Flanked by senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , left, senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , second from left, and senator \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2 , right, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer offers remarks during a press conference.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210714eh7e0028n\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\asp